translate chinese strings:

    old "Ready to go to Triberg and finish the job, [protag]?"
    new "Ready to go to Triberg and finish the job, [protag]?\n准备好去Triberg完成任务了吗，[protag]？"

    old "When you're ready just let me know."
    new "When you're ready just let me know.\n等你准备好了就告诉我。"

    old "There are no big towns in this area, however several traveling merchants can be found alongside the borders. Probably reselling whatever 'treasure' the adventurers found in this dangerous place."
    new "There are no big towns in this area, however several traveling merchants can be found alongside the borders. Probably reselling whatever 'treasure' the adventurers found in this dangerous place.\n这一带没有大城镇，不过在边境沿线能找到几个行商。他们多半是在倒卖冒险者在这个危险之地找到的那些“宝藏”。"

    old "[protag], come in."
    new "[protag], come in.\n[protag]，请回答。"

    old "Nuala told me you wanted to see me?"
    new "Nuala told me you wanted to see me?\nNuala告诉我你想见我？"

    old "Ah the shaman. She has an impressive knowledge of the arcane, considering her young age."
    new "Ah the shaman. She has an impressive knowledge of the arcane, considering her young age.\n啊，是那位萨满。以她这样的年纪，她对奥术的造诣实在令人惊叹。"

    old "She does. What do you want to talk about?"
    new "She does. What do you want to talk about?\n确实如此。你想谈什么？"

    old "Nuala told me about the team meeting. It was a good idea."
    new "Nuala told me about the team meeting. It was a good idea.\nNuala跟我说了那次小队会议的事。那是个好主意。"

    old "To be entirely fair, it was Karen's."
    new "To be entirely fair, it was Karen's.\n说句公道话，那是Karen的主意。"

    old "I see. Anyway, I am pleased by your progress. However, I have bad news."
    new "I see. Anyway, I am pleased by your progress. However, I have bad news.\n我明白了。总之，我很满意你的进展。不过，我有坏消息。"

    old "Ugh. More bad news?"
    new "Ugh. More bad news?\n唉。又是坏消息？"

    old "I'm sorry, but I think you need to know. I am not sure what you'll find inside the Castle Of N'Mar on your infiltration mission..."
    new "I'm sorry, but I think you need to know. I am not sure what you'll find inside the Castle Of N'Mar on your infiltration mission...\n抱歉，但我想你应该知道。我不确定你在潜入N'Mar城堡的任务中会发现什么……"

    old "But?"
    new "But?\n但是？"

    old "Let's say that what you find is beyond your small team capabilities. That you need more people. Like, an army."
    new "Let's say that what you find is beyond your small team capabilities. That you need more people. Like, an army.\n这么说吧，你在里面发现的东西超出了你这个小队的能力范围。你需要更多人。比如，一支军队。"

    old "Could be. And?"
    new "Could be. And?\n有可能。然后呢？"

    old "To put it plainly, the Council is broke."
    new "To put it plainly, the Council is broke.\n说白了，议会已经破产了。"

    old "...what? The might Human Empire has no money?"
    new "...what? The might Human Empire has no money?\n……什么？强大的人类帝国居然没钱了？"

    old "They spent too much in recent years, with all the ongoing wars scattered in the four corners of Aravorn. You have no idea how much money gets wasted to run such a giant bureaucratic machine."
    new "They spent too much in recent years, with all the ongoing wars scattered in the four corners of Aravorn. You have no idea how much money gets wasted to run such a giant bureaucratic machine.\n这些年来他们开销太大，Aravorn各地战事不断。你根本无法想象，运转这么一台庞大的官僚机器要浪费多少钱。"

    old "I'm a merchant, I'm familiar with money issues. It's incredible how much money you waste on small things. I can imagine how it can be for an Empire."
    new "I'm a merchant, I'm familiar with money issues. It's incredible how much money you waste on small things. I can imagine how it can be for an Empire.\n我是商人，对钱的事很熟悉。你们在小事上浪费的钱多得惊人。我能想象，对一个帝国来说会是什么样。"

    old "Good."
    new "Good.\n很好。"

    old "If they hired me as debt collector, they would have more money now."
    new "If they hired me as debt collector, they would have more money now.\n如果他们雇我去讨债，现在就会有钱多了。"

    old "I doubt you could get back cash lost in the less...'official' business. Bribing enemy guards, hiring spies, paying ransoms, and so on."
    new "I doubt you could get back cash lost in the less...'official' business. Bribing enemy guards, hiring spies, paying ransoms, and so on.\n我看你是讨不回那些花在不太……“正规”事情上的钱。贿赂敌方守卫、雇佣间谍、支付赎金，诸如此类。"

    old "I see."
    new "I see.\n原来如此。"

    old "This is a big problem, Apolimesho. However, let me see first what's inside N'Mar, before we start to worry."
    new "This is a big problem, Apolimesho. However, let me see first what's inside N'Mar, before we start to worry.\n这是个很大的问题，Apolimesho。不过，在我们开始担心之前，先让我看看N'Mar里面到底是什么情况。"

    old "Though judging from what I saw during my first encounter, there are going to be many undead there."
    new "Though judging from what I saw during my first encounter, there are going to be many undead there.\n不过从我第一次遭遇时看到的情况来看，那里会有很多亡灵。"

    old "I'll keep thinking about a solution while you're away. And [protag]? You might want to visit Lothark and Horus."
    new "I'll keep thinking about a solution while you're away. And [protag]? You might want to visit Lothark and Horus.\n你离开的这段时间，我会继续想对策。还有，[protag]，你也许该去Lothark和Horus看看。"

    old "Why?"
    new "Why?\n为什么？"

    old "Lothark is a big commercial hub, probably the biggest of this area. They have rare items from all around Aravorn."
    new "Lothark is a big commercial hub, probably the biggest of this area. They have rare items from all around Aravorn.\nLothark是个大型商贸中心，可能是这一带最大的。那里有来自Aravorn各地的稀有物品。"

    old "Horus is well known for their magic schools. That's where I began my studies in magic long time ago. They probably can sell you powerful magical items."
    new "Horus is well known for their magic schools. That's where I began my studies in magic long time ago. They probably can sell you powerful magical items.\nHorus以魔法学院闻名。很久以前，我就是在那里开始学习魔法的。他们大概能卖给你强大的魔法物品。"

    old "Ah yes. I've traveled there a few times as merchant. I was so focused on my recruit efforts that I forgot."
    new "Ah yes. I've traveled there a few times as merchant. I was so focused on my recruit efforts that I forgot.\n啊，对。我当商人的时候去过那里几次。之前光顾着招兵买马，把这事忘了。"

    old "Thanks Apolimesho. I'll keep this in mind."
    new "Thanks Apolimesho. I'll keep this in mind.\n谢谢，Apolimesho。我会记住的。"

    old "Good luck in your efforts."
    new "Good luck in your efforts.\n祝你好运。"

    old "Hello, [protag]. How I may be of assistance?"
    new "Hello, [protag]. How I may be of assistance?\n你好，[protag]。有什么我能帮上忙的吗？"

    old "I'm a bit lost on what I should be doing next. Do you have any advice for me?"
    new "I'm a bit lost on what I should be doing next. Do you have any advice for me?\n我有点不知道该做什么了。你有什么建议吗？"

    old "Hmm. I would suggest you pay a visit to Karen. After all she offered one of her best warriors to help you. You should definitely take up on that offer."
    new "Hmm. I would suggest you pay a visit to Karen. After all she offered one of her best warriors to help you. You should definitely take up on that offer.\n嗯。我建议你去拜访一下Karen。毕竟她提出派一位她最优秀的战士来帮你。你绝对应该接受这个提议。"

    old "Keeping your team trained and well equipped is essential for your mission."
    new "Keeping your team trained and well equipped is essential for your mission.\n让你的队伍保持训练有素、装备精良，对你的任务至关重要。"

    old "Grimoire, Horus and the Citadel have an Arena and you can participate in non-lethal fights to test your team against skilled warriors and make experience."
    new "Grimoire, Horus and the Citadel have an Arena and you can participate in non-lethal fights to test your team against skilled warriors and make experience.\nGrimoire、Horus和Citadel都有竞技场，你可以参加非致命的对决，让队伍与技艺娴熟的战士较量，积累经验。"

    old "You can also browse the shops in each town if you need to equip yourself and your team."
    new "You can also browse the shops in each town if you need to equip yourself and your team.\n如果你需要给自己和队伍置办装备，也可以去各城镇的商店逛逛。"

    old "One last word of advice: "
    new "One last word of advice: \n最后一句忠告："

    old "Focus on building a good team. I'm sure Karen will be able to provide you with some leads."
    new "Focus on building a good team. I'm sure Karen will be able to provide you with some leads.\n专心打造一支好队伍。我相信Karen能给你一些线索。"

    old "Thanks, Apolimesho. I must go now."
    new "Thanks, Apolimesho. I must go now.\n谢谢，Apolimesho。我得走了。"

    old "May the Gods watch over you."
    new "May the Gods watch over you.\n愿诸神护佑你。"

    old "Bad luck! You didn't manage to defeat your opponents. But you can always try again..."
    new "Bad luck! You didn't manage to defeat your opponents. But you can always try again...\n运气不好！你没能击败对手。但你随时可以再试一次……"

    old "Congratulations on your victory! Because you won against the odds, your Reputation in [town] increased by [i] !"
    new "Congratulations on your victory! Because you won against the odds, your Reputation in [town] increased by [i] !\n恭喜你获胜！因为你是以弱胜强，你在[town]的声望提升了[i]点！"

    old "Congratulations on your victory! You have gained 1 Reputation in [town]!"
    new "Congratulations on your victory! You have gained 1 Reputation in [town]!\n恭喜你获胜！你在[town]获得了1点声望！"

    old "You reached the maximum reputation value of 50 in [town]. You can still train in the arena to get money and XP, but you won't get any more Reputation."
    new "You reached the maximum reputation value of 50 in [town]. You can still train in the arena to get money and XP, but you won't get any more Reputation.\n你在[town]的声望已达到上限50点。你仍可在竞技场训练以获取金钱和经验，但不会再获得声望。"

    old "Apolimesho. You asked to see me?"
    new "Apolimesho. You asked to see me?\nApolimesho。你找我？"

    old "Only 10 days left until full moon."
    new "Only 10 days left until full moon.\n离满月只剩10天了。"

    old "And I heard the training program is a success, most of the time your team is in the arena."
    new "And I heard the training program is a success, most of the time your team is in the arena.\n而且我听说训练计划很成功，你的队伍大部分时间都在竞技场。"

    old "To complete your equipment Queen Karen asked me to give you this. With best greetings from the Amazons' Treasury."
    new "To complete your equipment Queen Karen asked me to give you this. With best greetings from the Amazons' Treasury.\n为了补全你的装备，Karen女王让我把这个交给你。并带来Amazons宝库最诚挚的问候。"

    old "He gives me a small chest."
    new "He gives me a small chest.\n他给了我一个小箱子。"

    old "I think you found a good compromise between training and rest. Tired warriors don't fight well."
    new "I think you found a good compromise between training and rest. Tired warriors don't fight well.\n我想你在训练和休息之间找到了很好的平衡。疲惫的战士是打不好仗的。"

    old "Don't you think you should use the arenas to train your team? Overcoming the castle's defences will be hard."
    new "Don't you think you should use the arenas to train your team? Overcoming the castle's defences will be hard.\n你不觉得应该利用竞技场来训练你的队伍吗？攻克那座城堡的防线会很艰难。"

    old "Use it well. You must not fail."
    new "Use it well. You must not fail.\n好好利用。你绝不能失败。"

    old "Thank you, and give Queen Karen my regards."
    new "Thank you, and give Queen Karen my regards.\n谢谢，请代我向Karen女王问好。"

    old "The path to the Amazon domain is treacherous and narrow. The Amazons know how to make a territory naturally hostile to invaders, I'll certainly give them that."
    new "The path to the Amazon domain is treacherous and narrow. The Amazons know how to make a territory naturally hostile to invaders, I'll certainly give them that.\n通往Amazon领地的路险峻而狭窄。Amazons确实懂得如何让一片领土对入侵者天然充满敌意，这一点我不得不服。"

    old "The craggy rock path makes it easy to follow the narrow path without slipping, but I find myself constantly forced to adjust my balance along its uneven surface."
    new "The craggy rock path makes it easy to follow the narrow path without slipping, but I find myself constantly forced to adjust my balance along its uneven surface.\n嶙峋的岩石小路让人沿着狭窄的山路行走时不至于滑倒，但我发现自己不得不时刻在崎岖不平的路面上调整平衡。"

    old "In the distance, I can see the fortress. With its high walls and imposing towers, it appears intimidating, or at least as intimidating as a distant structure can. At least I know I've found the right place. There's no way that this structure can be anything other than the Amazon citadel."
    new "In the distance, I can see the fortress. With its high walls and imposing towers, it appears intimidating, or at least as intimidating as a distant structure can. At least I know I've found the right place. There's no way that this structure can be anything other than the Amazon citadel.\n远处，我能看到那座要塞。高耸的城墙和威严的塔楼让它显得气势逼人——至少，一座远景中的建筑能有多逼人，它就有多逼人。至少我知道自己来对了地方。这座建筑不可能是别的，只能是Amazon的要塞。"

    old "Stop right there, elf."
    new "Stop right there, elf.\n站住，精灵。"

    old "A voice from above catches me off guard."
    new "A voice from above catches me off guard.\n头顶传来一个声音，打得我措手不及。"

    old "I look up and spot an Amazon woman, perched upon a rock spire. Her blade is pointed toward me."
    new "I look up and spot an Amazon woman, perched upon a rock spire. Her blade is pointed toward me.\n我抬头看去，发现一名Amazon女人栖身在一根石尖之上。她的刀刃正指着我。"

    old "What business do you have here? What's your name, elf?"
    new "What business do you have here? What's your name, elf?\n你到这里来有何贵干？你叫什么名字，精灵？"

    old "Stop right there, dwarf."
    new "Stop right there, dwarf.\n站住，矮人。"

    old "What business do you have here? What's your name, dwarf?"
    new "What business do you have here? What's your name, dwarf?\n你到这里来有何贵干？你叫什么名字，矮人？"

    old "Stop right there, human."
    new "Stop right there, human.\n站住，人类。"

    old "What business do you have here? What's your name?"
    new "What business do you have here? What's your name?\n你到这里来有何贵干？你叫什么名字？"

    old "I'm [protag]. I'm-"
    new "I'm [protag]. I'm-\n我是[protag]。我——"

    old "You're here to see the queen."
    new "You're here to see the queen.\n你是来觐见女王的。"

    old "Yes, I was about to say that."
    new "Yes, I was about to say that.\n是的，我正要说这个。"

    old "The queen has been expecting you."
    new "The queen has been expecting you.\n女王一直在等你。"

    old "The woman leaps down from the spire, handing next to me. If she'd wanted to land with her blade pointed toward my chest, there's precious little I could have done to stop her."
    new "The woman leaps down from the spire, handing next to me. If she'd wanted to land with her blade pointed toward my chest, there's precious little I could have done to stop her.\n那女人从石尖上一跃而下，落在我身旁。要是她想让刀刃对着我的胸口落地，我几乎没有任何办法阻止她。"

    old "Best not to keep the queen waiting. Follow me."
    new "Best not to keep the queen waiting. Follow me.\n最好别让女王久等。跟我来。"

    old "Do you have a name?"
    new "Do you have a name?\n你有名字吗？"

    old "Not that you need to know it, but my name is Leena."
    new "Not that you need to know it, but my name is Leena.\n倒也不是你非要知道，不过我叫Leena。"

    old "Leena keeps her back turned to me, and I find myself quickening my pace to keep up with her."
    new "Leena keeps her back turned to me, and I find myself quickening my pace to keep up with her.\nLeena背对着我，我发现自己得加快脚步才能跟上她。"

    old "I hear the sound of shifting rocks above me, and look up to see another rock spire with an Amazon woman perched above me. It appears that Leena was only the first of many. Or maybe she wasn't the first. Who knows how many other women saw me from above while I was completely unaware?"
    new "I hear the sound of shifting rocks above me, and look up to see another rock spire with an Amazon woman perched above me. It appears that Leena was only the first of many. Or maybe she wasn't the first. Who knows how many other women saw me from above while I was completely unaware?\n我听到头顶传来岩石移动的声响，抬头看见另一根石尖上栖着一名Amazon女人。看来Leena只是许多人中的第一个。又或许她并不是第一个。谁知道在我浑然不觉的时候，上面有多少双女人的眼睛正看着我？"

    old "Are they all sentries? The women on the rocks, watching from above."
    new "Are they all sentries? The women on the rocks, watching from above.\n她们都是哨兵吗？就是那些在岩石上、从高处俯瞰的女人。"

    old "They're sentries, but they rotate. It's an Amazon warrior's duty to keep vigilant watch over her domain, and every warrior-in-training serves time on watch duty."
    new "They're sentries, but they rotate. It's an Amazon warrior's duty to keep vigilant watch over her domain, and every warrior-in-training serves time on watch duty.\n她们是哨兵，不过是轮值的。保持警惕地守望自己的领地是Amazon战士的职责，每个受训中的战士都要轮值放哨。"

    old "So you're a warrior-in-training?"
    new "So you're a warrior-in-training?\n所以你是在受训的战士？"

    old "No, I'm a trainer. Many of the woman that you see above were once students under me."
    new "No, I'm a trainer. Many of the woman that you see above were once students under me.\n不，我是教官。你在上面看到的许多女人，都曾是我的学生。"

    old "None of them are currently your students?"
    new "None of them are currently your students?\n现在没有一个是你的学生了？"

    old "No. Since I was promoted to captain of the guard, I've had more pressing matters to attend to."
    new "No. Since I was promoted to captain of the guard, I've had more pressing matters to attend to.\n没有。自从我被提拔为卫队长之后，就有更要紧的事务要处理了。"

    old "So you're no longer a teacher, then."
    new "So you're no longer a teacher, then.\n所以你已经不再教书了。"

    old "I still teach. But I have only one student. The queen's daughter."
    new "I still teach. But I have only one student. The queen's daughter.\n我还在教。只是我现在只有一个学生。女王的女儿。"

    old "The queen has a daughter?"
    new "The queen has a daughter?\n女王有个女儿？"

    old "Of course she does. A monarchy is only as strong as its bloodline. And as the young princess's teacher, it's my responsibility to help ensure the strength and integrity of that bloodline."
    new "Of course she does. A monarchy is only as strong as its bloodline. And as the young princess's teacher, it's my responsibility to help ensure the strength and integrity of that bloodline.\n她当然有。一个王室的强盛取决于它的血脉。而作为年轻公主的老师，帮助确保这条血脉的强大与纯正，是我的责任。"

    old "I hope my inquisitiveness isn't bothering you."
    new "I hope my inquisitiveness isn't bothering you.\n希望我的刨根问底没有打扰到你。"

    old "I've no particular fondness for conversation, but I'd have to have an incredibly thin skin for something as simple as a question to bother me. We're still quite a ways from the citadel. If you'd like to fill the silence with questioning, then go right ahead."
    new "I've no particular fondness for conversation, but I'd have to have an incredibly thin skin for something as simple as a question to bother me. We're still quite a ways from the citadel. If you'd like to fill the silence with questioning, then go right ahead.\n我本就不怎么喜欢闲聊，但要是一个简单的问题都能烦到我，那我的脸皮未免太薄了。我们离要塞还有相当一段路。如果你想用提问来打发这段沉默，那就尽管问吧。"

    old "Actually, there's something I find curious that I wanted to ask you."
    new "Actually, there's something I find curious that I wanted to ask you.\n其实，有件事我很好奇，想问问你。"

    old "Why do you refer to humans as... 'humans'? Aren't you Amazons human beings too?"
    new "Why do you refer to humans as... 'humans'? Aren't you Amazons human beings too?\n你们为什么把人类称作……“人类”？你们Amazons不也是人类吗？"

    old "We're not the only one. Have you ever met a Nomad? But to answer your question... I guess it all started when the human empire formed years ago. Many of us started to call you just 'humans' and it became widespread."
    new "We're not the only one. Have you ever met a Nomad? But to answer your question... I guess it all started when the human empire formed years ago. Many of us started to call you just 'humans' and it became widespread.\n我们不是唯一这么叫的。你见过Nomad吗？不过回答你的问题……我想这要追溯到多年前人类帝国建立的时候。那时我们中有很多人开始只把你们叫作“人类”，后来就传开了。"

    old "What's the queen like?"
    new "What's the queen like?\n女王是个什么样的人？"

    old "You've met Karen yourself, haven't you?"
    new "You've met Karen yourself, haven't you?\n你自己也见过Karen了，不是吗？"

    old "Yes, I have. But I didn't have time to gather much beyond the fact that she seems to hold a great deal of disdain for the elders of the human council."
    new "Yes, I have. But I didn't have time to gather much beyond the fact that she seems to hold a great deal of disdain for the elders of the human council.\n是的，我见过。不过除了她似乎对人类议会的那帮长老极其不屑之外，我没来得及了解更多。"

    old "She has plenty of company in that regard. Many people harbor dislike for the council of Grimoire, the Amazons perhaps most of all."
    new "She has plenty of company in that regard. Many people harbor dislike for the council of Grimoire, the Amazons perhaps most of all.\n在这件事上，她的同路人可不少。许多人对Grimoire议会都心怀不满，其中Amazons或许尤甚。"

    old "Amazons dislike humans?"
    new "Amazons dislike humans?\nAmazons讨厌人类？"

    old "Did I say anything about Amazons disliking humans? I hold no special affection for your culture, but neither do I harbor hatred. Individually, I have no bone to pick humans. Their leadership, on the other hand..."
    new "Did I say anything about Amazons disliking humans? I hold no special affection for your culture, but neither do I harbor hatred. Individually, I have no bone to pick humans. Their leadership, on the other hand...\n我说过Amazons讨厌人类了吗？我对你们的文化谈不上喜爱，但也没有怀恨在心。就个人而言，我并无意找人类的麻烦。至于他们的领导层，那就另当别论了……"

    old "Did I say anything about Amazons disliking humans? I hold no special affection for them, but neither do I harbor hatred. Individually, I have no bone to pick them. Their leadership, on the other hand..."
    new "Did I say anything about Amazons disliking humans? I hold no special affection for them, but neither do I harbor hatred. Individually, I have no bone to pick them. Their leadership, on the other hand...\n我说过Amazons讨厌人类了吗？我对他们谈不上喜爱，但也没有怀恨在心。就个人而言，我无意找他们的麻烦。至于他们的领导层，那就另当别论了……"

    old "Ah, well. The foibles of the empire are hardly uniquely human. Running an empire of that size is a difficult task. I suspect that if the elves or dwarves attempted such a task, their leadership would draw the same degree of hatred."
    new "Ah, well. The foibles of the empire are hardly uniquely human. Running an empire of that size is a difficult task. I suspect that if the elves or dwarves attempted such a task, their leadership would draw the same degree of hatred.\n啊，好吧。帝国的种种毛病并非人类独有。治理那样一个规模的帝国绝非易事。我猜想，若是精灵或矮人来接手这样的任务，他们的领导层也会招来同样程度的怨恨。"

    old "What about the Amazons? Do you think you could run an empire, spanning as wide as the one the humans now control?"
    new "What about the Amazons? Do you think you could run an empire, spanning as wide as the one the humans now control?\n那Amazons呢？你觉得你们能治理一个疆域如此辽阔、像现在人类所掌控的这样的帝国吗？"

    old "Ha. As if we would ever aspire to such a thing."
    new "Ha. As if we would ever aspire to such a thing.\n哈。说得好像我们会有那种野心似的。"

    old "I'm not sure that I follow."
    new "I'm not sure that I follow.\n我不太明白你的意思。"

    old "An Amazon does not measure the worth of something in its size or quantity, but in its strength and quality. Amazons seek to attain perfection, in and out of combat. How could one ever achieve perfection while spreading across the land like a plague?"
    new "An Amazon does not measure the worth of something in its size or quantity, but in its strength and quality. Amazons seek to attain perfection, in and out of combat. How could one ever achieve perfection while spreading across the land like a plague?\nAmazon衡量一件事物的价值，不凭它的大小或多寡，而凭它的力量与品质。Amazons追求极致，无论阵前还是阵后。像瘟疫一样四处蔓延，又怎么可能臻于极致？"

    old "The Amazon do not seek to grow their borders. We prize order too much to chase dreams of conquest."
    new "The Amazon do not seek to grow their borders. We prize order too much to chase dreams of conquest.\nAmazon不谋求扩张疆域。我们太珍视秩序，不屑于追逐征服的幻想。"

    old "What's it like, teaching the princess?"
    new "What's it like, teaching the princess?\n教公主是什么感觉？"

    old "Like teaching any other student, but with higher stakes."
    new "Like teaching any other student, but with higher stakes.\n就像教任何其他学生一样，只是赌注更高。"

    old "Higher stakes? How do you mean?"
    new "Higher stakes? How do you mean?\n更高的赌注？怎么说？"

    old "Not every Amazon trainee passes muster. Some fail to rise to the challenge, and take their own life."
    new "Not every Amazon trainee passes muster. Some fail to rise to the challenge, and take their own life.\n并非每个Amazon受训者都能达标。有些人没能迎接挑战，便结束了自己的生命。"

    old "That sounds barbaric."
    new "That sounds barbaric.\n这听起来很野蛮。"

    old "Call us barbarians if you like. But I hope you'll note that it is not the Amazons who have set about creating an empire which spans the continent. We are quite content to sit on our peninsula in isolation. Now, to conquer, that kind of behavior takes someone with a human's sensibilities."
    new "Call us barbarians if you like. But I hope you'll note that it is not the Amazons who have set about creating an empire which spans the continent. We are quite content to sit on our peninsula in isolation. Now, to conquer, that kind of behavior takes someone with a human's sensibilities.\n你大可以叫我们野蛮人。但我希望你能注意到，着手建立横跨大陆帝国的并不是Amazons。我们很满足于独处在自己的半岛上。而至于征服，那得是有人类那种心性的人才做得出来的事。"

    old "I'm not sure if I should resent that remark."
    new "I'm not sure if I should resent that remark.\n我不确定自己该不该对这句话感到愤懑。"

    old "If you call another culture's practices barbaric, you shouldn't take surprise when someone does the same back to you."
    new "If you call another culture's practices barbaric, you shouldn't take surprise when someone does the same back to you.\n你若把别的文化的做法称作野蛮，那别人也这么说你时，就不该感到意外。"

    old "For an Amazon, choosing to die by one's own blade is a mark of honor."
    new "For an Amazon, choosing to die by one's own blade is a mark of honor.\n对Amazon来说，选择死在自己的刀刃之下是一种荣耀。"

    old "So, those unable to face the challenges of war end their life to escape it. The coward's way out."
    new "So, those unable to face the challenges of war end their life to escape it. The coward's way out.\n那么，那些无法直面战争挑战的人，为了逃避而结束生命。这是懦夫的行径。"

    old "Do you really think that a coward has the strength to take their own life?"
    new "Do you really think that a coward has the strength to take their own life?\n你真的认为一个懦夫有力量结束自己的生命吗？"

    old "Suicide is an escape. Of course it's a cowardly act."
    new "Suicide is an escape. Of course it's a cowardly act.\n自杀是逃避。当然是懦弱之举。"

    old "It takes a special kind of fortitude to die by one's own blade. It is not a cowardly act to conquer pain and death."
    new "It takes a special kind of fortitude to die by one's own blade. It is not a cowardly act to conquer pain and death.\n死在自己的刀刃之下需要一种特殊的坚毅。战胜痛苦与死亡，绝非懦弱之举。"

    old "I suppose that's one way to achieve an honorable death."
    new "I suppose that's one way to achieve an honorable death.\n我想，那也算是获得体面死亡的一种方式。"

    old "Yes, it is. There is no death more honorable for an Amazon than death by the blade, even if that blade happens to be their own."
    new "Yes, it is. There is no death more honorable for an Amazon than death by the blade, even if that blade happens to be their own.\n是的。对Amazon而言，没有比死于刀刃之下更光荣的死法，即便那刀刃恰好是自己的。"

    old "However, for a princess, the consequences are much more dire. A princess holds in her hands not only her own honor, but the honor of her family. If a princess chooses death by her own blade before completing training, the crown cannot simply be passed down to a sibling. Her failure to pass muster calls into question the entire bloodline."
    new "However, for a princess, the consequences are much more dire. A princess holds in her hands not only her own honor, but the honor of her family. If a princess chooses death by her own blade before completing training, the crown cannot simply be passed down to a sibling. Her failure to pass muster calls into question the entire bloodline.\n然而，对一位公主来说，后果要严重得多。公主手中握着的不仅是她自己的荣誉，还有她家族的荣誉。如果公主在完成训练之前选择死在自己的刀刃之下，王冠并不能简单地传给某个手足。她未能达标，会让整条血脉受到质疑。"

    old "I thought that you said that suicide was an honorable way to die."
    new "I thought that you said that suicide was an honorable way to die.\n我记得你刚才还说自杀是光荣的死法。"

    old "Ritual suicide is a warrior's death. But a queen is called to be more than just a warrior. She is a leader. It is not enough for her to be strong. She must also be great."
    new "Ritual suicide is a warrior's death. But a queen is called to be more than just a warrior. She is a leader. It is not enough for her to be strong. She must also be great.\n仪式性的自尽是一个战士的死法。但女王被召唤，不只是要做一名战士。她是一位领袖。仅仅强大对她来说是不够的。她还必须伟大。"

    old "Sounds like a weighty responsibility."
    new "Sounds like a weighty responsibility.\n听起来责任沉重。"

    old "The princess understands the burden she shoulders, and she does not flinch in the face of challenge."
    new "The princess understands the burden she shoulders, and she does not flinch in the face of challenge.\n公主明白自己肩负的重担，面对挑战时，她毫不退缩。"

    old "I meant that must be a big responsibility for you. If a princess fails to pass muster, it must reflect poorly on her trainer."
    new "I meant that must be a big responsibility for you. If a princess fails to pass muster, it must reflect poorly on her trainer.\n我是指，那对你来说想必也是沉重的责任。如果一位公主未能达标，对她的教官来说肯定脸上无光。"

    old "I am the captain of the royal guard. If I'm to share in the prestige of the matriarchy, I must also be willing to accept the responsibility that comes with it. Teaching the princess is but one of many duties that I see to."
    new "I am the captain of the royal guard. If I'm to share in the prestige of the matriarchy, I must also be willing to accept the responsibility that comes with it. Teaching the princess is but one of many duties that I see to.\n我是王室卫队的队长。若我要分享母系氏族的荣光，就必须甘愿承担随之而来的责任。教导公主只是我照料的诸多职责之一。"

    old "So, Leena. Captain of the royal guard. How did you attain that title?"
    new "So, Leena. Captain of the royal guard. How did you attain that title?\n那么，Leena。王室卫队队长。你是如何得到这个头衔的？"

    old "I was deemed the best woman for the job."
    new "I was deemed the best woman for the job.\n我被认定是这一职位的最佳人选。"

    old "Sounds meritocratic."
    new "Sounds meritocratic.\n听起来是任人唯贤。"

    old "How else would you do it? Appoint someone who's not the best person for the position?"
    new "How else would you do it? Appoint someone who's not the best person for the position?\n不然还能怎么做？任命一个并非此位最佳人选的人吗？"

    old "Well, I think that's always what we'd like to do. Have the person who's best for the job, I mean. But sometimes, the question of who is the best isn't always an easy one to answer."
    new "Well, I think that's always what we'd like to do. Have the person who's best for the job, I mean. But sometimes, the question of who is the best isn't always an easy one to answer.\n嗯，我想那始终是我们想做的事。我是说，让最胜任的人来做。但有时，谁才是最胜任的这个问题，并不总是那么容易回答。"

    old "We have combat trials that do a fine job of answering that question for us. Of course, combat trials are anything but easy."
    new "We have combat trials that do a fine job of answering that question for us. Of course, combat trials are anything but easy.\n我们有比武试炼，能很好地替我们回答这个问题。当然，比武试炼可绝不轻松。"

    old "But combat trials only test your combat readiness. What about leadership qualities? How do you pick the best leader?"
    new "But combat trials only test your combat readiness. What about leadership qualities? How do you pick the best leader?\n但比武试炼只能检验你的战斗能力。领导才能呢？你们如何选出最优秀的领袖？"

    old "Those strongest in combat are strongest in all challenges they face. That is the way of the Amazon."
    new "Those strongest in combat are strongest in all challenges they face. That is the way of the Amazon.\n战斗中最强的人，面对一切挑战时也最强。这就是Amazon之道。"

    old "How do you justify that notion? Somebody surviving a combat trial only tells you how good someone is at killing."
    new "How do you justify that notion? Somebody surviving a combat trial only tells you how good someone is at killing.\n这个说法你怎么解释？一个人能在比武试炼中活下来，只能说明他有多擅长杀戮。"

    old "If you truly believe that a warrior's only strength is fighting, then you are truly a fool. But you are a man, so I'll muster all the patience I can and try to explain this very basic concept to you."
    new "If you truly believe that a warrior's only strength is fighting, then you are truly a fool. But you are a man, so I'll muster all the patience I can and try to explain this very basic concept to you.\n如果你真以为一个战士的力量只有战斗，那你可真是个蠢货。不过你是个男人，所以我会尽我所能拿出耐心，试着把这么基础的概念讲给你听。"

    old "You're wrong. But you have a pretty face, and I know that outside of the Amazon domain, girls with pretty faces aren't always held the highest standard of reasoning. So I'll explain it to you, and maybe when you go to sleep tonight you can do so feeling a bit smarter than when you woke up."
    new "You're wrong. But you have a pretty face, and I know that outside of the Amazon domain, girls with pretty faces aren't always held the highest standard of reasoning. So I'll explain it to you, and maybe when you go to sleep tonight you can do so feeling a bit smarter than when you woke up.\n你错了。不过你生得一张漂亮脸蛋，而我知道在Amazon领地之外，漂亮脸蛋的姑娘并不总被以最高的才智标准来要求。所以我就讲给你听，也许今晚入睡时，你会觉得自己比早上醒来时聪明了一点。"

    old "Have you ever seen a grand musical ensemble? They're quite popular among dwarves and humans of the upper echelons."
    new "Have you ever seen a grand musical ensemble? They're quite popular among dwarves and humans of the upper echelons.\n你见过大型音乐合奏吗？在上层社会的矮人和人类中，那相当流行。"

    old "I've seen musical ensembles many times, but I've seen a grand ensemble on only one occasion."
    new "I've seen musical ensembles many times, but I've seen a grand ensemble on only one occasion.\n音乐合奏我看过很多次，但大型合奏我只见过一回。"

    old "But you are familiar with the concept, yes? A single musical composer conceives in his mind a musical symphony, and through some form of notation, he creates a score which is distributed to a large group of musicians, who then rehearse the piece and perform it in tandem under his guidance."
    new "But you are familiar with the concept, yes? A single musical composer conceives in his mind a musical symphony, and through some form of notation, he creates a score which is distributed to a large group of musicians, who then rehearse the piece and perform it in tandem under his guidance.\n但你熟悉这个概念，对吧？一位作曲家在他脑海中构思出一部交响乐，再通过某种记谱方式写成乐谱，分发给一大批乐手，乐手们随后排练，并在他指导下协同演奏。"

    old "Yes, of course."
    new "Yes, of course.\n当然熟悉。"

    old "Now, you said that you saw a live performance. Which of those performing was the most skilled of the musicians?"
    new "Now, you said that you saw a live performance. Which of those performing was the most skilled of the musicians?\n那么，你说你看过现场演出。那些演奏者中，谁是最有造诣的乐手？"

    old "It would have to be the lead flutist. The flutist is the one who carries the melody, the most memorable part of the performance."
    new "It would have to be the lead flutist. The flutist is the one who carries the melody, the most memorable part of the performance.\n那必定是首席长笛手。长笛手承载着旋律，那是演出中最令人难忘的部分。"

    old "Wrong."
    new "Wrong.\n错。"

    old "A memorable performance is not always a skilled performance. Some of the most memorable experiences are those which are characterized by shocking incompetence."
    new "A memorable performance is not always a skilled performance. Some of the most memorable experiences are those which are characterized by shocking incompetence.\n令人难忘的演出未必是技艺精湛的演出。有些最令人难忘的经历，恰恰是以惊人的拙劣著称。"

    old "The trumpeter is the loudest in the ensemble. If there is any imperfection in his playing, the audience will quickly recognize it. The trumpeter is held to the highest standard of excellence, and thus he must be the most skilled of those on stage."
    new "The trumpeter is the loudest in the ensemble. If there is any imperfection in his playing, the audience will quickly recognize it. The trumpeter is held to the highest standard of excellence, and thus he must be the most skilled of those on stage.\n小号手在合奏中声音最响。他的演奏若有任何瑕疵，听众立刻就能察觉。小号手被以最高的卓越标准来要求，因此他必定是台上技艺最高超的人。"

    old "An interesting thought, but an incorrect one. Imperfections in trumpet play may be the most audible, but they won't stymie a performance the same way an incorrect drum beat might."
    new "An interesting thought, but an incorrect one. Imperfections in trumpet play may be the most audible, but they won't stymie a performance the same way an incorrect drum beat might.\n想法有趣，但并不正确。小号演奏的瑕疵或许最为响亮，但它对演出的破坏，远不及一个错误的鼓点。"

    old "The bass drummer plays a subtle role, and audiences may sometimes forget the drummer exists. But without him, the other musicians have no way to keep time. The drummer provides the beat. He, in effect, leads the other musicians. He must be the most skilled among them."
    new "The bass drummer plays a subtle role, and audiences may sometimes forget the drummer exists. But without him, the other musicians have no way to keep time. The drummer provides the beat. He, in effect, leads the other musicians. He must be the most skilled among them.\n低音鼓手扮演着不起眼的角色，听众有时甚至忘了还有鼓手。但没有他，其他乐手就无法掌握节拍。鼓手提供节奏。实际上，是他引领着其他乐手。他必定是其中技艺最高超的人。"

    old "Your line of thinking is correct. The one who leads the musicians, who directs them and tells them how to play, is indeed the most skilled among them. But that person is not the drummer."
    new "Your line of thinking is correct. The one who leads the musicians, who directs them and tells them how to play, is indeed the most skilled among them. But that person is not the drummer.\n你的思路对了。引领乐手、指挥他们、告诉他们如何演奏的人，确实是其中技艺最高超的。但那个人不是鼓手。"

    old "I think it would have to be the composer, who conducted the musicians."
    new "I think it would have to be the composer, who conducted the musicians.\n我想那必定是作曲家，是他指挥了乐手们。"

    old "Now, why would you say that? Many people performed, many of them wielding various instruments, yet you decided that the man who held no instrument was the most skilled musician among them. How is that?"
    new "Now, why would you say that? Many people performed, many of them wielding various instruments, yet you decided that the man who held no instrument was the most skilled musician among them. How is that?\n那么，你为何这么说？许多人参与演奏，其中许多人手持各式乐器，可你却断定那个手中没有乐器的人才是其中技艺最高的乐手。这是为什么？"

    old "Well, in order to direct the wind players on flute and piccolo, the composer must have a full understanding of the capability of those instruments. The same is true of every other instrument on stage."
    new "Well, in order to direct the wind players on flute and piccolo, the composer must have a full understanding of the capability of those instruments. The same is true of every other instrument on stage.\n嗯，为了指挥长笛和短笛的管乐手，作曲家必须对这些乐器的性能了然于胸。台上的其他乐器也是如此。"

    old "The composer must know not just one instrument, but all of them."
    new "The composer must know not just one instrument, but all of them.\n作曲家必须通晓的不只是一种乐器，而是全部。"

    old "What do you suppose might happen if the composer were to take up one of the instruments in the symphony? Do you image that his playing would be worse than a specialized musician?"
    new "What do you suppose might happen if the composer were to take up one of the instruments in the symphony? Do you image that his playing would be worse than a specialized musician?\n如果作曲家拿起交响乐中的某件乐器，你觉得会怎样？你以为他的演奏会比专业乐手逊色吗？"

    old "Actually, he'd probably be better. On a broad level, the composer understands how each instrument's part harmonizes with all the rest. Understand the whole, and you can better refine each individual part."
    new "Actually, he'd probably be better. On a broad level, the composer understands how each instrument's part harmonizes with all the rest. Understand the whole, and you can better refine each individual part.\n实际上，他或许会更出色。从宏观上看，作曲家懂得每件乐器的声部如何与其余声部彼此和谐。理解了整体，你才能更好地打磨每一个单独的声部。"

    old "To be the world's greatest ensemble flute player requires the mind of a composer. And to be the world's greatest warrior requires the mind of a leader."
    new "To be the world's greatest ensemble flute player requires the mind of a composer. And to be the world's greatest warrior requires the mind of a leader.\n要成为世上最伟大的合奏长笛手，需要作曲家的头脑；而要成为世上最伟大的战士，则需要领袖的头脑。"

    old "Yes."
    new "Yes.\n没错。"

    old "You may need to broaden your line of thinking. I've asked you about the most skilled of the musicians, and you've described the performance in terms of what you can hear. But there's another person involved in the performance, making no noise at all."
    new "You may need to broaden your line of thinking. I've asked you about the most skilled of the musicians, and you've described the performance in terms of what you can hear. But there's another person involved in the performance, making no noise at all.\n你也许需要放宽思路。我问你谁是最有造诣的乐手，你却只凭听见的来描述这场演出。但演出里还有另一个人，全程没有发出半点声响。"

    old "The one who composed and conducted the symphony."
    new "The one who composed and conducted the symphony.\n那个作曲并指挥交响乐的人。"

    old "Exactly. When composing the piece, he must have a full understanding of the capability of each instrument that appears on stage."
    new "Exactly. When composing the piece, he must have a full understanding of the capability of each instrument that appears on stage.\n正是。在谱写这部作品时，他必须对台上出现的每件乐器的性能了然于胸。"

    old "Moreover, it is the composer's role to test and know the absolute limits of each instrument. A conductor may use only a fraction of a flute's pitch range, but he knows the full extent of it, and that is something learned through practice and experience."
    new "Moreover, it is the composer's role to test and know the absolute limits of each instrument. A conductor may use only a fraction of a flute's pitch range, but he knows the full extent of it, and that is something learned through practice and experience.\n而且，检验并掌握每件乐器的极限，正是作曲家的职责。指挥家或许只用到长笛音域的一小部分，但他知晓其全部范围，那是靠练习和经验才能习得的。"

    old "But the composer's talents do not end there. It is one thing to master the flute or drum independently. It is quite another to understand each of them well enough to fully understand how the two can be combined and interwoven to produce a symphony."
    new "But the composer's talents do not end there. It is one thing to master the flute or drum independently. It is quite another to understand each of them well enough to fully understand how the two can be combined and interwoven to produce a symphony.\n但作曲家的才华不止于此。单独精通长笛或鼓是一回事；能把它们各自都理解得足够透彻，从而完全明白二者如何交融交织、谱成一部交响乐，则完全是另一回事。"

    old "In a musical symphony, the one with the greatest musical prowess never touches an instrument for the duration of the performance. And yet in his lifetime, he has spent far more time with those instruments than any one of the performers."
    new "In a musical symphony, the one with the greatest musical prowess never touches an instrument for the duration of the performance. And yet in his lifetime, he has spent far more time with those instruments than any one of the performers.\n在一部交响乐中，音乐造诣最高的人在整个演出期间从不触碰乐器。然而终其一生，他与那些乐器相处的时间，远比任何一位演奏者都长。"

    old "Being a great warrior is about more than knowing how best to swing a sword. Being a great warrior requires practice, dedication, discipline."
    new "Being a great warrior is about more than knowing how best to swing a sword. Being a great warrior requires practice, dedication, discipline.\n成为一名伟大的战士，不只是懂得如何挥剑挥得最好。它需要苦练、专注与自律。"

    old "A great warrior can look a foe in the eyes and understand their disposition, their confidence, and their level of competence. A true warrior has presence, and can strike fear into the hearts of her foes with a roar, or lull them into a false sense of security by faking a vulnerability."
    new "A great warrior can look a foe in the eyes and understand their disposition, their confidence, and their level of competence. A true warrior has presence, and can strike fear into the hearts of her foes with a roar, or lull them into a false sense of security by faking a vulnerability.\n伟大的战士能与敌人四目相对，洞悉对方的性情、信心与身手。真正的战士自带气场，她能以一声怒吼让敌人胆寒，也能佯装破绽，让敌人陷入虚假的安心。"

    old "A great warrior knows when to strike and when to feint, when to advance and when to retreat, when to act and when to be reactive. A great warrior possesses not only deftness of hand and foot, but also charisma, wisdom, and strength of will."
    new "A great warrior knows when to strike and when to feint, when to advance and when to retreat, when to act and when to be reactive. A great warrior possesses not only deftness of hand and foot, but also charisma, wisdom, and strength of will.\n伟大的战士知道何时出击、何时佯攻，何时前进、何时后撤，何时主动、何时应变。伟大的战士不仅手脚灵巧，还拥有魅力、智慧与意志的力量。"

    old "Those sound like exactly the attributes of a great leader."
    new "Those sound like exactly the attributes of a great leader.\n这些听上去正是伟大领袖的品格。"

    old "You learn quickly, [protag]. Perhaps I was wrong to dismiss you as nothing more than just a pretty face."
    new "You learn quickly, [protag]. Perhaps I was wrong to dismiss you as nothing more than just a pretty face.\n你学得很快，[protag]。也许我当初不该把你只当成一张漂亮脸蛋来打发。"

    old "You learn quickly, [protag]. Perhaps you're not quite so dumb as you look."
    new "You learn quickly, [protag]. Perhaps you're not quite so dumb as you look.\n你学得很快，[protag]。也许你没看起来那么笨。"

    old "Is that your attempt at flattery?"
    new "Is that your attempt at flattery?\n这就是你奉承人的方式吗？"

    old "I meant it neither as applause or slight. You merely surprised me."
    new "I meant it neither as applause or slight. You merely surprised me.\n我这话既非夸奖也非轻慢。你只是让我吃了一惊。"

    old "Well, I never expected an Amazon warrior to lecture me on the theory of symphonic musical performance. I wonder, Leena. What kind of warrior are you, exactly?"
    new "Well, I never expected an Amazon warrior to lecture me on the theory of symphonic musical performance. I wonder, Leena. What kind of warrior are you, exactly?\n嗯，我从未想过会有一位Amazon战士给我上交响乐演奏理论课。我很好奇，Leena。你究竟是什么样的战士？"

    old "Leena smirks."
    new "Leena smirks.\nLeena冷笑了一下。"

    old "You don't get to be captain of the Queen's royal guard without being in some way exceptional. My talents extend beyond my prowess in combat, and I'm hardly the only of my kind to be skilled in multiple disciplines. Keep your eyes open, and you just might find that we Amazons are full of surprises."
    new "You don't get to be captain of the Queen's royal guard without being in some way exceptional. My talents extend beyond my prowess in combat, and I'm hardly the only of my kind to be skilled in multiple disciplines. Keep your eyes open, and you just might find that we Amazons are full of surprises.\n若非在某些方面出类拔萃，是当不上女王王室卫队队长的。我的才能不只在战场上的骁勇，而且像我这样精通多门技艺的人，在我族中并不少见。睁大眼睛，你会发现我们Amazons处处都是惊喜。"

    old "We've arrived. Let's go meet the queen now."
    new "We've arrived. Let's go meet the queen now.\n我们到了。现在去见女王吧。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. You took your time getting here."
    new "Ah, [protag]. You took your time getting here.\n啊，[protag]。你可真是一路慢悠悠的。"

    old "Well, I did have to walk."
    new "Well, I did have to walk.\n呃，我毕竟得靠两条腿走过来。"

    old "Ha. I suppose I do have you at a disadvantage, being that you don't have wings."
    new "Ha. I suppose I do have you at a disadvantage, being that you don't have wings.\n哈。我猜我确实占了你的便宜，毕竟你没有翅膀。"

    old "Well, you don't have wings, either. At least, not that I can see. You have to borrow them."
    new "Well, you don't have wings, either. At least, not that I can see. You have to borrow them.\n可你也没有翅膀啊。至少我看不到。你的翅膀还得借。"

    old "Karen raises her hand to her mouth and stifles a laugh."
    new "Karen raises her hand to her mouth and stifles a laugh.\nKaren抬手掩住嘴，忍住笑。"

    old "You know, [protag], I'm glad that you've managed to catch me in a better mood than the last time we met. I apologize for any prior rudeness. Being forced to share company with humans always puts foulness in my temper."
    new "You know, [protag], I'm glad that you've managed to catch me in a better mood than the last time we met. I apologize for any prior rudeness. Being forced to share company with humans always puts foulness in my temper.\n你知道，[protag]，我很高兴这次见面，我的心情比上次好。我为先前的无礼道歉。被迫与人类作伴，总让我的脾气变得很糟。"

    old "No offense."
    new "No offense.\n无意冒犯。"

    old "None taken."
    new "None taken.\n我没往心里去。"

    old "If your skills as an errand-runner as good as your sense of humor, I believe that you and I will get along famously."
    new "If your skills as an errand-runner as good as your sense of humor, I believe that you and I will get along famously.\n如果你的跑腿功夫和你的幽默感一样好，我相信我们会相处得极好。"

    old "Am I just an errand-runner?"
    new "Am I just an errand-runner?\n我只是个跑腿的吗？"

    old "You're an emissary of the council of Grimoire. Your job is to ingratiate yourself to various people who can assist in furthering the interests of the human empire. That involves doing a lot of favors for people. So yes, I'd say you're an errand-runner."
    new "You're an emissary of the council of Grimoire. Your job is to ingratiate yourself to various people who can assist in furthering the interests of the human empire. That involves doing a lot of favors for people. So yes, I'd say you're an errand-runner.\n你是Grimoire议会的使者。你的差事，是去讨各种能协助推进人类帝国利益的人欢心。那得帮人办很多事。所以是的，我会说你就是个跑腿的。"

    old "Of course, I'll do what I can to support you. Our goals are shared, after all, though the humans are in a great deal more immediate peril than the denizens of my domain."
    new "Of course, I'll do what I can to support you. Our goals are shared, after all, though the humans are in a great deal more immediate peril than the denizens of my domain.\n当然，我会尽力支持你。毕竟我们的目标一致，只不过人类眼下所面临的危险，比我这领地里的子民要迫切得多。"

    old "To that end, I'd like to have one of my best accompany you. You've had a chance to meet Leena, I hope."
    new "To that end, I'd like to have one of my best accompany you. You've had a chance to meet Leena, I hope.\n为此，我想让我麾下最出色的战士之一随你同行。希望你已经见过Leena了。"

    old "She escorted me here, per your instructions, I presume. We exchanged a few words en route."
    new "She escorted me here, per your instructions, I presume. We exchanged a few words en route.\n我猜她是奉你的指示护送我来此的。路上我们聊了几句。"

    old "Well, you're assembling a task force, and that means you need fighters. Leena is one of the best."
    new "Well, you're assembling a task force, and that means you need fighters. Leena is one of the best.\n嗯，你在组建一支特遣队，那就需要战士。Leena是最出色的之一。"

    old "My queen, I serve at your pleasure. However..."
    new "My queen, I serve at your pleasure. However...\n女王陛下，我愿听候您的差遣。不过……"

    old "Don't misunderstand, Leena. I don't mean for you to accompany [protag] on [hisher] diplomatic exploits. Those are tasks for [himher] and [himher] alone. You're still captain of the guard. You have responsibilities here in the citadel."
    new "Don't misunderstand, Leena. I don't mean for you to accompany [protag] on [hisher] diplomatic exploits. Those are tasks for [himher] and [himher] alone. You're still captain of the guard. You have responsibilities here in the citadel.\n别误会，Leena。我不是要你陪[protag]去进行[hisher]的外交活动。那些事得由[himher]独自去做。你仍是卫队队长。你要塞里还有职责在身。"

    old "However, when the time comes, [protag] will need the company of fighters to invade N'Mar under cover of darkness. At that time, you will be available to assist [himher]."
    new "However, when the time comes, [protag] will need the company of fighters to invade N'Mar under cover of darkness. At that time, you will be available to assist [himher].\n不过，时机到来时，[protag]将需要战士随行，趁着夜色入侵N'Mar。届时，你要随时准备协助[himher]。"

    old "So, until that time, I'm to serve in my capacity as captain of the guard?"
    new "So, until that time, I'm to serve in my capacity as captain of the guard?\n那么，在那之前，我就以卫队队长的身份尽职？"

    old "Yes. Your normal duties will be uninterrupted."
    new "Yes. Your normal duties will be uninterrupted.\n是的。你的日常职责不会中断。"

    old "That being said, I do hope that you find time to spend with [protag] before your big mission. If you're to properly assist each other in combat, you'll need to learn to trust each other. Leena, make yourself available to [protag]. Of course, this is solely at [protag]'s discretion."
    new "That being said, I do hope that you find time to spend with [protag] before your big mission. If you're to properly assist each other in combat, you'll need to learn to trust each other. Leena, make yourself available to [protag]. Of course, this is solely at [protag]'s discretion.\n话虽如此，我确实希望你们在大任务之前，能抽出时间和[protag]相处。若要在战斗中彼此配合得当，你们就得学会互相信任。Leena，你要随时听候[protag]的差遣。当然，这完全由[protag]自行决定。"

    old "I agree. We should find some time for combat training."
    new "I agree. We should find some time for combat training.\n我同意。我们应该抽点时间进行战斗训练。"

    old "Train together, yes. That is certainly time well-spent. But please, [protag], I hope you'll take the time to get to personally know Leena. Sometimes, getting to know someone as a person can be the fastest way to forge a bond of trust. And having that bond of trust can be critical when locked in battle."
    new "Train together, yes. That is certainly time well-spent. But please, [protag], I hope you'll take the time to get to personally know Leena. Sometimes, getting to know someone as a person can be the fastest way to forge a bond of trust. And having that bond of trust can be critical when locked in battle.\n一起训练，没错，那当然是值得花的时间。不过，[protag]，我希望你能花时间真正去了解Leena这个人。有时，把一个人作为人来了解，是铸就信任纽带最快的途径。而在激战中，这条信任纽带可能至关重要。"

    old "You'll be recruiting many allies. Learn to trust them, not only as combatants, but as people."
    new "You'll be recruiting many allies. Learn to trust them, not only as combatants, but as people.\n你还会招募许多盟友。学会信任他们，不仅把他们当作战士，也当作人。"

    old "You can come to the citadel any time you wish to speak to Leena. I'll be certain that she has time for you."
    new "You can come to the citadel any time you wish to speak to Leena. I'll be certain that she has time for you.\n你想和Leena谈话，随时可以来要塞。我会确保她有空见你。"

    old "I'll also be available. If you need any suggestions or tips on where to locate potential allies, I can offer you some potential leads."
    new "I'll also be available. If you need any suggestions or tips on where to locate potential allies, I can offer you some potential leads.\n我也会随时候命。如果你需要关于在哪里寻找潜在盟友的建议或提示，我可以给你一些线索。"

    old "I may have to take you up on that offer at some point."
    new "I may have to take you up on that offer at some point.\n我可能总得在某个时候接受你的提议。"

    old "Hello, [protag]. What business brings you here today?"
    new "Hello, [protag]. What business brings you here today?\n你好，[protag]。今天是什么风把你吹来了？"

    old "I'm in search of new allies, and you said you have leads."
    new "I'm in search of new allies, and you said you have leads.\n我在寻找新的盟友，你说过你有线索。"

    old "Indeed I do. What kind of ally are you looking for, exactly?"
    new "Indeed I do. What kind of ally are you looking for, exactly?\n我确实有。你到底想找什么样的盟友？"

    old "I'm looking for..."
    new "I'm looking for...\n我想找……"

    old "I'm looking for someone sneaky and devious."
    new "I'm looking for someone sneaky and devious.\n我想找个狡猾又阴险的人。"

    old "Sneaky and devious, eh? You're aware that you're looking for potential allies here, not enemies, right?"
    new "Sneaky and devious, eh? You're aware that you're looking for potential allies here, not enemies, right?\n狡猾又阴险，嗯？你知道你在这里找的是潜在盟友，不是敌人，对吧？"

    old "Cunning and deceit can be useful tools. I'd be remiss if I excluded someone from the ranks of my task force simply because they had an unsavory past."
    new "Cunning and deceit can be useful tools. I'd be remiss if I excluded someone from the ranks of my task force simply because they had an unsavory past.\n诡计与欺骗可以是有用的工具。若只因某人过去不太光彩就把他排除在特遣队之外，那就是我的失职了。"

    old "I thought you wanted the best."
    new "I thought you wanted the best.\n我以为你想要最优秀的。"

    old "I do. And it's hard to be the best without being a little bit crafty. Infamy and talent sometimes go hand in hand."
    new "I do. And it's hard to be the best without being a little bit crafty. Infamy and talent sometimes go hand in hand.\n我是想要最优秀的。而要成为最优秀的人，很难不稍微耍点手腕。恶名与才华有时是相伴而生的。"

    old "So, you want someone crafty and infamous. I wonder, would you be willing to join forces with an assassin?"
    new "So, you want someone crafty and infamous. I wonder, would you be willing to join forces with an assassin?\n那么，你想要个既会耍手腕又声名狼藉的人。我想知道，你愿意和一名刺客联手吗？"

    old "I'm certainly not above it."
    new "I'm certainly not above it.\n我绝没有不愿意。"

    old "Alright. Far be it from me to discourage you from doing what's best for the mission. Tell me, are you familiar with the Great Forest?"
    new "Alright. Far be it from me to discourage you from doing what's best for the mission. Tell me, are you familiar with the Great Forest?\n好吧。我岂能劝阻你去做对任务最有利的事。告诉我，你熟悉Great Forest吗？"

    old "I'm an elf. What do you think?"
    new "I'm an elf. What do you think?\n我是精灵。你觉得呢？"

    old "I would assume yes, but I didn't want to assume."
    new "I would assume yes, but I didn't want to assume.\n我本想说熟悉，但我不想妄加揣测。"

    old "I know it well enough."
    new "I know it well enough.\n我熟悉得很。"

    old "There's an elf assassin who goes by the name of Kusho. Charming fellow, good with a bow. Has something of a code of honor, he's the kind to turn down a job on moral grounds. That policy makes him a bit polarizing, as assassins go."
    new "There's an elf assassin who goes by the name of Kusho. Charming fellow, good with a bow. Has something of a code of honor, he's the kind to turn down a job on moral grounds. That policy makes him a bit polarizing, as assassins go.\n有个精灵刺客，人称Kusho。是个迷人的家伙，弓术了得。他有那么一套荣誉准则，是会出于道义拒绝接活的那种人。就刺客而言，这一套让他显得有些两极分化。"

    old "Kusho's usually the sort to leave a calling card when finishing a job. A corrupt nobleman here, a wanted criminal there, he'll leave a way for people to get in touch if they admire his work. And besides that, he likes the recognition. He has a bit of an ego."
    new "Kusho's usually the sort to leave a calling card when finishing a job. A corrupt nobleman here, a wanted criminal there, he'll leave a way for people to get in touch if they admire his work. And besides that, he likes the recognition. He has a bit of an ego.\nKusho通常在完成一单活后会留下记号。这里一个腐败的贵族，那里一个被通缉的罪犯，他都会留下联络途径，供欣赏他手笔的人联系他。而且除此之外，他也喜欢这份名声。他有点自负。"

    old "If he's earned the right to brag, then he's someone I want by my side."
    new "If he's earned the right to brag, then he's someone I want by my side.\n如果他有资格吹嘘，那他正是我想留在身边的人。"

    old "Well, that may be a problem. Kusho has not been seen recently."
    new "Well, that may be a problem. Kusho has not been seen recently.\n嗯，那可能是个问题。Kusho最近都没人见过。"

    old "Has he gone into retirement?"
    new "Has he gone into retirement?\n他隐退了吗？"

    old "Who can say? For a long time I'd thought him dead, but rumors are that people have spotted him in some of the smaller settlements of the Great Forest. That, or someone who looks like him. If you want to find him, I'd recommend asking around the capital. You know how to get to GrandTree, I'm sure."
    new "Who can say? For a long time I'd thought him dead, but rumors are that people have spotted him in some of the smaller settlements of the Great Forest. That, or someone who looks like him. If you want to find him, I'd recommend asking around the capital. You know how to get to GrandTree, I'm sure.\n谁能说得准呢？很长一段时间里我都以为他死了，但有传言说，有人在大森林的一些小聚落里见过他。要么就是个长得像他的人。如果你想找他，我建议去首都附近打听打听。你肯定知道怎么去GrandTree。"

    old "Sure I do. I'll make GrandTree one of my next destinations, and see if I can find anything about this Kusho fellow. Thanks for the tip, Karen."
    new "Sure I do. I'll make GrandTree one of my next destinations, and see if I can find anything about this Kusho fellow. Thanks for the tip, Karen.\n我当然知道。我会把GrandTree作为接下来的目的地之一，看看能不能打听到这位Kusho的消息。谢谢你的线索，Karen。"

    old "Any time."
    new "Any time.\n随时奉陪。"

    old "I'm looking for someone tenacious and steadfast."
    new "I'm looking for someone tenacious and steadfast.\n我想找个坚韧又坚定的人。"

    old "Tenacious and steadfast. I do believe you've just described a dwarf."
    new "Tenacious and steadfast. I do believe you've just described a dwarf.\n坚韧又坚定。我相信你描述的正是矮人。"

    old "Any particular dwarf you had in mind?"
    new "Any particular dwarf you had in mind?\n你心里有具体哪位矮人吗？"

    old "Unfortunately not. My suggestion would be that you head to Hammerhands and ask around. See what you can dig up. Someone with your natural charisma will get far more information from direct inquiry than I could hope to discover from the various reports that make their way to me."
    new "Unfortunately not. My suggestion would be that you head to Hammerhands and ask around. See what you can dig up. Someone with your natural charisma will get far more information from direct inquiry than I could hope to discover from the various reports that make their way to me.\n很遗憾没有。我建议你去Hammerhands四处打听一下。看看能挖出什么来。凭你天生的魅力，直接打听能获得的信息，会比我从送到我手上的各种报告里挖到的多得多。"

    old "Besides, you're a dwarf. You should already know more about this than me."
    new "Besides, you're a dwarf. You should already know more about this than me.\n再说了，你是矮人。这些事你应该比我更清楚。"

    old "That may be the case, but I'd still appreciate your perspective."
    new "That may be the case, but I'd still appreciate your perspective.\n也许是吧，但我还是想听听你的看法。"

    old "Where exactly in Hammerhands ought I begin looking? Do you have connections with any noble houses I might make contact with?"
    new "Where exactly in Hammerhands ought I begin looking? Do you have connections with any noble houses I might make contact with?\n在Hammerhands，我具体该从哪里开始找？你认识哪些贵族世家，能让我搭上关系吗？"

    old "The best connections that you'll find in Hammerhands are out on the street. Don't trust a noble to tell you what the common men already know. Go do where the workers loosen their tongues."
    new "The best connections that you'll find in Hammerhands are out on the street. Don't trust a noble to tell you what the common men already know. Go do where the workers loosen their tongues.\n你在Hammerhands能找到的最好的门路就在街上。别指望贵族告诉你平民早就知道的事。去那些工人们酒后吐真言的地方。"

    old "A pub, then."
    new "A pub, then.\n那就是酒馆了。"

    old "Sitting and pubs and listening for rumors isn't normally the kind of fact-finding I would encourage. But when it comes to the dwarven lands..."
    new "Sitting and pubs and listening for rumors isn't normally the kind of fact-finding I would encourage. But when it comes to the dwarven lands...\n坐在酒馆里听人嚼舌根，通常不是我鼓励的那种调查方式。不过说到矮人的地盘嘛……"

    old "Point taken. I'll head off to Hammerhands and see what I can find out."
    new "Point taken. I'll head off to Hammerhands and see what I can find out.\n明白。我这就去Hammerhands，看看能查出什么。"

    old "Keep an open ear. Make friends. Help can sometimes come from where you least expect it."
    new "Keep an open ear. Make friends. Help can sometimes come from where you least expect it.\n竖起耳朵。多交朋友。帮助有时会来自你最意想不到的地方。"

    old "Are you speaking from experience?"
    new "Are you speaking from experience?\n你这是在谈自己的经验吗？"

    old "Maybe I'll be ready to answer that question some day. Anyway, you've got business to do."
    new "Maybe I'll be ready to answer that question some day. Anyway, you've got business to do.\n也许总有一天我会回答这个问题。总之，你还有正事要办。"

    old "Indeed. I guess I have some leg work to do."
    new "Indeed. I guess I have some leg work to do.\n确实。我想我还有不少跑腿的活要干。"

    old "I'm looking for someone brave and adventurous."
    new "I'm looking for someone brave and adventurous.\n我想找个勇敢又有冒险精神的人。"

    old "Brave and adventurous, eh? You know, word came to me about a group of treasure hunters from Grimoire who decided that they wanted to make the lost artifacts of the Chzulu ruins their own."
    new "Brave and adventurous, eh? You know, word came to me about a group of treasure hunters from Grimoire who decided that they wanted to make the lost artifacts of the Chzulu ruins their own.\n勇敢又有冒险精神，嗯？你知道，我听说Grimoire有一伙寻宝者，他们打定主意要把Chzulu废墟里遗失的神器据为己有。"

    old "The Chzulu ruins? Down in the Unforgiving Swamps?"
    new "The Chzulu ruins? Down in the Unforgiving Swamps?\nChzulu废墟？就在Unforgiving Swamps那里？"

    old "The same."
    new "The same.\n正是。"

    old "That's mighty treacherous adventuring indeed. They must be a courageous band of treasure hunters."
    new "That's mighty treacherous adventuring indeed. They must be a courageous band of treasure hunters.\n那确实是九死一生的冒险。他们一定是一群勇敢的寻宝者。"

    old "No, they were foolhardy treasure hunters who got wise partway through their trip. Somehow, they managed to penetrate one of the ruins' innermost catacombs, but on their way out, they ran into lizardmen."
    new "No, they were foolhardy treasure hunters who got wise partway through their trip. Somehow, they managed to penetrate one of the ruins' innermost catacombs, but on their way out, they ran into lizardmen.\n不，他们是一群莽撞的寻宝者，走到半路才变得聪明起来。不知怎的，他们设法钻进了废墟最深处的地窖之一，但出来的时候撞上了蜥蜴人。"

    old "And they were killed?"
    new "And they were killed?\n然后他们被杀了？"

    old "No, they fled and lived to tell the tale. That's how I'm able to tell you this part of the story. 'Killed by lizardmen' is a bit specific of a description of their fate. Had they actually fallen victim to the beasts, the story would end with something like 'and they were never heard from ever again.'"
    new "No, they fled and lived to tell the tale. That's how I'm able to tell you this part of the story. 'Killed by lizardmen' is a bit specific of a description of their fate. Had they actually fallen victim to the beasts, the story would end with something like 'and they were never heard from ever again.'\n不，他们逃了出来，活下来讲述了这段经历。所以我才能告诉你故事的这部分。要是他们真沦为那些野兽的猎物，故事就会以“从此再无音讯”之类的句子收尾了。"

    old "The point is, they got some treasure part of the way out. Three bags, filled with whatever they were able to loot. Now, these would-be adventurers have been known to exaggerate, but I know those ruins, and even the slightest of artifacts must be quite a boon."
    new "The point is, they got some treasure part of the way out. Three bags, filled with whatever they were able to loot. Now, these would-be adventurers have been known to exaggerate, but I know those ruins, and even the slightest of artifacts must be quite a boon.\n关键是，他们出来时带出了些财宝。三个袋子，装满了他们能搜刮到的东西。这些所谓的冒险家素来喜欢夸大其词，但我知道那些废墟，哪怕是最不起眼的神器，也肯定价值不菲。"

    old "Why are you telling me this?"
    new "Why are you telling me this?\n你为什么要告诉我这些？"

    old "I guess I'm not telling you what you asked for, am I? You came here asking if I knew anyone brave and adventurous to join you on your quest, and here I am telling you about a group of cowardly spelunkers."
    new "I guess I'm not telling you what you asked for, am I? You came here asking if I knew anyone brave and adventurous to join you on your quest, and here I am telling you about a group of cowardly spelunkers.\n我猜我没有在回答你的问题，对吧？你来问我认不认识勇敢又爱冒险、愿意加入你征途的人，我却给你讲了一群胆小的洞穴探险者的故事。"

    old "But maybe you could succeed where they failed."
    new "But maybe you could succeed where they failed.\n但也许在他们失败的地方，你能成功。"

    old "You think I should go treasure hunting?"
    new "You think I should go treasure hunting?\n你觉得我该去寻宝？"

    old "Why not? You're looking to beg and borrow favors wherever you can. Having the capital to buy a favor or two might not hurt."
    new "Why not? You're looking to beg and borrow favors wherever you can. Having the capital to buy a favor or two might not hurt.\n为什么不呢？你不正到处乞求、讨借人情吗？手头有资本能买下一两个人情，也无妨。"

    old "And who knows? You could encounter a fellow treasure hunter if you spend enough time near those ruins. You might just find the ally you're looking for."
    new "And who knows? You could encounter a fellow treasure hunter if you spend enough time near those ruins. You might just find the ally you're looking for.\n而且谁知道呢？你要是在那些废墟附近待得够久，说不定能遇到一位寻宝的同道。也许你就能找到你要找的盟友。"

    old "You really think that I might stumble upon someone there?"
    new "You really think that I might stumble upon someone there?\n你真觉得我可能在那边碰上什么人？"

    old "Karen laughs."
    new "Karen laughs.\nKaren笑了。"

    old "Of course not. Fear of lizardmen has made the place vacant of all but the most foolhardy adventurers, and the thing about foolhardy adventurers is that their foolhardiness as a tendency to get them less alive than you'd probably like to be. But it's a nice thought, isn't it?"
    new "Of course not. Fear of lizardmen has made the place vacant of all but the most foolhardy adventurers, and the thing about foolhardy adventurers is that their foolhardiness as a tendency to get them less alive than you'd probably like to be. But it's a nice thought, isn't it?\n当然不是。对蜥蜴人的恐惧让那里除了最莽撞的冒险者外空无一人，而莽撞冒险者的毛病就在于，他们的莽撞往往让他们活得没你希望的那样长。不过，这想法挺好，不是吗？"

    old "Anyway, if you'd like to go chasing after golden relics, you now know were to begin looking. You can get a bit richer, or die trying. Or maybe ignore that suggestion entirely. You have better things you could be doing, haven't you?"
    new "Anyway, if you'd like to go chasing after golden relics, you now know were to begin looking. You can get a bit richer, or die trying. Or maybe ignore that suggestion entirely. You have better things you could be doing, haven't you?\n总之，你要是想去追那些黄金遗物，现在知道该从哪里着手了。你可以小赚一笔，或者把命搭进去。又或者干脆无视这个建议。你还有更重要的事可以做，不是吗？"

    old "Maybe so. Exploring the swamp ought to be worth a good story or two, though."
    new "Maybe so. Exploring the swamp ought to be worth a good story or two, though.\n也许吧。不过探索那片沼泽，总该值得上一两个好故事。"

    old "Exactly! You know, the more that I think about it, the more I think it's a good idea. Go treasure hunting in the Unforgiving Swamp. What have you got to lose? Apart from your life, I mean."
    new "Exactly! You know, the more that I think about it, the more I think it's a good idea. Go treasure hunting in the Unforgiving Swamp. What have you got to lose? Apart from your life, I mean.\n没错！你知道，我想得越多，越觉得这是个好主意。去Unforgiving Swamp寻宝吧。你有什么可失去的？我是指，除了你的命。"

    old "Hey now. If there's one thing I've a talent for, it's surviving."
    new "Hey now. If there's one thing I've a talent for, it's surviving.\n嘿。要说有什么是我擅长的，那就是活命。"

    old "Well then, [protag]. Why don't you go survive the Unforgiving Swamps?"
    new "Well then, [protag]. Why don't you go survive the Unforgiving Swamps?\n那好，[protag]。你为什么不去Unforgiving Swamps闯一闯，活着回来？"

    old "Maybe I will, Karen. Maybe I will."
    new "Maybe I will, Karen. Maybe I will.\n也许我会的，Karen。也许我会的。"

    old "Queen Karen? You wanted to see me?"
    new "Queen Karen? You wanted to see me?\nKaren女王？你找我？"

    old "Oh it's you. Please come forward."
    new "Oh it's you. Please come forward.\n哦，是你啊。请上前来。"

    old "I've learned of something that I think will interest you, [protag]."
    new "I've learned of something that I think will interest you, [protag].\n我得知了一些事，我想你会感兴趣的，[protag]。"

    old "Something good?"
    new "Something good?\n是好事吗？"

    old "Quite the opposite, I'm afraid. Trouble in the desert."
    new "Quite the opposite, I'm afraid. Trouble in the desert.\n恐怕恰恰相反。沙漠里出事了。"

    old "What kind of trouble are we talking about?"
    new "What kind of trouble are we talking about?\n什么样的麻烦？"

    old "Rumors have been circulating that there's some kind of corruption stemming from the desert."
    new "Rumors have been circulating that there's some kind of corruption stemming from the desert.\n一直有传言说，沙漠里滋生出某种腐化。"

    old "Connected to the corruption spreading from Castle N'Mar, no doubt."
    new "Connected to the corruption spreading from Castle N'Mar, no doubt.\n想必与N'Mar城堡蔓延开来的腐化有关。"

    old "Actually, there is some doubt. The desert's dunes are home to more than a few notable landmarks."
    new "Actually, there is some doubt. The desert's dunes are home to more than a few notable landmarks.\n其实还有些存疑。沙漠的沙丘间，可不止几处知名的地标。"

    old "Landmarks, such as?"
    new "Landmarks, such as?\n地标，比如说？"

    old "The tomb of Urd is supposedly the resting place of a great warrior who was known for his dealings with the occult."
    new "The tomb of Urd is supposedly the resting place of a great warrior who was known for his dealings with the occult.\nUrd之墓据说是一位伟大战士的安息之地，他因与神秘法术打交道而闻名。"

    old "You said 'tomb' and 'resting place.' Is a dead man giving us trouble?"
    new "You said 'tomb' and 'resting place.' Is a dead man giving us trouble?\n你说了“墓”和“安息之地”。是个死人给我们惹麻烦吗？"

    old "It certainly wouldn't be the first time the dead had given you trouble, eh?"
    new "It certainly wouldn't be the first time the dead had given you trouble, eh?\n死人给你惹麻烦，这肯定不是头一回了，对吧？"

    old "Have you notified the council? This seems like the kind of thing that we should have more information about."
    new "Have you notified the council? This seems like the kind of thing that we should have more information about.\n你通知议会了吗？这种事似乎应该掌握更多信息才对。"

    old "As I said, rumors have been circulating. Evidently the council doesn't think that's justification enough to launch an investigation, especially when it's a matter so far from their borders."
    new "As I said, rumors have been circulating. Evidently the council doesn't think that's justification enough to launch an investigation, especially when it's a matter so far from their borders.\n正如我所说，一直有传言在流传。显然议会认为这不足以成为发起调查的理由，尤其这地方离他们的疆界如此之远。"

    old "And so you're bringing this to my attention."
    new "And so you're bringing this to my attention.\n所以你就把这事告诉我了。"

    old "Yes. If you decide to investigate this matter. I suspect the council will provide little in the way of assistance. If you want help, you'll likely have to seek it from the people that it affects most. The desert dwellers."
    new "Yes. If you decide to investigate this matter. I suspect the council will provide little in the way of assistance. If you want help, you'll likely have to seek it from the people that it affects most. The desert dwellers.\n是的。如果你决定调查此事，我怀疑议会几乎帮不上什么忙。你若需要帮助，恐怕得从受影响最深的人那里去找。也就是沙漠里的居民。"

    old "People who live in the desert?"
    new "People who live in the desert?\n住在沙漠里的人？"

    old "That region is home to many nomadic groups."
    new "That region is home to many nomadic groups.\n那个地区是许多游牧部族的家园。"

    old "Where should I look for them?"
    new "Where should I look for them?\n我该去哪里找他们？"

    old "Think about what the word 'nomad' means, [protag]. They are wanderers. They likely have mobile settlements. Any location I could provide you with would likely be outdated by the time you arrived."
    new "Think about what the word 'nomad' means, [protag]. They are wanderers. They likely have mobile settlements. Any location I could provide you with would likely be outdated by the time you arrived.\n想想“游牧”这个词的含义，[protag]。他们是漂泊者。他们很可能有流动的营地。我能给你的任何地点，等你赶到时多半都已过时了。"

    old "So I'm just supposed to wander about aimlessly, hoping to bump into someone."
    new "So I'm just supposed to wander about aimlessly, hoping to bump into someone.\n所以我就只能漫无目的地乱走，指望撞上什么人。"

    old "Maybe. My recommendation would be to simply investigate the tomb of Urd and see if that's the origin point for any dark dealings we should know about. But if you encounter any natives along the way, it certainly can't hurt to ask for their assistance. At the very least, they should be able to assist you in locating the tomb and navigating there safely."
    new "Maybe. My recommendation would be to simply investigate the tomb of Urd and see if that's the origin point for any dark dealings we should know about. But if you encounter any natives along the way, it certainly can't hurt to ask for their assistance. At the very least, they should be able to assist you in locating the tomb and navigating there safely.\n也许吧。我的建议是直接去调查Urd之墓，看看那里是否就是我们应该知晓的任何黑暗勾当的源头。不过你沿途若遇到当地人，向他们求助肯定没有坏处。至少，他们应该能帮你找到墓地，并安全地领你过去。"

    old "Should my safety be a concern?"
    new "Should my safety be a concern?\n我的安全会是问题吗？"

    old "Just keep your wits about you if you decide to go. If you have more pressing matters to attend to, I don't mean to distract you. I know that sending you out to investigate rumors is perhaps outside the scope of your responsibilities, but I thought you would want to know."
    new "Just keep your wits about you if you decide to go. If you have more pressing matters to attend to, I don't mean to distract you. I know that sending you out to investigate rumors is perhaps outside the scope of your responsibilities, but I thought you would want to know.\n你若决定去，就务必保持警惕。如果你有更紧迫的事要处理，我并不想让你分心。我知道，派你去调查传言也许超出了你的职责范围，但我想你会想知道这事。"

    old "And thank you for the information, Karen. Sometimes, the most frightening truths begin as mere rumors."
    new "And thank you for the information, Karen. Sometimes, the most frightening truths begin as mere rumors.\n谢谢你的消息，Karen。有时，最可怕的真相最初不过是些传言。"

    old "Always the pessimist. Well, at least you won't be disappointed."
    new "Always the pessimist. Well, at least you won't be disappointed.\n你总是这么悲观。也罢，至少你不会失望。"

    old "I find Dasyra in Grimoire, where we last met."
    new "I find Dasyra in Grimoire, where we last met.\n我在Grimoire找到了Dasyra，就在我们上次见面的地方。"

    old "Hello, Dasyra. How have you been?"
    new "Hello, Dasyra. How have you been?\n你好，Dasyra。你最近怎么样？"

    old "I suppose I can't complain. I've been getting along just fine. Though I wish I could say the same for Galan."
    new "I suppose I can't complain. I've been getting along just fine. Though I wish I could say the same for Galan.\n我想我也没什么可抱怨的。我过得挺好。虽然我倒希望Galan也能如此。"

    old "Galan's fate has been occupying my mind as well. I've been thinking, maybe we should go back for him."
    new "Galan's fate has been occupying my mind as well. I've been thinking, maybe we should go back for him.\nGalan的命运也一直萦绕在我心头。我一直在想，也许我们该回去找他。"

    old "I was hoping you'd say that. Galan's fate is something that weighs on my conscience. Not a day goes by that I don't think about him."
    new "I was hoping you'd say that. Galan's fate is something that weighs on my conscience. Not a day goes by that I don't think about him.\n我正希望你会这么说。Galan的命运一直压在我的良心上。没有一天我不想着他。"

    old "At first, I was afraid to even think about asking about him. What if he met his demise that night, or the day after? It's not the kind of thing I'd want to hear about. But I don't want to hide from the truth—whatever it is—for any longer."
    new "At first, I was afraid to even think about asking about him. What if he met his demise that night, or the day after? It's not the kind of thing I'd want to hear about. But I don't want to hide from the truth—whatever it is—for any longer.\n起初，我连问都不敢问起他。万一他那晚，或者第二天就遇难了呢？那不是我想听到的消息。但我再也不想逃避真相了——不管真相是什么。"

    old "Even if he has met his end, I want to hear about it. If he's deceased, I want that closure, for what good it'll do me or you. But more importantly, if he's trapped, and there's something that we can do to free him...well, we have to try, don't we?"
    new "Even if he has met his end, I want to hear about it. If he's deceased, I want that closure, for what good it'll do me or you. But more importantly, if he's trapped, and there's something that we can do to free him...well, we have to try, don't we?\n即便他真已遇难，我也想知道。如果他去世了，我想要个了断，哪怕这了断对你我都没什么实际用处。但更重要的是，如果他被困住了，而我们有什么办法能救他……那我们就必须试一试，不是吗？"

    old "That's the thinking. How soon would you be ready to head back to Hammerhands?"
    new "That's the thinking. How soon would you be ready to head back to Hammerhands?\n就是这个理。你多久能准备好回Hammerhands？"

    old "How about right now?"
    new "How about right now?\n现在就走怎么样？"

    old "I'm ready if you are."
    new "I'm ready if you are.\n你准备好我就准备好了。"

    old "Lovely. Just give me a few moments to gather some belongings."
    new "Lovely. Just give me a few moments to gather some belongings.\n好极了。给我点时间收拾一下东西。"

    old "We arrive at the outskirts of Hammerhands and enter a tavern to inquire for information."
    new "We arrive at the outskirts of Hammerhands and enter a tavern to inquire for information.\n我们抵达Hammerhands的郊外，走进一家酒馆打听消息。"

    old "Do you think that the people here will know anything about our situation?"
    new "Do you think that the people here will know anything about our situation?\n你觉得这里的人会知道我们的情况吗？"

    old "If Edgar Arasmas wants people to know something, they'll know, even as far from his estate as this tavern. Or at least, people who are in the business of staying informed will know it. Bartender!"
    new "If Edgar Arasmas wants people to know something, they'll know, even as far from his estate as this tavern. Or at least, people who are in the business of staying informed will know it. Bartender!\n如果Edgar Arasmas想让人们知道什么，他们就会知道，哪怕是离他庄园这么远的酒馆。至少，那些以消息灵通为业的人会知道。酒保！"

    old "What can I get you two?"
    new "What can I get you two?\n两位要点什么？"

    old "Some information, if you don't mind."
    new "Some information, if you don't mind.\n要点消息，如果你不介意的话。"

    old "Information is always on tap, provided you're ready to tip."
    new "Information is always on tap, provided you're ready to tip.\n消息随时都有，就看你愿不愿意给小费。"

    old "Of course. I always tip for good service. What can you tell me about the Arasmas estate? Any arrest warrants out in his name? I heard rumors about a pair of fugitives escaping his dungeon."
    new "Of course. I always tip for good service. What can you tell me about the Arasmas estate? Any arrest warrants out in his name? I heard rumors about a pair of fugitives escaping his dungeon.\n当然。服务好我向来都付小费。你能告诉我关于Arasmas庄园的事吗？有以他名义发出的逮捕令吗？我听说有一对逃犯从他的地牢里逃了出来。"

    old "The bartender scratches at his chin and shakes his head."
    new "The bartender scratches at his chin and shakes his head.\n酒保挠了挠下巴，摇了摇头。"

    old "I haven't heard anything about that. In fact, to my knowledge, there haven't been any recent arrests on behalf of the Arasmas estate recently, either. The last I can remember is some accountant, one of Edgar's own, who was imprisoned for embezzling from the Arasmas coffers. Though, who knows whether those charges are trumped up or not."
    new "I haven't heard anything about that. In fact, to my knowledge, there haven't been any recent arrests on behalf of the Arasmas estate recently, either. The last I can remember is some accountant, one of Edgar's own, who was imprisoned for embezzling from the Arasmas coffers. Though, who knows whether those charges are trumped up or not.\n那事我没听说过。事实上，据我所知，最近也没有以Arasmas庄园名义进行的逮捕。我记得最近的一桩，是某个会计，Edgar自己的人，因为挪用Arasmas金库的钱而入狱。不过谁知道那些指控是不是捏造的。"

    old "Who indeed. I also heard something about a theft from the Arasmas estate. Some kind of jewelry heist or something."
    new "Who indeed. I also heard something about a theft from the Arasmas estate. Some kind of jewelry heist or something.\n是啊，谁知道呢。我还听说Arasmas庄园发生了失窃。像是珠宝劫案之类的。"

    old "Well, that's bad information, by my estimation. I've heard nothing about theft from Arasmas, either through official channels or, well, you know. The other kind."
    new "Well, that's bad information, by my estimation. I've heard nothing about theft from Arasmas, either through official channels or, well, you know. The other kind.\n嗯，依我看，那是假消息。我从没听说过Arasmas庄园有失窃的事，无论是通过官方渠道，还是，呃，你知道的那种。"

    old "Interesting. I guess it was just a rumor. Thanks for the information, barkeep."
    new "Interesting. I guess it was just a rumor. Thanks for the information, barkeep.\n有意思。看来那只是谣言。谢谢你的消息，酒保。"

    old "Dasyra reaches into her pocket and pulls out a coin. She tosses it to the bartender, and he snatches it out of the air."
    new "Dasyra reaches into her pocket and pulls out a coin. She tosses it to the bartender, and he snatches it out of the air.\nDasyra把手伸进口袋，掏出一枚硬币。她把硬币抛给酒保，酒保在空中一把接住。"

    old "Anything else I can help you folks with?"
    new "Anything else I can help you folks with?\n还有什么能帮二位的吗？"

    old "I think we're good, thanks."
    new "I think we're good, thanks.\n我想没有了，谢谢。"

    old "The bartender nods and slides down the bar, answering the beckon of another patron."
    new "The bartender nods and slides down the bar, answering the beckon of another patron.\n酒保点点头，顺着吧台滑了过去，去招呼另一位客人的叫唤。"

    old "So? What do you make of that?"
    new "So? What do you make of that?\n那么？你怎么看？"

    old "Well, we know that there's no warrant for our arrest. That means that we're free to move about the city. We could even march right into Arasmas's own public hall without fear."
    new "Well, we know that there's no warrant for our arrest. That means that we're free to move about the city. We could even march right into Arasmas's own public hall without fear.\n嗯，我们知道没有针对我们的逮捕令。也就是说我们可以在城里自由走动。我们甚至可以大摇大摆走进Arasmas自己的会堂，也无所畏惧。"

    old "I'm not sure about the 'without fear' part, but yes, it does seem that both you and I are free people as was as the city and its nobles are concerned."
    new "I'm not sure about the 'without fear' part, but yes, it does seem that both you and I are free people as was as the city and its nobles are concerned.\n“无所畏惧”这部分我可没把握，不过没错，就这座城及其贵族而言，你我似乎确实都是自由身。"

    old "It seems that Edgar is trying to cover up the whole incident. No record of our arrest, or Galan's. That means that Galan is safe, for the time being. After all, he can't very well execute a prisoner that doesn't officially exist."
    new "It seems that Edgar is trying to cover up the whole incident. No record of our arrest, or Galan's. That means that Galan is safe, for the time being. After all, he can't very well execute a prisoner that doesn't officially exist.\n看来Edgar是想把整件事都压下来。没有我们被捕的记录，也没有Galan的。这意味着Galan暂时是安全的。毕竟，他总不好处决一个在官方记录里根本不存在、也从未被捕的囚犯。"

    old "You're not worried they might snuff him out off the books?"
    new "You're not worried they might snuff him out off the books?\n你不担心他们偷偷把他做掉、不留记录吗？"

    old "Surprising as it is, hiding a prisoner is a lot easier than hiding a body. Besides, if Edgar ever wants to bargain with us, he needs leverage."
    new "Surprising as it is, hiding a prisoner is a lot easier than hiding a body. Besides, if Edgar ever wants to bargain with us, he needs leverage.\n说来也怪，藏一个囚犯比藏一具尸体容易多了。再说，Edgar要是想跟我们讨价还价，他就需要筹码。"

    old "Why would Edgar Arasmas want to bargain with us?"
    new "Why would Edgar Arasmas want to bargain with us?\nEdgar Arasmas为什么要跟我们讨价还价？"

    old "Have you forgotten how this ordeal started?"
    new "Have you forgotten how this ordeal started?\n你忘了这场磨难是怎么开始的吗？"

    old "Dasyra pulls the brooch out."
    new "Dasyra pulls the brooch out.\nDasyra把那枚胸针掏了出来。"

    old "That's right. You actually got away with stealing that. The theft was never reported. As far as the law is concerned, it belongs to you now."
    new "That's right. You actually got away with stealing that. The theft was never reported. As far as the law is concerned, it belongs to you now.\n没错。你居然真的偷走它还逃了出来。这桩失窃从未被报案。就法律而言，它现在归你了。"

    old "As I said, it looks like Edgar is trying to keep the world from finding out that whole day ever happened. So, you and I are off without penalty, and one brooch richer. Galan, on the other hand, hasn't been so fortunate."
    new "As I said, it looks like Edgar is trying to keep the world from finding out that whole day ever happened. So, you and I are off without penalty, and one brooch richer. Galan, on the other hand, hasn't been so fortunate.\n正如我所说，看来Edgar是想让整个世界永远别知道那天发生过什么。所以，你我没有受罚，还多了枚胸针。而Galan，就没那么走运了。"

    old "I'm not sure what this brooch is worth to Edgar, but given that he was willing to chase me for it, it might mean more than we expect. Might be worth the life of a captured dwarf, eh?"
    new "I'm not sure what this brooch is worth to Edgar, but given that he was willing to chase me for it, it might mean more than we expect. Might be worth the life of a captured dwarf, eh?\n我不确定这枚胸针对Edgar来说值多少，但既然他愿意追着我不放，它的意义可能超出我们的预期。说不定能抵一个被俘矮人的命，嗯？"

    old "Maybe. But I'm curious about that brooch and what it's worth to Edgar. I think that we should do our research before we sit down at the bargaining table. Or even walk up to it."
    new "Maybe. But I'm curious about that brooch and what it's worth to Edgar. I think that we should do our research before we sit down at the bargaining table. Or even walk up to it.\n也许吧。但我很好奇那枚胸针，以及它对Edgar的价值。我想我们在坐到谈判桌前，甚至走近谈判桌之前，都该先做做功课。"

    old "Meaning?"
    new "Meaning?\n什么意思？"

    old "Meaning we find out what is so special about that brooch of yours. Let's find someone who might know."
    new "Meaning we find out what is so special about that brooch of yours. Let's find someone who might know.\n意思是，我们得弄清你那枚胸针到底有什么特别。我们去找个可能知情的人吧。"

    old "After some searching, we locate a reputable jeweler in the heart of Hammerhands."
    new "After some searching, we locate a reputable jeweler in the heart of Hammerhands.\n一番寻找之后，我们在Hammerhands中心找到了一位信誉卓著的珠宝商。"

    old "Hmm. This is an interesting piece. You said your name was Dasyra, did you not?"
    new "Hmm. This is an interesting piece. You said your name was Dasyra, did you not?\n嗯。这是件有意思的物件。你说你叫Dasyra，对吧？"

    old "That's right."
    new "That's right.\n没错。"

    old "Dasyra, it's hard for me to tell much about this. It's a bit of an awkward age. It's a modern piece, but not fresh. Were it an older relic, I might be able to identify from the handiwork who made it, but in recent years the number of people crafting these sort of trinkets has grown too numerous to keep track of."
    new "Dasyra, it's hard for me to tell much about this. It's a bit of an awkward age. It's a modern piece, but not fresh. Were it an older relic, I might be able to identify from the handiwork who made it, but in recent years the number of people crafting these sort of trinkets has grown too numerous to keep track of.\nDasyra，这件东西我很难说清多少。它的年代有点尴尬。是件现代物件，但又不算新。要是更古老的遗物，我也许能凭手工认出是谁做的，但近些年来，制作这类小饰品的人多得数都数不过来。"

    old "On the other hand, it's not new enough for me to draw conclusions based on the quality of the materials used—our records don't go back that far. I'd say this piece is maybe thirty years old, give or take a decade."
    new "On the other hand, it's not new enough for me to draw conclusions based on the quality of the materials used—our records don't go back that far. I'd say this piece is maybe thirty years old, give or take a decade.\n另一方面，它又不够新，我无法凭所用材料的品质下结论——我们的记录追溯不到那么久远。要我说，这件东西大概有三十年历史，前后差个十年。"

    old "That sounds about right. To my knowledge, it's about as old as I am, or a little older."
    new "That sounds about right. To my knowledge, it's about as old as I am, or a little older.\n听起来差不多。据我所知，它大概和我年纪相仿，或者稍大一点。"

    old "I did find something interesting about it. It seems to have some faint magical signatures, based on what I can measure. I did my best to try and awaken whatever magical properties it might have, but my tests were inconclusive. This one has me stumped. Sorry, missy. I wish I had more to tell you."
    new "I did find something interesting about it. It seems to have some faint magical signatures, based on what I can measure. I did my best to try and awaken whatever magical properties it might have, but my tests were inconclusive. This one has me stumped. Sorry, missy. I wish I had more to tell you.\n我确实发现了一些有意思的地方。根据我能测出的结果，它似乎带有某种微弱的魔法印记。我尽了最大努力，想唤醒它可能具有的魔法属性，但测试都没有定论。这件东西把我难住了。抱歉，小姐。真希望我能多告诉你一些。"

    old "Well, you've done your best, and that you were able to get this far is helpful enough. I always suspected that their might be some kind of magic living in that brooch, but never knew how to go about awakening such things. What did you try?"
    new "Well, you've done your best, and that you were able to get this far is helpful enough. I always suspected that their might be some kind of magic living in that brooch, but never knew how to go about awakening such things. What did you try?\n嗯，你已经尽力了，能查到这一步已经很有帮助。我一直怀疑那枚胸针里或许藏着某种魔法，但从不知道怎么去唤醒它。你试了些什么？"

    old "Oh, I paired it to several power sources. Heating to extreme temperatures—not so extreme as to damage the metal, mind you—and even tried some alchemy-based catalysts. There were several tests that actually increased the magical readings I got from it, but whatever triggers this thing's powers, well, that's a mystery that still needs to be solved."
    new "Oh, I paired it to several power sources. Heating to extreme temperatures—not so extreme as to damage the metal, mind you—and even tried some alchemy-based catalysts. There were several tests that actually increased the magical readings I got from it, but whatever triggers this thing's powers, well, that's a mystery that still needs to be solved.\n哦，我把它连接到了几种能量源上。加热到极高温度——注意，还没高到会损伤金属的程度——甚至试过一些炼金术的催化剂。有几次测试确实提高了我从它身上测到的魔法读数，但究竟是什么触发了这东西的力量，这个谜还有待解开。"

    old "Do let me know if you discover anything about it. You've piqued my curiosity."
    new "Do let me know if you discover anything about it. You've piqued my curiosity.\n你要是发现了什么，一定告诉我。你勾起了我的好奇心。"

    old "The jeweler picks up the brooch and offers it to Dasyra. She takes the brooch, squeals as it touches her hand, and it drops to the floor."
    new "The jeweler picks up the brooch and offers it to Dasyra. She takes the brooch, squeals as it touches her hand, and it drops to the floor.\n珠宝商拿起胸针，递给Dasyra。她接过胸针，手一碰就惊叫起来，胸针掉到了地上。"

    old "Sorry, it's still a bit warm from my testing—"
    new "Sorry, it's still a bit warm from my testing—\n抱歉，我刚测试过，它还有点烫——"

    old "[protag], did you see that?"
    new "[protag], did you see that?\n[protag]，你看见了吗？"

    old "See what?"
    new "See what?\n看见什么？"

    old "Dasyra picks the brooch up off the floor, and lifts it up. A faint glow emanates from the brooch as she cradles it in her palm."
    new "Dasyra picks the brooch up off the floor, and lifts it up. A faint glow emanates from the brooch as she cradles it in her palm.\nDasyra把胸针从地上捡起来，高高举起。她把它托在掌心，胸针上泛起一道微弱的光。"

    old "Now, this is a surprise. Dasyra, would you mind if I inspected that for a moment?"
    new "Now, this is a surprise. Dasyra, would you mind if I inspected that for a moment?\n这倒是个意外。Dasyra，你介意我检查它一下吗？"

    old "Dasyra hands the brooch to the jeweler, and it immediately stops glowing. He turns it over in his hands several times, then hands it back to Dasyra. As soon as she touches it, it regains its luminescent properties."
    new "Dasyra hands the brooch to the jeweler, and it immediately stops glowing. He turns it over in his hands several times, then hands it back to Dasyra. As soon as she touches it, it regains its luminescent properties.\nDasyra把胸针递给珠宝商，它立刻就不发光了。他把胸针在手里翻了几次，又递回给Dasyra。她一碰到它，它就又恢复了发光。"

    old "Interesting. In my testing, I detected magic, but couldn't determine a trigger. Now, I think we've found it. Dasyra, is this brooch...is it somehow special to you? Could it have some connection to you? You said it was older than you are."
    new "Interesting. In my testing, I detected magic, but couldn't determine a trigger. Now, I think we've found it. Dasyra, is this brooch...is it somehow special to you? Could it have some connection to you? You said it was older than you are.\n有意思。我测试时探测到了魔法，却无法确定触发条件。现在，我想我们找到了。Dasyra，这枚胸针……它对你有某种特殊意义吗？它会不会和你有某种关联？你说它比你的年纪还大。"

    old "It belonged to my mother."
    new "It belonged to my mother.\n它是我母亲的。"

    old "That might explain it. Dasyra, I'm going to need to do some more testing on this, with your help if you don't mind."
    new "That might explain it. Dasyra, I'm going to need to do some more testing on this, with your help if you don't mind.\n那或许能解释得通。Dasyra，我需要再做一些测试，如果你不介意的话，希望你能帮忙。"

    old "How long do you expect this to take?"
    new "How long do you expect this to take?\n你预计这要花多久？"

    old "If we want to be comprehensive, probably all day. Maybe longer. Would you be able to come in tomorrow as well, if it came to that?"
    new "If we want to be comprehensive, probably all day. Maybe longer. Would you be able to come in tomorrow as well, if it came to that?\n要是想做得全面，恐怕得一整天。也许更久。如果真需要，你明天能再来吗？"

    old "That could be arranged."
    new "That could be arranged.\n可以安排。"

    old "[protag], I don't see any reason for you to sit here looking bored while we examine the brooch. Why don't you leave me here, and we'll take as long as we need to figure out what exactly this brooch is supposed to be. We can regroup in several days, or whenever you have the time. Sound good?"
    new "[protag], I don't see any reason for you to sit here looking bored while we examine the brooch. Why don't you leave me here, and we'll take as long as we need to figure out what exactly this brooch is supposed to be. We can regroup in several days, or whenever you have the time. Sound good?\n[protag]，我看不出你有什么理由坐在这里，干看着我们检查胸针而无聊透顶。你不如把我留在这里，我们慢慢弄清楚这枚胸针到底是什么。过几天，或者等你有空的时候，我们再碰头。听起来怎么样？"

    old "Sure. No sense in us trying to decide what to do next before we have all the information. I'll catch you later. I'm not sure what exactly our next meeting will hold, but I look forward to it."
    new "Sure. No sense in us trying to decide what to do next before we have all the information. I'll catch you later. I'm not sure what exactly our next meeting will hold, but I look forward to it.\n好。在掌握全部信息之前，我们没必要急着决定下一步。我回头再来找你。我不知道我们下次见面会有什么结果，但我很期待。"

    old "Thanks [protag]. Of course, if you need me urgently for any reason, I'll interrupt the tests, come with you and resume them later."
    new "Thanks [protag]. Of course, if you need me urgently for any reason, I'll interrupt the tests, come with you and resume them later.\n谢谢，[protag]。当然，如果你有急事需要我，我会打断测试，跟你一起走，之后再回来继续。"

    old "I return to Hammerhands and locate Dasyra at the jeweler's shop."
    new "I return to Hammerhands and locate Dasyra at the jeweler's shop.\n我回到Hammerhands，在珠宝店找到了Dasyra。"

    old "Ah, Dasyra, it appears that your companion is here."
    new "Ah, Dasyra, it appears that your companion is here.\n啊，Dasyra，看来你的同伴来了。"

    old "[protag], I was wondering when you'd come around again. Your visit is actually well-timed. I think that we've done as much as we can here."
    new "[protag], I was wondering when you'd come around again. Your visit is actually well-timed. I think that we've done as much as we can here.\n[protag]，我正想着你什么时候会再来。你来得正好。我想我们在这里能做的都做了。"

    old "What's the scoop on the brooch?"
    new "What's the scoop on the brooch?\n胸针有什么新发现？"

    old "By my estimation, this is what's sometimes referred to as a resonator stone. It has a few magical properties, but nothing too useful."
    new "By my estimation, this is what's sometimes referred to as a resonator stone. It has a few magical properties, but nothing too useful.\n据我估计，这就是有时被称作共鸣石的东西。它带有一些魔法属性，但没什么大用。"

    old "You might be able to perform a few simple parlor tricks: light a pipe with the snap of a finger, levitate a small napkin, drink water from a cup without raising it to your lips, and so on. Very simple and trivial tasks that are more impressive than they are practical."
    new "You might be able to perform a few simple parlor tricks: light a pipe with the snap of a finger, levitate a small napkin, drink water from a cup without raising it to your lips, and so on. Very simple and trivial tasks that are more impressive than they are practical.\n你也许能施展几个简单的小把戏：打个响指点燃烟斗，让一小块餐巾悬浮，不用把杯子举到嘴边就能喝到水，诸如此类。都是些简单琐碎、看着唬人却并不实用的小事。"

    old "The thing that makes these resonators so interesting is the way that they are made."
    new "The thing that makes these resonators so interesting is the way that they are made.\n让这些共鸣石如此有趣的地方，在于它们的制作方式。"

    old "I don't have much documentation on the process itself, but it's the kind of artifact that is forged by both a jeweler and a witch in most cases, combining things like metals and precious stones with bits of a person's hair or spit. Through the forging process, the resonator becomes attuned to a specific user. That's how even someone with zero magical aptitude can perform simple magic tricks using a resonator."
    new "I don't have much documentation on the process itself, but it's the kind of artifact that is forged by both a jeweler and a witch in most cases, combining things like metals and precious stones with bits of a person's hair or spit. Through the forging process, the resonator becomes attuned to a specific user. That's how even someone with zero magical aptitude can perform simple magic tricks using a resonator.\n关于制作过程本身，我手头的资料不多，但这类器物多数情况下是由珠宝商和女巫共同锻造的，把金属、宝石之类的东西与人的头发或唾液混在一起。通过锻造过程，共鸣石会与特定使用者相契合。所以，即便是一个完全没有魔法天赋的人，也能用它施展简单的魔法把戏。"

    old "I don't understand. This resonator was made specially for Dasyra? Dasyra, is this something your mother could have made when you were just an infant?"
    new "I don't understand. This resonator was made specially for Dasyra? Dasyra, is this something your mother could have made when you were just an infant?\n我不明白。这枚共鸣石是专门为Dasyra打造的吗？Dasyra，这会不会是你母亲在你还小的时候做的东西？"

    old "I don't think so. As far as I know, my mother had this brooch before I was born."
    new "I don't think so. As far as I know, my mother had this brooch before I was born.\n我想不是。据我所知，我母亲在我出生前就有这枚胸针了。"

    old "That is in line with my own hypothesis regarding this artifact. You see, resonators have another interesting property. They're specially attuned to a specifc user, but the traits that allow an individual to use the resonator are partly hereditary. It would stand to reason that if the resonator had been attuned to Dasyra's mother, then Dasyra would possess some of that attunement as well."
    new "That is in line with my own hypothesis regarding this artifact. You see, resonators have another interesting property. They're specially attuned to a specifc user, but the traits that allow an individual to use the resonator are partly hereditary. It would stand to reason that if the resonator had been attuned to Dasyra's mother, then Dasyra would possess some of that attunement as well.\n这与我对这件器物的假设相符。你看，共鸣石还有另一个有趣的特性。它们与特定使用者相契合，但让一个人能使用共鸣石的那些特质，部分是遗传的。按理说，如果共鸣石是与Dasyra的母亲相契合的，那么Dasyra也会继承一部分这种契合。"

    old "Now, granted, Dasyra and her mother are not the same person. Every person is a mix of two parents, after all. That would explain why the resonator doesn't respond as strongly to Dasyra. For one thing, she's noticed nothing special about the brooch at first. It wasn't until I began applying different chemical rubs to it that it started responding to her touch."
    new "Now, granted, Dasyra and her mother are not the same person. Every person is a mix of two parents, after all. That would explain why the resonator doesn't respond as strongly to Dasyra. For one thing, she's noticed nothing special about the brooch at first. It wasn't until I began applying different chemical rubs to it that it started responding to her touch.\n当然，Dasyra和她母亲并不是同一个人。毕竟，每个人都是父母的结合体。这就解释了为什么共鸣石对Dasyra的反应不那么强烈。首先，她一开始并没有注意到胸针有什么特别。直到我开始给它涂上不同的化学药剂，它才开始对她的触碰产生反应。"

    old "My theory is that simply cleaning the brooch and exposing it to different power sources helped to catalyze its response to her. Also, the resonator doesn't respond that strongly to her."
    new "My theory is that simply cleaning the brooch and exposing it to different power sources helped to catalyze its response to her. Also, the resonator doesn't respond that strongly to her.\n我的理论是，仅仅是清洁胸针、把它暴露在不同的能量源下，就帮助催化了它对她的反应。而且，共鸣石对她的反应也没有那么强烈。"

    old "I've gotten a little better at using it. The glow when I touch it is a lot stronger, and it actually gets a little warm. But I can't, for example, light a fire using it, which I believe was its original intended function."
    new "I've gotten a little better at using it. The glow when I touch it is a lot stronger, and it actually gets a little warm. But I can't, for example, light a fire using it, which I believe was its original intended function.\n我使用它时已经熟练了一点。我碰它时，光芒强了很多，它实际上还会有点发热。但比如说，我还不能用它点火，而我相信点火才是它最初被设计的功能。"

    old "One of the questions I had for Dasyra is how and why her mother could have had this brooch made. As I mentioned, the process for creating a resonator like this is far from trivial."
    new "One of the questions I had for Dasyra is how and why her mother could have had this brooch made. As I mentioned, the process for creating a resonator like this is far from trivial.\n我想问Dasyra的问题之一是，她母亲怎么会、又为什么要让人做这枚胸针。正如我提到的，打造这样一枚共鸣石的过程绝非易事。"

    old "One of the attractions of an artifact like this is that it can be used as a display of wealth, so how a woman of modest means managed to have one made is a serious question indeed."
    new "One of the attractions of an artifact like this is that it can be used as a display of wealth, so how a woman of modest means managed to have one made is a serious question indeed.\n这种器物的吸引力之一，是它可以用来炫耀财富，所以一个家境平平的女人怎么会有财力打造它，确实是个严肃的问题。"

    old "My mother worked as a maid for Faberge Arasmas. It must have paid for the brooch to be made, as a gift. In fact, it wouldn't surprise me if old man Faberge himself was the jeweler to make this brooch."
    new "My mother worked as a maid for Faberge Arasmas. It must have paid for the brooch to be made, as a gift. In fact, it wouldn't surprise me if old man Faberge himself was the jeweler to make this brooch.\n我母亲给Faberge Arasmas当女仆。一定是挣来的钱付了打造胸针的费用，作为礼物。事实上，就算这枚胸针正是Faberge老人亲手打造的，我也不会惊讶。"

    old "That would make sense. After all, Faberge Arasmas was a jeweler first, nobleman second. Though he didn't practice commercial jewelery-making in his later years, it's not inconceivable that he could have kept up jewel-making as a private hobby, and made personal effects such as this one for the people who worked on his estate."
    new "That would make sense. After all, Faberge Arasmas was a jeweler first, nobleman second. Though he didn't practice commercial jewelery-making in his later years, it's not inconceivable that he could have kept up jewel-making as a private hobby, and made personal effects such as this one for the people who worked on his estate.\n那就说得通了。毕竟，Faberge Arasmas首先是珠宝商，其次才是贵族。尽管他晚年不再从事商业珠宝制作，但他把珠宝制作作为私人爱好保留下来、并为在他庄园里工作的人打造这样的私人物件，并非不可想象。"

    old "Faberge was well-known for his generosity."
    new "Faberge was well-known for his generosity.\nFaberge素以慷慨著称。"

    old "Indeed. I think the most compelling case for assuming that this is Faberge Arasmas's own handiwork is the fact that there's no stamp or seal anywhere on the brooch. A commercial jeweler would have left a personal stamp, partly just due to simple practice, and partly as a verification of authenticity."
    new "Indeed. I think the most compelling case for assuming that this is Faberge Arasmas's own handiwork is the fact that there's no stamp or seal anywhere on the brooch. A commercial jeweler would have left a personal stamp, partly just due to simple practice, and partly as a verification of authenticity.\n确实。我认为，最能说明这是Faberge Arasmas亲手之作的一点是，这枚胸针上没有任何印戳或印记。商业珠宝商会留下个人印戳，一方面出于习惯，一方面也是作为真品的凭证。"

    old "It's possible that this brooch did once have a commercial stamp that was either deliberately filed away, or worn off with age. But I doubt that myself, as I found no evidence of excessive wear or tampering."
    new "It's possible that this brooch did once have a commercial stamp that was either deliberately filed away, or worn off with age. But I doubt that myself, as I found no evidence of excessive wear or tampering.\n这枚胸针过去或许确实有过商业印戳，只是后来被故意锉掉，或者随岁月磨损了。但我自己对此存疑，因为我没有发现任何过度磨损或被动手脚的痕迹。"

    old "While there's no way to verify for certain that this brooch was specially made by Faberge Arasmas as a personal gift to Dasyra's mother, all the signs point to it. And if that is true, this is a very enticing piece indeed."
    new "While there's no way to verify for certain that this brooch was specially made by Faberge Arasmas as a personal gift to Dasyra's mother, all the signs point to it. And if that is true, this is a very enticing piece indeed.\n虽然无法确证这枚胸针是Faberge Arasmas特意作为私人礼物送给Dasyra母亲的，但一切迹象都指向这一点。若果真如此，这确实是件非常诱人的物件。"

    old "What's so enticing about it?"
    new "What's so enticing about it?\n它有什么诱人的？"

    old "Faberge Arasmas was one of the famous jewelers in all of Hammerhands. If someone found a never-before-seen brooch made by the man himself, uncovered after decades of being buried away in a vault somewhere, it could cause quite the stir among enthusiasts."
    new "Faberge Arasmas was one of the famous jewelers in all of Hammerhands. If someone found a never-before-seen brooch made by the man himself, uncovered after decades of being buried away in a vault somewhere, it could cause quite the stir among enthusiasts.\nFaberge Arasmas是Hammerhands全境最著名的珠宝商之一。如果有人发现一枚从未见过的、由他本人打造的胸针，在某个金库里埋藏几十年后重见天日，那会在爱好者中引起不小的轰动。"

    old "If this brooch went to auction, it could fetch...well, let's just say that if Dasyra sold this brooch, she wouldn't have to work for a very long time."
    new "If this brooch went to auction, it could fetch...well, let's just say that if Dasyra sold this brooch, she wouldn't have to work for a very long time.\n这枚胸针要是拿去拍卖，能卖出……好吧，这么说吧，如果Dasyra卖掉它，她很长一段时间都不用工作了。"

    old "Not going to happen. There are things in this world more valuable than money. That brooch is one of them."
    new "Not going to happen. There are things in this world more valuable than money. That brooch is one of them.\n不会发生的。这世上有些东西比钱更宝贵。那枚胸针就是其中之一。"

    old "Fair enough, fair enough. By all means, keep the brooch. A jeweler like me should understand more than anyone the value of a sentiment over money. After all, the value of a wedding ring has less to do with the handiwork or craftsmanship of the man who made it than the love of and devotion of the man who bought it."
    new "Fair enough, fair enough. By all means, keep the brooch. A jeweler like me should understand more than anyone the value of a sentiment over money. After all, the value of a wedding ring has less to do with the handiwork or craftsmanship of the man who made it than the love of and devotion of the man who bought it.\n说得好，说得好。请务必留着这枚胸针。像我这样的珠宝商，应该比任何人都更明白情意胜过金钱的道理。毕竟，一枚婚戒的价值，与其说在于打造者的手艺，不如说在于购买者的爱与奉献。"

    old "Thank you for all your assistance. You've been a tremendous help. As for payment—"
    new "Thank you for all your assistance. You've been a tremendous help. As for payment—\n谢谢你的所有帮助。你帮了大忙。至于报酬——"

    old "I wouldn't dream of taking it. As you just said yourself, there are things more valuable in this world than money, sentiment ranking high among them. Spending several days handling a brooch made by Faberge Arasmas himself—admiring his handiwork and technique, seeing his unique flair and style—it's all a jeweler like me could ever dream of."
    new "I wouldn't dream of taking it. As you just said yourself, there are things more valuable in this world than money, sentiment ranking high among them. Spending several days handling a brooch made by Faberge Arasmas himself—admiring his handiwork and technique, seeing his unique flair and style—it's all a jeweler like me could ever dream of.\n我可从没想过要收。正如你刚才自己说的，这世上有些东西比金钱更宝贵，情意便是其中翘楚。花上好几天摆弄一枚Faberge Arasmas亲手打造的胸针——欣赏他的手艺与技法，见识他独有的风格与神采——这正是一个珠宝商梦寐以求的一切。"

    old "Take the brooch, and my blessing. You've certainly blessed me by bringing it here."
    new "Take the brooch, and my blessing. You've certainly blessed me by bringing it here.\n收下胸针，也收下我的祝福。你把它带到这里，就已经是我的福气了。"

    old "I—I have no words. Thank you."
    new "I—I have no words. Thank you.\n我——我不知该说什么。谢谢你。"

    old "So, where do we go from here?"
    new "So, where do we go from here?\n那么，我们接下来怎么办？"

    old "I had talked about using this brooch as leverage to get Galan out of jail. But now that I know what it's worth..."
    new "I had talked about using this brooch as leverage to get Galan out of jail. But now that I know what it's worth...\n我之前说过，要用这枚胸针当筹码，把Galan从牢里救出来。但现在我知道了它的价值……"

    old "Dasyra trails off, and I look her in the eye, questioningly."
    new "Dasyra trails off, and I look her in the eye, questioningly.\nDasyra的声音渐渐低了下去，我用询问的目光看着她。"

    old "Oh, please don't get the wrong idea. I have no intention of running off with this thing and leaving Galan to rot. His fate weighs heavily on my soul, and no amount of riches would change that. What I mean is this: knowing what this brooch is worth, I think we may be able to get more than just Galan's freedom."
    new "Oh, please don't get the wrong idea. I have no intention of running off with this thing and leaving Galan to rot. His fate weighs heavily on my soul, and no amount of riches would change that. What I mean is this: knowing what this brooch is worth, I think we may be able to get more than just Galan's freedom.\n哦，请别误会。我绝没有想拿着这东西跑掉、让Galan烂在牢里的意思。他的命运沉甸甸地压在我心上，多少财富都改变不了这一点。我的意思是：既然知道了这枚胸针的价值，我想我们也许能得到的，不止是Galan的自由。"

    old "What did you have in mind? Do you intend to barter it for riches from the Arasmas estate?"
    new "What did you have in mind? Do you intend to barter it for riches from the Arasmas estate?\n你有什么打算？你打算拿它去换Arasmas庄园的财富吗？"

    old "This brooch was stolen from my mother by the wicked Edgar Arasmas. He covered his tracks well to make it look legal. In fact, he was able to take it by abusing the rule of inheritance. But if we can prove that he deliberately destroyed his father's will to usurp the estate, including that which rightfully belonged to my mother, it would be the ultimate in grand larceny."
    new "This brooch was stolen from my mother by the wicked Edgar Arasmas. He covered his tracks well to make it look legal. In fact, he was able to take it by abusing the rule of inheritance. But if we can prove that he deliberately destroyed his father's will to usurp the estate, including that which rightfully belonged to my mother, it would be the ultimate in grand larceny.\n这枚胸针是邪恶的Edgar Arasmas从我母亲那里偷走的。他把痕迹掩饰得很好，让它看起来像是合法的。事实上，他是通过滥用继承规则才把它弄到手的。但如果我们能证明，他为了篡夺庄园而蓄意毁掉了他父亲的遗嘱，包括那些本属于我母亲的东西，那就是天大的窃盗了。"

    old "I'm not suggesting that we bargain with Edgar Arasmas. I'm suggesting that we take him down. It's more personal now than it's ever been."
    new "I'm not suggesting that we bargain with Edgar Arasmas. I'm suggesting that we take him down. It's more personal now than it's ever been.\n我不是建议我们和Edgar Arasmas讨价还价。我是建议我们扳倒他。这件事如今比以往任何时候都更私人了。"

    old "The fact that this magical brooch reacts to my touch the way it does proves that it was made specifically for my mother. That's a fact that can't be hidden by destroying a will. This could be the evidence that we need to expose Edgar as the thief he is."
    new "The fact that this magical brooch reacts to my touch the way it does proves that it was made specifically for my mother. That's a fact that can't be hidden by destroying a will. This could be the evidence that we need to expose Edgar as the thief he is.\n这枚魔法胸针对我触碰的反应方式证明，它是专门为我母亲打造的。这一事实无法靠毁掉一份遗嘱来掩盖。这可能就是我们需要的证据，用来揭穿Edgar这个窃贼的真面目。"

    old "So, where do we start?"
    new "So, where do we start?\n那我们该从哪里开始？"

    old "I wish I knew."
    new "I wish I knew.\n我也希望自己知道。"

    old "We need a strategy. Bringing an accusation like this against a nobleman isn't something that you do without planning. We need someone who has experience dealing with political situations."
    new "We need a strategy. Bringing an accusation like this against a nobleman isn't something that you do without planning. We need someone who has experience dealing with political situations.\n我们需要一个策略。对一个贵族提出这样的指控，不是不假思索就能做的事。我们需要一位有处理政治局面经验的人。"

    old "I wish I knew someone that matched that description."
    new "I wish I knew someone that matched that description.\n我真希望我认识个符合这个描述的人。"

    old "I am friends with some important people in Grimoire, and this seems like an important enough matter to bother them about. Dasyra, have you ever met an archwizard?"
    new "I am friends with some important people in Grimoire, and this seems like an important enough matter to bother them about. Dasyra, have you ever met an archwizard?\n我在Grimoire认识一些大人物，这事足够重要，值得去麻烦他们。Dasyra，你见过大法师吗？"

    old "Can't say I have. But I get the impression that's about to change."
    new "Can't say I have. But I get the impression that's about to change.\n不能说见过。但我的感觉是，这马上就要变了。"

    old "Let's head back to Grimoire. Will probably take a couple of days, but I should be able to arrange a meeting with Apolimesho."
    new "Let's head back to Grimoire. Will probably take a couple of days, but I should be able to arrange a meeting with Apolimesho.\n我们回Grimoire吧。大概要几天，但我应该能安排和Apolimesho见一面。"

    old "Dasyra and I meet Apolimesho in one of the Grimoire council's private chambers and explain our findings to him."
    new "Dasyra and I meet Apolimesho in one of the Grimoire council's private chambers and explain our findings to him.\nDasyra和我在Grimoire议会的一间密室里见了Apolimesho，向他说明了我们的发现。"

    old "Dasyra, that brooch of yours is indeed something very special. Even I, as a practitioner of magic, find it fascinating. I can't begin to imagine the cultural and historical value it must hold if it is indeed the handiwork of a famous jeweler."
    new "Dasyra, that brooch of yours is indeed something very special. Even I, as a practitioner of magic, find it fascinating. I can't begin to imagine the cultural and historical value it must hold if it is indeed the handiwork of a famous jeweler.\nDasyra，你的那枚胸针确实非常特别。即便是我这样的魔法修行者，也觉得它引人入胜。如果它真是一位著名珠宝商的手笔，我简直无法想象它承载的文化与历史价值。"

    old "That being said, I'm not sure that you can form a case against Edgar Arasmas, if this is your only evidence. I think that he's made very sure of that."
    new "That being said, I'm not sure that you can form a case against Edgar Arasmas, if this is your only evidence. I think that he's made very sure of that.\n话虽如此，我不确定仅凭这一件证据，你就能对Edgar Arasmas立案。我想他早就做足了万全准备。"

    old "How do you mean?"
    new "How do you mean?\n这话怎么说？"

    old "From what you've told me, both you and Dasyra aren't being pursued for the theft of this item. It was never reported stolen. Is that correct?"
    new "From what you've told me, both you and Dasyra aren't being pursued for the theft of this item. It was never reported stolen. Is that correct?\n按你们告诉我的，你和Dasyra都没有因为这件物品的失窃而被追捕。它从未被报失。是这样吗？"

    old "If that's the case, then how do you intend to prove that he wrongfully took it in the first place? You have no material evidence. Edgar can claim that the brooch was in Dasyra's possession all along. By taking the brooch back, you've removed the very thing that could have incriminated him."
    new "If that's the case, then how do you intend to prove that he wrongfully took it in the first place? You have no material evidence. Edgar can claim that the brooch was in Dasyra's possession all along. By taking the brooch back, you've removed the very thing that could have incriminated him.\n如果是这样，那你打算怎么证明他一开始就是非法占有了它？你没有物证。Edgar可以声称胸针一直在Dasyra手里。拿回胸针，反而等于销毁了本可以给他定罪的东西。"

    old "Furthermore, the only way that you can prove that Edgar seized the entire estate wrongfully is if you can prove that he burned the will. Even if this brooch was originally willed to your mother, that fact is irrelevant if the document can't be brought up to verify it."
    new "Furthermore, the only way that you can prove that Edgar seized the entire estate wrongfully is if you can prove that he burned the will. Even if this brooch was originally willed to your mother, that fact is irrelevant if the document can't be brought up to verify it.\n再者，要证明Edgar非法夺占了整座庄园，唯一的办法就是证明他烧了遗嘱。即便这枚胸针原本是遗赠给你母亲的，只要无法取出那份文件来验证，这一事实也就无关紧要了。"

    old "Even if we can show that Edgar knew that his father's will being 'lost' would profit him, that proves only that he had motive to destroy the will."
    new "Even if we can show that Edgar knew that his father's will being 'lost' would profit him, that proves only that he had motive to destroy the will.\n即便我们能证明Edgar明知父亲的遗嘱“遗失”会让他得利，那也只能证明他有销毁遗嘱的动机。"

    old "Were this an ordinary civil case, we could look up the history of his last will and testament in public record. However, Faberge, being a nobleman, assumed that his estate would be the safest place to store the will. A reasonable assumption, for a man who is no stranger to protecting his own possessions. His will was never a matter of public record."
    new "Were this an ordinary civil case, we could look up the history of his last will and testament in public record. However, Faberge, being a nobleman, assumed that his estate would be the safest place to store the will. A reasonable assumption, for a man who is no stranger to protecting his own possessions. His will was never a matter of public record.\n如果这是普通的民事案件，我们可以去公开记录里查他最后遗嘱的历史。然而，Faberge身为贵族，认定自己的庄园是存放遗嘱最安全的地方。对于一个向来善于守护自己财物的人来说，这假设合情合理。他的遗嘱从来就不是公开记录。"

    old "Dasyra, you suggested that we go after Edgar using the law. Unfortunately, that's just not possible. The secret to Edgar's success in usurping his father's estate is that he is using the law as his tool. Law states that in the absence of a will, custody of Faberge goes to his eldest offspring."
    new "Dasyra, you suggested that we go after Edgar using the law. Unfortunately, that's just not possible. The secret to Edgar's success in usurping his father's estate is that he is using the law as his tool. Law states that in the absence of a will, custody of Faberge goes to his eldest offspring.\nDasyra，你建议我们借助法律来追查Edgar。遗憾的是，这行不通。Edgar能成功篡夺他父亲的庄园，秘诀就在于他把法律当成了工具。法律规定，在没有遗嘱的情况下，Faberge的监护权归于他最大的子嗣。"

    old "Edgar could be despised in the eyes of the public, or disowned by his own father, but none of that matters in the eyes of the law. Without a will to say otherwise, birthright determines the inheritance of a noble estate. As Faberge's only descendant, Edgar controls the estate."
    new "Edgar could be despised in the eyes of the public, or disowned by his own father, but none of that matters in the eyes of the law. Without a will to say otherwise, birthright determines the inheritance of a noble estate. As Faberge's only descendant, Edgar controls the estate.\nEdgar或许在公众眼中遭人唾弃，或许被亲生父亲断绝了关系，但在法律眼里，这些都不重要。没有遗嘱另作说明，出身决定了一个贵族庄园的继承权。作为Faberge唯一的后裔，Edgar掌控着庄园。"

    old "Blast it. I think you're right, Apolimesho. Edgar's going to get away with it."
    new "Blast it. I think you're right, Apolimesho. Edgar's going to get away with it.\n该死。我想你说得对，Apolimesho。Edgar要逍遥法外了。"

    old "So what do we do now?"
    new "So what do we do now?\n那我们该怎么办？"

    old "Galan's still waiting for us. I talked before about using this brooch as a bargaining chip. Edgar has at least done us the courtesy of allowing us to keep it. With no report of its theft, it should rightfully belong to me, especially now that I can prove it belonged to my mother."
    new "Galan's still waiting for us. I talked before about using this brooch as a bargaining chip. Edgar has at least done us the courtesy of allowing us to keep it. With no report of its theft, it should rightfully belong to me, especially now that I can prove it belonged to my mother.\nGalan还在等我们。我之前说过，要把这枚胸针当作筹码。Edgar至少给了我们一个面子，让我们留着它。既然它的失窃没有报案，它就该名正言顺属于我，尤其现在我能证明它属于我母亲。"

    old "As much as it pains me to do this, I think we may need to barter this for Galan's freedom. Maybe we can extract some other wealth from Edgar as well."
    new "As much as it pains me to do this, I think we may need to barter this for Galan's freedom. Maybe we can extract some other wealth from Edgar as well.\n尽管这样做让我很痛苦，但我想我们也许得用它来换取Galan的自由。也许我们还能从Edgar那里再榨出些别的财富。"

    old "Apolimesho, what do you think about this?"
    new "Apolimesho, what do you think about this?\nApolimesho，你觉得呢？"

    old "I see nothing wrong with Dasyra's plan. If she is now recognized as the legal owner of the brooch, then you should be able to barter it for your friend's freedom."
    new "I see nothing wrong with Dasyra's plan. If she is now recognized as the legal owner of the brooch, then you should be able to barter it for your friend's freedom.\n我看Dasyra的计划没什么不妥。如果她现在被认定为胸针的合法主人，那么你应该能拿它去换你朋友的自由。"

    old "That being said, Edgar has proven himself to be nothing but greedy and dishonest. If you set foot on the Arasmas estate again, who knows what could happen? Edgar could accuse you of trespassing or some other crime, lock you up, and confiscate the brooch."
    new "That being said, Edgar has proven himself to be nothing but greedy and dishonest. If you set foot on the Arasmas estate again, who knows what could happen? Edgar could accuse you of trespassing or some other crime, lock you up, and confiscate the brooch.\n话虽如此，Edgar已经证明了自己贪得无厌、满口谎言。你要是再踏进Arasmas庄园，谁知道会发生什么？Edgar可以指控你非法侵入或别的什么罪名，把你关起来，没收胸针。"

    old "I would recommend that you enter a formal negotiation, mediated by a neutral party. [protag], you're an emissary of the council of Grimoire, and I think that this matter is important enough to qualify as council business."
    new "I would recommend that you enter a formal negotiation, mediated by a neutral party. [protag], you're an emissary of the council of Grimoire, and I think that this matter is important enough to qualify as council business.\n我建议你们进行一场由中立方主持的正式谈判。[protag]，你是Grimoire议会的使者，我认为这件事足够重要，配得上作为议会事务来对待。"

    old "I can write a letter of request to one of the judges in Hammerhands to request formal mediation between you and the Faberge estate."
    new "I can write a letter of request to one of the judges in Hammerhands to request formal mediation between you and the Faberge estate.\n我可以给Hammerhands的一位法官写一封请求信，请求在你和Faberge庄园之间进行正式调解。"

    old "That is, of course, assuming that Dasyra is willing to allow [protag] here to represent her interests in formal mediation. I'm afraid it's necessary in order to justify a request on behalf of the council."
    new "That is, of course, assuming that Dasyra is willing to allow [protag] here to represent her interests in formal mediation. I'm afraid it's necessary in order to justify a request on behalf of the council.\n当然，这得假定Dasyra愿意让[protag]代表她的利益参加正式调解。恐怕这是必要的，以便让代表议会提出的请求师出有名。"

    old "That's not a problem. [protag] here has saved my skin more than once. If I can trust [himher] with my life, I can trust [himher] with my mother's brooch."
    new "That's not a problem. [protag] here has saved my skin more than once. If I can trust [himher] with my life, I can trust [himher] with my mother's brooch.\n那不成问题。这里的[protag]不止一次救过我的命。如果我能把性命托付给[himher]，那我也能把母亲的胸针托付给[himher]。"

    old "If Edgar is as greedy as I think he is, he'll accept the offer for mediation. I'll send my letter along. The mediation session should be ready within several days time. I'll let you know the exact day when I know it."
    new "If Edgar is as greedy as I think he is, he'll accept the offer for mediation. I'll send my letter along. The mediation session should be ready within several days time. I'll let you know the exact day when I know it.\n如果Edgar像我想的那么贪婪，他就会接受调解的提议。我会把信寄出去。调解会应该几天内就能准备就绪。等我知道确切日期，会告诉你。"

    old "Apolimesho, a messenger told us that you wanted to see Dasyra and I?"
    new "Apolimesho, a messenger told us that you wanted to see Dasyra and I?\nApolimesho，有信使说你想见我和Dasyra？"

    old "Yes, it is about the mediation."
    new "Yes, it is about the mediation.\n是的，是关于调解的事。"

    old "Did Edgar accept?"
    new "Did Edgar accept?\nEdgar接受了吗？"

    old "Yes. The mediation will take place next week. I'll send you a messenger to tell the exact day."
    new "Yes. The mediation will take place next week. I'll send you a messenger to tell the exact day.\n接受了。调解下周举行。我会派信使告诉你确切日期。"

    old "Good, I'll write it down so I don't forget about it."
    new "Good, I'll write it down so I don't forget about it.\n好，我把它记下来，免得忘了。"

    old "Thank you Apolimesho for all your help."
    new "Thank you Apolimesho for all your help.\n谢谢你的所有帮助，Apolimesho。"

    old "You're welcome."
    new "You're welcome.\n不客气。"

    old "I arrive with Dasyra at the courthouse appointed for our negotiation with Edgar Arasmas."
    new "I arrive with Dasyra at the courthouse appointed for our negotiation with Edgar Arasmas.\n我和Dasyra来到指定的法院，准备与Edgar Arasmas进行谈判。"

    old "We are standing outside the mediation chamber, waiting for the judge, when our adversary arrives."
    new "We are standing outside the mediation chamber, waiting for the judge, when our adversary arrives.\n我们站在调解庭外等候法官，这时我们的对手到了。"

    old "Ah, Dasyra. So pleasant to see you again."
    new "Ah, Dasyra. So pleasant to see you again.\n啊，Dasyra。再次见到你真高兴。"

    old "The pleasure is all yours, Edgar."
    new "The pleasure is all yours, Edgar.\nEdgar，高兴的只有你一个。"

    old "You two know each other?"
    new "You two know each other?\n你们俩认识？"

    old "Of course Dasyra and I are acquainted. Her mother worked for my father. I remember when you were just a wee girl, Dasyra."
    new "Of course Dasyra and I are acquainted. Her mother worked for my father. I remember when you were just a wee girl, Dasyra.\nDasyra和我当然认识。她母亲给我父亲干过活。我还记得你是个小姑娘的时候呢，Dasyra。"

    old "And I remember when you were an even smaller lad, Edgar. I'm two years older than you. My mother brought me to your newborn ceremony."
    new "And I remember when you were an even smaller lad, Edgar. I'm two years older than you. My mother brought me to your newborn ceremony.\n我也记得你还是个更小的毛头小子的时候，Edgar。我比你大两岁。我母亲带我去过你的新生庆典。"

    old "My, my. Was seeing me for the first time really that memorable? I didn't realize I made such an impression. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised, there's scarcely a woman in this city who can ignore my charms."
    new "My, my. Was seeing me for the first time really that memorable? I didn't realize I made such an impression. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised, there's scarcely a woman in this city who can ignore my charms.\n哎呀，哎呀。第一次见到我真的那么难忘吗？我竟不知道自己给人留下如此深刻的印象。我想我也不该惊讶，这城里几乎没有哪个女人能无视我的魅力。"

    old "Well, you'll find one such woman standing right here."
    new "Well, you'll find one such woman standing right here.\n那你眼前就正好站着这样一个女人。"

    old "Besides, shouldn't a woman like you desire youth? The fact that you are two years my senior hardly seems something to brag about. You'll never win a man's affections by telling him that you're older than him."
    new "Besides, shouldn't a woman like you desire youth? The fact that you are two years my senior hardly seems something to brag about. You'll never win a man's affections by telling him that you're older than him.\n再说，你这样的女人难道不该渴望青春吗？你比我年长两岁，这似乎没什么好炫耀的。你告诉一个男人你比他大，可永远赢不来他的爱慕。"

    old "If you believe that I have any desire to 'win your affections,' you are beyond delusional."
    new "If you believe that I have any desire to 'win your affections,' you are beyond delusional.\n你要是以为我有半点“赢得你爱慕”的念头，那你可是妄想过头了。"

    old "And yet, here you are, ready to meet me as I go to mediate with your companion here. [protag], was it?"
    new "And yet, here you are, ready to meet me as I go to mediate with your companion here. [protag], was it?\n可你还是来了，准备好见我了，就因为我正要去和你的同伴调解。[protag]，对吧？"

    old "That's me."
    new "That's me.\n正是在下。"

    old "Edgar extends a hand. Dasyra opens her mouth to protest, but I take his hand and shake it anyway."
    new "Edgar extends a hand. Dasyra opens her mouth to protest, but I take his hand and shake it anyway.\nEdgar伸出一只手。Dasyra张嘴想要抗议，但我还是握住了他的手。"

    old "I hope we can find common ground."
    new "I hope we can find common ground.\n希望我们能找到共同点。"

    old "Actually, about that. I was hoping that I might negotiate with you regarding the, ahem, item in question before the judge arrives. It might do us some good to get this resolved without the law being involved, eh?"
    new "Actually, about that. I was hoping that I might negotiate with you regarding the, ahem, item in question before the judge arrives. It might do us some good to get this resolved without the law being involved, eh?\n其实，说到这个。我本希望在法官到来之前，就，呃，那件有争议的物品和你先谈谈。不惊动法律就把这事解决，对我们或许都有好处，嗯？"

    old "Well, let's just say that, hypothetically, I were to release one of my prisoners as part of the deal that we negotiate. That would be a bit of an embarrassment for me. Entirely legal, you understand, but a bit questionable to the discerning eyes of other nobles."
    new "Well, let's just say that, hypothetically, I were to release one of my prisoners as part of the deal that we negotiate. That would be a bit of an embarrassment for me. Entirely legal, you understand, but a bit questionable to the discerning eyes of other nobles.\n嗯，这么说吧，假设我要释放我的一名囚犯，作为我们谈成的交易的一部分。那对我来说有点丢脸。你明白的，完全合法，但在其他贵族挑剔的目光下，有点说不过去。"

    old "And what a shame it would be for you to be known as someone who makes shady deals."
    new "And what a shame it would be for you to be known as someone who makes shady deals.\n而被人知道你是个做见不得光交易的人，那该多可惜啊。"

    old "The sarcasm in Dasyra's voice couldn't be thicker."
    new "The sarcasm in Dasyra's voice couldn't be thicker.\nDasyra语气里的讽刺浓得不能再浓了。"

    old "I pride myself on my stellar reputation, despite what you may think of me, Dasyra."
    new "I pride myself on my stellar reputation, despite what you may think of me, Dasyra.\n我一向以自己的良好名声为荣，不管你怎么看我，Dasyra。"

    old "So if we reach an agreement before the judge arrives, you get to save face. What's in it for us, Edgar?"
    new "So if we reach an agreement before the judge arrives, you get to save face. What's in it for us, Edgar?\n所以，如果我们在法官到来前达成协议，你就能保住面子。那我们能得到什么，Edgar？"

    old "Well, I can offer you more favorable terms. I could, for example, offer to release a prisoner of your choosing in exchange for the brooch, and a sizable sum as well. Say, a thousand gold pieces."
    new "Well, I can offer you more favorable terms. I could, for example, offer to release a prisoner of your choosing in exchange for the brooch, and a sizable sum as well. Say, a thousand gold pieces.\n嗯，我可以给你更优厚的条件。比如说，我可以释放一名你指定的囚犯，以换取胸针，外加一笔可观的数目。比如，一千金币。"

    old "If the judge arrives, I may feel...less charitable. I must warn you that I am somewhat renowned for my talent as a negotiator. You may not get terms this favorable once I argue the law. Things may get a bit messier once the judge arrives."
    new "If the judge arrives, I may feel...less charitable. I must warn you that I am somewhat renowned for my talent as a negotiator. You may not get terms this favorable once I argue the law. Things may get a bit messier once the judge arrives.\n要是法官来了，我可能会觉得……不那么慷慨了。我得提醒你，我多少以谈判才华闻名。等我一上法庭讲法律，你可就拿不到这么优厚的条件了。法官一到，事情可能会变得更难看。"

    old "So, what do you say? Handshake deal? Let's settle this on our own. Me and you, right here. No judge. Just an exchange across the table. A thousand gold pieces, and the freedom of your friend, in exchange for that one little trinket."
    new "So, what do you say? Handshake deal? Let's settle this on our own. Me and you, right here. No judge. Just an exchange across the table. A thousand gold pieces, and the freedom of your friend, in exchange for that one little trinket.\n所以，你怎么说？握手成交？我们自己解决。我和你，就在这儿。没有法官。只是桌对面的交换。一千金币，加上你朋友的自由，换那一个小玩意儿。"

    old "We'll take the deal."
    new "We'll take the deal.\n我们接受这笔交易。"

    old "[protag], are you mad? Do you really trust this man to uphold his end of a handshake deal?"
    new "[protag], are you mad? Do you really trust this man to uphold his end of a handshake deal?\n[protag]，你疯了吗？你真信这人会信守一个握手交易？"

    old "No, I don't. Which is why I'm going to have to insist that I see Galan released before we proceed further. Once I see Galan walk free, I'll hand over the brooch for the gold."
    new "No, I don't. Which is why I'm going to have to insist that I see Galan released before we proceed further. Once I see Galan walk free, I'll hand over the brooch for the gold.\n不，我不信。所以我必须坚持，先看到Galan获释，我们再继续。等我看到Galan自由了，我就交出胸针，换取黄金。"

    old "Now, now. Trust is a two-way street, [protag]. I understand that you're reluctant to trust me. But what about me trusting you?"
    new "Now, now. Trust is a two-way street, [protag]. I understand that you're reluctant to trust me. But what about me trusting you?\n哎呀，哎呀。信任是相互的，[protag]。我理解你不愿信任我。但我要信任你呢？"

    old "Here's what I propose. We'll do the exchange in three parts. I'll release your friend. Then you give me the brooch. Then, and only then, will you receive the gold."
    new "Here's what I propose. We'll do the exchange in three parts. I'll release your friend. Then you give me the brooch. Then, and only then, will you receive the gold.\n我的提议是这样。我们把交换分三步进行。我释放你的朋友。然后你把胸针给我。然后，也只有到那时，你才会拿到黄金。"

    old "Fine."
    new "Fine.\n行。"

    old "We walk to the Arasmas gates, led by Edgar, and Dasyra and I wait outside while Edgar enters the estate, presumably to free Galan."
    new "We walk to the Arasmas gates, led by Edgar, and Dasyra and I wait outside while Edgar enters the estate, presumably to free Galan.\n我们由Edgar领着走到Arasmas大门前，Dasyra和我在外面等候，Edgar则进入庄园，想必是去释放Galan。"

    old "I can't believe you're cutting a deal with him now, after all we've been through."
    new "I can't believe you're cutting a deal with him now, after all we've been through.\n我真不敢相信，在经历了这一切之后，你现在居然和他做起了交易。"

    old "You were ready for this, Dasyra. You were ready to trade your brooch for Galan's freedom. That's exactly what we're doing."
    new "You were ready for this, Dasyra. You were ready to trade your brooch for Galan's freedom. That's exactly what we're doing.\nDasyra，你本来就准备好了。你准备拿胸针换Galan的自由。我们现在做的正是这件事。"

    old "I still have a bad feeling about this."
    new "I still have a bad feeling about this.\n我对这事还是有种不祥的预感。"

    old "We wait several minutes in silence, until a guard emerges, leading Galan behind him."
    new "We wait several minutes in silence, until a guard emerges, leading Galan behind him.\n我们默默等了好几分钟，直到一名守卫出现，身后领着Galan。"

    old "Lord Edgar Arasmas has found it in his heart to pardon this man, who is guilty of crimes against the Arasmas house."
    new "Lord Edgar Arasmas has found it in his heart to pardon this man, who is guilty of crimes against the Arasmas house.\nEdgar Arasmas大人发慈悲，赦免了此人，他犯有侵害Arasmas家族的罪行。"

    old "Galan has the look of a defeated man. His arms seem thinner than I remember them, almost as if his muscles have begun to atrophy away due to hunger. How long has it been since your last meal, Galan? I'm not sure I want to know the answer."
    new "Galan has the look of a defeated man. His arms seem thinner than I remember them, almost as if his muscles have begun to atrophy away due to hunger. How long has it been since your last meal, Galan? I'm not sure I want to know the answer.\nGalan看起来像个战败的人。他的手臂比我记忆中的更细，仿佛肌肉已因饥饿而开始萎缩。你上一顿饭是多久以前吃的，Galan？我不确定自己想知道答案。"

    old "Now, I trust that you have something for me as well."
    new "Now, I trust that you have something for me as well.\n那么，我相信你也有东西要给我。"

    old "The guard rests a hand on his hip, and looks at me expectantly."
    new "The guard rests a hand on his hip, and looks at me expectantly.\n守卫把手叉在腰上，满含期待地看着我。"

    old "I look at Dasyra, and she looks down at her feet with a displeased expression."
    new "I look at Dasyra, and she looks down at her feet with a displeased expression.\n我看向Dasyra，她垂下目光看着自己的脚，一脸不悦。"

    old "I produce the brooch from my pocket and hand it to the guard."
    new "I produce the brooch from my pocket and hand it to the guard.\n我从口袋里掏出胸针，交给守卫。"

    old "Ah, a gift for Lord Arasmas, I presume. I will take it to him now. Perhaps he may offer a gift in return."
    new "Ah, a gift for Lord Arasmas, I presume. I will take it to him now. Perhaps he may offer a gift in return.\n啊，我想这是给Arasmas大人的礼物。我现在就拿给他。也许他会回赠一份礼物。"

    old "The guard disappears into the estate's main hall, where I presume his master is waiting."
    new "The guard disappears into the estate's main hall, where I presume his master is waiting.\n守卫消失在庄园的主厅里，我猜他的主子正在那里等着。"

    old "Galan, are you okay? Did they...do anything to you?"
    new "Galan, are you okay? Did they...do anything to you?\nGalan，你没事吧？他们有没有……对你做什么？"

    old "I've been better. But I've been a lot worse, too. There wasn't any torture or things of that sort, if that's what you're asking. But they don't feed their prisoners very well."
    new "I've been better. But I've been a lot worse, too. There wasn't any torture or things of that sort, if that's what you're asking. But they don't feed their prisoners very well.\n我好过，也糟过。没有拷打之类的事，如果你问的是这个。不过他们给囚犯的伙食可不算好。"

    old "We'll get you a hot meal when we're all done here."
    new "We'll get you a hot meal when we're all done here.\n等这里的事办完，我们就给你弄顿热饭。"

    old "Doesn't even need to be a hot meal. It's not hard to beat bread and water."
    new "Doesn't even need to be a hot meal. It's not hard to beat bread and water.\n也用不着是热饭。能比面包和凉水强就不错了。"

    old "We wait outside the gate, and several more minutes pass. I begin to get antsy."
    new "We wait outside the gate, and several more minutes pass. I begin to get antsy.\n我们在大门外等着，又过了好几分钟。我开始坐立不安。"

    old "Gee, I wonder what might be keeping him."
    new "Gee, I wonder what might be keeping him.\n哎呀，真不知道是什么事让他耽搁了。"

    old "Several more minutes pass. A guard emerges."
    new "Several more minutes pass. A guard emerges.\n又过了好几分钟。一名守卫走了出来。"

    old "What are you still doing here?"
    new "What are you still doing here?\n你们还在这里干什么？"

    old "Is there any word from Edgar on the, ah, compensation?"
    new "Is there any word from Edgar on the, ah, compensation?\nEdgar对那，呃，补偿有什么说法吗？"

    old "As I recall, you gave Edgar Arasmas a gift, with the thought that perhaps he might reciprocate. He, however, is under no obligation to do so, and has declined to offer a gift in exchange, as is his right."
    new "As I recall, you gave Edgar Arasmas a gift, with the thought that perhaps he might reciprocate. He, however, is under no obligation to do so, and has declined to offer a gift in exchange, as is his right.\n就我所记得的，你送了Edgar Arasmas一件礼物，想着他也许会回赠。然而，他并没有义务这么做，他已依其权利，拒绝回赠礼物。"

    old "But.."
    new "But..\n可是……"

    old "That's it, [protag]. There's nothing more to be done. This is what happens when you make a handshake deal with a man you know to be dishonest."
    new "That's it, [protag]. There's nothing more to be done. This is what happens when you make a handshake deal with a man you know to be dishonest.\n就是这样了，[protag]。没什么可做的了。你跟一个明知不诚实的人做握手交易，结果就是这样。"

    old "I guess I should have expected this."
    new "I guess I should have expected this.\n我想我早该料到的。"

    old "I'm none too happy about this, but don't feel too bad. After all, we did accomplish our most important goal."
    new "I'm none too happy about this, but don't feel too bad. After all, we did accomplish our most important goal.\n我对此很不高兴，但你也别太难过。毕竟，我们确实达成了最重要的目标。"

    old "If you're all done, I think that Galan would very much like something to eat."
    new "If you're all done, I think that Galan would very much like something to eat.\n如果你们都办完了，我想Galan非常想吃点东西。"

    old "Alright."
    new "Alright.\n好吧。"

    old "I leave the two, promising them to check back in a few days."
    new "I leave the two, promising them to check back in a few days.\n我离开他们俩，答应几天后再来看看。"

    old "I look past the guard, past the gate to the estate. If there are more guards there, I don't see them."
    new "I look past the guard, past the gate to the estate. If there are more guards there, I don't see them.\n我越过守卫，望向庄园的大门。要是那里还有更多守卫，我并没有看见。"

    old "Dasyra, Galan. Please follow my next instructions very carefully."
    new "Dasyra, Galan. Please follow my next instructions very carefully.\nDasyra，Galan。请非常仔细地听我接下来的指示。"

    old "Galan and Dasyra both turn to me with a look of expectation."
    new "Galan and Dasyra both turn to me with a look of expectation.\nGalan和Dasyra都转向我，一脸期待。"

    old "When we're all done here, we'll meet back in Grimoire. Understand?"
    new "When we're all done here, we'll meet back in Grimoire. Understand?\n等这里的事办完，我们在Grimoire碰头。明白吗？"

    old "Galan and Dasyra nod."
    new "Galan and Dasyra nod.\nGalan和Dasyra点了点头。"

    old "I hand the brooch to Dasyra."
    new "I hand the brooch to Dasyra.\n我把胸针递给Dasyra。"

    old "Now, run."
    new "Now, run.\n现在，跑。"

    old "Dasyra takes off running, and Galan begins running behind her, but he loses his balance and tumbles to the ground."
    new "Dasyra takes off running, and Galan begins running behind her, but he loses his balance and tumbles to the ground.\nDasyra拔腿就跑，Galan也跟着跑起来，却失去平衡，摔倒在地上。"

    old "The Arasmas guard reaches for his weapon, but I lunge forward, driving my elbow into his chest, and he's knocked to the ground. He lets out a groan, and I give him a kick in the chest for good measure, then reach down to help Galan off the ground."
    new "The Arasmas guard reaches for his weapon, but I lunge forward, driving my elbow into his chest, and he's knocked to the ground. He lets out a groan, and I give him a kick in the chest for good measure, then reach down to help Galan off the ground.\nArasmas的守卫伸手去摸武器，但我猛冲向前，一肘撞进他的胸口，他被打翻在地。他发出一声呻吟，我又补上一脚踹在他胸口，然后俯身去扶Galan起身。"

    old "My leg. Maybe broken. I don't think it can hold my weight."
    new "My leg. Maybe broken. I don't think it can hold my weight.\n我的腿。可能断了。我想它撑不住我的重量。"

    old "Well then, I guess I'll have to."
    new "Well then, I guess I'll have to.\n那好，看来只好由我来背了。"

    old "[protag]! Behind you!"
    new "[protag]! Behind you!\n[protag]！你身后！"

    old "This time you won't catch me by surprise!"
    new "This time you won't catch me by surprise!\n这次你别想再偷袭到我！"

    old "Quickly, let's dispose of him before running away."
    new "Quickly, let's dispose of him before running away.\n快，趁逃跑之前把他解决掉。"

    old "I'm not dying for a stupid brooch!"
    new "I'm not dying for a stupid brooch!\n我才不会为了一枚破胸针送命！"

    old "Wise choice. Now step aside."
    new "Wise choice. Now step aside.\n聪明的选择。现在让开。"

    old "The guard moves away from us, with no intention of chasing us. However, he might still alert other guards, so we need to move."
    new "The guard moves away from us, with no intention of chasing us. However, he might still alert other guards, so we need to move.\n守卫从我们身边退开，没有追赶的意思。不过，他可能还是会惊动其他守卫，所以我们必须行动了。"

    old "Give me the brooch now!"
    new "Give me the brooch now!\n现在把胸针给我！"

    old "Take it!"
    new "Take it!\n拿去吧！"

    old "Dasyra throws the brooch far away in the opposite direction. The guard is distracted and runs towards the precious jewelry."
    new "Dasyra throws the brooch far away in the opposite direction. The guard is distracted and runs towards the precious jewelry.\nDasyra把胸针朝相反的方向远远扔了出去。守卫分了神，朝那件珍贵的首饰跑去。"

    old "Thanks Dasyra, you probably bought us enough time to escape."
    new "Thanks Dasyra, you probably bought us enough time to escape.\n谢了，Dasyra，你大概为我们争取到了足够的逃跑时间。"

    old "Here we are again. I need your help."
    new "Here we are again. I need your help.\n又到这一步了。我需要你帮忙。"

    old "I crouch down, and help Galan onto my back. He wraps his arms around my shoulders, and I grip him by the thighs, being careful not to put any pressure on his damaged leg."
    new "I crouch down, and help Galan onto my back. He wraps his arms around my shoulders, and I grip him by the thighs, being careful not to put any pressure on his damaged leg.\n我蹲下身，把Galan扶到我背上。他双臂环住我的肩膀，我托住他的大腿，小心不压到他那条受伤的腿。"

    old "As I stand, I'm surprised at how light Galan is. They must have been starving him. No wonder he wasn't able to run and keep his balance. His bones must be as brittle as glass."
    new "As I stand, I'm surprised at how light Galan is. They must have been starving him. No wonder he wasn't able to run and keep his balance. His bones must be as brittle as glass.\n站起身时，我惊讶于Galan竟如此之轻。他们一定一直在饿着他。难怪他跑不起来，也保持不了平衡。他的骨头一定像玻璃一样脆。"

    old "I take off running, and after several twists and turns, I find what seems to be an abandoned alcove in a dark alley. After waiting out the pursuit, we make our way back to the city perimeter, and I find a horse to cart the injured Galan back to Grimoire."
    new "I take off running, and after several twists and turns, I find what seems to be an abandoned alcove in a dark alley. After waiting out the pursuit, we make our way back to the city perimeter, and I find a horse to cart the injured Galan back to Grimoire.\n我拔腿就跑，左拐右拐之后，在一条暗巷里找到一个看似废弃的凹处。等追兵过去之后，我们回到城市边缘，我找到一匹马，把受伤的Galan载回了Grimoire。"

    old "After we arrive in Grimoire, I leave them, with the promise to check back in a few days."
    new "After we arrive in Grimoire, I leave them, with the promise to check back in a few days.\n抵达Grimoire后，我离开他们，答应几天后再来看看。"

    old "I'm sorry, Edgar, but I just can't accept those terms."
    new "I'm sorry, Edgar, but I just can't accept those terms.\n抱歉，Edgar，但我实在无法接受那些条件。"

    old "A thousand gold pieces not enough to sweeten the deal for you? Fine. Fifteen hundred."
    new "A thousand gold pieces not enough to sweeten the deal for you? Fine. Fifteen hundred.\n一千金币还不够让你动心？行。一千五。"

    old "No."
    new "No.\n不行。"

    old "Two thousand."
    new "Two thousand.\n两千。"

    old "Name your price, then."
    new "Name your price, then.\n那就开个价吧。"

    old "I'll begin naming prices once the judge arrives to mediate our disagreement."
    new "I'll begin naming prices once the judge arrives to mediate our disagreement.\n等法官来主持调解我们的分歧，我再开始开价。"

    old "That does not strike me as wise. You are leaving a lot of money on the table."
    new "That does not strike me as wise. You are leaving a lot of money on the table.\n这在我看来并不明智。你这是把一大笔钱白白留在桌上。"

    old "Edgar, a handshake deal is good only insofar as both parties can trust each other. And I am hard-pressed to think of a dwarf that I trust less than I trust you. There's a reason that we're meeting you here, on neutral territory, for mediation. Let the judge do his job."
    new "Edgar, a handshake deal is good only insofar as both parties can trust each other. And I am hard-pressed to think of a dwarf that I trust less than I trust you. There's a reason that we're meeting you here, on neutral territory, for mediation. Let the judge do his job.\nEdgar，握手交易只有在双方互相信任时才成立。而要我想出一个比你还让我信不过的矮人，我实在想不出来。我们约在这个中立的地方见面调解，是有原因的。让法官做他的工作吧。"

    old "You're going to wish that you hadn't said that."
    new "You're going to wish that you hadn't said that.\n你会后悔说过这话的。"

    old "I guess we'll find out when the judge arrives."
    new "I guess we'll find out when the judge arrives.\n我想等法官到了，我们自然见分晓。"

    old "Final offer. Five thousand gold pieces and your friend's freedom for the brooch. If you don't accept this deal, I will make you regret it."
    new "Final offer. Five thousand gold pieces and your friend's freedom for the brooch. If you don't accept this deal, I will make you regret it.\n最后报价。五千金币，加上你朋友的自由，换那枚胸针。你要是不接受这笔交易，我会让你后悔的。"

    old "Not a chance in hell, Edgar."
    new "Not a chance in hell, Edgar.\n绝无可能，Edgar。"

    old "So, now you're threatening me? I can't imagine why I find myself not inclined to make a handshake deal with a man who has just threatened to 'make me regret it' if I reject his offer."
    new "So, now you're threatening me? I can't imagine why I find myself not inclined to make a handshake deal with a man who has just threatened to 'make me regret it' if I reject his offer.\n所以，你现在是在威胁我了？我实在想不明白，一个刚威胁我“会让我后悔”的人，我怎么会愿意跟他做握手交易。"

    old "Several minutes pass as we eye each other silently. The judge arrives, exactly at the scheduled time."
    new "Several minutes pass as we eye each other silently. The judge arrives, exactly at the scheduled time.\n我们默默对视，好几分钟过去了。法官准时到达。"

    old "Edgar Arasmas, and [protag] of Grimoire, I presume?"
    new "Edgar Arasmas, and [protag] of Grimoire, I presume?\nEdgar Arasmas，还有Grimoire的[protag]，对吧？"

    old "Edgar steps forward to shake the judge's hand."
    new "Edgar steps forward to shake the judge's hand.\nEdgar上前与法官握手。"

    old "Your Honor, I am nobleman Arasmas, and this here is [protag] of Grimoire. Thank you so much for taking time out of your busy schedule to mediate this appointment. I am profusely grateful."
    new "Your Honor, I am nobleman Arasmas, and this here is [protag] of Grimoire. Thank you so much for taking time out of your busy schedule to mediate this appointment. I am profusely grateful.\n法官大人，我是贵族Arasmas，这位是Grimoire的[protag]。万分感谢您从百忙之中抽出时间来主持这次调解。我感激不尽。"

    old "Maybe you should save your gratitude until after we reach an arrangment. Let's get this underway, shall we?"
    new "Maybe you should save your gratitude until after we reach an arrangment. Let's get this underway, shall we?\n你也许该把感激留到达成协议之后。我们开始吧，好吗？"

    old "Now, my understanding is that this negotation is concerning primarily a personal effect of some sort?"
    new "Now, my understanding is that this negotation is concerning primarily a personal effect of some sort?\n那么，据我了解，这场谈判主要涉及某种个人物品？"

    old "That's right, Your Honor."
    new "That's right, Your Honor.\n没错，法官大人。"

    old "Well, let's see it."
    new "Well, let's see it.\n好，我们来看看。"

    old "I produce Dasyra's brooch from my pocket and place it on a table at the center of the room."
    new "I produce Dasyra's brooch from my pocket and place it on a table at the center of the room.\n我从口袋里掏出Dasyra的胸针，放在房间中央的桌上。"

    old "Your Honor, the nature of this disagreement will become apparent if we inspect the item itself. You see, this brooch is the handiwork of my father, the famous Faberge Arasmas."
    new "Your Honor, the nature of this disagreement will become apparent if we inspect the item itself. You see, this brooch is the handiwork of my father, the famous Faberge Arasmas.\n法官大人，只要我们检查一下物品本身，这场分歧的性质就会一目了然。您看，这枚胸针正是我父亲、著名的Faberge Arasmas的手艺。"

    old "Is this true?"
    new "Is this true?\n这是真的吗？"

    old "As far as we know, yes. This brooch was created by Faberge."
    new "As far as we know, yes. This brooch was created by Faberge.\n就我们所知，是的。这枚胸针是Faberge打造的。"

    old "So, Edgar. Do you have a point with this?"
    new "So, Edgar. Do you have a point with this?\n那么，Edgar。你说这个，是想说明什么？"

    old "It is my intention to prove that this brooch rightfully belongs to my estate, and that this dwarf woman and her companion have no rightful claim to it."
    new "It is my intention to prove that this brooch rightfully belongs to my estate, and that this dwarf woman and her companion have no rightful claim to it.\n我的意图是证明，这枚胸针理应属于我的庄园，而这个矮人女子和她的同伴对它的任何主张都不合法。"

    old "Edgar, the fact that your father made this brooch doesn't tell us anything about its ownership. Faberge was a jeweler. He made many similar effects, which he then sold. That is how the construction of jewelry typically works."
    new "Edgar, the fact that your father made this brooch doesn't tell us anything about its ownership. Faberge was a jeweler. He made many similar effects, which he then sold. That is how the construction of jewelry typically works.\nEdgar，你父亲打造了这枚胸针这一事实，并不能说明它的所有权归属。Faberge是珠宝商。他做过许多类似的物件，然后出售。珠宝的制作通常就是如此。"

    old "[protag], just so that we can be clear, how did this item come into the possession of the party you are representing?"
    new "[protag], just so that we can be clear, how did this item come into the possession of the party you are representing?\n[protag]，为了把事情说清楚，这件物品是如何落到你代理的一方手中的？"

    old "Perhaps Dasyra here would be best qualified to answer that question."
    new "Perhaps Dasyra here would be best qualified to answer that question.\n也许让Dasyra本人来回答这个问题最合适。"

    old "The brooch was a gift, from Faberge to my mother. My mother worked on his estate for many years, a fact which Edgar himself should be able to verify."
    new "The brooch was a gift, from Faberge to my mother. My mother worked on his estate for many years, a fact which Edgar himself should be able to verify.\n这枚胸针是一件礼物，是Faberge送给我母亲的。我母亲在他的庄园里工作多年，这一事实Edgar本人应该能够证实。"

    old "That Dasyra's mother worked for my father is a well-known fact. And I do not intend to dispute that my father created this brooch as a gift. However, I am confident that upon inspecting this brooch, we will discover that Dasyra is quite delusional in claiming that it was a gift for her mother."
    new "That Dasyra's mother worked for my father is a well-known fact. And I do not intend to dispute that my father created this brooch as a gift. However, I am confident that upon inspecting this brooch, we will discover that Dasyra is quite delusional in claiming that it was a gift for her mother.\nDasyra的母亲为我父亲工作是众所周知的事实。我也无意否认我父亲打造这枚胸针作为礼物。然而，我有信心，只要检查这枚胸针，我们就会发现，Dasyra声称这是送给她母亲的礼物，纯属妄想。"

    old "Your Honor, I will allow you to do the honors and inspect the brooch for yourself."
    new "Your Honor, I will allow you to do the honors and inspect the brooch for yourself.\n法官大人，就请您亲自检查这枚胸针吧。"

    old "Edgar reaches into his pocket and pulls out a small object shaped like a pen."
    new "Edgar reaches into his pocket and pulls out a small object shaped like a pen.\nEdgar把手伸进口袋，掏出一个笔形的小物件。"

    old "My father stamped all of his commercial works with his name. That is standard practice for any jeweler. However, what is not commonly known is that my father also stamped pieces that he handed out as gifts. The stamping he applied to gifts was much more subtle: so subtle, in fact, that it can only be observed using this tool which my father created."
    new "My father stamped all of his commercial works with his name. That is standard practice for any jeweler. However, what is not commonly known is that my father also stamped pieces that he handed out as gifts. The stamping he applied to gifts was much more subtle: so subtle, in fact, that it can only be observed using this tool which my father created.\n我父亲会在他所有的商业作品上盖他的名字。这是任何珠宝商的标准做法。然而，不为人所知的是，我父亲也会在他作为礼物送出的物件上盖章。他用于礼物的印章要隐蔽得多：事实上，隐蔽到只有用我父亲发明的这件工具才能看到。"

    old "Edgar presses down on the base of the pen-like object, and a blue flame comes out."
    new "Edgar presses down on the base of the pen-like object, and a blue flame comes out.\nEdgar按下那个笔形物件的底部，一道蓝色火焰喷了出来。"

    old "Your Honor, if you use the light from this specially-crafted instrument, you should be able to read some lettering on the back of the brooch."
    new "Your Honor, if you use the light from this specially-crafted instrument, you should be able to read some lettering on the back of the brooch.\n法官大人，用这件特制仪器发出的光，您应该能读到胸针背面的一些铭文。"

    old "The judge takes the lighter from Edgar, and holds it up to the brooch, turning it over in his hand. From the lighter's blue glow, lettering becomes visible."
    new "The judge takes the lighter from Edgar, and holds it up to the brooch, turning it over in his hand. From the lighter's blue glow, lettering becomes visible.\n法官从Edgar手中接过打火机，举到胸针旁，把胸针在手中翻转。借着打火机的蓝光，铭文显现了出来。"

    old "It says here....ahem. 'To my dearest, my lover, the mother of my child.'"
    new "It says here....ahem. 'To my dearest, my lover, the mother of my child.'\n上面写着……咳咳。“致我最亲爱的人，我的爱人，我孩子的母亲。”"

    old "Now, who else could this brooch have been made for, but my mother? Faberge clearly addressed this to 'the mother of his child.' He had only one child, me. Your Honor, I don't believe that I should need to explain further."
    new "Now, who else could this brooch have been made for, but my mother? Faberge clearly addressed this to 'the mother of his child.' He had only one child, me. Your Honor, I don't believe that I should need to explain further.\n那么，除了我母亲，这枚胸针还能是为谁打造的呢？Faberge明明白白把它题赠给“他孩子的母亲”。他只有一个孩子，就是我。法官大人，我想我不必再解释下去了。"

    old "This is...quite unexpected. [protag], do you have anything to say in response?"
    new "This is...quite unexpected. [protag], do you have anything to say in response?\n这……实在出人意料。[protag]，你有什么要回应的吗？"

    old "Forgive me, Your Honor, but I would like to see the lettering for myself. Edgar, do you mind?"
    new "Forgive me, Your Honor, but I would like to see the lettering for myself. Edgar, do you mind?\n请原谅，法官大人，我想亲眼看看那行铭文。Edgar，你介意吗？"

    old "Not at all."
    new "Not at all.\n一点也不。"

    old "I pick up the brooch, and inspect it by the light of Edgar's blue flame. The lettering is as the judge read it. 'To my dearest, my lover, the mother of my child.'"
    new "I pick up the brooch, and inspect it by the light of Edgar's blue flame. The lettering is as the judge read it. 'To my dearest, my lover, the mother of my child.'\n我拿起胸针，借着Edgar蓝色火焰的光检查。铭文正如法官所读。“致我最亲爱的人，我的爱人，我孩子的母亲。”"

    old "Of course, it seems only fair that Edgar should be able to verify the lettering himself."
    new "Of course, it seems only fair that Edgar should be able to verify the lettering himself.\n当然，让Edgar本人也能核实铭文，才显得公平。"

    old "I hand the brooch to Edgar. He accepts it, and it begins emitting a faint glow."
    new "I hand the brooch to Edgar. He accepts it, and it begins emitting a faint glow.\n我把胸针递给Edgar。他接过去，它开始泛起微弱的光。"

    old "Now, that's interesting. Edgar, were you planning to tell us about this feature of the brooch? It seems to have a natural affinity for you."
    new "Now, that's interesting. Edgar, were you planning to tell us about this feature of the brooch? It seems to have a natural affinity for you.\n这可就有意思了。Edgar，你打算跟我们说说胸针的这个特性吗？它似乎对你有天然的亲和力。"

    old "Edgar turns the brooch over in his hands with a look of surprise."
    new "Edgar turns the brooch over in his hands with a look of surprise.\nEdgar把胸针在手里翻转，一脸惊讶。"

    old "Edgar, is this phenomenon something you recognize? You are familiar with jewelry through your father's work, aren't you?"
    new "Edgar, is this phenomenon something you recognize? You are familiar with jewelry through your father's work, aren't you?\nEdgar，这种现象你认识吗？通过你父亲的工作，你对珠宝很熟悉，对吧？"

    old "Yes, I am, but I've never seen anything like this."
    new "Yes, I am, but I've never seen anything like this.\n熟悉，但我从没见过这样的事。"

    old "Does the word 'resonator' mean anything to you?"
    new "Does the word 'resonator' mean anything to you?\n“共鸣器”这个词，对你有意义吗？"

    old "Edgar snaps his fingers and nods."
    new "Edgar snaps his fingers and nods.\nEdgar打了个响指，点了点头。"

    old "Yes. Now I understand. Your Honor, a resonator is a jewel which is assembled through, well, a bit of witchcraft and a bit of craftsmanship on the part of a jeweler."
    new "Yes. Now I understand. Your Honor, a resonator is a jewel which is assembled through, well, a bit of witchcraft and a bit of craftsmanship on the part of a jeweler.\n对。现在我明白了。法官大人，共鸣器是一种宝石，它的组装需要，嗯，一点巫术，再加上珠宝商的一点手艺。"

    old "Witchcraft, you say?"
    new "Witchcraft, you say?\n巫术，你说？"

    old "The technique used to create the jewel is not the issue."
    new "The technique used to create the jewel is not the issue.\n打造这颗宝石所用的技术，不是问题所在。"

    old "Your Honor, as I said, this brooch was a gift to my mother. I had never discovered it until now, but I now believe that this brooch was actually enchanted with some of my mother's person. Perhaps a hair, or some of her spit. Whatever the case, this special gift to my mother had unique magical properties which only she could unlock."
    new "Your Honor, as I said, this brooch was a gift to my mother. I had never discovered it until now, but I now believe that this brooch was actually enchanted with some of my mother's person. Perhaps a hair, or some of her spit. Whatever the case, this special gift to my mother had unique magical properties which only she could unlock.\n法官大人，正如我所说，这枚胸针是送给我母亲的礼物。我直到现在才发现，但我现在相信，这枚胸针实际上被附上了我母亲的某些部分。也许是一根头发，或者是她的一点唾液。无论如何，这件送给我母亲的特别礼物，有着只有她才能解锁的独特魔法属性。"

    old "I, being the son of my mother, am slightly attuned to the brooch myself. That is why it glows at my touch, when it did not react to either you or [protag]."
    new "I, being the son of my mother, am slightly attuned to the brooch myself. That is why it glows at my touch, when it did not react to either you or [protag].\n我，作为我母亲的儿子，自己与这枚胸针也有几分契合。所以它才会在我的触碰下发亮，而对您或[protag]却没有反应。"

    old "Interesting. [protag], since you were the one to bring up the concept of this 'resonator,' do you agree with Edgar's reasoning here?"
    new "Interesting. [protag], since you were the one to bring up the concept of this 'resonator,' do you agree with Edgar's reasoning here?\n有意思。[protag]，既然是你提出了“共鸣器”这个概念，你同意Edgar这里的推论吗？"

    old "Partly, Your Honor. It is true that resonators are magical items attuned to a specific owner, and some of the magical attunement may be hereditary. As you've seen, this brooch reacts to Edgar, but not to me or you. However, there is someone else in this room who hasn't had a chance to touch the brooch. With your permission, I'd like to allow Dasyra the opportunity."
    new "Partly, Your Honor. It is true that resonators are magical items attuned to a specific owner, and some of the magical attunement may be hereditary. As you've seen, this brooch reacts to Edgar, but not to me or you. However, there is someone else in this room who hasn't had a chance to touch the brooch. With your permission, I'd like to allow Dasyra the opportunity.\n部分同意，法官大人。共鸣器确实是与特定主人相契合的魔法物品，而其中部分契合是遗传的。正如您所见，这枚胸针对Edgar有反应，对您和我却没有。不过，这房间里还有一个人没碰过胸针。承蒙允许，我想给Dasyra这个机会。"

    old "I'll allow it."
    new "I'll allow it.\n我准了。"

    old "Dasyra steps forward and clasps the brooch in her hands. It begins to glow, even more radiantly than when Edgar held it."
    new "Dasyra steps forward and clasps the brooch in her hands. It begins to glow, even more radiantly than when Edgar held it.\nDasyra走上前，双手握住胸针。它开始发光，比Edgar握着时更加耀眼。"

    old "What in the...Your Honor, this must be some kind of trickery."
    new "What in the...Your Honor, this must be some kind of trickery.\n这……法官大人，这一定是某种障眼法。"

    old "Dasyra sets the brooch down, and its glow fades. Then she rests a finger on it, and it begins to glow again."
    new "Dasyra sets the brooch down, and its glow fades. Then she rests a finger on it, and it begins to glow again.\nDasyra放下胸针，它的光芒黯淡下去。然后她把一根手指搭在上面，它又开始发光。"

    old "It seems to be reacting to her touch, just as it reacted to your touch, Edgar. I perceive no tricks being played here."
    new "It seems to be reacting to her touch, just as it reacted to your touch, Edgar. I perceive no tricks being played here.\n它似乎在对她的触碰产生反应，正如对你的触碰一样，Edgar。我看不出这里有什么障眼法。"

    old "Your Honor, this is not my first time seeing the brooch react to Dasyra like this. At the time, Dasyra explained to me that the brooch had belonged to her mother. I assumed, based on the fact that Dasyra had some affinity for the brooch due to the hereditary nature of that affinity, that she had inherited that from her mother."
    new "Your Honor, this is not my first time seeing the brooch react to Dasyra like this. At the time, Dasyra explained to me that the brooch had belonged to her mother. I assumed, based on the fact that Dasyra had some affinity for the brooch due to the hereditary nature of that affinity, that she had inherited that from her mother.\n法官大人，这不是我第一次看到胸针对Dasyra有这样的反应。当时Dasyra向我解释说，胸针曾属于她母亲。我基于Dasyra因这种契合的遗传性而对胸针有几分亲和，推断她是从她母亲那里继承了这一点。"

    old "Edgar here observed his own reaction to the brooch, and decided that he must have inherited that affinity from his mother."
    new "Edgar here observed his own reaction to the brooch, and decided that he must have inherited that affinity from his mother.\nEdgar在这里观察到了自己对胸针的反应，便断定他一定是从他母亲那里继承了这种亲和。"

    old "Clearly, both of these theories must be wrong. Edgar and Dasyra have different mothers. If the brooch was attuned to Edgar's mother, then it would not react to Dasyra. And if it had been attuned to Dasyra's mother, then it would not react to Edgar."
    new "Clearly, both of these theories must be wrong. Edgar and Dasyra have different mothers. If the brooch was attuned to Edgar's mother, then it would not react to Dasyra. And if it had been attuned to Dasyra's mother, then it would not react to Edgar.\n显然，这两个理论必然都是错的。Edgar和Dasyra有不同的母亲。如果胸针与Edgar的母亲相契合，它就不会对Dasyra有反应。如果它与Dasyra的母亲相契合，它就不会对Edgar有反应。"

    old "Both Dasyra and Edgar have an affinity for this brooch. They must have inherited that affinity from the same parent."
    new "Both Dasyra and Edgar have an affinity for this brooch. They must have inherited that affinity from the same parent.\nDasyra和Edgar都对这枚胸针有亲和力。他们一定是从同一位父母那里继承了这种亲和。"

    old "Are you saying that..."
    new "Are you saying that...\n你是说……"

    old "I am saying that both Edgar and Dasyra have the same father. This brooch is proof."
    new "I am saying that both Edgar and Dasyra have the same father. This brooch is proof.\n我是说，Edgar和Dasyra有同一个父亲。这枚胸针就是证据。"

    old "Fine. Your Honor, I am willing to accept [protag]'s theory here. However, that doesn't change the facts of this case at all. It simply means that my father attuned the brooch to himself before gifting it to my mother, or Dasyra's. We can't determine at this point."
    new "Fine. Your Honor, I am willing to accept [protag]'s theory here. However, that doesn't change the facts of this case at all. It simply means that my father attuned the brooch to himself before gifting it to my mother, or Dasyra's. We can't determine at this point.\n好。法官大人，我愿意接受[protag]的理论。然而，这丝毫改变不了本案的事实。这只不过说明，我父亲在把它送给我母亲、或Dasyra的母亲之前，先让胸针与他自己相契合了。这点我们现在无法确定。"

    old "However, consider this, Your Honor: I knew of the writing on the back of the brooch, even as it was in [protag] and Dasyra's possession. How could I have known this, unless I had access to the brooch prior? Your Honor, I submit this claim: I had prior ownership of this brooch. I inherited it as part of my father's estate. These two stole it from me."
    new "However, consider this, Your Honor: I knew of the writing on the back of the brooch, even as it was in [protag] and Dasyra's possession. How could I have known this, unless I had access to the brooch prior? Your Honor, I submit this claim: I had prior ownership of this brooch. I inherited it as part of my father's estate. These two stole it from me.\n不过，法官大人，请想想这一点：即便胸针在[protag]和Dasyra手中，我也知道它背面的铭文。除非我此前接触过这枚胸针，否则我怎么会知道？法官大人，我提出如下主张：我曾是这枚胸针的先前所有者。我把它作为父亲庄园的一部分继承了下来。是这两个人从我这里偷走了它。"

    old "Edgar, I think that you may be missing the larger issue here."
    new "Edgar, I think that you may be missing the larger issue here.\nEdgar，我想你可能忽略了这里更大的问题。"

    old "Which is...?"
    new "Which is...?\n什么问题……？"

    old "Edgar, how did you come to inherit your father's estate? Was it willed to you?"
    new "Edgar, how did you come to inherit your father's estate? Was it willed to you?\nEdgar，你是怎么继承你父亲庄园的？是遗赠给你的吗？"

    old "We never found my dear father's last will and testament, rest his soul. By rules of inheritance, his estate is bequeathed to his eldest child by default. That would be me."
    new "We never found my dear father's last will and testament, rest his soul. By rules of inheritance, his estate is bequeathed to his eldest child by default. That would be me.\n我们从未找到我敬爱父亲的最后遗嘱，愿他安息。按照继承规则，他的庄园默认传给最大的孩子。那就是我。"

    old "Your Honor, until now, it was assumed that Faberge Arasmas had only one child. Edgar. But today, through this brooch, we have established that he fathered not one, but two children. Dasyra has just as strong an affinity to Faberge's resonator as Edgar."
    new "Your Honor, until now, it was assumed that Faberge Arasmas had only one child. Edgar. But today, through this brooch, we have established that he fathered not one, but two children. Dasyra has just as strong an affinity to Faberge's resonator as Edgar.\n法官大人，直到现在，人们一直以为Faberge Arasmas只有一个孩子。Edgar。但今天，通过这枚胸针，我们确定了，他生下的不是一个，而是两个孩子。Dasyra与Faberge的共鸣器的亲和力，和Edgar一样强。"

    old "Edgar, you said it yourself. I am two years your elder."
    new "Edgar, you said it yourself. I am two years your elder.\nEdgar，你自己说过。我比你大两岁。"

    old "And that means, that by rules of inheritance..."
    new "And that means, that by rules of inheritance...\n而这意味着，按照继承规则……"

    old "That means that you are not your father's heir, Edgar. By birth right, his estate should have been left to Dasyra here."
    new "That means that you are not your father's heir, Edgar. By birth right, his estate should have been left to Dasyra here.\n也就是说，你不是你父亲的继承人，Edgar。按出身而言，他的庄园本该留给这里的Dasyra。"

    old "That's absurd. Your Honor, Dasyra here is a bastard, an embarrassment to the Faberge name. That he sired a child with one of his maids is something that he would have endeavored hard to keep secret. My father explicitly willed the majority of his estate to me."
    new "That's absurd. Your Honor, Dasyra here is a bastard, an embarrassment to the Faberge name. That he sired a child with one of his maids is something that he would have endeavored hard to keep secret. My father explicitly willed the majority of his estate to me.\n荒谬。法官大人，这里的Dasyra是个私生女，是Faberge这个姓氏的耻辱。他和一个女仆生下孩子这种事，他一定会竭力保密。我父亲明确把庄园的大部分遗赠给了我。"

    old "If that's the case, then produce the will and testament to prove it."
    new "If that's the case, then produce the will and testament to prove it.\n如果真是这样，那就拿出遗嘱来证明。"

    old "That's impossible. That document was destroyed."
    new "That's impossible. That document was destroyed.\n不可能。那份文件被销毁了。"

    old "Edgar, how did you know that your father's will was destroyed?"
    new "Edgar, how did you know that your father's will was destroyed?\nEdgar，你怎么知道你父亲的遗嘱被销毁了？"

    old "Your Honor, I misspoke. His will was lost. Never found. But if it were here today, it would prove that my father intended for me to be the rightful heir of his primary estate. There were smaller properties bequeathed to others, but the house of Arasmas belongs to me."
    new "Your Honor, I misspoke. His will was lost. Never found. But if it were here today, it would prove that my father intended for me to be the rightful heir of his primary estate. There were smaller properties bequeathed to others, but the house of Arasmas belongs to me.\n法官大人，我说错了。他的遗嘱是遗失了。从未找到。但如果今天在这里，它会证明我父亲打算让我成为主要庄园的合法继承人。还有一些较小的财产遗赠给了别人，但Arasmas的家宅是属于我的。"

    old "For a document that was lost and never found, you certainly seem to know a lot about it, Edgar."
    new "For a document that was lost and never found, you certainly seem to know a lot about it, Edgar.\n对于一份遗失、从未找到的文件，你似乎对它了解得不少啊，Edgar。"

    old "Your Honor-"
    new "Your Honor-\n法官大人——"

    old "You've already dug yourself into a deep enough hole, Edgar. Let me tell you what I see here. I believe that you are right: your father did everything he could to keep his bastard child secret from the outside world. He kept her identity hidden from everyone. Including both you and her."
    new "You've already dug yourself into a deep enough hole, Edgar. Let me tell you what I see here. I believe that you are right: your father did everything he could to keep his bastard child secret from the outside world. He kept her identity hidden from everyone. Including both you and her.\n你已经给自己挖了够深的坑了，Edgar。让我告诉你我看到了什么。我相信你说得对：你父亲想尽一切办法，让他的私生子对外界保密。他对所有人隐瞒了她的身份。包括你和她。"

    old "You believed you were an only child, and as his only legitimate child, your father intended to leave behind his estate to you. Of course, certain portions of it were bequeathed to others as well."
    new "You believed you were an only child, and as his only legitimate child, your father intended to leave behind his estate to you. Of course, certain portions of it were bequeathed to others as well.\n你一直以为自己是独生子，而作为他唯一名正言顺的孩子，你父亲本打算把庄园留给你。当然，其中某些部分也遗赠给了别人。"

    old "Had you simply allowed his last will and testament to be discovered and read, you would have inherited the majority of your father's riches. However, a majority was not enough for you. You wanted all of it. And you presumed that if you destroyed his will, the rule of inheritance would allow you to reap it all for yourself."
    new "Had you simply allowed his last will and testament to be discovered and read, you would have inherited the majority of your father's riches. However, a majority was not enough for you. You wanted all of it. And you presumed that if you destroyed his will, the rule of inheritance would allow you to reap it all for yourself.\n要是你任由他的最后遗嘱被发现并宣读，你本可以继承你父亲的大部分财富。然而，大部分对你来说还不够。你想要全部。你断定，只要毁了他的遗嘱，继承规则就能让你把一切都据为己有。"

    old "What you didn't expect was that the rule of inheritance, the rule which you used to legally steal from your father's other heirs would backfire so drastically."
    new "What you didn't expect was that the rule of inheritance, the rule which you used to legally steal from your father's other heirs would backfire so drastically.\n你没料到的是，继承规则——那条被你用来合法窃取你父亲其他继承人财产的规则——竟会如此狠狠地反噬。"

    old "Dasyra, your father's estate should rightfully belong to you. I am going to open the events of this mediation up to public record. To retroactively reassign an inheritance years after a man's death, and reassign this amount of wealth, is no small task. This process will take many days, possibly weeks or months."
    new "Dasyra, your father's estate should rightfully belong to you. I am going to open the events of this mediation up to public record. To retroactively reassign an inheritance years after a man's death, and reassign this amount of wealth, is no small task. This process will take many days, possibly weeks or months.\nDasyra，你父亲的庄园理应属于你。我会把这次调解的全过程纳入公开记录。要在一个男人去世多年后追溯性地重新分配一笔遗产、并重新分配这么大一笔财富，绝非易事。这个过程需要许多天，可能要几周甚至几个月。"

    old "But as a servant of justice and a servant of the law, I will make sure that this is made right. You are, of course, free to leave, but I suggest that you remain in Hammerhands until it is complete."
    new "But as a servant of justice and a servant of the law, I will make sure that this is made right. You are, of course, free to leave, but I suggest that you remain in Hammerhands until it is complete.\n但作为正义与法律的仆人，我会确保这件事得到纠正。你当然可以自由离开，但我建议你留在Hammerhands，直到事情办完。"

    old "Thank you, Your Honor."
    new "Thank you, Your Honor.\n谢谢你，法官大人。"

    old "Edgar storms away, furious, without a word."
    new "Edgar storms away, furious, without a word.\nEdgar怒气冲冲地拂袖而去，一言不发。"

    old "[protag], thank you. I guess I'll need to stay here for a while."
    new "[protag], thank you. I guess I'll need to stay here for a while.\n[protag]，谢谢你。我想我得在这里待上一阵了。"

    old "I'll come back and check with you in a couple of days to see how things go."
    new "I'll come back and check with you in a couple of days to see how things go.\n过几天我会回来找你，看看进展如何。"

    old "Good. However, if you need me in some mission, don't be afraid to ask for my help."
    new "Good. However, if you need me in some mission, don't be afraid to ask for my help.\n好。不过，如果你在什么任务中需要我，别不敢开口求助。"

    old "Don't worry. Even in your absence I'll make sure things keep going."
    new "Don't worry. Even in your absence I'll make sure things keep going.\n别担心。即便你不在，我也会确保一切照常推进。"

    old "Good. I'll be leaving you two now."
    new "Good. I'll be leaving you two now.\n好。那我先离开你们俩了。"

    old "I am surprised to find Dasyra back in Grimoire so soon."
    new "I am surprised to find Dasyra back in Grimoire so soon.\n我惊讶地发现Dasyra这么快就回到了Grimoire。"

    old "[protag], so good to see you again."
    new "[protag], so good to see you again.\n[protag]，再次见到你真好。"

    old "Hello, Dasyra. Or should I say, Lady Arasmas?"
    new "Hello, Dasyra. Or should I say, Lady Arasmas?\n你好，Dasyra。还是我该说，Arasmas夫人？"

    old "I guess that's who I am now, isn't it? I wish the title suited me better. I certainly don't feel like a proper lady, even less than Edgar was a proper lord."
    new "I guess that's who I am now, isn't it? I wish the title suited me better. I certainly don't feel like a proper lady, even less than Edgar was a proper lord.\n我想那确实是我现在的身份了，不是吗？我真希望这头衔更适合我。我一点也不觉得自己像个正经的贵妇，甚至比Edgar当正经老爷时还差得远。"

    old "What's become of Edgar, anyway?"
    new "What's become of Edgar, anyway?\n话说回来，Edgar后来怎么样了？"

    old "Oh, he plundered the Arasmas estate, took what money he could find, and made off into the night. I'm not sure there's much that can be done to find him now, though at least we can be fairly confident that he won't be coming back again."
    new "Oh, he plundered the Arasmas estate, took what money he could find, and made off into the night. I'm not sure there's much that can be done to find him now, though at least we can be fairly confident that he won't be coming back again.\n哦，他洗劫了Arasmas庄园，卷走了能弄到的钱，连夜潜逃了。现在想再找到他，恐怕没什么办法了，不过至少我们可以相当肯定，他不会再回来了。"

    old "So, you're in charge of the Arasmas estate right now?"
    new "So, you're in charge of the Arasmas estate right now?\n所以，现在由你掌管Arasmas庄园？"

    old "Not entirely. The court currently has custody of the estate, but control is being transferred to me, bit by bit. It will take months, as the judge said. Meanwhile, I'll be staying here in Grimoire."
    new "Not entirely. The court currently has custody of the estate, but control is being transferred to me, bit by bit. It will take months, as the judge said. Meanwhile, I'll be staying here in Grimoire.\n不完全是。法庭目前托管着庄园，但控制权正一点一点移交给我。正如法官所说，这需要几个月。同时，我会留在Grimoire。"

    old "Of course, my first action as Lady Arasmas was to go to the dungeon and have someone released."
    new "Of course, my first action as Lady Arasmas was to go to the dungeon and have someone released.\n当然，我作为Arasmas夫人的第一件事，就是去地牢里释放一个人。"

    old "Hello, [protag]."
    new "Hello, [protag].\n你好，[protag]。"

    old "Galan!"
    new "Galan!\nGalan！"

    old "What a ride this has been. I never imagined when I stopped to assist a damsel in distress that she'd turn out to be a noble lady."
    new "What a ride this has been. I never imagined when I stopped to assist a damsel in distress that she'd turn out to be a noble lady.\n这一路可真够曲折的。我当初停下来救一个落难的姑娘时，从没想过她竟会是一位贵族小姐。"

    old "Neither did I."
    new "Neither did I.\n我也没想过。"

    old "And me least of all."
    new "And me least of all.\n最没想过的就是我了。"

    old "Dasyra begins laughing, and her contagious laughter infects me and Galan as well."
    new "Dasyra begins laughing, and her contagious laughter infects me and Galan as well.\nDasyra笑了起来，她那富有感染力的笑声也感染了我和Galan。"

    old "Dasyra told me about your mission. About how you're fighting the undead of N'Mar. I'd like to help."
    new "Dasyra told me about your mission. About how you're fighting the undead of N'Mar. I'd like to help.\nDasyra跟我讲了你的任务。讲了你们如何与N'Mar的亡灵战斗。我想帮忙。"

    old "Galan, if you've gone through this whole ordeal and still want to help us fight, you're exactly the kind of person I want fighting at my side. We'll make it happen."
    new "Galan, if you've gone through this whole ordeal and still want to help us fight, you're exactly the kind of person I want fighting at my side. We'll make it happen.\nGalan，如果你经历了这一整场磨难，仍愿意帮我们战斗，那你正是我想并肩作战的人。我们会让你如愿的。"

    old "Of course, I'm not about to abandon your cause either."
    new "Of course, I'm not about to abandon your cause either.\n当然，我也不会放弃你的事业。"

    old "Dasyra, circumstances have changed. You're a noble lady now."
    new "Dasyra, circumstances have changed. You're a noble lady now.\nDasyra，情况已经变了。你现在是贵族小姐了。"

    old "From what I've experienced so far, being a noble woman mostly means just sitting around all day. Quite boring. A lady has to have some excitement in her life, and nothing's more thrilling than staring death right in the face."
    new "From what I've experienced so far, being a noble woman mostly means just sitting around all day. Quite boring. A lady has to have some excitement in her life, and nothing's more thrilling than staring death right in the face.\n从我至今的经历来看，做个贵族女人，主要就是整天无所事事地坐着。无聊得很。一个贵妇的生活总得有点刺激，而没有什么比直视死亡更令人兴奋的了。"

    old "Fair enough. You are an accomplished healer, Dasyra. I guess we shouldn't let that go to waste."
    new "Fair enough. You are an accomplished healer, Dasyra. I guess we shouldn't let that go to waste.\n说得也是。你是个出色的治疗师，Dasyra。我想我们不该浪费这份本事。"

    old "About that. I've spent some more time studying my mother's brooch. It was designed as a relatively simple object, intended to confer mild magical abilities. However, I've found with a bit of training that I can use it to amplify my own existing magical talents."
    new "About that. I've spent some more time studying my mother's brooch. It was designed as a relatively simple object, intended to confer mild magical abilities. However, I've found with a bit of training that I can use it to amplify my own existing magical talents.\n说到这个。我花了更多时间研究我母亲的胸针。它被设计成一件相对简单的物件，意在赋予轻微的魔法能力。不过，经过一番训练，我发现可以用它来增幅我自己原有的魔法天赋。"

    old "How so?"
    new "How so?\n怎么个增幅法？"

    old "Well, simply wearing this seems to amplify the effects of my healing magic."
    new "Well, simply wearing this seems to amplify the effects of my healing magic.\n嗯，光是戴着它，似乎就能放大我治疗魔法的效果。"

    old "Sounds useful."
    new "Sounds useful.\n听起来很有用。"

    old "Indeed. I never imagined that this brooch might have properties which might make it useful in a combat situation, but this world is full of surprises."
    new "Indeed. I never imagined that this brooch might have properties which might make it useful in a combat situation, but this world is full of surprises.\n确实。我从没想过这枚胸针会有能在战斗中派上用场的特性，但这个世界处处充满惊喜。"

    old "I suppose I should know that better than anyone. Never did I ever dream that Faberge Arasmas might be my father. But..."
    new "I suppose I should know that better than anyone. Never did I ever dream that Faberge Arasmas might be my father. But...\n我想我比任何人都该明白这一点。我做梦也没想过Faberge Arasmas会是我的父亲。但是……"

    old "I'm a bit torn. For my entire life, I have looked at Faberge as a noble, generous, and benevolent man. But all this time, he was my father, and never acknowledged me. If what Edgar said was correct, he willed his estate to Edgar instead."
    new "I'm a bit torn. For my entire life, I have looked at Faberge as a noble, generous, and benevolent man. But all this time, he was my father, and never acknowledged me. If what Edgar said was correct, he willed his estate to Edgar instead.\n我有点纠结。我这一生，都把Faberge看作一个高尚、慷慨、仁慈的人。可这整个时间，他都是我的父亲，却从未承认过我。如果Edgar说的是真的，他反倒把庄园遗赠给了Edgar。"

    old "I find it troubling, for reasons that I can't exactly put into words. I know I was his bastard child. It would have been scandalous if it were known that his first-born was the child of one of his maids. It almost seems unreasonable for me to begrudge him for that. But for him to never acknowledge me..."
    new "I find it troubling, for reasons that I can't exactly put into words. I know I was his bastard child. It would have been scandalous if it were known that his first-born was the child of one of his maids. It almost seems unreasonable for me to begrudge him for that. But for him to never acknowledge me...\n这让我感到困扰，原因我也说不清道不明。我知道我是他的私生女。如果让人知道他的长女是他一个女仆的孩子，那会是一桩丑闻。我为此怨恨他似乎有些说不过去。但他从未承认过我……"

    old "It's not that I wanted to be his heir. But I lived my entire youth without ever knowing my father's love."
    new "It's not that I wanted to be his heir. But I lived my entire youth without ever knowing my father's love.\n我倒不是想当他的继承人。但我整个青春，都不曾体会过父亲的爱。"

    old "Dasyra, your father was an odd man. But I don't think he's as cold and calloused as you may be making him out to be."
    new "Dasyra, your father was an odd man. But I don't think he's as cold and calloused as you may be making him out to be.\nDasyra，你父亲是个古怪的人。但我觉得他并不像你所说的那样冷酷无情。"

    old "For a bit, we believed that Faberge gifted your mother a resonator which was attuned specifically to her. That made a certain amount of sense: it was a special gift, so why not imbue it with the essence of its recipient, so that she might wield some minor magical power with it?"
    new "For a bit, we believed that Faberge gifted your mother a resonator which was attuned specifically to her. That made a certain amount of sense: it was a special gift, so why not imbue it with the essence of its recipient, so that she might wield some minor magical power with it?\n曾有一阵子，我们以为Faberge送给你母亲的共鸣器是专门与她相契合的。那很有道理：这是一份特别的礼物，所以何不融入接受者的精髓，好让她能用它施展些许微弱的魔法呢？"

    old "But as we found out, the resonator was actually attuned to Faberge himself. Yet we know that it was a gift for your mother, based on the lettering on the back. How odd, for him to construct a brooch which had magical properties which could only be used to him, and then gift that brooch away."
    new "But as we found out, the resonator was actually attuned to Faberge himself. Yet we know that it was a gift for your mother, based on the lettering on the back. How odd, for him to construct a brooch which had magical properties which could only be used to him, and then gift that brooch away.\n但后来我们发现，共鸣器其实是与Faberge本人相契合的。然而，从背面的铭文看，我们又知道那是送给你母亲的礼物。多么奇怪，他打造了一枚只有他自己能使用的魔法胸针，然后又把它送了出去。"

    old "Do you want to know what I think? I think that when he created that resonator and gifted it to your mother, he had you in mind. By creating a resonator that was attuned to him, he was creating an artifact which any of his offspring could use to claim their bloodline. Edgar would have had no use of such a thing."
    new "Do you want to know what I think? I think that when he created that resonator and gifted it to your mother, he had you in mind. By creating a resonator that was attuned to him, he was creating an artifact which any of his offspring could use to claim their bloodline. Edgar would have had no use of such a thing.\n你想知道我怎么想吗？我想，当他打造那枚共鸣器并送给你母亲时，他心里想的是你。通过打造一枚与自己相契合的共鸣器，他是在创造一件任何他的后代都能用来证明自己血脉的器物。Edgar根本用不上这种东西。"

    old "Perhaps Faberge made that brooch, for exactly such a time as this. He could have remained forever silent about the fact that he had a daughter. But he left a way for you to trace your lineage back to him, even in his death."
    new "Perhaps Faberge made that brooch, for exactly such a time as this. He could have remained forever silent about the fact that he had a daughter. But he left a way for you to trace your lineage back to him, even in his death.\n也许Faberge打造那枚胸针，正是为了今天这样的时刻。他本可以永远沉默下去，不提自己有个女儿。但他留下了一条路，让你即便在他死后，也能追认自己的血脉。"

    old "That may not be the love that you wanted from your father. But this brooch was made for a reason. This brooch was made for you, Dasyra."
    new "That may not be the love that you wanted from your father. But this brooch was made for a reason. This brooch was made for you, Dasyra.\n那也许不是你从父亲那里想要得到的爱。但这枚胸针是有缘由才被打造的。这枚胸针是为你而造的，Dasyra。"

    old "Tears stream down Dasyra's face, and she leaps into my arms and buries her face in my shoulder."
    new "Tears stream down Dasyra's face, and she leaps into my arms and buries her face in my shoulder.\n泪水顺着Dasyra的脸颊流下，她扑进我怀里，把脸埋在我的肩头。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. For everything. Thank you."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. For everything. Thank you.\n谢谢你，[protag]。为这一切。谢谢你。"

    old "I reunite with Dasyra and Galan back in Grimoire."
    new "I reunite with Dasyra and Galan back in Grimoire.\n我在Grimoire与Dasyra和Galan重聚。"

    old "Hello, Galan. I hope you're doing well."
    new "Hello, Galan. I hope you're doing well.\n你好，Galan。希望你恢复得不错。"

    old "I'm doing well enough. That leg of mine has started to heal, and I'm up to the point where I can hobble around on my own. I'll be limping for awhile, but I should be fully recovered within several months."
    new "I'm doing well enough. That leg of mine has started to heal, and I'm up to the point where I can hobble around on my own. I'll be limping for awhile, but I should be fully recovered within several months.\n我恢复得挺好。我那条腿开始愈合了，已经可以自己一瘸一拐地走动了。我还会跛一阵子，但几个月内应该能完全康复。"

    old "I could try healing you with my magic?"
    new "I could try healing you with my magic?\n我可以用魔法试着治疗你？"

    old "Sadly, this kind of damage runs a bit deeper. Being imprisoned in Faberge's dungeon, well, I didn't have much in the way of sustenance. Lack of nourishment weakens a man's constitution, and brittle bones aren't a problem that you can instantly fix using magic. Fortunately, I think that a healthy amount of rest and eating well will do the trick."
    new "Sadly, this kind of damage runs a bit deeper. Being imprisoned in Faberge's dungeon, well, I didn't have much in the way of sustenance. Lack of nourishment weakens a man's constitution, and brittle bones aren't a problem that you can instantly fix using magic. Fortunately, I think that a healthy amount of rest and eating well will do the trick.\n遗憾的是，这种损伤要更深一些。被关在Faberge的地牢里，嗯，我没什么东西可以果腹。缺乏营养会削弱一个人的体质，而脆弱的骨头不是用魔法就能立刻修复的问题。幸运的是，我想充分的休息加上好好吃饭就能解决问题。"

    old "My understanding is that you're building an army of sorts. I wish I had the strength to fight with you, but I think I should be good to go in a few months time if you'll have me. Could even be weeks, if I push myself."
    new "My understanding is that you're building an army of sorts. I wish I had the strength to fight with you, but I think I should be good to go in a few months time if you'll have me. Could even be weeks, if I push myself.\n据我了解，你在组建一支军队。我真希望自己有力量与你并肩作战，不过我想，几个月后我应该就能上阵了，如果你要我的话。要是我逼一逼自己，说不定几周就行。"

    old "Recovering your strength and letting that leg heal is your job now, Galan. I wouldn't dream of bringing you into combat with us, especially considering that it's partly my fault that you wound up with that busted leg."
    new "Recovering your strength and letting that leg heal is your job now, Galan. I wouldn't dream of bringing you into combat with us, especially considering that it's partly my fault that you wound up with that busted leg.\n恢复体力、让腿愈合，才是你现在的工作，Galan。我从没想过把你带上战场，尤其考虑到你那条腿会断，还有一部分是我的责任。"

    old "[protag], there's something I've been meaning to tell you. I took my brooch to your friend Apolimesho. The archwizard. He spent some time studying, and I've spent some time training, and I think we may have found a practical use for it."
    new "[protag], there's something I've been meaning to tell you. I took my brooch to your friend Apolimesho. The archwizard. He spent some time studying, and I've spent some time training, and I think we may have found a practical use for it.\n[protag]，有件事我一直想告诉你。我把我的胸针拿给你朋友Apolimesho看了。那位大法师。他花了一些时间研究，我花了一些时间练习，我想我们可能找到它的实际用途了。"

    old "What's that?"
    new "What's that?\n什么用途？"

    old "Ordinarily, a resonator like this is used as a source of weak magic. But if I draw my magic from a different source, and channel it through the resonator, it can actually act as an amplifier of sorts. I can use this brooch to strengthen my healing powers."
    new "Ordinarily, a resonator like this is used as a source of weak magic. But if I draw my magic from a different source, and channel it through the resonator, it can actually act as an amplifier of sorts. I can use this brooch to strengthen my healing powers.\n通常，这样的共鸣器被用作弱魔法的来源。但如果我从另一个来源汲取魔法，再通过共鸣器引导，它实际上能起到一种放大器的作用。我可以用这枚胸针来强化我的治疗能力。"

    old "That sounds useful."
    new "That sounds useful.\n听起来很有用。"

    old "Indeed it does. Who imagined that this brooch would have practical applications?"
    new "Indeed it does. Who imagined that this brooch would have practical applications?\n确实。谁能想到这枚胸针会有实际用途呢？"

    old "I can't wait to see those powers in action."
    new "I can't wait to see those powers in action.\n我迫不及待想看到那些力量施展出来。"

    old "Me too. Actually..."
    new "Me too. Actually...\n我也是。其实……"

    old "Dasyra holds the brooch in her palm as she casts a magic spell on Galan, who looks surprised."
    new "Dasyra holds the brooch in her palm as she casts a magic spell on Galan, who looks surprised.\nDasyra把胸针托在掌心，对一脸惊讶的Galan施展了一道魔法。"

    old "Wha...what did you just do? I feel great!"
    new "Wha...what did you just do? I feel great!\n什……你刚才做了什么？我感觉棒极了！"

    old "That was exhausting. But it seems it worked."
    new "That was exhausting. But it seems it worked.\n那真累人。不过看来奏效了。"

    old "What just happened here?"
    new "What just happened here?\n刚才发生了什么？"

    old "I cast one of the most powerful healing spells I know on Galan, using the brooch."
    new "I cast one of the most powerful healing spells I know on Galan, using the brooch.\n我用胸针，对Galan施了我所知道的最强治疗法术之一。"

    old "[protag], I feel much better. Sure, I'm not as good as we first met, I'll need more time to recover my full strength. However, I think I could fight alongside you now, if you want me."
    new "[protag], I feel much better. Sure, I'm not as good as we first met, I'll need more time to recover my full strength. However, I think I could fight alongside you now, if you want me.\n[protag]，我感觉好多了。当然，我还不如我们第一次见面时那么好，我还需要更多时间来恢复全部体力。不过，我想我现在就能和你并肩作战了，如果你需要我的话。"

    old "What can I say? That was impressive! And surely I want you to fight with me, Galan."
    new "What can I say? That was impressive! And surely I want you to fight with me, Galan.\n我能说什么呢？太了不起了！我当然想让你和我并肩作战，Galan。"

    old "I hope you're fine recovering here in Grimoire. I don't think that any of you can go back to Hammerhands for a long time."
    new "I hope you're fine recovering here in Grimoire. I don't think that any of you can go back to Hammerhands for a long time.\n希望你们在Grimoire恢复得不错。我想你们谁都别在很长一段时间里回Hammerhands了。"

    old "I doubt Edgar wants to continue pursuing us. At this point, we're just not worth his effort. He got duped, and he's probably in no hurry to expose that fact. That said, Hammerhands has left a rather foul taste in my mouth. Staying here in Grimoire sounds like a fine idea to me."
    new "I doubt Edgar wants to continue pursuing us. At this point, we're just not worth his effort. He got duped, and he's probably in no hurry to expose that fact. That said, Hammerhands has left a rather foul taste in my mouth. Staying here in Grimoire sounds like a fine idea to me.\n我怀疑Edgar还想继续追着我们不放。事到如今，我们根本不值得他费力气。他被人耍了，估计也不急着把这事宣扬出去。话虽如此，Hammerhands在我嘴里留下了相当糟糕的余味。留在Grimoire对我来说是个好主意。"

    old "I agree. Just the smell of the air in Hammerhands seems unpleasant to me now."
    new "I agree. Just the smell of the air in Hammerhands seems unpleasant to me now.\n我同意。如今光是Hammerhands空气里的味道，就让我很不舒服。"

    old "Jasper?"
    new "Jasper?\nJasper？"

    old "Hello Dasyra. And you must be Galan! Pleased to meet you, I'm Jasper."
    new "Hello Dasyra. And you must be Galan! Pleased to meet you, I'm Jasper.\n你好，Dasyra。你一定是Galan！幸会，我是Jasper。"

    old "Hello. Are you helping [protag] in [hisher] mission too?"
    new "Hello. Are you helping [protag] in [hisher] mission too?\n你好。你也在协助[protag]执行[hisher]的任务吗？"

    old "Yes, and forgive me but I overheard what you said."
    new "Yes, and forgive me but I overheard what you said.\n是的，请原谅，我无意中听到了你们的谈话。"

    old "Of course. You always overheard people. Every time, completely 'by accident'."
    new "Of course. You always overheard people. Every time, completely 'by accident'.\n当然。你总是“无意”听到别人说话。每一次都“纯属巧合”。"

    old "What can I say, I'm curious. Anyway, about Hammerhands: many people in town can't stand Edgar now. Of course, he tried his best to hide what happened, but rumors spread."
    new "What can I say, I'm curious. Anyway, about Hammerhands: many people in town can't stand Edgar now. Of course, he tried his best to hide what happened, but rumors spread.\n我能说什么呢，我好奇心重。总之，关于Hammerhands：如今城里很多人都受不了Edgar。当然，他竭力隐瞒发生的事，但谣言已经传开了。"

    old "Rumors spread? And you had no role in this?"
    new "Rumors spread? And you had no role in this?\n谣言传开了？这事你没掺一脚？"

    old "I only talked to a few people I know there. Nothing big. But enough to warrant us a good reputation there."
    new "I only talked to a few people I know there. Nothing big. But enough to warrant us a good reputation there.\n我只跟我认识的那几个人聊了聊。没什么大不了的。但足以让我们在那里赢得不错的名声。"

    old "Heh, I know you since five minutes but I already like you."
    new "Heh, I know you since five minutes but I already like you.\n嘿，我才认识你五分钟，就已经喜欢上你了。"

    old "Thank you! Anyway, while it's better for you two to stay here in Grimoire, we should have no troubles if we want to visit Hammerhands to buy items and such. People there like us more than Edgar."
    new "Thank you! Anyway, while it's better for you two to stay here in Grimoire, we should have no troubles if we want to visit Hammerhands to buy items and such. People there like us more than Edgar.\n谢谢！总之，虽然你们俩最好留在Grimoire，但我们要是想去Hammerhands买买东西什么的，也不会有麻烦。那里的人喜欢我们胜过Edgar。"

    old "Hello, Galan. How has your health been?"
    new "Hello, Galan. How has your health been?\n你好，Galan。你身体怎么样了？"

    old "Oh, I've recovered just fine. A few days of eating decent meals and sleeping with a pillow under your head can do wonders for a man's constitution."
    new "Oh, I've recovered just fine. A few days of eating decent meals and sleeping with a pillow under your head can do wonders for a man's constitution.\n哦，我恢复得很好。几天来好好吃饭，睡觉时头下垫个枕头，就能让一个人的体质发生奇迹。"

    old "Like I said, the worst I had to deal with when I was kept prisoner by Arasmas was the lack of food. I don't think I'm too worse for wear."
    new "Like I said, the worst I had to deal with when I was kept prisoner by Arasmas was the lack of food. I don't think I'm too worse for wear.\n正如我说的，被Arasmas囚禁时，我要面对的最糟的事就是缺吃的。我想我还没怎么被折磨垮。"

    old "Ah, Dasyra, glad to see you're here as well."
    new "Ah, Dasyra, glad to see you're here as well.\n啊，Dasyra，很高兴你也在。"

    old "Dasyra here has been looking out for me. Not that I need much looking after, but the company is appreciated."
    new "Dasyra here has been looking out for me. Not that I need much looking after, but the company is appreciated.\nDasyra一直在照看我。我倒不需要多少照看，不过有她作伴我很感激。"

    old "Galan, there's something I've been meaning to tell you. Now that I have both you and [protag] here, I think it's time that I come clean."
    new "Galan, there's something I've been meaning to tell you. Now that I have both you and [protag] here, I think it's time that I come clean.\nGalan，有件事我一直想告诉你。现在你和[protag]都在这里，我想是时候坦白了。"

    old "Come clean? About what?"
    new "Come clean? About what?\n坦白？坦白什么？"

    old "Galan, there's something I've been meaning to say to you. Now that [protag] is here, I think it's time for me to offer you a proper apology."
    new "Galan, there's something I've been meaning to say to you. Now that [protag] is here, I think it's time for me to offer you a proper apology.\nGalan，有些话我一直想对你说。现在[protag]来了，我想是时候向你正式道歉了。"

    old "Apology? What for?"
    new "Apology? What for?\n道歉？为什么？"

    old "Do you remember when the three of us first met?"
    new "Do you remember when the three of us first met?\n你还记得我们三个第一次见面的时候吗？"

    old "Galan laughs deep enough that the floor under him begins vibrating."
    new "Galan laughs deep enough that the floor under him begins vibrating.\nGalan笑得如此用力，连他脚下的地板都开始震动。"

    old "Of course I remember. How could I forget?"
    new "Of course I remember. How could I forget?\n我当然记得。怎么会忘呢？"

    old "The Arasmas men were arresting me for theft. I told you that the brooch they accused me of stealing belonged to my mother. That was true. It really did belong to my mother. But I implied a falsehood. I really did steal it from the Arasmas estate."
    new "The Arasmas men were arresting me for theft. I told you that the brooch they accused me of stealing belonged to my mother. That was true. It really did belong to my mother. But I implied a falsehood. I really did steal it from the Arasmas estate.\nArasmas的人以偷窃罪逮捕我。我告诉你，他们指控我偷的那枚胸针属于我母亲。那是真的。它确实属于我母亲。但我暗示了一句谎话。我确实是从Arasmas庄园把它偷出来的。"

    old "So? It's not like I was punished for doing nothing. I participated in that scuffle of my own accord. I can't blame you for that."
    new "So? It's not like I was punished for doing nothing. I participated in that scuffle of my own accord. I can't blame you for that.\n所以呢？我又不是因为什么都没做才受的罚。我是自愿卷入那场混战的。我不能怪你。"

    old "But you spent time in jail, and it was a result of a real crime that I committed. That's...that's something that weighed on me quite heavily."
    new "But you spent time in jail, and it was a result of a real crime that I committed. That's...that's something that weighed on me quite heavily.\n但你坐了牢，而那是因我犯下的真实罪行而起。那……那件事一直沉沉地压在我心上。"

    old "Well, you came back for me in the end. That's what counts, right?"
    new "Well, you came back for me in the end. That's what counts, right?\n嗯，你最后还是回来找我了。这才重要，对吧？"

    old "Come to think of it...didn't you end up giving that brooch to Edgar in exchange for my freedom? The same brooch that started this whole ordeal?"
    new "Come to think of it...didn't you end up giving that brooch to Edgar in exchange for my freedom? The same brooch that started this whole ordeal?\n想想看……你最后不是把那个胸针交给了Edgar，来换我的自由吗？就是那枚引发这一切磨难的胸针？"

    old "Yes. Ironic, isn't it? We somehow wound up right back where we started, with none of us imprisoned, and that brooch in Edgar's custody."
    new "Yes. Ironic, isn't it? We somehow wound up right back where we started, with none of us imprisoned, and that brooch in Edgar's custody.\n是的。很讽刺，不是吗？我们兜兜转转又回到了原点，我们谁都没被关押，而那枚胸针落在了Edgar手里。"

    old "Well, I consider myself richer for the experience."
    new "Well, I consider myself richer for the experience.\n嗯，我觉得经此一遭，自己更富有了。"

    old "That's certainly not something I expected to hear from a man who just spent time imprisoned."
    new "That's certainly not something I expected to hear from a man who just spent time imprisoned.\n这真不像一个刚坐过牢的人会说出来的话。"

    old "I feel like you're greatly overestimating the amount of trauma I suffered in that dungeon. Trust me, I've experienced worse."
    new "I feel like you're greatly overestimating the amount of trauma I suffered in that dungeon. Trust me, I've experienced worse.\n我觉得你大大高估了我在那地牢里受的创伤。相信我，我经历过更糟的。"

    old "As a result of that ordeal, I managed to meet two people, who cared enough about me that they invested time, effort, and some of their own wealth to help me. You can't put a price on that."
    new "As a result of that ordeal, I managed to meet two people, who cared enough about me that they invested time, effort, and some of their own wealth to help me. You can't put a price on that.\n因为那场磨难，我得以结识两个人，他们如此在意我，不惜投入时间、精力，还有自己的一些财富来帮我。这是无价的。"

    old "Dasyra begins crying and hugs Galan."
    new "Dasyra begins crying and hugs Galan.\nDasyra哭了起来，拥抱了Galan。"

    old "I'm truly humbled."
    new "I'm truly humbled.\n我实在受之有愧。"

    old "Galan, I believe you once told me you were a man with an affinity for battle."
    new "Galan, I believe you once told me you were a man with an affinity for battle.\nGalan，我记得你曾告诉我，你是个对战斗有亲和力的人。"

    old "You got me. I spent the time learning to use a hammer in combat, and I find that I enjoy myself very much when I get a chance to swing it."
    new "You got me. I spent the time learning to use a hammer in combat, and I find that I enjoy myself very much when I get a chance to swing it.\n你猜对了。我花时间学会了在战斗中使用锤子，而且我发现，一有机会挥舞它，我就非常享受。"

    old "How would you like the opportunity to use that hammer of yours to cave in some zombie skulls?"
    new "How would you like the opportunity to use that hammer of yours to cave in some zombie skulls?\n你想不想要个机会，用你那把锤子去砸烂一些僵尸的头骨？"

    old "Zombies, skeletons, bears, wolves, doesn't matter to me. I just like fighting. If you need a fighter, I'm there."
    new "Zombies, skeletons, bears, wolves, doesn't matter to me. I just like fighting. If you need a fighter, I'm there.\n僵尸、骷髅、熊、狼，对我来说都一样。我只是喜欢打架。你要是需要个战士，我就来。"

    old "Excellent. Let me fill you in on the details."
    new "Excellent. Let me fill you in on the details.\n太好了。让我把细节告诉你。"

    old "I spot a familiar-looking dwarf in the market district of Grimoire."
    new "I spot a familiar-looking dwarf in the market district of Grimoire.\n我在Grimoire的市场区看到了一个眼熟的矮人。"

    old "Hey, Dasyra."
    new "Hey, Dasyra.\n嘿，Dasyra。"

    old "Dasyra turns to face me, and wears a startled expression until a look of recognition replaces it."
    new "Dasyra turns to face me, and wears a startled expression until a look of recognition replaces it.\nDasyra转身面向我，先是一脸惊讶，随即换成了认出我的神情。"

    old "Oh! Hello, [protag]."
    new "Oh! Hello, [protag].\n哦！你好，[protag]。"

    old "What brings you to the market today?"
    new "What brings you to the market today?\n今天是什么风把你吹到市场来的？"

    old "Dasyra points to a basket hanging from her arm. It contains several light orange fruits."
    new "Dasyra points to a basket hanging from her arm. It contains several light orange fruits.\nDasyra指了指挂在她臂弯里的篮子。里面装着几个浅橙色的水果。"

    old "I came to buy persimmons. I tried a persimmon for the first time when we came here after fleeing Hammerhands, and now I'm an addict."
    new "I came to buy persimmons. I tried a persimmon for the first time when we came here after fleeing Hammerhands, and now I'm an addict.\n我来买柿子。我们逃出Hammerhands来到这里后，我第一次尝了柿子，如今我上了瘾。"

    old "Ah, have you got a bit of a sweet tooth?"
    new "Ah, have you got a bit of a sweet tooth?\n啊，你有点爱吃甜食？"

    old "Apparently yes. When I was growing up, I didn't get to eat sweet foods often. There were candy vendors in Hammerhands, but buying candy was a bit beyond the means of a maid's daughter, so I only got to eat it on special occasions when my mother received it as a gift from the Arasmas family."
    new "Apparently yes. When I was growing up, I didn't get to eat sweet foods often. There were candy vendors in Hammerhands, but buying candy was a bit beyond the means of a maid's daughter, so I only got to eat it on special occasions when my mother received it as a gift from the Arasmas family.\n看来是的。我小时候并不常吃到甜食。Hammerhands有卖糖果的小贩，但买糖果对一个女仆的女儿来说有点超出能力，所以我只能在特殊场合吃到，也就是我母亲从Arasmas家收到糖果作礼物的时候。"

    old "Now I'm out of Hammerhands, and it's a bit of a delight to find that sweet things literally grow on trees."
    new "Now I'm out of Hammerhands, and it's a bit of a delight to find that sweet things literally grow on trees.\n如今我离开了Hammerhands，发现甜的东西居然真能长在树上，这真叫人欢喜。"

    old "You don't have fruit trees in Hammerhands?"
    new "You don't have fruit trees in Hammerhands?\nHammerhands没有果树吗？"

    old "It's not that odd, if you stop to think about it. Think about where Hammerhands is located. It's rocky. The soil is dry, and it doesn't rain often. It's not the kind of place you'd want to start an orchard."
    new "It's not that odd, if you stop to think about it. Think about where Hammerhands is located. It's rocky. The soil is dry, and it doesn't rain often. It's not the kind of place you'd want to start an orchard.\n你细想想，也不奇怪。想想Hammerhands的地理位置。那里岩石遍布。土壤干燥，又不常下雨。那不是你想开果园的地方。"

    old "Do people in Hammerhands ever import fruit from the more lush parts of the continents?"
    new "Do people in Hammerhands ever import fruit from the more lush parts of the continents?\nHammerhands的人有没有从大陆上更丰饶的地方进口水果？"

    old "In Hammerhands, fresh fruit is even more expensive than candy. Most of the expense involved is the cost of transporting it."
    new "In Hammerhands, fresh fruit is even more expensive than candy. Most of the expense involved is the cost of transporting it.\n在Hammerhands，新鲜水果比糖果还贵。费用的大头都在运输成本上。"

    old "Yes, I know a thing or two about that. Transporting goods is costly, and transporting fresh fruit and vegetables is both costly and difficult."
    new "Yes, I know a thing or two about that. Transporting goods is costly, and transporting fresh fruit and vegetables is both costly and difficult.\n是啊，这个我略知一二。运货成本高，而运输新鲜蔬果既昂贵又困难。"

    old "Speaking from experience?"
    new "Speaking from experience?\n这是经验之谈？"

    old "I was a merchant, once upon a time, before I got caught up in this vampire-hunting business."
    new "I was a merchant, once upon a time, before I got caught up in this vampire-hunting business.\n我曾经是个商人，在卷入这猎杀吸血鬼的差事之前。"

    old "So, you know."
    new "So, you know.\n所以，你懂的。"

    old "After all, fresh fruit doesn't keep very long. Most of it would probably be bruised and over-ripe by the time you hauled it from Grimoire to Hammerhands."
    new "After all, fresh fruit doesn't keep very long. Most of it would probably be bruised and over-ripe by the time you hauled it from Grimoire to Hammerhands.\n毕竟，新鲜水果放不久。等你把它从Grimoire一路运到Hammerhands，大部分恐怕已经碰伤、熟过头了。"

    old "What about dried or preserved fruit?"
    new "What about dried or preserved fruit?\n那果干或者蜜饯呢？"

    old "Those exist, though I think most people just preferred candy. After all, eating fruit out of a can isn't really the same as biting into a fresh persimmon, is it? I think the appeal of fruit isn't just the flavor. It's also about the texture. That's why I like persimmons so much. I think they're just the right amount of juicy."
    new "Those exist, though I think most people just preferred candy. After all, eating fruit out of a can isn't really the same as biting into a fresh persimmon, is it? I think the appeal of fruit isn't just the flavor. It's also about the texture. That's why I like persimmons so much. I think they're just the right amount of juicy.\n那些是有的，不过我想大多数人还是宁愿要糖果。毕竟，吃罐头里的水果，和咬上一口新鲜的柿子，终究不是一回事，对吧？我想水果的魅力不只在于味道。也在于口感。所以我这么喜欢柿子。我觉得它们的汁水恰到好处。"

    old "Anyway, enjoying the finer things in life is still a new experience to me."
    new "Anyway, enjoying the finer things in life is still a new experience to me.\n总之，享受生活中更精致的东西，对我来说仍是种新体验。"

    old "It's nice to indulge now and then, even if it is just a piece of fruit."
    new "It's nice to indulge now and then, even if it is just a piece of fruit.\n偶尔放纵一下挺好，哪怕只是一块水果。"

    old "Just a piece of fruit for you, and an absolute rarity for a poor girl growing up in Hammerhands."
    new "Just a piece of fruit for you, and an absolute rarity for a poor girl growing up in Hammerhands.\n对你来说只是一块水果，对一个在Hammerhands长大的穷丫头来说，却是绝对的稀罕物。"

    old "It's kind of funny to hear you describe a fresh persimmon as 'one of the finer things in life.' I think it's the kind of thing that people around here take for granted."
    new "It's kind of funny to hear you describe a fresh persimmon as 'one of the finer things in life.' I think it's the kind of thing that people around here take for granted.\n听你把一个新鲜柿子形容成“生活中更精致的东西之一”，还挺有趣的。我觉得那正是这里的人习以为常的东西。"

    old "I spent a lot of my childhood lusting after things that other people took for granted."
    new "I spent a lot of my childhood lusting after things that other people took for granted.\n我童年的大把时光，都花在了渴求别人习以为常的东西上。"

    old "My childhood was a bit odd. I was exposed to the finer things in life without being able to enjoy most of them myself."
    new "My childhood was a bit odd. I was exposed to the finer things in life without being able to enjoy most of them myself.\n我的童年有点古怪。我接触得到生活中更精致的东西，自己却无法享受其中大多数。"

    old "Ah, because of your mother's profession?"
    new "Ah, because of your mother's profession?\n啊，是因为你母亲的职业？"

    old "Yes. My mother was a poor—well, not exactly poor, but she was a woman of modest means. And she worked for someone who was, to be quite frank, very wealthy."
    new "Yes. My mother was a poor—well, not exactly poor, but she was a woman of modest means. And she worked for someone who was, to be quite frank, very wealthy.\n是的。我母亲很穷——嗯，也不完全是穷，但她是个家境平平的女人。而她为之干活的人，坦白说，非常富有。"

    old "And she worked for someone who was the epitome of wealth."
    new "And she worked for someone who was the epitome of wealth.\n她为一位财富的化身干活。"

    old "Yes. Old Faberge Arasmas never did indulge in excess, but even a 'modest' nobleman takes for granted many pleasures that his employees could never hope to enjoy."
    new "Yes. Old Faberge Arasmas never did indulge in excess, but even a 'modest' nobleman takes for granted many pleasures that his employees could never hope to enjoy.\n是的。老Faberge Arasmas从不放纵铺张，但即便一个“朴素”的贵族，也会把许多他的雇员永远无法企及的乐趣视为理所当然。"

    old "Such as?"
    new "Such as?\n比如说？"

    old "Eating meat at every meal. Every dinner, even the quiet ones that Faberge ate alone in his study, he would always have some kind of meat. A steak, a pork chop, a bit of veal, sometimes just some strips of bacon. Eating meat was very ordinary for him."
    new "Eating meat at every meal. Every dinner, even the quiet ones that Faberge ate alone in his study, he would always have some kind of meat. A steak, a pork chop, a bit of veal, sometimes just some strips of bacon. Eating meat was very ordinary for him.\n每餐吃肉。每一顿晚餐，哪怕是Faberge独自在书房里安静享用的那些，也总会有某种肉。一块牛排，一块猪排，一点小牛肉，有时只是几条培根。吃肉对他来说再平常不过。"

    old "And it wasn't for you."
    new "And it wasn't for you.\n对你却不是。"

    old "Let's just say that meat is a lot more expensive than bread. And when you have to be mindful of your spending, it's pretty easy to come to the conclusion that bread is enough."
    new "Let's just say that meat is a lot more expensive than bread. And when you have to be mindful of your spending, it's pretty easy to come to the conclusion that bread is enough.\n这么说吧，肉比面包贵得多。而当你必须精打细算时，就很容易得出有面包就够了的结论。"

    old "Eating only bread sounds kind of dreadful."
    new "Eating only bread sounds kind of dreadful.\n光吃面包听起来有点可怕。"

    old "Oh, I didn't think of it that way. There are lots of different ways that you can make bread. 'Bread' is a term that is about as vague as the word 'meat.' It comes in many different varieties."
    new "Oh, I didn't think of it that way. There are lots of different ways that you can make bread. 'Bread' is a term that is about as vague as the word 'meat.' It comes in many different varieties.\n哦，我倒不这么看。做面包有很多不同的方法。“面包”这个词，跟“肉”这个词一样含糊。它有很多不同的种类。"

    old "Care to enlighten me?"
    new "Care to enlighten me?\n能给我讲讲吗？"

    old "Oh, where to start. Let's see, there's rye bread, sourdough bread, corn bread, flat bread, bread sticks, buckwheat potato bread, and sweet bread for special occasions."
    new "Oh, where to start. Let's see, there's rye bread, sourdough bread, corn bread, flat bread, bread sticks, buckwheat potato bread, and sweet bread for special occasions.\n哦，从哪说起呢。让我想想，有黑麦面包、酸面包、玉米面包、扁面包、面包棒、荞麦土豆面包，还有特殊场合的甜面包。"

    old "I didn't realize you were such an expert."
    new "I didn't realize you were such an expert.\n我倒不知道你还是个行家。"

    old "I'm not an expert. Just a girl who spent many hours of her youth in the kitchen."
    new "I'm not an expert. Just a girl who spent many hours of her youth in the kitchen.\n我不是行家。只是个年轻时在厨房里耗了大把时间的姑娘。"

    old "Wait, you made your own bread?"
    new "Wait, you made your own bread?\n等等，你自己做面包？"

    old "Making bread at home is better than buying it, and it's a lot more fun, too. Variety is good for the sake of appetite, but it also helps things from getting too repetitive in the kitchen."
    new "Making bread at home is better than buying it, and it's a lot more fun, too. Variety is good for the sake of appetite, but it also helps things from getting too repetitive in the kitchen.\n在家做面包比买来好，而且也有趣得多。花样多有利于食欲，也能让厨房里的活不至于太单调。"

    old "It's actually been many years since the last time I fired up an oven. Maybe I should do it again some time, for old time's sake."
    new "It's actually been many years since the last time I fired up an oven. Maybe I should do it again some time, for old time's sake.\n其实，我上次生炉子烤面包，已经是很多年前的事了。也许什么时候我该再做一次，就当怀旧。"

    old "If you want to bake bread, then you should do it."
    new "If you want to bake bread, then you should do it.\n如果你想烤面包，那就去做吧。"

    old "It's...it's kind of weird. On a certain level, I'm not sure if I'd enjoy baking bread again. On one hand, I really did enjoy doing it as a child. On the other hand, just thinking about it reminds me of the other parts of my childhood, which weren't as pleasant."
    new "It's...it's kind of weird. On a certain level, I'm not sure if I'd enjoy baking bread again. On one hand, I really did enjoy doing it as a child. On the other hand, just thinking about it reminds me of the other parts of my childhood, which weren't as pleasant.\n这……这有点怪。从某种层面上说，我不确定自己还会不会喜欢烤面包。一方面，我小时候确实很喜欢做这事。另一方面，一想到它，就让我想起童年里那些不那么愉快的部分。"

    old "Ah. So you're not sure if you even want to trigger that nostalgia."
    new "Ah. So you're not sure if you even want to trigger that nostalgia.\n啊。所以你甚至不确定自己是否想勾起那份怀旧。"

    old "Yeah."
    new "Yeah.\n嗯。"

    old "Well, it's up to you."
    new "Well, it's up to you.\n嗯，这由你决定。"

    old "Maybe I'll make some and give you some to try."
    new "Maybe I'll make some and give you some to try.\n也许我会做一点，给你尝尝。"

    old "Listening to you talk about the way you used to make bread makes me want to try some of it for myself."
    new "Listening to you talk about the way you used to make bread makes me want to try some of it for myself.\n听你讲你过去做面包的样子，让我自己也想尝一尝了。"

    old "Oh, be careful what you wish for, [protag]."
    new "Oh, be careful what you wish for, [protag].\n哦，你可要小心自己许的愿，[protag]。"

    old "What, are you an incompetent baker?"
    new "What, are you an incompetent baker?\n怎么，你是个蹩脚的面包师吗？"

    old "Let's just say that my skills have had more than a few years to atrophe."
    new "Let's just say that my skills have had more than a few years to atrophe.\n这么说吧，我的手艺已经荒废了好几年了。"

    old "Well, if you do decide to start making bread again, and you need a taste-tester, let me know."
    new "Well, if you do decide to start making bread again, and you need a taste-tester, let me know.\n嗯，如果你真决定重新开始做面包，又需要一个试吃的人，就告诉我。"

    old "Alright, [protag]. I'll let you know if I require your services as a taste-tester."
    new "Alright, [protag]. I'll let you know if I require your services as a taste-tester.\n好的，[protag]。如果我需要你当试吃员，我会通知你的。"

    old "Hello, Dasyra."
    new "Hello, Dasyra.\n你好，Dasyra。"

    old "Ah, [protag]! It's good to see you."
    new "Ah, [protag]! It's good to see you.\n啊，[protag]！见到你真好。"

    old "What have you been up to recently? Have you decided to pursue your old passion of bread-making?"
    new "What have you been up to recently? Have you decided to pursue your old passion of bread-making?\n你最近在忙什么？你决定重拾烤面包的旧爱了吗？"

    old "As a matter of fact, yes. Though...things didn't go so well."
    new "As a matter of fact, yes. Though...things didn't go so well.\n事实上，是的。不过……进展不太顺利。"

    old "What was the problem? Are you having trouble finding a kitchen?"
    new "What was the problem? Are you having trouble finding a kitchen?\n出了什么问题？是找不到厨房吗？"

    old "No, I found a local baker who was kind enough to let me use his facilities after he had shut down business for the day. I got all of the ingredients ready to cook. However, the outcome was a bit lacking."
    new "No, I found a local baker who was kind enough to let me use his facilities after he had shut down business for the day. I got all of the ingredients ready to cook. However, the outcome was a bit lacking.\n不，我找到了一位好心的本地面包师，他打烊后愿意把地方借给我用。我把所有原料都备齐了。不过，结果有点差强人意。"

    old "In what sense?"
    new "In what sense?\n怎么个差法？"

    old "Dasyra reaches into the basket hanging from her arm and pulls out a piece of bread that looks like a pita."
    new "Dasyra reaches into the basket hanging from her arm and pulls out a piece of bread that looks like a pita.\nDasyra把手伸进臂弯的篮子里，掏出一块像皮塔饼一样的面包。"

    old "This was the result."
    new "This was the result.\n这就是成果。"

    old "Do you want me to try it?"
    new "Do you want me to try it?\n你想让我尝尝吗？"

    old "I really wouldn't recommend it. If there was any doubt in my mind as to whether the result was good or not, I'd want your opinion. But I'm pretty certain that this batch was a bit of a disaster."
    new "I really wouldn't recommend it. If there was any doubt in my mind as to whether the result was good or not, I'd want your opinion. But I'm pretty certain that this batch was a bit of a disaster.\n我真不建议你尝。要是我心里对结果好坏还有半点疑虑，我倒想听听你的意见。但我相当确定，这一炉是场灾难。"

    old "Okay, I'll take your word for it. Still, it's bread. It's not like there's a lot of complex flavors that go into something like that. How exactly do you make bad bread?"
    new "Okay, I'll take your word for it. Still, it's bread. It's not like there's a lot of complex flavors that go into something like that. How exactly do you make bad bread?\n好吧，我信你的。不过，说到底它还是面包。又不是说那里面会有什么复杂的味道。到底怎么能把面包做坏呢？"

    old "It's all about the consistency. When you bake bread, you want it to taste like, well, baked bread. If the bread doesn't taste like it's been baked—if it comes out with a wet, doughy consistency, that's when you know that something's gone horribly wrong."
    new "It's all about the consistency. When you bake bread, you want it to taste like, well, baked bread. If the bread doesn't taste like it's been baked—if it comes out with a wet, doughy consistency, that's when you know that something's gone horribly wrong.\n关键全在质地。烤面包时，你希望它尝起来像，嗯，烤过的面包。如果面包尝起来不像烤过——出炉时湿乎乎的、面糊一样，那你就知道出了大岔子。"

    old "Ah. That happened to you?"
    new "Ah. That happened to you?\n啊。你就遇上了这种情况？"

    old "Yup. I blame the air."
    new "Yup. I blame the air.\n对。我把这归咎于空气。"

    old "I'm sorry. The air?"
    new "I'm sorry. The air?\n不好意思。空气？"

    old "Why don't you let me be the judge of that?"
    new "Why don't you let me be the judge of that?\n为什么不让我来当裁判呢？"

    old "Alright, if you insist. But don't say I didn't warn you."
    new "Alright, if you insist. But don't say I didn't warn you.\n好吧，既然你坚持。但可别说我没警告过你。"

    old "Dasyra hands me the piece of bread, and I bite into it. The bread is tough, and I have to physically pull the bread away from my face to tear off a bite."
    new "Dasyra hands me the piece of bread, and I bite into it. The bread is tough, and I have to physically pull the bread away from my face to tear off a bite.\nDasyra把那块面包递给我，我咬了下去。面包很硬，我不得不把面包从脸前拽开，才撕下一口。"

    old "I chew for several seconds. The bread has a doughy consistency, almost like it's not fully cooked, despite the outside of it being hard and cracked."
    new "I chew for several seconds. The bread has a doughy consistency, almost like it's not fully cooked, despite the outside of it being hard and cracked.\n我嚼了好几秒。面包有股面糊般的质地，几乎像是没完全烤熟，尽管外面又硬又裂。"

    old "After several more slow and painful chews, I manage to choke it down."
    new "After several more slow and painful chews, I manage to choke it down.\n又慢又痛苦地嚼了好几下之后，我总算把它咽了下去。"

    old "Well? How bad was it?"
    new "Well? How bad was it?\n怎么样？有多糟？"

    old "It wasn't that bad..."
    new "It wasn't that bad...\n没那么糟……"

    old "The pained expression on your face says otherwise. I've never seen someone look so unhappy as they chewed."
    new "The pained expression on your face says otherwise. I've never seen someone look so unhappy as they chewed.\n你脸上痛苦的表情可不是这么说的。我从没见过有人嚼东西时脸色这么难看。"

    old "Ah, well. I guess there's no use in trying to hide it."
    new "Ah, well. I guess there's no use in trying to hide it.\n啊，好吧。我想再藏着掖着也没用。"

    old "Okay, you were right. It's pretty bad."
    new "Okay, you were right. It's pretty bad.\n好吧，你说得对。确实很糟。"

    old "I knew that I wasn't going to make something delicious on my first attempt, but I'm surprised that things went so wrong."
    new "I knew that I wasn't going to make something delicious on my first attempt, but I'm surprised that things went so wrong.\n我早知道第一次尝试做不出什么美味，但我惊讶事情竟会错得这么离谱。"

    old "Where exactly did things go wrong?"
    new "Where exactly did things go wrong?\n到底哪里出了错？"

    old "It's the air."
    new "It's the air.\n是空气。"

    old "The air?"
    new "The air?\n空气？"

    old "The air is different here in Grimoire, compared to Hammerhands. It's a lot more humid. Hammerhands is dry. When I cooked in Hammerhands, I would actually add more water to the dough, to give the bread a proper moistness and make sure that it baked evenly. I carried those habits with me to Grimoire. So I ended up making the dough too wet."
    new "The air is different here in Grimoire, compared to Hammerhands. It's a lot more humid. Hammerhands is dry. When I cooked in Hammerhands, I would actually add more water to the dough, to give the bread a proper moistness and make sure that it baked evenly. I carried those habits with me to Grimoire. So I ended up making the dough too wet.\n与Hammerhands相比，Grimoire的空气不一样。这里潮湿得多。Hammerhands很干燥。我在Hammerhands做饭时，会往面团里多加些水，让面包有适当的湿润度，并确保烤得均匀。我把这些习惯带到了Grimoire。结果我把面团弄得太湿了。"

    old "Ah. That would explain the doughy consistency."
    new "Ah. That would explain the doughy consistency.\n啊。那就解释了那股面糊般的质地。"

    old "Also, it's colder here in Grimoire. When I was in Hammerhands, I would take the bread out of the oven early, and let the bread finish outside the oven."
    new "Also, it's colder here in Grimoire. When I was in Hammerhands, I would take the bread out of the oven early, and let the bread finish outside the oven.\n而且，Grimoire这里更冷。我在Hammerhands时，会提前把面包从烤箱里拿出来，让面包在烤箱外完成烘烤。"

    old "You know, when you take bread out of the oven, the outside is actually hotter than the interior. So if you take out out early, the hot exterior will actually continue to heat up the inside. It seems strange, but the inside of the bread can actually get hotter after it comes out of the oven."
    new "You know, when you take bread out of the oven, the outside is actually hotter than the interior. So if you take out out early, the hot exterior will actually continue to heat up the inside. It seems strange, but the inside of the bread can actually get hotter after it comes out of the oven.\n你知道，面包出炉时，外面其实比里面更热。所以如果你提前取出来，滚烫的外壳会继续加热里面。这听起来奇怪，但面包出炉后，里面其实会变得更热。"

    old "That seems like a counter-intuitive idea, but I'll take your word for it."
    new "That seems like a counter-intuitive idea, but I'll take your word for it.\n这想法听起来有违直觉，但我信你的。"

    old "The problem is that if the ambient temperature is too cold, then the bread's crust cools faster, and that prevents the inside from baking all the way through."
    new "The problem is that if the ambient temperature is too cold, then the bread's crust cools faster, and that prevents the inside from baking all the way through.\n问题在于，如果环境温度太低，面包的外皮就会冷却得更快，从而阻止里面被完全烤透。"

    old "So, going from a hot and dry climate to Grimoire resulted in my bread being undercooked. That means an unpleasant, doughy, and tough texture."
    new "So, going from a hot and dry climate to Grimoire resulted in my bread being undercooked. That means an unpleasant, doughy, and tough texture.\n所以，从炎热干燥的气候来到Grimoire，导致我的面包没烤熟。结果就是那种令人不快、面糊一样、又硬又韧的质地。"

    old "Sorry things didn't turn out better."
    new "Sorry things didn't turn out better.\n很遗憾事情没能更好些。"

    old "It's okay. It was a good learning experience. I'll do better next time."
    new "It's okay. It was a good learning experience. I'll do better next time.\n没关系。这是一次很好的学习经历。下次我会做得更好。"

    old "Next time?"
    new "Next time?\n下次？"

    old "The bread came out bad, but in the process of making it, I realized that I really enjoy baking. I thought it would trigger some nostalgia in me, but I think that the real appeal for me was the process itself. Mixing ingredients, kneading dough, and smelling the hot loaf as it comes out of the oven, everything about it just felt right to me."
    new "The bread came out bad, but in the process of making it, I realized that I really enjoy baking. I thought it would trigger some nostalgia in me, but I think that the real appeal for me was the process itself. Mixing ingredients, kneading dough, and smelling the hot loaf as it comes out of the oven, everything about it just felt right to me.\n面包做坏了，但在做的过程中，我意识到自己真的很喜欢烘焙。我原以为它会勾起我的一些怀旧，但我觉得真正吸引我的，是这个过程本身。混合配料、揉面团、闻着热腾腾的面包出炉的香气，这一切都让我觉得无比妥帖。"

    old "Until I got to the tasting part, that is."
    new "Until I got to the tasting part, that is.\n直到到了品尝那一步，就是另一回事了。"

    old "I have no illusions of ever being exceptionally good at this. But you know, it does make a good hobby. Just a little something to distract me from the horrors of the world."
    new "I have no illusions of ever being exceptionally good at this. But you know, it does make a good hobby. Just a little something to distract me from the horrors of the world.\n我从没幻想过自己能做得特别出色。但你知道，它确实是个好爱好。只是件能让我从世间的恐怖中分分心的小事。"

    old "I'm glad you've found a hobby, Dasyra. I know we're all focused on our mission, and the business of N'Mar weighs heavily on my mind, but it's important to find ways to stay sane. It seems like baking is that little escape for you."
    new "I'm glad you've found a hobby, Dasyra. I know we're all focused on our mission, and the business of N'Mar weighs heavily on my mind, but it's important to find ways to stay sane. It seems like baking is that little escape for you.\n我很高兴你找到了一个爱好，Dasyra。我知道我们都专注于任务，N'Mar的事也沉沉压在我心上，但找到保持清醒的办法很重要。看来烘焙就是你的小小出口。"

    old "What about you? How do you escape from the trials and tribulations of these trying times?"
    new "What about you? How do you escape from the trials and tribulations of these trying times?\n你呢？你如何从这些艰难时日的考验与磨难中抽身？"

    old "Me? I come and visit my friends, and listen to them tell me about their hobbies."
    new "Me? I come and visit my friends, and listen to them tell me about their hobbies.\n我？我来探望朋友，听他们讲讲自己的爱好。"

    old "Well, I'm glad to have been of service, then."
    new "Well, I'm glad to have been of service, then.\n那么，能帮上忙，我很高兴。"

    old "It's nice to have a distraction from the horrors of the world...but make sure you're not cooking up any new horrors, alright?"
    new "It's nice to have a distraction from the horrors of the world...but make sure you're not cooking up any new horrors, alright?\n能从世间的恐怖中分分心是件好事……不过你可要当心，别再折腾出新的恐怖来，好吗？"

    old "Har, har. Don't worry, [protag]. I won't subject you to any of my baking until it's actually fit for consumption."
    new "Har, har. Don't worry, [protag]. I won't subject you to any of my baking until it's actually fit for consumption.\n哈，哈。别担心，[protag]。在我的烘焙真正能入口之前，我不会拿你当试验品的。"

    old "Anyway, thanks for stopping by. It's is nice to have someone to talk to about things, even the unimportant things of life."
    new "Anyway, thanks for stopping by. It's is nice to have someone to talk to about things, even the unimportant things of life.\n总之，谢谢你顺路来看我。能有人聊聊，哪怕是生活中无关紧要的小事，也真好。"

    old "Hey, Dasyra. What's in the basket?"
    new "Hey, Dasyra. What's in the basket?\n嘿，Dasyra。篮子里是什么？"

    old "Ah, this? Just some ingredients I wanted to experiment with. I'm used to baking with flour, but I met an herbalist who suggested that I try buckwheat instead."
    new "Ah, this? Just some ingredients I wanted to experiment with. I'm used to baking with flour, but I met an herbalist who suggested that I try buckwheat instead.\n啊，这个？只是些我想试验的原料。我习惯用面粉烘焙，但我遇到了一位草药师，她建议我改用荞麦试试。"

    old "What's the difference?"
    new "What's the difference?\n有什么区别？"

    old "Hell if I know. But she seemed to know what she was talking about, so I thought I'd give it a try. It never hurts to try something once, right?"
    new "Hell if I know. But she seemed to know what she was talking about, so I thought I'd give it a try. It never hurts to try something once, right?\n鬼知道呢。但她似乎很懂行，所以我想试试。试试一次总没坏处，对吧？"

    old "I'm normally skeptical of people who claim that I need to try the thing that they are selling. But she seemed nice enough."
    new "I'm normally skeptical of people who claim that I need to try the thing that they are selling. But she seemed nice enough.\n我通常对那种声称我得试试他们在卖的东西的人持怀疑态度。不过她人看起来够和善。"

    old "Wait. You bought the buckwheat from the same person who convinced you that trying buckwheat was a good idea?"
    new "Wait. You bought the buckwheat from the same person who convinced you that trying buckwheat was a good idea?\n等等。你从同一个人那里买的荞麦，就是那个说服你试荞麦是好主意的人？"

    old "I know, I know. It does skew her incentives somewhat. But the herbalist I was talking to happened to be a dwarf, and in Grimoire, dwarves seem to do each other right."
    new "I know, I know. It does skew her incentives somewhat. But the herbalist I was talking to happened to be a dwarf, and in Grimoire, dwarves seem to do each other right.\n我知道，我知道。这确实让她的动机有点歪。不过跟我聊的那位草药师恰好是个矮人，而在Grimoire，矮人们似乎彼此照应。"

    old "Where did you manage to find a dwarf in a city like Grimoire?"
    new "Where did you manage to find a dwarf in a city like Grimoire?\n你是怎么在Grimoire这样的城市里找到一个矮人的？"

    old "In one of the dwarven neighborhoods. Where else? You know Grimoire isn't all humans, right?"
    new "In one of the dwarven neighborhoods. Where else? You know Grimoire isn't all humans, right?\n在矮人聚居的街区里啊。还能在哪？你知道Grimoire不全都是人类，对吧？"

    old "Of course, of course. I passed several elves on the way here. Still, dwarves seem to be few and far between. I was actually worried that you'd find yourself feeling out of place in Grimoire."
    new "Of course, of course. I passed several elves on the way here. Still, dwarves seem to be few and far between. I was actually worried that you'd find yourself feeling out of place in Grimoire.\n当然，当然。我来这儿的路上还经过了好几个精灵。不过，矮人似乎少之又少。我其实一直担心，你会觉得自己在Grimoire格格不入。"

    old "Quite the opposite, actually. Like I said, I've found neighborhoods where dwarves congregate, and there seems to be a real sense of solidarity among them. In a weird way, it actually feels more like being at home than when I was living in Hammerhands."
    new "Quite the opposite, actually. Like I said, I've found neighborhoods where dwarves congregate, and there seems to be a real sense of solidarity among them. In a weird way, it actually feels more like being at home than when I was living in Hammerhands.\n恰恰相反。正如我所说，我找到了矮人聚居的街区，他们之间似乎有种真正的团结感。说来也怪，那比我住在Hammerhands时更让我有家的感觉。"

    old "How is that?"
    new "How is that?\n怎么会？"

    old "In Hammerhands, it's a dwarf-eat-dwarf world. Not literally, of course. Our culture frowns upon cannibalism."
    new "In Hammerhands, it's a dwarf-eat-dwarf world. Not literally, of course. Our culture frowns upon cannibalism.\n在Hammerhands，那是个矮人吃矮人的世界。当然，不是字面意思。我们的文化是看不起同类相食的。"

    old "Most cultures do."
    new "Most cultures do.\n大多数文化都这样。"

    old "Anyway, in the dwarf capital, everyone is looking out for themselves. It can be hard to find friends. But in a city like Grimoire, there seems to be this feeling amongst dwarves that we need to stick together."
    new "Anyway, in the dwarf capital, everyone is looking out for themselves. It can be hard to find friends. But in a city like Grimoire, there seems to be this feeling amongst dwarves that we need to stick together.\n总之，在矮人首都，人人都只顾自己。很难交到朋友。但在Grimoire这样的城市里，矮人之间似乎有种我们必须抱团的感觉。"

    old "It's probably different for you as a human."
    new "It's probably different for you as a human.\n对你这个人类来说，情况大概不一样。"

    old "Humans in Grimoire behave in a way similar to what you described of the dwarves in Hammerhands. Lots of people looking out for number one."
    new "Humans in Grimoire behave in a way similar to what you described of the dwarves in Hammerhands. Lots of people looking out for number one.\nGrimoire的人类，行为和你描述的Hammerhands矮人很相似。很多人都在为自己打算。"

    old "But people seem to have this tendency to band together in times of crisis. When everyone faces down a collective threat, they work for the greater good."
    new "But people seem to have this tendency to band together in times of crisis. When everyone faces down a collective threat, they work for the greater good.\n但人们似乎有种在危机时刻抱团的倾向。当每个人都面对共同的威胁时，他们会为更大的利益而行动。"

    old "Have you noticed something similar, being an elf?"
    new "Have you noticed something similar, being an elf?\n作为精灵，你也注意到了类似的事吗？"

    old "Yes, I've noticed the same thing. It can be a subtle thing. I wouldn't go as far as to say that every dwarf here wants to be my friend. But they do seem to be more trusting. Whenever we pass each other on the street, we smile at each other."
    new "Yes, I've noticed the same thing. It can be a subtle thing. I wouldn't go as far as to say that every dwarf here wants to be my friend. But they do seem to be more trusting. Whenever we pass each other on the street, we smile at each other.\n是的，我注意到了同样的事。那可能是件微妙的事。我不至于说这里的每个矮人都想和我交朋友。但他们确实显得更信任人了。每当我们在街上擦肩而过，都会彼此微笑。"

    old "Surely you've noticed it as well. Dwarves in Grimoire seem to assume the best of other dwarves. Whenever you meet a fellow dwarf, you have an instant rapport."
    new "Surely you've noticed it as well. Dwarves in Grimoire seem to assume the best of other dwarves. Whenever you meet a fellow dwarf, you have an instant rapport.\n你肯定也注意到了。Grimoire的矮人似乎总把其他矮人往好处想。每当你遇到一个矮人同胞，立刻就有种默契。"

    old "I'm not sure what it's like for you, being that you're, ah..."
    new "I'm not sure what it's like for you, being that you're, ah...\n我不确定你是什么感受，毕竟你是，呃……"

    old "It's not a dirty word, Dasyra. I'm a half elf."
    new "It's not a dirty word, Dasyra. I'm a half elf.\n这又不是脏话，Dasyra。我是个半精灵。"

    old "I think I understand the sense of solidarity you describe. Personally, I'm a bit envious. I always feel like a bit of an outsider, whether I'm among elves or humans. And a lot of other half elfs try to pass themselves off as elves, so when someone like me shows up, there's a bit of tension. Maybe they're afraid of being exposed."
    new "I think I understand the sense of solidarity you describe. Personally, I'm a bit envious. I always feel like a bit of an outsider, whether I'm among elves or humans. And a lot of other half elfs try to pass themselves off as elves, so when someone like me shows up, there's a bit of tension. Maybe they're afraid of being exposed.\n我想我明白你描述的那种团结感。就我个人而言，我有点羡慕。无论身处精灵还是人类之中，我总觉得自己像个局外人。而且很多其他半精灵都试图把自己冒充成精灵，所以像我这样的人一出现，气氛就有点紧张。也许他们是怕被拆穿。"

    old "Is it hard?"
    new "Is it hard?\n那很难熬吗？"

    old "I live with it."
    new "I live with it.\n我习惯了。"

    old "Anyway, I'm glad to hear that Grimoire has treated you well."
    new "Anyway, I'm glad to hear that Grimoire has treated you well.\n总之，我很高兴Grimoire待你不薄。"

    old "So am I. Thanks for bringing me here, [protag]. When we fled here from Hammerhands, I never dreamed that it might be the city I'd fall in love with."
    new "So am I. Thanks for bringing me here, [protag]. When we fled here from Hammerhands, I never dreamed that it might be the city I'd fall in love with.\n我也是。谢谢你把我带到这里，[protag]。我们从Hammerhands逃到这里时，我从没想过，这会是我爱上的城市。"

    old "Hey, [protag]. How's it going?"
    new "Hey, [protag]. How's it going?\n嘿，[protag]。最近怎么样？"

    old "Just checking in on you. How goes the bread-making?"
    new "Just checking in on you. How goes the bread-making?\n就是来看看你。做面包的事进展如何？"

    old "Ah, that? Well, I gave it a few more tries, and I think I'm just not cut out for baking."
    new "Ah, that? Well, I gave it a few more tries, and I think I'm just not cut out for baking.\n啊，那个？嗯，我又试了几次，我想我天生就不是做烘焙的料。"

    old "Really? You're giving up on it?"
    new "Really? You're giving up on it?\n真的？你要放弃了？"

    old "I wouldn't say I'm giving up as much as I'm resolving to move onto something else. Though, what exactly my new hobby should be, I'm not quite sure of."
    new "I wouldn't say I'm giving up as much as I'm resolving to move onto something else. Though, what exactly my new hobby should be, I'm not quite sure of.\n与其说是放弃，不如说是打定主意转向别的事。不过，我的新爱好具体该是什么，我还不太确定。"

    old "Still, I'm glad that I spent time baking. I learned something about myself in the process."
    new "Still, I'm glad that I spent time baking. I learned something about myself in the process.\n不过，我还是很高兴自己花了时间烘焙。在这个过程中，我更了解了自己。"

    old "What did you learn?"
    new "What did you learn?\n你了解到什么？"

    old "I perform best in times of need."
    new "I perform best in times of need.\n我在危难时刻表现得最好。"

    old "I don't follow."
    new "I don't follow.\n我没听懂。"

    old "When I was a girl, I made bread because it was cheaper than buying it. My bread-making was something born out of poverty. On a certain level, I enjoyed it. But the reason I did it is because I had to."
    new "When I was a girl, I made bread because it was cheaper than buying it. My bread-making was something born out of poverty. On a certain level, I enjoyed it. But the reason I did it is because I had to.\n我还是个女孩时，做面包是因为它比买便宜。我做面包，是穷困逼出来的。从某种程度上说，我乐在其中。但我做这事，是因为我不得不做。"

    old "Now, going back to baking as an adult, I don't approach it with the same sense of severity. It's more of a hobby at this point."
    new "Now, going back to baking as an adult, I don't approach it with the same sense of severity. It's more of a hobby at this point.\n如今，成年后重回烘焙，我不再带着同样的紧迫感了。眼下它更像个爱好。"

    old "Is that a problem?"
    new "Is that a problem?\n那是个问题吗？"

    old "Baking is a science. It requires a lot of attention to detail. When I was a girl working with limited resources, you can be sure that I never spilled anything. Every ounce of flour was accounted for. I paid very close attention to the details."
    new "Baking is a science. It requires a lot of attention to detail. When I was a girl working with limited resources, you can be sure that I never spilled anything. Every ounce of flour was accounted for. I paid very close attention to the details.\n烘焙是一门科学。它需要大量对细节的关注。当我还是个资源有限的女孩时，你可以确信我从不洒漏任何东西。每一盎司面粉都算得清清楚楚。我对细节极其上心。"

    old "But coming back to it as an adult, I just don't approach it with the same level of precision. I'm not as fastidious as I once was. The sense of necessity and pressure is gone. I begin working in the kitchen, and my mind begins to wander. I lose my sense of focus, and I don't concentrate fully on the task in front of me."
    new "But coming back to it as an adult, I just don't approach it with the same level of precision. I'm not as fastidious as I once was. The sense of necessity and pressure is gone. I begin working in the kitchen, and my mind begins to wander. I lose my sense of focus, and I don't concentrate fully on the task in front of me.\n但成年后回到这件事上，我就是没法再以同样的精度去对待它了。我不再像从前那样一丝不苟。那种必要感和压力消失了。我在厨房里开始干活，心思就开始飘走。我失去了专注感，无法把全部心神放在眼前的活上。"

    old "Back then...I was hungry. I knew that my ability to eat depended on my ability to bake. That gave me a kind of vigilance that I can't match now."
    new "Back then...I was hungry. I knew that my ability to eat depended on my ability to bake. That gave me a kind of vigilance that I can't match now.\n那时候……我很饿。我知道自己能不能吃上饭，取决于我能不能烤好面包。那给了我一种如今无法企及的警觉。"

    old "Maybe you just need to try cooking on an empty stomach."
    new "Maybe you just need to try cooking on an empty stomach.\n也许你只是需要饿着肚子做饭试试。"

    old "It's not the same. No matter how I approach it, cooking is a hobby now. I'm not worried about feeding myself, or my mother. I know I won't go hungry now. And because of that, I've lost my edge."
    new "It's not the same. No matter how I approach it, cooking is a hobby now. I'm not worried about feeding myself, or my mother. I know I won't go hungry now. And because of that, I've lost my edge.\n不一样的。无论我怎么对待它，做饭如今只是个爱好。我不再担心喂饱自己，或者我母亲。我知道现在自己不会挨饿了。正因如此，我失去了那股锐气。"

    old "I think that's why I came to like combat so much. There's a certain sense of peril in the throes of combat that I find energizing. When I get injured, it's exhilarating, in a sense. And the closer to death I am, the more focused I feel."
    new "I think that's why I came to like combat so much. There's a certain sense of peril in the throes of combat that I find energizing. When I get injured, it's exhilarating, in a sense. And the closer to death I am, the more focused I feel.\n我想这就是我如此喜欢战斗的原因。战斗的厮杀中有种危险感，让我觉得充满活力。当我受伤时，从某种意义上说，那很令人兴奋。我离死亡越近，就越专注。"

    old "Do you think that's odd? Do you have a similar kind of reaction in extremely stressful situations?"
    new "Do you think that's odd? Do you have a similar kind of reaction in extremely stressful situations?\n你觉得这奇怪吗？你在极端紧张的情况下，也会有类似的反应吗？"

    old "I perform best when the pressure is on and the stakes are high."
    new "I perform best when the pressure is on and the stakes are high.\n我在压力逼近、赌注高昂时表现得最好。"

    old "See, you know what I'm talking about."
    new "See, you know what I'm talking about.\n看，你知道我在说什么。"

    old "I don't know, Dasyra. When I'm in a stressful situation, I tend to perform worse."
    new "I don't know, Dasyra. When I'm in a stressful situation, I tend to perform worse.\n我不知道，Dasyra。我处于紧张状态时，往往会表现得更糟。"

    old "Well, perhaps you got into the wrong line of work, then. I hear that fighting vampires can be pretty stressful."
    new "Well, perhaps you got into the wrong line of work, then. I hear that fighting vampires can be pretty stressful.\n嗯，那你也许是入错了行。我听说打吸血鬼可是相当紧张的。"

    old "I mean, I can hold up under pressure. But I'm most effective when I'm relaxed and feel in control of the situation."
    new "I mean, I can hold up under pressure. But I'm most effective when I'm relaxed and feel in control of the situation.\n我是说，我在压力下撑得住。但我在放松、感觉掌控局面时最有效率。"

    old "So, is that your secret? You always feel like you're in control?"
    new "So, is that your secret? You always feel like you're in control?\n所以，这就是你的秘诀？你总觉得自己掌控着局面？"

    old "I wouldn't say that I crave danger. But when it comes to me, I welcome it with open arms. In fact, part of me is tempted to go and seek it out."
    new "I wouldn't say that I crave danger. But when it comes to me, I welcome it with open arms. In fact, part of me is tempted to go and seek it out.\n我不会说我渴望危险。但当危险找上我时，我会张开双臂迎接它。事实上，我有一部分心思，还真想去主动寻找它。"

    old "That's funny, Dasyra. Looking at you, most people probably wouldn't expect a woman of your stature and constitution to be a thrill-seeker."
    new "That's funny, Dasyra. Looking at you, most people probably wouldn't expect a woman of your stature and constitution to be a thrill-seeker.\n真有趣，Dasyra。光看你的样子，大多数人大概想不到，你这样身材体格的女子会是个寻求刺激的人。"

    old "Think about what I was doing when you met me. I was stealing from a high-powered man with a reputation for ruthlessness for no reason other than to satisfy a personal vendetta. That's not the kind of behavior you'd expect from a mild-mannered person."
    new "Think about what I was doing when you met me. I was stealing from a high-powered man with a reputation for ruthlessness for no reason other than to satisfy a personal vendetta. That's not the kind of behavior you'd expect from a mild-mannered person.\n想想你遇见我时我在做什么。我在从一个以冷酷无情著称的权贵那里偷东西，不为别的，只为泄一己私愤。那可不是一个性情温和的人会做的事。"

    old "True, true."
    new "True, true.\n确实，确实。"

    old "I don't know what it is. Whenever I'm confronted with danger, it feels like everything is up to fate. And in a weird way, that gives me a certain sense of peace."
    new "I don't know what it is. Whenever I'm confronted with danger, it feels like everything is up to fate. And in a weird way, that gives me a certain sense of peace.\n我不知道那是什么。每当我面对危险时，感觉一切都交给了命运。说来也怪，这反而给了我某种平静。"

    old "And that's why you're bad at making bread."
    new "And that's why you're bad at making bread.\n而这就是你做不好面包的原因。"

    old "Ha. Yes, I guess you're right. I just need to find a more dangerous hobby."
    new "Ha. Yes, I guess you're right. I just need to find a more dangerous hobby.\n哈。是啊，我想你说得对。我只是需要找个更危险的爱好。"

    old "Try not to get into too much trouble, okay?"
    new "Try not to get into too much trouble, okay?\n尽量别惹上太多麻烦，好吗？"

    old "Oh, of course. When I said I needed to find a more dangerous hobby, I was just joking. Sort of."
    new "Oh, of course. When I said I needed to find a more dangerous hobby, I was just joking. Sort of.\n哦，当然。我说要找个更危险的爱好，只是开玩笑。算是吧。"

    old "'Sort of?' That doesn't sound very reassuring."
    new "'Sort of?' That doesn't sound very reassuring.\n“算是吧”？这听起来可不怎么让人安心。"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. I'll stay safe. I'm not going to seek out danger. But if danger comes to me, I'm not going to shirk away from it."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. I'll stay safe. I'm not going to seek out danger. But if danger comes to me, I'm not going to shirk away from it.\n别担心，[protag]。我会注意安全的。我不会去主动寻找危险。但危险要是找上我，我也不会退缩。"

    old "Well, that's good to know. If you were the type to run and cower in the face of danger, you wouldn't be very helpful in N'Mar."
    new "Well, that's good to know. If you were the type to run and cower in the face of danger, you wouldn't be very helpful in N'Mar.\n嗯，知道这点很好。如果你是那种一遇危险就逃跑退缩的人，那在N'Mar可帮不上什么忙。"

    old "Well, do whatever you think you need to do, Dasyra. If you want to go thrill-seeking, then venture forth and confront danger."
    new "Well, do whatever you think you need to do, Dasyra. If you want to go thrill-seeking, then venture forth and confront danger.\n嗯，做你认为需要做的事吧，Dasyra。如果你想去寻求刺激，那就放手去冒险，直面危险。"

    old "You seem to be taking this revelation very well. But please, you can rest assured that I have no attention of placing myself in danger's way."
    new "You seem to be taking this revelation very well. But please, you can rest assured that I have no attention of placing myself in danger's way.\n你似乎把这事看得很开。不过请放心，我并没有把自己置于险境的意思。"

    old "I'll enjoy danger when it comes. But I'm not going to deliberately put myself in peril. At least, not until this whole business with N'Mar is done and over with."
    new "I'll enjoy danger when it comes. But I'm not going to deliberately put myself in peril. At least, not until this whole business with N'Mar is done and over with.\n危险来临时，我会享受它。但我不会故意把自己置于危险之中。至少，在N'Mar的整件事了结之前不会。"

    old "Anyway, thanks for hearing me out, [protag]. It feels a little bit crazy for me to hear myself say these things out loud, but in a way, I've come to understand myself better."
    new "Anyway, thanks for hearing me out, [protag]. It feels a little bit crazy for me to hear myself say these things out loud, but in a way, I've come to understand myself better.\n总之，谢谢听我说完，[protag]。听自己把这些话大声说出来，感觉有点疯狂，但从某种程度上说，我更了解自己了。"

    old "[protag]!"
    new "[protag]!\n[protag]！"

    old "Ah, Dasyra. You look excited."
    new "Ah, Dasyra. You look excited.\n啊，Dasyra。你看起来很兴奋。"

    old "Yes, I was actually hoping to talk to you about something."
    new "Yes, I was actually hoping to talk to you about something.\n是的，其实我正想和你谈件事。"

    old "What is it?"
    new "What is it?\n是什么事？"

    old "I've been thinking about what lies ahead for me once our mission is complete."
    new "I've been thinking about what lies ahead for me once our mission is complete.\n我一直在想，任务完成后，等待我的会是什么。"

    old "Well, we've already ruled out the possibility of you going back to baking."
    new "Well, we've already ruled out the possibility of you going back to baking.\n嗯，我们已经排除了你回去做烘焙的可能了。"

    old "I've quite enjoyed serving under you. Getting into fights with fiends, offering the aid of my staff where necessary. Serving as a healer on the front lines."
    new "I've quite enjoyed serving under you. Getting into fights with fiends, offering the aid of my staff where necessary. Serving as a healer on the front lines.\n我很享受在你麾下效力的日子。与恶魔交战，在必要时施展我的法杖相助。在前线担任治疗师。"

    old "Yes, and you're quite good at it."
    new "Yes, and you're quite good at it.\n是的，而且你做得相当出色。"

    old "I'd like to keep on doing it."
    new "I'd like to keep on doing it.\n我想继续做下去。"

    old "How do you plan to do that?"
    new "How do you plan to do that?\n你打算怎么做？"

    old "Right now, I serve under you, and you serve the interests of the council. One day, hopefully, the menace of N'Mar will be no more. But the council will still be there. And I imagine that the council will still have business that needs doing."
    new "Right now, I serve under you, and you serve the interests of the council. One day, hopefully, the menace of N'Mar will be no more. But the council will still be there. And I imagine that the council will still have business that needs doing.\n眼下，我为你效力，而你为议会的利益效力。希望有一天，N'Mar的威胁不复存在。但议会仍会存在。我想，议会也仍会有需要办的事。"

    old "You know, the Empire of man will always have need of special forces to carry out certain tasks."
    new "You know, the Empire of man will always have need of special forces to carry out certain tasks.\n你知道，人类帝国总需要特种部队去执行某些任务。"

    old "You'd rather serve the council of Grimoire than go back to Hammerhands?"
    new "You'd rather serve the council of Grimoire than go back to Hammerhands?\n你宁可为Grimoire议会效力，也不愿回Hammerhands？"

    old "I like Hammerhands well enough, but I feel like Grimoire is more deserving of my loyalty. I've never been particularly fond of the Hammerhands aristocracy, and I'd like to spend as little time around them as possible."
    new "I like Hammerhands well enough, but I feel like Grimoire is more deserving of my loyalty. I've never been particularly fond of the Hammerhands aristocracy, and I'd like to spend as little time around them as possible.\n我挺喜欢Hammerhands的，但我觉得Grimoire更值得我的忠诚。我从来都不怎么喜欢Hammerhands的贵族，我愿意尽量少和他们打交道。"

    old "So, what exactly do you have in mind?"
    new "So, what exactly do you have in mind?\n那么，你具体有什么打算？"

    old "I was going to ask you the same question. Right now, you are effectively my contact with Grimoire's council. Will you continue to be that, even after the business in N'Mar is done and over with? Or should I be acquainting myself with them more directly?"
    new "I was going to ask you the same question. Right now, you are effectively my contact with Grimoire's council. Will you continue to be that, even after the business in N'Mar is done and over with? Or should I be acquainting myself with them more directly?\n我正想问你同样的问题。眼下，你实际上是我与Grimoire议会的联络人。等N'Mar的事彻底了结之后，你还会继续担任这个角色吗？还是说我该更直接地去结识他们？"

    old "I pause a moment, and Dasyra senses my hesitation."
    new "I pause a moment, and Dasyra senses my hesitation.\n我停顿了片刻，Dasyra察觉到了我的犹豫。"

    old "Maybe you're not sure yourself. I can understand that. I was pretty unsure about my own future until a few days ago."
    new "Maybe you're not sure yourself. I can understand that. I was pretty unsure about my own future until a few days ago.\n也许你自己也不确定。我能理解。直到几天前，我对自己的未来也相当迷茫。"

    old "[protag], what's important is that I've decided to pledge my loyalty to Grimoire and the interests of its council members. For now, that means serving under you. Maybe one day, it will mean something different. But know this: for as long as the menace of N'Mar remains at large, you have my complete loyalty."
    new "[protag], what's important is that I've decided to pledge my loyalty to Grimoire and the interests of its council members. For now, that means serving under you. Maybe one day, it will mean something different. But know this: for as long as the menace of N'Mar remains at large, you have my complete loyalty.\n[protag]，重要的是，我已经决定向Grimoire及其议会成员的利益宣誓效忠。眼下，这意味着为你效力。也许有一天，它会意味着别的事。但你要知道：只要N'Mar的威胁一天还在逍遥，你就拥有我完全的忠诚。"

    old "I appreciate the words of affirmation, Dasyra. Having your loyalty is a real privilege."
    new "I appreciate the words of affirmation, Dasyra. Having your loyalty is a real privilege.\n我很感激你的这番话，Dasyra。拥有你的忠诚是真正的荣幸。"

    old "I find Dasyra in a tavern on Grimoire, where I last meet her."
    new "I find Dasyra in a tavern on Grimoire, where I last meet her.\n我在Grimoire的一家酒馆找到了Dasyra，就在我上次见她的地方。"

    old "Hello, [protag]!"
    new "Hello, [protag]!\n你好，[protag]！"

    old "Hello Dasyra. You seem happy."
    new "Hello Dasyra. You seem happy.\n你好，Dasyra。你看起来很开心。"

    old "I am. I just met with Nuala. It's nice to talk with a fellow caster, especially a fellow healer."
    new "I am. I just met with Nuala. It's nice to talk with a fellow caster, especially a fellow healer.\n我是很开心。我刚见了Nuala。能和一位同是施法者、尤其是同是治疗师的人聊聊，真好。"

    old "I'm glad to see that you two are getting along so well. Both of you are valued contributors to our cause."
    new "I'm glad to see that you two are getting along so well. Both of you are valued contributors to our cause.\n我很高兴看到你们俩相处得这么好。你们都是我们事业中宝贵的贡献者。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. I also met with the other party members..."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. I also met with the other party members...\n谢谢，[protag]。我也见了其他队友……"

    old "Something wrong with any of them?"
    new "Something wrong with any of them?\n他们谁有问题吗？"

    old "Oh no, not at all! I just wanted to say...thank you."
    new "Oh no, not at all! I just wanted to say...thank you.\n哦，不，完全没有！我只是想说……谢谢你。"

    old "You know, before... this, I really didn't have many friends. I mean, I knew some people, but this is different."
    new "You know, before... this, I really didn't have many friends. I mean, I knew some people, but this is different.\n你知道，在这……之前，我真的没有多少朋友。我是说，我认识一些人，但这次不一样。"

    old "We are all different. Different races, cultures, we come from very distant places."
    new "We are all different. Different races, cultures, we come from very distant places.\n我们各不相同。不同的种族、文化，来自非常遥远的地方。"

    old "Yet, we are all together in this, and I know that every one of us is doing their best to help each other and to reach our goal."
    new "Yet, we are all together in this, and I know that every one of us is doing their best to help each other and to reach our goal.\n然而，我们在这件事上聚到了一起，而且我知道，我们每个人都在尽最大努力互相帮助，达成我们的目标。"

    old "Exactly! And isn't this amazing? It's like if we're all under some sort of charming spell."
    new "Exactly! And isn't this amazing? It's like if we're all under some sort of charming spell.\n没错！这难道不令人惊叹吗？就好像我们都被施了某种迷人的咒语。"

    old "I think I know the name of that spell: friendship."
    new "I think I know the name of that spell: friendship.\n我想我知道那个咒语的名字：友谊。"

    old "I don't know, Dasyra. Calling the others 'friends' might be a bit too much."
    new "I don't know, Dasyra. Calling the others 'friends' might be a bit too much.\n我不知道，Dasyra。把别人称作“朋友”也许有点过了。"

    old "Some of our companions are here only because of necessity. Because they wouldn't know what to do, or where to go."
    new "Some of our companions are here only because of necessity. Because they wouldn't know what to do, or where to go.\n我们的一些同伴来这只是出于需要。因为他们不知道该做什么，也不知道该去哪里。"

    old "Aww, [protag] why you must always ruin everything?"
    new "Aww, [protag] why you must always ruin everything?\n哎呀，[protag]，你为什么总要扫大家的兴？"

    old "Pardon me?"
    new "Pardon me?\n你说什么？"

    old "You're too cynical. Sure, it may be true that for some people it started as you said. But I can already feel it's different. The bonds of friendship can spring up even where you least expect them."
    new "You're too cynical. Sure, it may be true that for some people it started as you said. But I can already feel it's different. The bonds of friendship can spring up even where you least expect them.\n你太愤世嫉俗了。当然，对有些人来说，事情也许确实像你说的那样开始。但我已经能感觉到不一样了。友谊的纽带可以萌芽，哪怕是在你最意想不到的地方。"

    old "As we fight and adventure together, inevitably we'll get to know better each other, and like each other more."
    new "As we fight and adventure together, inevitably we'll get to know better each other, and like each other more.\n随着我们一起战斗、一起冒险，我们不可避免会更好地了解彼此，也越来越喜欢彼此。"

    old "...I hope you're right, Dasyra. I would like that."
    new "...I hope you're right, Dasyra. I would like that.\n……我希望你说得对，Dasyra。我很乐意如此。"

    old "I'm sure this is what will happen."
    new "I'm sure this is what will happen.\n我确信事情会是这样。"

    old "Dasyra looks up at me and smiles."
    new "Dasyra looks up at me and smiles.\nDasyra抬头看着我，笑了。"

    old "I need to go now, was nice talking to you."
    new "I need to go now, was nice talking to you.\n我得走了，很高兴和你聊天。"

    old "Same for me. Just call me if you need help with anything!"
    new "Same for me. Just call me if you need help with anything!\n我也一样。有什么需要帮忙的就叫我！"

    old "If I'm to go rumor-chasing, a pub seems a good place as any to start."
    new "If I'm to go rumor-chasing, a pub seems a good place as any to start.\n如果我要去追查谣言，酒馆似乎和任何地方一样，都是个不错的起点。"

    old "I spot a trio of burly-looking dwarves huddled around...something."
    new "I spot a trio of burly-looking dwarves huddled around...something.\n我看到三个魁梧的矮人，围在一起……不知在看什么。"

    old "Eh, what are you looking at?"
    new "Eh, what are you looking at?\n呃，你在看什么？"

    old "Nothing at all. I was just passing by."
    new "Nothing at all. I was just passing by.\n没什么。我只是路过。"

    old "Well then, keep walking."
    new "Well then, keep walking.\n那就继续走。"

    old "I turn my back on the dwarves, and begin shuffling away."
    new "I turn my back on the dwarves, and begin shuffling away.\n我背对那几个矮人，开始拖着步子离开。"

    old "What is it there that's caught your interest, boys?"
    new "What is it there that's caught your interest, boys?\n是什么东西让你们这么感兴趣，伙计们？"

    old "Why the hell do you care?"
    new "Why the hell do you care?\n关你屁事？"

    old "I don't care particularly, I was just curious."
    new "I don't care particularly, I was just curious.\n我倒不怎么在意，只是好奇。"

    old "Well, maybe you should mind your own damn business."
    new "Well, maybe you should mind your own damn business.\n那你也许该管好自己的破事。"

    old "I was just looking at your stupid face."
    new "I was just looking at your stupid face.\n我只是在看你那张蠢脸。"

    old "I'm sorry, little piggy. I must not have heard you right. What was it that you were just saying?"
    new "I'm sorry, little piggy. I must not have heard you right. What was it that you were just saying?\n抱歉，小猪。我刚才怕是听错了。你刚才说什么来着？"

    old "I was saying, this little piggy is in the market for some half-wit oafs like you who want to start shit."
    new "I was saying, this little piggy is in the market for some half-wit oafs like you who want to start shit.\n我在说，这只小猪正要找几个像你这样想找茬的蠢货。"

    old "The ringleader laughs."
    new "The ringleader laughs.\n领头的那个笑了起来。"

    old "I can tell that you're not from around here, so I'll give you one more chance. There's three of us, and one of you. Now, what do you have to say?"
    new "I can tell that you're not from around here, so I'll give you one more chance. There's three of us, and one of you. Now, what do you have to say?\n我看得出你不是本地人，所以再给你一次机会。我们有三个人，你只有一个。现在，你还有什么要说的？"

    old "Help!"
    new "Help!\n救命！"

    old "I hear the cry of a woman's voice."
    new "I hear the cry of a woman's voice.\n我听到一个女人的呼喊声。"

    old "Shut up, you dumb bitch."
    new "Shut up, you dumb bitch.\n闭嘴，你这个蠢货。"

    old "I hear the sound of a slap, followed by a slight whimper."
    new "I hear the sound of a slap, followed by a slight whimper.\n我听到一记耳光声，接着是一声轻微的呜咽。"

    old "I don't think that you want to mix yourself up in this business. Just turn around, and walk away."
    new "I don't think that you want to mix yourself up in this business. Just turn around, and walk away.\n我想你并不想掺和进这档子事。转身走开吧。"

    old "I don't think I can leave in good conscience until I know what you boys are up to."
    new "I don't think I can leave in good conscience until I know what you boys are up to.\n在弄清你们这伙人想干什么之前，我良心上过不去，走不了。"

    old "If you need to know, she's a thief. We were just relieving her of her stolen property."
    new "If you need to know, she's a thief. We were just relieving her of her stolen property.\n如果你非要知道，她是个小偷。我们只是要让她交出偷来的东西。"

    old "What did she steal?"
    new "What did she steal?\n她偷了什么？"

    old "It's no business of yours."
    new "It's no business of yours.\n这不关你的事。"

    old "I think it is my business."
    new "I think it is my business.\n我觉得这就是我的事。"

    old "We don't answer to you. If you want a piece of me, just try and take it."
    new "We don't answer to you. If you want a piece of me, just try and take it.\n我们不向你交代。你要是想找我麻烦，尽管放马过来。"

    old "You're right, it is none of my business."
    new "You're right, it is none of my business.\n你说得对，这不关我的事。"

    old "I turn my back and begin walking away."
    new "I turn my back and begin walking away.\n我转过身，开始走开。"

    old "Get your damn hands off her."
    new "Get your damn hands off her.\n把你的脏手从她身上拿开。"

    old "If you feel that strongly about it, why don't you come and make us?"
    new "If you feel that strongly about it, why don't you come and make us?\n你要真这么在意，怎么不过来逼我们拿开？"

    old "They have me outnumbered three to one. I hate to play the part of a coward, but a wise man doesn't pick battles he can't handle."
    new "They have me outnumbered three to one. I hate to play the part of a coward, but a wise man doesn't pick battles he can't handle.\n他们以三对一压过我。我讨厌扮演懦夫的角色，但聪明人不会去打一场自己应付不来的架。"

    old "That was a cheap shot."
    new "That was a cheap shot.\n刚才那一下真够卑鄙的。"

    old "What are you slovenly bastards up to?"
    new "What are you slovenly bastards up to?\n你们这群邋遢的混蛋在搞什么？"

    old "I look over my shoulder and see another dwarf has joined the scene."
    new "I look over my shoulder and see another dwarf has joined the scene.\n我回头一看，另一个矮人加入了现场。"

    old "Who the hell are you?"
    new "Who the hell are you?\n你他妈是谁？"

    old "My name is Galan."
    new "My name is Galan.\n我叫Galan。"

    old "Well, Galan. I suggest that you move on. There's nothing happening here of interest to you."
    new "Well, Galan. I suggest that you move on. There's nothing happening here of interest to you.\n好，Galan。我劝你继续赶路。这里没有你感兴趣的事。"

    old "I catch sight of a female dwarf. One of the slovenly drunks has hold of both her arms and is pinning them behind her back. A disgusting grin is plastered across his wide face."
    new "I catch sight of a female dwarf. One of the slovenly drunks has hold of both her arms and is pinning them behind her back. A disgusting grin is plastered across his wide face.\n我看到一名女矮人。其中一个邋遢的醉汉抓住她的双臂，反扭在背后。他那张宽脸上挂着一个令人作呕的笑容。"

    old "I don't think that this is a fight I can walk away from in good conscience."
    new "I don't think that this is a fight I can walk away from in good conscience.\n我不认为这是一场我在良心上能转身离开的架。"

    old "I pick up a rock at throw it at the fat dwarf restraining the woman."
    new "I pick up a rock at throw it at the fat dwarf restraining the woman.\n我捡起一块石头，朝那个制住女人的胖矮人扔去。"

    old "Hey, fat boy."
    new "Hey, fat boy.\n嘿，胖子。"

    old "Hmm?"
    new "Hmm?\n嗯？"

    old "The fat dwarf turns toward me, just in time for the rock to hit him square in the forehead. The female dwarf dashes forward to escape his lunge, and picks a staff up off the ground."
    new "The fat dwarf turns toward me, just in time for the rock to hit him square in the forehead. The female dwarf dashes forward to escape his lunge, and picks a staff up off the ground.\n那胖矮人朝我转过身来，石头正好不偏不倚砸中他的额头。那女矮人猛地向前冲去，躲开他扑来的身子，从地上捡起一根法杖。"

    old "Thanks, stranger. The name's Dasyra."
    new "Thanks, stranger. The name's Dasyra.\n谢了，陌生人。我叫Dasyra。"

    old "The surly dwarf draws several daggers from his pouch and points one of them at me."
    new "The surly dwarf draws several daggers from his pouch and points one of them at me.\n那个凶巴巴的矮人从袋子里抽出几把匕首，用其中一把指着我。"

    old "You're going to wish you hadn't done that."
    new "You're going to wish you hadn't done that.\n你会后悔这么做的。"

    old "So, you have a few daggers. Lets see if they can match up to my hammer."
    new "So, you have a few daggers. Lets see if they can match up to my hammer.\n所以，你有几把匕首。我们瞧瞧它们敌不敌得过我的锤子。"

    old "Come on, boys. Let's show these idiots what we're made of."
    new "Come on, boys. Let's show these idiots what we're made of.\n上吧，伙计们。让这些白痴看看我们的厉害。"

    old "The two other dwarves draw their weapons."
    new "The two other dwarves draw their weapons.\n另外两个矮人拔出了武器。"

    old "Dasyra grasps her staff, holding it in a defensive posture."
    new "Dasyra grasps her staff, holding it in a defensive posture.\nDasyra握紧她的法杖，摆出防御的架势。"

    old "You like to pick on the weak. But there's three of us now. Are you really ready for a fair fight?"
    new "You like to pick on the weak. But there's three of us now. Are you really ready for a fair fight?\n你们喜欢欺负弱者。但现在我们有三个了。你们真的准备好打一场公平的架了吗？"

    old "I was born ready to beat down little pigs like you."
    new "I was born ready to beat down little pigs like you.\n我生来就准备好揍扁你们这样的小猪了。"

    old "I lunge at the nearest dwarf, driving my fist into his face. He stumbles two steps back and topples onto the ground."
    new "I lunge at the nearest dwarf, driving my fist into his face. He stumbles two steps back and topples onto the ground.\n我冲向最近的矮人，一拳砸在他脸上。他踉跄退了两步，仰面摔倒在地。"

    old "I turn my attention to the other two dwarves."
    new "I turn my attention to the other two dwarves.\n我把注意力转向另外两个矮人。"

    old "There's the girl I heard earlier. One of the dwarves is restraining her from behind while the other turns toward me."
    new "There's the girl I heard earlier. One of the dwarves is restraining her from behind while the other turns toward me.\n那是我先前听到声音的姑娘。其中一个矮人从背后制住她，另一个则朝我转过身来。"

    old "I lunge forward and knock him off balance, then give him to the chest. He hits the ground with a thud, and I give him a kick to the ribs for good measure."
    new "I lunge forward and knock him off balance, then give him to the chest. He hits the ground with a thud, and I give him a kick to the ribs for good measure.\n我猛冲向前，撞得他失去平衡，然后一拳打在他胸口。他砰的一声摔在地上，我又补上一脚踹在他肋部。"

    old "The last remaining dwarf lets go of the woman and reaches down to pick a rock off the ground."
    new "The last remaining dwarf lets go of the woman and reaches down to pick a rock off the ground.\n最后一个矮人放开了那个女人，俯身从地上捡起一块石头。"

    old "None of that."
    new "None of that.\n休想。"

    old "I deliver a spinning kick, knocking the rock out of his hands. He looks up at me in panic, and falls to the ground, cowering."
    new "I deliver a spinning kick, knocking the rock out of his hands. He looks up at me in panic, and falls to the ground, cowering.\n我踢出一记旋踢，把石头从他手中踢飞。他惊慌地抬头看我，摔倒在地，瑟缩着。"

    old "Are you alright, miss?"
    new "Are you alright, miss?\n你没事吧，小姐？"

    old "I think I'm alright. Do you have a name for me to thank you by?"
    new "I think I'm alright. Do you have a name for me to thank you by?\n我想我没事。你叫什么名字？我好谢谢你。"

    old "I'm [protag]."
    new "I'm [protag].\n我是[protag]。"

    old "I owe you a debt of gratitude, [protag]. My name is Dasyra."
    new "I owe you a debt of gratitude, [protag]. My name is Dasyra.\n我欠你一份恩情，[protag]。我叫 Dasyra。"

    old "What were these men bothering you about?"
    new "What were these men bothering you about?\n这些人在找你什么麻烦？"

    old "This brooch of mine. It was my mother's. One of them spotted it and claimed that I had stolen it."
    new "This brooch of mine. It was my mother's. One of them spotted it and claimed that I had stolen it.\n是我这枚胸针。它是我母亲的。他们中有个人看见了，就说是我偷的。"

    old "Well, I think that-"
    new "Well, I think that-\n嗯，我觉得——"

    old "Watch out!"
    new "Watch out!\n当心！"

    old "I turn my head just in time to see the punch coming at me. I feel the impact hit my jaw and suddenly the world begins spinning around me. I stumble forward several steps and collapse onto the ground."
    new "I turn my head just in time to see the punch coming at me. I feel the impact hit my jaw and suddenly the world begins spinning around me. I stumble forward several steps and collapse onto the ground.\n我及时转过头，正好看到那一拳朝我挥来。我感觉到拳头砸中了下巴，突然间整个世界都开始天旋地转。我踉跄着向前几步，倒在了地上。"

    old "Arrogant fool. Don't start a street brawl unless you know how to deliver a knockout punch."
    new "Arrogant fool. Don't start a street brawl unless you know how to deliver a knockout punch.\n傲慢的蠢货。没本事一拳把人打趴下，就别在街上寻衅滋事。"

    old "My name's Galan. And I don't take kindly to those who prey on the weak."
    new "My name's Galan. And I don't take kindly to those who prey on the weak.\n我叫 Galan。我最看不惯欺负弱者的人。"

    old "And I don't take kindly to those who stick their nose in business that isn't theirs."
    new "And I don't take kindly to those who stick their nose in business that isn't theirs.\n而我最看不惯那些多管闲事的人。"

    old "The surly dwarf pulls out several daggers."
    new "The surly dwarf pulls out several daggers.\n那个阴沉的矮人拔出几把匕首。"

    old "This one here already made the mistake of joining a fight they had no business in. Don't make it your mistake as well."
    new "This one here already made the mistake of joining a fight they had no business in. Don't make it your mistake as well.\n这个人已经犯了错，掺和进一场与他无关的打斗。你别再犯同样的错。"

    old "So, you have weapons. Let's see if they can match up to my hammer."
    new "So, you have weapons. Let's see if they can match up to my hammer.\n这么说，你们有武器。那就看看它们能不能敌过我的锤子。"

    old "Come on, boys. Let's show this fool what we're made of."
    new "Come on, boys. Let's show this fool what we're made of.\n上吧，伙计们。让这蠢货见识见识我们的本事。"

    old "The two other dwarves get to their feet and draw their weapons."
    new "The two other dwarves get to their feet and draw their weapons.\n另外两个矮人站起身来，拔出了武器。"

    old "I try to get to my feet, but I struggle under my own weight and fall to the ground again."
    new "I try to get to my feet, but I struggle under my own weight and fall to the ground again.\n我试着站起来，却在自身体重下挣扎着，又摔回地上。"

    old "Looks like that sucker punch got the better of you. Hold still for a moment."
    new "Looks like that sucker punch got the better of you. Hold still for a moment.\n看来那一记偷袭把你打得不轻。先别动。"

    old "Dasyra kneels down next to me, places her hand on my forehead, and mumbles a chant I can't quite hear."
    new "Dasyra kneels down next to me, places her hand on my forehead, and mumbles a chant I can't quite hear.\nDasyra 在我身边跪下，把手放到我额头上，低声念着我听不太清的一段咒语。"

    old "Can you stand now?"
    new "Can you stand now?\n现在你能站起来了吗？"

    old "To my surprise, I find that I have no difficulty in getting to my feet."
    new "To my surprise, I find that I have no difficulty in getting to my feet.\n让我惊讶的是，我发现自己毫不费力就站了起来。"

    old "How did you-"
    new "How did you-\n你是怎么——"

    old "No time to explain. They've drawn weapons."
    new "No time to explain. They've drawn weapons.\n没时间解释了。他们已经拔了武器。"

    old "Dasyra points her staff at the leader of the slovenly dwarves."
    new "Dasyra points her staff at the leader of the slovenly dwarves.\nDasyra 用法杖指向那群邋遢矮人的头目。"

    old "Ugh..."
    new "Ugh...\n呃……"

    old "What the hell just happened here?"
    new "What the hell just happened here?\n这里到底发生了什么事？"

    old "These three men were harassing this woman."
    new "These three men were harassing this woman.\n这三个男人在骚扰这位女士。"

    old "These three men are members of the Arasmas estate guard. If they had a quarrel with this woman, it was for good reason. And for the three of you to assault them as a group is a serious crime."
    new "These three men are members of the Arasmas estate guard. If they had a quarrel with this woman, it was for good reason. And for the three of you to assault them as a group is a serious crime.\n这三个男人是 Arasmas 庄园的守卫。若他们与这位女士起了争执，那定有正当缘由。而你们三人结伙袭击他们，是重罪。"

    old "What? They had no uniforms! How could we know?"
    new "What? They had no uniforms! How could we know?\n什么？他们又没穿制服！我们怎么知道？"

    old "Silence!"
    new "Silence!\n闭嘴！"

    old "You may have caught these men at a disadvantage, but I can assure you that you'll be held to account for your actions. Guards!"
    new "You may have caught these men at a disadvantage, but I can assure you that you'll be held to account for your actions. Guards!\n你们或许趁这几人不备占了便宜，但我向你们保证，你们会为自己的行为负责。守卫！"

    old "What did you fools expect to happen? You don't cross weapons with members of the guards of house Arasmas and expect to come out on top."
    new "What did you fools expect to happen? You don't cross weapons with members of the guards of house Arasmas and expect to come out on top.\n你们这些蠢货以为会怎样？跟 Arasmas 家族的守卫刀兵相向，还想讨着好？"

    old "Hold up. What happened here?"
    new "Hold up. What happened here?\n等等。这里出了什么事？"

    old "Captain! We just dispatched these troublemakers."
    new "Captain! We just dispatched these troublemakers.\n队长！我们刚刚收拾了这几个闹事的。"

    old "What did they do?"
    new "What did they do?\n他们做了什么？"

    old "The surly dwarf points at Dasyra."
    new "The surly dwarf points at Dasyra.\n那个阴沉的矮人指向 Dasyra。"

    old "We caught this one stealing. When we confronted the woman, her two companions drew weapons on us. We had no choice but to subdue them by force."
    new "We caught this one stealing. When we confronted the woman, her two companions drew weapons on us. We had no choice but to subdue them by force.\n我们抓到她偷东西。等我们上前盘问这女人时，她的两个同伴就朝我们拔了武器。我们别无选择，只能动武制服他们。"

    old "That's not-"
    new "That's not-\n不是那样——"

    old "Silence. Assaulting a guard with a deadly weapon is a serious charge. These men had the legal authority to strike you dead in their own self defense. You should be grateful that things did not go further. Guards, arrest these three."
    new "Silence. Assaulting a guard with a deadly weapon is a serious charge. These men had the legal authority to strike you dead in their own self defense. You should be grateful that things did not go further. Guards, arrest these three.\n闭嘴。持致命武器袭击守卫是重罪。这些人本有权正当防卫，当场把你击毙都不为过。事情没闹到那一步，你们该心存感激。守卫，把这三人抓起来。"

    old "As assailants who have committed crimes against the Arasmas estate, you will be held here to await trial and sentencing at the hands of our Lord Arasmas. Your hearing will be held tomorrow morning."
    new "As assailants who have committed crimes against the Arasmas estate, you will be held here to await trial and sentencing at the hands of our Lord Arasmas. Your hearing will be held tomorrow morning.\n作为对 Arasmas 庄园犯下罪行的袭击者，你们将被关押在此，等候我们的 Arasmas 大人亲自审判量刑。你们的听证会将于明早举行。"

    old "The windowless iron door slams shut, leaving us alone with only each other and the rats for company."
    new "The windowless iron door slams shut, leaving us alone with only each other and the rats for company.\n没有窗户的铁门砰地关上，只剩下我们彼此，还有老鼠作伴。"

    old "Have either of you got plans for escape?"
    new "Have either of you got plans for escape?\n你们俩有逃出去的打算吗？"

    old "What if we just wait it out and let ourselves go to trial? Ultimately, it will be the word of us three against the three guards. I'm sure that we can explain our case against them, especially since the thievery charge will hold no weight. We can claim that we were acting in self defense."
    new "What if we just wait it out and let ourselves go to trial? Ultimately, it will be the word of us three against the three guards. I'm sure that we can explain our case against them, especially since the thievery charge will hold no weight. We can claim that we were acting in self defense.\n要不我们干脆等着，去接受审判呢？归根结底，就是我们三人跟那三个守卫各执一词。我相信我们能把对质他们的案子说清楚，尤其那个偷窃的指控根本站不住脚。我们可以声称自己是出于自卫。"

    old "I wouldn't expect a fair trial. Old Edgar's not the type to listen to reason."
    new "I wouldn't expect a fair trial. Old Edgar's not the type to listen to reason.\n我可不敢指望什么公正的审判。老 Edgar 可不是讲道理的人。"

    old "Edgar Arasmas only cares about the wealth of his own estate. There's not a chance he'll side against his own men. It would undermine the credibility of his family's name."
    new "Edgar Arasmas only cares about the wealth of his own estate. There's not a chance he'll side against his own men. It would undermine the credibility of his family's name.\nEdgar Arasmas 只在乎自己庄园的财富。他绝不可能护着自己人以外的人。那会损害他家族名声的信誉。"

    old "But the trial has to be public. There has to be some accountability."
    new "But the trial has to be public. There has to be some accountability.\n可审判必须公开。总得有个说法。"

    old "Here is how I expect the trial to go. We will be pulled from the dungeon, one at a time, to testify in our own defense."
    new "Here is how I expect the trial to go. We will be pulled from the dungeon, one at a time, to testify in our own defense.\n我料想审判会是这样：我们会一个个被带出地牢，为自己辩护作证。"

    old "Three separate trials, each one pitting the word of the lone defendant against three Arasmas guards. The word of three men versus the word of one will make it trivial for Arasmas to find the defendant guilty."
    new "Three separate trials, each one pitting the word of the lone defendant against three Arasmas guards. The word of three men versus the word of one will make it trivial for Arasmas to find the defendant guilty.\n三场分开的审判，每场都是孤身一人的被告去对三个 Arasmas 守卫的证词。三人的证词对一人的证词，Arasmas 要判被告有罪简直易如反掌。"

    old "But the defendant can claim there were other witnesses being held in confinement."
    new "But the defendant can claim there were other witnesses being held in confinement.\n但被告可以声称还有其他证人被关押着。"

    old "Arasmas can deny that the two others are locked up and claim that they fled the scene and were not available to testify. I'm sure that this dungeon is filled with hidden rooms that he could use to hide any one of us from the public eye. We may be in one of them right now."
    new "Arasmas can deny that the two others are locked up and claim that they fled the scene and were not available to testify. I'm sure that this dungeon is filled with hidden rooms that he could use to hide any one of us from the public eye. We may be in one of them right now.\nArasmas 可以否认另外两人被关押，声称他们逃离了现场、无法出庭作证。我相信这地牢里满是暗室，他能借此把我们中的任何一个人藏起来，不让人看见。我们现在待的可能就是其中一间。"

    old "After he's found the first defendant guilty and executes them, he simply repeats the process with the next defendant several days later, claiming that the defendant was just recently apprehended and arrested."
    new "After he's found the first defendant guilty and executes them, he simply repeats the process with the next defendant several days later, claiming that the defendant was just recently apprehended and arrested.\n等他判第一个被告有罪并处决之后，过几天再对下一个被告如法炮制，声称这人是不久前刚抓获逮捕的。"

    old "If Arasmas wants us to be found guilty and executed, it will happen, make no mistake."
    new "If Arasmas wants us to be found guilty and executed, it will happen, make no mistake.\n如果 Arasmas 想让我们被判有罪、处以死刑，那这事就一定会发生，别抱侥幸。"

    old "And Arasmas certainly wants us dead. If we are found innocent and released, it would be a great embarrassment to his estate."
    new "And Arasmas certainly wants us dead. If we are found innocent and released, it would be a great embarrassment to his estate.\n而 Arasmas 当然巴不得我们死。我们若被判无罪释放，那对他庄园来说是莫大的耻辱。"

    old "So our only way out of here alive is to break ourselves out."
    new "So our only way out of here alive is to break ourselves out.\n所以我们想要活着离开这里，唯一的办法就是自己越狱。"

    old "We won't be breaking out so much as breaking up."
    new "We won't be breaking out so much as breaking up.\n我们要做的与其说是往外逃，不如说是往上挖。"

    old "Galan points up."
    new "Galan points up.\nGalan 向上指了指。"

    old "We're underground. See that opening? That's the surface. That's how we're breathing right now."
    new "We're underground. See that opening? That's the surface. That's how we're breathing right now.\n我们在地下。看到那个开口了吗？那就是地面。我们现在就是靠它呼吸的。"

    old "If we try to dig ourselves out, we'll just embed ourselves further in Arasmas's underground webs. The only way to go is up. We're thirty, maybe forty feet underground."
    new "If we try to dig ourselves out, we'll just embed ourselves further in Arasmas's underground webs. The only way to go is up. We're thirty, maybe forty feet underground.\n我们要是往外挖，只会更深地陷进 Arasmas 的地下网里。唯一的出路是向上。我们现在在地下三十、也许四十英尺深。"

    old "Well, I don't think any of us are that tall. Even if we stacked ourselves up, standing on each other's shoulders, we might get to half of that height."
    new "Well, I don't think any of us are that tall. Even if we stacked ourselves up, standing on each other's shoulders, we might get to half of that height.\n嗯，我觉得我们谁也没那么高。就算叠起来、踩在彼此肩膀上，大概也只够到一半的高度。"

    old "Right. Which means we need to build ourselves a ladder."
    new "Right. Which means we need to build ourselves a ladder.\n没错。也就是说我们得给自己造一架梯子。"

    old "I look around the room. I see nothing apart from brick walls and a dirt floor. The only items of note are some metal restraints on the floor, and a few rats which thankfully seem to be keeping to themselves."
    new "I look around the room. I see nothing apart from brick walls and a dirt floor. The only items of note are some metal restraints on the floor, and a few rats which thankfully seem to be keeping to themselves.\n我环顾房间，除了砖墙和泥地，什么也没看到。唯一显眼的东西就是地上的几副金属镣铐，还有几只老鼠——幸好它们看起来只顾着自己，不搭理我们。"

    old "Not a lot to build a ladder from."
    new "Not a lot to build a ladder from.\n可用来造梯子的材料不多。"

    old "Galan walks to the wall and runs a finger along the mortar between two bricks. The mortar begins to flake away."
    new "Galan walks to the wall and runs a finger along the mortar between two bricks. The mortar begins to flake away.\nGalan 走到墙边，用手指沿着两块砖之间的灰浆划了一下。灰浆开始簌簌剥落。"

    old "We can remove bricks in the wall to give ourselves footholds and hand holds to climb."
    new "We can remove bricks in the wall to give ourselves footholds and hand holds to climb.\n我们可以把墙上的砖抠出来，给自己弄出攀爬用的落脚点和抓手。"

    old "Look what I've found."
    new "Look what I've found.\n看我找到了什么。"

    old "Dasyra holds up a broken metal chain link."
    new "Dasyra holds up a broken metal chain link.\nDasyra 举起一截断掉的金属链环。"

    old "Found this in an an old broken set of leg irons over there in the corner. Might be good for digging."
    new "Found this in an an old broken set of leg irons over there in the corner. Might be good for digging.\n在那边角落里一副破旧的脚镣里找到的。说不定挖起来好用。"

    old "Dasyra hands the metal link to Galan."
    new "Dasyra hands the metal link to Galan.\nDasyra 把那截金属链环递给 Galan。"

    old "Well, iron is harder than old mortar. This will make a fine digging tool, I think."
    new "Well, iron is harder than old mortar. This will make a fine digging tool, I think.\n嗯，铁可比老灰浆硬。我想这会是件不错的挖掘工具。"

    old "We should chip away at the mortar and leave the bricks in the wall until we're ready to climb out. We wouldn't want our escape route to be seen before we're ready to use it."
    new "We should chip away at the mortar and leave the bricks in the wall until we're ready to climb out. We wouldn't want our escape route to be seen before we're ready to use it.\n我们应该先把灰浆凿掉，砖先留在墙上，等准备好爬出去再说。我们可不想在动手之前就让逃跑路线暴露。"

    old "It would be bad if we got caught digging. I'll stand watch at the door. There's no window to see through, but if I keep my ear pressed to the door, I'll be able to hear the guards' footsteps if they come to check on us."
    new "It would be bad if we got caught digging. I'll stand watch at the door. There's no window to see through, but if I keep my ear pressed to the door, I'll be able to hear the guards' footsteps if they come to check on us.\n要是挖的时候被抓个正着就糟了。我去门口望风。那里没有窗户可看，但只要我把耳朵贴在门上，守卫要是过来查看，我就能听见他们的脚步声。"

    old "Well then, I'll get started with digging."
    new "Well then, I'll get started with digging.\n好，那我开始挖。"

    old "I can act as relief for either of you if you need to rest. Let me know if you want me to take over for you."
    new "I can act as relief for either of you if you need to rest. Let me know if you want me to take over for you.\n你们谁要是需要歇会儿，我都可以来顶替。想让我接手就言语一声。"

    old "Sounds like a plan. Let's get to it."
    new "Sounds like a plan. Let's get to it.\n听起来是个好主意。动手吧。"

    old "Ho, Galan."
    new "Ho, Galan.\n嗨，Galan。"

    old "Hey there. Your name's [protag], right?"
    new "Hey there. Your name's [protag], right?\n嘿，你叫[protag]，对吧？"

    old "That's me. Need any assistance over here?"
    new "That's me. Need any assistance over here?\n是我。这边需要帮忙吗？"

    old "If you're asking if I'm getting tired, the answer is no. The digging is easy. But it's quite boring, and I wouldn't mind a conversation partner if you've got nothing to do."
    new "If you're asking if I'm getting tired, the answer is no. The digging is easy. But it's quite boring, and I wouldn't mind a conversation partner if you've got nothing to do.\n你要问我累不累，答案是不累。挖起来挺轻松。就是无聊得很，你要是没事，我倒不介意有个人说说话。"

    old "I glance at the door. Dasyra seems to be going fine."
    new "I glance at the door. Dasyra seems to be going fine.\n我朝门口瞥了一眼。Dasyra 那边似乎一切正常。"

    old "Sure, I can keep you company."
    new "Sure, I can keep you company.\n好啊，我可以陪陪你。"

    old "So, what brings someone like you to the city of Hammerhands? You don't have the look of someone who spends much time in the dwarven lands."
    new "So, what brings someone like you to the city of Hammerhands? You don't have the look of someone who spends much time in the dwarven lands.\n那么，是什么风把你这样的人吹到 Hammerhands 城来的？你看着可不像是常在矮人地界混的人。"

    old "Hmm? What makes you say that?"
    new "Hmm? What makes you say that?\n嗯？何出此言？"

    old "Well, for one thing, your voice sounds entirely too clean. The dwarven lands as a pleasant enough place, but one thing you'll never escape is the endless smog. You can't breathe the air of a city like Hammerhands before your voice starts to get worse for wear."
    new "Well, for one thing, your voice sounds entirely too clean. The dwarven lands as a pleasant enough place, but one thing you'll never escape is the endless smog. You can't breathe the air of a city like Hammerhands before your voice starts to get worse for wear.\n嗯，头一条，你的嗓音听起来太干净了。矮人地界倒也算宜人，但有一样东西你躲都躲不掉——那无休无止的烟尘。只要你在 Hammerhands 这样的城里呼吸上空气，嗓子迟早要被磨得沙哑。"

    old "The air is pretty thick."
    new "The air is pretty thick.\n这空气确实够呛。"

    old "If you find yourself short of breath, just give your nose a good blow."
    new "If you find yourself short of breath, just give your nose a good blow.\n要是觉得喘不上气，就好好擤擤鼻子。"

    old "Thanks for the tip."
    new "Thanks for the tip.\n多谢提醒。"

    old "I pull out a handkerchief and blow my nose into it. I'm shocked to find that my handkerchief has suddenly turned black."
    new "I pull out a handkerchief and blow my nose into it. I'm shocked to find that my handkerchief has suddenly turned black.\n我掏出手帕擤了擤鼻子，吃惊地发现手帕一下子变黑了。"

    old "Frightened by the sight of what just came out of your nose?"
    new "Frightened by the sight of what just came out of your nose?\n被刚擤出来的东西吓着了？"

    old "You could say that."
    new "You could say that.\n可以这么说。"

    old "Galan laughs."
    new "Galan laughs.\nGalan 笑了。"

    old "That's what you've been breathing all day. A bit gross when you see it all collected like that, isn't it? But that's just everyday life in Hammerhands."
    new "That's what you've been breathing all day. A bit gross when you see it all collected like that, isn't it? But that's just everyday life in Hammerhands.\n这就是你一整天呼吸进去的东西。堆在一起看是有点恶心，对吧？可这就是 Hammerhands 的日常。"

    old "So, you're not from around here. That would explain your reckless behavior in the street earlier."
    new "So, you're not from around here. That would explain your reckless behavior in the street earlier.\n这么说，你不是本地人。那就能解释你先前在街上的鲁莽举动了。"

    old "What about you? You joined the fight, too."
    new "What about you? You joined the fight, too.\n你呢？你不也掺和进那场架了。"

    old "Yes, and it was reckless of me, too. But I'm a bit reckless. Not in my nature, but it's a habit I've picked up. A bad habit, though I've had worse."
    new "Yes, and it was reckless of me, too. But I'm a bit reckless. Not in my nature, but it's a habit I've picked up. A bad habit, though I've had worse.\n没错，我也够鲁莽的。不过我这人确实有点鲁莽。倒不是天性如此，是染上的毛病。算个坏毛病，虽然我染过更糟的。"

    old "Worse?"
    new "Worse?\n更糟的？"

    old "I used to be a villain. But I grew tired of it, so I decided to be a hero instead. Not the wisest career choice for someone who values his hide, but it's a marked improvement over my previous lot in life."
    new "I used to be a villain. But I grew tired of it, so I decided to be a hero instead. Not the wisest career choice for someone who values his hide, but it's a marked improvement over my previous lot in life.\n我以前是个恶棍。但后来腻了，就决定改当英雄。对惜命的人来说，这不算最明智的职业选择，可比起我从前那光景，已经是长足进步了。"

    old "You used to be a villain?"
    new "You used to be a villain?\n你以前是恶棍？"

    old "Yup. I'm not all that proud of that chapter of my life. Just doing the best I can to make up for it. Maybe one day I'll have done enough good to make up for the bad."
    new "Yup. I'm not all that proud of that chapter of my life. Just doing the best I can to make up for it. Maybe one day I'll have done enough good to make up for the bad.\n对。我对人生那一段可不怎么自豪。只是尽力去弥补。也许有一天，我做的善事能抵过那些恶行。"

    old "Well, alright then."
    new "Well, alright then.\n嗯，好吧。"

    old "I lean against the wall while Galan continues carving."
    new "I lean against the wall while Galan continues carving.\n我靠在墙上，Galan 则继续凿着灰浆。"

    old "Of course, I don't want there to be any secrets between us. If we're going to be partners in crime here, I don't want you to feel like you can't trust me. And if full disclosure is what it takes to build trust, well, you can have it."
    new "Of course, I don't want there to be any secrets between us. If we're going to be partners in crime here, I don't want you to feel like you can't trust me. And if full disclosure is what it takes to build trust, well, you can have it.\n当然，我不希望我们之间有什么秘密。既然要在这里当犯罪同伙，我不想让你觉得不能信任我。而如果坦诚相告才能建立信任，那好，我全都告诉你。"

    old "Really? That's all it takes for you to open up to someone? Just getting locked in the same cell?"
    new "Really? That's all it takes for you to open up to someone? Just getting locked in the same cell?\n真的吗？要你向人敞开心扉，只需要同关一间牢房就够了？"

    old "We're here because we worked toward a common goal outside. And we're now working toward a common goal inside. You seem like the trustworthy sort."
    new "We're here because we worked toward a common goal outside. And we're now working toward a common goal inside. You seem like the trustworthy sort.\n我们之所以在这里，是因为在外面为共同的目标并肩作战。如今在里头，我们也朝着共同的目标努力。你看着就是值得信赖的那类人。"

    old "Don't you want to know anything more about me?"
    new "Don't you want to know anything more about me?\n你不想再多了解我一些吗？"

    old "Not particularly. Don't care to know much more than I do about missy over there, either. I've been giving you the benefit of the doubt so far, and being that doubt's something so beneficial, I don't have much reason to remove it now, do I?"
    new "Not particularly. Don't care to know much more than I do about missy over there, either. I've been giving you the benefit of the doubt so far, and being that doubt's something so beneficial, I don't have much reason to remove it now, do I?\n倒也不特别想。那边那位小姐，我也不想多打听。到目前为止我一直对你持善意怀疑，既然这怀疑这么有益，我现在也没什么理由撤掉它，对吧？"

    old "I feel comfortable knowing what I do know about you, and I'm not sure knowing more would help me feel any more comfortable. But you can feel free to ask me anything you like. I'll let you know when you're crossing into uncomfortable territory."
    new "I feel comfortable knowing what I do know about you, and I'm not sure knowing more would help me feel any more comfortable. But you can feel free to ask me anything you like. I'll let you know when you're crossing into uncomfortable territory.\n对现在了解到的你，我感到很自在；再多了解，我也不确定会不会更自在。不过你想问我什么都尽管问。等你问到让人不自在的地方，我会提醒你。"

    old "You mentioned sins in your past."
    new "You mentioned sins in your past.\n你提到过你过去的罪孽。"

    old "Yep."
    new "Yep.\n对。"

    old "Can you give me some idea of what you were talking about?"
    new "Can you give me some idea of what you were talking about?\n能大致说说你指的是什么吗？"

    old "Well, subtlety isn't my strong suit, so I'll just tell it to you like it is."
    new "Well, subtlety isn't my strong suit, so I'll just tell it to you like it is.\n嗯，拐弯抹角不是我的强项，那我就直说了。"

    old "I used to be a mercenary. A sellsword, though I eventually came to favor axes and hammers over swords. I had a talent for fighting, and I'd offer that talent to anyone who was willing to pay me."
    new "I used to be a mercenary. A sellsword, though I eventually came to favor axes and hammers over swords. I had a talent for fighting, and I'd offer that talent to anyone who was willing to pay me.\n我以前是个雇佣兵，靠卖刀剑过活，不过后来我渐渐更爱用斧头和锤子。我有打架的天赋，谁愿意付钱，我就把这天赋卖给谁。"

    old "There's a reason I came to favor more brutish weapon. It turned out that my real talent for killing didn't come from any particular skill with a weapon, or some carefully-honed battle sense. No, the thing that made me a great fighter was my uncanny ability to lose my temper."
    new "There's a reason I came to favor more brutish weapon. It turned out that my real talent for killing didn't come from any particular skill with a weapon, or some carefully-honed battle sense. No, the thing that made me a great fighter was my uncanny ability to lose my temper.\n我更偏爱粗笨的武器，是有原因的。原来我杀人的真正天赋，并不来自什么精妙的武器技艺，也不靠久经磨炼的战斗直觉。不，让我成为出色战士的，是我那说来就来的火爆脾气。"

    old "I could do it almost on demand. Still can, actually. And there's this wonderful thing about rage: it gives you great fortitude and tenacity. A fighter fueled by rage does not feel fear or intimidation or fatigue."
    new "I could do it almost on demand. Still can, actually. And there's this wonderful thing about rage: it gives you great fortitude and tenacity. A fighter fueled by rage does not feel fear or intimidation or fatigue.\n我几乎能召之即来。其实现在也还能。愤怒有个妙处：它带给你惊人的坚韧和顽强。被怒火点燃的战士，不会感到恐惧、怯懦，也不会疲惫。"

    old "And while anger may not do great things to a fighter's dexterity, more fights are won by force than finesse. It's hard to find a more forceful fighter than one who is driven by rage."
    new "And while anger may not do great things to a fighter's dexterity, more fights are won by force than finesse. It's hard to find a more forceful fighter than one who is driven by rage.\n虽然愤怒对战士的灵巧并无多大助益，但打赢战斗更多靠的是力量而非巧劲。你很难找到比被怒火驱使的战士更有力量的斗士了。"

    old "You're a berserker."
    new "You're a berserker.\n你是个狂战士。"

    old "A man with a hammer who goes berserk. A berserker. That's a good way of putting it."
    new "A man with a hammer who goes berserk. A berserker. That's a good way of putting it.\n一个抡着锤子、会发狂的男人。狂战士。这个说法不错。"

    old "Anyway, I had a gift for fighting. Seemed it was the only thing I was good at. So I decided to charge for it."
    new "Anyway, I had a gift for fighting. Seemed it was the only thing I was good at. So I decided to charge for it.\n总之，我有打架的天赋。似乎那是我唯一擅长的事。于是我就决定拿它来收费。"

    old "The thing I discovered is that people with the money to hire a mercenary aren't the most scrupulous of folks. In fact, I'm convinced that behind every great fortune, you'll find a crime. You don't get to have large sums of money without taking it from someone."
    new "The thing I discovered is that people with the money to hire a mercenary aren't the most scrupulous of folks. In fact, I'm convinced that behind every great fortune, you'll find a crime. You don't get to have large sums of money without taking it from someone.\n我发现，请得起雇佣兵的人，往往不是什么良善之辈。事实上，我深信每一笔巨额财富背后都藏着罪行。你若不从别人手里夺，是攒不下大钱的。"

    old "There was one fellow who hired me who was not such a man. He was a traveling merchant. A good, honest man. That was his downfall, really."
    new "There was one fellow who hired me who was not such a man. He was a traveling merchant. A good, honest man. That was his downfall, really.\n不过雇我的人里，倒有一个不是这样的。他是个行商，一个老实厚道的好人。这也正是他的祸根。"

    old "This merchant hired me as a bodyguard. He was taking jewelry from Grimoire to Hammerhands, and wanted me along to protect his goods."
    new "This merchant hired me as a bodyguard. He was taking jewelry from Grimoire to Hammerhands, and wanted me along to protect his goods.\n这商人雇我当保镖。他要从 Grimoire 运一批珠宝到 Hammerhands，想让我一路护货。"

    old "Thing was, he didn't have the money to pay me. But he did have the jewelry. So he offered the following arrangement: I would escort him from Grimoire to Hammerhands, and that upon arrival he would sell the jewelry to the waiting vendor and pay me my usual fee."
    new "Thing was, he didn't have the money to pay me. But he did have the jewelry. So he offered the following arrangement: I would escort him from Grimoire to Hammerhands, and that upon arrival he would sell the jewelry to the waiting vendor and pay me my usual fee.\n问题是，他没钱付我。但他手里有那批珠宝。于是他提了个安排：我护送他从 Grimoire 到 Hammerhands，抵达后他把珠宝卖给等候的买主，再按老价钱付我酬劳。"

    old "I had no other work available, so I agreed to do the job on credit. He didn't have any collateral besides the jewelry itself, but that was good enough for me."
    new "I had no other work available, so I agreed to do the job on credit. He didn't have any collateral besides the jewelry itself, but that was good enough for me.\n我手头也没别的活，就同意赊账接下这趟差事。他除了珠宝本身拿不出别的抵押，但对我来说也够了。"

    old "Anyway, I saw the man all the way to Hammerhands. But when we arrived, a small problem was discovered. The buyer insisted that the jewelry must be appraised, you see. And the appraiser told him that the jewelry was counterfeit."
    new "Anyway, I saw the man all the way to Hammerhands. But when we arrived, a small problem was discovered. The buyer insisted that the jewelry must be appraised, you see. And the appraiser told him that the jewelry was counterfeit.\n总之，我把那人一路送到了 Hammerhands。可到了地方，出了个小岔子。买主坚持珠宝必须先鉴定。鉴定师告诉他，这批珠宝是赝品。"

    old "The solution, at this point, was very simple. The merchant only needed to offer the appraiser a bribe. Get him to lie and say the jewelry was legitimate."
    new "The solution, at this point, was very simple. The merchant only needed to offer the appraiser a bribe. Get him to lie and say the jewelry was legitimate.\n到这一步，解决办法很简单。商人只需给鉴定师塞笔贿赂，让他撒个谎，说珠宝是真品。"

    old "The merchant would get his money, the appraiser would take his cut, I would get paid, and the buyer would receive his fake goods and be none the wiser. Ignorance is bliss, don't you know. Everyone leaves happy."
    new "The merchant would get his money, the appraiser would take his cut, I would get paid, and the buyer would receive his fake goods and be none the wiser. Ignorance is bliss, don't you know. Everyone leaves happy.\n商人拿到他的钱，鉴定师分他那一份，我拿到酬劳，买主收下假货还蒙在鼓里。无知是福嘛，你懂的。皆大欢喜。"

    old "I'd seen that exact deception happen dozens of times before. In fact, I figured that kind of trickery was probably exactly how the merchant wound up with the counterfeit jewelry in the first place. Bribing appraisers is simply a matter of course when you're a small-time merchant."
    new "I'd seen that exact deception happen dozens of times before. In fact, I figured that kind of trickery was probably exactly how the merchant wound up with the counterfeit jewelry in the first place. Bribing appraisers is simply a matter of course when you're a small-time merchant.\n这种把戏我先前见过几十回了。其实我猜，商人当初弄到这批假珠宝，八成就是中了同样的骗局。做小本买卖的商人，贿赂鉴定师本就是家常便饭。"

    old "But the damned honest fool wouldn't do it. He couldn't in good conscience sell the jewels knowing they were fake. And that was a problem for us, because suddenly he was left with no way to pay me."
    new "But the damned honest fool wouldn't do it. He couldn't in good conscience sell the jewels knowing they were fake. And that was a problem for us, because suddenly he was left with no way to pay me.\n可那个该死的诚实傻瓜偏不肯。他明知珠宝是假的，良心过不去，卖不出手。这可给我们出了难题——他一下子没辙付我钱了。"

    old "He told me that he would find a way to repay the debt, that he would write me a promissory note, but I was hearing none of it."
    new "He told me that he would find a way to repay the debt, that he would write me a promissory note, but I was hearing none of it.\n他说他会想办法还上这笔债，会给我写张欠条，可我一个字也听不进去。"

    old "I was furious. I couldn't control my rage. And, in that flurry of rage, I did what I had done so many times before. I pulled out my axe and I killed a man. I killed that merchant."
    new "I was furious. I couldn't control my rage. And, in that flurry of rage, I did what I had done so many times before. I pulled out my axe and I killed a man. I killed that merchant.\n我暴怒不已，压不住怒火。就在那阵狂怒之中，我做了过去干过无数次的事。我拔出斧子，杀了一个人。我杀了那个商人。"

    old "The next day, I took the jewelry to another appraiser. I figured I'd bribe him to claim it was legitimate and maybe he could find a vendor for me."
    new "The next day, I took the jewelry to another appraiser. I figured I'd bribe him to claim it was legitimate and maybe he could find a vendor for me.\n第二天，我把珠宝带到另一位鉴定师那里。我寻思着贿赂他，让他说珠宝是真品，说不定他还能帮我找个买主。"

    old "But as it turned out, I didn't need to bribe him. The jewelry had been legitimate the entire time. The first appraiser was a crook who figured that he could extort a bribe out of the merchant."
    new "But as it turned out, I didn't need to bribe him. The jewelry had been legitimate the entire time. The first appraiser was a crook who figured that he could extort a bribe out of the merchant.\n可到头来，我根本不用贿赂他。那批珠宝自始至终都是真品。头一个鉴定师是个骗子，盘算着从商人身上敲一笔贿赂。"

    old "I got a lot of money from selling that jewelry. Far and above what the merchant owed me. I killed that man over nothing. And he was the only one who did nothing wrong."
    new "I got a lot of money from selling that jewelry. Far and above what the merchant owed me. I killed that man over nothing. And he was the only one who did nothing wrong.\n那批珠宝卖了一大笔钱，远远超过商人欠我的数目。我为一文不值的由头杀了那个人。而他，是唯一一个没有做错任何事的人。"

    old "I drank most of that money. I spent many nights alone, thinking about what I'd done, with only ale for company."
    new "I drank most of that money. I spent many nights alone, thinking about what I'd done, with only ale for company.\n那笔钱大半让我喝进了肚。多少个夜晚我独自枯坐，想着自己犯下的罪，只有麦酒作伴。"

    old "There's a part to this story that I didn't mention. The merchant was traveling with his wife and child. They were there when I went to confront the merchant about the debt he owed me."
    new "There's a part to this story that I didn't mention. The merchant was traveling with his wife and child. They were there when I went to confront the merchant about the debt he owed me.\n这故事还有一段我没提。那商人是带着妻儿上路的。我去找他讨债时，他们都在场。"

    old "Their screams still haunt my nightmares. The sound of sheer terror in their quivering voices, the sound of their bones snapping as the iron did its deed."
    new "Their screams still haunt my nightmares. The sound of sheer terror in their quivering voices, the sound of their bones snapping as the iron did its deed.\n他们的惨叫至今缠着我的噩梦。颤抖的声音里满是极度的恐惧，还有铁器落下时骨头碎裂的声响。"

    old "No one knows what I did that day. I left no witnesses, and it's not at all unusual for traveling merchants to simply disappear. But I know what I did."
    new "No one knows what I did that day. I left no witnesses, and it's not at all unusual for traveling merchants to simply disappear. But I know what I did.\n没人知道我那天做了什么。我没留下目击者，而行商凭空失踪也实在不算稀奇。可我知道自己做了什么。"

    old "I'd like to say that I've become a new man, but you can't simply erase your past by claiming to disown it. I still remember standing above their bloody remains, axe in hand. That man was me."
    new "I'd like to say that I've become a new man, but you can't simply erase your past by claiming to disown it. I still remember standing above their bloody remains, axe in hand. That man was me.\n我多想说自己已焕然一新，但过去不是你说断绝就能抹掉的。我仍记得自己手持斧头，站在他们血淋淋的尸首旁。那个人，就是我。"

    old "And no amount of good I do in this life will ever change that. But I still try. Gods, do I try."
    new "And no amount of good I do in this life will ever change that. But I still try. Gods, do I try.\n而这一生无论做多少善事，都改变不了那一切。可我仍在努力。众神在上，我是真的拼了命在努力。"

    old "That's who I am."
    new "That's who I am.\n这就是我。"

    old "I sit in silence as Galan continues to etch away at the mortar in the wall."
    new "I sit in silence as Galan continues to etch away at the mortar in the wall.\n我静静坐着，Galan 继续凿着墙上的灰浆。"

    old "You're a brute. A thug. You're not even a man."
    new "You're a brute. A thug. You're not even a man.\n你是个暴徒，是个恶棍。你根本不算个男人。"

    old "You're right. What you've just said about me is entirely true, and I'm not one to begrudge a man for telling the truth."
    new "You're right. What you've just said about me is entirely true, and I'm not one to begrudge a man for telling the truth.\n你说得对。你刚才说的关于我的每一句都是实话，而我从不会因为谁说了实话就记恨他。"

    old "That monster, who flew into a rage and killed that family, I've done everything I can to escape him. But he keeps coming back to haunt me. After a lifetime of losing your temper, it becomes part of who you are."
    new "That monster, who flew into a rage and killed that family, I've done everything I can to escape him. But he keeps coming back to haunt me. After a lifetime of losing your temper, it becomes part of who you are.\n那个暴怒之下杀了那一家人的怪物，我拼尽一切想摆脱他。可他还是一次次回来纠缠我。当你一辈子都在失控发怒，它就变成了你的一部分。"

    old "I wish I could say I'm now fully in control of my actions, but the truth is, I'm not. And that terrifies me."
    new "I wish I could say I'm now fully in control of my actions, but the truth is, I'm not. And that terrifies me.\n我多希望自己现在能完全掌控自己的行为，可事实是，我做不到。而这让我害怕。"

    old "You're a stronger man than most."
    new "You're a stronger man than most.\n你比大多数人更坚强。"

    old "That's certainly not the response I expected."
    new "That's certainly not the response I expected.\n这可不是我料想的回应。"

    old "You've descended to some of the darkest depths a man's soul can experienced. You embodied the epitome of wretchedness. For a man to come back from that experience, reflect on it honestly, and say that he wants to get better, that's what I call heroic."
    new "You've descended to some of the darkest depths a man's soul can experienced. You embodied the epitome of wretchedness. For a man to come back from that experience, reflect on it honestly, and say that he wants to get better, that's what I call heroic.\n你沉入过一个灵魂所能经历的最黑暗的深渊，集种种不堪于一身。一个人能从那样的经历中爬回来，诚实地反省，并且说出他想要变好——在我看来，那就是英雄。"

    old "The horrible thing you've done will never go away. That will always be part of you. But everything you've done since then—every good deed you've done—that's also the real you. You're endeavoring to be the best person you can be. And I'd never begrudge you for that."
    new "The horrible thing you've done will never go away. That will always be part of you. But everything you've done since then—every good deed you've done—that's also the real you. You're endeavoring to be the best person you can be. And I'd never begrudge you for that.\n你做过的可怕之事永远不会消失，它将永远是你的一部分。但自那以后你所做的一切——每一件善行——那同样也是真实的你。你在努力成为最好的自己。我绝不会为此而怪你。"

    old "You're quite charitable. But I'm afraid that despite my best efforts, that man who flew into a rage and killed that poor family, he's still haunting me to this day."
    new "You're quite charitable. But I'm afraid that despite my best efforts, that man who flew into a rage and killed that poor family, he's still haunting me to this day.\n你真是宽厚。但恐怕，任凭我再怎么努力，那个暴怒之下杀了那可怜一家的男人，至今仍缠着我不放。"

    old "I wish I could keep my temper under wraps. I wish I were fully in control of my actions. But sometimes, my temper takes over. I'm getting better at controlling it. But I fear I will always be at the mercy of its whims."
    new "I wish I could keep my temper under wraps. I wish I were fully in control of my actions. But sometimes, my temper takes over. I'm getting better at controlling it. But I fear I will always be at the mercy of its whims.\n我多希望能把脾气牢牢收住，希望能完全掌控自己的行为。可有时，脾气还是会占了上风。我在学着更好地控制它，但我怕自己终究只能任由它摆布。"

    old "You're just a man, Galan. You've done evil in your life. We all have. And you try to do good. I'm not sure if that makes you a good or virtuous person. But I know that you can't let a single bad action define who you are as a person."
    new "You're just a man, Galan. You've done evil in your life. We all have. And you try to do good. I'm not sure if that makes you a good or virtuous person. But I know that you can't let a single bad action define who you are as a person.\n你只是个凡人，Galan。你这一生做过恶，我们谁都做过。而你也努力行善。我不敢说这能否让你成为好人或德行之人，但我知道，你不能让单单一件恶行就定义你这个人。"

    old "But my rage—the rage that drove me to slay an innocent family—will always be a part of who I am."
    new "But my rage—the rage that drove me to slay an innocent family—will always be a part of who I am.\n可我的愤怒——那驱使我杀害无辜一家的愤怒——将永远是我的一部分。"

    old "I've tried for years and years to chase it away. To control my temper. I'm doing my best to tame it. To remain calm at all times. But there are still times when it takes over. It could happen at any time. And that terrifies me."
    new "I've tried for years and years to chase it away. To control my temper. I'm doing my best to tame it. To remain calm at all times. But there are still times when it takes over. It could happen at any time. And that terrifies me.\n我年复一年想把它赶走，想控制住脾气。我正尽力驯服它，时刻保持冷静。可仍有些时候它会占据上风。它随时可能发作。而这让我害怕。"

    old "You want to know what the funniest thing is? Looking at the walls of this dungeon, I think this might be where I belong. It's like justice caught up with me. This is exactly where a rage-crazed berserker like me belongs. If this was the fate I was subjected to, I wouldn't complain."
    new "You want to know what the funniest thing is? Looking at the walls of this dungeon, I think this might be where I belong. It's like justice caught up with me. This is exactly where a rage-crazed berserker like me belongs. If this was the fate I was subjected to, I wouldn't complain.\n你想知道最讽刺的是什么吗？望着这地牢的墙，我觉得也许我就该待在这里。像是报应终于追上了我。这里正是我这种被狂怒支配的狂战士该待的地方。若这就是我的命，我无话可说。"

    old "If it was just me, I might not even be trying to escape. But you two. You and her, you don't belong here. So I'll keep digging."
    new "If it was just me, I might not even be trying to escape. But you two. You and her, you don't belong here. So I'll keep digging.\n若只有我一个人，我或许连逃都不会逃。可你们俩——你和她，你们不该待在这里。所以我会继续挖。"

    old "Well, I think that I already know enough about you. Enough to trust you as a partner in crime, anyway."
    new "Well, I think that I already know enough about you. Enough to trust you as a partner in crime, anyway.\n嗯，我想我对你已经了解得够多了。总之，足够信任你当我的犯罪同伙。"

    old "I appreciate it."
    new "I appreciate it.\n承蒙信任。"

    old "I think that I've said everything I have to say. I'm making fine progress picking away at this wall. Why don't you go and keep the lady over there company?"
    new "I think that I've said everything I have to say. I'm making fine progress picking away at this wall. Why don't you go and keep the lady over there company?\n我想该说的我都说了。我凿这面墙进展不错。你不如去陪陪那边那位女士？"

    old "Hey, [protag]."
    new "Hey, [protag].\n嘿，[protag]。"

    old "You want me to take over for you?"
    new "You want me to take over for you?\n要我替你吗？"

    old "No need. Keeping watch is easy work. It is dull, though. I wouldn't mind having you here to entertain me."
    new "No need. Keeping watch is easy work. It is dull, though. I wouldn't mind having you here to entertain me.\n不用。望风这活儿轻松，就是无聊。你在这儿给我解解闷，我倒不介意。"

    old "Are you sure I won't be a distraction?"
    new "Are you sure I won't be a distraction?\n你确定我不会让你分心？"

    old "I can hear the pacing of the guards well enough, and they're not even on the same level as us. Trust me, if one of them starts getting close enough to check on us, I'll know it loud and clear."
    new "I can hear the pacing of the guards well enough, and they're not even on the same level as us. Trust me, if one of them starts getting close enough to check on us, I'll know it loud and clear.\n守卫来回踱步的动静我听得一清二楚，他们跟我们根本不在同一层。信我，只要有谁走近到能查看我们的地步，我立刻就能察觉。"

    old "Well, if you say so."
    new "Well, if you say so.\n好吧，你这么说就行。"

    old "I wouldn't say so if it wasn't so."
    new "I wouldn't say so if it wasn't so.\n要不是这样，我才不会这么说。"

    old "So, [protag]. Is this your first run-in with Lord Arasmas's ilk?"
    new "So, [protag]. Is this your first run-in with Lord Arasmas's ilk?\n那么，[protag]。这是你头一回跟 Arasmas 大人那号人打交道吗？"

    old "Me? I've no prior run-ins with the man."
    new "Me? I've no prior run-ins with the man.\n我吗？我以前可从没跟那人打过交道。"

    old "It's rare, the man in this city who doesn't have some sort of business with Edgar Arasmas. Either you're one of the many who he's ingratiated himself to, or one of those he's bent to suit his own ends."
    new "It's rare, the man in this city who doesn't have some sort of business with Edgar Arasmas. Either you're one of the many who he's ingratiated himself to, or one of those he's bent to suit his own ends.\n在这城里，跟 Edgar Arasmas 没有半点瓜葛的人可不多见。你要么是他拉拢过的众多人之一，要么是他为了自己的目的而摆布过的人之一。"

    old "He fancies himself a champion. If he thinks he can get something from you, he's all smiles, but he's no time for those he considers losers."
    new "He fancies himself a champion. If he thinks he can get something from you, he's all smiles, but he's no time for those he considers losers.\n他自诩为豪杰。只要觉得能从你身上捞到好处，他就满面堆笑；可对瞧不上眼的人，他半点时间也不给。"

    old "I wonder, could I bargain or broker some kind of deal with him?"
    new "I wonder, could I bargain or broker some kind of deal with him?\n我在想，我能不能跟他讨价还价，或者谈成什么交易？"

    old "I doubt he'll have an ear for anything you have to say. To him, you're just a street ruffian. Edgar Arasmas sees the fact that you're in his dungeon as sufficient evidence of that."
    new "I doubt he'll have an ear for anything you have to say. To him, you're just a street ruffian. Edgar Arasmas sees the fact that you're in his dungeon as sufficient evidence of that.\n我怀疑他根本不会听你多说一句。在他眼里，你不过是个街头混混。你如今蹲在他的地牢里，在 Edgar Arasmas 看来就足以证明这一点。"

    old "It wasn't always like this. Edgar Arasmas's father was quite a benevolent soul."
    new "It wasn't always like this. Edgar Arasmas's father was quite a benevolent soul.\n并非向来如此。Edgar Arasmas 的父亲是位相当仁慈的人。"

    old "Edgar's father?"
    new "Edgar's father?\nEdgar 的父亲？"

    old "Faberge Arasmas."
    new "Faberge Arasmas.\nFaberge Arasmas。"

    old "I snap my fingers."
    new "I snap my fingers.\n我打了个响指。"

    old "I recognize this name. The famous jeweler."
    new "I recognize this name. The famous jeweler.\n我认得这个名字。那位著名的珠宝商。"

    old "Yes. Old Faberge made quite the fortune from his jeweling. That's really the best thing about the city of Hammerhands, you know. Faberge Arasmas wasn't born into money. He was a tradesman. He earned his fortune through beautiful handiwork, and from that built a house that is now an economic powerhouse."
    new "Yes. Old Faberge made quite the fortune from his jeweling. That's really the best thing about the city of Hammerhands, you know. Faberge Arasmas wasn't born into money. He was a tradesman. He earned his fortune through beautiful handiwork, and from that built a house that is now an economic powerhouse.\n没错。老 Faberge 靠珠宝手艺发了大财。这其实是 Hammerhands 城最了不起的地方，你知道的。Faberge Arasmas 并非生来富有，他是个手艺人，凭一手精美绝伦的手艺挣下家业，又以此建起一座如今举足轻重的豪门。"

    old "Faberge knew what it meant to work for a living. He did his best to bless everyone he came across. He wasn't excessively generous with his wealth, but had a knack for rewarding those who showed their loyalty to him. It's part of what made him such a great businessman."
    new "Faberge knew what it meant to work for a living. He did his best to bless everyone he came across. He wasn't excessively generous with his wealth, but had a knack for rewarding those who showed their loyalty to him. It's part of what made him such a great businessman.\nFaberge 深知靠劳动谋生意味着什么。他尽其所能善待每一个遇见的人。他对财富并不一味慷慨，却很懂得犒赏对他忠心之人。这也正是他成为杰出商人的原因之一。"

    old "After awhile it became common knowledge that if you helped Faberge Arasmas succeed, he would do everything in his power to ensure you enjoyed part of that success."
    new "After awhile it became common knowledge that if you helped Faberge Arasmas succeed, he would do everything in his power to ensure you enjoyed part of that success.\n过了一阵子，人们都知道了：只要你助 Faberge Arasmas 成功，他就会倾尽全力，让你也分享那份成功。"

    old "If Faberge Arasmas is the best of what Hammerhands has to offer, then Edgar Arasmas is some of the worst. Wealth is hereditary, you see, and Edgar possesses none of the positive qualities of his father while wielding the same fortune."
    new "If Faberge Arasmas is the best of what Hammerhands has to offer, then Edgar Arasmas is some of the worst. Wealth is hereditary, you see, and Edgar possesses none of the positive qualities of his father while wielding the same fortune.\n若说 Faberge Arasmas 是 Hammerhands 最优秀的一面，那 Edgar Arasmas 就是最糟糕的一面。财富可以世袭，你瞧，Edgar 手握同样的家产，身上却没有半分父亲的优点。"

    old "Edgar Arasmas doesn't seek out partners, he seeks out tools. He doesn't create wealth, he steals it. And he tramples over anyone who gets in his way."
    new "Edgar Arasmas doesn't seek out partners, he seeks out tools. He doesn't create wealth, he steals it. And he tramples over anyone who gets in his way.\nEdgar Arasmas 找的不是伙伴，而是工具。他不创造财富，只会掠夺。凡挡他道的人，都被他踩在脚下。"

    old "Are you speaking from personal experience?"
    new "Are you speaking from personal experience?\n你这是亲身经历过的？"

    old "Well, yes. Us, right now, here in this dungeon, for instance."
    new "Well, yes. Us, right now, here in this dungeon, for instance.\n嗯，是啊。比如说，此刻待在这地牢里的我们。"

    old "I see what you mean."
    new "I see what you mean.\n我明白你的意思。"

    old "Of course it comes as no surprise that the minions of the new Lord Arasmas are every bit as self-serving and nasty as the man they serve. Preying on the weak is how you get into Edgar's good graces, don't you know. Though, we're not exactly weak are we?"
    new "Of course it comes as no surprise that the minions of the new Lord Arasmas are every bit as self-serving and nasty as the man they serve. Preying on the weak is how you get into Edgar's good graces, don't you know. Though, we're not exactly weak are we?\n当然，新 Arasmas 大人的那些爪牙，跟他们伺候的主子一样自私下作，这也不足为奇。想讨得 Edgar 的欢心，就得欺凌弱小，你不知道吗。不过，我们可不算好欺负的，对吧？"

    old "I'd say we gave them a run for their money."
    new "I'd say we gave them a run for their money.\n我看我们可够他们喝一壶的。"

    old "You know, this is all quite new to me. I'm a healer, not a fighter. I'm not the sort who regularly gets into street fights."
    new "You know, this is all quite new to me. I'm a healer, not a fighter. I'm not the sort who regularly gets into street fights.\n你知道吗，这些对我都挺新鲜。我是个治疗师，不是战士，也不是那种三天两头在街上打架的人。"

    old "You could have had me fooled."
    new "You could have had me fooled.\n你可真会装，我还真信了。"

    old "Dasyra laughs and gives my chest a light shove."
    new "Dasyra laughs and gives my chest a light shove.\nDasyra 笑了，轻轻推了下我的胸口。"

    old "Stop it, you."
    new "Stop it, you.\n去你的，别闹。"

    old "No, I mean it. You held your own out there. It's not a common thing, being able to maintain your composure when angry-looking men start swinging swords at you."
    new "No, I mean it. You held your own out there. It's not a common thing, being able to maintain your composure when angry-looking men start swinging swords at you.\n不，我是认真的。你在外面那一架打得相当不错。当满脸凶相的男人朝你挥剑时，还能沉得住气，这可不常见。"

    old "It's funny. I never fancied myself a fighter, but in that moment of combat, standing by your side, it was like I was operating in a higher state of consciousness. It was like I became suddenly aware of my own mortality, but also aware of the mortality of the men who were attacking me."
    new "It's funny. I never fancied myself a fighter, but in that moment of combat, standing by your side, it was like I was operating in a higher state of consciousness. It was like I became suddenly aware of my own mortality, but also aware of the mortality of the men who were attacking me.\n说来有趣。我从没觉得自己是块当战士的料，可就在交战的那一刻，站在你身边，我仿佛进入了一种更高的意识状态。我忽然意识到自己也会死，同时也意识到那些攻击我的人同样会死。"

    old "Everything else, the entire world of worries and stress I'd been carrying until that moment, they all ceased to be relevant."
    new "Everything else, the entire world of worries and stress I'd been carrying until that moment, they all ceased to be relevant.\n其余的一切——直到那一刻我一直背负的满世界忧虑和压力——全都不再重要了。"

    old "You look like the kind of person who has seen combat before. How do you feel about it? Do you relish combat? Or is it something you dislike?"
    new "You look like the kind of person who has seen combat before. How do you feel about it? Do you relish combat? Or is it something you dislike?\n你看着像是见过战阵的人。你对战斗是什么感觉？是享受，还是厌恶？"

    old "You want to know the truth? I find combat exhilarating."
    new "You want to know the truth? I find combat exhilarating.\n想知道实话吗？我觉得战斗令人热血沸腾。"

    old "It is, isn't it?"
    new "It is, isn't it?\n确实如此，不是吗？"

    old "Is there anything more common to the conscious experience than fighting for your survival? We do it every day. Sometimes it's just as simple as finding a way to feed ourselves."
    new "Is there anything more common to the conscious experience than fighting for your survival? We do it every day. Sometimes it's just as simple as finding a way to feed ourselves.\n有哪件事比为自己的生存而战更贴近人的日常体验呢？我们每天都在做。有时简单到只是想方设法填饱肚子。"

    old "But to have that entire struggle compressed into a few tense moments, to have that opportunity to prove yourself, to say 'I deserve to exist, and I will not be defeated', that's exciting."
    new "But to have that entire struggle compressed into a few tense moments, to have that opportunity to prove yourself, to say 'I deserve to exist, and I will not be defeated', that's exciting.\n可当那整场挣扎被压缩进短短几个紧绷的瞬间，当你有机会证明自己，说出「我配得上活下去，我不会被打倒」——那才叫激动人心。"

    old "You know, if you had met me on the street a day ago and said those words to me, I'd be terrified of you. I'd think you were some kind of crazy."
    new "You know, if you had met me on the street a day ago and said those words to me, I'd be terrified of you. I'd think you were some kind of crazy.\n你知道吗，若是一天前你在街上遇见我，对我说出这番话，我会怕你的。我会觉得你大概是疯了。"

    old "But having experienced what you experienced today, I agree with you completely. The thrill of combat is intoxicating on a physical level."
    new "But having experienced what you experienced today, I agree with you completely. The thrill of combat is intoxicating on a physical level.\n但经历了你今天所经历的一切，我完全赞同你的看法。战斗的刺激，在肉体层面上令人沉醉。"

    old "Those guards probably saw me as an easy target. I'm almost glad I got the chance to show them a thing or two."
    new "Those guards probably saw me as an easy target. I'm almost glad I got the chance to show them a thing or two.\n那些守卫大概把我当成了好欺负的目标。能有机会给他们点颜色瞧瞧，我几乎感到庆幸。"

    old "I've been in battle before. It never stops being terrifying."
    new "I've been in battle before. It never stops being terrifying.\n我以前上过战场。那种恐惧从未停止过。"

    old "Then what made you join the fight in my defense today?"
    new "Then what made you join the fight in my defense today?\n那你今天为什么还出手为我解围？"

    old "Honestly? I was driven by fear. Fear of what might happen to you if I did nothing."
    new "Honestly? I was driven by fear. Fear of what might happen to you if I did nothing.\n说实话？是恐惧驱使我那么做的。我怕自己若袖手旁观，你会遭遇不测。"

    old "Sometimes, oftentimes, the fear of the consequences of my own inaction is greater than my fear of death by the sword. And in those moments, I fight."
    new "Sometimes, oftentimes, the fear of the consequences of my own inaction is greater than my fear of death by the sword. And in those moments, I fight.\n有时，常常是，我对自己不作为所生后果的恐惧，压过了我对死于剑下的恐惧。而在那些时刻，我会战斗。"

    old "Thanks for coming to my rescue."
    new "Thanks for coming to my rescue.\n谢谢你来救我。"

    old "Well, thanks to my heroic actions, you can now live to see the inside of an underground dungeon."
    new "Well, thanks to my heroic actions, you can now live to see the inside of an underground dungeon.\n嗯，多亏了我的英勇举动，你现在可以活着见识见识地下地牢的里头了。"

    old "Dasyra laughs."
    new "Dasyra laughs.\nDasyra 笑了。"

    old "Well, combat is necessary, sometimes."
    new "Well, combat is necessary, sometimes.\n嗯，战斗有时是必要的。"

    old "Dasyra cocks her head and gives me a quizzical look."
    new "Dasyra cocks her head and gives me a quizzical look.\nDasyra 歪了歪头，一脸困惑地看着我。"

    old "Combat is not inherently glorious, nor is it inherently bad. It's simply a means to an end. For some people, that end is, 'That person over there has something that I want for myself.'"
    new "Combat is not inherently glorious, nor is it inherently bad. It's simply a means to an end. For some people, that end is, 'That person over there has something that I want for myself.'\n战斗本身既非光荣，也非邪恶。它不过是达成目的的手段。对有些人来说，那个目的是「那边那个人有我想要的东西」。"

    old "For my self, that end usually 'I would very much appreciate it if those menacing men were incapacitated so that they could menace me no longer'."
    new "For my self, that end usually 'I would very much appreciate it if those menacing men were incapacitated so that they could menace me no longer'.\n对我自己来说，那个目的大抵是「要是那些凶神恶煞的男人被制伏，没法再来威胁我，我会万分感激」。"

    old "I like the way you think."
    new "I like the way you think.\n我喜欢你这思路。"

    old "Do you want to know what's funny?"
    new "Do you want to know what's funny?\n你想知道好笑的是什么吗？"

    old "Dasyra smiles and reaches into her blouse."
    new "Dasyra smiles and reaches into her blouse.\nDasyra 微笑着，把手伸进她的上衣里。"

    old "I still have the brooch."
    new "I still have the brooch.\n胸针还在我这儿。"

    old "That's right. That's why those guards were harassing you in the first place, isn't it? They were trying to take it from you?"
    new "That's right. That's why those guards were harassing you in the first place, isn't it? They were trying to take it from you?\n没错。那些守卫起初找你麻烦，为的就是这个，对吧？他们想从你手里抢走它？"

    old "Yes indeed."
    new "Yes indeed.\n正是。"

    old "They did a pretty thorough job of frisking me on the way in. They got everything from me but my dignity. How did you manage to sneak that past them?"
    new "They did a pretty thorough job of frisking me on the way in. They got everything from me but my dignity. How did you manage to sneak that past them?\n进来时他们把我搜了个遍，搜得可彻底了，除了尊严，我身上什么都给拿走了。你是怎么把它偷带过去的？"

    old "That's a personal subject. I'll leave it up to your imagination."
    new "That's a personal subject. I'll leave it up to your imagination.\n这是私人话题。就留给你自行想象吧。"

    old "Do you regret that you didn't oblige them the first time they asked you to hand it over? I'm not saying that I think extortionists should be rewarded, but sometimes the consequences for standing up for yourself are worse than getting walked all over."
    new "Do you regret that you didn't oblige them the first time they asked you to hand it over? I'm not saying that I think extortionists should be rewarded, but sometimes the consequences for standing up for yourself are worse than getting walked all over.\n他们第一次叫你交出胸针时，你没照做，可曾后悔？我不是说该让敲诈勒索者得逞，只是有时，奋起反抗的代价，比任人践踏还要惨。"

    old "You mean like now?"
    new "You mean like now?\n你是说像现在这样？"

    old "Well, yes."
    new "Well, yes.\n嗯，是啊。"

    old "Dasyra chuckles and cradles the brooch in her palm."
    new "Dasyra chuckles and cradles the brooch in her palm.\nDasyra 轻笑起来，把胸针捧在掌心。"

    old "Well, of course there are few things worse than being held prisoner in a dungeon, awaiting a death sentence. If I had known how things would have played out, obviously I wouldn't have handled things the way that I did."
    new "Well, of course there are few things worse than being held prisoner in a dungeon, awaiting a death sentence. If I had known how things would have played out, obviously I wouldn't have handled things the way that I did.\n嗯，当然，很少有比被关在地牢里等死更糟的事了。若早知事情会闹成这样，我显然不会那样处理。"

    old "But who could have known things would end like this, with the three of us looking at the inside of a cell? Kind of hard to anticipate any of the things that ended up happening, no?"
    new "But who could have known things would end like this, with the three of us looking at the inside of a cell? Kind of hard to anticipate any of the things that ended up happening, no?\n可谁能料到事情会落到这般田地，我们三个会一起望着牢房的内壁呢？到头来发生的这些，哪一件都不好预料，对吧？"

    old "I guess you're right."
    new "I guess you're right.\n我想你说得对。"

    old "What about you? Do you regret what you did?"
    new "What about you? Do you regret what you did?\n你呢？你后悔自己所做的事吗？"

    old "You're asking if I would have just walked by and let those men have their way with you?"
    new "You're asking if I would have just walked by and let those men have their way with you?\n你是问我，当时是不是该径直走过，任由那些人对你为所欲为？"

    old "Well, when you put it like that, it sounds awfully cold. But do you think that I would really be worse off than I am right now if I had just minded my own business?"
    new "Well, when you put it like that, it sounds awfully cold. But do you think that I would really be worse off than I am right now if I had just minded my own business?\n嗯，你这么一说，就显得我格外凉薄了。可你觉得，我当时若只扫门前雪，眼下真会比现在更糟吗？"

    old "Are you upset that I stopped to help you?"
    new "Are you upset that I stopped to help you?\n我停下脚步帮你，你不高兴了？"

    old "Not at all. I was just turning your question around on you. Actually, I wonder if you've got your own hide to worry about."
    new "Not at all. I was just turning your question around on you. Actually, I wonder if you've got your own hide to worry about.\n完全没有。我不过是把你的问题原样抛回给你。其实，我在想，你是不是也该操心操心自己的性命。"

    old "Do you suppose there's someone out there that is wondering why you didn't come home tonight? Do you have a family? Children? A lover? Someone who would be worse off if you never saw the light of day again?"
    new "Do you suppose there's someone out there that is wondering why you didn't come home tonight? Do you have a family? Children? A lover? Someone who would be worse off if you never saw the light of day again?\n你说外面会不会有人在纳闷，你今晚怎么没回家？你有家室吗？有孩子吗？有恋人吗？有没有人，会因为你再也见不到天日而更加难过？"

    old "I can think of a few people who would be quite upset by my disappearance. Some of them putting a lot of faith in me, actually."
    new "I can think of a few people who would be quite upset by my disappearance. Some of them putting a lot of faith in me, actually.\n我能想到有几个人，会因我的失踪而非常难过。其中有些人，其实对我寄予厚望。"

    old "Don't give me any more details. I don't want any of us—me or you—giving ourselves any more reason to feel guilty about what happened today."
    new "Don't give me any more details. I don't want any of us—me or you—giving ourselves any more reason to feel guilty about what happened today.\n别再跟我细说了。我不想让我们任何人——无论是我还是你——再为今天的事多添一份内疚。"

    old "What's done is done. We did what we thought was best, and it's led us here. Let's just do our best to get out, eh?"
    new "What's done is done. We did what we thought was best, and it's led us here. Let's just do our best to get out, eh?\n木已成舟。我们做了自认为最好的事，结果落到了这里。眼下只管尽力逃出去吧，嗯？"

    old "Our friend over there said he was getting pretty lonely. His name's Galan, isn't it?"
    new "Our friend over there said he was getting pretty lonely. His name's Galan, isn't it?\n那边那位朋友说，他一个人怪寂寞的。他叫 Galan，对吧？"

    old "I believe so."
    new "I believe so.\n我想是的。"

    old "Why don't you see if Galan needs a hand over there?"
    new "Why don't you see if Galan needs a hand over there?\n你不如去看看 Galan 那边要不要搭把手？"

    old "Sure, I'll go check on him."
    new "Sure, I'll go check on him.\n好，我去看看他。"

    old "Dasyra yawns audibly, then turns to Galan and yells across the cell."
    new "Dasyra yawns audibly, then turns to Galan and yells across the cell.\nDasyra 打了个响亮的哈欠，接着转向 Galan，隔着牢房喊道。"

    old "How are we coming along over there, Galan?"
    new "How are we coming along over there, Galan?\nGalan，那边进展如何？"

    old "Not so loud."
    new "Not so loud.\n别这么大声。"

    old "Oh, come on. It's nightfall. You think they're going to come check on us? If they had any intention of feeding us, they would have done it by now."
    new "Oh, come on. It's nightfall. You think they're going to come check on us? If they had any intention of feeding us, they would have done it by now.\n哎呀，得了吧。都入夜了。你还以为他们会来查看我们？他们要有心喂我们，早就喂了。"

    old "[protag], tell Dasyra to keep quiet. There's no reason for us to be yelling across at each other like this. If she needs to say something to me, she can say it through you."
    new "[protag], tell Dasyra to keep quiet. There's no reason for us to be yelling across at each other like this. If she needs to say something to me, she can say it through you.\n[protag]，让 Dasyra 安静点。我们没必要这样隔着牢房大喊。她若想对我说什么，通过你转达便是。"

    old "I step toward Dasyra and put a hand on her shoulder."
    new "I step toward Dasyra and put a hand on her shoulder.\n我走向 Dasyra，把手搭在她肩上。"

    old "I know you're getting antsy, but we—"
    new "I know you're getting antsy, but we—\n我知道你有些坐不住了，但我们——"

    old "The door behind Dasyra swings open, sending her tumbling forward into my arms."
    new "The door behind Dasyra swings open, sending her tumbling forward into my arms.\nDasyra 身后的门猛地打开，把她撞得向前扑进我怀里。"

    old "Oy. What's all that noise in here?"
    new "Oy. What's all that noise in here?\n喂，这里头吵吵什么？"

    old "Galan freezes, clenching the digging tool in his fist. I wrap my arms around Dasyra, and I feel her breathing stop."
    new "Galan freezes, clenching the digging tool in his fist. I wrap my arms around Dasyra, and I feel her breathing stop.\nGalan 僵在原地，拳头死死攥着挖掘工具。我环臂抱住 Dasyra，感到她的呼吸都停了。"

    old "The guard looks at me, then down at Dasyra, then up at me again."
    new "The guard looks at me, then down at Dasyra, then up at me again.\n守卫看看我，又低头看看 Dasyra，再抬头看向我。"

    old "What's all this?"
    new "What's all this?\n这是怎么回事？"

    old "These two just got into a little fight. I was splitting them up."
    new "These two just got into a little fight. I was splitting them up.\n这两人刚才拌了几句嘴。我在劝架。"

    old "The guard spits at my feet."
    new "The guard spits at my feet.\n守卫朝我脚边啐了一口。"

    old "Pity there isn't much daylight left. It'd be a real pleasure to see these two go at it. I know a few other guards who'd like to place bets on that. Personally, my money'd be on the feller over there."
    new "Pity there isn't much daylight left. It'd be a real pleasure to see these two go at it. I know a few other guards who'd like to place bets on that. Personally, my money'd be on the feller over there.\n可惜没剩多少天光了。不然看他俩打一场可真是乐事。我认得几个守卫，准想押注。要我说，我的钱押在那边那家伙身上。"

    old "The guard points a finger at Galan."
    new "The guard points a finger at Galan.\n守卫伸手指向 Galan。"

    old "You, mustache. Where're you from?"
    new "You, mustache. Where're you from?\n你，留胡子的。你打哪儿来的？"

    old "From just outside Hammerhands, sir. Grew up in the basin."
    new "From just outside Hammerhands, sir. Grew up in the basin.\nHammerhands 城外，大人。在盆地里长大。"

    old "The basin, eh? They breed fighters out there, do they?"
    new "The basin, eh? They breed fighters out there, do they?\n盆地，嗯？那地方净出打手，是吧？"

    old "Street brawls aren't an uncommon sight."
    new "Street brawls aren't an uncommon sight.\n街头斗殴在那儿不算稀罕事。"

    old "Well then."
    new "Well then.\n那敢情好。"

    old "The guard gives Galan a nasty look."
    new "The guard gives Galan a nasty look.\n守卫恶狠狠地瞪了 Galan 一眼。"

    old "Don't go roughin' up the other prisoners too much, you hear? Not until we've had a chance to put wager on it, at least."
    new "Don't go roughin' up the other prisoners too much, you hear? Not until we've had a chance to put wager on it, at least.\n别把其他囚犯揍得太狠，听见没？至少等我们先押上注再说。"

    old "I'll restrain myself."
    new "I'll restrain myself.\n我会克制的。"

    old "Sleep tight. Behave yourselves and there might be breakfast in the morning."
    new "Sleep tight. Behave yourselves and there might be breakfast in the morning.\n睡个好觉。老实点，明早兴许有早饭吃。"

    old "The guard backs out the door, and it swings shut behind him."
    new "The guard backs out the door, and it swings shut behind him.\n守卫退出门外，门在他身后合上。"

    old "I feel Dasyra beginning to breath heavily."
    new "I feel Dasyra beginning to breath heavily.\n我感到 Dasyra 开始喘起粗气。"

    old "Are you okay?"
    new "Are you okay?\n你还好吗？"

    old "Dasyra nods."
    new "Dasyra nods.\nDasyra 点了点头。"

    old "[protag], put your ear to the door. I'd like a word with the girl."
    new "[protag], put your ear to the door. I'd like a word with the girl.\n[protag]，把耳朵贴到门上。我想跟这姑娘说几句话。"

    old "Galan grabs Dasyra by the shoulders and shoves her against the wall. He leans in until their faces are only an inch apart."
    new "Galan grabs Dasyra by the shoulders and shoves her against the wall. He leans in until their faces are only an inch apart.\nGalan 抓住 Dasyra 的肩膀，把她推到墙上。他俯身凑近，直到两人的脸相距不过一寸。"

    old "What the hell."
    new "What the hell.\n搞什么鬼。"

    old "What. The. Hell."
    new "What. The. Hell.\n搞。什。么。鬼。"

    old "How the hell did that just happen? Why is it that when a guard walks in to check on us, I stand there like an idiot in front of a wall missing several bricks and a digging tool in my hand?"
    new "How the hell did that just happen? Why is it that when a guard walks in to check on us, I stand there like an idiot in front of a wall missing several bricks and a digging tool in my hand?\n刚才那到底是怎么发生的？为什么守卫进来查看时，我像个白痴一样，站在一堵缺了好几块砖的墙前，手里还攥着挖掘工具？"

    old "Dasyra stares back at Galan, wide-eyed."
    new "Dasyra stares back at Galan, wide-eyed.\nDasyra 瞪大眼睛回望 Galan。"

    old "You had one job, woman. One job! Stand at the door and listen for approaching guards. You hear something, you say something. Was that really too much for you to handle?"
    new "You had one job, woman. One job! Stand at the door and listen for approaching guards. You hear something, you say something. Was that really too much for you to handle?\n你就一个任务，女人。就一个任务！站在门口听守卫有没有靠近。听到动静就说一声。这点事你都做不好吗？"

    old "Even simply doing nothing would have been better than trying to start a shouting match in here. If you kept your trap shut, or used even the slightest bit of discretion in keeping your voice down, that guard would have had no reason to come down here."
    new "Even simply doing nothing would have been better than trying to start a shouting match in here. If you kept your trap shut, or used even the slightest bit of discretion in keeping your voice down, that guard would have had no reason to come down here.\n哪怕你什么都不做，也比在这儿吵吵嚷嚷强。你要是闭上嘴，或者哪怕稍微留神放低声音，那守卫根本就没理由下来。"

    old "Galan turns his back on Dasyra, then spins around, swinging a fist toward her head."
    new "Galan turns his back on Dasyra, then spins around, swinging a fist toward her head.\nGalan 背过身去，又猛地转回来，一拳朝她头部挥去。"

    old "Galan stops mid swing. He looks at his fist, then at Dasyra. Tears are running down her cheeks."
    new "Galan stops mid swing. He looks at his fist, then at Dasyra. Tears are running down her cheeks.\nGalan 挥到一半停住了。他看看自己的拳头，又看看 Dasyra。泪水正顺着她的脸颊淌下。"

    old "Gods. I'm sorry. I'm bloody sorry."
    new "Gods. I'm sorry. I'm bloody sorry.\n天哪。对不起。真他娘的对不起。"

    old "I'm sorry. This...sometimes I lose control. I'm sorry you had to see that."
    new "I'm sorry. This...sometimes I lose control. I'm sorry you had to see that.\n对不起。我……有时会失控。很抱歉让你看到这一幕。"

    old "Dasyra? Can you forgive me?"
    new "Dasyra? Can you forgive me?\nDasyra？你能原谅我吗？"

    old "Dasyra nods silently."
    new "Dasyra nods silently.\nDasyra 默默点了点头。"

    old "We're all going a little stir-crazy in here. We're lucky. It was too dark for him to see anything. We're safe. And we're going to get out of here."
    new "We're all going a little stir-crazy in here. We're lucky. It was too dark for him to see anything. We're safe. And we're going to get out of here.\n我们在这儿都憋得有点疯。算我们走运，里头太黑，他什么也没看清。我们安全了。而且我们会离开这里。"

    old "We're going to get out of here tonight. I'm halfway to carving enough footholds for us to reach the top. We'll be out of here before dawn breaks."
    new "We're going to get out of here tonight. I'm halfway to carving enough footholds for us to reach the top. We'll be out of here before dawn breaks.\n我们今晚就出去。落脚点我已挖好一半，够我们爬到顶了。天亮之前我们就能离开。"

    old "Galan, are you good to keep digging?"
    new "Galan, are you good to keep digging?\nGalan，你还能接着挖吗？"

    old "I've been going well so far, and I think I have it in me to finish this job."
    new "I've been going well so far, and I think I have it in me to finish this job.\n到目前为止我都挖得挺顺，我觉得自己有劲头把这活儿干完。"

    old "I'll keep an eye to the door. Dasyra, why don't you rest? Try to get some sleep, if you feel so inclined."
    new "I'll keep an eye to the door. Dasyra, why don't you rest? Try to get some sleep, if you feel so inclined.\n我盯着门口。Dasyra，你歇会儿吧？要是想睡，就睡上一觉。"

    old "Dasyra slinks off to a far corner of the cell, away from me and Galan."
    new "Dasyra slinks off to a far corner of the cell, away from me and Galan.\nDasyra 悄悄挪到牢房远处的一角，离我和 Galan 远远的。"

    old "The next hour passes uneventfully. I give myself a slap on the face every time I catch myself yawning, while Galan continues to carve our path out of the cell."
    new "The next hour passes uneventfully. I give myself a slap on the face every time I catch myself yawning, while Galan continues to carve our path out of the cell.\n接下来一小时平安无事。每回察觉自己在打哈欠，我就扇自己一耳光，而 Galan 则继续凿着我们逃出牢房的路。"

    old "After what must be hours later, Dasyra interrupts my boredom with a tap on the shoulder."
    new "After what must be hours later, Dasyra interrupts my boredom with a tap on the shoulder.\n想必过了好几个小时，Dasyra 拍了拍我的肩膀，打断我的百无聊赖。"

    old "[protag], can you talk?"
    new "[protag], can you talk?\n[protag]，能说会儿话吗？"

    old "Sure, I can listen and talk. What is it?"
    new "Sure, I can listen and talk. What is it?\n当然，我既能听也能说。什么事？"

    old "There's something I need to tell you."
    new "There's something I need to tell you.\n有件事我得告诉你。"

    old "I stole the brooch."
    new "I stole the brooch.\n胸针是我偷的。"

    old "What?"
    new "What?\n什么？"

    old "When you first found me on the street, getting accosted by the three Arasmas guards, they were arresting me for stealing the brooch."
    new "When you first found me on the street, getting accosted by the three Arasmas guards, they were arresting me for stealing the brooch.\n你最初在街上找到我时，我正被那三个 Arasmas 守卫拦住，他们是因为我偷了胸针而要抓我。"

    old "I thought you said it was your mother's."
    new "I thought you said it was your mother's.\n你不是说那是你母亲的。"

    old "My mother worked as a maid for Faberge Arasmas. He paid her a generous wage for her service, but he wanted an additional way to reward her for her years of loyalty and service."
    new "My mother worked as a maid for Faberge Arasmas. He paid her a generous wage for her service, but he wanted an additional way to reward her for her years of loyalty and service.\n我母亲在 Faberge Arasmas 家当女佣。他为她的辛劳付了丰厚的工钱，却还想另寻法子酬谢她多年来的忠心与服侍。"

    old "Faberge made the brooch, specially crafted as a gift for my mother. But as an honest broker who wanted to avoid even the appearance of impropriety, Faberge kept all of his transactions and wealth transfers—including personal gifts—a matter of public record."
    new "Faberge made the brooch, specially crafted as a gift for my mother. But as an honest broker who wanted to avoid even the appearance of impropriety, Faberge kept all of his transactions and wealth transfers—including personal gifts—a matter of public record.\nFaberge 打造了这枚胸针，是专为我母亲做的礼物。但作为一位正直的商人，他连一点不正当的嫌疑都不想沾，于是把自己的每一笔交易和财产转移——包括私人馈赠——都作为公开记录留存。"

    old "Faberge was afraid it might appear scandalous if he gifted such an item to one of his maids. He was a married man, after all."
    new "Faberge was afraid it might appear scandalous if he gifted such an item to one of his maids. He was a married man, after all.\nFaberge 担心，把这样一件东西送给自家女佣会惹来风言风语。毕竟他是有家室的人。"

    old "To get around this, Faberge named my mother in his will as the recipient of the jewel—and a rather significant portion of his estate as well."
    new "To get around this, Faberge named my mother in his will as the recipient of the jewel—and a rather significant portion of his estate as well.\n为了绕开这层顾虑，Faberge 在遗嘱中把我母亲列为那枚珠宝的受赠人——连同他相当可观的一部分家产。"

    old "But when Faberge died and Edgar took his place, Edgar claimed that the will could not be found. I'm certain that Edgar destroyed it. Faberge knew that his son was a greedy man, and I doubt that he willed even an iota of his wealth to Edgar."
    new "But when Faberge died and Edgar took his place, Edgar claimed that the will could not be found. I'm certain that Edgar destroyed it. Faberge knew that his son was a greedy man, and I doubt that he willed even an iota of his wealth to Edgar.\n可 Faberge 死后，Edgar 接了他的位子，却声称遗嘱找不到了。我敢肯定，是 Edgar 毁了它。Faberge 深知自己的儿子贪得无厌，我怀疑他连自己财富的一丝一毫都不愿留给 Edgar。"

    old "But common law dictates that in cases where a will does not exist or cannot be found, the most direct descendant of the deceased be named as the sole recipient of the estate."
    new "But common law dictates that in cases where a will does not exist or cannot be found, the most direct descendant of the deceased be named as the sole recipient of the estate.\n但普通法规定，凡遗嘱不存在或找不到的情形，应指定死者最直接的继承人为遗产的唯一受领人。"

    old "My mother never received what she was due, the brooch included. Edgar took by might what was hers by right."
    new "My mother never received what she was due, the brooch included. Edgar took by might what was hers by right.\n我母亲从未得到她应得的一切，包括那枚胸针。Edgar 用强权夺走了本属于她的东西。"

    old "But you have no way of proving that it was rightfully hers if the will was destroyed."
    new "But you have no way of proving that it was rightfully hers if the will was destroyed.\n可遗嘱既已销毁，你就没法证明那本属于她。"

    old "That's right. And that's why I had to steal the brooch back."
    new "That's right. And that's why I had to steal the brooch back.\n没错。所以我才非把胸针偷回来不可。"

    old "And you're telling me this just now?"
    new "And you're telling me this just now?\n你现在才告诉我？"

    old "I know. I should have said something earlier."
    new "I know. I should have said something earlier.\n我知道。我早该说出来的。"

    old "Yeah, a lot earlier. Like before we dove in and assaulted several guards on your behalf."
    new "Yeah, a lot earlier. Like before we dove in and assaulted several guards on your behalf.\n是啊，早得多。比如说，在我们冲上去、为你袭击好几个守卫之前。"

    old "I'm sorry. I never intended for things to happen like they did. Everything happened so fast. Once weapons were drawn, I was just operating on instinct. It didn't even occur to me to try and explain the situation until we were being hauled off."
    new "I'm sorry. I never intended for things to happen like they did. Everything happened so fast. Once weapons were drawn, I was just operating on instinct. It didn't even occur to me to try and explain the situation until we were being hauled off.\n对不起。我从没想过事情会变成那样。一切都发生得太快了。武器一拔出来，我就全凭本能行事。直到我们被拖走，我都没想起要解释一下情况。"

    old "All this time, I was thinking that we were all the victims of some guards who were wrongfully abusing their power to accost an innocent woman. But it turns out that they were making a legitimate arrest. And all of us are here for real crimes."
    new "All this time, I was thinking that we were all the victims of some guards who were wrongfully abusing their power to accost an innocent woman. But it turns out that they were making a legitimate arrest. And all of us are here for real crimes.\n一直以来，我都以为我们是受害者，是那些守卫滥用职权拦下一个无辜女子。可原来他们是在依法抓人。而我们几个，都是因为真正的罪行才待在这里。"

    old "I turn away from Dasyra and bury my head in my hands."
    new "I turn away from Dasyra and bury my head in my hands.\n我转过身去背对 Dasyra，把头埋进双手。"

    old "What a mess. What a horrible mess."
    new "What a mess. What a horrible mess.\n一团糟。真是一团糟。"

    old "I feel the touch of Dasyra's hand on my shoulder, and I spin around and bat her hand away. I raise a hand, and she flinches."
    new "I feel the touch of Dasyra's hand on my shoulder, and I spin around and bat her hand away. I raise a hand, and she flinches.\n我感觉到 Dasyra 的手搭在我肩上，猛地转身把她的手拨开。我抬起一只手，她瑟缩了一下。"

    old "Listen, I'm not angry. Well, maybe I am. But that's not helping us escape. So I'm going to do my best to put all of this behind us. We all made choices that got us here. You made choices. I made choices. Maybe not informed choices, but I'm here because of things that I did. Galan made those choices, too."
    new "Listen, I'm not angry. Well, maybe I am. But that's not helping us escape. So I'm going to do my best to put all of this behind us. We all made choices that got us here. You made choices. I made choices. Maybe not informed choices, but I'm here because of things that I did. Galan made those choices, too.\n听着，我不生气。好吧，也许有点。但生气也帮不了我们逃出去。所以我会尽力把这一切抛到脑后。我们都是因各自的选择才落到这里。你做过选择，我也做过选择。也许不是明智的选择，但我是因自己所做的事才落到这里。Galan 也做了他的选择。"

    old "Why are you telling me about this?"
    new "Why are you telling me about this?\n你为什么要告诉我这些？"

    old "I figured you deserved to know."
    new "I figured you deserved to know.\n我觉得你应当知道。"

    old "You waited this long to tell me. There's a got to be a reason for that."
    new "You waited this long to tell me. There's a got to be a reason for that.\n你拖了这么久才告诉我。这一定有原因。"

    old "I didn't know how you'd react."
    new "I didn't know how you'd react.\n我不知道你会是什么反应。"

    old "Yes. When we got locked up, I was an unknown entity at first. You needed to gain my trust. The most important thing was having unity between the three of us, so that we could focus on escaping. That's what you were thinking. Right?"
    new "Yes. When we got locked up, I was an unknown entity at first. You needed to gain my trust. The most important thing was having unity between the three of us, so that we could focus on escaping. That's what you were thinking. Right?\n对。我们刚被关进来时，我对你来说起初是个来路不明的陌生人。你需要赢得我的信任。最重要的是我们三人一条心，这样才能专心逃出去。你当时是这么想的，对吧？"

    old "Yes, exactly."
    new "Yes, exactly.\n对，正是如此。"

    old "Well, it's still true, Dasyra. We're still in this dungeon. We still need to escape. In fact, the hardest part of our escape still lies ahead of us. And now on top of everything, I've got this thing that you've just dumped on me."
    new "Well, it's still true, Dasyra. We're still in this dungeon. We still need to escape. In fact, the hardest part of our escape still lies ahead of us. And now on top of everything, I've got this thing that you've just dumped on me.\n嗯，这些如今也还是事实，Dasyra。我们仍在地牢里，仍得逃出去。事实上，越狱最难的部分还在后头。而现在雪上加霜，你又把这档子事甩到了我头上。"

    old "I'm not sure you realize what you've just dropped on me here, Dasyra. You see, all this time, I was thinking that you were the victim of a wrongful accusation, and Galan and I were heroes rushing to your defense."
    new "I'm not sure you realize what you've just dropped on me here, Dasyra. You see, all this time, I was thinking that you were the victim of a wrongful accusation, and Galan and I were heroes rushing to your defense.\nDasyra，我不确定你有没有意识到你刚把什么抛给了我。你看，一直以来我都以为你是被冤枉的受害者，而我和 Galan 是赶来为你出头的英雄。"

    old "But now I find out that you were committing a real crime. And I committed a real crime by assaulting those guards. We're all here in this dungeon because of real crimes."
    new "But now I find out that you were committing a real crime. And I committed a real crime by assaulting those guards. We're all here in this dungeon because of real crimes.\n可现在我发现，你犯下了真正的罪行，而我袭击那些守卫，也犯下了真正的罪行。我们之所以都蹲在这地牢里，全是因为真正的罪行。"

    old "Gods. Dasyra, I really could have done without the confession. I'm really not seeing how that gets us any closer to our goal here."
    new "Gods. Dasyra, I really could have done without the confession. I'm really not seeing how that gets us any closer to our goal here.\n天哪。Dasyra，我还真宁愿你没来坦白。我实在看不出这能让我们离目标更近一步。"

    old "Dasyra looks at the floor, head bowed. Her voice softens to a whimper."
    new "Dasyra looks at the floor, head bowed. Her voice softens to a whimper.\nDasyra 低着头望向地面。她的声音软了下来，几近啜泣。"

    old "I'm sorry."
    new "I'm sorry.\n对不起。"

    old "Well, what's done is done. Now we need to figure out what happens next."
    new "Well, what's done is done. Now we need to figure out what happens next.\n唉，木已成舟。现在得想想接下来怎么办。"

    old "You haven't told Galan about this?"
    new "You haven't told Galan about this?\n你还没把这事告诉 Galan？"

    old "No. I thought you should be the first to know."
    new "No. I thought you should be the first to know.\n没有。我觉得你应当第一个知道。"

    old "We have to tell Galan about this. You've told me, and he deserves to know as much as I do. Maybe you can't keep this secret from him, but I sure can't."
    new "We have to tell Galan about this. You've told me, and he deserves to know as much as I do. Maybe you can't keep this secret from him, but I sure can't.\n我们必须告诉 Galan。你既已告诉了我，那他也该和我一样知道实情。也许你能对他守住这个秘密，可我是万万守不住。"

    old "Okay. I'll tell him."
    new "Okay. I'll tell him.\n好。我去告诉他。"

    old "Okay. We'll need to wait for the right moment to tell him, though. He needs to be in a receptive mood."
    new "Okay. We'll need to wait for the right moment to tell him, though. He needs to be in a receptive mood.\n好。不过我们得等到合适的时机再告诉他。得等他心情能听得进去的时候。"

    old "I agree."
    new "I agree.\n我同意。"

    old "Dasyra, I think I know Galan well enough to know when that time will be. I can't say for certain right now when it will be. But I'll let you know when that time comes. I'll be there with you to tell him. Until that then, you'll need to sit on this. Okay?"
    new "Dasyra, I think I know Galan well enough to know when that time will be. I can't say for certain right now when it will be. But I'll let you know when that time comes. I'll be there with you to tell him. Until that then, you'll need to sit on this. Okay?\nDasyra，我想我对 Galan 已足够了解，能判断那个时机何时到来。眼下我还说不准具体是什么时候，但时机一到，我会告诉你。我会陪着你一起去告诉他。在那之前，你得先把这秘密憋在心里。好吗？"

    old "Okay."
    new "Okay.\n好。"

    old "Galan needs to know the truth, but it might be best if it doesn't come from you."
    new "Galan needs to know the truth, but it might be best if it doesn't come from you.\nGalan 需要知道真相，但最好别由你亲口告诉他。"

    old "I'll tell him. Maybe not right now, but...when the time feels right. Can you trust me on this?"
    new "I'll tell him. Maybe not right now, but...when the time feels right. Can you trust me on this?\n我会告诉他。也许不是现在，而是……等时机合适的时候。这件事你能信我吗？"

    old "We can't tell Galan about this. You've just given me one more thing to worry about here. Galan doesn't need this weighing on his mind, too. And who can say how he'll react?"
    new "We can't tell Galan about this. You've just given me one more thing to worry about here. Galan doesn't need this weighing on his mind, too. And who can say how he'll react?\n这件事不能告诉 Galan。你刚刚又给我添了一件要操心的事。Galan 没必要再让这事压在心里。而且谁知道他会作何反应？"

    old "There's no way that we can tell Galan the truth. Not now, anyway. If it's weighing on your conscience, and you feel the need to confess, save it until we're all out of here safe and sound."
    new "There's no way that we can tell Galan the truth. Not now, anyway. If it's weighing on your conscience, and you feel the need to confess, save it until we're all out of here safe and sound.\n我们没法告诉 Galan 真相，至少现在不行。要是这事压在你良心上，让你觉得非坦白不可，那就留到我们全都安然逃出去之后再说。"

    old "I understand."
    new "I understand.\n我明白了。"

    old "You keep an ear to the door. I'm going to go talk to Galan."
    new "You keep an ear to the door. I'm going to go talk to Galan.\n你留神听门口的动静。我去跟 Galan 谈谈。"

    old "I walk across the cell. Galan has begun ascending as he continues to dig footholds in the wall, each higher than the next. His feet are now level with my head."
    new "I walk across the cell. Galan has begun ascending as he continues to dig footholds in the wall, each higher than the next. His feet are now level with my head.\n我穿过牢房。Galan 一边继续在墙上凿落脚点，一边开始向上攀，一个比一个高。他的双脚如今已与我的头齐平。"

    old "Ho, Galan. How's the weather up there?"
    new "Ho, Galan. How's the weather up there?\n嗨，Galan。上头的天气怎么样？"

    old "Galan looks down at me."
    new "Galan looks down at me.\nGalan 低头看我。"

    old "Not much better up here than I imagine it is down there. Progress is still going steady. I estimate another hour, maybe two at the rate I'm going."
    new "Not much better up here than I imagine it is down there. Progress is still going steady. I estimate another hour, maybe two at the rate I'm going.\n上面也没比下面强多少。进度还算稳当。照我这速度，估摸再有一小时，也许两小时。"

    old "You doing okay up there? It's no trouble for you to keep your balance and dig at the same time? You only have two hands, you know."
    new "You doing okay up there? It's no trouble for you to keep your balance and dig at the same time? You only have two hands, you know.\n你在上头还好吧？一边保持平衡一边挖，不费劲吗？你可只有两只手啊。"

    old "My position up here is pretty far from precarious. I don't have very far to fall, and these bricks are nice and flat. I've climbed mountains while carrying an injured man, and this isn't even one tenth as difficult."
    new "My position up here is pretty far from precarious. I don't have very far to fall, and these bricks are nice and flat. I've climbed mountains while carrying an injured man, and this isn't even one tenth as difficult.\n我这位置离危险还远着呢。摔也摔不了多高，而且这些砖又平又好抓。我背着一个伤员都爬过山，这连那十分之一的难度都不到。"

    old "Really? That sounds like an interesting story."
    new "Really? That sounds like an interesting story.\n真的？听起来是个有趣的故事。"

    old "Not much of a story. I was climbing a mountain with another man, he was injured, and the closest way to get help was up. He did a fine job of staying steady on my back, so the only real struggle for me was the extra weight."
    new "Not much of a story. I was climbing a mountain with another man, he was injured, and the closest way to get help was up. He did a fine job of staying steady on my back, so the only real struggle for me was the extra weight.\n算不上什么故事。我跟另一个人爬山，他受了伤，而最近的求救地点就在山上。他稳稳趴在我背上，所以我唯一的难处就是多出来的分量。"

    old "You want company over here, or should I leave you be?"
    new "You want company over here, or should I leave you be?\n你要我在这儿陪你，还是让我别打扰你？"

    old "As you prefer. I could go either way."
    new "As you prefer. I could go either way.\n随你。我怎样都行。"

    old "I walk to a corner of the cell and lean my back against the wall. I shut my eyes, concentrate on taking long breaths, and drift off to sleep."
    new "I walk to a corner of the cell and lean my back against the wall. I shut my eyes, concentrate on taking long breaths, and drift off to sleep.\n我走到牢房一角，背靠着墙。我闭上眼，专注地做深呼吸，渐渐睡去。"

    old "In that case, I think I'd like to stay up with you. Maybe I can relieve you if you start feeling sores."
    new "In that case, I think I'd like to stay up with you. Maybe I can relieve you if you start feeling sores.\n既然这样，我想我还是陪你熬着吧。你要是开始觉得酸痛，说不定我能替你一会儿。"

    old "Like I said, this here is nothing. You don't spent years climbing mountains without developing sure feet and hard hands."
    new "Like I said, this here is nothing. You don't spent years climbing mountains without developing sure feet and hard hands.\n就像我说的，这点活不算什么。你爬了好几年的山，自然练出稳当的脚和粗糙的手。"

    old "Your hands are callused?"
    new "Your hands are callused?\n你的手长满老茧？"

    old "Of course. Some of the calluses are from toting heavy weapons. But you normally don't start bleeding after your first day of swinging an axe."
    new "Of course. Some of the calluses are from toting heavy weapons. But you normally don't start bleeding after your first day of swinging an axe.\n当然。有些老茧是搬重武器磨出来的。不过你通常不会在头一天抡斧子就磨出血。"

    old "But you do bleed when climbing?"
    new "But you do bleed when climbing?\n可爬山就会出血？"

    old "Sure. The best rocks for climbing are ones with rough surfaces. You don't want your hands and feet sliding around when the ground is a hundred or more feet below. Rough rocks and soft hands are a combination that often results in blood."
    new "Sure. The best rocks for climbing are ones with rough surfaces. You don't want your hands and feet sliding around when the ground is a hundred or more feet below. Rough rocks and soft hands are a combination that often results in blood.\n当然。最适合攀爬的岩石，表面都很粗糙。脚下是上百英尺的深渊时，你总不想手脚打滑吧。粗糙的岩壁配上细嫩的手，往往就是血淋淋的下场。"

    old "Sounds like an ordeal."
    new "Sounds like an ordeal.\n听起来像场折磨。"

    old "A little bleeding is nothing to cry about. That's how you turn soft hands into hard hands. Pain is what you feel when weakness is leaving the body. I think the proudest thing I can say is that I've lived a painful life."
    new "A little bleeding is nothing to cry about. That's how you turn soft hands into hard hands. Pain is what you feel when weakness is leaving the body. I think the proudest thing I can say is that I've lived a painful life.\n流点血没什么好哭的。细嫩的手就是这么磨成铁手的。疼痛，就是软弱离你而去时你感受到的东西。我想我最引以为傲的，莫过于自己这一生过得很苦。"

    old "A painful life is a sign of strength?"
    new "A painful life is a sign of strength?\n过苦日子就是强大的象征？"

    old "Getting strong isn't easy. Of course you're going to encounter some pain on the way there."
    new "Getting strong isn't easy. Of course you're going to encounter some pain on the way there.\n变强本就不易。路上当然要吃些苦头。"

    old "How about you? Have you lived a painful life?"
    new "How about you? Have you lived a painful life?\n你呢？你这辈子过得苦吗？"

    old "I've had my fair share of hardship."
    new "I've had my fair share of hardship.\n我的苦难也没少受。"

    old "That's lucky for you. Every life has hardship. You managed to get all of that up front. The best years of your life are ahead of you."
    new "That's lucky for you. Every life has hardship. You managed to get all of that up front. The best years of your life are ahead of you.\n那你算走运。哪段人生都有苦处，而你把这些都提前吃完了。你人生最好的岁月还在前头等着你。"

    old "I can't really say that I have. My life hasn't always been easy, but on the whole, life has treated me pretty well."
    new "I can't really say that I have. My life hasn't always been easy, but on the whole, life has treated me pretty well.\n这话我可不敢说。我的日子并非总是一帆风顺，但总的来说，生活待我还算不错。"

    old "Unlucky for you, then."
    new "Unlucky for you, then.\n那你不走运咯。"

    old "Unlucky?"
    new "Unlucky?\n不走运？"

    old "Yeah. Every life has some amount of suffering. The lucky people are the ones who get all of their troubles and trials front-loaded. If your life has been easy so far, then you're in for some tough years down the road."
    new "Yeah. Every life has some amount of suffering. The lucky people are the ones who get all of their troubles and trials front-loaded. If your life has been easy so far, then you're in for some tough years down the road.\n对。每段人生都有那么些苦难。走运的人，是那些把麻烦和磨砺都提前吃尽的人。你的日子若一直顺遂，那往后的岁月怕是有的苦头吃。"

    old "I'm not sure I can agree with you."
    new "I'm not sure I can agree with you.\n我不敢苟同。"

    old "What do you mean?"
    new "What do you mean?\n这话怎讲？"

    old "Well, some people are born into wealth and have ease and comfort all their lives. And some people are born destitute and stay that way until the day they die. Just because things start bad doesn't mean they get good. In fact, I'd say the opposite is true. Those who are born poor tend to stay poor."
    new "Well, some people are born into wealth and have ease and comfort all their lives. And some people are born destitute and stay that way until the day they die. Just because things start bad doesn't mean they get good. In fact, I'd say the opposite is true. Those who are born poor tend to stay poor.\n嗯，有些人含着金汤匙出生，一辈子安逸舒适；也有些人出生赤贫，直到咽气都翻不了身。开头糟糕，并不代表往后会好。事实上，我倒觉得恰恰相反——穷人家的孩子往往一辈子都穷。"

    old "I can see how someone like you would think that. But you're not seeing the big picture."
    new "I can see how someone like you would think that. But you're not seeing the big picture.\n我明白你这样的人会这么想。可你没看到全局。"

    old "I've known many noblemen who were born wealthy and have had nothing but the most luxurious of lives. They never want for anything. They have no worries, no struggles, no tribulations. And those people are some of the most miserable I've ever known."
    new "I've known many noblemen who were born wealthy and have had nothing but the most luxurious of lives. They never want for anything. They have no worries, no struggles, no tribulations. And those people are some of the most miserable I've ever known.\n我认识许多贵族，生来富有，一辈子只过最奢侈的日子。他们什么都不缺，没有忧愁、没有挣扎、没有磨难。而这些人，恰恰是我见过最痛苦的一群。"

    old "Can you imagine that kind of existence? They sleep all day because they have nothing to live for. They drink the finest of wines, but to them, those fine wines are normal. Something ordinary. Not something that can be enjoyed. Imagine how miserable those people must be, imbibing the finest all their lives, yet never knowing it!"
    new "Can you imagine that kind of existence? They sleep all day because they have nothing to live for. They drink the finest of wines, but to them, those fine wines are normal. Something ordinary. Not something that can be enjoyed. Imagine how miserable those people must be, imbibing the finest all their lives, yet never knowing it!\n你能想象那种活法吗？他们整日昏睡，因为没什么值得为之而活。他们喝的是最上等的酒，可对他们来说，那美酒不过是寻常之物，是稀松平常、无从享受的东西。想想那些人该有多可悲——一生都在享用最上等的东西，却从未察觉！"

    old "I once met an old man who lived in a mud hut in the Orcish Wastes. He was born a nomad, but I knew him only for the last days of his life. He succumbed to old age less than a week after I met him."
    new "I once met an old man who lived in a mud hut in the Orcish Wastes. He was born a nomad, but I knew him only for the last days of his life. He succumbed to old age less than a week after I met him.\n我曾遇见一位老人，住在 Orcish Wastes 的一间泥屋里。他生来是个游牧民，可我认识他时，已是他生命最后的日子。与我相识不到一周，他就因年迈过世了。"

    old "The Orcish Wastes. Can you imagine a more hellish existence? Living in a rotting, withered land, with only the most miserable of company. Ogres and Cyclopses, not the kind of neighbors I would choose, I tell you that."
    new "The Orcish Wastes. Can you imagine a more hellish existence? Living in a rotting, withered land, with only the most miserable of company. Ogres and Cyclopses, not the kind of neighbors I would choose, I tell you that.\nOrcish Wastes。你能想象比这更地狱般的活法吗？住在一片腐烂枯萎的土地上，身边只有最可悲的伴儿。Ogres 和 Cyclopses——我跟你说，那可不是我想挑的邻居。"

    old "But that man, in the few precious days I knew him, he had a look of contentedness like I've never seen. He was thrilled to be living in a mud hut in the worst place in the world. He was born a nomad, you see, and waking up every morning with a familiar roof over his head was something he treasured."
    new "But that man, in the few precious days I knew him, he had a look of contentedness like I've never seen. He was thrilled to be living in a mud hut in the worst place in the world. He was born a nomad, you see, and waking up every morning with a familiar roof over his head was something he treasured.\n可那个人，在我认识他的寥寥几天里，脸上却带着我从未见过的知足。住在世界上最糟糕的地方的一间泥屋里，他却乐在其中。你瞧，他生来是个游牧民，每天早上醒来，头顶都有个熟悉的屋檐，这对他来说格外珍贵。"

    old "Every morning, he walked two miles to the same well to get water for himself. You know, so that he wouldn't die. And walking that same path every day, having that rigid routine, was enough to bring him happiness."
    new "Every morning, he walked two miles to the same well to get water for himself. You know, so that he wouldn't die. And walking that same path every day, having that rigid routine, was enough to bring him happiness.\n每天早上，他走两英里去同一口井打水，就为了让自己活下来。而每天走同样的路、过着那种刻板的作息，就足以让他幸福。"

    old "He was born a poor man, and he died a poor man. But he worked and struggled in his early years, and he died a happy man."
    new "He was born a poor man, and he died a poor man. But he worked and struggled in his early years, and he died a happy man.\n他生来贫穷，死时也贫穷。可早年他辛劳拼搏，最终是带着幸福离开的。"

    old "'Good' and 'happiness' are in the eye of the beholder. What's pleasant is not always what's best for you."
    new "'Good' and 'happiness' are in the eye of the beholder. What's pleasant is not always what's best for you.\n「好」与「幸福」全在观者眼中。令人愉悦的，未必是对你最好的。"

    old "That's why I don't mind being perched up here, digging away at this wall with a poorly-improvised but perfectly adequate digging tool. Whatever comes after, I know that I'll enjoy it more if I toil harder now."
    new "That's why I don't mind being perched up here, digging away at this wall with a poorly-improvised but perfectly adequate digging tool. Whatever comes after, I know that I'll enjoy it more if I toil harder now.\n正因如此，我才不介意挂在这上头，用这件凑合却足够趁手的工具凿墙。不管接下来如何，我知道，现在越卖力，往后就越能珍惜所得。"

    old "I look up at Galan. He continues to dutifully scrape away at the wall with the twisted fragment of metal. And in the dim light of the moon, I can see what looks like a smile etched upon his face."
    new "I look up at Galan. He continues to dutifully scrape away at the wall with the twisted fragment of metal. And in the dim light of the moon, I can see what looks like a smile etched upon his face.\n我抬头望向 Galan。他继续用那截扭曲的金属片，尽责地刮着墙。在昏暗的月光下，我仿佛看见他脸上刻着一抹笑意。"

    old "His smile is not broad. It isn't the smile of a victorious man, or a joyful man. It's the look of a man who is perfectly content with his lot in life."
    new "His smile is not broad. It isn't the smile of a victorious man, or a joyful man. It's the look of a man who is perfectly content with his lot in life.\n他的笑容并不灿烂。那不是胜利者或欢欣者的笑，而是一个对自己的人生际遇心满意足的人的神情。"

    old "Galan doesn't know about Dasyra stealing the brooch."
    new "Galan doesn't know about Dasyra stealing the brooch.\nGalan 还不知道 Dasyra 偷胸针的事。"

    old "Maybe now is the best time to tell him."
    new "Maybe now is the best time to tell him.\n也许此刻正是告诉他的最好时机。"

    old "Galan, I need to tell you something."
    new "Galan, I need to tell you something.\nGalan，我得跟你说件事。"

    old "Well, go ahead and say it."
    new "Well, go ahead and say it.\n行，说吧。"

    old "Do you remember the altercation on the street that got us here?"
    new "Do you remember the altercation on the street that got us here?\n你还记得把我们弄到这儿的街头冲突吗？"

    old "Galan snorts."
    new "Galan snorts.\nGalan 哼了一声。"

    old "Yes, I remember it."
    new "Yes, I remember it.\n记得，我记得。"

    old "Do you remember why those guards were harassing Dasyra in the first place?"
    new "Do you remember why those guards were harassing Dasyra in the first place?\n你还记得那些守卫起初为什么找 Dasyra 的麻烦吗？"

    old "Something about her stealing a brooch."
    new "Something about her stealing a brooch.\n好像是她偷了一枚胸针。"

    old "What about it?"
    new "What about it?\n那又怎样？"

    old "She actually did steal the brooch."
    new "She actually did steal the brooch.\n她确实偷了那枚胸针。"

    old "Galan snorts, and I hear what sounds like a chuckle."
    new "Galan snorts, and I hear what sounds like a chuckle.\nGalan 哼了一声，我听到那声音像是轻笑。"

    old "Well, I guess we got what was coming to us."
    new "Well, I guess we got what was coming to us.\n嗯，我看我们也是自食其果。"

    old "We?"
    new "We?\n我们？"

    old "Her, for stealing it in the first place. And you and me, for leaping before we looked. We're reaping what we've sown, aren't we?"
    new "Her, for stealing it in the first place. And you and me, for leaping before we looked. We're reaping what we've sown, aren't we?\n她，谁让她先偷了它。还有你和我，谁让咱们没看明白就冲了上去。我们这是自食其果，对吧？"

    old "That's not the response I expected to hear."
    new "That's not the response I expected to hear.\n这不是我料想的反应。"

    old "[protag], truth is, I know that I'm no hero. Sometimes I like to pretend that I am. But when I jump into the fray, telling myself that I'm doing justice by defending the weak, I'm really lying to myself. Because the truth is, when I get into a fight, it's for one reason and one reason only: I like to fight."
    new "[protag], truth is, I know that I'm no hero. Sometimes I like to pretend that I am. But when I jump into the fray, telling myself that I'm doing justice by defending the weak, I'm really lying to myself. Because the truth is, when I get into a fight, it's for one reason and one reason only: I like to fight.\n[protag]，说真的，我知道自己不是什么英雄。有时我喜欢装成英雄。可当我冲进混战，告诉自己是在行侠仗义、保护弱者时，其实是在骗自己。因为真相是，我打架只为一个原因，也唯有这一个原因：我喜欢打架。"

    old "Of course, I try to avoid wanton fighting. But when the chance to join a fight presents itself, I'm never going to walk away from it."
    new "Of course, I try to avoid wanton fighting. But when the chance to join a fight presents itself, I'm never going to walk away from it.\n当然，我尽量不无故斗殴。可一旦有架可打的机会摆在面前，我从来不会转身走开。"

    old "I'm a ruffian at heart. Sometimes, I end up doing the right thing, and most of the time it's by accident. I belong in this cell. And I'm not going to resent anyone except myself for the way things turned out."
    new "I'm a ruffian at heart. Sometimes, I end up doing the right thing, and most of the time it's by accident. I belong in this cell. And I'm not going to resent anyone except myself for the way things turned out.\n我骨子里就是个暴徒。有时我也碰巧做了好事，大多数时候纯属凑巧。我活该待在这牢房里。事情变成这样，除了我自己，我谁也不怨。"

    old "That said, I don't fancy the notion of you two being marched off to be executed. I guess I'm a little worried about my own hide as well. So let's save the moral discussion until after we've busted our way out of here. Okay?"
    new "That said, I don't fancy the notion of you two being marched off to be executed. I guess I'm a little worried about my own hide as well. So let's save the moral discussion until after we've busted our way out of here. Okay?\n话虽如此，我可不想看着你们俩被押去处死。我想，我也有点担心自己的小命。所以，这道德探讨，还是等咱们逃出去之后再说吧。行吗？"

    old "You know about Dasyra stealing the brooch because she told you after we were locked up, is that right?"
    new "You know about Dasyra stealing the brooch because she told you after we were locked up, is that right?\n你知道 Dasyra 偷胸针的事，是因为关进来后她告诉了你，对吧？"

    old "Well, I can't blame her for not coming to me first with it, not after my little outburst earlier."
    new "Well, I can't blame her for not coming to me first with it, not after my little outburst earlier.\n嗯，我不能怪她没先来告诉我，毕竟我刚才发了那一通脾气。"

    old "You want to let her know that I know and everything is good between us?"
    new "You want to let her know that I know and everything is good between us?\n你想让她知道，我已知晓此事，而咱们之间一切如常？"

    old "Alright, I'll let her know that everything's fine."
    new "Alright, I'll let her know that everything's fine.\n好，我会告诉她一切都好。"

    old "I walk across the cell. Dasyra looks up at me, expectantly."
    new "I walk across the cell. Dasyra looks up at me, expectantly.\n我穿过牢房。Dasyra 满怀期待地抬头看我。"

    old "I told Galan that you stole the brooch."
    new "I told Galan that you stole the brooch.\n我把你偷胸针的事告诉了 Galan。"

    old "Dasyra's eyes get wide."
    new "Dasyra's eyes get wide.\nDasyra 瞪大了眼睛。"

    old "What did he say?"
    new "What did he say?\n他说什么了？"

    old "He says there's nothing to forgive. He says he's the one responsible for his actions, not you."
    new "He says there's nothing to forgive. He says he's the one responsible for his actions, not you.\n他说没什么可原谅的。他说该为自己的行为负责的是他，不是你。"

    old "So everything is okay between us?"
    new "So everything is okay between us?\n那我们之间一切都好？"

    old "Yeah. He sent me over to tell you. I think he's not sure he has the words to tell you himself. But he seemed actually somewhat amused about the whole thing."
    new "Yeah. He sent me over to tell you. I think he's not sure he has the words to tell you himself. But he seemed actually somewhat amused about the whole thing.\n是啊。他让我过来告诉你。我想他自己是不知道该怎么跟你说。不过，对整件事他倒似乎觉得有几分好笑。"

    old "It is kind of comical, isn't it? This whole ordeal."
    new "It is kind of comical, isn't it? This whole ordeal.\n确实有点滑稽，不是吗？这整场磨难。"

    old "I'm not sure comical is the word I'd use...but it has been quite the experience. It'll be quite the story to tell, if I ever have occasion to tell it."
    new "I'm not sure comical is the word I'd use...but it has been quite the experience. It'll be quite the story to tell, if I ever have occasion to tell it.\n滑稽这词我倒未必会用……不过这确实是场难忘的经历。若有机会讲起，倒会是个不错的故事。"

    old "Well, I guess at this point all we have to do is wait for Galan to finish our escape route."
    new "Well, I guess at this point all we have to do is wait for Galan to finish our escape route.\n嗯，我想眼下我们只需等 Galan 把逃跑路线挖好。"

    old "I think you should tell her that yourself, Galan."
    new "I think you should tell her that yourself, Galan.\nGalan，我觉得这话还是你亲口跟她说为好。"

    old "Well, alright. I'm not to keen on getting myself down from this perch, so why don't you send her over?"
    new "Well, alright. I'm not to keen on getting myself down from this perch, so why don't you send her over?\n嗯，好吧。我不太想从这高处下来，你不如让她过来？"

    old "Galan would like a word with you. I can watch the door while you speak with him."
    new "Galan would like a word with you. I can watch the door while you speak with him.\nGalan 想跟你谈谈。你跟他说话时，我来盯着门。"

    old "Everything's going to be fine. Galan's got an earnest soul."
    new "Everything's going to be fine. Galan's got an earnest soul.\n不会有事的。Galan 是个心地坦诚的人。"

    old "Are you sure?"
    new "Are you sure?\n你确定吗？"

    old "If you can trust me, then you can trust him."
    new "If you can trust me, then you can trust him.\n你既能信我，便能信他。"

    old "Dasyra walks across the cell and speaks to Galan. I can't hear their conversation, but the look of relief on Dasyra's face tells me everything is going to be alright."
    new "Dasyra walks across the cell and speaks to Galan. I can't hear their conversation, but the look of relief on Dasyra's face tells me everything is going to be alright.\nDasyra 穿过牢房，跟 Galan 交谈。我听不见他们的对话，但 Dasyra 脸上如释重负的神情告诉我，一切都会好起来的。"

    old "Open my mouth to say something, then stop myself short."
    new "Open my mouth to say something, then stop myself short.\n我张口想说点什么，却又戛然而止。"

    old "You got something to say?"
    new "You got something to say?\n你有话要说？"

    old "No, it's nothing. I should probably leave you be. And please, don't hesitate to ask for my help here if you need it."
    new "No, it's nothing. I should probably leave you be. And please, don't hesitate to ask for my help here if you need it.\n不，没什么。我大概还是别打扰你了。还有，要是需要我帮忙，请尽管开口。"

    old "Careful, if you keep on offering like that I might have to take you up on it."
    new "Careful, if you keep on offering like that I might have to take you up on it.\n小心点，你再这么一直主动请缨，我怕是真要当真的。"

    old "I should probably let you do your thing. I'm going to go see if I can catch a few moments of sleep before we bust our way out of here."
    new "I should probably let you do your thing. I'm going to go see if I can catch a few moments of sleep before we bust our way out of here.\n我大概还是该让你忙你的。我去看看能不能在逃出去之前小睡片刻。"

    old "Sleep tight, friend. I'll let you know when we're ready to bounce our way out of here."
    new "Sleep tight, friend. I'll let you know when we're ready to bounce our way out of here.\n睡个好觉，朋友。等咱们准备好开溜，我会叫你的。"

    old "The next few hours pass uneventfully."
    new "The next few hours pass uneventfully.\n接下来几个小时平安无事。"

    old "I try to sleep, but my nervous energy makes it hard to keep my eyes shut."
    new "I try to sleep, but my nervous energy makes it hard to keep my eyes shut.\n我试着入睡，可紧张的情绪让我难以合眼。"

    old "I keep my mind busy by envisioning our escape."
    new "I keep my mind busy by envisioning our escape.\n我在脑中一遍遍想象着逃跑的情景，让自己不至于胡思乱想。"

    old "It should be simple. Once we climb out of this cell, we should be somewhere within the walls of the Arasmas estate. From there, we simply make our way to the perimeter, climb over the wall, and run off under cover of darkness."
    new "It should be simple. Once we climb out of this cell, we should be somewhere within the walls of the Arasmas estate. From there, we simply make our way to the perimeter, climb over the wall, and run off under cover of darkness.\n应该不难。我们爬出牢房后，应该就身处 Arasmas 庄园的围墙之内。从那里，我们径直走向外围，翻过墙，借着夜色逃走便是。"

    old "My mind fills with visions of creeping across the grounds, ascending the wall surrounding the estate, and running off to leave this place forever. And as these visions dance in my head, I find myself slowly drifting off to sleep."
    new "My mind fills with visions of creeping across the grounds, ascending the wall surrounding the estate, and running off to leave this place forever. And as these visions dance in my head, I find myself slowly drifting off to sleep.\n我脑中浮现出蹑手蹑脚穿过庭院、攀上环绕庄园的墙、然后逃之夭夭、永远离开此地的画面。这些画面在脑海里翻飞之际，我发觉自己渐渐沉入了梦乡。"

    old "[protag], wake up."
    new "[protag], wake up.\n[protag]，醒醒。"

    old "Where..."
    new "Where...\n在哪儿……"

    old "It's time to go."
    new "It's time to go.\n该走了。"

    old "I blink myself awake, and see Dasyra and Galan standing above me, their faces barely illuminated in the moonlight."
    new "I blink myself awake, and see Dasyra and Galan standing above me, their faces barely illuminated in the moonlight.\n我眨着眼醒来，看见 Dasyra 和 Galan 站在我上方，月光下他们的脸庞几乎看不真切。"

    old "The sun will rise soon. We need to be out of here well before then."
    new "The sun will rise soon. We need to be out of here well before then.\n太阳快升起来了。我们得在那之前早早离开。"

    old "Well then, let's get going."
    new "Well then, let's get going.\n那好，动身吧。"

    old "I follow Galan over to the wall, where bricks have been removed from the wall to provide handholds and footholds leading all the way to the top of the cell, where an opening to the outside world allows air in. And hopefully, allows prisoners out."
    new "I follow Galan over to the wall, where bricks have been removed from the wall to provide handholds and footholds leading all the way to the top of the cell, where an opening to the outside world allows air in. And hopefully, allows prisoners out.\n我跟着 Galan 走到墙边，那里已拆下许多砖，留出抓手和落脚点，一路通向牢房顶部。顶上有个通往外面世界的开口，让空气进来，也希望能让囚犯出去。"

    old "I'm thinking we ought to go lightest up first. Dasyra, then you, then me bringing up the rear. And one at a time. A fall would be bad enough, we don't need to be crushing each other if one of us comes tumbling down."
    new "I'm thinking we ought to go lightest up first. Dasyra, then you, then me bringing up the rear. And one at a time. A fall would be bad enough, we don't need to be crushing each other if one of us comes tumbling down.\n我想咱们该让最轻的先上。Dasyra 先，然后你，我殿后。而且一个一个来。摔下来就够糟了，若有人滚落，可别再把彼此压个结实。"

    old "Sounds good. Dasyra, you ready?"
    new "Sounds good. Dasyra, you ready?\n好主意。Dasyra，准备好了吗？"

    old "Dasyra nods and turns to the wall."
    new "Dasyra nods and turns to the wall.\nDasyra 点点头，转向墙壁。"

    old "Ready."
    new "Ready.\n好了。"

    old "Dasyra begins climbing, cautiously at first, but once she gains sure footing she makes her way to the top without much difficulty. She disappears over the edge, then pokes her head over the hole and beckons for us to follow."
    new "Dasyra begins climbing, cautiously at first, but once she gains sure footing she makes her way to the top without much difficulty. She disappears over the edge, then pokes her head over the hole and beckons for us to follow.\nDasyra 开始攀爬，起初小心翼翼，但站稳脚跟后，便没费多大力气爬到了顶。她翻过边沿消失了，随后从洞口探出头，招手示意我们跟上。"

    old "Galan and I exchange a nod, and I begin climbing."
    new "Galan and I exchange a nod, and I begin climbing.\nGalan 和我彼此点头，随后我开始攀爬。"

    old "The footholds are sturdy enough. Galan must have gone through some real trouble to carve through the mortar if it's this solid."
    new "The footholds are sturdy enough. Galan must have gone through some real trouble to carve through the mortar if it's this solid.\n落脚点相当牢靠。能凿得这般结实，Galan 想必费了不少劲。"

    old "I'm about halfway up when I feel myself getting light-headed."
    new "I'm about halfway up when I feel myself getting light-headed.\n爬到大约一半时，我发觉自己有些头晕。"

    old "Don't look down."
    new "Don't look down.\n别往下看。"

    old "I close my eyes and continue my ascent. My hands easily find the slots Galan has carved out, and several moments later, I thrust my arm into the air and my hand is kissed by the cool nighttime breeze."
    new "I close my eyes and continue my ascent. My hands easily find the slots Galan has carved out, and several moments later, I thrust my arm into the air and my hand is kissed by the cool nighttime breeze.\n我闭上眼睛继续向上。我的手轻松地摸到 Galan 凿出的凹槽，片刻之后，我把手臂探向空中，清凉的夜风轻吻着我的手掌。"

    old "I hoist myself out of the hole, and take a look around. We're in a niche at the corner of a stone building."
    new "I hoist myself out of the hole, and take a look around. We're in a niche at the corner of a stone building.\n我把自己从洞口撑出去，环顾四周。我们在一座石砌建筑拐角处的凹龛里。"

    old "Dasyra grins at me, and I grin back."
    new "Dasyra grins at me, and I grin back.\nDasyra 冲我咧嘴一笑，我也回以一笑。"

    old "I lean over the edge, and motion to Galan. He begins climbing."
    new "I lean over the edge, and motion to Galan. He begins climbing.\n我俯身探到边沿，朝 Galan 示意。他开始攀爬。"

    old "As Galan climbs, I poke my head out of the niche and survey our surroundings."
    new "As Galan climbs, I poke my head out of the niche and survey our surroundings.\n趁 Galan 攀爬时，我从凹龛里探出头，打量四周。"

    old "Ornamental trees in little plots of soil dot the estate in front of us. A small stream of water runs across the state several feet away. We must be in a courtyard of some sort."
    new "Ornamental trees in little plots of soil dot the estate in front of us. A small stream of water runs across the state several feet away. We must be in a courtyard of some sort.\n我们前方，庄园里点缀着一小片一小片土壤里栽种的观赏树。几英尺外，一道细小的水流蜿蜒穿过。我们想必身处某处庭院之中。"

    old "I hear Galan grunting, and turn around to see him lifting himself out of the hole."
    new "I hear Galan grunting, and turn around to see him lifting himself out of the hole.\n我听见 Galan 的闷哼声，转身看见他正把自己从洞里撑出来。"

    old "Dasyra points past some trees and whispers to us."
    new "Dasyra points past some trees and whispers to us.\nDasyra 指向几棵树后面，低声对我们说。"

    old "I think that's the wall of the estate. Beyond it is the neighboring estate. We'll need to follow to wall to the front, where it meets the street. Then we can climb over and be out of here."
    new "I think that's the wall of the estate. Beyond it is the neighboring estate. We'll need to follow to wall to the front, where it meets the street. Then we can climb over and be out of here.\n我想那就是庄园的围墙。墙外是相邻的庄园。我们得沿着墙走到前面，也就是它和街道相接的地方。然后翻过去，就能离开这里了。"

    old "They lock the front gate at night, and it requires the strength of several men to open. But that's good news for us. It means that even if we are seen climbing over the wall, it'll be hard for any roaming guards to follow us."
    new "They lock the front gate at night, and it requires the strength of several men to open. But that's good news for us. It means that even if we are seen climbing over the wall, it'll be hard for any roaming guards to follow us.\n夜里前门会上锁，得要好几个人的力气才打得开。不过这对我们倒是好事。也就是说，就算我们翻墙时被看见，巡逻的守卫也很难追上来。"

    old "Alright, let's go. Light feet."
    new "Alright, let's go. Light feet.\n好，走吧。脚步放轻。"

    old "Hold on a moment."
    new "Hold on a moment.\n等一下。"

    old "Galan motions behind us. There's what looks like a small encampment set up."
    new "Galan motions behind us. There's what looks like a small encampment set up.\nGalan 朝我们身后示意。那里像是搭了个小营地。"

    old "What's an encampment like that doing in the middle of a noble estate?"
    new "What's an encampment like that doing in the middle of a noble estate?\n贵族的庄园正当中，怎么会有那样一个营地？"

    old "The guards set these up at night. They rotate the guard shifts at night, and some of them sleep in tents like these so that they don't have to constantly leave and exit the estate during the night. Some of them actually prefer sleeping outside on hot summer nights."
    new "The guards set these up at night. They rotate the guard shifts at night, and some of them sleep in tents like these so that they don't have to constantly leave and exit the estate during the night. Some of them actually prefer sleeping outside on hot summer nights.\n是守卫夜里搭的。他们晚上轮班，有些人就睡在这种帐篷里，省得夜里反复进出庄园。其实有些人还就喜欢在炎热的夏夜睡在外面。"

    old "There's a bunch of stuff there. And I think I recognize the shape of that hammer."
    new "There's a bunch of stuff there. And I think I recognize the shape of that hammer.\n那里堆着一堆东西。我想我认出了那把锤子的形状。"

    old "Let's check it out. Quietly, of course."
    new "Let's check it out. Quietly, of course.\n去看看。当然，悄悄的。"

    old "We creep over to the encampment. Luckily, there doesn't seem to be anyone sleeping here at the moment."
    new "We creep over to the encampment. Luckily, there doesn't seem to be anyone sleeping here at the moment.\n我们蹑手蹑脚摸到营地旁。幸运的是，这会儿似乎没人在此睡觉。"

    old "This is certainly my hammer."
    new "This is certainly my hammer.\n这的确是我的锤子。"

    old "And this is my staff."
    new "And this is my staff.\n这是我的法杖。"

    old "And it looks like my possessions are here, too. Strange for them to leave it just lying about here..."
    new "And it looks like my possessions are here, too. Strange for them to leave it just lying about here...\n看来我的物品也在这儿。真奇怪，他们就这么随手丢在这里……"

    old "See that table with the deck of cards? They were probably going to gamble to decide how to divide our possessions amongst themselves."
    new "See that table with the deck of cards? They were probably going to gamble to decide how to divide our possessions amongst themselves.\n看到那张摆着纸牌的桌子了吗？他们八成是打算赌上几把，来决定怎么瓜分我们的财物。"

    old "Well, I guess we'll just have to steal their prize pot."
    new "Well, I guess we'll just have to steal their prize pot.\n嗯，我看我们只好把他们这份彩头偷走咯。"

    old "I don't think it counts as stealing if it was originally yours to start with."
    new "I don't think it counts as stealing if it was originally yours to start with.\n要是本来就是你的东西，我看那也不算偷。"

    old "Alright, we have our things back, but we still need to get out of here. Let's get to the edge of the courtyard, where we can hide in the shadows."
    new "Alright, we have our things back, but we still need to get out of here. Let's get to the edge of the courtyard, where we can hide in the shadows.\n好，东西都拿回来了，可我们还得离开这里。到庭院边上去吧，那里能躲在阴影里。"

    old "We tread softly across the courtyard to the front wall, then begin making our way toward the front wall."
    new "We tread softly across the courtyard to the front wall, then begin making our way toward the front wall.\n我们轻手轻脚穿过庭院，朝前墙方向摸去。"

    old "Dasyra holds a finger to her lips, then motions toward two guards, standing in front of the house. The front of the house is dimly lit, with only two torches for light, but if we continue along the side wall, we'll surely pass through their field of vision."
    new "Dasyra holds a finger to her lips, then motions toward two guards, standing in front of the house. The front of the house is dimly lit, with only two torches for light, but if we continue along the side wall, we'll surely pass through their field of vision.\nDasyra 把手指竖在唇边，然后朝站在屋前的两个守卫示意。屋前灯火昏暗，只有两支火把照明，可我们若继续沿侧墙走，势必会进入他们的视野。"

    old "I nod and lower my voice to a whisper."
    new "I nod and lower my voice to a whisper.\n我点点头，把声音压低成耳语。"

    old "We need to expose ourselves to these two guards to reach the front, there's no way around it. How should we approach it?"
    new "We need to expose ourselves to these two guards to reach the front, there's no way around it. How should we approach it?\n要到达前面，就非得在这两个守卫面前暴露不可，别无他法。我们该怎么过去？"

    old "I say we make a run for it. By the time the guards realize what's happening, we'll have a head start, and they probably won't have enough time to catch up."
    new "I say we make a run for it. By the time the guards realize what's happening, we'll have a head start, and they probably won't have enough time to catch up.\n我说咱们拔腿就跑。等守卫反应过来，我们已抢先一步，他们八成来不及追上。"

    old "I wouldn't be so sure. Arasmas has attack dogs by one of the side yards, and if we're seen running, they'll likely send the dogs after us. You can't outrun dogs like those."
    new "I wouldn't be so sure. Arasmas has attack dogs by one of the side yards, and if we're seen running, they'll likely send the dogs after us. You can't outrun dogs like those.\n我可没这么把握。Arasmas 在一个侧院养了恶犬，我们若被发现逃跑，他们多半会放狗追来。那种狗你可跑不过。"

    old "So what do you suggest?"
    new "So what do you suggest?\n那你有什么建议？"

    old "We should attack the guards. Take them out before anyone else knows what's happening. Then, if no one sees us, we can sneak along the wall like we planned."
    new "We should attack the guards. Take them out before anyone else knows what's happening. Then, if no one sees us, we can sneak along the wall like we planned.\n我们应该攻击守卫，在旁人察觉之前把他们放倒。然后，只要没人看见，我们就能按原计划沿墙溜走。"

    old "Hmm."
    new "Hmm.\n嗯……"

    old "Dasyra and Galan turn to me with a look of expectation. How are we to proceed?"
    new "Dasyra and Galan turn to me with a look of expectation. How are we to proceed?\nDasyra 和 Galan 满含期待地转向我。我们该如何行动？"

    old "Let's make a run for it. If the send the dogs after us, we'll just have to deal with them."
    new "Let's make a run for it. If the send the dogs after us, we'll just have to deal with them.\n咱们拔腿跑吧。他们若放狗追来，那也只能硬着头皮应付了。"

    old "On my mark, we run for the front. Okay?"
    new "On my mark, we run for the front. Okay?\n听我号令，一起朝前面跑。明白吗？"

    old "They nod."
    new "They nod.\n他们点点头。"

    old "I hold up five fingers and count down. Four, three, two, one..."
    new "I hold up five fingers and count down. Four, three, two, one...\n我举起五根手指倒数。四、三、二、一……"

    old "I close my fist and we begin running. No looking back, eyes on the prize."
    new "I close my fist and we begin running. No looking back, eyes on the prize.\n我攥紧拳头，我们拔腿就跑。别回头，盯住目标。"

    old "Hey!"
    new "Hey!\n嘿！"

    old "The guards start running after us. We should have no trouble outrunning the guards, but within moments I hear the barking of dogs in the distance. We're well ahead of them, but the sound of barking grows closer with every passing moment."
    new "The guards start running after us. We should have no trouble outrunning the guards, but within moments I hear the barking of dogs in the distance. We're well ahead of them, but the sound of barking grows closer with every passing moment.\n守卫们开始追赶。甩掉这些守卫本不成问题，可没过片刻，我便听见远处传来狗吠。我们遥遥领先，可狗吠声却一刻比一刻逼近。"

    old "Keep running!"
    new "Keep running!\n继续跑！"

    old "We get halfway across the courtyard when I year a yelp from Dasyra. I spin around just in time to see one of the dogs lunge at her."
    new "We get halfway across the courtyard when I year a yelp from Dasyra. I spin around just in time to see one of the dogs lunge at her.\n我们跑到庭院半途时，我听见 Dasyra 一声尖叫。我猛地转身，正好看见一条狗朝她扑去。"

    old "We'll have to fight our way out of this one. Weapons ready!"
    new "We'll have to fight our way out of this one. Weapons ready!\n这一关咱们得杀出去了。抄家伙！"

    old "We've wasted enough time fighting. Time to run."
    new "We've wasted enough time fighting. Time to run.\n我们已经浪费够多时间打架了。该跑了。"

    old "The wall is fifty feet away. I can't see Galan or Dasyra, but I can hear their breath on either side of me, following several feet behind. The guards follow in hot pursuit."
    new "The wall is fifty feet away. I can't see Galan or Dasyra, but I can hear their breath on either side of me, following several feet behind. The guards follow in hot pursuit.\n墙还有五十英尺远。我看不见 Galan 或 Dasyra，却能听见他们在我两侧、身后几英尺处喘息。守卫紧追不舍。"

    old "Let's attack the guards. Hopefully no one sees us."
    new "Let's attack the guards. Hopefully no one sees us.\n咱们攻击守卫。但愿没人看见。"

    old "We creep through the shadows towards the guards, until we're so close that I can make out the shape of the individual hairs on their chins."
    new "We creep through the shadows towards the guards, until we're so close that I can make out the shape of the individual hairs on their chins.\n我们借着阴影朝守卫潜行，近到连他们下巴上一根根胡须的形状都看得清。"

    old "Attack!"
    new "Attack!\n上！"

    old "We manage to subdue the guards, but I hear yelling from inside."
    new "We manage to subdue the guards, but I hear yelling from inside.\n我们总算制伏了守卫，却听见屋内传来喊声。"

    old "What's going on out there?"
    new "What's going on out there?\n外面出什么事了？"

    old "I'm not sure. It's probably nothing."
    new "I'm not sure. It's probably nothing.\n不清楚。大概没什么吧。"

    old "I think we should investigate..."
    new "I think we should investigate...\n我觉得该去看看……"

    old "Are you sure? Ugh."
    new "Are you sure? Ugh.\n你确定吗？啧。"

    old "It doesn't seem like they're on to us just yet, but we shouldn't tarry. Move quickly, but stay quiet in the shadows, just like we planned."
    new "It doesn't seem like they're on to us just yet, but we shouldn't tarry. Move quickly, but stay quiet in the shadows, just like we planned.\n他们似乎还没察觉我们，可我们也不该耽搁。快走，但要像计划的那样，在阴影里保持安静。"

    old "We get halfway toward our goal when I hear the sound of a door opening and footsteps leaving the estate."
    new "We get halfway toward our goal when I hear the sound of a door opening and footsteps leaving the estate.\n我们朝目标走到一半时，我听见开门声和脚步声离开庄园。"

    old "Hey, we've got several men down! What happened to these guys?"
    new "Hey, we've got several men down! What happened to these guys?\n嘿，好几个人倒下了！这些家伙怎么回事？"

    old "This doesn't look good..."
    new "This doesn't look good...\n这下可糟了……"

    old "Stay quiet. They still haven't seen us..."
    new "Stay quiet. They still haven't seen us...\n别出声。他们还没发现我们……"

    old "We continue creeping along. We're but a mere fifty feet from the wall when I hear the sound of yelling behind us."
    new "We continue creeping along. We're but a mere fifty feet from the wall when I hear the sound of yelling behind us.\n我们继续潜行。离墙只剩区区五十英尺时，我听见身后传来喊叫声。"

    old "Hey! Look, out there! Three of them!"
    new "Hey! Look, out there! Three of them!\n嘿！快看，那边！三个！"

    old "The jig is up. Run!"
    new "The jig is up. Run!\n露馅了。快跑！"

    old "We break into a sprint for the wall."
    new "We break into a sprint for the wall.\n我们朝着墙拔腿狂奔。"

    old "I can't see Galan or Dasyra, but I can hear their breath on either side of me, following several feet behind. The guards follow in hot pursuit."
    new "I can't see Galan or Dasyra, but I can hear their breath on either side of me, following several feet behind. The guards follow in hot pursuit.\n我看不见 Galan 或 Dasyra，却能听见他们在我两侧、身后几英尺处喘息。守卫紧追不舍。"

    old "Intruders!"
    new "Intruders!\n有闯入者！"

    old "I hear a door open. More guards must be emerging from somewhere else on the estate, but they're long behind us now."
    new "I hear a door open. More guards must be emerging from somewhere else on the estate, but they're long behind us now.\n我听见有门打开。想必有更多守卫从庄园别处涌出，可他们此刻已被我们远远甩在身后。"

    old "I reach the front wall. It's more fence than wall, twenty feet high with vertical metal bars, each several inches apart."
    new "I reach the front wall. It's more fence than wall, twenty feet high with vertical metal bars, each several inches apart.\n我冲到前墙边。说是墙，倒更像栅栏，二十英尺高，竖着一根根金属栏杆，每根相隔几英寸。"

    old "Climb!"
    new "Climb!\n爬！"

    old "I grasp two of the metal bars and begin climbing. Left arm up. Right arm up. Left arm. Right arm. Left. Right."
    new "I grasp two of the metal bars and begin climbing. Left arm up. Right arm up. Left arm. Right arm. Left. Right.\n我抓住两根金属栏杆，开始向上爬。左臂上，右臂上。左臂，右臂。左，右。"

    old "Galan and Dasyra follow several seconds behind me. I reach the top of the wall."
    new "Galan and Dasyra follow several seconds behind me. I reach the top of the wall.\nGalan 和 Dasyra 落后我几秒跟上。我爬到了墙顶。"

    old "[protag], help me!"
    new "[protag], help me!\n[protag]，帮帮我！"

    old "I hoist myself onto the top of the wall and look back at Galan and Dasyra. Two guards have caught up to us, with more on the way. Galan and Dasyra have climbed high enough to avoid their weapons, but the guards have begun throwing rocks at them."
    new "I hoist myself onto the top of the wall and look back at Galan and Dasyra. Two guards have caught up to us, with more on the way. Galan and Dasyra have climbed high enough to avoid their weapons, but the guards have begun throwing rocks at them.\n我攀上墙顶，回头看向 Galan 和 Dasyra。两个守卫追了上来，还有更多正赶来。Galan 和 Dasyra 已爬得够高，够不着他们的兵器，可守卫们已开始朝他们扔石头。"

    old "A rock hits Galan on the arm, and his grip loosens."
    new "A rock hits Galan on the arm, and his grip loosens.\n一块石头砸中 Galan 的手臂，他抓握的手松了。"

    old "Augh-"
    new "Augh-\n啊——"

    old "I'm slipping!"
    new "I'm slipping!\n我抓不住了！"

    old "I reach down and grab Dasyra by the arm. I pull her up and she catches the top of the wall with her feet."
    new "I reach down and grab Dasyra by the arm. I pull her up and she catches the top of the wall with her feet.\n我俯身抓住 Dasyra 的手臂，把她拉上来，她用脚勾住了墙顶。"

    old "Shit!"
    new "Shit!\n该死！"

    old "Galan is hanging by one arm. I reach down and grab him, but a rock hits me in the hand and I lose my grip on him."
    new "Galan is hanging by one arm. I reach down and grab him, but a rock hits me in the hand and I lose my grip on him.\nGalan 只剩一只手臂吊着。我俯身抓住他，可一块石头砸中我的手，我松开了他。"

    old "Galan tumbles downward, hitting the ground and landing on his back. A guard runs up from the direction of the house and kicks him in the chest. Galan curls up on the ground."
    new "Galan tumbles downward, hitting the ground and landing on his back. A guard runs up from the direction of the house and kicks him in the chest. Galan curls up on the ground.\nGalan 滚落下去，摔在地上，仰面朝天。一个守卫从屋子的方向冲来，朝他的胸口踹了一脚。Galan 蜷缩在地。"

    old "Three more guards come running up. There are now six guards on the ground, with more on the way."
    new "Three more guards come running up. There are now six guards on the ground, with more on the way.\n又有三个守卫冲来。如今地面上有六个守卫，还有更多正赶来。"

    old "Run! Run!"
    new "Run! Run!\n快跑！快跑！"

    old "We have to go, Dasyra."
    new "We have to go, Dasyra.\n我们得走了，Dasyra。"

    old "Dasyra and I bound over the wall and slide to the ground outside the estate, then take off running. Dasyra overtakes me, and I follow her, taking several turns in the road until we arrive at a deserted allyway, far away from the Arasmas estate."
    new "Dasyra and I bound over the wall and slide to the ground outside the estate, then take off running. Dasyra overtakes me, and I follow her, taking several turns in the road until we arrive at a deserted allyway, far away from the Arasmas estate.\n我和 Dasyra 翻过墙，滑落到庄园外的地面，随即拔腿狂奔。Dasyra 超过了我，我跟着她，在路上拐了几个弯，直到来到一条荒僻的小巷，远离了 Arasmas 庄园。"

    old "What are we going to do?"
    new "What are we going to do?\n我们该怎么办？"

    old "I wish we could do something for Galan, but I don't think there's anything we can do. He's guilty in the eyes of the law, and you and I will be imprisoned if we go back and try to help him. I'm going to leave this city. Tonight, if at all possible."
    new "I wish we could do something for Galan, but I don't think there's anything we can do. He's guilty in the eyes of the law, and you and I will be imprisoned if we go back and try to help him. I'm going to leave this city. Tonight, if at all possible.\n我多希望能为 Galan 做点什么，可我觉得我们无能为力。在律法眼中他是有罪的，而你我若回去帮他，也会被关进大牢。我要离开这座城，今晚，只要有可能就走。"

    old "What about me?"
    new "What about me?\n那我呢？"

    old "You? I don't know. Can't you go back to your life?"
    new "You? I don't know. Can't you go back to your life?\n你？我不知道。你不能回到自己的生活里去吗？"

    old "They'll be looking for me. I don't know anywhere I'll be safe."
    new "They'll be looking for me. I don't know anywhere I'll be safe.\n他们会搜捕我的。我不知道哪儿才安全。"

    old "Well then, you can come with me to Grimoire. It may not be a permanent solution, but we can take the time to decide what to do next once Hammerhands is far behind us."
    new "Well then, you can come with me to Grimoire. It may not be a permanent solution, but we can take the time to decide what to do next once Hammerhands is far behind us.\n那么，你可以跟我去 Grimoire。这也许不是长久之计，但等 Hammerhands 被我们远远甩在身后，我们有的是时间决定下一步。"

    old "I'll go with you, then. To Grimoire."
    new "I'll go with you, then. To Grimoire.\n那我就跟你走。去 Grimoire。"

    old "Galan is hanging by one arm. I reach down and grab his hand, pulling him up on top of the wall. He catches the top of the wall with both feet."
    new "Galan is hanging by one arm. I reach down and grab his hand, pulling him up on top of the wall. He catches the top of the wall with both feet.\nGalan 只剩一只手臂吊着。我俯身抓住他的手，把他拉上墙顶。他用双脚勾住了墙顶。"

    old "Ah!"
    new "Ah!\n啊！"

    old "Dasyra is sliding down the wall. Galan and I both reach out to grab her, but she's already slid beyond our reach."
    new "Dasyra is sliding down the wall. Galan and I both reach out to grab her, but she's already slid beyond our reach.\nDasyra 正沿着墙往下滑。我和 Galan 都伸手去抓她，可她已经滑出了我们够得着的范围。"

    old "One of the guards grabs her by the legs, pulling her off the wall. Another quickly steps up to grab her by the arms."
    new "One of the guards grabs her by the legs, pulling her off the wall. Another quickly steps up to grab her by the arms.\n一个守卫抓住她的腿，把她从墙上拽下。另一个迅速上前，抓住她的手臂。"

    old "Four more guards come running up from the house. There are now six guards on the ground below us, with more on the way."
    new "Four more guards come running up from the house. There are now six guards on the ground below us, with more on the way.\n又有四个守卫从屋子方向冲来。如今我们下方地面上有六个守卫，还有更多正赶来。"

    old "Dasyra!"
    new "Dasyra!\nDasyra！"

    old "Go! You have to go!"
    new "Go! You have to go!\n走！你们快走！"

    old "Let's go, Galan. There's nothing we can do."
    new "Let's go, Galan. There's nothing we can do.\n我们走吧，Galan。我们无能为力了。"

    old "Galan and I bound over the wall and slide to the ground outside the estate, then take off running. We take several twists and turns through allies, with Galan leading the way. We don't stop running until we're far, far away from the Arasmas estate."
    new "Galan and I bound over the wall and slide to the ground outside the estate, then take off running. We take several twists and turns through allies, with Galan leading the way. We don't stop running until we're far, far away from the Arasmas estate.\n我和 Galan 翻过墙，滑落到庄园外的地面，随即拔腿狂奔。我们穿过一条条小巷，几经拐弯，由 Galan 带路。直到远远、远远离开了 Arasmas 庄园，我们才停下脚步。"

    old "What do we do now?"
    new "What do we do now?\n我们现在怎么办？"

    old "I don't think there's anything we can do for Dasyra. She's guilty in the eyes of the law. You and I are, too. We'll be imprisoned if we go back and try to help her. I'm going to leave this city tonight. It won't be long before they leave the estate to search the city for us."
    new "I don't think there's anything we can do for Dasyra. She's guilty in the eyes of the law. You and I are, too. We'll be imprisoned if we go back and try to help her. I'm going to leave this city tonight. It won't be long before they leave the estate to search the city for us.\n我想我们帮不了 Dasyra 了。在律法眼中她是有罪的，你我也是。我们若回去帮她，也会被关进大牢。我今晚就离开这座城。用不了多久，他们就会离开庄园，进城搜捕我们。"

    old "I have no destination to head for. There's no place that I call home."
    new "I have no destination to head for. There's no place that I call home.\n我没有目的地可去。这世上没有我能称之为家的地方。"

    old "I'm headed for Grimoire. You're welcome to accompany me if you like. We'll decide what to do once Hammerhand is far behind us."
    new "I'm headed for Grimoire. You're welcome to accompany me if you like. We'll decide what to do once Hammerhand is far behind us.\n我要去 Grimoire。你愿意的话，欢迎与我同行。等 Hammerhands 被我们远远甩在身后，再决定怎么办。"

    old "I find Dasyra at the inn where we agreed to meet."
    new "I find Dasyra at the inn where we agreed to meet.\n我在约好碰面的旅店找到了 Dasyra。"

    old "Dasyra."
    new "Dasyra.\nDasyra。"

    old "[protag]."
    new "[protag].\n[protag]。"

    old "I take it you have questions for me."
    new "I take it you have questions for me.\n我猜你有问题想问我。"

    old "Yes, I do."
    new "Yes, I do.\n是的，我有。"

    old "Well, go ahead. We've been to hell and back together, so any question you have, I'll answer."
    new "Well, go ahead. We've been to hell and back together, so any question you have, I'll answer.\n那问吧。我们是一起出生入死过的，你问什么，我都答。"

    old "Who are you, and what were you doing in Hammerhands?"
    new "Who are you, and what were you doing in Hammerhands?\n你是谁，你在 Hammerhands 做什么？"

    old "I'm an operator working on behalf of the council of Grimoire. I was in Hammerhands looking for potential allies."
    new "I'm an operator working on behalf of the council of Grimoire. I was in Hammerhands looking for potential allies.\n我是一名探员，为 Grimoire 议会效力。我在 Hammerhands 寻找潜在的盟友。"

    old "Allies in what, exactly?"
    new "Allies in what, exactly?\n到底是什么事的盟友？"

    old "There's been dire business happening at the Castle of N'mar. For a long time, it's been an isolated problem. But recently, the elders of Grimoire decided that it was a problem for the people of Grimoire."
    new "There's been dire business happening at the Castle of N'mar. For a long time, it's been an isolated problem. But recently, the elders of Grimoire decided that it was a problem for the people of Grimoire.\nN'mar 城堡里正发生着可怕的事。长久以来，那一直是个孤立的祸患。可最近，Grimoire 的长老们认定，那已是 Grimoire 子民的忧患了。"

    old "The Castle of N'mar is a den of evil, and it's leaking. My mission is to do something about it."
    new "The Castle of N'mar is a den of evil, and it's leaking. My mission is to do something about it.\nN'mar 城堡是个邪恶的巢穴，如今恶在向外蔓延。我的任务就是去解决它。"

    old "You're going to do 'something' about it? What, exactly?"
    new "You're going to do 'something' about it? What, exactly?\n你要去「解决」它？具体怎么做？"

    old "Well, I'm going to invade. Me, and whatever allies I can assemble."
    new "Well, I'm going to invade. Me, and whatever allies I can assemble.\n嗯，我要攻打进去。就我，加上我能集结到的所有盟友。"

    old "And your quest brought you to Hammerhands."
    new "And your quest brought you to Hammerhands.\n而你的使命把你带到了 Hammerhands。"

    old "Well, did you find the allies you were looking for in Hammerhands?"
    new "Well, did you find the allies you were looking for in Hammerhands?\n那么，你在 Hammerhands 找到想找的盟友了吗？"

    old "Maybe you can answer that question for me, Dasyra."
    new "Maybe you can answer that question for me, Dasyra.\n也许这个问题该由你来替我回答，Dasyra。"

    old "I found a pair of people that I would consider myself confident to fight alongside as allies. One of them didn't make it out of the city with me. The other did."
    new "I found a pair of people that I would consider myself confident to fight alongside as allies. One of them didn't make it out of the city with me. The other did.\n我找到了两个人，我自信能与他们并肩作战。其中一人没能随我出城，另一个出来了。"

    old "A faint smile forms on Dasyra's face."
    new "A faint smile forms on Dasyra's face.\nDasyra 脸上浮现出一抹淡淡的微笑。"

    old "You want me to go fight the undead with you."
    new "You want me to go fight the undead with you.\n你想让我跟你一起去对付不死族。"

    old "You seem like you might be cut out for this kind of thing, Dasyra. You're a healer, and your talents could come in handy when fighting the undead. And we've faced combat together, in case you need me to remind you how it is that we ended up meeting. I think you'd make an excellent ally."
    new "You seem like you might be cut out for this kind of thing, Dasyra. You're a healer, and your talents could come in handy when fighting the undead. And we've faced combat together, in case you need me to remind you how it is that we ended up meeting. I think you'd make an excellent ally.\nDasyra，你看起来就是干这事的料。你是治疗师，与不死族交战时，你的本领大有用处。而且我们并肩作战过——需要我提醒你我们是怎么相遇的吗？我想你会是个出色的盟友。"

    old "How can I say anything but yes? It's the least I can do."
    new "How can I say anything but yes? It's the least I can do.\n我又怎能拒绝呢？这是我至少该做的。"

    old "No. I got caught up in...that Arasmas business before I had the chance to go looking around."
    new "No. I got caught up in...that Arasmas business before I had the chance to go looking around.\n没有。我还来不及四处打探，就卷进了……那桩 Arasmas 的麻烦事。"

    old "Are you sure you didn't find anyone that you'd want to accompany on your creepy adventures around N'mar?"
    new "Are you sure you didn't find anyone that you'd want to accompany on your creepy adventures around N'mar?\n你确定没找到想带着一起去 N'mar 闯荡的人吗？"

    old "Pretty sure."
    new "Pretty sure.\n相当确定。"

    old "What about..."
    new "What about...\n那……"

    old "Dasyra puts her arms oh her hips and cocks her head."
    new "Dasyra puts her arms oh her hips and cocks her head.\nDasyra 双手叉腰，歪着头。"

    old "You?"
    new "You?\n你呢？"

    old "I know I don't look like much. But I'm a healer. Those can come in handy when you're fighting the undead. And though I don't have much combat experience, I think I can hold my own. What do you say?"
    new "I know I don't look like much. But I'm a healer. Those can come in handy when you're fighting the undead. And though I don't have much combat experience, I think I can hold my own. What do you say?\n我知道自己看着不怎么起眼。但我是个治疗师，跟不死族交战时，这一手能派上用场。而且我虽然战斗经验不多，想来也能自保。你觉得呢？"

    old "If you're offering your help, I don't think I can say no. We've fought alongside one another once before, and I'd trust you with my life again."
    new "If you're offering your help, I don't think I can say no. We've fought alongside one another once before, and I'd trust you with my life again.\n你既愿出手相助，我实在无法拒绝。我们先前并肩作战过，我愿再次把性命托付给你。"

    old "I'm glad to be of service."
    new "I'm glad to be of service.\n能帮上忙，我很高兴。"

    old "I'll stay here in Grimoire. If you need me, I'm here."
    new "I'll stay here in Grimoire. If you need me, I'm here.\n我会留在 Grimoire。你若需要我，我就在这里。"

    old "I encounter Galan at the inn where we agreed to meet."
    new "I encounter Galan at the inn where we agreed to meet.\n我在约好碰面的旅店遇见了 Galan。"

    old "Galan."
    new "Galan.\nGalan。"

    old "Do you want to talk about what happened?"
    new "Do you want to talk about what happened?\n你想谈谈发生的事吗？"

    old "What exactly did you want to talk about?"
    new "What exactly did you want to talk about?\n你具体想谈什么？"

    old "I'm thinking about how we left Dasyra."
    new "I'm thinking about how we left Dasyra.\n我在想我们抛下 Dasyra 的事。"

    old "I mean, when all is said and done, I guess she is living in the hole she dug for herself. Still, we did leave her."
    new "I mean, when all is said and done, I guess she is living in the hole she dug for herself. Still, we did leave her.\n我的意思是，说来说去，她大概也是自掘坟墓。可说到底，我们终究还是抛下了她。"

    old "We would have taken her with us if we could. Things just didn't work out."
    new "We would have taken her with us if we could. Things just didn't work out.\n我们若能带她走，早就带了。只是事与愿违。"

    old "I guess you're right. She did the crime, and now she'll pay the penalty."
    new "I guess you're right. She did the crime, and now she'll pay the penalty.\n我想你说得对。她犯了罪，如今自食其果。"

    old "And I guess there's nothing to be gained by subjecting ourselves to the same fate."
    new "And I guess there's nothing to be gained by subjecting ourselves to the same fate.\n而我想，把自己也搭进同样的命运，也捞不到什么好处。"

    old "Galan, there's something you need to know about Dasyra."
    new "Galan, there's something you need to know about Dasyra.\nGalan，关于 Dasyra，有件事你需要知道。"

    old "When we found Dasyra on the street, getting accosted by those Arasmas guards, they claimed that she was a thief, and they were apprehending her."
    new "When we found Dasyra on the street, getting accosted by those Arasmas guards, they claimed that she was a thief, and they were apprehending her.\n我们在街上发现 Dasyra 时，她正被那些 Arasmas 守卫拦住。他们声称她是个小偷，正在捉拿她。"

    old "Yes, I remember the whole incident quite clearly."
    new "Yes, I remember the whole incident quite clearly.\n对，整件事我记得清清楚楚。"

    old "They claimed that she stole the brooch she was carrying."
    new "They claimed that she stole the brooch she was carrying.\n他们声称，她偷了她随身携带的那枚胸针。"

    old "Yes. What about it?"
    new "Yes. What about it?\n对。那又怎样？"

    old "The brooch that she was carrying actually was stolen from the Arasmas estate."
    new "The brooch that she was carrying actually was stolen from the Arasmas estate.\n她携带的那枚胸针，确实是从 Arasmas 庄园偷来的。"

    old "Wow."
    new "Wow.\n哇。"

    old "Galan takes a few steps back and buries his mouth in his hand."
    new "Galan takes a few steps back and buries his mouth in his hand.\nGalan 后退几步，用手捂住嘴。"

    old "I guess I shouldn't be too surprised. I figured something of the sort was possible. I mean, I didn't exactly bother to fact-find when I arrived at the scene. I saw a woman struggling, presumed she was a victim, and leapt to action."
    new "I guess I shouldn't be too surprised. I figured something of the sort was possible. I mean, I didn't exactly bother to fact-find when I arrived at the scene. I saw a woman struggling, presumed she was a victim, and leapt to action.\n我想我也不必太意外。我早料到有这种可能。我是说，我赶到现场时，压根没费心去核实。我看见一个女人在挣扎，就当她是受害者，冲上去就动手了。"

    old "I did the same thing."
    new "I did the same thing.\n我也一样。"

    old "Well. What's done is done. I guess she'll have to live with the choices she's made."
    new "Well. What's done is done. I guess she'll have to live with the choices she's made.\n唉，木已成舟。我想她得为自己所做的选择承担后果了。"

    old "I guess there's no reason for us to subject ourselves to the same fate. I've been across these lands, far and wide, and truth be told, Hammerhands is pretty far from being the nicest place I've ever stayed. I don't think I'll be going back any time soon."
    new "I guess there's no reason for us to subject ourselves to the same fate. I've been across these lands, far and wide, and truth be told, Hammerhands is pretty far from being the nicest place I've ever stayed. I don't think I'll be going back any time soon.\n我想我们也没理由把自己搭进同样的命运。这片土地我纵横走过，说句实话，Hammerhands 离我待过的最舒服的地方还差得远。我想我短期内不会回去了。"

    old "So, what's are you up to next? We've just put one ordeal behind us, what ordeal remains to be dealt with for you?"
    new "So, what's are you up to next? We've just put one ordeal behind us, what ordeal remains to be dealt with for you?\n那么，你接下来要做什么？我们刚了结一桩磨难，你面前还剩下什么磨难要对付？"

    old "The Castle of N'Mar is leaking corruption. It has been, for a long time. But it's getting to be a problem for Grimoire. And it's a problem for me."
    new "The Castle of N'Mar is leaking corruption. It has been, for a long time. But it's getting to be a problem for Grimoire. And it's a problem for me.\nN'Mar 城堡正在向外渗出邪恶。这情形由来已久。可如今，它已渐渐成为 Grimoire 的祸患。也是我的祸患。"

    old "So what are you going to do about it?"
    new "So what are you going to do about it?\n那你打算怎么办？"

    old "Invade the castle. Put an end to whatever evil lurks within. I have the backing of Grimoire's leadership."
    new "Invade the castle. Put an end to whatever evil lurks within. I have the backing of Grimoire's leadership.\n攻打进城堡。终结潜伏其中的一切邪恶。我有 Grimoire 领导层的支持。"

    old "Do you suppose another man with a hammer would be useful on your mission?"
    new "Do you suppose another man with a hammer would be useful on your mission?\n你觉得，你的任务里再添一个抡锤子的人，可还派得上用场？"

    old "Are you offering?"
    new "Are you offering?\n你这是在请缨？"

    old "Aye. If there's one thing I'm good for, it's fighting. Haven't fought ghouls before, but I imagine fighting a ghoul isn't much different from fighting a man. Anything will succumb if you hit it hard enough, and I'm good at hitting things."
    new "Aye. If there's one thing I'm good for, it's fighting. Haven't fought ghouls before, but I imagine fighting a ghoul isn't much different from fighting a man. Anything will succumb if you hit it hard enough, and I'm good at hitting things.\n正是。要说我有一样拿手本事，那就是打架。食尸鬼我倒没打过，不过我想，跟食尸鬼打和跟人打也差不了多少。只要砸得够狠，什么东西都得趴下，而我正擅长砸东西。"

    old "I'd appreciate your help. You're a capable fighter, Galan. I know that from first-hand experience."
    new "I'd appreciate your help. You're a capable fighter, Galan. I know that from first-hand experience.\n有你相助，我感激不尽。你是个能打的战士，Galan。这一点我亲身体会过。"

    old "Grimoire's a nice enough place. I can call it home until I'm done helping you with your ghoul-hunting."
    new "Grimoire's a nice enough place. I can call it home until I'm done helping you with your ghoul-hunting.\nGrimoire 这地方不错。在我帮你除完食尸鬼之前，我可以把它当作家。"

    old "I begin trekking down the road to Farshade. If Kusho has been absent from the capital for this long, it's probable that he's taken up temporary residence in one of the great forest's smaller settlements. Farshade seems as good a place as any to inquire about his whereabouts."
    new "I begin trekking down the road to Farshade. If Kusho has been absent from the capital for this long, it's probable that he's taken up temporary residence in one of the great forest's smaller settlements. Farshade seems as good a place as any to inquire about his whereabouts.\n我踏上通往 Farshade 的路。Kusho 离开都城这么久，很可能在大森林里某个较小的聚落临时落脚。想打听他的下落，Farshade 似乎是个不错的去处。"

    old "I'm less than an hour into my journey when I encounter the first unexpected difficulty."
    new "I'm less than an hour into my journey when I encounter the first unexpected difficulty.\n出发还不到一小时，我就遇上了第一个意外麻烦。"

    old "Several trees have been shattered at the roots, their trunks splayed across the main trail."
    new "Several trees have been shattered at the roots, their trunks splayed across the main trail.\n好几棵树被从根部击断，树干横七竖八地倒在主道上。"

    old "I peer beyond the fractured stumps of trees that once stood proud against the backdrop of the forest. A sea of smashed splinters extends further than I can see from the path."
    new "I peer beyond the fractured stumps of trees that once stood proud against the backdrop of the forest. A sea of smashed splinters extends further than I can see from the path.\n我朝那些断裂树桩的远方张望，它们曾傲然挺立在森林背景下。一片碎木的海洋，从我立足的小径一直延伸到目力难及之处。"

    old "Clearly, something caused this damage. The question is, what?"
    new "Clearly, something caused this damage. The question is, what?\n显然，是有什么东西造成了这场破坏。问题是，是什么呢？"

    old "I climb over the demolished tree branches and begin following the path that has been so violently carved through the trees and foliage. I step along logs and hop from stump to stump to avoid being caught in the dense underbrush."
    new "I climb over the demolished tree branches and begin following the path that has been so violently carved through the trees and foliage. I step along logs and hop from stump to stump to avoid being caught in the dense underbrush.\n我翻过被毁的树枝，开始沿着这条被暴力碾过树木枝叶的路径前行。我踩着倒木走，从一个个树桩间跳跃，以免陷进密实的灌木丛。"

    old "My progress is slow, but the midday sun shines bright along the pathway, no longer obstructed by the towering branches of the trees that have been toppled in this path of destruction."
    new "My progress is slow, but the midday sun shines bright along the pathway, no longer obstructed by the towering branches of the trees that have been toppled in this path of destruction.\n我行进缓慢，但正午的阳光明亮地洒在小径上，不再被那些在这条毁灭之路上倾倒的巨树枝叶所遮挡。"

    old "Eventually I reach a small clearing, and discover what I can only presume is the source of the destruction."
    new "Eventually I reach a small clearing, and discover what I can only presume is the source of the destruction.\n最终我来到一小片空地，发现了那场破坏的元凶——我只能这么推测。"

    old "It's a massive beast-"
    new "It's a massive beast-\n那是一只巨兽——"

    old "What ever destruction this beast wreaked, it doesn't seem to pose an imminent danger in its current state. It can't hurt to get a closer look."
    new "What ever destruction this beast wreaked, it doesn't seem to pose an imminent danger in its current state. It can't hurt to get a closer look.\n不管这只野兽曾造成多大的破坏，眼下它的状态似乎不构成迫在眉睫的危险。凑近看看也无妨。"

    old "I creep up until I'm close enough to feel the warmth of the beast's breath on my face. Much to my surprise, the breath has a crisp, almost loamy odor to it. This beast doesn't appear to be a flesh-eater."
    new "I creep up until I'm close enough to feel the warmth of the beast's breath on my face. Much to my surprise, the breath has a crisp, almost loamy odor to it. This beast doesn't appear to be a flesh-eater.\n我蹑手蹑脚靠近，直到能感受到野兽呼出的气息扑在脸上。令我惊讶的是，那气息带着一股清新、近乎泥土的气味。这只野兽似乎并非食肉之兽。"

    old "Waves of scaled flesh ripple and eb with each breath. In its slumbering state, the beast has an almost majestic appearance."
    new "Waves of scaled flesh ripple and eb with each breath. In its slumbering state, the beast has an almost majestic appearance.\n随着每一次呼吸，它鳞甲覆盖的躯体一阵阵起伏。沉睡之中，这野兽竟有一种近乎威严的气度。"

    old "Perhaps it's best to let sleeping beasts lie."
    new "Perhaps it's best to let sleeping beasts lie.\n也许最好还是别去打扰沉睡的野兽。"

    old "I turn around and flinch as I hear the sound of metal whiz past my ear."
    new "I turn around and flinch as I hear the sound of metal whiz past my ear.\n我转过身，忽听金属破空声擦过耳畔，吓得一缩。"

    old "I look back at the slumbering beast. A piece of metal is lodged in its neck."
    new "I look back at the slumbering beast. A piece of metal is lodged in its neck.\n我回头看向沉睡的野兽。一截金属钉在它的脖颈上。"

    old "Pardon my projectile."
    new "Pardon my projectile.\n多有冒犯，刚才那支箭。"

    old "I look up toward the source of the voice, and an elf drops down from the forest canopy, landing beside the beast. He whips out a blade and swiftly draws it across the beast's throat."
    new "I look up toward the source of the voice, and an elf drops down from the forest canopy, landing beside the beast. He whips out a blade and swiftly draws it across the beast's throat.\n我循声抬头，一个精灵从林冠上跃下，落在野兽身旁。他抽出一柄利刃，飞快地划过野兽的喉咙。"

    old "Blood gushes from the newly-formed wound. The elf wipes his blade on the underbrush and sheathes it."
    new "Blood gushes from the newly-formed wound. The elf wipes his blade on the underbrush and sheathes it.\n鲜血从新开的伤口喷涌而出。精灵在灌木上拭净刀刃，收刀入鞘。"

    old "I have to question what business someone like you has getting this close to a rampaging woodcrasher."
    new "I have to question what business someone like you has getting this close to a rampaging woodcrasher.\n我倒要问问，你这样的人，凑到一头狂暴的 woodcrasher 跟前做什么。"

    old "Rampaging? He looked pretty serene to me, up until the moment you drove an arrow through his neck."
    new "Rampaging? He looked pretty serene to me, up until the moment you drove an arrow through his neck.\n狂暴？在我看来他安详得很，直到你那一箭射穿他的脖子。"

    old "Actually, it's a she. See the ridges around the neck? Only females have them."
    new "Actually, it's a she. See the ridges around the neck? Only females have them.\n其实，是她。看到脖子周围的脊棱了吗？只有雌性才有。"

    old "I can't say I'm an expert on the species native to this forest."
    new "I can't say I'm an expert on the species native to this forest.\n我可不敢说自己是这片森林原生物种的专家。"

    old "She's not native. Look at these trees. Or what's left of them."
    new "She's not native. Look at these trees. Or what's left of them.\n她不是本地的物种。看看这些树，或者说看看它们剩下的样子。"

    old "He gestures to the path of demolished forest that I followed to arrive here."
    new "He gestures to the path of demolished forest that I followed to arrive here.\n他朝那条我一路跟来的、被夷平的森林路径示意。"

    old "There wouldn't be much forest left if these woodcrashers were prancing about on the regular."
    new "There wouldn't be much forest left if these woodcrashers were prancing about on the regular.\n要是这些 woodcrasher 三天两头四处乱闯，这森林怕是早就剩不下多少了。"

    old "Where did it come from?"
    new "Where did it come from?\n它是从哪儿来的？"

    old "The elf shrugs."
    new "The elf shrugs.\n精灵耸了耸肩。"

    old "Your guess is as good as mine. Well, actually, maybe it isn't. I'm probably more qualified to remark on the matters of this forest than you are. At least, I presume."
    new "Your guess is as good as mine. Well, actually, maybe it isn't. I'm probably more qualified to remark on the matters of this forest than you are. At least, I presume.\n你的猜测和我的也差不多。嗯，其实，也许未必。论起这片森林的事，我大概比你更有发言权。至少我这么以为。"

    old "Are you saying I look like I don't belong here?"
    new "Are you saying I look like I don't belong here?\n你是说，我看起来不像属于这里？"

    old "That, and you smell like you don't belong here. Did you come from the city? Because you've got the smell of the city on you."
    new "That, and you smell like you don't belong here. Did you come from the city? Because you've got the smell of the city on you.\n不光看起来，你闻起来也不像属于这里。你是从城里来的吧？你身上带着城里的味儿。"

    old "What does that mean?"
    new "What does that mean?\n这是什么意思？"

    old "I hear a low growl around us."
    new "I hear a low growl around us.\n我听见四周传来低沉的嗥叫。"

    old "It means that there are creatures around here who know that you don't belong."
    new "It means that there are creatures around here who know that you don't belong.\n意思是，这附近有些生灵，知道你不属于这里。"

    old "A wolf steps into the clearing. I can see only one wolf, but I hear growling from both the left and the right. It doesn't take a keen eye to see that we're surrounded."
    new "A wolf steps into the clearing. I can see only one wolf, but I hear growling from both the left and the right. It doesn't take a keen eye to see that we're surrounded.\n一头狼踏入空地。我只能看见一头，却听见左右两侧都有嗥叫。不必眼尖也看得出，我们被包围了。"

    old "I've still yet to appraise you as a friend or foe, but would you assist me in dispatching these wolves? Seeing as how this is partly your fault."
    new "I've still yet to appraise you as a friend or foe, but would you assist me in dispatching these wolves? Seeing as how this is partly your fault.\n我还没把你判成是友是敌，不过，你愿不愿帮我收拾掉这些狼？毕竟这事有几分是你招来的。"

    old "Let's do this."
    new "Let's do this.\n动手吧。"

    old "I suggest that we move. More might be coming. And we should get away from this bloody woodcrasher."
    new "I suggest that we move. More might be coming. And we should get away from this bloody woodcrasher.\n我建议咱们离开。可能还有更多要来。而且我们该离这头血淋淋的 woodcrasher 远点。"

    old "So was it the scent of blood that drew the wolves, or the smell of the city on me? Because you seemed to imply it was the latter."
    new "So was it the scent of blood that drew the wolves, or the smell of the city on me? Because you seemed to imply it was the latter.\n那么，引来狼群的，是血腥味，还是我身上的城市味？因为刚才听你的意思，似乎更偏向后者。"

    old "It was both. The scent of blood drew the wolves, but wolves know that where there's blood, there's often another predator. But when they smelled you, an outsider, they felt emboldened to attack. They can smell weakness."
    new "It was both. The scent of blood drew the wolves, but wolves know that where there's blood, there's often another predator. But when they smelled you, an outsider, they felt emboldened to attack. They can smell weakness.\n两者都有。血腥味引来了狼群，但狼知道，有血的地方往往还有别的掠食者。可它们闻出你是个外来者，便壮起胆子进攻了。它们嗅得出软弱。"

    old "Are you calling me weak?"
    new "Are you calling me weak?\n你是说我软弱？"

    old "That's not my opinion of you, but the wolves seemed to think so. I think you proved them wrong in combat, so the last laugh is yours."
    new "That's not my opinion of you, but the wolves seemed to think so. I think you proved them wrong in combat, so the last laugh is yours.\n那不是我对你的看法，但狼群似乎这么想。我想你在战斗中已证明它们错了，所以笑到最后的是你。"

    old "Now, then."
    new "Now, then.\n那么，现在。"

    old "His gaze narrows on my face and he gives me an appraising look."
    new "His gaze narrows on my face and he gives me an appraising look.\n他的目光在我脸上收紧，用打量人的眼神看着我。"

    old "I feel you owe me an introduction."
    new "I feel you owe me an introduction.\n我觉得你还欠我个自我介绍。"

    old "And what brings you to the great forest?"
    new "And what brings you to the great forest?\n是什么风把你吹到大森林来的？"

    old "I'm looking for a certain someone. An elf assassin named Kusho."
    new "I'm looking for a certain someone. An elf assassin named Kusho.\n我在找一个人。一个名叫 Kusho 的精灵刺客。"

    old "The elf chuckles."
    new "The elf chuckles.\n精灵轻笑起来。"

    old "Funny, that. Well, you've found him. What business do you have with me?"
    new "Funny, that. Well, you've found him. What business do you have with me?\n有意思。嗯，你找到他了。你找我有什么事？"

    old "I'm here on behalf of Grimoire's leadership."
    new "I'm here on behalf of Grimoire's leadership.\n我代表 Grimoire 的领导层而来。"

    old "And what interest does Grimoire's leadership have in an elf assassin like me?"
    new "And what interest does Grimoire's leadership have in an elf assassin like me?\nGrimoire 的领导层，对我这样一个精灵刺客有什么兴趣？"

    old "Surely you've heard of the recent events surrounding the Castle of N'mar."
    new "Surely you've heard of the recent events surrounding the Castle of N'mar.\nN'mar 城堡近来的事，你想必听说过。"

    old "Yes, I've been quite aware. A man of my occupation can't persist long without his ear to the ground. But you haven't answered my question, so I'll ask again: what does the leadership of Grimoire have with an elf assassin like me? To who do I owe this referral?"
    new "Yes, I've been quite aware. A man of my occupation can't persist long without his ear to the ground. But you haven't answered my question, so I'll ask again: what does the leadership of Grimoire have with an elf assassin like me? To who do I owe this referral?\n对，我很清楚。干我这行的，不眼观六路耳听八方，可撑不了多久。不过你还没回答我的问题，所以我再问一遍：Grimoire 的领导层，跟我这样的精灵刺客有什么相干？是谁把我引荐给你的？"

    old "Queen Karen of the Amazons suggested that you might prove a helpful ally."
    new "Queen Karen of the Amazons suggested that you might prove a helpful ally.\n是 Amazons 的 Karen 女王，说你说不定会是个得力的盟友。"

    old "A wry grin creeps across Kusho's face and he allows himself a slight chuckle."
    new "A wry grin creeps across Kusho's face and he allows himself a slight chuckle.\nKusho 脸上掠过一抹苦笑，又不禁轻声一笑。"

    old "Is that so? I suppose I should be delighted to hear her speak so highly of my talents. What exactly is the task at hand? Do you have a specific job in mind?"
    new "Is that so? I suppose I should be delighted to hear her speak so highly of my talents. What exactly is the task at hand? Do you have a specific job in mind?\n是吗？她如此抬举我的本事，我想我该感到荣幸。眼下到底是什么任务？你心里可有具体的活儿？"

    old "We're infiltrating the castle of N'Mar. I'm assembling a special forces unit of sorts."
    new "We're infiltrating the castle of N'Mar. I'm assembling a special forces unit of sorts.\n我们要潜入 N'Mar 城堡。我正在组建一支类似特种小队的力量。"

    old "So you'd have me working as part of a group? Well, solo work really is my preference. But infiltration sounds right up my alley. I imagine the castle of N'Mar is full of hiding locations. That architecture is ripe with nooks and crannies. And shadows. I do like shadows."
    new "So you'd have me working as part of a group? Well, solo work really is my preference. But infiltration sounds right up my alley. I imagine the castle of N'Mar is full of hiding locations. That architecture is ripe with nooks and crannies. And shadows. I do like shadows.\n所以你是要我加入一个团队行事？嗯，说实话我偏爱单干。不过潜入这活儿，正合我的胃口。我想 N'Mar 城堡里到处都有藏身之处。那建筑满是犄角旮旯。还有阴影。我确实喜欢阴影。"

    old "Does that mean I can expect your assistance?"
    new "Does that mean I can expect your assistance?\n这么说，我可以指望你的帮助了？"

    old "Well, the work intrigues me. And I'm sure that, as a representative of Grimoire who's gone to such great lengths to find me, you surely possess the means to make this job worth my time. Unfortunately, I'm not presently in a position to accept."
    new "Well, the work intrigues me. And I'm sure that, as a representative of Grimoire who's gone to such great lengths to find me, you surely possess the means to make this job worth my time. Unfortunately, I'm not presently in a position to accept.\n嗯，这活儿很让我心动。而且我相信，作为 Grimoire 的代表，你费了这么大劲来找我，想必也有本事让这趟差事值回我的时间。可惜，眼下我还无法应承。"

    old "You see, I'm preoccupied with another job. Were it not for that, I'd be entirely open to your proposition."
    new "You see, I'm preoccupied with another job. Were it not for that, I'd be entirely open to your proposition.\n你看，我正被另一桩差事缠身。若不是如此，我对你的提议完全敞开。"

    old "How soon would you be available?"
    new "How soon would you be available?\n你多久能空出来？"

    old "I can't say for certain at this point. I'll be available as soon as I finish my current job."
    new "I can't say for certain at this point. I'll be available as soon as I finish my current job.\n眼下我还说不准。等手头这桩活儿了结，我就能腾出空来。"

    old "Maybe I help to speed things along."
    new "Maybe I help to speed things along.\n也许我能帮你加快进度。"

    old "I doubt that very much. Although I'm not opposed to collaborating with others in certain situations, hunting is something I very much prefer to do alone. Here in the forest, I've no need for assistance."
    new "I doubt that very much. Although I'm not opposed to collaborating with others in certain situations, hunting is something I very much prefer to do alone. Here in the forest, I've no need for assistance.\n我对此深表怀疑。虽然我并非在任何情形下都拒绝与人合作，但狩猎这件事，我非常愿意独自进行。在这森林里，我不需要帮手。"

    old "The only way that you could help me with this hunt is if you delivered the bounty directly to me. If you could offer me that kind of assistance, I'd help you with your N'Mar problem free of charge."
    new "The only way that you could help me with this hunt is if you delivered the bounty directly to me. If you could offer me that kind of assistance, I'd help you with your N'Mar problem free of charge.\n你能在这桩狩猎上帮我的唯一方式，就是把猎物直接送到我手上。你若能提供那样的帮助，我便分文不取，帮你解决 N'Mar 的麻烦。"

    old "Is that a challenge?"
    new "Is that a challenge?\n这是在下战书？"

    old "I can't stop you from taking it as one, but I doubt that your search will prove a very fruitful endeavor. Trust me: I'm quite skilled at what I do. I'm familiar with the lay of these lands. And I've been out here for weeks without results to show for it."
    new "I can't stop you from taking it as one, but I doubt that your search will prove a very fruitful endeavor. Trust me: I'm quite skilled at what I do. I'm familiar with the lay of these lands. And I've been out here for weeks without results to show for it.\n你要当成战书，我也拦不住，但我怀疑你的搜寻怕是难有收获。相信我：干这行我相当在行，这片土地的地势我也熟悉。可我在这片林子里转了几个星期，也没见着什么成果。"

    old "I doubt very much that someone like you would succeed where I've failed. Here's my honest suggestion: find someone else to help you with your castle invasion."
    new "I doubt very much that someone like you would succeed where I've failed. Here's my honest suggestion: find someone else to help you with your castle invasion.\n我非常怀疑，在我失手的地方，你这样的人能成事。这是我的肺腑之言：另找别人去帮你攻打城堡吧。"

    old "I'm not looking for just anyone. Getting here to meet you was no small task. I came here because I wanted the best. I came here because I wanted you."
    new "I'm not looking for just anyone. Getting here to meet you was no small task. I came here because I wanted the best. I came here because I wanted you.\n我要找的不是随便什么人。能到这里见到你，已非易事。我来，是因为我要最好的。我来，是因为我要你。"

    old "Kusho chuckles."
    new "Kusho chuckles.\nKusho 轻笑起来。"

    old "I appreciate the flattery, and I'll be the last to disagree with you. I'm good, and I daresay I'm one of the best when it comes to assassinations."
    new "I appreciate the flattery, and I'll be the last to disagree with you. I'm good, and I daresay I'm one of the best when it comes to assassinations.\n承蒙夸奖，我也绝不会反驳你。我很出色，甚至敢说，论刺杀，我是最顶尖的那一档。"

    old "But you're looking for a much more general sort of talent. And you're a fool if you think that my talents are so unique that there aren't many other elves equally as qualified to help you with your little castle invasion. In fact, I'm hunting one of them right now."
    new "But you're looking for a much more general sort of talent. And you're a fool if you think that my talents are so unique that there aren't many other elves equally as qualified to help you with your little castle invasion. In fact, I'm hunting one of them right now.\n可你要找的，是种更宽泛的本事。而且，你若以为我的才能独一无二、再无别的精灵同样有资格帮你那小小的城堡之役，那你就傻了。事实上，我现在正在猎杀其中之一。"

    old "What's his name?"
    new "What's his name?\n他叫什么名字？"

    old "Kusho turns his back to me and begins walking deeper into the forest. He glances over his shoulder to yell back to me."
    new "Kusho turns his back to me and begins walking deeper into the forest. He glances over his shoulder to yell back to me.\nKusho 背过身去，开始朝森林深处走去。他回头瞥了一眼，冲我喊道。"

    old "Vaeril."
    new "Vaeril.\nVaeril。"

    old "Why are you hunting him?"
    new "Why are you hunting him?\n你为什么要猎杀他？"

    old "Kusho ignores my call and continues receding further into the forest. I rush forward and attempt to follow, but his legs expertly navigate through the dense brush at a pace I could never hope to match. Within moments, I've lost sight of him."
    new "Kusho ignores my call and continues receding further into the forest. I rush forward and attempt to follow, but his legs expertly navigate through the dense brush at a pace I could never hope to match. Within moments, I've lost sight of him.\nKusho 不理我的追问，继续向森林深处退去。我冲上前想跟上，可他的双腿在密林中穿行如飞，那速度我望尘莫及。片刻之间，我已看不见他的踪影。"

    old "Considering that I encountered Kusho through a combination of sheer dumb luck and a level of compassion that seems uncharacteristic for a man who considers the role of assassin his primary occupation, I suppose I feel I should feel lucky that I even met him."
    new "Considering that I encountered Kusho through a combination of sheer dumb luck and a level of compassion that seems uncharacteristic for a man who considers the role of assassin his primary occupation, I suppose I feel I should feel lucky that I even met him.\n想到我与 Kusho 相遇，靠的是十足的运气，再加上他那份对一名以刺客为本业的人来说颇为反常的恻隐之心，我想，能见上他一面，我已经算走运了。"

    old "Perhaps if I find this Vaeril that Kusho is hunting, I can win another audience with Kusho. But I doubt very much he'll give me the time of day otherwise. Still, is it even worth trying? I suppose I should ask around to find out."
    new "Perhaps if I find this Vaeril that Kusho is hunting, I can win another audience with Kusho. But I doubt very much he'll give me the time of day otherwise. Still, is it even worth trying? I suppose I should ask around to find out.\n也许，我若能找到 Kusho 正在猎杀的 Vaeril，就能再赢得一次与他面谈的机会。否则，我十分怀疑他连正眼都不会给我。不过，这到底值不值得一试？我想我该四处打听打听。"

    old "It's probably worth my while to make another venture out to Farshade. My first attempt earned me an unexpected audience with Kusho. Even if the first time was an accident, it might happen again, right?"
    new "It's probably worth my while to make another venture out to Farshade. My first attempt earned me an unexpected audience with Kusho. Even if the first time was an accident, it might happen again, right?\n再往 Farshade 跑一趟，大概是值得的。头一回出去，就意外地见到了 Kusho。即便那次是巧合，说不定还能再来一回，对吧？"

    old "And even if the first time was by accident, there's still sense in asking about Kusho in the remote elven settlements. Perhaps I'll get closer to finding Kusho, even if my journey isn't detailed this time."
    new "And even if the first time was by accident, there's still sense in asking about Kusho in the remote elven settlements. Perhaps I'll get closer to finding Kusho, even if my journey isn't detailed this time.\n而且，即便那次纯属偶然，去偏远的精灵聚落打听 Kusho，也自有其道理。也许这一趟我的行程虽不周详，却能离找到 Kusho 更近一步。"

    old "The road to Farshade is beginning to grow on me. As I follow the beaten path, the small twists and turns take on a certain familiarity. By midday, I've reached the site of my first meeting with Kusho, with the trees still splayed across the path as evidence of the woodcrasher's previous activity."
    new "The road to Farshade is beginning to grow on me. As I follow the beaten path, the small twists and turns take on a certain familiarity. By midday, I've reached the site of my first meeting with Kusho, with the trees still splayed across the path as evidence of the woodcrasher's previous activity.\n通往 Farshade 的路，我渐渐走出了感情。沿着这条被人踩踏的小径前行，那些小小的曲折拐弯也带上几分熟悉。到正午时分，我已抵达与 Kusho 初次相遇的地方，树木仍横在道上，印证着那 woodcrasher 先前的行径。"

    old "Rest in peace, young woodcrasher. I hope Kusho made a useful meal of you."
    new "Rest in peace, young woodcrasher. I hope Kusho made a useful meal of you.\n安息吧，年轻的 woodcrasher。但愿 Kusho 把你做成了顿像样的饭。"

    old "I climb over the trampled logs and continue along the path until I reach a second obstacle."
    new "I climb over the trampled logs and continue along the path until I reach a second obstacle.\n我翻过被踩踏的倒木，沿路继续前行，直到遇上第二处障碍。"

    old "To say the path is obstructed is the ultimate understatement. Trees are collapsed onto the pathway laterally, as far as I can see. Which, with the height of the trees obscuring my vision, admittedly isn't very far."
    new "To say the path is obstructed is the ultimate understatement. Trees are collapsed onto the pathway laterally, as far as I can see. Which, with the height of the trees obscuring my vision, admittedly isn't very far.\n说这路被堵了，简直是最大的轻描淡写。极目所见，树木横七竖八地倒在道上。而高耸的树木遮住视线，我也确实看不了多远。"

    old "This is probably the work of the same sort of beast. A woodcrasher, Kusho called it. The beast is aptly named. As far as I can see up the road, there doesn't appear to be a single part of the beaten path that isn't completely covered with splintered wood. A massive swath of this part of the forest has been completely demolished."
    new "This is probably the work of the same sort of beast. A woodcrasher, Kusho called it. The beast is aptly named. As far as I can see up the road, there doesn't appear to be a single part of the beaten path that isn't completely covered with splintered wood. A massive swath of this part of the forest has been completely demolished.\n这八成是同一种野兽干的。Kusho 叫它 woodcrasher。这名字起得恰如其分。沿路望过去，这条被踩踏的小径，似乎没有一处不被碎木完全覆盖。这片森林的很大一块，已被彻底夷平。"

    old "Perhaps it was a beast much larger than the one I saw Kusho killed. Or perhaps they run in packs. Either way, it doesn't look like I'm going to make much progress along this road, at least by conventional means."
    new "Perhaps it was a beast much larger than the one I saw Kusho killed. Or perhaps they run in packs. Either way, it doesn't look like I'm going to make much progress along this road, at least by conventional means.\n也许这是头比 Kusho 杀死的那只大得多的野兽。又或者，它们是成群出没。不管怎样，走这条路，我怕是难有进展，至少用寻常法子不行。"

    old "I think it's time for me to take Kusho's advice. The path is no way to travel, it's time for me to travel like a native."
    new "I think it's time for me to take Kusho's advice. The path is no way to travel, it's time for me to travel like a native.\n我想，是时候听 Kusho 的劝了。这条路没法走，我该像当地人那样赶路了。"

    old "I amble up the fallen trees blocking the path and ascend until I can see the lowest branches of the trees off the road which still stand erect."
    new "I amble up the fallen trees blocking the path and ascend until I can see the lowest branches of the trees off the road which still stand erect.\n我慢步攀上堵路的倒木，向上爬去，直到能看见路旁仍挺立着的树木最低处的枝桠。"

    old "The climbing is far easier than I anticipated. Numerous branches protrude from the trunk of the tree, and climbing up them is almost like ascending a spiraling ladder."
    new "The climbing is far easier than I anticipated. Numerous branches protrude from the trunk of the tree, and climbing up them is almost like ascending a spiraling ladder.\n攀爬比我想象的容易得多。树干上伸出许多枝桠，攀着它们向上，几乎像登一架盘旋的梯子。"

    old "Some of the smaller branches buckle under my weight, but after testing the weight of each branch with one foot, I quickly fall into a rhythm of shifting my weight between branches."
    new "Some of the smaller branches buckle under my weight, but after testing the weight of each branch with one foot, I quickly fall into a rhythm of shifting my weight between branches.\n有些较细的枝桠在我体重下弯折，但我先用一只脚试探每根枝桠的承重，很快便找到了在枝桠间转移重心的节奏。"

    old "As I climb further, the branches become thicker and sturdier, and strong enough that I can put my full weight on any one of them without the slightest bowing."
    new "As I climb further, the branches become thicker and sturdier, and strong enough that I can put my full weight on any one of them without the slightest bowing.\n越往上爬，枝桠越粗越结实，结实到我全身重量压上去，任何一根都纹丝不弯。"

    old "The higher I go, the more I come to realize how it is that the elves native to this region call these trees their homes. Although I am many feet above the floor of the forest, my position doesn't feel perilous in the slightest."
    new "The higher I go, the more I come to realize how it is that the elves native to this region call these trees their homes. Although I am many feet above the floor of the forest, my position doesn't feel perilous in the slightest.\n爬得越高，我越明白这片地区的精灵为何把这些树当作家园。虽然我已离地面许多英尺，所处位置却一点也不觉得危险。"

    old "As I get closer to the uppermost canopy of the forest, my journey upon the tree branches becomes less like climbing and more like walking. The interlocking branches of these trees are almost as much as the path as the route I was walking along the ground."
    new "As I get closer to the uppermost canopy of the forest, my journey upon the tree branches becomes less like climbing and more like walking. The interlocking branches of these trees are almost as much as the path as the route I was walking along the ground.\n离最顶层的林冠越近，我在枝桠上的行进就越不似攀爬，而更像行走。这些树枝交错相连，几乎和我在地面走的那条路一样畅通。"

    old "Well. The path below may be blocked, but it seems I've discovered a new path of sorts."
    new "Well. The path below may be blocked, but it seems I've discovered a new path of sorts.\n嗯。下面的路也许被堵了，但我似乎发现了一条别样的新路。"

    old "I begin walking along the branches that crest the forest canopy. Well, Kusho, I had my doubts, but it seems you were correct: walking atop the trees really is the best way to to travel."
    new "I begin walking along the branches that crest the forest canopy. Well, Kusho, I had my doubts, but it seems you were correct: walking atop the trees really is the best way to to travel.\n我开始沿着越过林冠的枝桠行走。嗯，Kusho，我原本将信将疑，看来你说得没错：在树梢上行走，当真是赶路的最佳方式。"

    old "I hear a bellowing roar in the distance and tense for a moment."
    new "I hear a bellowing roar in the distance and tense for a moment.\n我听见远处传来一声低沉的咆哮，不由紧绷了一瞬。"

    old "However, the tension quickly leaves my shoulders. The bellow came from below. Whatever beasts might roam about on the forest floor, I'm completely safe from them above."
    new "However, the tension quickly leaves my shoulders. The bellow came from below. Whatever beasts might roam about on the forest floor, I'm completely safe from them above.\n然而，紧绷感很快便从肩头散去。那咆哮来自下方。不管林地上游荡着怎样的野兽，我在高处都绝对安全。"

    old "The bellow grows louder and closer, but the roars are nearly drowned out by the sound of the leaves vibrating all around me."
    new "The bellow grows louder and closer, but the roars are nearly drowned out by the sound of the leaves vibrating all around me.\n咆哮声越来越响、越来越近，却几乎被我四周树叶震颤的声响淹没。"

    old "The sound of rattling leaves is replaced by a new sound: the sound of cracking wood."
    new "The sound of rattling leaves is replaced by a new sound: the sound of cracking wood.\n树叶簌簌作响的声音，被一种新的声响取代：木头断裂的声音。"

    old "The tree I'm standing on begins to topple, and for a moment I flail, hoping for something, anything to grab onto."
    new "The tree I'm standing on begins to topple, and for a moment I flail, hoping for something, anything to grab onto.\n我脚下的树开始倾倒，一时间我双臂乱挥，只盼能抓住点什么，什么都行。"

    old "I wrap my arms around the trunk of the nearest tree, and pray that when we hit the ground, it will be me on top of the tree trunk, and not the other way around."
    new "I wrap my arms around the trunk of the nearest tree, and pray that when we hit the ground, it will be me on top of the tree trunk, and not the other way around.\n我双臂抱住最近一棵树的树干，心里祈祷着：等落地时，但愿是我趴在树干上面，而不是被压在下面。"

    old "I close my eyes, and brace for the moment of impact."
    new "I close my eyes, and brace for the moment of impact.\n我闭上眼睛，绷紧身子，等着撞击的那一刻。"

    old "."
    new ".\n。"

    old "..."
    new "...\n……"

    old "How did I get here?"
    new "How did I get here?\n我是怎么到这儿来的？"

    old "I was up in the canopy. The trees fell...and so did I."
    new "I was up in the canopy. The trees fell...and so did I.\n我先前在林冠之上。树倒了……我也跟着掉了下来。"

    old "I look around. The woodcrasher who brought me to the forest floor seems to be long gone."
    new "I look around. The woodcrasher who brought me to the forest floor seems to be long gone.\n我环顾四周。把我撞落到林地上的那头 woodcrasher，似乎早已离去。"

    old "I survey the wreckage around me. I suppose I should feel lucky not to have been crushed by any of the falling trees."
    new "I survey the wreckage around me. I suppose I should feel lucky not to have been crushed by any of the falling trees.\n我打量四周的狼藉。我想，没被倒下的树木砸扁，我该感到庆幸。"

    old "I attempt to stand, and a searing pain shoots through my leg. I collapse onto the ground."
    new "I attempt to stand, and a searing pain shoots through my leg. I collapse onto the ground.\n我试着站起来，一阵灼痛猛地窜过腿部。我瘫倒在地。"

    old "With considerable effort, I force myself into sitting position and examine my legs. The right leg seems to be fully intact. My left leg...I wish I could say the same. Is it broken? Whatever the case, it clearly won't hold my weight."
    new "With considerable effort, I force myself into sitting position and examine my legs. The right leg seems to be fully intact. My left leg...I wish I could say the same. Is it broken? Whatever the case, it clearly won't hold my weight.\n我费了好大劲，硬撑着坐起身，检查双腿。右腿似乎完好无损。左腿……我倒希望能这么说。是断了吗？无论如何，它显然撑不住我的体重了。"

    old "Climb? Forget climbing. I can't even walk. I can't even stand."
    new "Climb? Forget climbing. I can't even walk. I can't even stand.\n爬？别提爬了。我连走都走不了，连站都站不起来。"

    old "Is this where I die? Alone, an incapable prisoner trapped in the elements and my own battered and broken body?"
    new "Is this where I die? Alone, an incapable prisoner trapped in the elements and my own battered and broken body?\n这里就是我丧命之地吗？孤身一人，一个被困于荒野、也被困于自己伤痕累累、支离破碎躯体的废人？"

    old "Hello!"
    new "Hello!\n有人吗！"

    old "I yell."
    new "I yell.\n我喊道。"

    old "Is anyone out here?"
    new "Is anyone out here?\n这附近有人吗？"

    old "Disconcertingly, I hear no echo. I suppose the underbrush of the forest absorbs sound too well for my message to carry very far."
    new "Disconcertingly, I hear no echo. I suppose the underbrush of the forest absorbs sound too well for my message to carry very far.\n令人不安的是，我没有听见任何回音。我想，是森林的灌木把声音吸收得太好，我的呼喊传不了多远。"

    old "Hello! Is anyone out there?"
    new "Hello! Is anyone out there?\n有人吗！外面有人吗？"

    old "I hear only the forest."
    new "I hear only the forest.\n我听到的只有森林的声响。"

    old "In Grimoire, I was warned that the forest was hostile to strangers. I assumed that this was a caution against the hostile natives, not the forest itself."
    new "In Grimoire, I was warned that the forest was hostile to strangers. I assumed that this was a caution against the hostile natives, not the forest itself.\n在 Grimoire 时，就有人告诫我，这片森林对外来者满怀敌意。我原以为那是警告我提防怀有敌意的当地人，而不是森林本身。"

    old "Oh, how I wish I might encounter one of those hostile woodfolk. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be much traffic this part of the forest. I've tread very far off the beaten path."
    new "Oh, how I wish I might encounter one of those hostile woodfolk. Unfortunately, there doesn't seem to be much traffic this part of the forest. I've tread very far off the beaten path.\n啊，我多希望能碰上那些敌意森森的林中人。可惜，森林这一带似乎没什么人迹。我早已远远偏离了常走的路。"

    old "In fact, if my goal was to be completely unfindable, I've found the perfect spot to hide from potential rescuers. The perfect spot to die and rot alone."
    new "In fact, if my goal was to be completely unfindable, I've found the perfect spot to hide from potential rescuers. The perfect spot to die and rot alone.\n事实上，若我的目标就是彻底让人找不到，那我算是找到了绝佳之处，能把潜在救援者都躲开。一个孤零零死去、腐烂的绝佳之地。"

    old "Are you happy? Is this what you wanted all along?"
    new "Are you happy? Is this what you wanted all along?\n你满意了吗？这就是你一直想要的？"

    old "The forest offers no response."
    new "The forest offers no response.\n森林默不作答。"

    old "I'm at your mercy now, great forest. Do your worst."
    new "I'm at your mercy now, great forest. Do your worst.\n伟大的森林，如今我任你摆布了。尽管放马过来吧。"

    old "I'd say she already has."
    new "I'd say she already has.\n我倒觉得，她已经出手了。"

    old "My neck twists in the direction of the voice. Surely I can't have imagined it."
    new "My neck twists in the direction of the voice. Surely I can't have imagined it.\n我猛地转头朝声音的方向望去。那声音绝不可能是我的幻觉。"

    old "Hello! I'm an emissary from Grimoire. Please, if you can help me, I'll find a way to compensate you."
    new "Hello! I'm an emissary from Grimoire. Please, if you can help me, I'll find a way to compensate you.\n你好！我是 Grimoire 派来的使者。求求你，你若能帮我，我定会设法报答。"

    old "A face pokes out through the bramble and splintered wood above me."
    new "A face pokes out through the bramble and splintered wood above me.\n一张脸从我上方的荆棘和碎木间探了出来。"

    old "Are you injured?"
    new "Are you injured?\n你受伤了吗？"

    old "My leg is looking pretty bad."
    new "My leg is looking pretty bad.\n我的腿伤得不轻。"

    old "Bad enough that you can't stand?"
    new "Bad enough that you can't stand?\n伤得站不起来了？"

    old "That's putting it gently."
    new "That's putting it gently.\n这还是说得轻了。"

    old "A figure emerges and kneels down beside me."
    new "A figure emerges and kneels down beside me.\n一个人影现身，在我身旁跪下。"

    old "You're in quite a bad way. Do you have any friends nearby?"
    new "You're in quite a bad way. Do you have any friends nearby?\n你的状况相当糟糕。附近有同伴吗？"

    old "This new figure may be friend or foe. If he is a foe, it certainly won't do me any good to let him know that I'm defenseless."
    new "This new figure may be friend or foe. If he is a foe, it certainly won't do me any good to let him know that I'm defenseless.\n这个新出现的人，是敌是友尚难断定。若他是敌人，让他知道我已毫无还手之力，绝没有好下场。"

    old "I am traveling with friends. We've only temporarily separated, and I suspect that they'll catch up without too much delay. But your assistance is appreciated in the meantime."
    new "I am traveling with friends. We've only temporarily separated, and I suspect that they'll catch up without too much delay. But your assistance is appreciated in the meantime.\n我是和朋友们一起赶路的。我们只是暂时走散，我想他们用不了多久就会赶上。不过，这段期间你的帮助，我感激不尽。"

    old "That claim seems doubtful to me."
    new "That claim seems doubtful to me.\n这话在我听来，颇为可疑。"

    old "What reason would I have to lie to you?"
    new "What reason would I have to lie to you?\n我有什么理由要骗你？"

    old "Well, if you were traveling alone, it would be quite a danger to admit it. Lone travelers make ripe targets, you know. I can appreciate your circumstances."
    new "Well, if you were traveling alone, it would be quite a danger to admit it. Lone travelers make ripe targets, you know. I can appreciate your circumstances.\n嗯，若你孤身赶路，承认这一点可是相当危险。独行客是最容易下手的目标，你知道的。你的处境，我能体谅。"

    old "But right now you have a problem, and I suspect things will go smoother here if we're both completely honest about the present circumstances. You're out here alone in need of help, and I'm ready to provide it. Am I wrong?"
    new "But right now you have a problem, and I suspect things will go smoother here if we're both completely honest about the present circumstances. You're out here alone in need of help, and I'm ready to provide it. Am I wrong?\n但眼下你遇到了麻烦，我想，若我们彼此都对现状完全坦诚，事情会顺利得多。你孤身在此，急需帮助，而我愿意出手。我说错了吗？"

    old "You're...not wrong."
    new "You're...not wrong.\n你……没说错。"

    old "Alright then. Lie still, try not to move, and pardon the dust and splinters."
    new "Alright then. Lie still, try not to move, and pardon the dust and splinters.\n那好。躺好别动，请多包涵那些尘土和木屑。"

    old "Unfortunately, I have not."
    new "Unfortunately, I have not.\n很遗憾，我没有。"

    old "That's a hell of a thing to admit, but I'll take you at your word. Lie still, try not to move, and forgive any sticks that may fall on you. Try to keep your head down, eh?"
    new "That's a hell of a thing to admit, but I'll take you at your word. Lie still, try not to move, and forgive any sticks that may fall on you. Try to keep your head down, eh?\n敢这么承认，可真有你的。不过我就信你这一回。躺好别动，若有什么树枝落到你身上，还请见谅。尽量把头低下，嗯？"

    old "If you're asking me to remain motionless, I think I can handle that without any trouble."
    new "If you're asking me to remain motionless, I think I can handle that without any trouble.\n你若要我一动不动，我想这我还是办得到的，不费事。"

    old "Motionless is good. If your hands are still good for anything, you might want to use them shielding that face of yours."
    new "Motionless is good. If your hands are still good for anything, you might want to use them shielding that face of yours.\n一动不动最好。你那双手若还派得上用场，不妨用来护住你的脸。"

    old "I raise my arms and draw them in front of my face to block any falling debris. Dust and splinters begin falling down onto me, and I reflexively close my eyes."
    new "I raise my arms and draw them in front of my face to block any falling debris. Dust and splinters begin falling down onto me, and I reflexively close my eyes.\n我举起双臂挡在脸前，以防有碎屑掉落。尘土和木屑开始落在我身上，我下意识闭上了眼睛。"

    old "I hear the creak of wooden branches bending above me. I hear the sound of wood cracking and flinch."
    new "I hear the creak of wooden branches bending above me. I hear the sound of wood cracking and flinch.\n我听见头顶木枝弯折的吱嘎声，又听见木头断裂的声响，不由一缩。"

    old "I'm [protag], by the way. Have you got a name of your own to share?"
    new "I'm [protag], by the way. Have you got a name of your own to share?\n对了，我叫 [protag]。你方便告诉我你的名字吗？"

    old "The elf ponders my question for a moment."
    new "The elf ponders my question for a moment.\n精灵沉吟片刻。"

    old "That's a difficult question to answer. It's been a very long time since I've had another person that I might have address me by name. I've been known by many names."
    new "That's a difficult question to answer. It's been a very long time since I've had another person that I might have address me by name. I've been known by many names.\n这个问题可不好答。已经很久很久，没有人会叫我的名字了。我有过许多名字。"

    old "Do you have a real name amongst those?"
    new "Do you have a real name amongst those?\n那些名字里，有没有一个真名？"

    old "I had a real name once, yes. But I suspect it's one of the many names I've long since forgotten."
    new "I had a real name once, yes. But I suspect it's one of the many names I've long since forgotten.\n我曾有过真名，是的。但我猜，它早已是我遗忘已久的众多名字之一了。"

    old "Well, what would you like me to call you?"
    new "Well, what would you like me to call you?\n那你想让我怎么称呼你？"

    old "You can call me the elf who lives in the glade. That's what I am, after all."
    new "You can call me the elf who lives in the glade. That's what I am, after all.\n你可以叫我「住在林间空地的精灵」。毕竟，我就是这么个人。"

    old "That's a bit of a mouthful. How about I just call you Glade?"
    new "That's a bit of a mouthful. How about I just call you Glade?\n这称呼可有点绕口。不如我就叫你 Glade 吧？"

    old "Glade. What an interesting name. It'll do, I suppose. It certainly fits. You can go ahead and call me Glade, but don't be surprised if it takes me a bit of time to get used to it."
    new "Glade. What an interesting name. It'll do, I suppose. It certainly fits. You can go ahead and call me Glade, but don't be surprised if it takes me a bit of time to get used to it.\nGlade。多有意思的名字。我想，倒也可以。确实很贴切。你就叫我 Glade 吧，只是若我一时半会儿还不太习惯，也莫要见怪。"

    old "You can open your eyes, by the way."
    new "You can open your eyes, by the way.\n对了，你可以睁开眼睛了。"

    old "I open my eyes and see the face of my benefactor towering over me."
    new "I open my eyes and see the face of my benefactor towering over me.\n我睁开眼，看见恩人的脸庞正俯视着我。"

    old "I'm going to assume that leg of yours is broken. This isn't the safest place to tary about, so immobilizing it isn't an option."
    new "I'm going to assume that leg of yours is broken. This isn't the safest place to tary about, so immobilizing it isn't an option.\n我就当你那条腿断了。这地方不宜久留，所以固定伤腿并不现实。"

    old "So what's the next course of action?"
    new "So what's the next course of action?\n那下一步该怎么办？"

    old "Wait."
    new "Wait.\n等着。"

    old "Glade picks out a sturdy-looking branch and pulls out a knife. He drives the knife down the center of the branch, cleaving it in half, and puts the two wooden halves on either side of my leg."
    new "Glade picks out a sturdy-looking branch and pulls out a knife. He drives the knife down the center of the branch, cleaving it in half, and puts the two wooden halves on either side of my leg.\nGlade 挑出一根看着结实的树枝，抽出一把刀。他把刀顺着树枝正中劈下，将其剖成两半，再把两片木头夹在我腿的两侧。"

    old "You have any rope on you?"
    new "You have any rope on you?\n你身上有绳子吗？"

    old "Unfortunately, I haven't got any rope on me. If you're looking to bind something, I think the fabric of my clothing may be the best thing available."
    new "Unfortunately, I haven't got any rope on me. If you're looking to bind something, I think the fabric of my clothing may be the best thing available.\n很遗憾，我身上没带绳子。你若想捆扎东西，我想我衣服的布料大概是眼下最好用的了。"

    old "That'll do."
    new "That'll do.\n那就够了。"

    old "I tear a strip of cloth from the bottom of my undershirt and hand it to Glade. He draws the strip around my leg, binding the wood to it."
    new "I tear a strip of cloth from the bottom of my undershirt and hand it to Glade. He draws the strip around my leg, binding the wood to it.\n我从内衣下摆撕下一根布条，递给 Glade。他把布条缠过我的腿，把木片捆在腿上。"

    old "There you go. Now we have a splint. Not my best work, but it'll do long enough."
    new "There you go. Now we have a splint. Not my best work, but it'll do long enough.\n好了。现在有副夹板了。不是我最好的手艺，但撑一阵子不成问题。"

    old "Long enough for what?"
    new "Long enough for what?\n撑一阵子做什么？"

    old "Long enough to get you out of the way of any roaming wild beasties. Your other leg's good enough to hold your weight, isn't it? Come on, let's go."
    new "Long enough to get you out of the way of any roaming wild beasties. Your other leg's good enough to hold your weight, isn't it? Come on, let's go.\n撑到把你带离那些游荡野兽的路径。你另一条腿还撑得住体重，对吧？来，走吧。"

    old "Glade lifts me from the ground and wraps his arm across his shoulders, supporting my weight."
    new "Glade lifts me from the ground and wraps his arm across his shoulders, supporting my weight.\nGlade 把我从地上扶起，把手臂搭在自己肩上，架住我的体重。"

    old "We've got three legs between the two of us, you see? Here's how we're going to do it: left leg and middle leg, that's me. Right leg, that's you. We're going to go left, middle, right, in that order. Ready?"
    new "We've got three legs between the two of us, you see? Here's how we're going to do it: left leg and middle leg, that's me. Right leg, that's you. We're going to go left, middle, right, in that order. Ready?\n咱们俩加起来，一共有三条腿，明白吗？咱们这么走：左腿和中腿，是我的；右腿，是你的。按左、中、右的顺序迈步。准备好了吗？"

    old "I brace myself against Glade's side, and we begin hobbling away from the mess of broken splinters."
    new "I brace myself against Glade's side, and we begin hobbling away from the mess of broken splinters.\n我靠着 Glade 的身侧稳住自己，我们开始踉踉跄跄地远离那堆破碎的木屑。"

    old "Eventually we arrive at a slope. Glade lifts me into a hammock hanging from two trees, and I sit up and allow my legs to dangle."
    new "Eventually we arrive at a slope. Glade lifts me into a hammock hanging from two trees, and I sit up and allow my legs to dangle.\n最终我们来到一处坡地。Glade 把我扶进一张悬在两棵树间的吊床，我坐起身，任双腿垂荡着。"

    old "What is this place?"
    new "What is this place?\n这是什么地方？"

    old "This is home. Or at least it has been, ever since the woodcrashers showed up."
    new "This is home. Or at least it has been, ever since the woodcrashers showed up.\n这是家。或者说，自从 woodcrasher 出现以来，这里一直是家。"

    old "You live on the side of a hill?"
    new "You live on the side of a hill?\n你住在山坡上？"

    old "Other way around, actually. It's a gully. A river used to run through here, ages ago. The waters have dried up, but its left its mark on the landscape."
    new "Other way around, actually. It's a gully. A river used to run through here, ages ago. The waters have dried up, but its left its mark on the landscape.\n其实正相反。这是条沟壑。很久以前，曾有河流从这里流过。如今水已干涸，却在这片地貌上留下了痕迹。"

    old "Why here?"
    new "Why here?\n为什么选这里？"

    old "I told you, I came here after the woodcrashers showed up. There's not much that can stop them when they get to charging. But a ravine like this, it'll bring them to a stop swifter than anything. And when they feel the ground sloping downward, they know well enough to stay away. A woodcrasher doesn't live long if he lets himself get caught in a ditch."
    new "I told you, I came here after the woodcrashers showed up. There's not much that can stop them when they get to charging. But a ravine like this, it'll bring them to a stop swifter than anything. And when they feel the ground sloping downward, they know well enough to stay away. A woodcrasher doesn't live long if he lets himself get caught in a ditch.\n我说过了，woodcrasher 出现之后，我才搬到这儿来。它们一旦冲锋起来，几乎没什么拦得住。但像这样的沟壑，能让它们比什么都快地停下来。它们一感到地面往下倾斜，就懂得远远避开。一只 woodcrasher 若让自己陷进沟里，可活不长久。"

    old "I see. Trees can't stop them. But the ground can."
    new "I see. Trees can't stop them. But the ground can.\n我明白了。树拦不住它们，但地面能。"

    old "Exactly. You spend enough time in these woods, you get to know the locations of these natural barriers."
    new "Exactly. You spend enough time in these woods, you get to know the locations of these natural barriers.\n正是。你在这林子里待得够久，自然就摸清了这些天然屏障的位置。"

    old "So, we're safe. Now what?"
    new "So, we're safe. Now what?\n这么说，我们安全了。接下来呢？"

    old "Glade's eyes narrow and he cocks his head to the side, scrutinizing my face."
    new "Glade's eyes narrow and he cocks his head to the side, scrutinizing my face.\nGlade 眯起眼睛，头歪向一侧，细细端详我的脸。"

    old "I think now would be a good time for you to answer a few questions. I've been doing more than my share of talking, and it seems to me that between the two of us, you have the most to explain."
    new "I think now would be a good time for you to answer a few questions. I've been doing more than my share of talking, and it seems to me that between the two of us, you have the most to explain.\n我想，现在你该回答几个问题了。我说的话已远超我该说的分量，而在我看来，咱们两人当中，最该解释的是你。"

    old "I place my hands in front of me, palms turned upward."
    new "I place my hands in front of me, palms turned upward.\n我把双手摊在面前，掌心朝上。"

    old "Ask away."
    new "Ask away.\n尽管问吧。"

    old "Who are you? Earlier you were blubbering something about being an emissary from Grimoire. What's all that about?"
    new "Who are you? Earlier you were blubbering something about being an emissary from Grimoire. What's all that about?\n你是谁？先前你含含糊糊说了些什么，说自己是 Grimoire 的使者。那都是怎么回事？"

    old "We're assembling a special forces team to infiltrate the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "We're assembling a special forces team to infiltrate the Castle of N'Mar.\n我们在组建一支特种小队，潜入 N'Mar 城堡。"

    old "N'Mar. Should that name mean anything to me?"
    new "N'Mar. Should that name mean anything to me?\nN'Mar。这名字我该认得吗？"

    old "N'Mar lies in the fields outlying Grimoire. Recently, the area has become shrouded in mist, and that mist has brought on all sorts of unpleasant phenomena."
    new "N'Mar lies in the fields outlying Grimoire. Recently, the area has become shrouded in mist, and that mist has brought on all sorts of unpleasant phenomena.\nN'Mar 坐落在 Grimoire 外围的原野上。近来，那一带被雾气笼罩，而雾气带来了种种不祥的异象。"

    old "And you think that this is a problem that can be solved within the castle itself?"
    new "And you think that this is a problem that can be solved within the castle itself?\n而你认为，这个问题能在城堡内部解决？"

    old "Some dark magic is in play here. I'm not looking to start a fight. In fact, I'd like to avoid one. But we do have questions, and I'm hoping to find answers. Preferably without them knowing."
    new "Some dark magic is in play here. I'm not looking to start a fight. In fact, I'd like to avoid one. But we do have questions, and I'm hoping to find answers. Preferably without them knowing.\n这里头有某种黑暗魔法作祟。我不想挑起争斗，事实上，我巴不得避开。但我们确实心有疑问，而我希望寻得答案。最好是在他们毫无察觉的情况下。"

    old "Glade strokes his chin."
    new "Glade strokes his chin.\nGlade 抚着下巴。"

    old "So, you're a spy."
    new "So, you're a spy.\n这么说，你是个探子。"

    old "I raise both of my hands in submission."
    new "I raise both of my hands in submission.\n我举起双手，以示顺从。"

    old "I assure you, I did not come to the Great Forest to spy on you or your people."
    new "I assure you, I did not come to the Great Forest to spy on you or your people.\n我向你保证，我来大森林，不是来监视你或你的族人的。"

    old "Glade laughs."
    new "Glade laughs.\nGlade 笑了。"

    old "I have no doubt of that. If you were here to spy on me, you'd be quite a bad one, to be disclosing your plans. In fact, I'm not sure you have any assurance that I won't run off and tell the people of N'Mar that you intend to pay them an unwanted visit."
    new "I have no doubt of that. If you were here to spy on me, you'd be quite a bad one, to be disclosing your plans. In fact, I'm not sure you have any assurance that I won't run off and tell the people of N'Mar that you intend to pay them an unwanted visit.\n这我倒毫不怀疑。你若来监视我，却把自己的计划全盘托出，那你这探子当得可真差劲。事实上，你也没什么把握能保证我不会跑掉，去告诉 N'Mar 的人，说你们打算不请自来。"

    old "Somehow, you don't strike me as the type of fellow who would be in cahoots with vampires."
    new "Somehow, you don't strike me as the type of fellow who would be in cahoots with vampires.\n不知怎的，你看着不像是会跟吸血鬼勾结的那号人。"

    old "You should be careful not to judge people on appearances. But you are right. I don't know any vampires personally, and if I did, I doubt very much that I would be on friendly terms with any of them. Though, I'm not the type to be on friendly terms with anyone."
    new "You should be careful not to judge people on appearances. But you are right. I don't know any vampires personally, and if I did, I doubt very much that I would be on friendly terms with any of them. Though, I'm not the type to be on friendly terms with anyone.\n你该当心，别以貌取人。不过你说得对。我不认识任何吸血鬼，即便认识，我也十分怀疑自己会与其中任何一个交好。虽然，我也本就不是会跟谁交好的人。"

    old "I look around at the clearing, devoid of any other people, elven or otherwise."
    new "I look around at the clearing, devoid of any other people, elven or otherwise.\n我环顾空地，四下再无他人，无论精灵还是别的什么。"

    old "You certainly do seem to be the type who keeps to himself. I never imagined your solitude was due to misanthropy."
    new "You certainly do seem to be the type who keeps to himself. I never imagined your solitude was due to misanthropy.\n你看着确实像独来独往的人。只是我没想到，你的离群索居竟是因为厌世。"

    old "You've just met me. It seems a bit premature to judge my character when we've had not more than an hour to share words."
    new "You've just met me. It seems a bit premature to judge my character when we've had not more than an hour to share words.\n你才刚认识我。我们交谈不过一个多小时，现在就评判我的品性，未免为时过早。"

    old "You took the time to save me, and that doesn't strike me as the behavior of a man with diminuitive character."
    new "You took the time to save me, and that doesn't strike me as the behavior of a man with diminuitive character.\n你肯花时间救我，这在我看来，不像是个品格卑下之人会做的事。"

    old "Some will have drinks with a man one day, and slay him the next. You can't judge the body of a man's character from a single act. You know nothing of the sins or virtues of my past."
    new "Some will have drinks with a man one day, and slay him the next. You can't judge the body of a man's character from a single act. You know nothing of the sins or virtues of my past.\n有些人今天还与人把酒言欢，第二天就把人杀了。你不能凭一桩举动就断定一个人的品性。我过去的罪孽与德行，你一无所知。"

    old "I think I'm a great deal more concerned with tomorrow than I am with yesterday. And my interest in tomorrow pales in comparison to my interest in today."
    new "I think I'm a great deal more concerned with tomorrow than I am with yesterday. And my interest in tomorrow pales in comparison to my interest in today.\n我想，比起昨天，我更关心明天。而我对明天的关切，又远不及我对今天的关切。"

    old "Well, there's not much left for you to do today. You're not walking out of this forest as you are. That leg will need some time to heal."
    new "Well, there's not much left for you to do today. You're not walking out of this forest as you are. That leg will need some time to heal.\n嗯，你今天也没剩什么可做的了。照你现在这样，是走不出这森林的。那条腿得花些时间养伤。"

    old "How much time are we talking?"
    new "How much time are we talking?\n要多久？"

    old "Four weeks at the very least. Six would be better."
    new "Four weeks at the very least. Six would be better.\n至少四周。六周更稳妥。"

    old "That's going to be a problem."
    new "That's going to be a problem.\n那可麻烦了。"

    old "Ah, yes. Your business in N'Mar. Your mission has a certain sense of urgency to it, yes?"
    new "Ah, yes. Your business in N'Mar. Your mission has a certain sense of urgency to it, yes?\n啊，对。你在 N'Mar 的事务。你的任务多少有些紧迫，是吧？"

    old "The mission is time-sensitive, yes. We're committed to strike on the next full moon. And besides that, I've much business to attend to between now and then."
    new "The mission is time-sensitive, yes. We're committed to strike on the next full moon. And besides that, I've much business to attend to between now and then.\n任务确实刻不容缓。我们定在下一个满月发起行动。况且，在那之前我还有许多事要办。"

    old "Well, that's a problem, isn't it? I must confess, I am sympathetic to your plight. I've no fondness for those who walk and talk in death. And if I am being truthful, I'm in no way eager to support your recovery for the next few weeks. So I've a proposal to make."
    new "Well, that's a problem, isn't it? I must confess, I am sympathetic to your plight. I've no fondness for those who walk and talk in death. And if I am being truthful, I'm in no way eager to support your recovery for the next few weeks. So I've a proposal to make.\n嗯，这确实是个难题，不是吗？我得承认，我对你的处境深表同情。我对那些死后仍行走言说的东西毫无好感。而且说实话，我也不怎么想接下来几周都照料你养伤。所以，我有个提议。"

    old "Let's hear it."
    new "Let's hear it.\n说来听听。"

    old "I'll do something about this recovery problem of yours, and in return, you'll leave this place and tell no one of my presence here. I was living quite well before you stumbled along, and I'd very much like to continue as I was after you leave."
    new "I'll do something about this recovery problem of yours, and in return, you'll leave this place and tell no one of my presence here. I was living quite well before you stumbled along, and I'd very much like to continue as I was after you leave.\n我来解决你的伤愈问题，作为回报，你得离开这里，且不得向任何人透露我在此地。在你闯进来之前，我日子过得很舒坦；你走后，我很想继续那么过。"

    old "I can abide by that request. Whatever secrets you may have will remain safe."
    new "I can abide by that request. Whatever secrets you may have will remain safe.\n这个要求我能照办。无论你有什么秘密，我都会守口如瓶。"

    old "You're agreeing to hide my secrets, even without knowing what they are?"
    new "You're agreeing to hide my secrets, even without knowing what they are?\n你连我的秘密是什么都不知道，就答应替我隐瞒？"

    old "Yes. Whatever secrets you have, I'll keep them."
    new "Yes. Whatever secrets you have, I'll keep them.\n是。你有什么秘密，我都替你守着。"

    old "Well, I'm about to share a secret with you right about now."
    new "Well, I'm about to share a secret with you right about now.\n嗯，我此刻正要与你分享一个秘密。"

    old "Glade places one hand on my broken leg, and another hand on the tree my hammock is hanging from."
    new "Glade places one hand on my broken leg, and another hand on the tree my hammock is hanging from.\nGlade 一手按在我断腿上，另一手按在我吊床所悬的树上。"

    old "You might want to close your eyes for this."
    new "You might want to close your eyes for this.\n这一下，你最好闭上眼睛。"

    old "Glade closes his eyes and his grip on both the tree and my leg tightens. I grit my teeth under the increased pressure."
    new "Glade closes his eyes and his grip on both the tree and my leg tightens. I grit my teeth under the increased pressure.\nGlade 闭上眼睛，握住树和我的腿的手都收紧了。加重的力道下，我咬紧了牙关。"

    old "The skin on Glade's hands begins trembling, and takes on an almost luminescent glow."
    new "The skin on Glade's hands begins trembling, and takes on an almost luminescent glow.\nGlade 手上的皮肤开始颤抖，泛起近乎发光的光晕。"

    old "The color begins to drain from the tree, and I hear the old wood creaking as pain shoots into my leg. Glade's fingers drive deeper and deeper into my leg, and the skin under his fingers begins to flush with color. My body begins trembling."
    new "The color begins to drain from the tree, and I hear the old wood creaking as pain shoots into my leg. Glade's fingers drive deeper and deeper into my leg, and the skin under his fingers begins to flush with color. My body begins trembling.\n树上的颜色开始流失，我听见老树吱嘎作响，同时一阵疼痛窜入我的腿。Glade 的手指越掐越深，他指下的皮肤开始泛起血色。我的身体开始颤抖。"

    old "I hear the sound of a branch snapping, and look back up at the tree. It's wood has taken on a dark shade of gray, and a branch falls to the ground not three places from where I sit."
    new "I hear the sound of a branch snapping, and look back up at the tree. It's wood has taken on a dark shade of gray, and a branch falls to the ground not three places from where I sit.\n我听见树枝折断的声音，抬头回望那棵树。它的木质已蒙上一层暗灰色，一根树枝坠落到地上，离我坐处不过三尺。"

    old "Glade loosens his grip on the tree and my leg, and looks me in the eye."
    new "Glade loosens his grip on the tree and my leg, and looks me in the eye.\nGlade 松开按在树上和我腿上的手，直视我的眼睛。"

    old "I shut my eyes."
    new "I shut my eyes.\n我闭上了眼睛。"

    old "Glade tightens his grip on my leg. I grit my teeth under the increased pressure."
    new "Glade tightens his grip on my leg. I grit my teeth under the increased pressure.\nGlade 收紧抓住我腿的手。加重的力道下，我咬紧了牙关。"

    old "I hear...something. Like a buzzing, pulsating noise, coming from the hand that's gripping my leg."
    new "I hear...something. Like a buzzing, pulsating noise, coming from the hand that's gripping my leg.\n我听见……某种声响。一种嗡嗡的、搏动般的声音，从那只紧抓我腿的手上传出。"

    old "I hear the old wood of the tree above us creaking as pain shoots into my leg. Glade's fingers drive deeper and deeper into my leg, and the skin under his fingers begins to tingle. The jitter spreads until finally my entire body is trembling."
    new "I hear the old wood of the tree above us creaking as pain shoots into my leg. Glade's fingers drive deeper and deeper into my leg, and the skin under his fingers begins to tingle. The jitter spreads until finally my entire body is trembling.\n我听见头顶老树吱嘎作响，同时一阵疼痛窜入我的腿。Glade 的手指越掐越深，他指下的皮肤开始发麻。那种震颤蔓延开来，直到最后我全身都颤抖起来。"

    old "I hear the sound of a branch snapping, followed by the thud of something hitting the ground in front of me. Lucky I wasn't underneath that branch when it fell."
    new "I hear the sound of a branch snapping, followed by the thud of something hitting the ground in front of me. Lucky I wasn't underneath that branch when it fell.\n我听见树枝折断的声音，接着是什么东西砸在面前地上的闷响。幸好树枝落下时，我不在它正下方。"

    old "Glade loosens his grip my leg."
    new "Glade loosens his grip my leg.\nGlade 松开了抓着我腿的手。"

    old "You can open your eyes now."
    new "You can open your eyes now.\n你现在可以睁开眼睛了。"

    old "How does your leg feel?"
    new "How does your leg feel?\n你的腿感觉如何？"

    old "I bend my leg at the knee and realize that the pain has vanished. I look down and find myself startled to see no trace of my injury."
    new "I bend my leg at the knee and realize that the pain has vanished. I look down and find myself startled to see no trace of my injury.\n我屈膝活动腿，发觉疼痛已消失。低头一看，我吃惊地发现，伤处竟没留下半点痕迹。"

    old "It's healed. Or, it appears to be."
    new "It's healed. Or, it appears to be.\n它痊愈了。或者说，看上去是痊愈了。"

    old "Try standing."
    new "Try standing.\n试着站站看。"

    old "I place both legs on the ground gingerly, and stand out of the hammock, shifting my weight between both legs. I take a few steps forward. No pain, no limp, no sign my leg was ever injured."
    new "I place both legs on the ground gingerly, and stand out of the hammock, shifting my weight between both legs. I take a few steps forward. No pain, no limp, no sign my leg was ever injured.\n我小心翼翼地把双腿放到地上，从吊床里站起，在两腿间交替承重。我向前走了几步。不疼，不瘸，毫无受伤过的痕迹。"

    old "Good as new."
    new "Good as new.\n完好如初。"

    old "Well, not quite. Still, it's good enough to walk on, and I'm sure that with a good night's sleep you'll be back up to your usual self."
    new "Well, not quite. Still, it's good enough to walk on, and I'm sure that with a good night's sleep you'll be back up to your usual self.\n嗯，也不尽然。不过走路是够用了，我敢说，再好好睡上一夜，你就能恢复如常。"

    old "I look up at the tree. The plant that was green and vibrant with life only moments now stands replaced by a pitiful withered snag."
    new "I look up at the tree. The plant that was green and vibrant with life only moments now stands replaced by a pitiful withered snag.\n我抬头望向那棵树。方才还翠绿蓬勃、生机盎然的那株树，此刻已变成一株可怜巴巴的枯萎残桩。"

    old "I lock eyes with Glade."
    new "I lock eyes with Glade.\n我与 Glade 四目相对。"

    old "What sorcery is this? What are you, Glade?"
    new "What sorcery is this? What are you, Glade?\n这是什么法术？Glade，你究竟是什么？"

    old "Glade casts a sorrowful eye at the lifeless snag."
    new "Glade casts a sorrowful eye at the lifeless snag.\nGlade 朝那株了无生机的残桩投去悲伤的目光。"

    old "I'm a druid. Or I was one, once. I'm not sure what you call someone who steals the life force from trees."
    new "I'm a druid. Or I was one, once. I'm not sure what you call someone who steals the life force from trees.\n我是德鲁伊。或者说，我曾经是。我也不知道，该把窃取树木生命力的人叫作什么。"

    old "I take a step toward Glade and place a hand on his shoulder."
    new "I take a step toward Glade and place a hand on his shoulder.\n我朝 Glade 走近一步，把手搭在他肩上。"

    old "I'm not sure if there's a name for what you are. But I do know that I can call you my rescuer. Whatever it is that you have, it's a gift. And I'm grateful that you've chosen to share this gift with me."
    new "I'm not sure if there's a name for what you are. But I do know that I can call you my rescuer. Whatever it is that you have, it's a gift. And I'm grateful that you've chosen to share this gift with me.\n我不确定你的这种身份有没有个叫法。但我知道，我可以称你为我的救命恩人。你身上无论拥有的是什么，那都是一份天赋。你愿与我分享这份天赋，我感激不尽。"

    old "I think it would be best for you to leave now. You did say you had urgent business, after all. I can show you the way out of the forest, but we need to start moving now if we're to make it out before nightfall."
    new "I think it would be best for you to leave now. You did say you had urgent business, after all. I can show you the way out of the forest, but we need to start moving now if we're to make it out before nightfall.\n我想，你现在最好离开。毕竟你说过有要事在身。我可以带你出森林，但要赶在天黑前出去，我们得立刻动身。"

    old "I stand at the edge of the great forest. I look through the dense foliage and can scarcely see more than a stone's throw ahead of me. Perhaps that density of greenery is a barrier, a warning of sorts."
    new "I stand at the edge of the great forest. I look through the dense foliage and can scarcely see more than a stone's throw ahead of me. Perhaps that density of greenery is a barrier, a warning of sorts.\n我站在大森林边缘。透过密实的枝叶望去，面前一箭之地外的东西都几乎看不清。也许，那浓密的绿意是一道屏障，一种警告。"

    old "Well, I disregarded the forest's warnings once before, and it punished me in perhaps the worst way imaginable. And yet I lived to tell about it, with a bit of help from Glade."
    new "Well, I disregarded the forest's warnings once before, and it punished me in perhaps the worst way imaginable. And yet I lived to tell about it, with a bit of help from Glade.\n嗯，我先前无视过森林的警告，而它用也许是最可怕的方式惩罚了我。然而，靠着 Glade 的一点帮助，我活下来讲述了这一切。"

    old "I shift my weight between my legs. Whatever lingered of my leg wound seems to have healed since my last visit to the forest. I suppose I should thank Glade. I'll be seeing him, anyway. I don't see any other way to carry on with my mission."
    new "I shift my weight between my legs. Whatever lingered of my leg wound seems to have healed since my last visit to the forest. I suppose I should thank Glade. I'll be seeing him, anyway. I don't see any other way to carry on with my mission.\n我在两腿间交替承重。自上回离开森林，我腿伤的余痛似乎都已痊愈。我想我该感谢 Glade。反正我会见到他。除了找他，我看不到继续使命的其他路。"

    old "If I'm to gain Kusho's help in fighting the menace of N'Mar, I'll need someone better trained than I at navigating these woods. Someone who knows the lay of the land, and better still if it's someone who can help me out of a jam if needed. Who else could I turn to but Glade?"
    new "If I'm to gain Kusho's help in fighting the menace of N'Mar, I'll need someone better trained than I at navigating these woods. Someone who knows the lay of the land, and better still if it's someone who can help me out of a jam if needed. Who else could I turn to but Glade?\n若要取得 Kusho 的帮助来对抗 N'Mar 的威胁，我还需要个比我更擅长在这林间穿行的人。一个熟悉地势的人，最好还能在必要时帮我脱困。除了 Glade，我还能去找谁呢？"

    old "Perhaps he'll think it tasteless to ask another favor of him so soon. Perhaps charity is an attribute he possesses in limited quantities. But I won't know until I find out."
    new "Perhaps he'll think it tasteless to ask another favor of him so soon. Perhaps charity is an attribute he possesses in limited quantities. But I won't know until I find out.\n也许他会觉得，这么快又向他开口求助，实在不识趣。也许他的善心本就有限。但不试一试，我终究不会知道。"

    old "I dive into forest, and begin heading back to Glade's spot by the river, where I saw him last."
    new "I dive into forest, and begin heading back to Glade's spot by the river, where I saw him last.\n我钻进森林，开始折回我上次见到 Glade 时他所在的河边。"

    old "Glade's nowhere to be seen. I shouldn't be surprised that he's out and about, and I'm perfectly content to wait. The gully should afford me protection from any roaming woodcrashers."
    new "Glade's nowhere to be seen. I shouldn't be surprised that he's out and about, and I'm perfectly content to wait. The gully should afford me protection from any roaming woodcrashers.\n四处不见 Glade 的身影。他出门走动，我倒也不该惊讶，我也很乐意等上一等。这道沟壑应当能护我周全，免受游荡 woodcrasher 的侵扰。"

    old "I locate the hammock that once held me in my broken state, and realize that one of the trees that it's tied to has been transformed into a snag. Sorry, tree. Your vim and vigor is now mine. If it's any comfort to the tree, I can at least be a good steward of the health I've been given."
    new "I locate the hammock that once held me in my broken state, and realize that one of the trees that it's tied to has been transformed into a snag. Sorry, tree. Your vim and vigor is now mine. If it's any comfort to the tree, I can at least be a good steward of the health I've been given.\n我找到那张曾托住伤残的我吊床，发现系着它的其中一棵树，已经变成了残桩。抱歉了，树。你的活力如今归了我。若这能让树好受些，那我至少会好好珍惜这份被赐予的健康。"

    old "The snag is dead wood, but I try the hammock and it's still stiff enough to hold my weight, so I snuggle in to catch a brief respite. My legs have been in a near constant state of exhaustion from walking, so I appreciate the moments when the daytime affords me the chance to rest them."
    new "The snag is dead wood, but I try the hammock and it's still stiff enough to hold my weight, so I snuggle in to catch a brief respite. My legs have been in a near constant state of exhaustion from walking, so I appreciate the moments when the daytime affords me the chance to rest them.\n那残桩是枯木，但我试了试吊床，它仍结实得能撑住我，我便钻进去小憩片刻。一路走来，我的双腿几乎一直疲惫不堪，所以白天能逮到机会让它们歇歇，我格外珍惜。"

    old "Hours pass before I first hear the noise of an elf tumbling through the brush. I let out a whoop."
    new "Hours pass before I first hear the noise of an elf tumbling through the brush. I let out a whoop.\n过了好几个小时，我才头一回听见有精灵穿过灌木的窸窣声。我欢呼了一声。"

    old "Ho, Glade!"
    new "Ho, Glade!\n嗨，Glade！"

    old "Glade stops in his tracks."
    new "Glade stops in his tracks.\nGlade 停下脚步。"

    old "What are you doing here?"
    new "What are you doing here?\n你在这儿做什么？"

    old "I owe you a debt of gratitude for your assistance in my moment of peril. But I'm hoping you can help me once more. I'm looking for someone."
    new "I owe you a debt of gratitude for your assistance in my moment of peril. But I'm hoping you can help me once more. I'm looking for someone.\n我危难之时蒙你相助，欠你一份恩情。但我希望你能再帮我一次。我在找一个人。"

    old "You shouldn't have come here."
    new "You shouldn't have come here.\n你不该来这里。"

    old "I'm sorry. I know that you want to be left alone. Rest assured, I haven't told anyone of your presence."
    new "I'm sorry. I know that you want to be left alone. Rest assured, I haven't told anyone of your presence.\n对不起。我知道你想独处。你放心，我没向任何人透露你的行踪。"

    old "You should go. Now."
    new "You should go. Now.\n你该走了。现在就走。"

    old "I'm sorry, Glade. I shouldn't have come. I'll be on my way."
    new "I'm sorry, Glade. I shouldn't have come. I'll be on my way.\n对不起，Glade。我不该来的。我这就走。"

    old "I turn around, and hear the sound of a low whistle coming from a patch of nearby brush."
    new "I turn around, and hear the sound of a low whistle coming from a patch of nearby brush.\n我转过身，忽听附近一丛灌木里传来一声低低的口哨。"

    old "Glade, I still have business in these woods. The sooner I complete that business, the sooner I'll be out of here."
    new "Glade, I still have business in these woods. The sooner I complete that business, the sooner I'll be out of here.\nGlade，我在这林子里还有事要办。办得越早，我离开得也越早。"

    old "You misunderstand me. Please—"
    new "You misunderstand me. Please—\n你误会我了。请你——"

    old "Glade goes silent, and looks over my shoulder at something behind me. I hear the sound of rustling in the brush."
    new "Glade goes silent, and looks over my shoulder at something behind me. I hear the sound of rustling in the brush.\nGlade 沉默下来，目光越过我的肩头，看向我身后的什么东西。我听见灌木里传来窸窣声。"

    old "It seems you were followed. And I'm assuming those aren't friends of yours."
    new "It seems you were followed. And I'm assuming those aren't friends of yours.\n看来你被跟踪了。而且我猜，那几位不是你的朋友。"

    old "Two dark elves steps out of the brush."
    new "Two dark elves steps out of the brush.\n两个黑暗精灵从灌木中走出。"

    old "They're certainly not friends of mine. Do you know them?"
    new "They're certainly not friends of mine. Do you know them?\n他们当然不是我的朋友。你认识他们？"

    old "Only that they're dark elves, and they don't seem like they're here to make friends."
    new "Only that they're dark elves, and they don't seem like they're here to make friends.\n我只知道他们是黑暗精灵，而且看着不像是来交朋友的。"

    old "I think we all know how this ends."
    new "I think we all know how this ends.\n我想，结局如何，咱们都心知肚明。"

    old "Wait a minute. What is it you want?"
    new "Wait a minute. What is it you want?\n等等。你们想要什么？"

    old "Two things: all of your possessions, and no witnesses. Sorry, this only ends one way."
    new "Two things: all of your possessions, and no witnesses. Sorry, this only ends one way.\n两样东西：你们所有的财物，还有不留活口。抱歉，这事只有一种了法。"

    old "This is not worth dying for."
    new "This is not worth dying for.\n这可不值得搭上性命。"

    old "Agreed. Let's go."
    new "Agreed. Let's go.\n同意。动手吧。"

    old "These woods are dangerous. They're home only to those living in exile."
    new "These woods are dangerous. They're home only to those living in exile.\n这片林子很危险。只有流亡者才以它为家。"

    old "Like you?"
    new "Like you?\n就像你？"

    old "I live in exile, much like those dark elves. I do my best to avoid them."
    new "I live in exile, much like those dark elves. I do my best to avoid them.\n我流亡在外，跟那些黑暗精灵没两样。我尽力躲着他们。"

    old "I kneel before Glade. It's an act of extreme humility, but that's what I think the circumstances and Glade's character demand."
    new "I kneel before Glade. It's an act of extreme humility, but that's what I think the circumstances and Glade's character demand.\n我跪在 Glade 面前。这是极其谦卑的举动，但我想，眼下的情势和 Glade 的性情，正需要我如此。"

    old "Please, accept my apologies, both for bringing danger to you, and for asking for your assistance once more."
    new "Please, accept my apologies, both for bringing danger to you, and for asking for your assistance once more.\n请接受我的歉意，既为我把危险带给了你，也为我再次开口求你相助。"

    old "I swear, once I leave these woods, your existence here will remain a secret. But I need to call upon your help once more. Just some information would suffice, if you could spare it."
    new "I swear, once I leave these woods, your existence here will remain a secret. But I need to call upon your help once more. Just some information would suffice, if you could spare it.\n我发誓，一旦我离开这片林子，你在此地的存在将永远是秘密。但我需要再求你帮一次忙。若你肯透露，只给我一些消息便足矣。"

    old "I told you that I was looking for someone. An elf assassin by the name of Kusho. I know that he resides in these woods. But I have no idea where to begin looking for him."
    new "I told you that I was looking for someone. An elf assassin by the name of Kusho. I know that he resides in these woods. But I have no idea where to begin looking for him.\n我告诉过你，我在找一个人。一个名叫 Kusho 的精灵刺客。我知道他栖身于这片林子里，却不知该从何找起。"

    old "Kusho. The name is familiar. I presume you've looked for him in urban areas, yes?"
    new "Kusho. The name is familiar. I presume you've looked for him in urban areas, yes?\nKusho。这名字我耳熟。我猜你在城镇一带找过他，对吧？"

    old "Yes, I've asked around. Word on the street places him alone in these woods."
    new "Yes, I've asked around. Word on the street places him alone in these woods.\n是的，我四处打听过。街头传言说他独自待在这片林子里。"

    old "Do you have any information about what business he might have in these woods? It would be odd for him to disappear for something so trivial as the pursuit of the hunt of a wild beast, or solitude merely for solitude's sake."
    new "Do you have any information about what business he might have in these woods? It would be odd for him to disappear for something so trivial as the pursuit of the hunt of a wild beast, or solitude merely for solitude's sake.\n你可知道他在这林子里有何贵干？若只是为了追猎一只野兽这般琐事，或只为独处而独处，就这般销声匿迹，那也未免太奇怪了。"

    old "As a matter of fact, I do know. He has a mark."
    new "As a matter of fact, I do know. He has a mark.\n事实上，我确实知道。他有个目标。"

    old "No surprise there. I don't suppose you have the name of his mark."
    new "No surprise there. I don't suppose you have the name of his mark.\n这倒不意外。我想，你大概不知道他目标的名字吧。"

    old "As a matter of fact, I have."
    new "As a matter of fact, I have.\n事实上，我知道。"

    old "Glade arches an eyebrow."
    new "Glade arches an eyebrow.\nGlade 挑了挑眉。"

    old "What kind of assassin is he, that he'd allow that kind of information to float around to reach the likes of you?"
    new "What kind of assassin is he, that he'd allow that kind of information to float around to reach the likes of you?\n他算是哪门子刺客，竟让这种消息传得满天飞，都飘到你这种人耳朵里了？"

    old "He told me directly. We met in person. I...wasn't able to follow him, which is why I'm here now."
    new "He told me directly. We met in person. I...wasn't able to follow him, which is why I'm here now.\n是他亲口告诉我的。我们当面见过。我……没能跟住他，所以现在才会在这里。"

    old "Well, you wanted my help. Out with it. Who's this assassin hunting?"
    new "Well, you wanted my help. Out with it. Who's this assassin hunting?\n嗯，你想要我帮忙。快说吧。这个刺客在追杀谁？"

    old "A man named Vaeril."
    new "A man named Vaeril.\n一个叫 Vaeril 的人。"

    old "Glade's voice is barely a whisper."
    new "Glade's voice is barely a whisper.\nGlade 的声音轻得近乎耳语。"

    old "That's one name I was hoping the world would forget."
    new "That's one name I was hoping the world would forget.\n那是我巴望这世界能忘掉的名字。"

    old "Do you know him?"
    new "Do you know him?\n你认识他？"

    old "He's standing right in front of you."
    new "He's standing right in front of you.\n他正站在你面前。"

    old "I glance around."
    new "I glance around.\n我环顾四周。"

    old "Where?"
    new "Where?\n在哪儿？"

    old "It's me. I'm the one your elf assassin friend is hunting."
    new "It's me. I'm the one your elf assassin friend is hunting.\n就是我。你那精灵刺客朋友要猎杀的人，就是我。"

    old "I lock eyes with the elf standing in front of me, and time stands still for a moment. What is that look in his eyes? He has the eyes of a sad man, one with more regrets than I'm sure he'd care to share. But I have to know."
    new "I lock eyes with the elf standing in front of me, and time stands still for a moment. What is that look in his eyes? He has the eyes of a sad man, one with more regrets than I'm sure he'd care to share. But I have to know.\n我与面前这个精灵四目相对，时间仿佛凝固了一瞬。他眼中是怎样的神情？那是一个悲伤之人的眼睛，其中藏着比我确信他愿意吐露的还要多的悔恨。但我必须知道。"

    old "Why would he be hunting you?"
    new "Why would he be hunting you?\n他为什么要猎杀你？"

    old "Glade—Vaeril—shakes his head."
    new "Glade—Vaeril—shakes his head.\nGlade——Vaeril——摇了摇头。"

    old "You've known me for so very little time. And yet, in that very short span of time, you've seen what kind of elf I am. What kind of druid—if I can even be called that anymore—what kind of man I am."
    new "You've known me for so very little time. And yet, in that very short span of time, you've seen what kind of elf I am. What kind of druid—if I can even be called that anymore—what kind of man I am.\n你认识我的时间这么短。可就在这短短片刻里，你已经看清了我是什么样的精灵，什么样的德鲁伊——如果我还配得上这个称呼的话——什么样的人。"

    old "Druids are descended from Mother Nature herself. We are brothers and sisters of the forest. Our job is to protect the life of the forest, not steal it. And yet, look at me."
    new "Druids are descended from Mother Nature herself. We are brothers and sisters of the forest. Our job is to protect the life of the forest, not steal it. And yet, look at me.\n德鲁伊是 Mother Nature 本人的后裔。我们是森林的兄弟姐妹。我们的职责是守护森林的生命，而非窃取它。可你看看我。"

    old "Vaeril clenches his hands into fists and looks down at the ground."
    new "Vaeril clenches his hands into fists and looks down at the ground.\nVaeril 双手攥成拳头，低头望向地面。"

    old "I'm an aberration."
    new "I'm an aberration.\n我是个异类。"

    old "I'm an abomination."
    new "I'm an abomination.\n我是个可憎的怪物。"

    old "What the hell am I doing here?"
    new "What the hell am I doing here?\n我到底在这儿做什么？"

    old "I don't belong here."
    new "I don't belong here.\n我不属于这里。"

    old "Vaeril buries his face in his hands and sinks to his knees."
    new "Vaeril buries his face in his hands and sinks to his knees.\nVaeril 把脸埋进双手，双膝一软跪了下去。"

    old "They all know that I don't belong here."
    new "They all know that I don't belong here.\n他们都知道我不属于这里。"

    old "I can't blame the elves for banishing me from their territory. And I certainly can't blame this Kusho fellow for doing what I'm sure he knows is right."
    new "I can't blame the elves for banishing me from their territory. And I certainly can't blame this Kusho fellow for doing what I'm sure he knows is right.\n我不能怪精灵们把我逐出领地。我也绝不能怪 Kusho 那家伙，去做我相信他深知正确的事。"

    old "Perhaps there's another way. Perhaps I can parley with Kusho. You're living in exile. You're in isolation. You've been undiscovered for so long. Why should the elves care about your continued existence?"
    new "Perhaps there's another way. Perhaps I can parley with Kusho. You're living in exile. You're in isolation. You've been undiscovered for so long. Why should the elves care about your continued existence?\n也许还有别的办法。也许我能去跟 Kusho 谈谈。你流亡在外，与世隔绝，这么久都没人发现你。精灵们为何还要在意你是否继续存在？"

    old "Those are questions I don't have the answers to."
    new "Those are questions I don't have the answers to.\n这些问题的答案，我没有。"

    old "You came here to find a man named Vaeril. Now, you've found him. What do you intend to do about it?"
    new "You came here to find a man named Vaeril. Now, you've found him. What do you intend to do about it?\n你到这儿来，是为了找一个叫 Vaeril 的人。如今你找到他了。你打算怎么办？"

    old "I'm going to make this work, Vaeril. I'm not sure exactly how I'll do it, but I will. Can you trust me?"
    new "I'm going to make this work, Vaeril. I'm not sure exactly how I'll do it, but I will. Can you trust me?\n我会把这件事办成的，Vaeril。具体怎么办，我还不确定，但我一定会。你能信我吗？"

    old "Vaeril stands up and looks me in the eye."
    new "Vaeril stands up and looks me in the eye.\nVaeril 站起身，直视我的眼睛。"

    old "You trusted me with your life. It seems only fitting that I now trust you with mine."
    new "You trusted me with your life. It seems only fitting that I now trust you with mine.\n你曾把性命托付给我。如今，我把我的性命托付给你，似乎也理所应当。"

    old "Hello there, [protag]."
    new "Hello there, [protag].\n你好啊，[protag]。"

    old "Kusho. I didn't expect to see any of you. You struck me as exceptionally busy the last time we met."
    new "Kusho. I didn't expect to see any of you. You struck me as exceptionally busy the last time we met.\nKusho。我没想到会见到你们中的任何一个。上次见面时，你给我的印象可是忙得不可开交。"

    old "I am a busy man. But I'm pursuing a specific goal, and it behooves me to explore every possible avenue for advancing toward that goal."
    new "I am a busy man. But I'm pursuing a specific goal, and it behooves me to explore every possible avenue for advancing toward that goal.\n我是很忙。但我在追寻一个明确的目标，为向目标迈进，我理应探索每一条可能的路径。"

    old "I'm concerned with matters of this forest. That, you already know. But I've noticed that you've been spending more and more time here as of late. I was wondering why that might be."
    new "I'm concerned with matters of this forest. That, you already know. But I've noticed that you've been spending more and more time here as of late. I was wondering why that might be.\n我操心的是这片森林的事。这你已经知道了。但我注意到，你近来在这片林子里待的时间越来越长。我正纳闷这是为何。"

    old "How is it that you know that I've been spending my time in the forest?"
    new "How is it that you know that I've been spending my time in the forest?\n你怎么会知道我一直待在森林里？"

    old "My, my. Aren't you testy. The simple answer is that, being one who is unaccustomed to these woods, you are not someone who moves about with subtlety. I have eyes and ears in the forest that report back to me when they see odd things, and you are quite the oddity."
    new "My, my. Aren't you testy. The simple answer is that, being one who is unaccustomed to these woods, you are not someone who moves about with subtlety. I have eyes and ears in the forest that report back to me when they see odd things, and you are quite the oddity.\n哎哟哟，火气还不小。答案很简单：你不习惯这片林子，走动起来也谈不上悄无声息。我在森林里遍布耳目，一见怪事便会报给我，而你，实在是个十足的怪人。"

    old "I'll ask again, even though I think I already know the answer. What have you been up to in these woods?"
    new "I'll ask again, even though I think I already know the answer. What have you been up to in these woods?\n我再问一遍，尽管我想我已知晓答案。你在这林子里究竟在忙些什么？"

    old "I was looking for your mark. I figured that if your business in this forest was wrapped up, you might be more inclined to join me in exploring the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "I was looking for your mark. I figured that if your business in this forest was wrapped up, you might be more inclined to join me in exploring the Castle of N'Mar.\n我在找你的目标。我想，你若了结了在这森林里的事，或许会更愿意随我一道探索 N'Mar 城堡。"

    old "I was looking for Vaeril."
    new "I was looking for Vaeril.\n我在找 Vaeril。"

    old "Fair enough. I suppose you now have a stake in the action, don't you? I seem to have inadvertently made my struggle your struggle as well."
    new "Fair enough. I suppose you now have a stake in the action, don't you? I seem to have inadvertently made my struggle your struggle as well.\n倒也合理。我想，如今你也在这事里有了利害关系，不是吗？看来我不经意间，把我的缠斗也变成了你的缠斗。"

    old "Since I've devoted a considerable amount of time to searching for this fellow, I think I ought to know what exactly he's wanted for."
    new "Since I've devoted a considerable amount of time to searching for this fellow, I think I ought to know what exactly he's wanted for.\n既然我花了这么多时间搜寻这个人，我想我该知道，他究竟因何被追捕。"

    old "I never did tell you that, did I? I suppose I should inform you of the particulars."
    new "I never did tell you that, did I? I suppose I should inform you of the particulars.\n我确实没告诉过你，是吧？我想，我该把详情跟你说说。"

    old "Do you remember when we first met? You were getting a bit too close to a slumbering woodcrasher, and I made short work of it."
    new "Do you remember when we first met? You were getting a bit too close to a slumbering woodcrasher, and I made short work of it.\n还记得我们初次见面吗？你凑得离一头沉睡的 woodcrasher 太近，而我三两下就把它解决了。"

    old "Yes, I remember it well."
    new "Yes, I remember it well.\n记得，我记得很清楚。"

    old "This probably doesn't come as any surprise to you, but those woodcrashers aren't native to this forest. They're invasive."
    new "This probably doesn't come as any surprise to you, but those woodcrashers aren't native to this forest. They're invasive.\n这大概不会让你意外，不过那些 woodcrasher 并非这片森林的原生物种。它们是入侵者。"

    old "To say they've been causing problems would be putting it far too lightly. The forest is a living entity, in many ways no different from you and I. And every day it's being torn apart by those rampaging beasts."
    new "To say they've been causing problems would be putting it far too lightly. The forest is a living entity, in many ways no different from you and I. And every day it's being torn apart by those rampaging beasts.\n说它们制造了麻烦，实在是太过轻描淡写。森林是个活生生的存在，在许多方面与你我并无不同。而它每天都在被那些横冲直撞的野兽撕扯。"

    old "Trees, hundreds of feet tall and centuries old, are being flattened like nothing by those beasts. And when those trees fall, the creatures that called them home have nowhere to turn to."
    new "Trees, hundreds of feet tall and centuries old, are being flattened like nothing by those beasts. And when those trees fall, the creatures that called them home have nowhere to turn to.\n数百英尺高、历经数百年岁月的巨树，被那些野兽像碾草一般夷平。而树一倒，以树为家的生灵便无处容身。"

    old "The deer, the birds, even the elves who live here share a symbiotic relationship with this forest. The damage to a tree can have a ripple effect which affects all life in this forest."
    new "The deer, the birds, even the elves who live here share a symbiotic relationship with this forest. The damage to a tree can have a ripple effect which affects all life in this forest.\n鹿、鸟，甚至住在这里的精灵，都与这片森林共生共存。对一棵树的伤害，会激起涟漪般的连锁反应，波及这片森林里的所有生命。"

    old "A forest that was once lush and vibrant with life is now being filled with dead and rotting wood. Those woodcrashers are killing the forest, one tree at a time."
    new "A forest that was once lush and vibrant with life is now being filled with dead and rotting wood. Those woodcrashers are killing the forest, one tree at a time.\n曾经繁茂蓬勃、生机盎然的森林，如今却处处是枯死腐烂的木头。那些 woodcrasher 正一棵树接一棵树地杀死这片森林。"

    old "Every day that passes with those woodcrashers rampaging about, this forest grows closer to death. The forest, and everyone and everything living here, their lives are in the balance. The woodcrasher plague must be ended."
    new "Every day that passes with those woodcrashers rampaging about, this forest grows closer to death. The forest, and everyone and everything living here, their lives are in the balance. The woodcrasher plague must be ended.\nwoodcrasher 每多肆虐一天，这片森林就离死亡更近一步。森林，以及住在这里的每一个生灵，它们的性命都悬于一线。这 woodcrasher 之祸，必须了结。"

    old "How does this relate to Vaeril?"
    new "How does this relate to Vaeril?\n这和 Vaeril 有什么关系？"

    old "Vaeril was once a druid. Druids, if you don't know, are those blessed with the ability to commune with nature itself. A druid's connection with the forest is so intimate that they can feel the pain of the forest in their own body. As you might imagine, there's a lot of pain to be felt right now."
    new "Vaeril was once a druid. Druids, if you don't know, are those blessed with the ability to commune with nature itself. A druid's connection with the forest is so intimate that they can feel the pain of the forest in their own body. As you might imagine, there's a lot of pain to be felt right now.\nVaeril 曾是一名德鲁伊。你或许不知道，德鲁伊是蒙受天赐、能与自然本身沟通的人。德鲁伊与森林的联系如此亲密，以至于他们能亲身感受到森林的痛苦。正如你能想见，眼下能感受到的痛苦，实在太多。"

    old "But Vaeril...Vaeril is different. Whatever relationship he has with nature has become a horrible perversion of druid magic. Rather than sharing energy with the forest, Vaeril saps it. He can take the life force from a tree and make it his own."
    new "But Vaeril...Vaeril is different. Whatever relationship he has with nature has become a horrible perversion of druid magic. Rather than sharing energy with the forest, Vaeril saps it. He can take the life force from a tree and make it his own.\n但 Vaeril……Vaeril 不同。他与自然的种种联系，已异化为对德鲁伊魔法的可怕扭曲。Vaeril 非但不与森林分享能量，反而汲取它。他能夺走一棵树的生命力，据为己有。"

    old "Years ago, Vaeril was banished from his native village. He's been living alone, somewhere, some place in this forest ever since. And in that time, I suspect he's had the time to practice and develop whatever sinister magic he's practicing."
    new "Years ago, Vaeril was banished from his native village. He's been living alone, somewhere, some place in this forest ever since. And in that time, I suspect he's had the time to practice and develop whatever sinister magic he's practicing.\n多年前，Vaeril 被逐出了故乡的村落。自那以后，他一直独居在这片森林的某个角落。而在这期间，我怀疑他有的是时间，去修炼并精进他所施展的那种邪恶魔法。"

    old "You believe that Vaeril is conjuring the woodcrashers?"
    new "You believe that Vaeril is conjuring the woodcrashers?\n你相信那些 woodcrasher 是 Vaeril 召来的？"

    old "I don't know the mechanism by which the woodcrashers entered the forest. What I do know is that stopping Vaeril is the first step to ending the woodcrasher menace."
    new "I don't know the mechanism by which the woodcrashers entered the forest. What I do know is that stopping Vaeril is the first step to ending the woodcrasher menace.\nwoodcrasher 是如何进入森林的，我并不知道。我只知道，制住 Vaeril，是终结这场 woodcrasher 之祸的第一步。"

    old "Does Vaeril have to die?"
    new "Does Vaeril have to die?\nVaeril 非得死吗？"

    old "I don't think that imprisoning him will help the problem. Who knows what foul magic he might capable of using from imprisonment? Vaeril can't be allowed to live in this forest any longer, even in captivity."
    new "I don't think that imprisoning him will help the problem. Who knows what foul magic he might capable of using from imprisonment? Vaeril can't be allowed to live in this forest any longer, even in captivity.\n我不认为监禁他就能解决问题。谁知道他被囚禁着还能施展什么邪恶魔法？绝不能再让 Vaeril 留在这片森林里生活，哪怕是囚禁在此也不行。"

    old "What if Vaeril was imprisoned elsewhere? I'm sure that Grimoire could spare you those resources."
    new "What if Vaeril was imprisoned elsewhere? I'm sure that Grimoire could spare you those resources.\n若把 Vaeril 囚禁在别处呢？我相信 Grimoire 能拨给你这些资源。"

    old "Kusho strokes his chin thoughtfully."
    new "Kusho strokes his chin thoughtfully.\nKusho 若有所思地抚着下巴。"

    old "I suppose that would solve the issue of proximity. I doubt very much that Vaeril could affect the forest from as far away as Grimoire. And keeping him alive in captivity may get us closer to a solution. Who knows what secrets his lips will let loose?"
    new "I suppose that would solve the issue of proximity. I doubt very much that Vaeril could affect the forest from as far away as Grimoire. And keeping him alive in captivity may get us closer to a solution. Who knows what secrets his lips will let loose?\n我想，那倒能解决距离的问题。我十分怀疑，Vaeril 远在 Grimoire 还能影响这片森林。而且留他一条命、囚禁起来，或许能让我们更接近解决之道。谁知道他那张嘴会吐出什么秘密？"

    old "What do you suppose would happen if Vaeril left the forest of his own volition and was left a free man?"
    new "What do you suppose would happen if Vaeril left the forest of his own volition and was left a free man?\n假如 Vaeril 自愿离开森林，做个自由人，你觉得会怎样？"

    old "Completely unacceptable. I need complete assurance that he will never be able to return to this forest again, and I'm not one to take those guilty of crimes against nature at their word. He needs to be killed, or he needs to be imprisoned away from the forest."
    new "Completely unacceptable. I need complete assurance that he will never be able to return to this forest again, and I'm not one to take those guilty of crimes against nature at their word. He needs to be killed, or he needs to be imprisoned away from the forest.\n绝不可接受。我需要十足的保证，确保他再也不能回到这片森林。而我这个人，可不会听信那些犯下危害自然之罪的人的一面之词。他要么被杀，要么被囚禁在远离森林之处。"

    old "Why do you ask? Have you learned anything about Vaeril's whereabouts?"
    new "Why do you ask? Have you learned anything about Vaeril's whereabouts?\n你为何这么问？你可打探到了 Vaeril 的下落？"

    old "Better to keep my mouth shut unless I'm ready to turn Vaeril over to Kusho."
    new "Better to keep my mouth shut unless I'm ready to turn Vaeril over to Kusho.\n在我准备好把 Vaeril 交给 Kusho 之前，还是闭嘴为好。"

    old "Kusho, I think I can deliver Vaeril to you."
    new "Kusho, I think I can deliver Vaeril to you.\nKusho，我想我能把 Vaeril 交到你手上。"

    old "Well, I'll believe it when I see it."
    new "Well, I'll believe it when I see it.\n嗯，眼见为实，我且看着。"

    old "I think you misunderstand. I found him once, and I know where I can find him again."
    new "I think you misunderstand. I found him once, and I know where I can find him again.\n我想你误会了。我找到过他一次，也知道去哪儿能再找到他。"

    old "Well, if that's true, then well done."
    new "Well, if that's true, then well done.\n嗯，若真如此，那干得漂亮。"

    old "We're not going to kill him. We can capture him and escort him to Grimoire."
    new "We're not going to kill him. We can capture him and escort him to Grimoire.\n我们不会杀他。我们可以抓住他，押送他去 Grimoire。"

    old "My top priority is that Vaeril not escape. But yes, I can avoid lethal measures. I wouldn't be a very good assassin if my arrows were only good for killing."
    new "My top priority is that Vaeril not escape. But yes, I can avoid lethal measures. I wouldn't be a very good assassin if my arrows were only good for killing.\n我的头等要务，是别让 Vaeril 逃掉。不过，我确实可以避免痛下杀手。若我的箭只配杀人，那我也算不得什么好刺客了。"

    old "You stay behind me, or above, out of sight. I think that I can arrest him without a struggle, if you give me the chance to talk to him."
    new "You stay behind me, or above, out of sight. I think that I can arrest him without a struggle, if you give me the chance to talk to him.\n你留在我身后，或躲在上方，别让人看见。我想，只要给我机会跟他谈谈，就能不费刀兵把他拿下。"

    old "I'll remain out of your way. But if it looks like things are about to turn sour, I won't hesitate to apprehend him by force."
    new "I'll remain out of your way. But if it looks like things are about to turn sour, I won't hesitate to apprehend him by force.\n我不会碍你的事。但若情势眼看要变糟，我会毫不犹豫地动武拿下他。"

    old "I don't think it will come to that."
    new "I don't think it will come to that.\n我想，不至于走到那一步。"

    old "I lead Kusho back to the clearing by the gully. Kusho remains concealed in the foliage behind me."
    new "I lead Kusho back to the clearing by the gully. Kusho remains concealed in the foliage behind me.\n我领着 Kusho 回到沟壑旁的空地。Kusho 仍藏在我身后的枝叶间。"

    old "I let out a whoop, and hear a rustling of leaves above me. Vaeril emerges from the branches of a tree."
    new "I let out a whoop, and hear a rustling of leaves above me. Vaeril emerges from the branches of a tree.\n我吹了声口哨，听见头顶枝叶窸窣作响。Vaeril 从一棵树的枝桠间现出身来。"

    old "Vaeril, are you ready to leave this forest? Can you come to Grimoire with me?"
    new "Vaeril, are you ready to leave this forest? Can you come to Grimoire with me?\nVaeril，你准备好离开这片森林了吗？能随我去 Grimoire 吗？"

    old "I can."
    new "I can.\n我可以。"

    old "Are you ready for whatever fate awaits you there?"
    new "Are you ready for whatever fate awaits you there?\n你准备好面对在那里等候你的命运了吗？"

    old "I can keep you alive, but you need to cooperate. Can you do that for me?"
    new "I can keep you alive, but you need to cooperate. Can you do that for me?\n我能保你性命，但你需要配合。这你能为我做到吗？"

    old "Vaeril looks behind me and nods."
    new "Vaeril looks behind me and nods.\nVaeril 朝我身后看去，点了点头。"

    old "Hello, Kusho."
    new "Hello, Kusho.\n你好，Kusho。"

    old "Kusho emerges from the brush behind me, with his bow drawn."
    new "Kusho emerges from the brush behind me, with his bow drawn.\nKusho 从我身后的灌木中现身，弓已拉满。"

    old "Watch yourself, druid."
    new "Watch yourself, druid.\n当心了，德鲁伊。"

    old "Am I to understand that I'm being taken prisoner?"
    new "Am I to understand that I'm being taken prisoner?\n我该理解为，我是要被俘了吗？"

    old "That's correct. You can choose the life of a captive in Grimoire, or choose no life at all."
    new "That's correct. You can choose the life of a captive in Grimoire, or choose no life at all.\n没错。你可以选择在 Grimoire 当一名俘虏苟活，也可以选择干脆什么都不留。"

    old "I lean in and whisper in Vaeril's ear."
    new "I lean in and whisper in Vaeril's ear.\n我凑过去，在 Vaeril 耳边低语。"

    old "I may be able to set you free one day, but for now, I need your cooperation."
    new "I may be able to set you free one day, but for now, I need your cooperation.\n也许有一天我能放你自由，但现在，我需要你配合。"

    old "Very well. The life of a captive in Grimoire can't be much worse than the life of exile I'm trapped in now."
    new "Very well. The life of a captive in Grimoire can't be much worse than the life of exile I'm trapped in now.\n很好。在 Grimoire 当俘虏，总不会比我如今被困其中的流亡生活更糟。"

    old "Bind him."
    new "Bind him.\n把他绑起来。"

    old "I'm sorry that I have to do this."
    new "I'm sorry that I have to do this.\n抱歉，我不得不这么做。"

    old "Vaeril shrugs."
    new "Vaeril shrugs.\nVaeril 耸了耸肩。"

    old "It's what's necessary. And more than that, it's your duty. Your first loyalty should be to Grimoire, not me. No need to apologize."
    new "It's what's necessary. And more than that, it's your duty. Your first loyalty should be to Grimoire, not me. No need to apologize.\n这是必要的。而且不仅如此，这也是你的职责。你首先要效忠的是 Grimoire，而不是我。不必道歉。"

    old "I pull out a piece of rope, and tie Vaeril's hands together."
    new "I pull out a piece of rope, and tie Vaeril's hands together.\n我抽出一段绳子，把 Vaeril 的双手绑在一起。"

    old "With a second piece of rope, I bind Vaeril's legs together, loose enough that he can still walk, but tight enough that he can't run."
    new "With a second piece of rope, I bind Vaeril's legs together, loose enough that he can still walk, but tight enough that he can't run.\n我又用第二段绳子把 Vaeril 的双腿绑住，松得让他还能走，却紧得让他跑不了。"

    old "Kusho lowers his bow, and we begin the long march back to Grimoire."
    new "Kusho lowers his bow, and we begin the long march back to Grimoire.\nKusho 放下手中的弓，我们开始了返回 Grimoire 的漫长跋涉。"

    old "We're here to check in a prisoner."
    new "We're here to check in a prisoner.\n我们是来登记一名囚犯的。"

    old "Who's the arresting officer?"
    new "Who's the arresting officer?\n逮捕官是谁？"

    old "He's to be held here on the authority of the council of Grimoire, whom I represent."
    new "He's to be held here on the authority of the council of Grimoire, whom I represent.\n他将以 Grimoire 议会之名义被关押于此，而我正是议会的代表。"

    old "The council, hmm? In that case, I don't need to know anything further. But just to sate my curiosity, what's he being held here for?"
    new "The council, hmm? In that case, I don't need to know anything further. But just to sate my curiosity, what's he being held here for?\n议会，嗯？这样的话，我也不必再多问了。不过为了满足我的好奇心，他是因为什么被关在这里的？"

    old "Crimes against nature."
    new "Crimes against nature.\n危害自然之罪。"

    old "Crimes against nature? Like cutting down trees?"
    new "Crimes against nature? Like cutting down trees?\n危害自然？比如砍树吗？"

    old "He's a practitioner of sinister magics."
    new "He's a practitioner of sinister magics.\n他修习邪门的魔法。"

    old "Magic, you say? Is that going to be a problem in here? Wouldn't want any magical jailbreaks happening on my watch."
    new "Magic, you say? Is that going to be a problem in here? Wouldn't want any magical jailbreaks happening on my watch.\n魔法，你说？在这牢里会出问题吗？我可不想在当班时发生什么魔法越狱。"

    old "I look at the walls of the jail."
    new "I look at the walls of the jail.\n我打量着监狱的墙壁。"

    old "Do you have any trees in this jail?"
    new "Do you have any trees in this jail?\n这监狱里有树吗？"

    old "Not since last I checked."
    new "Not since last I checked.\n据我上次查看，没有。"

    old "Then I don't think he's going to be a problem."
    new "Then I don't think he's going to be a problem.\n那我想他不会惹出什么麻烦。"

    old "How long will this man be here?"
    new "How long will this man be here?\n这个人要在这里关多久？"

    old "Until I say otherwise."
    new "Until I say otherwise.\n直到我改口为止。"

    old "I pull the warden aside."
    new "I pull the warden aside.\n我把典狱长拉到一旁。"

    old "Can you do me a favor?"
    new "Can you do me a favor?\n你能帮我个忙吗？"

    old "What do you need?"
    new "What do you need?\n你需要什么？"

    old "Make sure he's not treated too harshly. His crimes are against elves, not humans."
    new "Make sure he's not treated too harshly. His crimes are against elves, not humans.\n务必别对他太苛刻。他犯的罪是针对精灵，不是针对人类。"

    old "If he doesn't give me trouble, then I don't see any reason for me to give him trouble. He won't be mistreated unless he does something to warrant it. And if he's as docile as he looks, I think we're going to get along just fine."
    new "If he doesn't give me trouble, then I don't see any reason for me to give him trouble. He won't be mistreated unless he does something to warrant it. And if he's as docile as he looks, I think we're going to get along just fine.\n只要他不给我惹麻烦，我也没理由找他麻烦。除非他做出什么该受罚的事，否则不会受到虐待。而他若真像看上去那么温顺，我想我们会相处得很好。"

    old "I exit the jail and find Kusho waiting for me outside."
    new "I exit the jail and find Kusho waiting for me outside.\n我走出监狱，看到 Kusho 正在外面等我。"

    old "Well, you've helped me solve my problem, so it seems only fair that I should help you with yours."
    new "Well, you've helped me solve my problem, so it seems only fair that I should help you with yours.\n你帮我解决了难题，那么按理说，我也该帮你解决你的麻烦。"

    old "I'm headed back to the forest. I'm none too fond of cities, and whenever I spend too much time in one, I get the impression that the feeling is mutual."
    new "I'm headed back to the forest. I'm none too fond of cities, and whenever I spend too much time in one, I get the impression that the feeling is mutual.\n我要回森林去了。我对城市向来没什么好感，而且每当我在城里待得太久，我总觉得城市对我也是这种感觉。"

    old "But when the time comes that you need me to go fight ghouls or vampires or whatever foulness might be lurking around N'Mar, let me know and I'll be there to assist you."
    new "But when the time comes that you need me to go fight ghouls or vampires or whatever foulness might be lurking around N'Mar, let me know and I'll be there to assist you.\n但等哪天你需要我去对付食尸鬼、吸血鬼，或是在 N'Mar 一带潜伏的任何秽物时，告诉我一声，我一定到场助你。"

    old "Well, I'll let you know if I do discover anything about Vaeril's whereabouts. But I doubt I'll have much luck finding him. You've been searching longer than I have, and you know these woods better than me. If you ever succeed in finding him, I hope you'll come to Grimoire and find me."
    new "Well, I'll let you know if I do discover anything about Vaeril's whereabouts. But I doubt I'll have much luck finding him. You've been searching longer than I have, and you know these woods better than me. If you ever succeed in finding him, I hope you'll come to Grimoire and find me.\n好，我若真查到 Vaeril 的下落，会告诉你。不过我想我多半找不到他。你找得比我久，对这些林子也比我熟。要是你最终找到了他，希望你能来 Grimoire 找我。"

    old "Of course. I'll join you once I've found and subdued the man. Until then, I'll be searching these woods, slaying woodcrashers where I find them, and searching for Vaeril."
    new "Of course. I'll join you once I've found and subdued the man. Until then, I'll be searching these woods, slaying woodcrashers where I find them, and searching for Vaeril.\n当然。等我找到并制服那个人，就去与你汇合。在那之前，我会搜遍这些林子，见一只毁木兽就杀一只，同时继续搜寻 Vaeril。"

    old "Now, if you'll excuse me, I have some business in Farshade to attend to. Apparently someone discovered a nest of woodcrashers near there."
    new "Now, if you'll excuse me, I have some business in Farshade to attend to. Apparently someone discovered a nest of woodcrashers near there.\n好了，恕我失陪，我在 Farshade 还有些事要办。听说有人在那一带发现了一窝毁木兽。"

    old "Kusho leaps into the air, grabbing the lowest-hanging branch of the tree, and swings out of sight. I hear the faint rustle of leaves above, growing more and more distant, until Kusho has left me far behind."
    new "Kusho leaps into the air, grabbing the lowest-hanging branch of the tree, and swings out of sight. I hear the faint rustle of leaves above, growing more and more distant, until Kusho has left me far behind.\nKusho 纵身跃起，抓住树上最低垂的树枝，一荡便消失在视线之外。我听见上方树叶窸窣轻响，越来越远，直到 Kusho 把我远远甩在身后。"

    old "If Kusho is attending to business in Farshade, now would be the ideal for me to escape this forest with Vaeril."
    new "If Kusho is attending to business in Farshade, now would be the ideal for me to escape this forest with Vaeril.\n既然 Kusho 去了 Farshade 办事，眼下正是我带着 Vaeril 逃出这片森林的最好时机。"

    old "I run back to the clearing near the gully where I met Vaeril before, and let out a whoop. I hear a rustling of leaves above me, and Vaeril emerges from the branches of a tree."
    new "I run back to the clearing near the gully where I met Vaeril before, and let out a whoop. I hear a rustling of leaves above me, and Vaeril emerges from the branches of a tree.\n我跑回先前遇见 Vaeril 的那条沟壑旁的空地，喊了一声。我听见头顶树叶沙沙作响，Vaeril 从一棵树的枝桠间现出身来。"

    old "Vaeril, let's leave this forest. Come to Grimoire with me. Aid me in my mission."
    new "Vaeril, let's leave this forest. Come to Grimoire with me. Aid me in my mission.\nVaeril，我们离开这片森林吧。跟我去 Grimoire，助我完成使命。"

    old "As you wish."
    new "As you wish.\n悉听尊便。"

    old "Vaeril looks over his shoulder with a forlorn glance before falling into step behind me."
    new "Vaeril looks over his shoulder with a forlorn glance before falling into step behind me.\nVaeril 恋恋不舍地回头望了一眼，随后跟在我身后迈开脚步。"

    old "So, this is Grimoire."
    new "So, this is Grimoire.\n那么，这就是 Grimoire 了。"

    old "There's an inn at the end of this street that can serve as your short-term lodging."
    new "There's an inn at the end of this street that can serve as your short-term lodging.\n这条街尽头有家旅店，可以作为你的临时住处。"

    old "So this is my home now?"
    new "So this is my home now?\n那这里现在就是我的家了？"

    old "This is where you live. But you don't have to call it home if you don't want to."
    new "This is where you live. But you don't have to call it home if you don't want to.\n这是你住的地方。但如果你不愿意，也不必称它为家。"

    old "Maybe I will call it home some day."
    new "Maybe I will call it home some day.\n也许有一天我会称它为家。"

    old "I'm sorry. I don't want to be a burden. I believe I can take care of myself well enough, so please don't worry too much on my behalf. And if you ever require assistance in your exploration of N'Mar, please don't hesitate to call upon me."
    new "I'm sorry. I don't want to be a burden. I believe I can take care of myself well enough, so please don't worry too much on my behalf. And if you ever require assistance in your exploration of N'Mar, please don't hesitate to call upon me.\n抱歉，我不想成为累赘。我相信自己能照顾好自己，所以请不必太为我担心。日后你探索 N'Mar 若需要帮忙，请尽管来找我。"

    old "After all, I did save you once. I'd hate for that to be for naught."
    new "After all, I did save you once. I'd hate for that to be for naught.\n毕竟，我救过你一次。我可不想那一次白白浪费。"

    old "I'll be certain to take you up on that offer in the future."
    new "I'll be certain to take you up on that offer in the future.\n将来我一定不会跟你客气。"

    old "Fare thee well, [protag]."
    new "Fare thee well, [protag].\n保重，[protag]。"

    old "Following my meeting with Apolimesho, I decided to leave Grimoire and head south, just in case Grimoire turned out to be on the frontier of an attack from the undead."
    new "Following my meeting with Apolimesho, I decided to leave Grimoire and head south, just in case Grimoire turned out to be on the frontier of an attack from the undead.\n与 Apolimesho 会面之后，我决定离开 Grimoire 南下，以防万一 Grimoire 恰好处于不死大军来袭的前线。"

    old "With Grimoire at my back, I headed to Triberg, one of the biggest towns in southern Issanis. It seemed a good place, a safe place to wait out any impending war with the undead. I picked a dwelling near the docks, just in case disaster struck and I needed to take a ship further away from the continent."
    new "With Grimoire at my back, I headed to Triberg, one of the biggest towns in southern Issanis. It seemed a good place, a safe place to wait out any impending war with the undead. I picked a dwelling near the docks, just in case disaster struck and I needed to take a ship further away from the continent.\n我背向 Grimoire，前往 Triberg，那是 Issanis 南部最大的城镇之一。那里似乎是个好去处，是个可以安然等待与不死族之间那场迫在眉睫的战争过去的安全之地。我在码头附近挑了一处住所，以防万一灾祸降临，需要乘船远离这片大陆。"

    old "Weeks passed without news from N'Mar, and slowly I settled into a daily routine. On occasion, my mind turned to Apolimesho's offer, and I briefly wondered what kind of life I might have led if I'd accepted his proposal, but I never thought to ever return to Grimoire. My life in Triberg was peaceful and pleasant, if a little boring."
    new "Weeks passed without news from N'Mar, and slowly I settled into a daily routine. On occasion, my mind turned to Apolimesho's offer, and I briefly wondered what kind of life I might have led if I'd accepted his proposal, but I never thought to ever return to Grimoire. My life in Triberg was peaceful and pleasant, if a little boring.\n几周过去，N'Mar 毫无音讯，我也慢慢安于日常的节奏。偶尔，我会想起 Apolimesho 的提议，不禁猜想当初若接受了他的请求，如今会过着怎样的生活；但我从未想过要回 Grimoire。我在 Triberg 的日子平静而惬意，只是稍显无聊。"

    old "By the end of my third month in Triberg, I had almost entirely forgotten about my meeting with Apolimesho, when I received news from N'Mar: Apolimesho had managed to assemble a team of skilled adventurers, who had undertaken the task of investigating N'Mar. They had apparently sustained heavy losses, though the problem seemed to be solved, by all accounts."
    new "By the end of my third month in Triberg, I had almost entirely forgotten about my meeting with Apolimesho, when I received news from N'Mar: Apolimesho had managed to assemble a team of skilled adventurers, who had undertaken the task of investigating N'Mar. They had apparently sustained heavy losses, though the problem seemed to be solved, by all accounts.\n到我待在 Triberg 的第三个月末，我几乎已把与 Apolimesho 的那次会面忘得一干二净，这时却收到了来自 N'Mar 的消息：Apolimesho 成功召集了一支技艺精湛的冒险者队伍，前去调查 N'Mar。据各方的说法，他们显然伤亡惨重，不过问题似乎已经解决。"

    old "I didn't get more details beyond that. Grimoire's leadership seemed very interested in keeping the whole ordeal private, due to the depressingly high number of casualties, but names began to leak out and rumors began to spread as people began telling tales of the adventures who had survived N'Mar, as well as those who had sacrificed their lives."
    new "I didn't get more details beyond that. Grimoire's leadership seemed very interested in keeping the whole ordeal private, due to the depressingly high number of casualties, but names began to leak out and rumors began to spread as people began telling tales of the adventures who had survived N'Mar, as well as those who had sacrificed their lives.\n除此之外，我再没有更多细节。由于伤亡数字高得令人沮丧，Grimoire 的当权者似乎极想把整件事压下去；但名字还是渐渐走漏，流言也随之四起——人们开始传颂那些从 N'Mar 生还的冒险者，以及那些献出生命的人的故事。"

    old "Most of the adventurers' names were unrecognizable to me, apart from Raven, who had a reputation as a witch hunter. But knowing how tales spread, perhaps those adventurers would soon be famous."
    new "Most of the adventurers' names were unrecognizable to me, apart from Raven, who had a reputation as a witch hunter. But knowing how tales spread, perhaps those adventurers would soon be famous.\n那些冒险者的名字我大多不认得，只有 Raven 例外，他以猎巫人闻名。不过既然故事传得那么快，或许那些冒险者很快就要声名鹊起了。"

    old "From time to time, I still question whether I made the right choice. On one hand, I missed what could have been the opportunity of a lifetime. I could have been one of those adventurers. But if I had joined them, would I have been one of the adventurers who survived? Or one of the casualties?"
    new "From time to time, I still question whether I made the right choice. On one hand, I missed what could have been the opportunity of a lifetime. I could have been one of those adventurers. But if I had joined them, would I have been one of the adventurers who survived? Or one of the casualties?\n我不时还会怀疑自己当初的选择是否正确。一方面，我错过的可能是一生难逢的机遇。我本可以成为那些冒险者中的一员。可若我真的加入了他们，我会是幸存下来的那一个，还是遇难的那一个？"

    old "I may not have chosen to take the path of grand adventure. But at least I'm alive."
    new "I may not have chosen to take the path of grand adventure. But at least I'm alive.\n我也许没有选择那条波澜壮阔的冒险之路，但至少我还活着。"

    old "I find Apolimesho waiting for me in Grimoire's main square. As I approach, I spot Karen standing beside him. Before she even opens her mouth, I know what she's about to say."
    new "I find Apolimesho waiting for me in Grimoire's main square. As I approach, I spot Karen standing beside him. Before she even opens her mouth, I know what she's about to say.\n我发现 Apolimesho 正在 Grimoire 的主广场上等我。走近时，我看到 Karen 站在他身旁。还没等她开口，我就知道她要说什么了。"

    old "You failed."
    new "You failed.\n你失败了。"

    old "The deadline has arrived. Do you have what you need to begin your next mission in N'Mar?"
    new "The deadline has arrived. Do you have what you need to begin your next mission in N'Mar?\n期限已到。你准备好开始在 N'Mar 下一项任务所需的一切了吗？"

    old "Well, I..."
    new "Well, I...\n这个，我……"

    old "You don't have enough men to undertake this mission. We wasted precious time."
    new "You don't have enough men to undertake this mission. We wasted precious time.\n你没有足够的人手来执行这项任务。我们白白浪费了宝贵的时间。"

    old "Unless you have some outstanding progress that you've been hiding from us, I'm afraid that Karen is right. The Council is very disappointed in you, and has reluctantly decided to ally with the Amazons. From now on, Karen will lead this operation."
    new "Unless you have some outstanding progress that you've been hiding from us, I'm afraid that Karen is right. The Council is very disappointed in you, and has reluctantly decided to ally with the Amazons. From now on, Karen will lead this operation.\n除非你还有什么瞒着我们的惊人进展，否则恐怕 Karen 说得没错。议会对你很失望，并已不情愿地决定与 Amazons 结盟。从现在起，这项行动将由 Karen 领导。"

    old "I..."
    new "I...\n我……"

    old "I open my mouth to protest, but no words come out. I know they're right. I didn't do my part of the deal."
    new "I open my mouth to protest, but no words come out. I know they're right. I didn't do my part of the deal.\n我张了张嘴想争辩，却一句话也说不出来。我知道他们说得对。我没有履行交易中自己那一份责任。"

    old "I understand. I'm sorry. I am sure Karen will solve the problem for you and the Council."
    new "I understand. I'm sorry. I am sure Karen will solve the problem for you and the Council.\n我明白了。我很抱歉。我相信 Karen 会为你和议会解决这个难题。"

    old "You can be sure of that."
    new "You can be sure of that.\n这一点你大可放心。"

    old "Karen doesn't seem happy about this, but she's the only one who could succeed where I've failed."
    new "Karen doesn't seem happy about this, but she's the only one who could succeed where I've failed.\nKaren 对此似乎并不高兴，但在我失败的地方，也只有她能够成功。"

    old "Apolimesho, what can I say? I'm sorry. I failed in my responsibilities. I failed you."
    new "Apolimesho, what can I say? I'm sorry. I failed in my responsibilities. I failed you.\nApolimesho，我还能说什么呢？我很抱歉。我辜负了自己的职责，也辜负了你。"

    old "I'll accept your apology. But do not wallow in your failure for too long. Perhaps this is all for the best. In the past, both the Grimoire council and the Amazons have been reluctant to ally with one another. This turn of events has shown them that they are better off cooperating, rather than trusting an unknown freelancer to take care of their business."
    new "I'll accept your apology. But do not wallow in your failure for too long. Perhaps this is all for the best. In the past, both the Grimoire council and the Amazons have been reluctant to ally with one another. This turn of events has shown them that they are better off cooperating, rather than trusting an unknown freelancer to take care of their business.\n我接受你的道歉。但别在失败里沉溺太久。也许这样反而最好。过去，Grimoire 议会和 Amazons 一直不愿结盟。这次事态的转变让他们明白，彼此合作才是上策，而不是把事务托付给一个无名之辈。"

    old "However, do not mistake my optimism for forgiveness. Make no mistake, [protag]. You have failed Grimoire, and it is unlikely you will be welcome here any time soon."
    new "However, do not mistake my optimism for forgiveness. Make no mistake, [protag]. You have failed Grimoire, and it is unlikely you will be welcome here any time soon.\n不过，别把我的乐观误当作原谅。听清楚了，[protag]。你辜负了 Grimoire，短期内这里恐怕都不会再欢迎你。"

    old "As much as Apolimesho's words sting, I can't help but feel their truth. I give Apolimesho a respectful nod and slink away without saying anything more in my defense."
    new "As much as Apolimesho's words sting, I can't help but feel their truth. I give Apolimesho a respectful nod and slink away without saying anything more in my defense.\nApolimesho 的话虽然刺痛人心，我却不得不承认那是事实。我向他恭敬地点了点头，不再为自己辩解，灰溜溜地离开了。"

    old "I leave Grimoire immediately, without bidding farewell to any of my companions. Even if Apolimesho hadn't effectively just banished me from the city, I think my own shame would be enough to keep me away from this city for a long, long time."
    new "I leave Grimoire immediately, without bidding farewell to any of my companions. Even if Apolimesho hadn't effectively just banished me from the city, I think my own shame would be enough to keep me away from this city for a long, long time.\n我立刻离开了 Grimoire，没有向任何同伴道别。即便 Apolimesho 不曾变相把我逐出这座城市，我自己的羞愧也足以让我在很长很长一段时间里远远避开它。"

    old "Following my meeting with the council, I decided to leave Grimoire and head south. It seemed the most sensible choice, knowing about the undead plan to attack."
    new "Following my meeting with the council, I decided to leave Grimoire and head south. It seemed the most sensible choice, knowing about the undead plan to attack.\n与议会会面之后，我决定离开 Grimoire 南下。既然得知了不死大军进攻的计划，这似乎是最明智的选择。"

    old "I traveled south, passing nearby the Great Forest by foot. It wasn't the fastest way around, but it was the safest route. And safety was the reason I chose to walk away from Grimoire."
    new "I traveled south, passing nearby the Great Forest by foot. It wasn't the fastest way around, but it was the safest route. And safety was the reason I chose to walk away from Grimoire.\n我徒步南下，从 Great Forest 附近经过。那不是最快的路，却是最安全的路线。而我当初选择离开 Grimoire，为的正是安全。"

    old "I was just at the edge of the forest when I heard a stirring in the woods."
    new "I was just at the edge of the forest when I heard a stirring in the woods.\n我正走到森林边缘，就听见林子里有动静。"

    old "Suddenly I hear a sound and I feel a pain on my back."
    new "Suddenly I hear a sound and I feel a pain on my back.\n突然，我听到一声响，随即背上传来一阵剧痛。"

    old "I'm sorry [protag]."
    new "I'm sorry [protag].\n对不起，[protag]。"

    old "You... what...the council? They paid you to kill me, didn't they?"
    new "You... what...the council? They paid you to kill me, didn't they?\n你……什么……议会？他们花钱雇你来杀我，是不是？"

    old "When they told me, I couldn't believe it. I couldn't believe that after what you did, you wanted to run away like a coward."
    new "When they told me, I couldn't believe it. I couldn't believe that after what you did, you wanted to run away like a coward.\n他们告诉我时，我简直不敢相信。我不敢相信，你在做了那些事后，竟想像个懦夫一样逃跑。"

    old "You... <coughs>... bastard! You'd do anything for money, don't you?"
    new "You... <coughs>... bastard! You'd do anything for money, don't you?\n你……咳咳……混蛋！你为了钱什么都肯干，是不是？"

    old "Money? Yes, of course I asked the council for a good sum of money to do this. But they didn't have the money. They said would pay me after the undead menace is over."
    new "Money? Yes, of course I asked the council for a good sum of money to do this. But they didn't have the money. They said would pay me after the undead menace is over.\n钱？没错，我当然向议会要了一笔可观的报酬才肯干这事。可他们拿不出钱，说等不死之患平息后再付我。"

    old "I did it because I couldn't let you screw our plans. I'm still in the team fighting the vampires. With Karen, Leena and the others."
    new "I did it because I couldn't let you screw our plans. I'm still in the team fighting the vampires. With Karen, Leena and the others.\n我这么做，是因为我不能让你毁了我们的计划。我仍在那支对抗吸血鬼的队伍里，和 Karen、Leena 他们并肩作战。"

    old "Shortly after you rejected their offer, Apolimesho got in touch with me. He told me about a certain elf that was living in Grimoire. You lied to me, [protag]. Then I found out that Vaeril had nothing to do with the forest corruption."
    new "Shortly after you rejected their offer, Apolimesho got in touch with me. He told me about a certain elf that was living in Grimoire. You lied to me, [protag]. Then I found out that Vaeril had nothing to do with the forest corruption.\n你拒绝他们的提议后不久，Apolimesho 就联系了我。他告诉我有个精灵住在 Grimoire。你骗了我，[protag]。后来我才查明，Vaeril 与森林腐化毫无关系。"

    old "I decided to join Karen who is now leading the strike team against the undead. But I couldn't let you get away with what you've done."
    new "I decided to join Karen who is now leading the strike team against the undead. But I couldn't let you get away with what you've done.\n我决定加入 Karen 的队伍，如今正由她率领突击队对抗不死族。但我不能让你干了那些事还逍遥法外。"

    old "Please understand, even if I'm not a fan of what you did, it's nothing personal. Simply, you know too much. You know a lot about the Council, Castle N'Mar, the plans, Grimoire's weak points, the strategy... what if vampires captured you and made you confess?"
    new "Please understand, even if I'm not a fan of what you did, it's nothing personal. Simply, you know too much. You know a lot about the Council, Castle N'Mar, the plans, Grimoire's weak points, the strategy... what if vampires captured you and made you confess?\n请理解，即便我不认同你的所作所为，这也无关私人恩怨。只是你知道得太多了。你对议会、Castle N'Mar、各项计划、Grimoire 的薄弱之处、战略部署……都了如指掌。万一吸血鬼抓到你，逼你招供怎么办？"

    old "I start to feel weak, because of all the blood I'm losing."
    new "I start to feel weak, because of all the blood I'm losing.\n由于失血过多，我开始感到虚弱。"

    old "And the others..."
    new "And the others...\n那其他人……"

    old "The others don't need to know. But honestly? After you left such in a hurry, without telling anyone, I don't think they'll miss you."
    new "The others don't need to know. But honestly? After you left such in a hurry, without telling anyone, I don't think they'll miss you.\n其他人不必知道。但说实话，你就那么匆匆离开，没跟任何人打招呼，我想他们不会想念你的。"

    old "I know I won't."
    new "I know I won't.\n我知道我不会。"

    old "I'm already far from town when I hear the first screams. The battle must have began. For a moment, I'm struck with a pang of guilt. The guilt of being a coward."
    new "I'm already far from town when I hear the first screams. The battle must have began. For a moment, I'm struck with a pang of guilt. The guilt of being a coward.\n听到第一声惨叫时，我早已远离城镇。战斗想必已经打响。有那么一瞬间，一阵愧疚攫住了我——身为懦夫的愧疚。"

    old "Maybe I am a coward, but I am alive, and I'm not facing the fury of the vampires right now. Hopefully my companions will manage without me."
    new "Maybe I am a coward, but I am alive, and I'm not facing the fury of the vampires right now. Hopefully my companions will manage without me.\n也许我确实是个懦夫，但我还活着，此刻也不必面对吸血鬼的暴怒。但愿同伴们没有我也能撑过去。"

    old "I increase my pace. I am safe south of Grimoire, but... the constant battle noises and screams irk me. They're distant, yet they seem so close."
    new "I increase my pace. I am safe south of Grimoire, but... the constant battle noises and screams irk me. They're distant, yet they seem so close.\n我加快脚步。在 Grimoire 以南我是安全的，可……那持续不断的厮杀声与惨叫搅得我心烦。它们明明很远，听来却如此之近。"

    old "I ride with my horse for several hours until it's almost dawn and there's no trace of the fog anymore. Suddenly, two familiar faces shows up before me. Zachary and Valery."
    new "I ride with my horse for several hours until it's almost dawn and there's no trace of the fog anymore. Suddenly, two familiar faces shows up before me. Zachary and Valery.\n我骑马赶了几个小时的路，直到天将破晓，雾气已无踪迹。突然，两张熟悉的面孔出现在我面前——Zachary 和 Valery。"

    old "We might ask you the same question."
    new "We might ask you the same question.\n我们倒想问你同样的问题。"

    old "I decided that, after all, you were right. I already did my part. I didn't want to risk dying in that battle."
    new "I decided that, after all, you were right. I already did my part. I didn't want to risk dying in that battle.\n我决定，毕竟你说得对。我已经尽了自己那份力，不想再冒着战死沙场的风险。"

    old "Oh, you followed my advice, good. There's a problem though. You see... we cannot really let you go."
    new "Oh, you followed my advice, good. There's a problem though. You see... we cannot really let you go.\n哦，你听了我的劝，很好。不过有个问题。你看……我们实在不能放你走。"

    old "What?! You're threatening me?"
    new "What?! You're threatening me?\n什么？！你在威胁我？"

    old "Good. What does this mean then?"
    new "Good. What does this mean then?\n好。那这又是什么意思？"

    old "My dear Valery wasn't finished. No. We aren't threatening you. We're simply taking you."
    new "My dear Valery wasn't finished. No. We aren't threatening you. We're simply taking you.\n我亲爱的 Valery 还没说完呢。不，我们不是在威胁你。我们只是要带你走。"

    old "You want to kill me? I thought we were allies? Or at least, not enemies."
    new "You want to kill me? I thought we were allies? Or at least, not enemies.\n你们想杀我？我还以为我们是盟友呢？至少，不是敌人。"

    old "We won't kill you. And we still want you as ally. We're going to turn you into a vampire."
    new "We won't kill you. And we still want you as ally. We're going to turn you into a vampire.\n我们不会杀你，也仍想要你做盟友。我们打算把你变成吸血鬼。"

    old "Don't you think that if I was interested, I would have accepted your offer already?"
    new "Don't you think that if I was interested, I would have accepted your offer already?\n你不觉得，如果我感兴趣的话，早就该接受你们的提议了吗？"

    old "Oh, but your opinion doesn't matter."
    new "Oh, but your opinion doesn't matter.\n哦，可你的意见并不重要。"

    old "Really? And after you turn me into a vampire, what's stopping me from taking my revenge?"
    new "Really? And after you turn me into a vampire, what's stopping me from taking my revenge?\n是吗？那你们把我变成吸血鬼之后，还有什么能阻止我报仇？"

    old "You won't become a normal vampire. You'll be... what's the right word. A vampire thrall? In practice, you'll be my eternal slave."
    new "You won't become a normal vampire. You'll be... what's the right word. A vampire thrall? In practice, you'll be my eternal slave.\n你不会变成普通的吸血鬼。你会成为……怎么说才准确呢。吸血鬼奴仆？实际上，你会是我永远的奴隶。"

    old "Slave! Hihihihihi!"
    new "Slave! Hihihihihi!\n奴隶！嘻嘻嘻嘻！"

    old "Valery's laugh chills the blood in my veins. The look in her eyes, she seems crazed with excitement at the idea."
    new "Valery's laugh chills the blood in my veins. The look in her eyes, she seems crazed with excitement at the idea.\nValery 的笑声让我血管里的血都凉了。她眼中的神情，似乎为这个念头兴奋得近乎疯狂。"

    old "What? Lies! That's not how it works!"
    new "What? Lies! That's not how it works!\n什么？一派胡言！根本不是这样的！"

    old "Trust me. I am a very old vampire. I know how this works. When we bite someone, depending how much blood we draw, how much pressure we put on the neck, and a couple other secrets, the victim can either be: dead, turn into a vampire, or become a thrall."
    new "Trust me. I am a very old vampire. I know how this works. When we bite someone, depending how much blood we draw, how much pressure we put on the neck, and a couple other secrets, the victim can either be: dead, turn into a vampire, or become a thrall.\n相信我。我是个活了很久的吸血鬼，清楚其中门道。我们咬人时，取决于吸多少血、在颈上施加多大压力，再加上另外几个诀窍，受害者的下场可能是：死去，变成吸血鬼，或者沦为奴仆。"

    old "You'll become a thrall."
    new "You'll become a thrall.\n你会沦为奴仆。"

    old "I try to turn the horse and run back, but as I perform the action I already know that's futile. They're faster than me. Faster than the horse. There's no way I can escape..."
    new "I try to turn the horse and run back, but as I perform the action I already know that's futile. They're faster than me. Faster than the horse. There's no way I can escape...\n我试图调转马头往回跑，可刚一动作，我就明白那是徒劳。他们比我快，比马还快。我根本逃不掉……"

    old "They're on me and my vision starts to blur, and I lose consciousness... this will be my destiny? To become a vampire's slave for eternity? Perhaps it was a fair punishment for my cowardice."
    new "They're on me and my vision starts to blur, and I lose consciousness... this will be my destiny? To become a vampire's slave for eternity? Perhaps it was a fair punishment for my cowardice.\n他们扑了上来，我的视线开始模糊，渐渐失去意识……这就会是我的命运吗？永远沦为吸血鬼的奴隶？或许，这是对我怯懦的应有惩罚。"

    old "After the triumph on the undead forces of N'Mar, I became a sort of local legend. The council wasn't the only one being interested in me."
    new "After the triumph on the undead forces of N'Mar, I became a sort of local legend. The council wasn't the only one being interested in me.\n在 N'Mar 战胜不死大军之后，我成了某种地方传奇。对我感兴趣的不只是议会。"

    old "I had a lot of possibilities. Left with the decision of who to work for, I was spoiled for choice. The Council, Lady Geraldine, Sir Cedric... everyone wanted me."
    new "I had a lot of possibilities. Left with the decision of who to work for, I was spoiled for choice. The Council, Lady Geraldine, Sir Cedric... everyone wanted me.\n我面前有许多可能。真要决定为谁效力，反倒挑花了眼。议会、Lady Geraldine、Sir Cedric……人人都想招揽我。"

    old "And I choose to work only for myself. I told everyone I was going to take a break to decide. Travel Aravorn a bit, discover new things. But it was a lie."
    new "And I choose to work only for myself. I told everyone I was going to take a break to decide. Travel Aravorn a bit, discover new things. But it was a lie.\n而我选择只为自己效力。我告诉所有人我要休息一阵、好好考虑，顺便游历一下 Aravorn，见识些新事物。但那都是谎话。"

    old "When Apolimesho approached me a few days after the victory on N'Mar, I was unsure what he wanted to talk about."
    new "When Apolimesho approached me a few days after the victory on N'Mar, I was unsure what he wanted to talk about.\n在 N'Mar 大捷后没几天，Apolimesho 找上我时，我不确定他想谈什么。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Come, sit down. May I offer you something?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Come, sit down. May I offer you something?\n啊，[protag]。来，坐下。要我给你来点什么吗？"

    old "I'm good, thanks Apolimesho. I suppose the Council appointed you to convince me to work for them again?"
    new "I'm good, thanks Apolimesho. I suppose the Council appointed you to convince me to work for them again?\n不用了，谢谢，Apolimesho。我猜是议会派你来说服我再为他们效力吧？"

    old "Actually, the Council doesn't know about this meeting."
    new "Actually, the Council doesn't know about this meeting.\n其实，议会并不知道这次会面。"

    old "Oh. Then what..."
    new "Oh. Then what...\n哦。那你这是……"

    old "Here's what's going to happen, [protag]. I don't know the details yet. But after what you've done, I'm sure the Council will make you an offer. Now, you could accept their offer. Or wait, in case someone else makes a better offer."
    new "Here's what's going to happen, [protag]. I don't know the details yet. But after what you've done, I'm sure the Council will make you an offer. Now, you could accept their offer. Or wait, in case someone else makes a better offer.\n接下来会这样，[protag]。我还不清楚细节，但凭你做过的事，我确信议会会向你开出条件。眼下，你可以接受他们的条件；或者再等等，看会不会有别人开出更好的价码。"

    old "I hear both Lady Geraldine and Cedric are very interested in your services as well as many other influential people in Aravorn. But if I may give you my humble advice?"
    new "I hear both Lady Geraldine and Cedric are very interested in your services as well as many other influential people in Aravorn. But if I may give you my humble advice?\n我听说 Lady Geraldine 和 Cedric 都对你有意，Aravorn 里其他许多权贵也一样。不过，容我斗胆进一言？"

    old "Go ahead, Apolimesho. I've only gotten this far because of your advice. We might not have a working relationship anymore, but that doesn't mean I'm going to stop listening when you take the time to offer words of wisdom."
    new "Go ahead, Apolimesho. I've only gotten this far because of your advice. We might not have a working relationship anymore, but that doesn't mean I'm going to stop listening when you take the time to offer words of wisdom.\n请讲，Apolimesho。我能走到今天，全靠你的指点。我们之间也许已不再共事，但这不意味着你肯花时间指点时，我会不听。"

    old "Don't accept any of their offers. If you work for someone else, you place your destiny in their hands. No matter how capable you might be, something will eventually go wrong. Something beyond your control. Something that might not even be your fault. But the blame will fall on you. When you work for someone else, you always risk being turned into their scapegoat."
    new "Don't accept any of their offers. If you work for someone else, you place your destiny in their hands. No matter how capable you might be, something will eventually go wrong. Something beyond your control. Something that might not even be your fault. But the blame will fall on you. When you work for someone else, you always risk being turned into their scapegoat.\n别接受他们任何一方的条件。为别人效力，就是把命运交到别人手里。无论你多有本事，事情终究会出岔子——某种你无法掌控、甚至根本怪不得你的岔子，可黑锅终究要落到你头上。为别人做事，你就总有被他们当作替罪羊的风险。"

    old "What I suggest is to work for yourself."
    new "What I suggest is to work for yourself.\n我的建议是，为你自己效力。"

    old "For myself? Exactly how?"
    new "For myself? Exactly how?\n为自己？具体怎么做？"

    old "I don't know the answer to this myself. But if there's one thing I've learned about you during the time we've spent together, it's that you're an ambitious [manwoman] with a good head on your shoulders. You'll find something. And something tells me you're the kind of person who's better suited to giving orders than receiving them."
    new "I don't know the answer to this myself. But if there's one thing I've learned about you during the time we've spent together, it's that you're an ambitious [manwoman] with a good head on your shoulders. You'll find something. And something tells me you're the kind of person who's better suited to giving orders than receiving them.\n这个答案我自己也不知道。不过，在我们相处的这段时间里，我若从你身上学到了一点什么，那就是你是个头脑清醒、志向远大的[manwoman]。你自会找到出路。而且我有种预感，你是那种更适合发号施令、而非听命于人的人。"

    old "I'm not sure where your journey ends. But I know that out there is an opportunity that you are uniquely qualified for, and you won't find it by working for someone else."
    new "I'm not sure where your journey ends. But I know that out there is an opportunity that you are uniquely qualified for, and you won't find it by working for someone else.\n我不知道你的旅程会止于何处。但我知道，外面有个非你莫属的机会，而那个机会，是你为别人效力时永远找不到的。"

    old "And so I decided to follow Apolimesho's advice. I traveled to Flowervale, a very prosperous region of Zoltar first colonized by elves and now an independent state. I reached its ancient capitol city, Sekh Tune."
    new "And so I decided to follow Apolimesho's advice. I traveled to Flowervale, a very prosperous region of Zoltar first colonized by elves and now an independent state. I reached its ancient capitol city, Sekh Tune.\n于是我决定听从 Apolimesho 的建议。我前往 Flowervale，那是 Zoltar 一处十分繁荣的地区，最初由精灵殖民，如今已成独立邦国。我抵达了它古老的首府 Sekh Tune。"

    old "There, I met with..."
    new "There, I met with...\n在那里，我见到了……"

    old "...Prince Lyari and married him."
    new "...Prince Lyari and married him.\n……Lyari 王子，并与他成婚。"

    old "...Princess Myriani and married her."
    new "...Princess Myriani and married her.\n……Myriani 公主，并与她成婚。"

    old "Apparently, King Edenfell just died, leaving behind an inexperienced heir. The Queen Magesta thought I was the best person to help rule the state and so she arranged this marriage."
    new "Apparently, King Edenfell just died, leaving behind an inexperienced heir. The Queen Magesta thought I was the best person to help rule the state and so she arranged this marriage.\n原来，King Edenfell 刚刚驾崩，只留下一位缺乏经验的继承人。Queen Magesta 认为我是协助治理这个国家的最佳人选，于是安排了这桩婚事。"

    old "Of course, everyone was surprised, since I don't come from any noble family. But with the queen to vouch for me, who would complain? Besides, after the events of N'Mar, I might not a noble, but I'm still a hero, well known thorough Aravorn."
    new "Of course, everyone was surprised, since I don't come from any noble family. But with the queen to vouch for me, who would complain? Besides, after the events of N'Mar, I might not a noble, but I'm still a hero, well known thorough Aravorn.\n自然，人人都很惊讶，因为我并非出身贵族。可有王后为我作保，谁又会抱怨呢？况且，经历了 N'Mar 那场风波，我虽不是贵族，却仍是名扬 Aravorn 的英雄。"

    old "And this time, I won't have to answer to anyone but myself. This time, I'm the one making the rules."
    new "And this time, I won't have to answer to anyone but myself. This time, I'm the one making the rules.\n而这一次，我除了自己，不必对任何人负责。这一次，制定规则的人是我。"

    old "I found myself a child of the night, and as I grew more accustomed to my vampire body, most nights found me out hunting for fresh prey to bring back to satisfy my hunger. Perhaps a lizardman from the swamp, or an animal from the wilds, or some person who had it coming."
    new "I found myself a child of the night, and as I grew more accustomed to my vampire body, most nights found me out hunting for fresh prey to bring back to satisfy my hunger. Perhaps a lizardman from the swamp, or an animal from the wilds, or some person who had it coming.\n我发现自己成了黑夜之子，随着对这副吸血鬼之躯日渐习惯，大多数夜晚我都在外狩猎新鲜猎物，带回来填饱饥饿。也许是沼泽里的蜥蜴人，也许是荒野中的野兽，又或是某个罪有应得之人。"

    old "Zachary and Valery really wanted me to stay with them. They thought I would be completely dependent on them."
    new "Zachary and Valery really wanted me to stay with them. They thought I would be completely dependent on them.\nZachary 和 Valery 真的很想让我留下。他们以为我会完全依赖他们。"

    old "Someone like me isn't really welcome in the world of the living. Existence can get lonely, sometimes."
    new "Someone like me isn't really welcome in the world of the living. Existence can get lonely, sometimes.\n像我这样的人，在生者的世界里并不受欢迎。有时，这样的存在会变得孤独。"

    old "Zachary and Valery had plans for the future, but fate is a cruel mistress."
    new "Zachary and Valery had plans for the future, but fate is a cruel mistress.\nZachary 和 Valery 原本对将来有所盘算，可命运是个残酷的情人。"

    old "Apparently, even without Humbra's help, Mother Morte wasn't so harmless as they thought. She took residence in the castle's dungeons. Deep down, where nobody would dare to go to face her close."
    new "Apparently, even without Humbra's help, Mother Morte wasn't so harmless as they thought. She took residence in the castle's dungeons. Deep down, where nobody would dare to go to face her close.\n原来，即便没有 Humbra 的帮助，Mother Morte 也远不像他们想的那般无害。她在城堡的地牢里落了脚——在那深深的地下，没人敢凑近去面对她的地方。"

    old "I'm not sure if being that deep down actually made her closer to the Under-Realm, but whatever the case, it seemed to be a place where she was able to practice her dark magics. Over time, her strength began to grow and foment."
    new "I'm not sure if being that deep down actually made her closer to the Under-Realm, but whatever the case, it seemed to be a place where she was able to practice her dark magics. Over time, her strength began to grow and foment.\n我不确定身处那么深的地下是否真让她更接近 Under-Realm，但无论如何，那里似乎是个能让她修习黑暗魔法的地方。日复一日，她的力量开始增长、酝酿。"

    old "She used her magic to cast a curse on Zachary and Valery, so that they could never leave the castle again even if they wanted to."
    new "She used her magic to cast a curse on Zachary and Valery, so that they could never leave the castle again even if they wanted to.\n她用魔法对 Zachary 和 Valery 施下诅咒，让他们即便想走，也再无法离开那座城堡。"

    old "Zachary and Valery, now trapped in the castle, rely on the likes of me to survive. A vampire can last a long time without feeding, especially one as old as Zachary, who has had a long time to practice using every drop of blood as efficiently as possible. But they grow weaker and weaker with every passing day, and now, they feel pain."
    new "Zachary and Valery, now trapped in the castle, rely on the likes of me to survive. A vampire can last a long time without feeding, especially one as old as Zachary, who has had a long time to practice using every drop of blood as efficiently as possible. But they grow weaker and weaker with every passing day, and now, they feel pain.\n如今被困在城堡里的 Zachary 和 Valery，只能靠我这样的人才能活命。吸血鬼能长时间不进食，尤其是像 Zachary 这般年迈的，他有的是时间去练习把每一滴血都用得尽可能高效。但他们还是一天比一天虚弱，如今已尝到痛苦。"

    old "In a way, I am a bit like their caretaker. They eat only when I feed them."
    new "In a way, I am a bit like their caretaker. They eat only when I feed them.\n从某种意义上说，我倒有点像他们的看护人。只有我喂食时，他们才有得吃。"

    old "I'm not sure quite what to do with them. They're a deceptive duo, not the sort I would come to trust, but they're useful to me for now. I'm a young vampire trying to learn more about the extent of my powers, and they're more experienced than I am."
    new "I'm not sure quite what to do with them. They're a deceptive duo, not the sort I would come to trust, but they're useful to me for now. I'm a young vampire trying to learn more about the extent of my powers, and they're more experienced than I am.\n我不太确定该拿他们怎么办。他们是一对狡诈的家伙，不是我信得过的那种人，但眼下他们对我还有用。我是个年轻的吸血鬼，正想更了解自己力量的边界，而他们比我更有经验。"

    old "Zachary can even be a good teacher, when he's in the right mood. In fact, I think my powers have already begun to match Valery's."
    new "Zachary can even be a good teacher, when he's in the right mood. In fact, I think my powers have already begun to match Valery's.\nZachary 心情好的时候，甚至能当个好老师。事实上，我觉得我的力量已经开始与 Valery 不相上下了。"

    old "The day will soon come when Zachary has taught me all that he can. And when that day comes, I suppose I'll be left with the decision of whether to kill them."
    new "The day will soon come when Zachary has taught me all that he can. And when that day comes, I suppose I'll be left with the decision of whether to kill them.\n用不了多久，Zachary 就会把他能教的都教给我。到那一天，我想我就要面对是否杀了他们的抉择。"

    old "Perhaps Zachary and Valery deserve to be killed for what they've done. But the more that I consider it, allowing them to continue to rot away might be the crueler punishment. Their current fate seems fitting."
    new "Perhaps Zachary and Valery deserve to be killed for what they've done. But the more that I consider it, allowing them to continue to rot away might be the crueler punishment. Their current fate seems fitting.\n或许 Zachary 和 Valery 罪该一死。可我越想越觉得，任由他们继续这般腐烂下去，或许是更残酷的惩罚。他们如今的处境，似乎正合适。"

    old "They wanted castle N'Mar for themselves, and now they have it. It may very well be their eternal prison."
    new "They wanted castle N'Mar for themselves, and now they have it. It may very well be their eternal prison.\n他们一心想把 Castle N'Mar 据为己有，如今如愿了。而那也很可能成为他们永恒的牢笼。"

    old "Sylrissa has been a wonderful partner. Despite my complete transformation into a vampire, she never showed any sign of fear or distrust towards me."
    new "Sylrissa has been a wonderful partner. Despite my complete transformation into a vampire, she never showed any sign of fear or distrust towards me.\nSylrissa 一直是个绝佳的伴侣。尽管我彻底变成了吸血鬼，她却从未对我流露过半点恐惧或不信任。"

    old "We're in Grimoire's catacombs now. Deep down the city."
    new "We're in Grimoire's catacombs now. Deep down the city.\n我们现在身处 Grimoire 的地下墓穴，城市深处。"

    old "Come on, [protag]! That giant rat is running away!"
    new "Come on, [protag]! That giant rat is running away!\n快，[protag]！那只巨鼠要跑了！"

    old "He can run, but there's no way he'll escape us. No one can outrace you. Well, except for me."
    new "He can run, but there's no way he'll escape us. No one can outrace you. Well, except for me.\n他能跑，但绝逃不出我们的手心。没人能跑得过你。嗯，除了我。"

    old "Ha! Challenge accepted!"
    new "Ha! Challenge accepted!\n哈！这个挑战我接下了！"

    old "I slow down on purpose. Sylrissa is fast, but she's no match with my skills now. I let her capture the prey."
    new "I slow down on purpose. Sylrissa is fast, but she's no match with my skills now. I let her capture the prey.\n我故意放慢速度。Sylrissa 很快，但如今以我的身手，她已不是对手。我把猎物让给了她。"

    old "Ta-dah! A delicious giant rat meal!"
    new "Ta-dah! A delicious giant rat meal!\n哒哒！一顿美味的巨鼠大餐！"

    old "You know, I like this."
    new "You know, I like this.\n你知道吗，我喜欢这样。"

    old "Rats are tasty indeed!"
    new "Rats are tasty indeed!\n老鼠确实好吃！"

    old "I wasn't really talking about the enjoyment of consuming rats. Even if for me its blood doesn't taste any different than another living prey. But I like that we can still be useful by hunting all those rats."
    new "I wasn't really talking about the enjoyment of consuming rats. Even if for me its blood doesn't taste any different than another living prey. But I like that we can still be useful by hunting all those rats.\n我说的倒不完全是吃老鼠的乐趣。毕竟对我来说，它的血和别的活物猎物尝起来没什么两样。但让我高兴的是，靠猎杀这些老鼠，我们还能派上用场。"

    old "When Apolimesho told me about this giant rats infestation problem, I told him we'd solve the problem very efficiently."
    new "When Apolimesho told me about this giant rats infestation problem, I told him we'd solve the problem very efficiently.\nApolimesho 跟我提起鼠患问题时，我告诉他，我们一定能高效地解决。"

    old "I'm surprised he still trust me. It takes a special kind of person to trust a vampire."
    new "I'm surprised he still trust me. It takes a special kind of person to trust a vampire.\n我很惊讶他仍信任我。肯信任一个吸血鬼，得是特别的人才行。"

    old "Someone special, like me?"
    new "Someone special, like me?\n像我这样特别的人？"

    old "Of course. No one's more special than you. Well, except for me."
    new "Of course. No one's more special than you. Well, except for me.\n当然。没人比你更特别。嗯，除了我。"

    old "Ha! That's one challenge that I won't take you up on."
    new "Ha! That's one challenge that I won't take you up on.\n哈！这个挑战我可就不接啦。"

    old "But [protag], you don't need to feel guilty just because you're a vampire. You proved that you're still committed to good when we fought together at N'Mar. Vampires aren't necessarily evil. Yes, many of them are blinded by their new powers and succumb to the dark side. But I never doubted you'd still be a good [manwoman]."
    new "But [protag], you don't need to feel guilty just because you're a vampire. You proved that you're still committed to good when we fought together at N'Mar. Vampires aren't necessarily evil. Yes, many of them are blinded by their new powers and succumb to the dark side. But I never doubted you'd still be a good [manwoman].\n可是 [protag]，你不必因为自己是吸血鬼就心怀愧疚。当初我们并肩作战于 N'Mar 时，你已经证明了仍心向良善。吸血鬼未必邪恶。没错，他们中许多人都被新获得的力量蒙蔽双眼，堕入黑暗。但我从不怀疑，你依然会是个善良的[manwoman]。"

    old "You're right, Sylrissa. It doesn't matter who we are, but how we behave, what we do."
    new "You're right, Sylrissa. It doesn't matter who we are, but how we behave, what we do.\n你说得对，Sylrissa。重要的不是我们是谁，而是我们如何行事、做了什么。"

    old "Right. This is just the beginning, [protag]. I'm sure we're destined to do greater things in future, together."
    new "Right. This is just the beginning, [protag]. I'm sure we're destined to do greater things in future, together.\n对。这不过是个开始，[protag]。我相信，未来我们注定会一起成就更伟大的事业。"

    old "Sylrissa flashes a smile at me. My heart might not be beating anymore, but sometimes I feel it could challenge the laws of the undead and still beat for her. My love, Sylrissa."
    new "Sylrissa flashes a smile at me. My heart might not be beating anymore, but sometimes I feel it could challenge the laws of the undead and still beat for her. My love, Sylrissa.\nSylrissa 朝我绽开一个笑容。我的心也许已不再跳动，但有时我觉得它能挑战不死之律，依然为她而跳。我的挚爱，Sylrissa。"

    old "My time together Sylrissa has been great. We've traveled Aravorn, stopping a few days on each city. We've been to Shacklesplit, Dingirra, Flowervale. And now we're on a boat heading back to Grimoire."
    new "My time together Sylrissa has been great. We've traveled Aravorn, stopping a few days on each city. We've been to Shacklesplit, Dingirra, Flowervale. And now we're on a boat heading back to Grimoire.\n和 Sylrissa 共度的时光十分美好。我们游历 Aravorn，每座城都小住几日。我们去过 Shacklesplit、Dingirra、Flowervale。如今我们正乘船返回 Grimoire。"

    old "So, my love, where we could go tomorrow?"
    new "So, my love, where we could go tomorrow?\n那么，我的爱人，我们明天去哪儿？"

    old "I was thinking that, since we're close to the Citadel, we could pay a visit to Karen?"
    new "I was thinking that, since we're close to the Citadel, we could pay a visit to Karen?\n我在想，既然我们离 Citadel 很近，何不去拜访一下 Karen？"

    old "Oh, Karen. Has been so long since I admired her body."
    new "Oh, Karen. Has been so long since I admired her body.\n哦，Karen。我好久没欣赏过她的身段了。"

    old "...are you trying to make me jealous again?"
    new "...are you trying to make me jealous again?\n……你又想让我吃醋了？"

    old "No, but it was the first thing that come to mind thinking about her."
    new "No, but it was the first thing that come to mind thinking about her.\n没有，只是一想到她，这念头第一个冒了出来。"

    old "Pff. I'm not sure if she'll want to see me again, since I'm no longer an important person."
    new "Pff. I'm not sure if she'll want to see me again, since I'm no longer an important person.\n切。我不确定她还想不想见我，毕竟我已不再是重要人物。"

    old "You really underestimate Karen if you think that she wouldn't want to see you anymore, only because you resigned from the title of Envoy!"
    new "You really underestimate Karen if you think that she wouldn't want to see you anymore, only because you resigned from the title of Envoy!\n如果你以为 Karen 只因你辞去 Envoy 头衔就不想再见你，那你可真是小看她了！"

    old "On the contrary, I think she probably respects you more now that you're no longer doing the Empire's bidding."
    new "On the contrary, I think she probably respects you more now that you're no longer doing the Empire's bidding.\n恰恰相反，我觉得你现在不再听命于帝国，她说不定更敬重你了。"

    old "There's still several hours before we arrive. We need to find a way to keep ourselves busy..."
    new "There's still several hours before we arrive. We need to find a way to keep ourselves busy...\n离靠岸还有好几个小时。我们得找点事打发时间……"

    old "Mhhm. I think I know where this conversation is going."
    new "Mhhm. I think I know where this conversation is going.\n嗯哼。我想我知道这话要往哪儿拐了。"

    old "We embrace and I kiss her passionately. I'm no longer an important person now, but I have all I ever wanted: the unconditional love of someone who I love just as strongly. Sylrissa's love."
    new "We embrace and I kiss her passionately. I'm no longer an important person now, but I have all I ever wanted: the unconditional love of someone who I love just as strongly. Sylrissa's love.\n我们相拥，我热情地吻了她。如今我已不再是重要人物，可我拥有想要的一切：一个我爱得同样深沉的人所给予的无条件的爱。那是 Sylrissa 的爱。"

    old "I drink the potion that Enok has prepared me. We wait several minutes, but nothing happens."
    new "I drink the potion that Enok has prepared me. We wait several minutes, but nothing happens.\n我喝下 Enok 为我调制的药水。我们等了几分钟，却什么也没发生。"

    old "Dang it."
    new "Dang it.\n该死。"

    old "Well, at least I didn't die."
    new "Well, at least I didn't die.\n嗯，至少我没死。"

    old "Oh please! Like if that wasn't even a possible outcome. You're already dead, remember."
    new "Oh please! Like if that wasn't even a possible outcome. You're already dead, remember.\n拜托！说得好像那根本不可能似的。你早就死了，记得吗。"

    old "I meant... oh, forget about it. Enok, as much as I appreciate your efforts, I think reversing the vampire transformation is something beyond your skills. Beyond anyone else!"
    new "I meant... oh, forget about it. Enok, as much as I appreciate your efforts, I think reversing the vampire transformation is something beyond your skills. Beyond anyone else!\n我是说……唉，算了。Enok，我虽然很感激你的努力，但逆转吸血鬼之躯，恐怕超出了你的能力范围。也超出了任何人的能力！"

    old "No! I studied so many alchemy books! I should be able to... I think I'm missing something obvious. Maybe we should ask Apolimesho? After all, he's one of the most famous alchemist of Aravorn!"
    new "No! I studied so many alchemy books! I should be able to... I think I'm missing something obvious. Maybe we should ask Apolimesho? After all, he's one of the most famous alchemist of Aravorn!\n不！我读了那么多炼金术的书！我应该能……我想我肯定漏掉了什么明摆着的东西。也许我们该去问 Apolimesho？毕竟，他可是 Aravorn 最有名的炼金术士之一！"

    old "Enok..."
    new "Enok...\nEnok……"

    old "Sorry. It's not like... I despise what you're now, [protag]. I am only trying to give your life back."
    new "Sorry. It's not like... I despise what you're now, [protag]. I am only trying to give your life back.\n抱歉。我并不是……我并非厌恶你如今的样子，[protag]。我只是想把你的人生还给你。"

    old "If you like what I am now, then please stop. I am happy with you. I know you might not believe me when I say it, but I'm happy just staying here with you, in the swamps, with that little shack you built by the river."
    new "If you like what I am now, then please stop. I am happy with you. I know you might not believe me when I say it, but I'm happy just staying here with you, in the swamps, with that little shack you built by the river.\n如果你喜欢我现在的样子，就请住手吧。和你在一起，我很幸福。我知道我这么说你可能不信，但只要能和你待在这里、待在这片沼泽里、待在你河边搭的那间小棚屋里，我就很幸福。"

    old "I can feed on animals, or lizardmen. I don't feel guilty for what I am."
    new "I can feed on animals, or lizardmen. I don't feel guilty for what I am.\n我可以靠动物或蜥蜴人果腹。我对自己如今的身份并不愧疚。"

    old "I come near Enok and place my finger on his lips to silence him."
    new "I come near Enok and place my finger on his lips to silence him.\n我走近 Enok，把手指按在他唇上，让他安静下来。"

    old "Promise me you'll stop those pointless experiments, and spend more time appreciating me for what I am now. You of all people should understand what this means."
    new "Promise me you'll stop those pointless experiments, and spend more time appreciating me for what I am now. You of all people should understand what this means.\n答应我，别再搞那些毫无意义的实验了，多花点时间欣赏我现在的样子。这件事的意义，你应该比谁都清楚。"

    old "Okay. I understand. I promise."
    new "Okay. I understand. I promise.\n好。我明白。我答应你。"

    old "Good. Now come here."
    new "Good. Now come here.\n很好。现在过来。"

    old "We lay down in the river's bank and enjoy a long kiss. I might not be an important person anymore. I might not be welcome in most cities. And I'm not a powerful vampire living in a castle. But I'm still happy, here with Enok, living day by day a simple life, trying all the delicious recipes he prepares for me."
    new "We lay down in the river's bank and enjoy a long kiss. I might not be an important person anymore. I might not be welcome in most cities. And I'm not a powerful vampire living in a castle. But I'm still happy, here with Enok, living day by day a simple life, trying all the delicious recipes he prepares for me.\n我们躺在河岸边，享受了一个悠长的吻。我也许不再是重要人物，也许在大多数城市都不受欢迎，也不再是住在城堡里的强大吸血鬼。但我依然幸福——就在这里，和 Enok 一起，日复一日过着简单的生活，尝遍他为我烹制的美味佳肴。"

    old "Maybe one day I'll be back doing great things, but for now? For now I'm happy."
    new "Maybe one day I'll be back doing great things, but for now? For now I'm happy.\n也许有一天我会重拾伟业，但现在？现在我很快乐。"

    old "Come on, [protag]! I can't wait to try it!"
    new "Come on, [protag]! I can't wait to try it!\n快来，[protag]！我等不及想尝一尝了！"

    old "This restaurant better be good. We traveled over half of Issanis to get here!"
    new "This restaurant better be good. We traveled over half of Issanis to get here!\n这家馆子最好名副其实。我们可是横穿了大半个 Issanis 才到这儿！"

    old "Trust me, you'll love it! It's the most famous of all Triberg."
    new "Trust me, you'll love it! It's the most famous of all Triberg.\n相信我，你会喜欢的！它可是全 Triberg 最有名的。"

    old "I must admit that Enok's company is anything but boring. He has many interests, from ancient history to magic, from pottery to painting. And, of course, cooking."
    new "I must admit that Enok's company is anything but boring. He has many interests, from ancient history to magic, from pottery to painting. And, of course, cooking.\n我得承认，有 Enok 作伴绝不无聊。他兴趣广泛，从上古历史到魔法，从制陶到绘画，当然，还有烹饪。"

    old "Everyone knows who we are thanks to our success against N'Mar, and even though some people give Enok odd looks from time to time, people's attitudes toward the naga race are slowly changing."
    new "Everyone knows who we are thanks to our success against N'Mar, and even though some people give Enok odd looks from time to time, people's attitudes toward the naga race are slowly changing.\n多亏我们对抗 N'Mar 的胜利，人人都知道我们是谁；尽管不时有人对 Enok 投以异样的目光，人们对 naga 一族的态度正在慢慢改观。"

    old "Enok has made friends in many places of the Empire, and we've become famous as the couple of two champions who managed to find love in the midst of a conflict that made us both heroes."
    new "Enok has made friends in many places of the Empire, and we've become famous as the couple of two champions who managed to find love in the midst of a conflict that made us both heroes.\nEnok 在帝国的许多地方都结交了朋友，而我们作为一对在战火中相恋、双双成为英雄的冠军情侣，也早已声名在外。"

    old "I still work with the council the Council in a diplomatic capacity, but my commitments are few, leaving me with lots of free time for myself, and for my love, Enok."
    new "I still work with the council the Council in a diplomatic capacity, but my commitments are few, leaving me with lots of free time for myself, and for my love, Enok.\n我仍以某种外交身份为议会效力，但职责不多，这让我有大把空闲时间留给自己，也留给我的爱人 Enok。"

    old "Who would have ever thought, that the night I met the decimated human army, I would have then made so many friends, become such an important figure, and triumph against such a powerful evil? It's all far beyond what I could have imagined."
    new "Who would have ever thought, that the night I met the decimated human army, I would have then made so many friends, become such an important figure, and triumph against such a powerful evil? It's all far beyond what I could have imagined.\n谁能想到，那晚我遇见残破的人类军队之后，竟会结交这么多朋友、成为如此举足轻重的人物，还战胜了那么强大的邪恶？这一切都远超我的想象。"

    old "But the greatest surprise of all was that I fell in love with a naga. And the love that has blossomed between me and Enok has been my greatest reward, as well."
    new "But the greatest surprise of all was that I fell in love with a naga. And the love that has blossomed between me and Enok has been my greatest reward, as well.\n但最大的惊喜，是我爱上了一个 naga。而在我与 Enok 之间绽放的爱情，同样是我最丰厚的回报。"

    old "I run at my new, unusual speed in the swamps. Enok and Sylrissa, in spite of their fast speed, still struggle to keep up."
    new "I run at my new, unusual speed in the swamps. Enok and Sylrissa, in spite of their fast speed, still struggle to keep up.\n我在沼泽里以自己那非比寻常的新速度奔跑。Enok 和 Sylrissa 尽管速度也很快，却仍跟得吃力。"

    old "The witch hunters are on our tails. We always tried to avoid confrontation with them. We never face them head on. But that doesn't stop them from trying to chase us."
    new "The witch hunters are on our tails. We always tried to avoid confrontation with them. We never face them head on. But that doesn't stop them from trying to chase us.\n猎巫人正紧追不舍。我们一向尽力避免与他们正面对抗，从不硬碰硬。可这并不能让他们放弃追捕。"

    old "Luckily, we're good at escaping."
    new "Luckily, we're good at escaping.\n幸运的是，我们很擅长脱身。"

    old "Phew. That was close."
    new "Phew. That was close.\n呼。好险。"

    old "The funniest thing is that they're chasing us, as if we're the ones who would lose if it came to a direct confrontation. If we decided to actually fight them, they'd all quickly die. Isn't it hilarious? They hunt us, thinking that we're afraid of them, but it's them that should be afraid of us."
    new "The funniest thing is that they're chasing us, as if we're the ones who would lose if it came to a direct confrontation. If we decided to actually fight them, they'd all quickly die. Isn't it hilarious? They hunt us, thinking that we're afraid of them, but it's them that should be afraid of us.\n最可笑的是，他们追着我们跑，好像真要正面对上，输的会是我们似的。我们若决意动手，他们全都活不过一时半刻。是不是很滑稽？他们来猎杀我们，以为我们怕他们，可该害怕的明明是他们。"

    old "Sylrissa!"
    new "Sylrissa!\nSylrissa！"

    old "No need to worry, Enok. I'm not going to give in to my new vampiric instincts so easily."
    new "No need to worry, Enok. I'm not going to give in to my new vampiric instincts so easily.\n别担心，Enok。我可不会那么轻易就向新的吸血鬼本能屈服。"

    old "I know, but... Sylrissa, you shouldn't say those things."
    new "I know, but... Sylrissa, you shouldn't say those things.\n我知道，可是…… Sylrissa，你不该说那些话。"

    old "My apologies, daddy Enok."
    new "My apologies, daddy Enok.\n抱歉啦，Enok 爸爸。"

    old "Oh, please!"
    new "Oh, please!\n哦，饶了我吧！"

    old "Sylrissa sensuously moves near Enok and his grumpy face quickly turns into a smile as she fills his face by small kisses."
    new "Sylrissa sensuously moves near Enok and his grumpy face quickly turns into a smile as she fills his face by small kisses.\nSylrissa 妩媚地凑近 Enok，用一连串细碎的吻盖满他的脸，他原本板着的面孔顿时化作了笑容。"

    old "We're safe now, right [protag]? Why don't we take a bath in this pond? Seems lovely."
    new "We're safe now, right [protag]? Why don't we take a bath in this pond? Seems lovely.\n我们现在安全了，对吧 [protag]？何不在这池塘里洗个澡？看起来真不错。"

    old "That's a good idea, Sylrissa. Since my body no longer gives off heat, I don't even care if the water is cold or not."
    new "That's a good idea, Sylrissa. Since my body no longer gives off heat, I don't even care if the water is cold or not.\n好主意，Sylrissa。既然我的身体不再散发热量，我甚至不在乎水冷不冷。"

    old "See, Enok? [protag] is enjoying [hisher] new powers already!"
    new "See, Enok? [protag] is enjoying [hisher] new powers already!\n瞧，Enok？[protag] 已经在享受[hisher]的新力量啦！"

    old "We all dive in the water and enjoy a passionate embrace, laced with gentle caresses and kisses. Has anyone else in the entire world ever wound up in a situation like the one I'm now in? I'm a vampire. In a three-way relationship with two nagas. I could live several hundred years and probably never encounter a relationship as novel as this one."
    new "We all dive in the water and enjoy a passionate embrace, laced with gentle caresses and kisses. Has anyone else in the entire world ever wound up in a situation like the one I'm now in? I'm a vampire. In a three-way relationship with two nagas. I could live several hundred years and probably never encounter a relationship as novel as this one.\n我们一齐潜入水中，享受着一个交织着温柔爱抚与亲吻的热烈拥抱。世上可还有人落入过像我如今这般境地？我是个吸血鬼，与两个 naga 维系着三人关系。哪怕活上几百年，我恐怕也再遇不到比这更新奇的感情了。"

    old "I don't know what the future has in store for me, but for now, I'm enjoying this moment."
    new "I don't know what the future has in store for me, but for now, I'm enjoying this moment.\n我不知道未来会为我准备什么，但此刻，我正尽情享受当下。"

    old "Are you sure it's a good idea, [protag]?"
    new "Are you sure it's a good idea, [protag]?\n你确定这是个好主意吗，[protag]？"

    old "I was invited by elder druid Myrth in person. Relax, Sylrissa."
    new "I was invited by elder druid Myrth in person. Relax, Sylrissa.\n是德鲁伊长老 Myrth 亲自邀请我的。放轻松，Sylrissa。"

    old "So it's true that elves are much more open regarding polyamorous relationships?"
    new "So it's true that elves are much more open regarding polyamorous relationships?\n这么说，精灵对多伴侣关系确实开明得多？"

    old "Yes, it's true. I really think we're making the right decision."
    new "Yes, it's true. I really think we're making the right decision.\n是的，确实如此。我真心觉得我们做的决定没错。"

    old "Haha, the face of Apolimesho when you told him that we were coming with you."
    new "Haha, the face of Apolimesho when you told him that we were coming with you.\n哈哈，你告诉他我们也要同去时，Apolimesho 那副表情。"

    old "Well, being the ambassador of the Human Empire in Grandtree is a big responsibility. He probably figured out what was going on between the three of us, but he had the good sense not to ask questions he didn't want to know the answers to."
    new "Well, being the ambassador of the Human Empire in Grandtree is a big responsibility. He probably figured out what was going on between the three of us, but he had the good sense not to ask questions he didn't want to know the answers to.\n毕竟，担任人类帝国驻 Grandtree 的大使责任重大。他多半已猜出我们三人之间的关系，但他很识趣，没去追问那些他不想知道答案的问题。"

    old "I hope I can access the elven library while we're there."
    new "I hope I can access the elven library while we're there.\n希望我们在那儿时，我能进得去精灵图书馆。"

    old "Maybe not immediately, but I'm sure over time Myrth and the other elves will learn to trust you both."
    new "Maybe not immediately, but I'm sure over time Myrth and the other elves will learn to trust you both.\n也许不会立刻如愿，但我相信，假以时日，Myrth 和其他精灵会学会信任你们俩的。"

    old "I will train with Kusho. I don't want my fighting skills to get rusty."
    new "I will train with Kusho. I don't want my fighting skills to get rusty.\n我要和 Kusho 一起训练。我可不想自己的战斗本领生疏了。"

    old "Considering how many assassination attempts my predecessor had, I think that is a good idea, Sylrissa."
    new "Considering how many assassination attempts my predecessor had, I think that is a good idea, Sylrissa.\n想想我的前任遭遇过多少次暗杀，这主意不错，Sylrissa。"

    old "And so here we are. We're at the gates of the biggest elven town of the area, Grandtree. I hold Enok's hand with my left hand and Sylrissa's hand with my right. I'm ready to begin this new chapter of my life, with both of them lovingly at my side."
    new "And so here we are. We're at the gates of the biggest elven town of the area, Grandtree. I hold Enok's hand with my left hand and Sylrissa's hand with my right. I'm ready to begin this new chapter of my life, with both of them lovingly at my side.\n于是我们来到了这里。我们站在这一带最大的精灵城镇 Grandtree 的城门前。我左手牵着 Enok，右手牵着 Sylrissa。我已准备好开启人生的新篇章，有他们俩满怀爱意地陪在身旁。"

    old "Enok and Sylrissa returned to the swamps to live out the rest of their days in peace. Though several cities within the Human Empire recognized them as heroes and extended them formal offers to become citizens, the two nagas ultimately decided that they were content to have only each other as company."
    new "Enok and Sylrissa returned to the swamps to live out the rest of their days in peace. Though several cities within the Human Empire recognized them as heroes and extended them formal offers to become citizens, the two nagas ultimately decided that they were content to have only each other as company.\nEnok 和 Sylrissa 回到沼泽，打算平静地度过余生。尽管人类帝国的几座城市都认可他们是英雄，并正式邀请他们入籍，这两个 naga 最终还是决定，只要有彼此作伴便已心满意足。"

    old "Occasionally, Enok and Sylrissa make brief appearances in Grimoire to visit friends or to purchase cooking ingredients for Enok."
    new "Occasionally, Enok and Sylrissa make brief appearances in Grimoire to visit friends or to purchase cooking ingredients for Enok.\n偶尔，Enok 和 Sylrissa 会到 Grimoire 短暂露面，拜访朋友，或是为 Enok 采买烹饪食材。"

    old "Although some Grimoire citizens were initially concerned that the presence of two nagas might frighten children in the city, Enok and Sylrissa turned out to be immensely popular with the children of Grimoire, who often ask to feel their scales when they make an appearance."
    new "Although some Grimoire citizens were initially concerned that the presence of two nagas might frighten children in the city, Enok and Sylrissa turned out to be immensely popular with the children of Grimoire, who often ask to feel their scales when they make an appearance.\n虽然起初有些 Grimoire 市民担心两个 naga 的出现会吓到城里的孩子，但事实证明，Enok 和 Sylrissa 极受 Grimoire 孩子们的欢迎，他们一露面，孩子们便常央求摸摸他们的鳞片。"

    old "After the battle of N'Mar, several elf groups invited Vaeril to GrandTree. Vaeril declined their invitation, and elected to stay in Grimoire, working in a city infirmary."
    new "After the battle of N'Mar, several elf groups invited Vaeril to GrandTree. Vaeril declined their invitation, and elected to stay in Grimoire, working in a city infirmary.\nN'Mar 之战后，有几个精灵团体邀请 Vaeril 前往 GrandTree。Vaeril 谢绝了邀请，选择留在 Grimoire，在城中一所医务室里工作。"

    old "After the battle of N'Mar, it became obvious that Vaeril wasn't the reason for the corruption of the Great Forest. He was forgiven and invited back to GrandTree. Vaeril declined their invitation, and elected to stay in Grimoire, working in a city infirmary."
    new "After the battle of N'Mar, it became obvious that Vaeril wasn't the reason for the corruption of the Great Forest. He was forgiven and invited back to GrandTree. Vaeril declined their invitation, and elected to stay in Grimoire, working in a city infirmary.\nN'Mar 之战后，人们终于明白，Vaeril 并非 Great Forest 腐化的元凶。他得到了谅解，并被邀请重返 GrandTree。Vaeril 谢绝了邀请，选择留在 Grimoire，在城中一所医务室里工作。"

    old "When asked why he chose to stay in the city rather than returning to the forest, Vaeril stated that Grimoire's poor and sick seemed to be the people most in need of his healing powers."
    new "When asked why he chose to stay in the city rather than returning to the forest, Vaeril stated that Grimoire's poor and sick seemed to be the people most in need of his healing powers.\n当被问及为何选择留在城市而不回森林时，Vaeril 表示，Grimoire 的穷人和病患似乎才是最需要他治愈之力的人。"

    old "I'm sorry, Vaeril. I feel as though you've lost something important because of me. You were starting to get along with the citizens of Grimoire, and... I feel like I forced you to leave because of what I've become."
    new "I'm sorry, Vaeril. I feel as though you've lost something important because of me. You were starting to get along with the citizens of Grimoire, and... I feel like I forced you to leave because of what I've become.\n对不起，Vaeril。我觉得你因为我失去了很重要的东西。你本来正渐渐和 Grimoire 的市民们处好关系，而……我总觉得是我变成这副样子，才逼得你离开。"

    old "It was my own choice, [protag]. I won't say that I was happy to leave behind my role at the infirmary, but...this is more important to me."
    new "It was my own choice, [protag]. I won't say that I was happy to leave behind my role at the infirmary, but...this is more important to me.\n那是我自己的选择，[protag]。我不会说离开医务室那份差事让我高兴，但……这对我来说更重要。"

    old "But once we reach Zoltar, what's the plan?"
    new "But once we reach Zoltar, what's the plan?\n可等我们到了 Zoltar，有什么打算？"

    old "Since our triumph against N'Mar, my name became rather famous. The fallen druid. The one who can heal any disease. God, sometimes I laugh when I hear such stories about me. They made me become a sort of legend."
    new "Since our triumph against N'Mar, my name became rather famous. The fallen druid. The one who can heal any disease. God, sometimes I laugh when I hear such stories about me. They made me become a sort of legend.\n自打我们在 N'Mar 凯旋，我的名字就变得颇有名气。堕落的德鲁伊，能治愈任何疾病的人。天哪，有时听到关于自己的这些传闻，我都不禁发笑。他们硬是把我传成了某种传奇。"

    old "The way you talk is making me start to feel a bit envious."
    new "The way you talk is making me start to feel a bit envious.\n你说话这口气，都让我开始有点嫉妒了。"

    old "Why? Your fame is much greater than mine. There's no legend greater than the one who became a vampire [himher]self to defeat the vampires of N'Mar."
    new "Why? Your fame is much greater than mine. There's no legend greater than the one who became a vampire [himher]self to defeat the vampires of N'Mar.\n为什么？你的名气可比我大多了。还有哪个传说，比得上为了击败 N'Mar 的吸血鬼而[himher]自身化作吸血鬼的那一位？"

    old "Yes, and that's what bothers me. That's the sort of notoriety that makes people start to fear you."
    new "Yes, and that's what bothers me. That's the sort of notoriety that makes people start to fear you.\n是啊，这正是让我烦恼的地方。正是那种名声，会让人们开始惧怕你。"

    old "It wouldn't bother me so much if it weren't for the fact that it's come to affect you, too. Now you have to hide just to be with me. You've been hiding for so long..."
    new "It wouldn't bother me so much if it weren't for the fact that it's come to affect you, too. Now you have to hide just to be with me. You've been hiding for so long...\n若不是它如今也牵连到了你，我倒不会这么介意。现在你为了和我在一起，不得不东躲西藏。你藏了那么久……"

    old "Exactly, [protag]. I have stayed hidden for most of my life. So when I say that I'm willing to go into hiding so that we can be together, I know what I'm talking about."
    new "Exactly, [protag]. I have stayed hidden for most of my life. So when I say that I'm willing to go into hiding so that we can be together, I know what I'm talking about.\n没错，[protag]。我大半辈子都在躲藏。所以当我说愿意为了我们在一起而继续隐匿时，我清楚自己在说什么。"

    old "Now that we're leaving behind Issanis, people will no longer recognize us. Tales of our adventures may make their way to Zoltar, but who will be able to look at us and realize that we're the one the legends are about? To them, we can just be two wanderers."
    new "Now that we're leaving behind Issanis, people will no longer recognize us. Tales of our adventures may make their way to Zoltar, but who will be able to look at us and realize that we're the one the legends are about? To them, we can just be two wanderers.\n如今我们离开 Issanis，人们不会再认出我们。我们的冒险故事或许会传到 Zoltar，但谁能看着我们，就认出我们正是传说里的那两位？在他们眼中，我们不过是两个流浪者。"

    old "Wanderers? Maybe...[pCharProf]s? That's what I was after all, before all of this began."
    new "Wanderers? Maybe...[pCharProf]s? That's what I was after all, before all of this began.\n流浪者？也许……是个[pCharProf]？说到底，在这一切开始之前，我就是那样的人。"

    old "If you prefer. What we'll pretend to be doesn't matter anyway. What matters is that here we can start a new life again, together. And the best part is, we've found a way to provide for your needs without needing to hurt anyone else."
    new "If you prefer. What we'll pretend to be doesn't matter anyway. What matters is that here we can start a new life again, together. And the best part is, we've found a way to provide for your needs without needing to hurt anyone else.\n随你高兴。我们假扮成什么并不重要。重要的是，在这里我们又能一起开始新生活。而最妙的是，我们已找到办法满足你的需求，不必再伤害任何人。"

    old "Indeed. Who would have thought that your life-channeling powers would make it possible for you to feed me from your own life force? I wonder if any other vampire has ever made the same discovery. I doubt it."
    new "Indeed. Who would have thought that your life-channeling powers would make it possible for you to feed me from your own life force? I wonder if any other vampire has ever made the same discovery. I doubt it.\n确实。谁能想到，你那导引生命的力量，竟能让你用自己的生命之力喂养我？我怀疑是否还有其他吸血鬼有过同样的发现。想必没有。"

    old "If that's what it takes to keep you from needing to kill to sate your vampiric hunger, then I'm more than willing to do it."
    new "If that's what it takes to keep you from needing to kill to sate your vampiric hunger, then I'm more than willing to do it.\n如果这样才能让你不必靠杀戮来满足吸血鬼的饥渴，那我非常乐意这么做。"

    old "Just make sure to stay well-fed. Remember, now you're eating for two."
    new "Just make sure to stay well-fed. Remember, now you're eating for two.\n你自己可要吃饱。记住，你现在是一个人吃、两个人补。"

    old "I suppose you're right."
    new "I suppose you're right.\n我想你说得对。"

    old "Vaeril looks out over the water, and I start to see a smile spread across his face. A smile of contentment. Vaeril doesn't smile often. But as I think about the life we have ahead of us, and the future we can now spend together, I think everything is going to be alright."
    new "Vaeril looks out over the water, and I start to see a smile spread across his face. A smile of contentment. Vaeril doesn't smile often. But as I think about the life we have ahead of us, and the future we can now spend together, I think everything is going to be alright.\nVaeril 眺望着水面，我看见一抹笑意在他脸上缓缓漾开——那是心满意足的笑容。Vaeril 不常笑。但想到我们即将共度的人生，想到如今能携手走过的未来，我觉得一切都会好起来。"

    old "I move in to hug Vaeril, and we share an embrace. He, the fallen druid. Me, the vampire. We are two misfits who don't belong anywhere in this world. But together, perhaps we can enjoy something resembling a normal life. But even if our life isn't going to be normal, I know I'm going to enjoy it, just as long as I have Vaeril by my side."
    new "I move in to hug Vaeril, and we share an embrace. He, the fallen druid. Me, the vampire. We are two misfits who don't belong anywhere in this world. But together, perhaps we can enjoy something resembling a normal life. But even if our life isn't going to be normal, I know I'm going to enjoy it, just as long as I have Vaeril by my side.\n我上前抱住 Vaeril，我们紧紧相拥。他，是堕落的德鲁伊；我，是吸血鬼。我们是两个与这世界格格不入的异类。但在一起，也许我们能过上某种近似寻常的日子。即便我们的生活不会寻常，我也知道我会乐在其中，只要有 Vaeril 陪在身边。"

    old "Are you ready, Vaeril?"
    new "Are you ready, Vaeril?\n准备好了吗，Vaeril？"

    old "Oh yes, [protag]! I'm almost done."
    new "Oh yes, [protag]! I'm almost done.\n哦，是啊，[protag]！我就快弄好了。"

    old "I'll wait for you outside."
    new "I'll wait for you outside.\n我到外面等你。"

    old "Months have passed, and Vaeril is still working at the infirmary of Grimoire. I was a bit annoyed at first, since I wanted to go away with him, to visit the world. Since the Council chose to renew my title as Envoy, I thought I would enjoy the opportunity to travel with the man I love."
    new "Months have passed, and Vaeril is still working at the infirmary of Grimoire. I was a bit annoyed at first, since I wanted to go away with him, to visit the world. Since the Council chose to renew my title as Envoy, I thought I would enjoy the opportunity to travel with the man I love.\n几个月过去，Vaeril 仍在 Grimoire 的医务室工作。起初我有些懊恼，因为我本想与他一同远行，去看看这世界。既然议会决定续封我的 Envoy 头衔，我原以为能借机和心爱之人一起旅行。"

    old "But it's become clear to me that Vaeril's work here is important to him. And it's part of what I love about him."
    new "But it's become clear to me that Vaeril's work here is important to him. And it's part of what I love about him.\n但我渐渐明白，Vaeril 在这里的工作对他很重要。而这正是我爱他的原因之一。"

    old "I'm finished! I'm here, [protag]. I'm sorry to have made you wait."
    new "I'm finished! I'm here, [protag]. I'm sorry to have made you wait.\n我忙完啦！我来了，[protag]。抱歉让你久等了。"

    old "The council has sent me to investigate the demons rumors on Everburn Mountains."
    new "The council has sent me to investigate the demons rumors on Everburn Mountains.\n议会派我去调查 Everburn Mountains 一带关于恶魔的传闻。"

    old "What? Are you sure you'll be safe?"
    new "What? Are you sure you'll be safe?\n什么？你确定自己会安全吗？"

    old "I think I can take care of myself...but I thought to myself, why take the chance? I should travel with someone. A companion, just in case I encounter trouble."
    new "I think I can take care of myself...but I thought to myself, why take the chance? I should travel with someone. A companion, just in case I encounter trouble.\n我想我照顾得了自己……不过我又转念一想，何必冒险？我该找个人同行。有个伴，万一遇到麻烦也好照应。"

    old "That sounds like an invitation."
    new "That sounds like an invitation.\n这话听起来像在邀请我。"

    old "Come on, Vaeril. Remember old times. Me and you, fighting the forces of evil."
    new "Come on, Vaeril. Remember old times. Me and you, fighting the forces of evil.\n来吧，Vaeril。想想从前。你和我，并肩对抗邪恶势力。"

    old "Vaeril remains silent, and I catch him stealing a glance at the infirmary beds behind us with a worried expression."
    new "Vaeril remains silent, and I catch him stealing a glance at the infirmary beds behind us with a worried expression.\nVaeril 沉默不语，我瞥见他面带忧色，偷偷望向我们身后的医务室病床。"

    old "I've spoken with several healers who have agreed to attend to your duties while you're away. One of them is someone you even know, Dasyra."
    new "I've spoken with several healers who have agreed to attend to your duties while you're away. One of them is someone you even know, Dasyra.\n我已经和几位治疗师谈过，他们都答应在你离开期间接手你的工作。其中一位你还认识——Dasyra。"

    old "Ah, well in that case, I suppose I have no reason to refuse. Is anyone else coming along?"
    new "Ah, well in that case, I suppose I have no reason to refuse. Is anyone else coming along?\n啊，既然如此，我想我也没有理由拒绝了。还有别人同行吗？"

    old "Kusho."
    new "Kusho.\nKusho。"

    old "Oh. Well, we're on speaking terms now, so-"
    new "Oh. Well, we're on speaking terms now, so-\n哦。嗯，我们现在能说得上话了，所以——"

    old "I'm joking, Vaeril. It'll just be me and you. It's only a reconnaissance mission, we don't want our group to be too large."
    new "I'm joking, Vaeril. It'll just be me and you. It's only a reconnaissance mission, we don't want our group to be too large.\n我开玩笑的，Vaeril。就我和你。这只是一次侦察任务，我们不想队伍太庞大。"

    old "I see. I hope the rumors I've heard about demons around Everburn aren't true."
    new "I see. I hope the rumors I've heard about demons around Everburn aren't true.\n我明白了。但愿我听说的那些关于 Everburn 一带恶魔的传闻不是真的。"

    old "Even if they are, I don't have anything to fear when you're at my side, Vaeril. I couldn't ask for a better travel companion."
    new "Even if they are, I don't have anything to fear when you're at my side, Vaeril. I couldn't ask for a better travel companion.\n就算是真的，只要有你在我身边，我也没什么好怕的，Vaeril。我再找不到比你更好的旅伴了。"

    old "Vaeril smiles at me. He still doesn't take compliments well. I give him a kiss on the cheek, and take his hand in mine as we begin walking toward our newest adventure. It'll be just me, Vaeril, and whatever awaits us en Everburn. I can't wait."
    new "Vaeril smiles at me. He still doesn't take compliments well. I give him a kiss on the cheek, and take his hand in mine as we begin walking toward our newest adventure. It'll be just me, Vaeril, and whatever awaits us en Everburn. I can't wait.\nVaeril 朝我微笑。他还是不习惯别人夸他。我在他脸颊上亲了一下，牵起他的手，一同走向我们最新的冒险。这一路只有我、Vaeril，还有 Everburn 上等待着我们的一切。我已经迫不及待了。"

    old "Leena resumed her duties as amazon Guard Captain. At Loren's request, Leena began training young Breza, and the two young amazons began showing great promise under Leena's tutelage."
    new "Leena resumed her duties as amazon Guard Captain. At Loren's request, Leena began training young Breza, and the two young amazons began showing great promise under Leena's tutelage.\nLeena 重新担起了 amazon 卫队队长的职责。应 Loren 之请，Leena 开始训练年轻的 Breza，这两个年轻的 amazon 在 Leena 的教导下展现出了巨大的潜力。"

    old "After some badgering from the princess, Leena allowed Loren to practice dual wielding, and soon Leena recognized in Loren a great potential which she hoped might one day surpass her own skill."
    new "After some badgering from the princess, Leena allowed Loren to practice dual wielding, and soon Leena recognized in Loren a great potential which she hoped might one day surpass her own skill.\n经不住公主的软磨硬泡，Leena 答应了让 Loren 练习双持武器。不久，Leena 便在 Loren 身上看到了巨大的潜力，并希望有朝一日她能超越自己的身手。"

    old "I spot Leena running towards me. I welcome her in my arms, but I start crying when I think of what she's giving up to come with me."
    new "I spot Leena running towards me. I welcome her in my arms, but I start crying when I think of what she's giving up to come with me.\n我看见 Leena 朝我跑来。我把她迎入怀中，可一想到她为了跟我走而放弃了什么，泪水便涌了出来。"

    old "Leena, you can't do this. You can still go back! It's not too late. You can still go back to the Citadel and keep your title and your...family."
    new "Leena, you can't do this. You can still go back! It's not too late. You can still go back to the Citadel and keep your title and your...family.\nLeena，你不能这么做。你还能回去的！现在还不算晚。你还能回 Citadel，保住你的头衔，还有你的……家人。"

    old "You're my family now, [protag]."
    new "You're my family now, [protag].\n现在你就是我的家人，[protag]。"

    old "But... you're renouncing everything to be with me."
    new "But... you're renouncing everything to be with me.\n可是……你为了和我在一起，抛弃了一切。"

    old "Yes, [protag]. I'm doing it to be with you. And that's why I'm fine with doing it. So stop crying, and let me feel like I'm doing the right thing."
    new "Yes, [protag]. I'm doing it to be with you. And that's why I'm fine with doing it. So stop crying, and let me feel like I'm doing the right thing.\n是的，[protag]。我这么做，就是为了和你在一起。正因为如此，我才心甘情愿。所以别哭了，让我觉得自己做的是对的。"

    old "I shake my head, and try to smile through the tears. For a moment, I briefly dwell on the fact that for all of the thing I've lost by becoming a vampire, I at least haven't lost the ability to cry."
    new "I shake my head, and try to smile through the tears. For a moment, I briefly dwell on the fact that for all of the thing I've lost by becoming a vampire, I at least haven't lost the ability to cry.\n我摇摇头，试着透过泪水微笑。有那么一瞬，我心想：变成吸血鬼后我失去了那么多，但至少，我还没失去哭泣的能力。"

    old "You know there's no other solution. Karen would have never let you enter the Citadel, no matter how close you were before you...decided to become a vampire."
    new "You know there's no other solution. Karen would have never let you enter the Citadel, no matter how close you were before you...decided to become a vampire.\n你知道没有别的办法。Karen 绝不会让你踏入 Citadel，无论在你……决定变成吸血鬼之前，你们曾有多亲近。"

    old "I can't just give up the feelings I have for you. If I could, I would. But I can't. So let me do this, [protag]. I want to be with you. The least you can do is respect that choice."
    new "I can't just give up the feelings I have for you. If I could, I would. But I can't. So let me do this, [protag]. I want to be with you. The least you can do is respect that choice.\n我无法就这样放弃对你的感情。若能放弃，我早就放弃了。可我不能。所以就让我这么做吧，[protag]。我想和你在一起。你至少可以尊重这个选择。"

    old "What are we going to do now?"
    new "What are we going to do now?\n我们现在该怎么办？"

    old "We'll move away somewhere. I know that I'm committing an act of treason against the amazons by abandoning them to be with you, and the fact that you and I are both heroes won't protect me against their laws."
    new "We'll move away somewhere. I know that I'm committing an act of treason against the amazons by abandoning them to be with you, and the fact that you and I are both heroes won't protect me against their laws.\n我们找个地方远走高飞。我知道，抛下族人跟你走，对 amazons 而言是叛国行径，即便你我都算英雄，也护不住我、逃不过他们的律法。"

    old "The way you speak of 'their laws' makes it sound as though you no longer consider yourself one of the amazons."
    new "The way you speak of 'their laws' makes it sound as though you no longer consider yourself one of the amazons.\n你口口声声说“他们的律法”，听起来好像你已不再把自己当作 amazon 中的一员。"

    old "I'd rather be with you than be one of the amazons. Let's move, [protag]. We can think about a long-term solution. But for now, let's just go away from here."
    new "I'd rather be with you than be one of the amazons. Let's move, [protag]. We can think about a long-term solution. But for now, let's just go away from here.\n比起当 amazon，我更愿意和你在一起。我们走吧，[protag]。长远之计可以慢慢想，但眼下，先离开这里。"

    old "We head in the direction of Grimoire. I know a few places where we can hide for a few days, provided we keep a low profile."
    new "We head in the direction of Grimoire. I know a few places where we can hide for a few days, provided we keep a low profile.\n我们朝 Grimoire 的方向进发。我知道几个能躲上几天的地方，只要保持低调就行。"

    old "As we move, I find myself frequently slowing to allow Leena to keep pace. It's easy to forget how much faster I move as a vampire. I'm sure Leena is pissed off about this, as she was always faster and more agile than me before my transformation."
    new "As we move, I find myself frequently slowing to allow Leena to keep pace. It's easy to forget how much faster I move as a vampire. I'm sure Leena is pissed off about this, as she was always faster and more agile than me before my transformation.\n一路上，我发现自己总得放慢速度等 Leena 跟上。人们很容易忘记，变成吸血鬼后我的速度有多快。Leena 一定为此很恼火，毕竟在我蜕变之前，她一向比我更快、更敏捷。"

    old "Let's stop a moment, you need to catch breath."
    new "Let's stop a moment, you need to catch breath.\n我们停一下，你得喘口气。"

    old "I'm fine."
    new "I'm fine.\n我没事。"

    old "No you aren't."
    new "No you aren't.\n不，你有事。"

    old "Alright, I'll take a rest. But [protag], I'm fine."
    new "Alright, I'll take a rest. But [protag], I'm fine.\n好吧，我歇一下。不过 [protag]，我真的没事。"

    old "We'll be fine."
    new "We'll be fine.\n我们会没事的。"

    old "I look into her eyes, and see the sparkle of hope in them. Perhaps there is hope for us yet."
    new "I look into her eyes, and see the sparkle of hope in them. Perhaps there is hope for us yet.\n我凝视着她的眼睛，看见其中闪烁的希望之光。也许，我们之间仍有希望。"

    old "I've spent a long time trying to convince myself that it will be fine. It's been a struggle. But when I hear you say it, Leena, I believe it."
    new "I've spent a long time trying to convince myself that it will be fine. It's been a struggle. But when I hear you say it, Leena, I believe it.\n我花了很长时间试图说服自己一切都会好起来。那很煎熬。可当我听你这么说时，Leena，我相信了。"

    old "Leena..."
    new "Leena...\nLeena……"

    old "Shh, [protag]. You don't have to say anything."
    new "Shh, [protag]. You don't have to say anything.\n嘘，[protag]。你什么都不必说。"

    old "Leena leans in and kisses me. I find my breath catching, and Leena's kiss reminds me what it's like to feel again."
    new "Leena leans in and kisses me. I find my breath catching, and Leena's kiss reminds me what it's like to feel again.\nLeena 俯身吻了我。我的呼吸不觉一窒，Leena 的吻让我再次想起“感受”是怎样的滋味。"

    old "It's a reminder that whatever life I have now, it's still one worth living."
    new "It's a reminder that whatever life I have now, it's still one worth living.\n它提醒着我，无论如今过着怎样的生活，这生活都依然值得过下去。"

    old "You know, if we keep stopping like this, we're never going to make it to Grimoire in time."
    new "You know, if we keep stopping like this, we're never going to make it to Grimoire in time.\n你知道的，再这样走走停停，我们怕是永远也赶不到 Grimoire 了。"

    old "Why bother with Grimoire? We're far enough from the citadel now. We can resume our travels tomorrow. Let's spend the night here."
    new "Why bother with Grimoire? We're far enough from the citadel now. We can resume our travels tomorrow. Let's spend the night here.\n何必非去 Grimoire？我们现在离 Citadel 已经够远了。明天再继续赶路也不迟。今晚就在这儿过夜吧。"

    old "Leena and I prepare to spend the night together, though I get the feeling that we won't be getting much strength."
    new "Leena and I prepare to spend the night together, though I get the feeling that we won't be getting much strength.\n我和 Leena 准备一起过夜，不过我总觉得，这一晚我们怕是恢复不了多少体力。"

    old "Forging a new life together with Leena will not be easy. But neither Leena nor I are the sort to embrace the sort of tame and easy way of doing things."
    new "Forging a new life together with Leena will not be easy. But neither Leena nor I are the sort to embrace the sort of tame and easy way of doing things.\n与 Leena 一起开创新生活并不容易。但我和 Leena 都不是那种安于平淡、图省事的人。"

    old "I'm not sure what the future holds. What I do know is that I love Leena. And if she was willing to give up everything to be with me, her feelings must be just as strong. What more could I possibly ask for?"
    new "I'm not sure what the future holds. What I do know is that I love Leena. And if she was willing to give up everything to be with me, her feelings must be just as strong. What more could I possibly ask for?\n我不确定未来会怎样。我确知的只有一点：我爱 Leena。而她既然甘愿放弃一切与我在一起，她的感情想必同样强烈。我还能再奢求什么呢？"

    old "The crowd around me cheers as queen Karen enters the square. I'm on my knees, awaiting Karen's blessings."
    new "The crowd around me cheers as queen Karen enters the square. I'm on my knees, awaiting Karen's blessings.\n当 Karen 女王步入广场时，我四周的人群欢呼起来。我跪在地上，等待 Karen 的祝福。"

    old "Amazon citizens! Today, I give [protag] the amazon citizenship. [HeShe] is now officially one of us."
    new "Amazon citizens! Today, I give [protag] the amazon citizenship. [HeShe] is now officially one of us.\nAmazon 的公民们！今天，我授予 [protag] amazon 公民身份。[HeShe]如今正式成为我们中的一员。"

    old "Karen moves a sword above my head following a ritual pattern, and then continues."
    new "Karen moves a sword above my head following a ritual pattern, and then continues.\nKaren 按仪式动作将一把剑在我头顶挥过，随后继续致辞。"

    old "But today, we're here to celebrate more than the addition of another citizen. We're here to celebrate the joining of two people."
    new "But today, we're here to celebrate more than the addition of another citizen. We're here to celebrate the joining of two people.\n但今天，我们要庆祝的不只是又添了一位公民。我们要庆祝的，是两个人的结合。"

    old "I squeeze Leena's hand, and she squeeze's my hand back. I feel my heart pounding in my chest as we gaze into each other's eyes, as Karen presides over us."
    new "I squeeze Leena's hand, and she squeeze's my hand back. I feel my heart pounding in my chest as we gaze into each other's eyes, as Karen presides over us.\n我捏了捏 Leena 的手，她也回捏了我的手。当我们四目相对，Karen 在旁主持时，我感觉到自己的心在胸膛里怦怦直跳。"

    old "Leena, our heroic guard captain, and [protag], the hero of the battle of N'Mar, have shared many victories. Now, they prepare to share the ultimate victory, a life together. Let all here today witness the forging of the bond of marriage between these two!"
    new "Leena, our heroic guard captain, and [protag], the hero of the battle of N'Mar, have shared many victories. Now, they prepare to share the ultimate victory, a life together. Let all here today witness the forging of the bond of marriage between these two!\nLeena，我们英勇的卫队长，与 N'Mar 之战的英雄 [protag]，已共同赢得了许多胜利。如今，他们将共同迎接最终的胜利——携手共度一生。让今天在座的诸位，一同见证这二人缔结婚姻的盟约！"

    old "May your love be as strong as your armor, and the bonds of marriage as strong as your blades. Leena, [protag], rise."
    new "May your love be as strong as your armor, and the bonds of marriage as strong as your blades. Leena, [protag], rise.\n愿你们的爱如铠甲般坚固，愿婚姻的纽带如刀剑般坚韧。Leena，[protag]，起身吧。"

    old "Leena and I stand up and the crowd around us falls silent."
    new "Leena and I stand up and the crowd around us falls silent.\n我和 Leena 站起身来，四周的人群安静下来。"

    old "What are you two waiting for? Kiss!"
    new "What are you two waiting for? Kiss!\n你们两个还等什么？亲一个！"

    old "The crowd erupts into cheers. In a way, it feels a bit embarrassing to share such an intimate moment in front of everyone, but it fills my heart with joy to know that the love I share with Leena is being vindicated by amazon tradition. An amazon tradition that I'm now a part of."
    new "The crowd erupts into cheers. In a way, it feels a bit embarrassing to share such an intimate moment in front of everyone, but it fills my heart with joy to know that the love I share with Leena is being vindicated by amazon tradition. An amazon tradition that I'm now a part of.\n人群爆发出欢呼。在众人面前分享如此亲密的时刻，多少有些难为情，但得知我与 Leena 的爱情得到了 amazon 传统的认可，我的心仍满是喜悦。而如今，我也是这传统的一部分了。"

    old "Leena, from now until the day I die, I will love you."
    new "Leena, from now until the day I die, I will love you.\nLeena，从今往后，直到我死去的那一天，我都会爱你。"

    old "I can't think of anyone I would rather spend the rest of my life with."
    new "I can't think of anyone I would rather spend the rest of my life with.\n我想不出还有谁，是我更愿与之共度余生的人。"

    old "After the success in N'Mar, Jasper received a personal invitation from Apolimesho to work with the council."
    new "After the success in N'Mar, Jasper received a personal invitation from Apolimesho to work with the council.\nN'Mar 一战告捷后，Jasper 收到了 Apolimesho 的亲自邀请，邀他与议会共事。"

    old "According to official council records, Jasper politely refused the offer. According to those who witnessed the meeting in person, the refusal was slightly less than polite, as Jasper's stated reason for refusing the offer was that he felt more safe and free with the Bastards Of The Sea than with 'the bastards of the Council.'"
    new "According to official council records, Jasper politely refused the offer. According to those who witnessed the meeting in person, the refusal was slightly less than polite, as Jasper's stated reason for refusing the offer was that he felt more safe and free with the Bastards Of The Sea than with 'the bastards of the Council.'\n据议会官方记录，Jasper 礼貌地回绝了这一邀请。而据亲眼目睹那次会面的人说，他的回绝可远谈不上礼貌，因为他给出的拒绝理由是：与 Bastards Of The Sea 在一起，比和“议会的那些混蛋”在一起更安全、更自在。"

    old "Those on the council say it is 'unlikely' that Jasper would be extended a similar offer in the future."
    new "Those on the council say it is 'unlikely' that Jasper would be extended a similar offer in the future.\n议会中的人表示，将来“不太可能”再向 Jasper 发出类似的邀请。"

    old "After the events of N'Mar, rumors spread that the 'Bastards Of The Sea', a pirate group led by Senya, started roaming the waters around N'Mar, looking for possible treasures."
    new "After the events of N'Mar, rumors spread that the 'Bastards Of The Sea', a pirate group led by Senya, started roaming the waters around N'Mar, looking for possible treasures.\nN'Mar 事件之后，有传言说，由 Senya 率领的海盗团伙 Bastards Of The Sea 开始在 N'Mar 附近水域游弋，搜寻可能的宝藏。"

    old "It only took a few mysterious disappearances of their crew to change their mind and sail for safer waters."
    new "It only took a few mysterious disappearances of their crew to change their mind and sail for safer waters.\n没过多久，他们便有数名船员神秘失踪，这足以让他们改变主意，驶向更安全的水域。"

    old "Are you sure you're fine with joining me, Jasper?"
    new "Are you sure you're fine with joining me, Jasper?\n你确定愿意跟我走吗，Jasper？"

    old "Of course. Shacklesplit sounds like the perfect place for us to start a new life."
    new "Of course. Shacklesplit sounds like the perfect place for us to start a new life.\n当然。Shacklesplit 听起来是我们开始新生活的绝佳之地。"

    old "I've been there a few times before in my previous line of work, and it was a pretty open minded town, but I am not sure if they'll accept me as I am now..."
    new "I've been there a few times before in my previous line of work, and it was a pretty open minded town, but I am not sure if they'll accept me as I am now...\n我以前干那行时去过几次，那是个相当开明的镇子，但我不确定他们能否接受如今的我……"

    old "There's only a way to find out."
    new "There's only a way to find out.\n只有去了才知道。"

    old "What if we don't like the answer we find? What if they run us out of town?"
    new "What if we don't like the answer we find? What if they run us out of town?\n要是我们得到的答案不尽人意呢？要是他们把我们赶出镇子呢？"

    old "Then we'll keep looking."
    new "Then we'll keep looking.\n那我们就继续找。"

    old "We might never find a place that welcomes my kind. Vampires are not well-liked."
    new "We might never find a place that welcomes my kind. Vampires are not well-liked.\n我们也许永远找不到一个欢迎我这种人的地方。吸血鬼并不讨人喜欢。"

    old "Jasper comes close and I can hear his heart beating. For a moment, I can almost imagine the sound of my own heart beating with the same rhythm. But that's not possible anymore."
    new "Jasper comes close and I can hear his heart beating. For a moment, I can almost imagine the sound of my own heart beating with the same rhythm. But that's not possible anymore.\nJasper 走近前来，我能听见他的心跳。有那么一瞬，我几乎能想象自己的心也以同样的节拍跳动。可那已不再可能。"

    old "Look, I know it won't be easy. But we'll keep looking and even if we will never find a place to stay, what does it matter? We will always have the open sea. And more importantly, we will always have each other."
    new "Look, I know it won't be easy. But we'll keep looking and even if we will never find a place to stay, what does it matter? We will always have the open sea. And more importantly, we will always have each other.\n听着，我知道这不容易。但我们会一直找下去，即便永远找不到落脚之处，又有什么关系？我们永远拥有广阔的大海。更重要的是，我们永远拥有彼此。"

    old "I feel a tear run down my cheek. Jasper's loyalty knows no bounds."
    new "I feel a tear run down my cheek. Jasper's loyalty knows no bounds.\n我感到一滴泪滑过脸颊。Jasper 的忠诚没有止境。"

    old "I can't believe you'd do this for me, Jasper."
    new "I can't believe you'd do this for me, Jasper.\n我简直不敢相信你会为我做到这个地步，Jasper。"

    old "You'd better start believing, [protag]. I told you before that I was committed to what we share together. This is what that commitment looks like."
    new "You'd better start believing, [protag]. I told you before that I was committed to what we share together. This is what that commitment looks like.\n你最好开始相信，[protag]。我早就说过，我对我们之间的一切矢志不渝。这份矢志不渝，就是现在这个样子。"

    old "What kind of life will we live together, though?"
    new "What kind of life will we live together, though?\n那我们以后会过上怎样的生活呢？"

    old "A good one. Even if all we have is each other, we'll make a good life. I'm sure of it."
    new "A good one. Even if all we have is each other, we'll make a good life. I'm sure of it.\n好生活。即便我们拥有的只有彼此，我们也能过出好日子。我确信。"

    old "I hold his hand, and together we watch the sea. The sun is starting to set. Maybe Jasper is right after all. Maybe all of this will work."
    new "I hold his hand, and together we watch the sea. The sun is starting to set. Maybe Jasper is right after all. Maybe all of this will work.\n我握住他的手，一同眺望大海。夕阳开始西沉。也许 Jasper 终究是对的。也许这一切都会好起来。"

    old "What's the next stop, Jasper?"
    new "What's the next stop, Jasper?\n下一站是哪儿，Jasper？"

    old "Hesperos, Locutia Islands."
    new "Hesperos, Locutia Islands.\nHesperos，Locutia Islands。"

    old "Far, far from Grimoire. It'll be a long trip."
    new "Far, far from Grimoire. It'll be a long trip.\n离 Grimoire 远得很。这会是段漫长的旅程。"

    old "I'm afraid so. It's not like you can choose where to go, [protag]. I told you to reject the offer when they chose to have you continue to act as Envoy, but you didn't listen."
    new "I'm afraid so. It's not like you can choose where to go, [protag]. I told you to reject the offer when they chose to have you continue to act as Envoy, but you didn't listen.\n恐怕是的。这可由不得你挑，[protag]。当初他们让你继续担任 Envoy 时，我就劝你回绝，可你不听。"

    old "They're paying me very well now, Jasper. They made me an offer I couldn't refuse!"
    new "They're paying me very well now, Jasper. They made me an offer I couldn't refuse!\n他们现在给我的报酬十分丰厚，Jasper。他们开出的条件，我实在无法拒绝！"

    old "Hmpf. I have to admit that the pay is good, yes."
    new "Hmpf. I have to admit that the pay is good, yes.\n哼。这我倒得承认，报酬确实不错。"

    old "I know it's not the way that you would choose to live your life, Jasper. But this way, both you and I can do what we want. And you don't have to be a pirate any longer."
    new "I know it's not the way that you would choose to live your life, Jasper. But this way, both you and I can do what we want. And you don't have to be a pirate any longer.\n我知道这不是你会选择的生活方式，Jasper。但这样一来，你我都能做自己想做的事。而你也不必再当海盗了。"

    old "You say that as if it's a good thing."
    new "You say that as if it's a good thing.\n你这话说得，好像那是件好事似的。"

    old "It is a good thing. Because now we have more time to spend together. Besides, even if you're no longer a pirate, you still make a fine navigator."
    new "It is a good thing. Because now we have more time to spend together. Besides, even if you're no longer a pirate, you still make a fine navigator.\n那确实是好事。因为现在我们能一起度过更多时光。再说，就算你不再是海盗，你依然是个出色的领航员。"

    old "Ha, I guess I'll have to settle for being the Envoy's navigator, then."
    new "Ha, I guess I'll have to settle for being the Envoy's navigator, then.\n哈，那我只好认命，当 Envoy 的领航员了。"

    old "Hopefully that will be enough to quell your spirit of adventure."
    new "Hopefully that will be enough to quell your spirit of adventure.\n希望这足以平息你那股冒险劲儿。"

    old "Being a glorified tour guide isn't much of an adventure, [protag]. But if it's with you, I think it's something that I'll be happy to do."
    new "Being a glorified tour guide isn't much of an adventure, [protag]. But if it's with you, I think it's something that I'll be happy to do.\n当个被捧上天的向导，可算不上什么冒险，[protag]。但若是和你一起，我想我会乐意为之。"

    old "Oh, but you'll be much more than a glorified tour guide, Jasper. Why, I'll need you at my side if anyone comes to make an attempt on my life. Haven't you heard? The Locutia Islands are in chaos, and it's believed that Rogan is behind the assassination of the last Envoy the empire sent."
    new "Oh, but you'll be much more than a glorified tour guide, Jasper. Why, I'll need you at my side if anyone comes to make an attempt on my life. Haven't you heard? The Locutia Islands are in chaos, and it's believed that Rogan is behind the assassination of the last Envoy the empire sent.\n哦，但你绝不只是个被捧上天的向导，Jasper。要是有人来行刺，我还得靠你在身边护我。你没听说吗？Locutia Islands 如今一片混乱，据说帝国派去的上一任 Envoy 遇刺，幕后黑手就是 Rogan。"

    old "I guess we'll never be done fighting."
    new "I guess we'll never be done fighting.\n看来我们永远摆脱不了争斗。"

    old "We can always hope, Jasper. But something tells me that if it does come to fighting, you'll be up to the challenge."
    new "We can always hope, Jasper. But something tells me that if it does come to fighting, you'll be up to the challenge.\n我们总可以心怀希望，Jasper。不过我有种预感，若真到了动手的地步，你定能应付得来。"

    old "I'm always up for a challenge. But I think the biggest challenge will be figuring out what to do with all of this free time now that most of our days will be spent traveling."
    new "I'm always up for a challenge. But I think the biggest challenge will be figuring out what to do with all of this free time now that most of our days will be spent traveling.\n我向来乐于迎接挑战。但我想，最大的挑战是——如今我们大多数日子都在赶路，得琢磨怎么打发这大把的空闲时间。"

    old "I have a few ideas..."
    new "I have a few ideas...\n我倒有几个主意……"

    old "Jasper comes closer and whispers into my ear."
    new "Jasper comes closer and whispers into my ear.\nJasper 凑近过来，在我耳边低语。"

    old "I hope you're thinking what I'm thinking. Why don't we go below deck to...relax a little?"
    new "I hope you're thinking what I'm thinking. Why don't we go below deck to...relax a little?\n希望你和我想的是同一件事。我们何不到甲板下面……放松一下？"

    old "I smile and nod, and Jasper and I head down to the hold. Our trip will be a long one, and a risky one. But with Jasper beside me, I think I'm ready for whatever danger might be ahead of us, and I know that I'll never get bored."
    new "I smile and nod, and Jasper and I head down to the hold. Our trip will be a long one, and a risky one. But with Jasper beside me, I think I'm ready for whatever danger might be ahead of us, and I know that I'll never get bored.\n我微笑着点点头，和 Jasper 一起下到船舱。这趟旅程漫长而又凶险。但有 Jasper 在身边，我想我已准备好面对前方的一切危险，也知道自己绝不会感到无聊。"

    old "After the battle of N'Mar, Nuala returned to the dunes to serve Larik and her people. Tales of her achievements spread throughout the Empire and beyond, and soon it became difficult to distinguish rumor and legend from fact."
    new "After the battle of N'Mar, Nuala returned to the dunes to serve Larik and her people. Tales of her achievements spread throughout the Empire and beyond, and soon it became difficult to distinguish rumor and legend from fact.\nN'Mar 之战后，Nuala 回到沙丘，为 Larik 和她的人民效力。她的功绩传遍了帝国内外，很快，流言、传说与事实便难以分辨。"

    old "People swear to have seen her regularly move away from the camp during the night, and turn herself into a beautiful desert cat to run freely amongst the dunes."
    new "People swear to have seen her regularly move away from the camp during the night, and turn herself into a beautiful desert cat to run freely amongst the dunes.\n人们赌咒发誓，说常看见她在夜里离开营地，把自己变成一只美丽的沙漠猫，在沙丘间自由奔跑。"

    old "I'm sorry to have broken your heart, Nuala."
    new "I'm sorry to have broken your heart, Nuala.\n很抱歉伤了你的心，Nuala。"

    old "I only came here to say goodbye to you, [protag]."
    new "I only came here to say goodbye to you, [protag].\n我来，只是想跟你道别，[protag]。"

    old "I...understand. I am happy to have the opportunity to say you goodbye too."
    new "I...understand. I am happy to have the opportunity to say you goodbye too.\n我……明白。我也很高兴能有这个机会向你道别。"

    old "Are you alright, Nuala? It looks as though you're limping."
    new "Are you alright, Nuala? It looks as though you're limping.\n你没事吧，Nuala？你好像一瘸一拐的。"

    old "Today I fought some orcs. We won, but we suffered losses. I was struck in the leg."
    new "Today I fought some orcs. We won, but we suffered losses. I was struck in the leg.\n今天我和一些 orcs 交过手。我们赢了，但也折损了人手。我的腿挨了一下。"

    old "She shows me her leg. A the wound is still open, and I can smell the blood. The delicious smell of human blood."
    new "She shows me her leg. A the wound is still open, and I can smell the blood. The delicious smell of human blood.\n她让我看她的腿。伤口还开着，我闻到了血腥味——人类血液那诱人的气味。"

    old "Nuala raises her gaze at me, like waiting for me to do something. I move closer to her in an instant and grab her hand. The hand where she's holding her staff."
    new "Nuala raises her gaze at me, like waiting for me to do something. I move closer to her in an instant and grab her hand. The hand where she's holding her staff.\nNuala 抬眼看我，像是在等我做点什么。我瞬间凑近她，抓住她的手——那只握着法杖的手。"

    old "You're under my control now. I could kill you if I wanted."
    new "You're under my control now. I could kill you if I wanted.\n你现在在我的掌控之下。我若要杀你，易如反掌。"

    old "And what do you intend to do with that control?"
    new "And what do you intend to do with that control?\n那你打算用这份掌控做些什么？"

    old "I lean in and kiss her on the lips. The kiss lasts only for a moment, but as I pull away, I see Nuala smiling at me."
    new "I lean in and kiss her on the lips. The kiss lasts only for a moment, but as I pull away, I see Nuala smiling at me.\n我俯身吻上她的唇。这一吻只持续片刻，但当我退开时，看见 Nuala 正对我微笑。"

    old "So, your bloodlust isn't so insatiable after all."
    new "So, your bloodlust isn't so insatiable after all.\n看来，你的嗜血之欲也并非那么难以餍足嘛。"

    old "Is that what this is? Some sort of test?"
    new "Is that what this is? Some sort of test?\n原来如此？这算某种考验？"

    old "Yes, I was testing you. Can you blame me? Seeing someone turned to a vampire is not an easy thing to deal with, [protag]. I had to be sure. I had to be sure that you wouldn't lose control."
    new "Yes, I was testing you. Can you blame me? Seeing someone turned to a vampire is not an easy thing to deal with, [protag]. I had to be sure. I had to be sure that you wouldn't lose control.\n是的，我在考验你。你能怪我吗？眼睁睁看着一个人变成吸血鬼，可不是件容易接受的事，[protag]。我必须确认。必须确认你不会失控。"

    old "I see Nuala's fierce and passionate eyes."
    new "I see Nuala's fierce and passionate eyes.\n我看见 Nuala 那双炽烈而热情的眼睛。"

    old "Well then, don't you think I've passed your little test?"
    new "Well then, don't you think I've passed your little test?\n那么，你不觉得我已经通过你的小小考验了吗？"

    old "You were able to resist the scent of my blood...but apparently my charm is too alluring for you to resist the chance to kiss me."
    new "You were able to resist the scent of my blood...but apparently my charm is too alluring for you to resist the chance to kiss me.\n你抵抗住了我血液的气味……但显然，我的魅力太过诱人，让你无法抗拒吻我的机会。"

    old "Well, can you blame me?"
    new "Well, can you blame me?\n那你能怪我吗？"

    old "No, I suppose not."
    new "No, I suppose not.\n不能，我想不能。"

    old "This time, it's Nuala who leans in to kiss me."
    new "This time, it's Nuala who leans in to kiss me.\n这一次，是 Nuala 俯身来吻我。"

    old "I guess that makes two of us."
    new "I guess that makes two of us.\n我想，这让我们俩扯平了。"

    old "I'm not sure what exactly it is that you've become, [protag]. But I'm willing to continue our relationship, however odd it may be."
    new "I'm not sure what exactly it is that you've become, [protag]. But I'm willing to continue our relationship, however odd it may be.\n我不确定你究竟变成了什么，[protag]。但我愿意继续我们之间的关系，不管它有多么奇特。"

    old "I'd like that, Nuala."
    new "I'd like that, Nuala.\n我很乐意，Nuala。"

    old "We hug each other, and behind her I see Sheeba. Sheeba then seems to almost nod in approval and then leaves."
    new "We hug each other, and behind her I see Sheeba. Sheeba then seems to almost nod in approval and then leaves.\n我们相拥在一起，在她身后，我看见了 Sheeba。Sheeba 似乎几乎点了点头表示赞许，随后便离开了。"

    old "I'm not sure if Nuala fully trusts me yet. But it seems that she's willing to give it a try. And I'll do everything that I can to make her happy. Whatever kind of relationship it is, I know that it's something that I want to cling to, no matter the cost."
    new "I'm not sure if Nuala fully trusts me yet. But it seems that she's willing to give it a try. And I'll do everything that I can to make her happy. Whatever kind of relationship it is, I know that it's something that I want to cling to, no matter the cost.\n我不确定 Nuala 是否已完全信任我。但她似乎愿意一试。而我会竭尽全力让她幸福。不管这是怎样一种关系，我都知道，这是我无论如何都想紧紧抓住的东西。"

    old "Larik raises his axe to the sky and yells. It's a deep, passionate, bellowing yell."
    new "Larik raises his axe to the sky and yells. It's a deep, passionate, bellowing yell.\nLarik 把斧头举向天空，放声长啸。那一声深沉而激昂，响彻天地。"

    old "The Dunemarchers welcome you, [protag] as the new groom for Nuala the shaman."
    new "The Dunemarchers welcome you, [protag] as the new groom for Nuala the shaman.\nDunemarchers 欢迎你，[protag]，成为萨满 Nuala 的新郎。"

    old "The Dunemarchers welcome you, [protag] as the new bride for Nuala the shaman."
    new "The Dunemarchers welcome you, [protag] as the new bride for Nuala the shaman.\nDunemarchers 欢迎你，[protag]，成为萨满 Nuala 的新娘。"

    old "Nuala looks absolutely radiant today. Her beauty on any day is striking, but today is a particularly special day. She grabs me by the arm and pulls me away from the center of camp."
    new "Nuala looks absolutely radiant today. Her beauty on any day is striking, but today is a particularly special day. She grabs me by the arm and pulls me away from the center of camp.\nNuala 今天看上去光彩照人。她的美平日里就已惊心动魄，而今天是个格外特别的日子。她一把抓住我的胳膊，把我从营地中央拉走。"

    old "Wait, where are we going? Is the ceremony over already?"
    new "Wait, where are we going? Is the ceremony over already?\n等等，我们要去哪儿？仪式已经结束了吗？"

    old "Oh, don't be silly. This is only the beginning. Tonight, when the sky is dark, we'll start a great fire by the totem over there. By tradition, the bigger the fire, the happier the marriage of the couple will be."
    new "Oh, don't be silly. This is only the beginning. Tonight, when the sky is dark, we'll start a great fire by the totem over there. By tradition, the bigger the fire, the happier the marriage of the couple will be.\n哦，别傻了。这才刚刚开始。今晚天色暗下来之后，我们会在那边的图腾旁燃起一堆大火。按传统，火燃得越大，这对新人的婚姻就越幸福。"

    old "We'd better make sure it's a big fire, then."
    new "We'd better make sure it's a big fire, then.\n那我们可得确保那是一场大火。"

    old "Oh, it will be a big fire, [protag]. The biggest fire these desert sands have ever seen. But first..."
    new "Oh, it will be a big fire, [protag]. The biggest fire these desert sands have ever seen. But first...\n哦，会是大火的，[protag]。这片沙漠沙地上前所未见的大火。不过在那之前……"

    old "Nuala leans into me, and I feel her chest touch mine as our bodies press against each other. Nuala, beautiful both in appearance as well as in substance."
    new "Nuala leans into me, and I feel her chest touch mine as our bodies press against each other. Nuala, beautiful both in appearance as well as in substance.\nNuala 依偎过来，我们的身体紧紧相贴，我感觉到她的胸口抵着我的胸口。Nuala，不仅外表美丽，内在也同样美好。"

    old "According to tradition, the newly married couple spends their afternoon alone in a tent apart from the rest of the tribe, not to be disturbed by anyone for any reason."
    new "According to tradition, the newly married couple spends their afternoon alone in a tent apart from the rest of the tribe, not to be disturbed by anyone for any reason.\n按照传统，新婚夫妇要单独在远离族人的帐篷里度过这个下午，无论出于什么理由，都不受任何人打扰。"

    old "That's a tradition I think I can get behind."
    new "That's a tradition I think I can get behind.\n这个传统，我想我很乐意配合。"

    old "It's a tradition passed down by our ancestors."
    new "It's a tradition passed down by our ancestors.\n这是我们祖先传下来的传统。"

    old "Well then, we'd best not let them down."
    new "Well then, we'd best not let them down.\n那我们最好别让他们失望。"

    old "You're thinking like one of the Dunemarchers already, [protag]. As if I needed another reason to know that I was right to choose you."
    new "You're thinking like one of the Dunemarchers already, [protag]. As if I needed another reason to know that I was right to choose you.\n你想得已经像个 Dunemarchers 了，[protag]。好像我还需要别的理由，来证明自己选对了你似的。"

    old "Nuala leads the way toward the tent, gripping my hand tightly."
    new "Nuala leads the way toward the tent, gripping my hand tightly.\nNuala 紧紧攥着我的手，朝帐篷走去。"

    old "There was once a time when I questioned whether joining the Dunemarchers was what I wanted to do with my life. But I'm convinced now more than ever that it was the right choice."
    new "There was once a time when I questioned whether joining the Dunemarchers was what I wanted to do with my life. But I'm convinced now more than ever that it was the right choice.\n曾经有那么一阵，我怀疑加入 Dunemarchers 是否是我想要的人生。可如今，我比任何时候都确信，那是个正确的选择。"

    old "Of all the adventures I've had in my life, I can imagine no adventure greater than the life I'm about to share with Nuala."
    new "Of all the adventures I've had in my life, I can imagine no adventure greater than the life I'm about to share with Nuala.\n在我一生经历的种种冒险中，我想不出还有哪一场，比即将与 Nuala 共度的人生更伟大。"

    old "Dasyra took her rightful place as the head of the Arasmas estate. Though initially uncomfortable with playing the role of a noble, she quickly became well-known throughout Hammerhands as a generous philanthropist."
    new "Dasyra took her rightful place as the head of the Arasmas estate. Though initially uncomfortable with playing the role of a noble, she quickly became well-known throughout Hammerhands as a generous philanthropist.\nDasyra 名正言顺地接掌了 Arasmas 家业。尽管起初她并不适应扮演贵族的角色，但很快，她便以慷慨的慈善家之名享誉整个 Hammerhands。"

    old "Many said that her heart was just as generous as that of her father, Faberge Arasmas. Many gentleman suiters have attempted to court her, but Dasyra has said that her heart belongs to the city of Hammerhands and the people she serves."
    new "Many said that her heart was just as generous as that of her father, Faberge Arasmas. Many gentleman suiters have attempted to court her, but Dasyra has said that her heart belongs to the city of Hammerhands and the people she serves.\n许多人说，她的心地与她父亲 Faberge Arasmas 一样慷慨。不少绅士曾试图追求她，但 Dasyra 表示，她的心属于 Hammerhands 这座城市，属于她所服务的人民。"

    old "Dasyra settled herself in Grimoire, and opened her own bakery. She hired other bakers to produce the goods that she sells, but she occasionally tries her hand at the art of bread-making, with mixed results."
    new "Dasyra settled herself in Grimoire, and opened her own bakery. She hired other bakers to produce the goods that she sells, but she occasionally tries her hand at the art of bread-making, with mixed results.\nDasyra 在 Grimoire 安顿下来，开了一家自己的面包店。她雇了别的面包师来制作出售的面点，偶尔也会亲自上手试试烤面包的手艺，结果时好时坏。"

    old "She still uses her healing abilities to help people in town, and she considers herself a citizen of the Empire, beloved by her neighbors in Grimoire."
    new "She still uses her healing abilities to help people in town, and she considers herself a citizen of the Empire, beloved by her neighbors in Grimoire.\n她仍用自己的治愈能力帮助镇上的人，并把自己视为帝国的一位公民，深受 Grimoire 邻里的爱戴。"

    old "Galan left Grimoire shortly after the final assault on N'Mar and traveled to Mount Kronos, where he met with Sauzer, a Master Of Truth."
    new "Galan left Grimoire shortly after the final assault on N'Mar and traveled to Mount Kronos, where he met with Sauzer, a Master Of Truth.\n在 N'Mar 的最后总攻之后不久，Galan 便离开了 Grimoire，前往 Mount Kronos，在那里他见到了一位 Master Of Truth——Sauzer。"

    old "He's learning to meditate and control himself. He's still there, with no plans to go back."
    new "He's learning to meditate and control himself. He's still there, with no plans to go back.\n他正在学习冥想与自我克制。他仍待在那里，没有回来的打算。"

    old "Galan disappeared after N'Mar. Rumors began to spread about what could have become of him. Some people claimed to have seen him around the outskirts of Hammerhands, while some claimed to have spotted him near the foothills of Mount Kronos. All of the rumors had one thing in common: Galan was always barehanded, never carrying a weapon."
    new "Galan disappeared after N'Mar. Rumors began to spread about what could have become of him. Some people claimed to have seen him around the outskirts of Hammerhands, while some claimed to have spotted him near the foothills of Mount Kronos. All of the rumors had one thing in common: Galan was always barehanded, never carrying a weapon.\nN'Mar 之后，Galan 便销声匿迹。关于他可能遭遇了什么，流言四起。有人声称在 Hammerhands 郊外见过他，也有人说在 Mount Kronos 的山麓附近瞥见过他。所有传闻都有一个共同点：Galan 总是赤手空拳，从不携带武器。"

    old "Kusho became very popular among the elves after the victory on N'Mar. A number of people approached him, hoping to hire him for his talents as an assassin, but Kusho declined every offer, claiming that none of them interested him."
    new "Kusho became very popular among the elves after the victory on N'Mar. A number of people approached him, hoping to hire him for his talents as an assassin, but Kusho declined every offer, claiming that none of them interested him.\nN'Mar 大捷后，Kusho 在精灵中声望大涨。不少人找上门来，想雇他当刺客，但 Kusho 拒绝了所有邀请，声称没有一件让他感兴趣。"

    old "Eventually, a very wealthy person in Dingirra paid him a fortune to become one of his personal guards. Kusho left Grandtree and moved to the town of Dingirra in Zoltar, and now uses his expertise in the art of assassination to foil assassination attempts..."
    new "Eventually, a very wealthy person in Dingirra paid him a fortune to become one of his personal guards. Kusho left Grandtree and moved to the town of Dingirra in Zoltar, and now uses his expertise in the art of assassination to foil assassination attempts...\n最终，Dingirra 一位极富有的人花重金请他做了自己的贴身护卫。Kusho 离开 Grandtree，搬到了 Zoltar 的 Dingirra 镇，如今正用他那刺杀技艺，去挫败一场场暗杀……"

    old "Larik kept leading his tribe in the years following the N'Mar events. He accomplished many more notable feats during his late years, but he never stopped telling stories about the time he spent serving with the lengendary hero [protag]."
    new "Larik kept leading his tribe in the years following the N'Mar events. He accomplished many more notable feats during his late years, but he never stopped telling stories about the time he spent serving with the lengendary hero [protag].\nN'Mar 事件之后的岁月里，Larik 一直带领着他的部落。晚年时，他又立下了许多显赫功绩，却始终不忘讲述自己与传奇英雄 [protag] 并肩作战的那段日子。"

    old "Eventually he became too old to rule, and one day decided to appoint Musamba, a young promising fighter, as his successor."
    new "Eventually he became too old to rule, and one day decided to appoint Musamba, a young promising fighter, as his successor.\n最终他年事已高，无力再统领部落，于是某天决定任命年轻有为的战士 Musamba 作他的继任者。"

    old "Take this!"
    new "Take this!\n接招！"

    old "Ha, to think I would be bested by the princess like this. But do you have what it takes to finish this fight?"
    new "Ha, to think I would be bested by the princess like this. But do you have what it takes to finish this fight?\n哈，没想到我竟会被公主这样击败。不过，你有本事结束这场战斗吗？"

    old "You can't escape from me! Enemy of the amazons, you have met your end!"
    new "You can't escape from me! Enemy of the amazons, you have met your end!\n你逃不出我的手心！amazons 的敌人，你的末日到了！"

    old "Augh! Princess Loren...you fought well."
    new "Augh! Princess Loren...you fought well.\n呃啊！Loren 公主……你打得漂亮。"

    old "Die now!"
    new "Die now!\n现在就受死吧！"

    old "That was a good fight, Ryzom! You can get up now."
    new "That was a good fight, Ryzom! You can get up now.\n打得不错，Ryzom！你现在可以起来了。"

    old "Ryzom? A-are you alright?"
    new "Ryzom? A-are you alright?\nRyzom？你、你没事吧？"

    old "Ryzom! I'm sorry! I'll go get—"
    new "Ryzom! I'm sorry! I'll go get—\nRyzom！对不起！我这就去找——"

    old "Yah!"
    new "Yah!\n呀！"

    old "Ryzom! You scared me! The way you were lying like that, I thought you were actually dead! You're not supposed to keep pretending after the fight is over!"
    new "Ryzom! You scared me! The way you were lying like that, I thought you were actually dead! You're not supposed to keep pretending after the fight is over!\nRyzom！你吓死我了！你那样躺着一动不动，我还以为你真死了！战斗结束就不该再装下去了！"

    old "Well then, if my play acting was good enough to fool you, then I must have been doing a good job, right?"
    new "Well then, if my play acting was good enough to fool you, then I must have been doing a good job, right?\n那，既然我的演技好到能骗过你，就说明我装得很像，对吧？"

    old "Yes, the best! You're not a very good fighter, but you're good at pretending."
    new "Yes, the best! You're not a very good fighter, but you're good at pretending.\n对，最像了！你打架不太行，但装死装得真好。"

    old "Well, if that's a compliment, I guess I'll have to take it. I don't feel like these games are very good training..."
    new "Well, if that's a compliment, I guess I'll have to take it. I don't feel like these games are very good training...\n好吧，如果这也算夸奖，那我就收下了。我倒觉得这些游戏算不上多好的训练……"

    old "I get plenty of training already, but the training is always so serious! So many rules, and so many specific steps to follow. Ryzom, the reason I like fighting with you is because it's about the pretending, not about the fighting."
    new "I get plenty of training already, but the training is always so serious! So many rules, and so many specific steps to follow. Ryzom, the reason I like fighting with you is because it's about the pretending, not about the fighting.\n我平时的训练已经够多了，可那些训练总是那么严肃！条条框框一大堆，还要照着具体的步骤来。Ryzom，我喜欢和你过招，是因为好玩、能装样子，而不是真为了打架。"

    old "Well then, are you done pretending? Or do I have to get ready for you to hit me with that stick again?"
    new "Well then, are you done pretending? Or do I have to get ready for you to hit me with that stick again?\n那么，你装够了吗？还是说，我得准备好再挨你那根棍子一下？"

    old "Oh, I'm not done yet. Take THIS!"
    new "Oh, I'm not done yet. Take THIS!\n哦，我还没完呢。接招！"

    old "Oh my. Is this..."
    new "Oh my. Is this...\n天哪。这是……"

    old "Oh no, the urn..."
    new "Oh no, the urn...\n哦不，那个骨灰瓮……"

    old "What's going on in here? Is that...is that the urn of...Herza!?"
    new "What's going on in here? Is that...is that the urn of...Herza!?\n这里怎么回事？那……那是……Herza 的骨灰瓮吗！？"

    old "...that urn was precious. Beyond precious! How did this happen? Princess, did you..."
    new "...that urn was precious. Beyond precious! How did this happen? Princess, did you...\n……那骨灰瓮很珍贵。珍贵得无以复加！这是怎么发生的？公主，是你……"

    old "I'm sorry. I—"
    new "I'm sorry. I—\n对不起。我——"

    old "Ma'am, I apologize. It was my fault."
    new "Ma'am, I apologize. It was my fault.\n夫人，我很抱歉。是我的错。"

    old "You broke this urn?"
    new "You broke this urn?\n是你打碎了这个骨灰瓮？"

    old "No! Ryzom, it was me who—"
    new "No! Ryzom, it was me who—\n不是的！Ryzom，是我——"

    old "Loren can't accept any blame for this. I should take the punishment."
    new "Loren can't accept any blame for this. I should take the punishment.\nLoren 不能为此担任何罪责。该受罚的是我。"

    old "For a slave like you, destroying an artifact as important as this is an offense that could be punishable by death. You understand this?"
    new "For a slave like you, destroying an artifact as important as this is an offense that could be punishable by death. You understand this?\n对你这样的奴隶来说，毁坏如此重要的圣物，可是足以处死的罪行。你明白吗？"

    old "I cannot tell a lie. It was due to my carelessness. Princess Loren was involved only as an observer to my transgression."
    new "I cannot tell a lie. It was due to my carelessness. Princess Loren was involved only as an observer to my transgression.\n我不能说谎。这都是我一时疏忽。Loren 公主只是目睹了我的过失。"

    old "Then I suppose you'll have to accept your fate."
    new "Then I suppose you'll have to accept your fate.\n那么，我想你只能接受自己的命运了。"

    old "Hold on."
    new "Hold on.\n且慢。"

    old "Queen Karen!"
    new "Queen Karen!\nKaren 女王！"

    old "What happened here?"
    new "What happened here?\n这里出了什么事？"

    old "The shattered glass you see is all that remains of Herza's urn. I broke it. I'm sorry, my queen."
    new "The shattered glass you see is all that remains of Herza's urn. I broke it. I'm sorry, my queen.\n你眼前这些碎屑，就是 Herza 骨灰瓮仅存的一切了。是我打碎的。对不起，我的女王。"

    old "Loren, is that really what happened?"
    new "Loren, is that really what happened?\nLoren，事情的经过真是这样吗？"

    old "No, it's not. Mother...it was me. We were playing and—"
    new "No, it's not. Mother...it was me. We were playing and—\n不，不是的。母亲……是我干的。我们当时在玩，然后——"

    old "Princess, you cannot accept responsibility—"
    new "Princess, you cannot accept responsibility—\n公主，您不能担这个责任——"

    old "Hush, Ryzom. Let the princess speak."
    new "Hush, Ryzom. Let the princess speak.\n住口，Ryzom。让公主说。"

    old "We were playing, and I swung at Ryzom and hit the wall behind him. The urn must have lost its balance and...and..."
    new "We were playing, and I swung at Ryzom and hit the wall behind him. The urn must have lost its balance and...and...\n我们当时在玩，我朝 Ryzom 挥了一棍，却打中了他身后的墙。那骨灰瓮一定是失去了平衡，然后……然后……"

    old "I see. Ryzom, that's not the story I heard you just tell."
    new "I see. Ryzom, that's not the story I heard you just tell.\n我明白了。Ryzom，这跟你刚才对我说的可不一样。"

    old "No. I'm sorry, my queen."
    new "No. I'm sorry, my queen.\n是的，我撒谎了。对不起，我的女王。"

    old "Why did you lie to me? Why did you interrupt to prevent my daughter from speaking the truth?"
    new "Why did you lie to me? Why did you interrupt to prevent my daughter from speaking the truth?\n你为什么要对我撒谎？为什么抢着打断，不让我女儿说出真相？"

    old "...I wanted to protect her from the consequences. A girl of her age should not have to answer for something like this."
    new "...I wanted to protect her from the consequences. A girl of her age should not have to answer for something like this.\n……我想护着她，不让她承担后果。她这个年纪的女孩，不该为这种事受过。"

    old "If Loren is to be the princess of the amazons, then she must be held to account for her actions. Ryzom, I'll not have you make a liar out of my daughter, nor will I have you lying to me in order to protect her."
    new "If Loren is to be the princess of the amazons, then she must be held to account for her actions. Ryzom, I'll not have you make a liar out of my daughter, nor will I have you lying to me in order to protect her.\n若 Loren 要当 amazons 的公主，她就必须为自己的行为负责。Ryzom，我绝不容你把我女儿变成撒谎之人，也绝不容你为了保护她而对我撒谎。"

    old "...I'm sorry, my queen."
    new "...I'm sorry, my queen.\n……对不起，我的女王。"

    old "Ryzom, come here. Let me see your face better."
    new "Ryzom, come here. Let me see your face better.\nRyzom，过来。让我看清你的脸。"

    old "...my queen."
    new "...my queen.\n……我的女王。"

    old "Thank you for trying to protect Loren. Were I in your place, I would have done the same thing."
    new "Thank you for trying to protect Loren. Were I in your place, I would have done the same thing.\n谢谢你尽力保护 Loren。若换作我在你的位置，我也会这么做。"

    old "But from now on, I ask that you do not lie to me. Not even if it is to protect Loren."
    new "But from now on, I ask that you do not lie to me. Not even if it is to protect Loren.\n但从今往后，我请你不要对我撒谎。即便撒谎是为了保护 Loren。"

    old "Of course, my queen."
    new "Of course, my queen.\n当然，我的女王。"

    old "Please, leave us. I'd like to speak to my daughter privately."
    new "Please, leave us. I'd like to speak to my daughter privately.\n请先退下吧。我想和女儿单独谈谈。"

    old "That Ryzom really is quite a fascinating individual."
    new "That Ryzom really is quite a fascinating individual.\n那个 Ryzom，真是个相当有趣的人。"

    old "What is it about him? At first glance, he really seems quite ordinary. And yet...there is something about that man that I can't quite put my finger on. I've never known a slave to behave as he does."
    new "What is it about him? At first glance, he really seems quite ordinary. And yet...there is something about that man that I can't quite put my finger on. I've never known a slave to behave as he does.\n他究竟哪里特别呢？乍一看，他确实平平无奇。可……那个男人身上有种我说不清道不明的东西。我从未见过哪个奴隶像他这般行事。"

    old "He's a kind person."
    new "He's a kind person.\n他是个善良的人。"

    old "Kindness is not so uncommon among slaves. In fact, even among slaves who lack kindness, it is not so uncommon for them to feign it out of a sense of self-interest."
    new "Kindness is not so uncommon among slaves. In fact, even among slaves who lack kindness, it is not so uncommon for them to feign it out of a sense of self-interest.\n善良在奴隶中并不罕见。事实上，即便是那些本不善良的奴隶，出于自利之心而装出善良，也屡见不鲜。"

    old "Even a cynical slave might try to get in the good graces of a princess by taking the blame for some minor transgression. After all, you will one day be ruler of this place. But it takes a special kind of person to accept responsibility to protect the princess when it might mean his own death."
    new "Even a cynical slave might try to get in the good graces of a princess by taking the blame for some minor transgression. After all, you will one day be ruler of this place. But it takes a special kind of person to accept responsibility to protect the princess when it might mean his own death.\n即便是精于算计的奴隶，也可能会为讨好公主，主动揽下些小过错的罪责。毕竟，你终有一天会成为这里的统治者。但要在可能搭上自己性命的情况下，仍肯为保护公主而担责，那就得是特别的人了。"

    old "When I heard that you had been spending time with one of the slaves, I was suspicious of his intents. But now that I've seen the man up close, he is...not what I expected."
    new "When I heard that you had been spending time with one of the slaves, I was suspicious of his intents. But now that I've seen the man up close, he is...not what I expected.\n当初听说你和一名奴隶走得近时，我怀疑过他的居心。可如今近看此人，他……与我想象的不一样。"

    old "He enjoys spending time with me. And I enjoy spending time with him."
    new "He enjoys spending time with me. And I enjoy spending time with him.\n他喜欢和我在一起。我也喜欢和他在一起。"

    old "I think I can see why. But don't forget, Loren. You are the princess of the amazons, and he is a slave."
    new "I think I can see why. But don't forget, Loren. You are the princess of the amazons, and he is a slave.\n我想我明白为什么了。但别忘了，Loren。你是 amazons 的公主，而他是个奴隶。"

    old "Are you not going to let me play with Ryzom anymore?"
    new "Are you not going to let me play with Ryzom anymore?\n你不再让我和 Ryzom 玩了吗？"

    old "No...no, I won't forbid you from playing with Ryzom. If anything, perhaps he is the best possible steward I could ask for. Ironically, his greatest fault seems to be his overwhelming protective instinct."
    new "No...no, I won't forbid you from playing with Ryzom. If anything, perhaps he is the best possible steward I could ask for. Ironically, his greatest fault seems to be his overwhelming protective instinct.\n不……不，我不会禁止你和 Ryzom 玩。要说起来，他或许还是我能求到的最好陪护。讽刺的是，他最大的缺点，似乎就是那过分的保护欲。"

    old "I can take care of myself. I don't need Ryzom or anyone else to protect me."
    new "I can take care of myself. I don't need Ryzom or anyone else to protect me.\n我能照顾好自己。我不需要 Ryzom 或任何人来保护我。"

    old "I think you're right, Loren. In fact, I'd say even at your age you're already a better fighter than he is. But you seem to enjoy his company, and I don't think it's wrong for you to spend time with him."
    new "I think you're right, Loren. In fact, I'd say even at your age you're already a better fighter than he is. But you seem to enjoy his company, and I don't think it's wrong for you to spend time with him.\n我想你说得对，Loren。事实上，我敢说，即便在你这个年纪，你的武艺已经胜过他。但你似乎喜欢他的陪伴，我也不觉得你和他相处有什么不妥。"

    old "Of course I want you to take your responsibilities seriously, but even so, I don't want you to train so hard that you forget to experience the joys of youth."
    new "Of course I want you to take your responsibilities seriously, but even so, I don't want you to train so hard that you forget to experience the joys of youth.\n我当然希望你认真对待自己的职责，但即便如此，我也不想你训练得那么苦，以至于忘了去体验青春的乐趣。"

    old "Besides, your ability to cultivate relationships and connect with others may prove just as important as your skill with those two blades. There is a difference between being a mere fighter and being a leader. Someone taught me that lesson not too long ago, and I won't be so quick to forget what [heshe] showed me."
    new "Besides, your ability to cultivate relationships and connect with others may prove just as important as your skill with those two blades. There is a difference between being a mere fighter and being a leader. Someone taught me that lesson not too long ago, and I won't be so quick to forget what [heshe] showed me.\n此外，你经营关系、与人交好的能力，也许并不亚于你那两把刀的武艺。仅仅做个战士，与做个领袖，是有区别的。不久前，有人教过我这一课，我不会这么快就忘记[heshe]让我明白的道理。"

    old "You can go now, Loren. Try not to get into any more trouble."
    new "You can go now, Loren. Try not to get into any more trouble.\n你可以走了，Loren。别再惹麻烦了。"

    old "Somewhere, deep in the Temple of Chzulu..."
    new "Somewhere, deep in the Temple of Chzulu...\n在 Temple of Chzulu 的深处，某个地方……"

    old "A young man falls to his knees in front of three lizardmen. One of them, the Lizardman King, speaks."
    new "A young man falls to his knees in front of three lizardmen. One of them, the Lizardman King, speaks.\n一个年轻人跪倒在三个蜥蜴人面前。其中一个——Lizardman King——开了口。"

    old "Your devotion to the cult of Chzulu is admirable, young human. You are the only one who has managed to survive the trials. Chzulu's favor must be upon you. What's your name?"
    new "Your devotion to the cult of Chzulu is admirable, young human. You are the only one who has managed to survive the trials. Chzulu's favor must be upon you. What's your name?\n你对 Chzulu 教派的虔诚令人钦佩，年轻的人类。你是唯一一个通过了重重考验的人。Chzulu 的恩宠必定降临在你身上。你叫什么名字？"

    old "My name's Ryzom."
    new "My name's Ryzom.\n我叫 Ryzom。"

    old "Do you know what the plan requires of you? Your life?"
    new "Do you know what the plan requires of you? Your life?\n你知道这项计划要求你付出什么吗？你的性命？"

    old "I'm ready to offer my life to Chzulu. I always was."
    new "I'm ready to offer my life to Chzulu. I always was.\n我已准备好把生命献给 Chzulu。我从来都是如此。"

    old "Shaman, come forward and do your magic."
    new "Shaman, come forward and do your magic.\n萨满，上前来，施展你的法术。"

    old "Two lizardmen shaman begin chanting some powerful spell on Ryzom."
    new "Two lizardmen shaman begin chanting some powerful spell on Ryzom.\n两名蜥蜴人萨满开始在 Ryzom 身上念诵某种强大的咒语。"

    old "With this powerful dark magic, nobody will be able to resist you. Is your mission clear?"
    new "With this powerful dark magic, nobody will be able to resist you. Is your mission clear?\n有了这强大的黑暗魔法，将无人能抗拒你。你的任务清楚了吗？"

    old "It is. I will masquerade as a fugitive of the Empire. When the amazons capture me, I will use a charming spell to befriend queen Karen."
    new "It is. I will masquerade as a fugitive of the Empire. When the amazons capture me, I will use a charming spell to befriend queen Karen.\n清楚了。我会伪装成帝国的逃犯。等 amazons 抓住我，我便用魅惑咒语接近 Karen 女王。"

    old "Once I have befriended her, I will initiate a physical relationship with her, then make her fall in love with me and run away."
    new "Once I have befriended her, I will initiate a physical relationship with her, then make her fall in love with me and run away.\n一旦我与她交好，我就会与她发生亲密关系，再让她爱上我，然后带她私奔。"

    old "And you know where to lead her."
    new "And you know where to lead her.\n而你知道该把她带往何处。"

    old "I'll lead her to the heart of lizardman territory. Right to this very temple. I swear it."
    new "I'll lead her to the heart of lizardman territory. Right to this very temple. I swear it.\n我会把她带到蜥蜴人领地的腹地。就带到这座神殿。我发誓。"

    old "Queen Karen is not to be killed until she is brought here, to the Temple of Chzulu. It is here that we will sacrifice her to Chzulu, God of Death. She must pay for defiling the undead forces of N'Mar!"
    new "Queen Karen is not to be killed until she is brought here, to the Temple of Chzulu. It is here that we will sacrifice her to Chzulu, God of Death. She must pay for defiling the undead forces of N'Mar!\n在 Karen 女王被带到此处、带到 Temple of Chzulu 之前，不得伤她性命。我们要在这里把她献祭给死神 Chzulu。她亵渎了 N'Mar 的不死大军，必须付出代价！"

    old "I will not fail. Queen Karen will be brought to you, alive. I will persist, even if it takes years."
    new "I will not fail. Queen Karen will be brought to you, alive. I will persist, even if it takes years.\n我不会失败。我会把 Karen 女王活着带到你们面前。哪怕要花上数年，我也会坚持到底。"

    old "You must remain patient, as we must remain patient. You may have to endure years of servitude, playing the role of a slave, before you are able to initiate contact."
    new "You must remain patient, as we must remain patient. You may have to endure years of servitude, playing the role of a slave, before you are able to initiate contact.\n你必须保持耐心，正如我们也须耐心。你或许得忍受多年的奴役，扮好奴隶的角色，才能开始接触。"

    old "It is only through persistent and unwavering commitment that your mission will be completed. If you have patience, your victory is assured. There is no way that Karen will be able to resist this magic."
    new "It is only through persistent and unwavering commitment that your mission will be completed. If you have patience, your victory is assured. There is no way that Karen will be able to resist this magic.\n唯有矢志不移、坚持不渝，你的任务方能完成。你若能耐心，胜利便已注定。Karen 绝无可能抗拒这种魔法。"

    old "I will not waver."
    new "I will not waver.\n我绝不会动摇。"

    old "Hail to the God Of Death!"
    new "Hail to the God Of Death!\n向死神致敬！"

    old "God Of Death! God Of Death!"
    new "God Of Death! God Of Death!\n死神！死神！"

    old "Where are you going? Stand your ground!"
    new "Where are you going? Stand your ground!\n你要去哪儿？守住阵地！"

    old "Captain Thomas, the army is in disarray! The undead are overwhelming us as we speak!"
    new "Captain Thomas, the army is in disarray! The undead are overwhelming us as we speak!\nThomas 队长，军队已经溃乱！就在我们说话的当口，不死大军已把我们淹没！"

    old "We must retreat—"
    new "We must retreat—\n我们必须撤退——"

    old "Before I can finish the sentence, I spot a volley of arrows headed our way."
    new "Before I can finish the sentence, I spot a volley of arrows headed our way.\n我话还没说完，就瞥见一阵箭雨朝我们这边飞来。"

    old "Get down!"
    new "Get down!\n卧倒！"

    old "I hit the ground, and I hear the sound of arrows whizzing through the air overhead, barely missing me. I look at Cedric, who has an arrow protruding from his chest."
    new "I hit the ground, and I hear the sound of arrows whizzing through the air overhead, barely missing me. I look at Cedric, who has an arrow protruding from his chest.\n我扑倒在地，听见箭矢从头顶呼啸而过，堪堪擦着我飞过。我看向 Cedric，一支箭正插在他的胸口。"

    old "Ugh—"
    new "Ugh—\n呃——"

    old "Cedric, I'm sorry."
    new "Cedric, I'm sorry.\nCedric，对不起。"

    old "Don't be, [protag]. A general who isn't willing to die with their army is no general at all. I—"
    new "Don't be, [protag]. A general who isn't willing to die with their army is no general at all. I—\n别这样，[protag]。一个不愿与自己的军队同生共死的将军，根本不配做将军。我——"

    old "With a wheezing sound, Cedric collapses to the ground."
    new "With a wheezing sound, Cedric collapses to the ground.\nCedric 发出一声喘息，颓然倒地。"

    old "There's no time. We have to retreat now!"
    new "There's no time. We have to retreat now!\n没时间了。我们必须立刻撤退！"

    old "I see the waves of undead streaming forward, as more and more soldiers buckle under the pressure of the ensuing horde. This battle is lost, and my decisions have no doubt played a role in that. Should these soldiers be the ones to pay the price?"
    new "I see the waves of undead streaming forward, as more and more soldiers buckle under the pressure of the ensuing horde. This battle is lost, and my decisions have no doubt played a role in that. Should these soldiers be the ones to pay the price?\n我看着不死大军如潮水般涌来，越来越多的士兵在随之而来的尸潮重压下溃败。这场仗已经输了，而我的决策无疑难辞其咎。难道该由这些士兵来付出代价吗？"

    old "We'll cover your men. Retreat!"
    new "We'll cover your men. Retreat!\n我们掩护你们的人。撤退！"

    old "Captain Thomas looks at me for a moment."
    new "Captain Thomas looks at me for a moment.\nThomas 队长看了我片刻。"

    old "Are you sure—"
    new "Are you sure—\n你确定——"

    old "Your only job now is to get out of here alive and take as many as you can with you. Move!"
    new "Your only job now is to get out of here alive and take as many as you can with you. Move!\n你现在唯一的任务，就是活着离开这里，能带走多少人，就带走多少人。走！"

    old "Captain Thomas nods, as if to say 'thank you.'"
    new "Captain Thomas nods, as if to say 'thank you.'\nThomas 队长点了点头，像是在说“谢谢”。"

    old "There's nothing to do now but fight, trying to buy as many precious seconds as we can for the retreating army."
    new "There's nothing to do now but fight, trying to buy as many precious seconds as we can for the retreating army.\n眼下除了战斗别无他法，尽力为撤退的军队多争取哪怕几秒宝贵的时间。"

    old "[protag], they're too many!"
    new "[protag], they're too many!\n[protag]，他们太多了！"

    old "As the ceaseless waves of undead continue to surround us, my mind races to come up with an exit strategy, and I find myself settling on only one conclusion: there's no escape. We can't back our way out of this fight, and we can't fight our way forward. The undead are too numerous, too unrelenting. This is where it ends."
    new "As the ceaseless waves of undead continue to surround us, my mind races to come up with an exit strategy, and I find myself settling on only one conclusion: there's no escape. We can't back our way out of this fight, and we can't fight our way forward. The undead are too numerous, too unrelenting. This is where it ends.\n不死大军一波接一波，无休无止地将我们围住，我的脑子飞速运转，想找条脱身之策，却只得出一个结论：无路可逃。我们既退不出这场战斗，也杀不出一条生路。不死族太多、太执着。一切就在这里结束了。"

    old "Did I make the right decision to stay and fight? I think Cedric would say so. He said it himself with his dying breath. A leader who isn't willing to die with their followers is no leader at all."
    new "Did I make the right decision to stay and fight? I think Cedric would say so. He said it himself with his dying breath. A leader who isn't willing to die with their followers is no leader at all.\n我选择留下来战斗，这个决定对吗？我想 Cedric 会说是对的。他临死前亲口说过：一个不愿与追随者同死的领袖，根本不配做领袖。"

    old "Ultimately, the loss of this battle is my responsibility. If anyone's to pay the cost fort his defeat, it should be me."
    new "Ultimately, the loss of this battle is my responsibility. If anyone's to pay the cost fort his defeat, it should be me.\n归根结底，这场败仗是我的责任。若有人要为这场失败付出代价，那也该是我。"

    old "A blow from the front knocks me onto my back, and for a brief moment, I look upward at the full moon. Then, the undead swarm over me, and everything goes black."
    new "A blow from the front knocks me onto my back, and for a brief moment, I look upward at the full moon. Then, the undead swarm over me, and everything goes black.\n正面一击把我掀翻在地，有那么短短一瞬，我仰望着满月。随后，不死大军扑到我身上，一切陷入黑暗。"

    old "Who's there?"
    new "Who's there?\n谁在那儿？"

    old "Relax, Enok. It's me, [protag]."
    new "Relax, Enok. It's me, [protag].\n别紧张，Enok。是我，[protag]。"

    old "Oh, hello, [protag]. Sorry for reacting like that. I guess I'm just not used to being alone. I think I've been getting a bit paranoid ever since... well, you know."
    new "Oh, hello, [protag]. Sorry for reacting like that. I guess I'm just not used to being alone. I think I've been getting a bit paranoid ever since... well, you know.\n哦，你好，[protag]。抱歉反应这么大。我想我只是还不习惯一个人。自打……嗯，你知道的，我就一直有点疑神疑鬼。"

    old "I do know: Sylrissa. Enok seems to be taking her absence pretty hard."
    new "I do know: Sylrissa. Enok seems to be taking her absence pretty hard.\n我确实知道：是 Sylrissa。Enok 似乎对她的离开难以释怀。"

    old "I obviously haven't known Sylrissa that long, but I already miss her too. Is that weird?"
    new "I obviously haven't known Sylrissa that long, but I already miss her too. Is that weird?\n显然，我认识 Sylrissa 还没多久，却也已经想念她了。这会不会很怪？"

    old "Not at all, [protag]. Not at all."
    new "Not at all, [protag]. Not at all.\n一点也不怪，[protag]。一点也不。"

    old "Sylrissa tends to have that effect. She's always gotten along well with others. She even somehow gets along with me. I haven't met many people who have managed to accomplish that."
    new "Sylrissa tends to have that effect. She's always gotten along well with others. She even somehow gets along with me. I haven't met many people who have managed to accomplish that.\nSylrissa 就是有这样的魔力。她和别人总能相处得很好，甚至和我都能合得来。能办到这一点的，我还没见过几个。"

    old "Really? That surprises me. I think you're plenty likeable."
    new "Really? That surprises me. I think you're plenty likeable.\n真的？这倒让我意外。我觉得你挺讨人喜欢的。"

    old "I appreciate that, [protag]."
    new "I appreciate that, [protag].\n谢谢你的夸奖，[protag]。"

    old "Scared?"
    new "Scared?\n害怕吗？"

    old "I'm not scared, [protag]. I know the surroundings well and, if things go bad, I can always use the river nearby to quickly swim to safety."
    new "I'm not scared, [protag]. I know the surroundings well and, if things go bad, I can always use the river nearby to quickly swim to safety.\n我不害怕，[protag]。这里的环境我很熟，万一情况不妙，我总能借着附近的河流迅速游到安全之处。"

    old "Unless the ones pursuing you are nagas too."
    new "Unless the ones pursuing you are nagas too.\n除非追你的也是 naga。"

    old "They won't come this far south. Trust me, this place is safe."
    new "They won't come this far south. Trust me, this place is safe.\n他们不会追到这么靠南的地方。相信我，这里很安全。"

    old "Honestly, I just feel lonely."
    new "Honestly, I just feel lonely.\n说实话，我只是觉得孤单。"

    old "So, it's not about having someone to watch your back. You just miss Sylrissa, huh?"
    new "So, it's not about having someone to watch your back. You just miss Sylrissa, huh?\n这么说，不是想要个人照应你。你就是想 Sylrissa 了，对吧？"

    old "Look, Enok. I have a lot of things vying for my time, but as soon as I get a moment I promise that we'll go look for her together. And, if she's alive, we'll find a way to rescue her."
    new "Look, Enok. I have a lot of things vying for my time, but as soon as I get a moment I promise that we'll go look for her together. And, if she's alive, we'll find a way to rescue her.\n听着，Enok。我手头有很多事要忙，但一有空闲，我保证我们一起去寻她。如果她还活着，我们一定想办法把她救出来。"

    old "That being said, you need to prepare yourself for the worst. It is very possible that she's already dead."
    new "That being said, you need to prepare yourself for the worst. It is very possible that she's already dead.\n话虽如此，你也要做好最坏的打算。她很可能已经死了。"

    old "I understand where you're coming from, but I refuse to believe that she's dead until I see the evidence for myself."
    new "I understand where you're coming from, but I refuse to believe that she's dead until I see the evidence for myself.\n我明白你的意思，但在亲眼见到证据之前，我拒绝相信她已经死了。"

    old "Were it anyone else, I would agree with you. The chances of survival are slim. But Sylrissa is resourceful. I can't help but think that she'll be alright somehow."
    new "Were it anyone else, I would agree with you. The chances of survival are slim. But Sylrissa is resourceful. I can't help but think that she'll be alright somehow.\n换了别人，我或许会赞同你。生还的希望确实渺茫。可 Sylrissa 足智多谋，我总忍不住觉得，她总会有办法安然无恙。"

    old "Enok, having hope is one thing, but this..."
    new "Enok, having hope is one thing, but this...\nEnok，抱有希望是一回事，可这样……"

    old "If she really is dead, then I will mourn her passing but I need to know for sure. As long as there is any lingering doubt, I won't be able to move on."
    new "If she really is dead, then I will mourn her passing but I need to know for sure. As long as there is any lingering doubt, I won't be able to move on.\n若她真的死了，我会为她的逝去哀悼，但我需要确切的答案。只要还有一丝疑虑，我就无法向前走。"

    old "Anyway, thank you for coming to visit me, [protag]. I know you're busy with much more important things right now."
    new "Anyway, thank you for coming to visit me, [protag]. I know you're busy with much more important things right now.\n不管怎样，谢谢你来看我，[protag]。我知道你现在正忙着更要紧的事。"

    old "He moves to rub the back of his neck. That's when I notice the rings on his right hand. I don't recall them being there the first time I met Enok."
    new "He moves to rub the back of his neck. That's when I notice the rings on his right hand. I don't recall them being there the first time I met Enok.\n他抬手揉了揉后颈。就在这时，我注意到他右手上的戒指。我记得第一次见到 Enok 时，那些戒指并不在。"

    old "Are those new?"
    new "Are those new?\n那些是新买的吗？"

    old "Oh? You finally noticed them? I was wondering what was taking you so long!"
    new "Oh? You finally noticed them? I was wondering what was taking you so long!\n哦？你终于注意到了？我还纳闷你怎么这么久都没发现呢！"

    old "There is an excited gleam in Enok's eyes that's hard to ignore. I get the feeling he'd be disappointed if I didn't ask about them at this point. I go ahead and humor him, figuring it'll be good to get his mind of Sylrissa for a bit."
    new "There is an excited gleam in Enok's eyes that's hard to ignore. I get the feeling he'd be disappointed if I didn't ask about them at this point. I go ahead and humor him, figuring it'll be good to get his mind of Sylrissa for a bit.\nEnok 眼里闪着难掩的兴奋光芒。我隐约觉得，此刻若我不问问这些戒指，他定会失望。于是我便顺了他的意，心想让他暂时别老想着 Sylrissa 也好。"

    old "They're really nice. Where did you find them?"
    new "They're really nice. Where did you find them?\n真漂亮。你在哪儿找到的？"

    old "I went back to the ruins up north and found them there. Don't worry though! I was careful."
    new "I went back to the ruins up north and found them there. Don't worry though! I was careful.\n我回了趟北边的废墟，在那儿找到的。别担心！我很小心的。"

    old "I'm having a hard time believing that explanation, Enok. The ruins were empty when we left. Where did you really find those rings? And why lie to me about it?"
    new "I'm having a hard time believing that explanation, Enok. The ruins were empty when we left. Where did you really find those rings? And why lie to me about it?\n这个解释让我很难相信，Enok。我们离开时，那片废墟是空的。你究竟是在哪儿找到这些戒指的？又为什么要为此对我撒谎？"

    old "You saw through my lie that easily, huh?"
    new "You saw through my lie that easily, huh?\n我的谎话就这么轻易被你戳穿了？"

    old "Enok sighs, but does decide to tell me the truth this time."
    new "Enok sighs, but does decide to tell me the truth this time.\nEnok 叹了口气，但这一次，他还是决定告诉我真相。"

    old "I stole them from a traveling merchant, a bit south of the swamps."
    new "I stole them from a traveling merchant, a bit south of the swamps.\n我从一个行商那里偷来的，就在沼泽南边不远。"

    old "You stole the rings!?"
    new "You stole the rings!?\n你偷了这些戒指！？"

    old "Perhaps 'stole' is the wrong word? It was a fair exchange. I guess it'd be more fitting to say that I was simply taking a reward for myself. You see, bandits attacked the merchant and I helped him solve-"
    new "Perhaps 'stole' is the wrong word? It was a fair exchange. I guess it'd be more fitting to say that I was simply taking a reward for myself. You see, bandits attacked the merchant and I helped him solve-\n也许“偷”这个词不太恰当？那是一次公平的交易。我想更贴切的说法是，我不过是为自己取了份报酬。你看，当时有匪徒袭击了那个商人，是我帮他解决了——"

    old "Do I even want to know what ended up happening to those bandits?"
    new "Do I even want to know what ended up happening to those bandits?\n我该不该问问，那些匪徒最后怎么样了？"

    old "Well, let's just say that they won't be robbing anyone in future."
    new "Well, let's just say that they won't be robbing anyone in future.\n这个嘛，这么说吧，他们以后再也抢不了任何人了。"

    old "Of course."
    new "Of course.\n当然。"

    old "Anyway, after the fight the merchant asked if there was any way he could repay me for saving him. I asked him if he had any rings I could have."
    new "Anyway, after the fight the merchant asked if there was any way he could repay me for saving him. I asked him if he had any rings I could have.\n总之，打完之后，那个商人问我，有没有什么办法能报答我的救命之恩。我便问他有没有戒指能给我。"

    old "From the look on his face, it's like he expected me to say that I didn't want a reward."
    new "From the look on his face, it's like he expected me to say that I didn't want a reward.\n看他那副表情，好像料定我会说不要报酬似的。"

    old "And yeah, maybe that would have been a nice thing to do, but it wasn't like it was an easy fight. I stuck my neck out for that guy. I deserved something for my efforts, right?"
    new "And yeah, maybe that would have been a nice thing to do, but it wasn't like it was an easy fight. I stuck my neck out for that guy. I deserved something for my efforts, right?\n是啊，也许那样做更显得高尚，但那场架打得可不容易。我可是为那家伙豁出了性命。我为自己挣点报酬，理所应当，对吧？"

    old "I guess..."
    new "I guess...\n我想也是……"

    old "Right! And if I wasn't there he would have lost all of his goods anyway. Probably his life too. A few rings is a small price to pay."
    new "Right! And if I wasn't there he would have lost all of his goods anyway. Probably his life too. A few rings is a small price to pay.\n对吧！而且要不是我在，他的货物早全没了，说不定连命都保不住。几枚戒指不过是小小的代价。"

    old "Okay. So, he didn't end up giving you the rings you wanted? Is that where this story is going?"
    new "Okay. So, he didn't end up giving you the rings you wanted? Is that where this story is going?\n好吧。所以，他最终没给你想要的戒指？故事是这么发展的吗？"

    old "Not quite."
    new "Not quite.\n也不尽然。"

    old "Enok pulls a bag from his side and then dumps it, dropping three shoddily made rings into the palm of his hand."
    new "Enok pulls a bag from his side and then dumps it, dropping three shoddily made rings into the palm of his hand.\nEnok 从身侧掏出一个小袋，倒了过来，三枚做工粗劣的戒指落进他的掌心。"

    old "He gave me these ones."
    new "He gave me these ones.\n他给了我这个。"

    old "Do you see these gems? They're all fake. And don't get me started on the craftsmanship. The worst part of it all was that he tried to act like he was giving me something really great."
    new "Do you see these gems? They're all fake. And don't get me started on the craftsmanship. The worst part of it all was that he tried to act like he was giving me something really great.\n你看到这些宝石了吗？全是假的。至于做工，那就更别提了。最气人的是，他还装出一副送了我什么稀世珍宝的样子。"

    old "So, instead of thanking you properly, he tried to trick you?"
    new "So, instead of thanking you properly, he tried to trick you?\n所以，他非但没好好谢你，还想糊弄你？"

    old "Exactly. I couldn't bring myself to let that slide."
    new "Exactly. I couldn't bring myself to let that slide.\n没错。我可咽不下这口气。"

    old "I pretended to believe him and, when he wasn't looking, I stole some genuinely nice rings from his cart. Considering what I did for him, I think this was a much fairer reward."
    new "I pretended to believe him and, when he wasn't looking, I stole some genuinely nice rings from his cart. Considering what I did for him, I think this was a much fairer reward.\n于是我假装信了他的话，趁他不注意，从他的货车上拿了几枚真正的好戒指。想想我为他做的那些，我觉得这份报酬公道多了。"

    old "Well... I can't say what you did was right, but it's not like I'm going to go hunt down the merchant and make you give the rings back."
    new "Well... I can't say what you did was right, but it's not like I'm going to go hunt down the merchant and make you give the rings back.\n这个……我不能说你的做法是对的，不过，我也不会去满世界找那个商人，逼你把戒指还回去。"

    old "If nothing else, maybe he at least learned that he shouldn't try to outsmart a naga."
    new "If nothing else, maybe he at least learned that he shouldn't try to outsmart a naga.\n至少，他或许能明白一件事：别想着耍一个 naga。"

    old "Maybe. We are pretty smart. And look! These rings are perfect for my fingers!"
    new "Maybe. We are pretty smart. And look! These rings are perfect for my fingers!\n也许吧。我们确实挺聪明。看！这些戒指戴在我手上刚刚好！"

    old "I may not agree with everything Enok has said today, but I can agree with that much."
    new "I may not agree with everything Enok has said today, but I can agree with that much.\nEnok 今天说的话，我未必句句赞同，但这一点我完全同意。"

    old "They do suit you."
    new "They do suit you.\n它们确实很配你。"

    old "Anyway, I need to get going. It was good seening you. Take care, Enok."
    new "Anyway, I need to get going. It was good seening you. Take care, Enok.\n好了，我得走了。见到你真好。保重，Enok。"

    old "See you soon, [protag]."
    new "See you soon, [protag].\n回头见，[protag]。"

    old "When I get to the swamp, I check the usual spot but I see no sign of Enok."
    new "When I get to the swamp, I check the usual spot but I see no sign of Enok.\n到了沼泽，我照例去老地方查看，却不见 Enok 的踪影。"

    old "However, before I start to worry, I hear a familiar voice coming from up high."
    new "However, before I start to worry, I hear a familiar voice coming from up high.\n不过，还没等我开始担心，就听见高处传来一个熟悉的声音。"

    old "[protag], I'm up here!"
    new "[protag], I'm up here!\n[protag]，我在上面！"

    old "I look up and see Enok standing on a tall, pointy rock not far from the river. It's not someplace a normal person could use as a lookout location, but Enok is able to balance on its tip using his tail."
    new "I look up and see Enok standing on a tall, pointy rock not far from the river. It's not someplace a normal person could use as a lookout location, but Enok is able to balance on its tip using his tail.\n我抬头望去，看见 Enok 站在离河不远的一块高耸尖岩上。那可不是普通人能用来瞭望的地方，但 Enok 能靠尾巴稳住身形，立在岩尖之上。"

    old "It's actually quite impressive."
    new "It's actually quite impressive.\n说实话，挺让人叹为观止。"

    old "What are you doing up there?"
    new "What are you doing up there?\n你在上面做什么？"

    old "I'm scouting the surroundings in order to determine the lizardmen patrol routes."
    new "I'm scouting the surroundings in order to determine the lizardmen patrol routes.\n我在观察四周，摸清蜥蜴人的巡逻路线。"

    old "This has to do with Sylrissa, right?"
    new "This has to do with Sylrissa, right?\n这跟 Sylrissa 有关，对吧？"

    old "Yes. And I have good news regarding that, by the way."
    new "Yes. And I have good news regarding that, by the way.\n是的。顺带一提，这方面我有好消息。"

    old "Enok's tail curls around the rock and, from there, he silently glides down its sides. It's a quick and graceful movement that has a bit of a mesmerizing quality to it."
    new "Enok's tail curls around the rock and, from there, he silently glides down its sides. It's a quick and graceful movement that has a bit of a mesmerizing quality to it.\nEnok 的尾巴缠住岩石，随后他悄无声息地顺着岩壁滑了下来。动作迅捷而优雅，带着几分令人着迷的味道。"

    old "Look at this."
    new "Look at this.\n看看这个。"

    old "Enok closes the distance between us and shows me his open hand."
    new "Enok closes the distance between us and shows me his open hand.\nEnok 凑近我，摊开手掌给我看。"

    old "It seems to be empty so I assume he's trying to indicate one of the rings he's wearing."
    new "It seems to be empty so I assume he's trying to indicate one of the rings he's wearing.\n他手里似乎空无一物，于是我猜，他指的应该是他戴着的某枚戒指。"

    old "Another ring? What does that have to do with Sylrissa?"
    new "Another ring? What does that have to do with Sylrissa?\n又一枚戒指？这和 Sylrissa 有什么关系？"

    old "No, not the rings. Look closer! Don't you see what I'm holding?"
    new "No, not the rings. Look closer! Don't you see what I'm holding?\n不，不是戒指。再仔细看！你看不到我拿着什么吗？"

    old "I take another look and this time manage to pick out a long, thread like strand of red."
    new "I take another look and this time manage to pick out a long, thread like strand of red.\n我又看了一眼，这次才辨认出一根长长的、线一样的红色丝缕。"

    old "...looks like hair?"
    new "...looks like hair?\n……看起来像头发？"

    old "Sylrissa's hair. I found some on my clothes."
    new "Sylrissa's hair. I found some on my clothes.\n是 Sylrissa 的头发。我在自己衣服上找到的。"

    old "And? How does that help us?"
    new "And? How does that help us?\n那又怎样？这能帮上什么忙？"

    old "I can cast a... locator spell of sorts. To use it, I just need something that belonged to the person I'm trying to find."
    new "I can cast a... locator spell of sorts. To use it, I just need something that belonged to the person I'm trying to find.\n我能施一种……类似定位的咒语。要用它，只需要一件属于我要找之人的东西。"

    old "Enok's grin widens as he finishes his point."
    new "Enok's grin widens as he finishes his point.\nEnok 说完，脸上的笑容咧得更大了。"

    old "Something like a strand of hair."
    new "Something like a strand of hair.\n比如一缕头发。"

    old "That's impressive. I never heard of a spell like that before though."
    new "That's impressive. I never heard of a spell like that before though.\n真了不起。不过这种咒语，我以前从没听说过。"

    old "Well, that's probably because it's dark magic. It's forbidden in the magic schools, but here in the swamps it's not like anyone is around to judge us."
    new "Well, that's probably because it's dark magic. It's forbidden in the magic schools, but here in the swamps it's not like anyone is around to judge us.\n那大概因为它是黑暗魔法。魔法学院里禁止这个，可在沼泽这种地方，又没人在旁边对我们评头论足。"

    old "Enok cautiously meets my gaze and waits as if he's expecting some kind of response. Perhaps he fears that I might disagree with him using dark magic."
    new "Enok cautiously meets my gaze and waits as if he's expecting some kind of response. Perhaps he fears that I might disagree with him using dark magic.\nEnok 小心翼翼地迎上我的目光，等着我的反应，似乎怕我会不赞成他用黑暗魔法。"

    old "I never understood why mages condemn the use of dark magic in the first place to be honest."
    new "I never understood why mages condemn the use of dark magic in the first place to be honest.\n说实话，我一直不明白，法师们最初为何要谴责使用黑暗魔法。"

    old "Maybe because of its demonic origins? And because it's corrupted many young mages in the past, driving them to madness?"
    new "Maybe because of its demonic origins? And because it's corrupted many young mages in the past, driving them to madness?\n也许因为它源自恶魔？又或者，过去它曾腐蚀过许多年轻法师，把他们逼入疯狂？"

    old "Right... I see your point."
    new "Right... I see your point.\n也对……我明白你的意思了。"

    old "But why are you using it then? Don't you fear the consequences?"
    new "But why are you using it then? Don't you fear the consequences?\n可那你为什么还要用它？你不怕后果吗？"

    old "No. I've been using it several years now and haven't noticed any side effects in my case."
    new "No. I've been using it several years now and haven't noticed any side effects in my case.\n不怕。我已经用了好几年，自己身上没发现任何副作用。"

    old "Interesting. How is that possible?"
    new "Interesting. How is that possible?\n有意思。这怎么可能？"

    old "We... we could perlustrate the area, hoping to find where Sylrissa is being held prisoner by chance."
    new "We... we could perlustrate the area, hoping to find where Sylrissa is being held prisoner by chance.\n我们……我们可以仔细搜遍这片区域，碰碰运气，看能不能找到 Sylrissa 被关押的地方。"

    old "Of course, considering the swamp's dimensions, the fact that moving through it is not easy, the lizardmen, treasure hunters and dangerous animals... By my estimation, it would probably take us between 3 or 4. Maybe 3, if we're lucky."
    new "Of course, considering the swamp's dimensions, the fact that moving through it is not easy, the lizardmen, treasure hunters and dangerous animals... By my estimation, it would probably take us between 3 or 4. Maybe 3, if we're lucky.\n当然，考虑到这片沼泽的广袤、穿行其中的艰难，再加上蜥蜴人、寻宝者和危险的野兽……照我估计，大概要花我们三四个。运气好的话，三个。"

    old "Three or four what? Days? Weeks?"
    new "Three or four what? Days? Weeks?\n三四个什么？天？周？"

    old "No, years."
    new "No, years.\n不，年。"

    old "What? Are you serious?!"
    new "What? Are you serious?!\n什么？你认真的？！"

    old "Yes, I am, when the life of my beloved friend is at stake."
    new "Yes, I am, when the life of my beloved friend is at stake.\n是的，认真的——既然这关系到我挚友的性命。"

    old "Sorry. I suppose you're right."
    new "Sorry. I suppose you're right.\n抱歉。我想你说得对。"

    old "I'm just wary of the potential effect dark magic could have on you."
    new "I'm just wary of the potential effect dark magic could have on you.\n我只是担心黑暗魔法可能对你产生的影响。"

    old "Ah, heard all the scary tales from the illustrious wizards? Apolimesho perhaps? You don't need to worry about me."
    new "Ah, heard all the scary tales from the illustrious wizards? Apolimesho perhaps? You don't need to worry about me.\n啊，听了那些声名显赫的法师们讲的故事？也许是 Apolimesho？你大可不必为我担心。"

    old "First of all, I'm a naga, not a human. Different races are bound to have different levels of tolerance. I think us nagas have more of a natural resistance to dark magic than a lot of the common races."
    new "First of all, I'm a naga, not a human. Different races are bound to have different levels of tolerance. I think us nagas have more of a natural resistance to dark magic than a lot of the common races.\n首先，我是 naga，不是人类。不同种族的耐受程度本就不同。我想，我们 naga 对黑暗魔法有着天生的抵抗力，比许多常见种族都强。"

    old "Second, even if that isn't the case, there are always exceptions. I've met a human who regularly practices dark magic and she looked... normal. Most of the time, anyway."
    new "Second, even if that isn't the case, there are always exceptions. I've met a human who regularly practices dark magic and she looked... normal. Most of the time, anyway.\n其次，就算并非如此，也总有例外。我认识一个经常修习黑暗魔法的人类，她看上去……很正常。至少大多数时候是。"

    old "Really?"
    new "Really?\n真的？"

    old "Yes. She lives in a shack north of here. I think her name was... Charaba. No. Bambara maybe?"
    new "Yes. She lives in a shack north of here. I think her name was... Charaba. No. Bambara maybe?\n真的。她住在北边的一间小屋里。我想她的名字叫……Charaba。不对。也许是 Bambara？"

    old "Yes. Bambara sounds right."
    new "Yes. Bambara sounds right.\n对，Bambara 听着没错。"

    old "I'm pretty sure Bambara isn't a name."
    new "I'm pretty sure Bambara isn't a name.\n我很确定，Bambara 不是个名字。"

    old "Still, whether Enok got this woman's name right or not doesn't exactly matter at the moment. We have more pressing issues to attend to."
    new "Still, whether Enok got this woman's name right or not doesn't exactly matter at the moment. We have more pressing issues to attend to.\n不过，眼下 Enok 有没有记对这个女人的名字，其实并不重要。我们还有更要紧的事要办。"

    old "All right. How does this spell work? Do you get a vision of the place or something?"
    new "All right. How does this spell work? Do you get a vision of the place or something?\n好吧。这咒语是怎么起作用的？你会在脑海中看到那地方的样子吗？"

    old "No, it's more like a compass."
    new "No, it's more like a compass.\n不，它更像一个罗盘。"

    old "Ah, I see. So it would give you a direction to follow, but you won't know exactly where she is?"
    new "Ah, I see. So it would give you a direction to follow, but you won't know exactly where she is?\n啊，我明白了。所以它会给你一个要去的方向，但你无法确切知道她在哪儿？"

    old "Yes. It's not perfect, but it's better than blindly wandering around the swamps for months hoping to stumble upon her randomly."
    new "Yes. It's not perfect, but it's better than blindly wandering around the swamps for months hoping to stumble upon her randomly.\n是的。它不完美，但总比在沼泽里盲目乱逛几个月、指望碰巧撞见她强。"

    old "I'm going to need your help, [protag]."
    new "I'm going to need your help, [protag].\n我需要你的帮助，[protag]。"

    old "I don't know how many lizardmen will be guarding her or what other perils await me. It'd be foolish to do this alone."
    new "I don't know how many lizardmen will be guarding her or what other perils await me. It'd be foolish to do this alone.\n我不知道会有多少蜥蜴人看守她，也不知道前方还有怎样的凶险。单枪匹马去，太鲁莽了。"

    old "I will help you, Enok. I just need some time to prepare."
    new "I will help you, Enok. I just need some time to prepare.\n我会帮你的，Enok。我只需要一点时间准备。"

    old "I can ask for some help too if you'd like. Some back up could be useful."
    new "I can ask for some help too if you'd like. Some back up could be useful.\n如果你愿意，我也可以再找些帮手。有点后援总有用处。"

    old "No. I think it's better if we go alone. A small rescue team won't be as easily noticed."
    new "No. I think it's better if we go alone. A small rescue team won't be as easily noticed.\n不。我想还是我们俩单独去比较好。小型的营救队伍不那么容易被发现。"

    old "Makes sense. Then it's decided. Give me some time to get ready and when I get back, we'll go rescue Sylrissa."
    new "Makes sense. Then it's decided. Give me some time to get ready and when I get back, we'll go rescue Sylrissa.\n有道理。那就这么定了。给我点时间准备，等我回来，我们就去救 Sylrissa。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. Please hurry. We don't know what their intentions are regarding Sylrissa."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. Please hurry. We don't know what their intentions are regarding Sylrissa.\n谢谢你，[protag]。请快一点。我们不知道他们对 Sylrissa 打着什么主意。"

    old "I find Enok at the usual spot. He makes his way over to me quickly, looking excited to see me."
    new "I find Enok at the usual spot. He makes his way over to me quickly, looking excited to see me.\n我在老地方找到了 Enok。他快步朝我走来，见到我显得很兴奋。"

    old "Finally! You're just in time!"
    new "Finally! You're just in time!\n终于来了！你来得正是时候！"

    old "Why? What happened?"
    new "Why? What happened?\n怎么了？出什么事了？"

    old "Enok's excitement is immediately replaced by a worried expression."
    new "Enok's excitement is immediately replaced by a worried expression.\nEnok 的兴奋瞬间被忧心忡忡的神情取代。"

    old "They... They want to..."
    new "They... They want to...\n他们……他们想……"

    old "I can't even bring myself to say it."
    new "I can't even bring myself to say it.\n这话我连说都说不出口。"

    old "Enok!"
    new "Enok!\nEnok！"

    old "They want to cook Sylrissa. Alive. And then, eat her."
    new "They want to cook Sylrissa. Alive. And then, eat her.\n他们想把 Sylrissa 活活煮熟。然后吃掉她。"

    old "Ugh. That's... unpleasant. Wait. How do you know that?"
    new "Ugh. That's... unpleasant. Wait. How do you know that?\n呃。这……太恶心了。等等。你是怎么知道的？"

    old "Enok lowers his gaze as a slight, embarassed blush creeps into his cheeks. I can't help but think that it's kind of cute."
    new "Enok lowers his gaze as a slight, embarassed blush creeps into his cheeks. I can't help but think that it's kind of cute.\nEnok 垂下目光，脸颊浮起一抹难为情的红晕。我忍不住觉得，这样倒有点可爱。"

    old "Well, um... I may have cast the locator spell and followed it for a bit and--"
    new "Well, um... I may have cast the locator spell and followed it for a bit and--\n这个，嗯……我可能施了那个定位咒，跟着它走了一小段，然后——"

    old "You went there alone?!"
    new "You went there alone?!\n你一个人去了那里？！"

    old "Yes! I'm sorry but I couldn't wait any longer!"
    new "Yes! I'm sorry but I couldn't wait any longer!\n是的！对不起，可我真的等不下去了！"

    old "You have to understand. Sylrissa is all I've had for a long time. She's essentially my sister!"
    new "You have to understand. Sylrissa is all I've had for a long time. She's essentially my sister!\n你得理解。长久以来，Sylrissa 就是我的一切。她简直就像我的妹妹！"

    old "Sister, uh? Or something more? Anyways..."
    new "Sister, uh? Or something more? Anyways...\n妹妹，嗯？还是不止于此？算了……"

    old "I see. I'm sorry. I understand and, well, I'm just glad that you're alright."
    new "I see. I'm sorry. I understand and, well, I'm just glad that you're alright.\n我明白了。抱歉。我理解，嗯，我只是很高兴你平安无事。"

    old "...Thank you."
    new "...Thank you.\n……谢谢你。"

    old "I give him a nod and then get us back on track."
    new "I give him a nod and then get us back on track.\n我朝他点点头，然后把话题拉回正轨。"

    old "What happened next?"
    new "What happened next?\n后来发生了什么？"

    old "I managed to find enough ingredients to make an invisibility potion, so made one and then drank it. Nobody could see me, not even the lizardmen with their formidable sight. I was safe as long as I was careful and didn't make any noise."
    new "I managed to find enough ingredients to make an invisibility potion, so made one and then drank it. Nobody could see me, not even the lizardmen with their formidable sight. I was safe as long as I was careful and didn't make any noise.\n我设法找齐了制作隐形药水的原料，于是做了一瓶喝了下去。没人能看见我，连那些视力惊人的蜥蜴人也看不见。只要我小心谨慎、不弄出响动，就很安全。"

    old "An invisibility potion? That's no trivial task. To pull off something like that... You must be very skilled as an alchemist, Enok."
    new "An invisibility potion? That's no trivial task. To pull off something like that... You must be very skilled as an alchemist, Enok.\n隐形药水？那可不是小菜一碟。能调出那种东西……你的炼金术一定相当精湛，Enok。"

    old "Thank you [protag]. I'm just lucky I was able to find the right ingredients here in the swamp. Anyway..."
    new "Thank you [protag]. I'm just lucky I was able to find the right ingredients here in the swamp. Anyway...\n谢谢你，[protag]。我只是运气好，在沼泽里恰好凑齐了合适的原料。总之……"

    old "I followed the spell until I found a small encampment of lizardmen. Initially, I thought it was a good news: if they took her to Chzulu temple up North, it'd be nearly impossible to infiltrate that place and rescue her."
    new "I followed the spell until I found a small encampment of lizardmen. Initially, I thought it was a good news: if they took her to Chzulu temple up North, it'd be nearly impossible to infiltrate that place and rescue her.\n我顺着咒语一路找去，直到发现一处蜥蜴人的小营地。起初我以为这是好消息：要是他们把她带去了北边的 Chzulu 神庙，那地方几乎不可能潜入救人。"

    old "This group looked like it was only a small camp of lizardmen, maybe some scouts. But then, I discovered a terrible truth: they're lizardmen devourers. I don't know if you ever had the displeasure of running into them on your previous job."
    new "This group looked like it was only a small camp of lizardmen, maybe some scouts. But then, I discovered a terrible truth: they're lizardmen devourers. I don't know if you ever had the displeasure of running into them on your previous job.\n那伙人看着只是一小群蜥蜴人，也许是什么斥候。可随后，我发现了一个可怕的事实：他们是蜥蜴人吞噬者。不知道你以前办事时，有没有倒霉地撞见过他们。"

    old "Luckily, no. They're not the kind of people who go around borrowing money. But I do know them by their name and their cannibalistic practices."
    new "Luckily, no. They're not the kind of people who go around borrowing money. But I do know them by their name and their cannibalistic practices.\n幸好没有。他们可不是那种会到处借钱的人。但我知道他们的名号，也知道他们吃人的行径。"

    old "No, though I once heard a story from a fellow merchant of how he barely escaped from an ambush set up by a group of them. He made sure to emphasize that they're known for eating people."
    new "No, though I once heard a story from a fellow merchant of how he barely escaped from an ambush set up by a group of them. He made sure to emphasize that they're known for eating people.\n没有，不过我听过一位商人同行讲的故事，说他如何从一伙他们的埋伏中死里逃生。他一再强调，这群人以吃人闻名。"

    old "Of course I know about them. The most savage of the lizardmen, they capture and cook their prey alive before eating them."
    new "Of course I know about them. The most savage of the lizardmen, they capture and cook their prey alive before eating them.\n我当然知道他们。他们是蜥蜴人中最野蛮的一支，会活捉猎物、活生生煮熟，再吃掉。"

    old "I heard some stories while studying at the academy of magic. They pratice cannibalism, don't they?"
    new "I heard some stories while studying at the academy of magic. They pratice cannibalism, don't they?\n我在魔法学院求学时听过一些故事。他们吃同类，对吧？"

    old "Yes, they follow the cult of the dead like most lizardmen, but they believe that by eating their prey, they absorb their soul and, in the process, please their god, Chzulu."
    new "Yes, they follow the cult of the dead like most lizardmen, but they believe that by eating their prey, they absorb their soul and, in the process, please their god, Chzulu.\n是的，他们和多数蜥蜴人一样信奉亡灵教派，但他们相信，吃掉猎物便能吸收其灵魂，从而取悦他们的神 Chzulu。"

    old "Hmm, I never thought about it before, but maybe the lizardmen are unaffected by the mist and N'Mar magic corruption. After all, they worship the god of death, and the source of the evil is undead..."
    new "Hmm, I never thought about it before, but maybe the lizardmen are unaffected by the mist and N'Mar magic corruption. After all, they worship the god of death, and the source of the evil is undead...\n嗯，我以前倒没想过，也许蜥蜴人不受浓雾和 N'Mar 魔法腐化的影响。毕竟，他们崇拜的是死神，而邪恶的源头正是不死族……"

    old "Enok's expression becomes more serious. He grabs my arm urgently, digging his fingers into my skin. He doesn't mean to hurt me. He's just worried. If his tight grip didn't make that obvious enough, his tone does."
    new "Enok's expression becomes more serious. He grabs my arm urgently, digging his fingers into my skin. He doesn't mean to hurt me. He's just worried. If his tight grip didn't make that obvious enough, his tone does.\nEnok 的神情愈发凝重。他急切地抓住我的手臂，手指几乎嵌进我的皮肤。他并非有意弄疼我，只是担心。若说那紧握的手还没能说明一切，他的语气也足以表明。"

    old "If we don't hurry, Sylrissa will be dead too."
    new "If we don't hurry, Sylrissa will be dead too.\n我们若再不快点，Sylrissa 也会没命。"

    old "I put my hand on his and give it a gentle squeeze in an attempt to reassure him. I think it helps since I do feel his grip on my arm loosen ever so slightly."
    new "I put my hand on his and give it a gentle squeeze in an attempt to reassure him. I think it helps since I do feel his grip on my arm loosen ever so slightly.\n我把手覆在他的手上，轻轻一捏，试图安抚他。我想这起了作用，因为我确实感觉到他抓着我手臂的力道稍稍松了些。"

    old "All right, let's go. Do you have a plan? How many of them are there?"
    new "All right, let's go. Do you have a plan? How many of them are there?\n好，我们走吧。你有计划吗？他们有多少人？"

    old "Enok gestures for me to follow him. We travel quickly but prioritize stealth as we make our way through the swamp."
    new "Enok gestures for me to follow him. We travel quickly but prioritize stealth as we make our way through the swamp.\nEnok 示意我跟着他。我们走得很快，但穿过沼泽时，始终把隐蔽放在首位。"

    old "I counted four of them but they're no ordinary lizardmen. Devourers are much stronger. Taking on all four of them by ourselves would likely end in failure. We need Sylrissa's help."
    new "I counted four of them but they're no ordinary lizardmen. Devourers are much stronger. Taking on all four of them by ourselves would likely end in failure. We need Sylrissa's help.\n我数了数，一共有四个，但他们可不是普通蜥蜴人。吞噬者要强壮得多。光靠我们俩去对付四个，多半会失败。我们需要 Sylrissa 帮忙。"

    old "So we should infiltrate, free Sylrissa, and then fight our way out?"
    new "So we should infiltrate, free Sylrissa, and then fight our way out?\n所以我们应该潜入进去，救出 Sylrissa，再杀出一条路来？"

    old "I think that's our best option. Of course, the tricky part will be freeing Sylrissa and casting a regeneration spell. I won't be able to cast it without revealing our presence."
    new "I think that's our best option. Of course, the tricky part will be freeing Sylrissa and casting a regeneration spell. I won't be able to cast it without revealing our presence.\n我想这是最稳妥的办法。当然，棘手的是救出 Sylrissa 后还要施展再生咒。而我一旦施咒，就难免暴露我们的行踪。"

    old "Why do you need to cast a regeneration spell? Is Sylrissa injured?"
    new "Why do you need to cast a regeneration spell? Is Sylrissa injured?\n你为什么要施再生咒？Sylrissa 受伤了吗？"

    old "Have you forgetten? They sliced her tail so she couldn't move."
    new "Have you forgetten? They sliced her tail so she couldn't move.\n你忘了吗？他们砍断了她的尾巴，让她无法动弹。"

    old "Ah, right. The tail. You nagas are powerless without it."
    new "Ah, right. The tail. You nagas are powerless without it.\n啊，对。尾巴。你们 naga 没了尾巴就无能为力了。"

    old "It's subtle, but a catch Enok glare at me before he manages to fix his expression. I definitely made him mad with my poor choice of words. Still, instead of bringing it up, he coughs and continues talking."
    new "It's subtle, but a catch Enok glare at me before he manages to fix his expression. I definitely made him mad with my poor choice of words. Still, instead of bringing it up, he coughs and continues talking.\n虽然很细微，但我还是捕捉到 Enok 在收敛表情前瞪了我一眼。我这番话用词不当，肯定惹他生气了。不过，他并没有发作，只是轻咳一声，继续往下说。"

    old "Our tail regrows quickly, but not instantaneously. A little magic help wouldn't hurt."
    new "Our tail regrows quickly, but not instantaneously. A little magic help wouldn't hurt.\n我们的尾巴长得很快，但也不是瞬间就能长好。来点魔法帮帮忙，总没坏处。"

    old "After some time, the swamp starts to disappear as we reach the outskirts of a jungle. In the distance, I see an imposing building. Curiously, there's no sign of the fog in this area."
    new "After some time, the swamp starts to disappear as we reach the outskirts of a jungle. In the distance, I see an imposing building. Curiously, there's no sign of the fog in this area.\n走了一阵，沼泽渐渐消失，我们来到一片丛林的外围。远处，我看见一座气势恢宏的建筑。奇怪的是，这一带竟没有浓雾的迹象。"

    old "That's the Chzulu temple? It's huge!"
    new "That's the Chzulu temple? It's huge!\n那就是 Chzulu 神庙？真大！"

    old "My initial awe at it's sheer size is quickly replaced by a more troublesome thought."
    new "My initial awe at it's sheer size is quickly replaced by a more troublesome thought.\n起初对它的宏伟的惊叹，很快被一个更令人不安的念头取代。"

    old "And it's not too far from where we are..."
    new "And it's not too far from where we are...\n而且它离我们的位置并不远……"

    old "True, but it is far away enough to prevent eventual reinforcements from arriving immediately. It shouldn't be an issue."
    new "True, but it is far away enough to prevent eventual reinforcements from arriving immediately. It shouldn't be an issue.\n没错，但已经远得足以让援军无法立刻赶到。这应该不成问题。"

    old "I take it that the main difficulty will be reaching Sylrissa without being spotted. Once we free and heal her, even if we're caught, we should stand a chance against the lizardmen devourers."
    new "I take it that the main difficulty will be reaching Sylrissa without being spotted. Once we free and heal her, even if we're caught, we should stand a chance against the lizardmen devourers.\n我想，最大的困难是神不知鬼不觉地接近 Sylrissa。一旦把她救出并治好，就算被发现，我们也该有与蜥蜴人吞噬者一战的把握。"

    old "If we get caught?"
    new "If we get caught?\n如果被发现呢？"

    old "Yes, why? I think it's possible to sneak out undetected, even if Sylrissa...Oh, I get it. There's no way she'll let them live after what they did to her."
    new "Yes, why? I think it's possible to sneak out undetected, even if Sylrissa...Oh, I get it. There's no way she'll let them live after what they did to her.\n是啊，怎么了？我觉得是有可能悄悄溜出去的，即便 Sylrissa……哦，我懂了。他们那样对她，她绝不会放他们活命。"

    old "Exactly."
    new "Exactly.\n没错。"

    old "Well, what do you think we should do, [protag]? I'll let you decide."
    new "Well, what do you think we should do, [protag]? I'll let you decide.\n那么，你觉得我们该怎么办，[protag]？由你来决定。"

    old "Can you make a few more invisibility potions?"
    new "Can you make a few more invisibility potions?\n你能再多调几瓶隐形药水吗？"

    old "Enok flashes me a big smile and pulls two small vials from his waist pocket and shows them to me."
    new "Enok flashes me a big smile and pulls two small vials from his waist pocket and shows them to me.\nEnok 冲我咧嘴一笑，从腰间口袋里掏出两个小瓶子给我看。"

    old "After making the first one, I made some extras. Just in case."
    new "After making the first one, I made some extras. Just in case.\n做完第一瓶后，我又多做了几瓶，以防万一。"

    old "Good thinking."
    new "Good thinking.\n想得周到。"

    old "We still need to be careful. They won't be able to see us, but they'll be able to hear any noises we make. We need to move slowly and silently for this plan to be successful. This isn't a problem for me thanks to my tail, but you might have more trouble."
    new "We still need to be careful. They won't be able to see us, but they'll be able to hear any noises we make. We need to move slowly and silently for this plan to be successful. This isn't a problem for me thanks to my tail, but you might have more trouble.\n我们仍须小心。他们看不见我们，却听得见我们发出的任何声响。要让计划成功，我们就得缓慢而无声地移动。多亏有尾巴，这对我来说不成问题，但你可能会吃力些。"

    old "You said 'this plan'? Let me guess, you also have a second plan?"
    new "You said 'this plan'? Let me guess, you also have a second plan?\n你说了“这个计划”？让我猜猜，你还有个备选方案？"

    old "Well... yes. I was thinking that one of us could distract the lizardmen while the other focuses on rescuing Sylrissa."
    new "Well... yes. I was thinking that one of us could distract the lizardmen while the other focuses on rescuing Sylrissa.\n嗯……是的。我在想，我们可以一个去引开蜥蜴人的注意，另一个专心营救 Sylrissa。"

    old "And by one of us, you mean me. You need to be the one who rescues Sylrissa since you're the one who can cast the regeneration spell."
    new "And by one of us, you mean me. You need to be the one who rescues Sylrissa since you're the one who can cast the regeneration spell.\n而你说的“一个”，指的是我。救 Sylrissa 的人必须是你，因为只有你能施再生咒。"

    old "Ahem, yes. You're correct once again."
    new "Ahem, yes. You're correct once again.\n咳咳，没错。你又猜对了。"

    old "I know it sounds bad, but you'd only need to make some noise, catch their attention, and survive until I came back with Sylrissa and help you."
    new "I know it sounds bad, but you'd only need to make some noise, catch their attention, and survive until I came back with Sylrissa and help you.\n我知道这听着不怎么样，但你只需要弄出点动静，吸引他们的注意，然后撑到我和 Sylrissa 赶回来帮你。"

    old "I'm not sure I like this plan. Then again, at least I could prepare myself and figure out a good way to keep the distance until Sylrissa is freed. If we get caught while we're invisible they'll be much closer to us and we'll be forced to fight."
    new "I'm not sure I like this plan. Then again, at least I could prepare myself and figure out a good way to keep the distance until Sylrissa is freed. If we get caught while we're invisible they'll be much closer to us and we'll be forced to fight.\n我不太喜欢这个方案。不过话说回来，至少我能提前做好准备，想个法子保持距离，直到 Sylrissa 获救。要是在隐形时被抓住，他们离我们会近得多，我们就不得不动手了。"

    old "Okay. Here, take it. This will make us invisible for about fifteen minutes."
    new "Okay. Here, take it. This will make us invisible for about fifteen minutes.\n好。给你，拿着。这能让我们隐形大约十五分钟。"

    old "What? That's not exactly a lot of time!"
    new "What? That's not exactly a lot of time!\n什么？这点时间可不算多！"

    old "What did you expect? I had to work with what was available here in the swamp. I only had right ingredients for minor potions of invisibility."
    new "What did you expect? I had to work with what was available here in the swamp. I only had right ingredients for minor potions of invisibility.\n你还指望什么？我只能用沼泽里现成的东西。手头的原料，也只够做几瓶次级隐形药水。"

    old "Hmm, well, I guess fifteen minutes should still be plenty of time if we drink the potions just before entering the camp."
    new "Hmm, well, I guess fifteen minutes should still be plenty of time if we drink the potions just before entering the camp.\n嗯，好吧，我想只要在进营地前才喝下药水，十五分钟应该也绰绰有余。"

    old "At least, I hope."
    new "At least, I hope.\n至少，我希望如此。"

    old "Exactly. Let's get closer."
    new "Exactly. Let's get closer.\n没错。我们靠近点。"

    old "We carefully move closer to the lizardmen devourers camp. From this new vantage point, I'm able to get a better idea of how huge these lizardman actually are. And they're not just bigger either. They're heavily muscled body and lethal aura is intimidating to say the least."
    new "We carefully move closer to the lizardmen devourers camp. From this new vantage point, I'm able to get a better idea of how huge these lizardman actually are. And they're not just bigger either. They're heavily muscled body and lethal aura is intimidating to say the least.\n我们小心翼翼地靠近蜥蜴人吞噬者的营地。从这个新观察点，我更能看清这些蜥蜴人究竟有多庞大。而且他们不只是个头大。那浑身虬结的肌肉和致命的杀气，光看着就令人胆寒。"

    old "Let's drink the potions now. Any closer and we risk being seen."
    new "Let's drink the potions now. Any closer and we risk being seen.\n我们现在就喝药水吧。再靠近就有被看见的风险了。"

    old "I nod and we both drink our respective potions. I feel a slight diziness as my body turns invisible. I can't see Enok at this point either. It seems the potions are working fine-- not that I doubted Enok's skills or anything."
    new "I nod and we both drink our respective potions. I feel a slight diziness as my body turns invisible. I can't see Enok at this point either. It seems the potions are working fine-- not that I doubted Enok's skills or anything.\n我点点头，我们各自喝下药水。身体隐形的瞬间，我感到一阵轻微的晕眩。此刻我也看不见 Enok 了。看来药水效果不错——倒不是说我怀疑过 Enok 的本事。"

    old "Enok?"
    new "Enok?\nEnok？"

    old "Shhh! We must not speak until we enter the tent!"
    new "Shhh! We must not speak until we enter the tent!\n嘘！在进帐篷之前，我们不能说话！"

    old "I know, but how can I follow you if I can't see you!?"
    new "I know, but how can I follow you if I can't see you!?\n我知道，可我看不见你，怎么跟着你！？"

    old "Ah. Good point. Here, take my hand."
    new "Ah. Good point. Here, take my hand.\n啊。说得对。来，牵着我的手。"

    old "It takes me a second to find Enok's hand, but when I do, Enok's fingers gently fasten around mine. From there, I follow his lead towards the camp. Not being able to see the person leading me is a bit disconcerting, but the way we seem to glide along has a strangely natural feel to it."
    new "It takes me a second to find Enok's hand, but when I do, Enok's fingers gently fasten around mine. From there, I follow his lead towards the camp. Not being able to see the person leading me is a bit disconcerting, but the way we seem to glide along has a strangely natural feel to it.\n我花了一小会儿才摸到 Enok 的手，摸到之后，他的手指便轻轻扣住了我的手。就这样，我由他领着朝营地走去。看不见领路的人，多少让人心里没底，但我们这般滑行的姿态，却有种奇异的自然之感。"

    old "It's so natural that Enok seems to forget I'm there and speeds up. At this rate, I'm not going to be able to keep up so I pull him back. We almost stumble into each other and, while I can't see him, I can sense that his face very close to mine."
    new "It's so natural that Enok seems to forget I'm there and speeds up. At this rate, I'm not going to be able to keep up so I pull him back. We almost stumble into each other and, while I can't see him, I can sense that his face very close to mine.\n这感觉太自然了，以至于 Enok 似乎忘了我在旁边，加快了脚步。照这速度，我可跟不上，于是把他往回拽了拽。我们差点撞到一起，虽然看不见他，我却能感觉到，他的脸离我很近。"

    old "It's a fresh smell. Like rainwater with a hint of honeysuckle. It's definitely not a scent I expected to catch on him, considering he lives in the swamp."
    new "It's a fresh smell. Like rainwater with a hint of honeysuckle. It's definitely not a scent I expected to catch on him, considering he lives in the swamp.\n那是一股清新的气味，像雨水里掺着一丝金银花的香。考虑到他住在沼泽里，这气味绝不像是会出现在他身上的。"

    old "Smells nice."
    new "Smells nice.\n真好闻。"

    old "My eyes bolt open in surprise. I hadn't meant to say that aloud!"
    new "My eyes bolt open in surprise. I hadn't meant to say that aloud!\n我惊得猛地睁大眼睛。我本没打算把这话说出口！"

    old "Ehm, sorry. That was... Well, I wanted to tell you to slow down. I can't keep up with you if you go so fast."
    new "Ehm, sorry. That was... Well, I wanted to tell you to slow down. I can't keep up with you if you go so fast.\n呃，抱歉。刚才那是……嗯，我本来是想让你慢一点。你走这么快，我跟不上。"

    old "Ah, I see. I'm sorry."
    new "Ah, I see. I'm sorry.\n啊，我明白了。抱歉。"

    old "Thank you."
    new "Thank you.\n谢谢。"

    old "And, [protag]? Y-you smell nice too."
    new "And, [protag]? Y-you smell nice too.\n还有，[protag]？你、你身上的味道也很好闻。"

    old "It's a good thing we're invisible because I feel myself blushing like never before!"
    new "It's a good thing we're invisible because I feel myself blushing like never before!\n幸好我们现在隐形了，因为我感觉自己的脸从没这么红过！"

    old "Stop! You're going too fast!"
    new "Stop! You're going too fast!\n停下！你走得太快了！"

    old "O-oh! Sorry, sorry. I guess I was too eager to reach her. I'll slow down now."
    new "O-oh! Sorry, sorry. I guess I was too eager to reach her. I'll slow down now.\n哦、哦！抱歉，抱歉。我想是我太急着到她身边了。我这就放慢。"

    old "<whispering> We're entering the camp now. No more talking and no noises! Understood?"
    new "<whispering> We're entering the camp now. No more talking and no noises! Understood?\n（低语）我们这就进营地了。别再说话，也别弄出响动！明白吗？"

    old "<whispering> Yes."
    new "<whispering> Yes.\n（低语）明白。"

    old "Things go smoothly until we reach the entrance of the tent. I can't talk with Enok since we're in the middle of the camp, but we still have to get inside somehow. The problem is that there are two lizardmen standing in our way."
    new "Things go smoothly until we reach the entrance of the tent. I can't talk with Enok since we're in the middle of the camp, but we still have to get inside somehow. The problem is that there are two lizardmen standing in our way.\n一切顺利，直到我们来到帐篷入口。我们身处营地中央，我没法和 Enok 交谈，可总得设法进去。问题是，有两个蜥蜴人正挡在我们前面。"

    old "I follow Enok's lead. Together, we move as slow as possible to avoid making any noise, and..."
    new "I follow Enok's lead. Together, we move as slow as possible to avoid making any noise, and...\n我跟着 Enok 行动。我们一起尽量放慢动作，避免弄出任何响动，然后……"

    old "I follow Enok, making sure to not touch anything or make any noise, and..."
    new "I follow Enok, making sure to not touch anything or make any noise, and...\n我跟着 Enok，小心翼翼，不碰任何东西，也不发出任何声音，然后……"

    old "...we're inside, completely unnoticed! I see Sylrissa, lying on the ground. She has a few bruises, but overall she's in a much better shape than I thought we'd find her in."
    new "...we're inside, completely unnoticed! I see Sylrissa, lying on the ground. She has a few bruises, but overall she's in a much better shape than I thought we'd find her in.\n……我们进来了，完全没被发现！我看见 Sylrissa 躺在地上。她身上有几处瘀伤，但整体状况比我预想的要好得多。"

    old "<whispering> Sylrissa, it's us! [protag] and Enok! We're invisible right now. Don't make any noise, okay?"
    new "<whispering> Sylrissa, it's us! [protag] and Enok! We're invisible right now. Don't make any noise, okay?\n（低语）Sylrissa，是我们！[protag] 和 Enok！我们现在隐形了。别出声，好吗？"

    old "Uh? I thought I heard Enok's voice. This place is driving me nuts..."
    new "Uh? I thought I heard Enok's voice. This place is driving me nuts...\n呃？我好像听见了 Enok 的声音。这地方快把我逼疯了……"

    old "<whispering> I thought you were already nuts."
    new "<whispering> I thought you were already nuts.\n（低语）我还以为你早就疯了呢。"

    old "[protag]? Is that you?"
    new "[protag]? Is that you?\n[protag]？是你吗？"

    old "Before I can reply, the invisibility potions' effects vanish, revealing both me and Enok at almost the same time."
    new "Before I can reply, the invisibility potions' effects vanish, revealing both me and Enok at almost the same time.\n我还没来得及回答，隐形药水的效力便消失了，我和 Enok 几乎同时现出了身形。"

    old "What the-"
    new "What the-\n这——"

    old "<whispering> Be quiet! We're here to free you!"
    new "<whispering> Be quiet! We're here to free you!\n（低语）小声点！我们是来救你的！"

    old "Oh!"
    new "Oh!\n哦！"

    old "Thank you! I can't wait!"
    new "Thank you! I can't wait!\n谢谢！我都等不及了！"

    old "I'll bet. I'd be itching to get out of here too if I'd been held captive here for the past few days."
    new "I'll bet. I'd be itching to get out of here too if I'd been held captive here for the past few days.\n我打赌你等不及。换我被关在这里好几天，我也早就想逃出去了。"

    old "What? No, I can't wait to cut those lizardmen open for what they did to me!"
    new "What? No, I can't wait to cut those lizardmen open for what they did to me!\n什么？不，我是等不及把那些蜥蜴人开膛破肚，报他们对我做下的那些事！"

    old "Enok looks at me, half laughing with an I-told-you-so expression and says:"
    new "Enok looks at me, half laughing with an I-told-you-so expression and says:\nEnok 看着我，带着一副“我早说过吧”的表情，半笑半叹地说："

    old "What did I tell you?"
    new "What did I tell you?\n我跟你说什么来着？"

    old "I keep an eye on the tent's entrance while Enok performs his regeneration spell. Sylrissa's tail regrows at incredible pace and, soon enough, she is able to stand up again."
    new "I keep an eye on the tent's entrance while Enok performs his regeneration spell. Sylrissa's tail regrows at incredible pace and, soon enough, she is able to stand up again.\nEnok 施展再生咒时，我一直盯着帐篷入口。Sylrissa 的尾巴以惊人的速度重新生长，没过多久，她便能再次站起来了。"

    old "Yay! Now let's go kill some lizardmen!"
    new "Yay! Now let's go kill some lizardmen!\n耶！现在我们去宰几个蜥蜴人吧！"

    old "Well, if Enok's spell didn't alert the lizardman to our presence, Sylrissa's war cry certainly did."
    new "Well, if Enok's spell didn't alert the lizardman to our presence, Sylrissa's war cry certainly did.\n好吧，就算 Enok 的咒语没惊动蜥蜴人，Sylrissa 这声战吼也肯定惊动了。"

    old "Don't worry. I'll be satisfied as long as I get to kill the ones who captured me. We can slip away after that."
    new "Don't worry. I'll be satisfied as long as I get to kill the ones who captured me. We can slip away after that.\n别担心。只要让我杀了那些抓我的人，我就满足了。之后我们再溜走。"

    old "I was hoping to slip away before having to kill anyone, but I guess there's no stopping Sylrissa."
    new "I was hoping to slip away before having to kill anyone, but I guess there's no stopping Sylrissa.\n我本来盼着能不用杀人就溜掉，但看来没人拦得住 Sylrissa。"

    old "We run outside and immediately come face to face with a group of four lizardmen. Luckily, only two of them are devourers."
    new "We run outside and immediately come face to face with a group of four lizardmen. Luckily, only two of them are devourers.\n我们跑出去，立刻与四个蜥蜴人打了个照面。幸运的是，其中只有两个是吞噬者。"

    old "It's them! Those two are the bastards that need to die!"
    new "It's them! Those two are the bastards that need to die!\n就是他们！该死的正是那两个混蛋！"

    old "...unfortunately, I hit a small rock with my foot, involuntarily kicking it! It flies straight into the face of one of the lizardmen!"
    new "...unfortunately, I hit a small rock with my foot, involuntarily kicking it! It flies straight into the face of one of the lizardmen!\n……不巧，我的脚踢中了一块小石子，把它不由自主地踢飞了出去！石子径直飞向其中一个蜥蜴人的脸！"

    old "Ouch! Mossaza ussala!"
    new "Ouch! Mossaza ussala!\n哎哟！Mossaza ussala！"

    old "My lizard is a bit rusty, but I think he called you son of ... and I'll leave the rest to your imagination."
    new "My lizard is a bit rusty, but I think he called you son of ... and I'll leave the rest to your imagination.\n我的蜥蜴语有点生疏了，但我想他是在骂你是……的儿子，剩下的就留给你自己想象吧。"

    old "We're still invisible, but the Lizardmen are able to determine roughly where we are and they run in our direction. They really do have more developed senses than other races."
    new "We're still invisible, but the Lizardmen are able to determine roughly where we are and they run in our direction. They really do have more developed senses than other races.\n我们仍处于隐形状态，可蜥蜴人们还是能大致判断出我们的方位，朝我们冲来。他们的感官确实比其他种族发达。"

    old "Issiders! Loza!"
    new "Issiders! Loza!\nIssiders！Loza！"

    old "Oh, I don't think so."
    new "Oh, I don't think so.\n哦，我看未必。"

    old "The air suddenly warps, crystalizing into what I recognize as a freezing spell. It spreads rapidly, encasing the two lizardman in a layer of ice."
    new "The air suddenly warps, crystalizing into what I recognize as a freezing spell. It spreads rapidly, encasing the two lizardman in a layer of ice.\n空气骤然扭曲，凝成我所认得的冰冻咒语。它迅速蔓延，把那两个蜥蜴人裹进了一层冰里。"

    old "I'll go inside the tent and free Sylrissa. The spell should buy us some time, but you need to keep them busy until I'm done!"
    new "I'll go inside the tent and free Sylrissa. The spell should buy us some time, but you need to keep them busy until I'm done!\n我进帐篷去救 Sylrissa。这咒语能给我们争取些时间，但你得拖住他们，直到我完事！"

    old "Err, right! Please hurry. They do not look friendly!"
    new "Err, right! Please hurry. They do not look friendly!\n呃，好的！请快点。他们看起来可不友善！"

    old "I'll do what I can."
    new "I'll do what I can.\n我会尽力的。"

    old "I don't know for how long I can keep this up. Where is-"
    new "I don't know for how long I can keep this up. Where is-\n我不知道还能撑多久。人在哪儿——"

    old "The lizardmen are hit from two quick strikes from behind, getting killed instantly on the spot!"
    new "The lizardmen are hit from two quick strikes from behind, getting killed instantly on the spot!\n两个蜥蜴人背后连遭两记快击，当场毙命！"

    old "Don't worry guys! Once again, the mighty Sylrissa has arrived to save the damsel in distress!"
    new "Don't worry guys! Once again, the mighty Sylrissa has arrived to save the damsel in distress!\n别担心，伙计们！强大的 Sylrissa 再次登场，来搭救遇险的少女啦！"

    old "Damsel?"
    new "Damsel?\n少女？"

    old "Oh come on, [protag], don't get offended. It's just a saying."
    new "Oh come on, [protag], don't get offended. It's just a saying.\n拜托，[protag]，别介意。只是句玩笑话。"

    old "Haha, glad to see you too, Sylrissa."
    new "Haha, glad to see you too, Sylrissa.\n哈哈，见到你我也很高兴，Sylrissa。"

    old "Moko! Chatubass."
    new "Moko! Chatubass.\nMoko！Chatubass。"

    old "Careful, four more lizardmen have joined the fight! We need to dispatch them quickly before more arrive!"
    new "Careful, four more lizardmen have joined the fight! We need to dispatch them quickly before more arrive!\n小心，又有四个蜥蜴人加入了战斗！我们得趁更多援兵赶到之前，速战速决！"

    old "I'll catch their attention and, with any luck, I'll be quick enough to avoid any close combat."
    new "I'll catch their attention and, with any luck, I'll be quick enough to avoid any close combat.\n我去吸引他们的注意力，运气好的话，我能快到躲开任何近身搏斗。"

    old "The lizardmen are much faster in water than on the solid ground. I think you should be able to outpace them if you keep that in mind."
    new "The lizardmen are much faster in water than on the solid ground. I think you should be able to outpace them if you keep that in mind.\n蜥蜴人在水里比在陆地上快得多。只要记住这一点，我想你应该能甩开他们。"

    old "Let's hope so. But please, try to be as quick as you can."
    new "Let's hope so. But please, try to be as quick as you can.\n但愿如此。不过请你务必尽快。"

    old "I will. I'm going to the opposite side of the camp. I think Sylrissa is being held in that red tent. As soon as I hear your distraction, I will dash inside and free her."
    new "I will. I'm going to the opposite side of the camp. I think Sylrissa is being held in that red tent. As soon as I hear your distraction, I will dash inside and free her.\n我会的。我去营地另一侧。我想 Sylrissa 就被关在那个红色帐篷里。一听到你制造的动静，我就冲进去救她。"

    old "Sounds good."
    new "Sounds good.\n听起来不错。"

    old "Good luck [protag], and thanks."
    new "Good luck [protag], and thanks.\n祝你好运，[protag]，谢谢。"

    old "I get in position behind a bush and try to follow Enok's movement as much as I can."
    new "I get in position behind a bush and try to follow Enok's movement as much as I can.\n我在一丛灌木后站好位置，尽量盯着 Enok 的动向。"

    old "Unfortunately, because of the dense jungle foliage, I lose sight of him. I wait a bit longer to make sure he's had enough time to get in position and then start making noise."
    new "Unfortunately, because of the dense jungle foliage, I lose sight of him. I wait a bit longer to make sure he's had enough time to get in position and then start making noise.\n可惜丛林枝叶茂密，我很快就看不见他了。我又多等了一会儿，确保他有足够时间就位，然后开始弄出声响。"

    old "Hey! You dumb grown up lizards!"
    new "Hey! You dumb grown up lizards!\n嘿！你们这些傻乎乎的大蜥蜴！"

    old "Oko? Ssshen!"
    new "Oko? Ssshen!\nOko？Ssshen！"

    old "Yes, I'm talking about you! Stupid creature! I came to kill you all!"
    new "Yes, I'm talking about you! Stupid creature! I came to kill you all!\n对，说的就是你们！蠢东西！我是来把你们全杀光的！"

    old "Tamaka. Eraze!"
    new "Tamaka. Eraze!\nTamaka。Eraze！"

    old "The two lizardman rush towards me."
    new "The two lizardman rush towards me.\n那两个蜥蜴人朝我冲来。"

    old "What did Enok say? They're slower on solid ground? They still seem pretty damn quick to me!"
    new "What did Enok say? They're slower on solid ground? They still seem pretty damn quick to me!\nEnok 是怎么说的？他们在陆地上更慢？在我看来，他们还是快得要命！"

    old "Those lizardman are fast, but let's see how much endurance they have. Hopefully not more than me..."
    new "Those lizardman are fast, but let's see how much endurance they have. Hopefully not more than me...\n那些蜥蜴人是快，可我倒要看看他们的耐力如何。但愿不比我的强……"

    old "Beside running, I could try to push them to the ground as soon as they get close. This should slow down and maybe injure them..."
    new "Beside running, I could try to push them to the ground as soon as they get close. This should slow down and maybe injure them...\n除了奔跑，我还可以等他们一靠近，就把他们扑倒在地。这应该能拖慢他们，说不定还能伤到他们……"

    old "I am not sure how I manage to do it, but I'm somehow able to keep them at bay for a long time. At least, it seems long to me."
    new "I am not sure how I manage to do it, but I'm somehow able to keep them at bay for a long time. At least, it seems long to me.\n我不确定自己是怎么做到的，但我竟把他们挡在远处撑了很久。至少在我看来，那已经很久了。"

    old "Mouha hazan!"
    new "Mouha hazan!\nMouha hazan！"

    old "What? Three more? This is a joke right?"
    new "What? Three more? This is a joke right?\n什么？又来三个？这是开玩笑吧？"

    old "Two of them, I could manage. But five? My tricks won't work once they have me surrounded."
    new "Two of them, I could manage. But five? My tricks won't work once they have me surrounded.\n两个我还能应付。可五个？一旦他们把我围住，我的把戏就不灵了。"

    old "And those three are devourers... Which, of course, means they're more dangerous than the others."
    new "And those three are devourers... Which, of course, means they're more dangerous than the others.\n而且新来的三个还是吞噬者……这当然意味着，他们比其他的更危险。"

    old "I try my best, but honestly keeping two lizardmen at a distance is a difficult task. While moving, I trip on a tree root and fall face down on the ground."
    new "I try my best, but honestly keeping two lizardmen at a distance is a difficult task. While moving, I trip on a tree root and fall face down on the ground.\n我尽了全力，可说实话，要和两个蜥蜴人保持距离绝非易事。移动中，我被树根绊了一下，面朝下摔倒在地。"

    old "The two lizardmen seize the opportunity and close the gap. One of them celebrates by kicking me in the chest."
    new "The two lizardmen seize the opportunity and close the gap. One of them celebrates by kicking me in the chest.\n两个蜥蜴人抓住机会逼近。其中一个甚至一脚踢在我胸口，算是庆祝。"

    old "I grit my teeth and try to absorb the blow, but a whimper of pain still manages to escape from my mouth."
    new "I grit my teeth and try to absorb the blow, but a whimper of pain still manages to escape from my mouth.\n我咬紧牙关，想硬扛下这一击，却仍有一声痛苦的呜咽从嘴里泄了出来。"

    old "I roll to the side and manage to avoid the lizardmen long enough to get to my feet. To my dismay, however, I see that three more lizardmen have arrived. Not normal ones either, devourers. I'm not generally someone who trembles in fear, but, in this instance, I begin shaking involuntarily."
    new "I roll to the side and manage to avoid the lizardmen long enough to get to my feet. To my dismay, however, I see that three more lizardmen have arrived. Not normal ones either, devourers. I'm not generally someone who trembles in fear, but, in this instance, I begin shaking involuntarily.\n我向旁一滚，勉强躲开蜥蜴人，站起身来。然而令我沮丧的是，我看见又来了三个蜥蜴人——还不是普通的，而是吞噬者。我一般不是个会因恐惧而发抖的人，但此刻，我的身体却不自觉地开始颤抖。"

    old "Is this how it all ends? Devoured alive by lizardmen in a unknown camp in the jungle?"
    new "Is this how it all ends? Devoured alive by lizardmen in a unknown camp in the jungle?\n难道一切就这样结束了吗？在丛林里一处无名营地，被蜥蜴人活活吞食？"

    old "Before I can finish my thought, I hear the flashing sound of metal followed by the disgusting plop of splattered meat as the top half of one of the devourers hits the ground. The bottom half of the severed corpse follows shortly after."
    new "Before I can finish my thought, I hear the flashing sound of metal followed by the disgusting plop of splattered meat as the top half of one of the devourers hits the ground. The bottom half of the severed corpse follows shortly after.\n还没等我想完，就听见金属破空的锐响，随后是血肉四溅、令人作呕的闷响——一个吞噬者的上半身砸在地上，被斩断的下半身紧接着也倒了下去。"

    old "Gotcha!"
    new "Gotcha!\n抓到你了！"

    old "See that devourer on the ground? He was the one who kindly cut my tail awhile back. Now that Enok's healed me up, I felt it was time to return the favor."
    new "See that devourer on the ground? He was the one who kindly cut my tail awhile back. Now that Enok's healed me up, I felt it was time to return the favor.\n看到地上那个吞噬者了吗？当初“好心”砍掉我尾巴的就是他。如今 Enok 把我治好了，我觉得是时候回敬他一下了。"

    old "Except that you cut his whole body in half, not his tail."
    new "Except that you cut his whole body in half, not his tail.\n只是你把他整个人劈成了两半，而不是只砍尾巴。"

    old "What can I say? I'm a generous person. I always like to give more than I got."
    new "What can I say? I'm a generous person. I always like to give more than I got.\n我能说什么呢？我这人大方，总喜欢加倍奉还。"

    old "Just a little, yes. As usual."
    new "Just a little, yes. As usual.\n只多一点，是的。一如既往。"

    old "...Hazel?"
    new "...Hazel?\n……Hazel？"

    old "Sylrissa! Enok! My sources were right. After all this time, I finally find you. It's time to end this once for all."
    new "Sylrissa! Enok! My sources were right. After all this time, I finally find you. It's time to end this once for all.\nSylrissa！Enok！我的情报没错。找了这么久，我终于找到你们了。是时候把这一切彻底了结了。"

    old "Wait. This is not a lizardman. What is happening here?"
    new "Wait. This is not a lizardman. What is happening here?\n等等。这不是蜥蜴人。这到底是怎么回事？"

    old "Kind of a long story-"
    new "Kind of a long story-\n说来话长——"

    old "Those two traitors left our tribe! The sentence is death! I came to take their lives."
    new "Those two traitors left our tribe! The sentence is death! I came to take their lives.\n这两个叛徒离开了我们的部落！他们被判了死刑！我是来取他们性命的。"

    old "Well, Hazel did a pretty good with 'the short version of the story'."
    new "Well, Hazel did a pretty good with 'the short version of the story'.\n嗯，Hazel 这“简短版”讲得倒挺不错。"

    old "The other lizardmen charge at us. We need to run, but we're going to have to deal with Hazel and the lizardmen group in front of us first."
    new "The other lizardmen charge at us. We need to run, but we're going to have to deal with Hazel and the lizardmen group in front of us first.\n其余的蜥蜴人朝我们冲来。我们必须逃跑，但得先解决掉面前的 Hazel 和这群蜥蜴人。"

    old "I hear more noise coming from the temple's direction. We need to run before we get overwhelmed!"
    new "I hear more noise coming from the temple's direction. We need to run before we get overwhelmed!\n我听见神庙方向传来更多声响。我们得在被彻底围困之前逃走！"

    old "Yeah, my thirst for revenge is satisfied for now. We can go."
    new "Yeah, my thirst for revenge is satisfied for now. We can go.\n是啊，我复仇的渴望暂时满足了。我们走吧。"

    old "We quickly flee the camp and don't stop running until we reach the swamp. I don't see any more signs of lizardmen chasing us. I think we made it."
    new "We quickly flee the camp and don't stop running until we reach the swamp. I don't see any more signs of lizardmen chasing us. I think we made it.\n我们迅速逃离营地，一路狂奔到沼泽才停下。我没再看到蜥蜴人追来的迹象。我想我们成功了。"

    old "We should be safe now."
    new "We should be safe now.\n我们现在应该安全了。"

    old "Sylrissa."
    new "Sylrissa.\nSylrissa。"

    old "They both smile and then wrap their arms around each other in a hug. It lingers longer than I'm comfortable with, making me feel like I'm intruding on the moment. I take a space back, intending to give them a little space, when Sylrissa's eyes meet mine. She crooks her finger at me, beckoning me to join them."
    new "They both smile and then wrap their arms around each other in a hug. It lingers longer than I'm comfortable with, making me feel like I'm intruding on the moment. I take a space back, intending to give them a little space, when Sylrissa's eyes meet mine. She crooks her finger at me, beckoning me to join them.\n两人相视一笑，然后张开双臂拥抱在一起。这一抱持续得比我觉得自在的时长还久，让我感到自己像是打扰了这一刻。我后退一步，想给他们留点空间，这时 Sylrissa 的目光与我相遇。她朝我勾了勾手指，招呼我加入他们。"

    old "[protag], you came back for me too."
    new "[protag], you came back for me too.\n[protag]，你也是回来找我的。"

    old "Is Sylrissa crying? I see water form at the edge of her eyes, but I can't be sure if it's sweat from the run or tears of joy."
    new "Is Sylrissa crying? I see water form at the edge of her eyes, but I can't be sure if it's sweat from the run or tears of joy.\nSylrissa 在哭吗？我看见她眼角有水光，却分不清那是奔跑出的汗，还是喜悦的泪。"

    old "I am an inspiration to everyone, aren't I?"
    new "I am an inspiration to everyone, aren't I?\n我是不是很能鼓舞大家？"

    old "Err... I was thinking more along the lines of you raising their morale with your involuntarily hilarious behavior."
    new "Err... I was thinking more along the lines of you raising their morale with your involuntarily hilarious behavior.\n呃……我想的更像是，你用自己那不自觉的滑稽举动提升了大家的士气。"

    old "Haha, nice, [protag]. You shouldn't underestimate humor though. Sometimes, in the darkest moments, it's the only thing that keeps you sane."
    new "Haha, nice, [protag]. You shouldn't underestimate humor though. Sometimes, in the darkest moments, it's the only thing that keeps you sane.\n哈哈，说得好，[protag]。不过你可别小看幽默。有时在最黑暗的时刻，它是唯一能让你保持清醒的东西。"

    old "True. Well said, Sylrissa."
    new "True. Well said, Sylrissa.\n没错。说得好，Sylrissa。"

    old "Aww, you're so sweet, [protag]!"
    new "Aww, you're so sweet, [protag]!\n哎呀，你真好，[protag]！"

    old "She moves closer to me, places her hands on her heart, and winks at me as she speaks in a soft, charming voice:"
    new "She moves closer to me, places her hands on her heart, and winks at me as she speaks in a soft, charming voice:\n她凑近我，双手按在心口，一边朝我眨眼，一边用柔美迷人的嗓音说："

    old "You make my little snake heart go bum bum."
    new "You make my little snake heart go bum bum.\n你让我这颗小蛇心扑通扑通地跳呢。"

    old "I am sure that she is doing it just to tease me but... she's succeeding. My heartbeat quickens and I begin feeling a bit hot."
    new "I am sure that she is doing it just to tease me but... she's succeeding. My heartbeat quickens and I begin feeling a bit hot.\n我确信她这么做只是想逗我，可……她成功了。我的心跳加速，身上也开始有点发烫。"

    old "Stop it, Sylrissa. [protag] just rescued you and you want to make [heshe] have a heart attack?"
    new "Stop it, Sylrissa. [protag] just rescued you and you want to make [heshe] have a heart attack?\n别闹了，Sylrissa。[protag] 刚救了你，你就想害[heshe]心脏病发作吗？"

    old "We all laugh and relax. Though... I'm not sure, but was that a hint of jealously I detected in Enok's comment?"
    new "We all laugh and relax. Though... I'm not sure, but was that a hint of jealously I detected in Enok's comment?\n我们都笑了起来，放松下来。虽然……我不太确定，但 Enok 那句话里，我是不是听出了一丝醋意？"

    old "We stand there hugging each other for a good minute. I think I've gained their loyalty forever in this moment."
    new "We stand there hugging each other for a good minute. I think I've gained their loyalty forever in this moment.\n我们站在那里，彼此拥抱了好一会儿。我想，在这一刻，我已永远赢得了他们的忠诚。"

    old "So, next stop is N'Mar, right?"
    new "So, next stop is N'Mar, right?\n那么，下一站就是 N'Mar 了，对吧？"

    old "Haha. I was hoping you were going to say that."
    new "Haha. I was hoping you were going to say that.\n哈哈。我就盼着你这么说呢。"

    old "You bet. No one has ever shown so much interest in me before- apart from Enok, of course."
    new "You bet. No one has ever shown so much interest in me before- apart from Enok, of course.\n那当然。除了 Enok，还从没有人对我这么上心过。"

    old "I'll be frank with you, [protag]: I don't know shit about the human empire and I don't care what happens to them, but what you did today... You've earned my trust. I'll follow you wherever you want, [protag]."
    new "I'll be frank with you, [protag]: I don't know shit about the human empire and I don't care what happens to them, but what you did today... You've earned my trust. I'll follow you wherever you want, [protag].\n我跟你直说吧，[protag]：我对人类帝国一无所知，也不在乎他们死活，但你今天的所作所为……赢得了我的信任。你想去哪儿，我就跟你去哪儿，[protag]。"

    old "And I'll gladly take you with me, Sylrissa."
    new "And I'll gladly take you with me, Sylrissa.\n我也很乐意带你一起走，Sylrissa。"

    old "I leave the swamp with a newfound ally and higher morale than before."
    new "I leave the swamp with a newfound ally and higher morale than before.\n我带着一位新结的盟友，以及比先前更高昂的士气，离开了沼泽。"

    old "I can already tell that today is going to be a busy day."
    new "I can already tell that today is going to be a busy day.\n我已经预感到，今天会是很忙的一天。"

    old "First, I need to meet with some of the council members to discuss matters regarding what's going on at N'Mar. After that, I'll have to make the usual rounds meeting up with the other members in my party before I can-"
    new "First, I need to meet with some of the council members to discuss matters regarding what's going on at N'Mar. After that, I'll have to make the usual rounds meeting up with the other members in my party before I can-\n首先，我得见几位议员，商讨有关 N'Mar 眼下局势的事。之后，我还得照例去和队里的其他成员碰头，然后才能——"

    old "[protag]? You're [protag] right?"
    new "[protag]? You're [protag] right?\n[protag]？你就是 [protag]，对吧？"

    old "Yes. Who's asking?"
    new "Yes. Who's asking?\n是的。你是哪位？"

    old "I'm only a messenger. I was told to deliver this urgent message to you."
    new "I'm only a messenger. I was told to deliver this urgent message to you.\n我只是个信使。有人托我把这封紧急信件交给你。"

    old "The boy hands me a letter and then dismisses himself, hurrying off to his next delivery. I unfold it, noting that the parchment the letter is written on has a familiar yet slightly unpleasant smell to it."
    new "The boy hands me a letter and then dismisses himself, hurrying off to his next delivery. I unfold it, noting that the parchment the letter is written on has a familiar yet slightly unpleasant smell to it.\n男孩把信递给我，随后便告退了，匆匆赶去送下一封信。我展开信纸，注意到写信用的羊皮纸上有股熟悉却又略让人不悦的气味。"

    old "Let's see... What do we have here?"
    new "Let's see... What do we have here?\n让我看看……这上面写了什么？"

    old "I begin reading the letter out loud."
    new "I begin reading the letter out loud.\n我开始大声读起信来。"

    old "Dear [protag], I need your help! Bring me: olive oil, salt, pepper, lemon--"
    new "Dear [protag], I need your help! Bring me: olive oil, salt, pepper, lemon--\n亲爱的 [protag]，我需要你的帮忙！给我带：橄榄油、盐、胡椒、柠檬——"

    old "Hold on... Is this for a food recipe?"
    new "Hold on... Is this for a food recipe?\n等等……这是份食谱吗？"

    old "I scan the rest of the list, noting that all of the other items seem to line up with that theory."
    new "I scan the rest of the list, noting that all of the other items seem to line up with that theory.\n我扫了一遍清单的其余部分，发现其他各项似乎也都印证了这个猜想。"

    old "Hm. Maybe the urgent part is at the end of the letter?"
    new "Hm. Maybe the urgent part is at the end of the letter?\n嗯。也许紧急的部分在信尾？"

    old "I continue reading to find that the rest of the letter consists of instructions regarding how I should go about picking the best ingredients."
    new "I continue reading to find that the rest of the letter consists of instructions regarding how I should go about picking the best ingredients.\n我继续读下去，发现信的其余部分全是教我该如何挑选上等食材的说明。"

    old "Signed, Enok, battlemage and aspiring cook."
    new "Signed, Enok, battlemage and aspiring cook.\n落款：Enok，战斗法师，兼志向远大的厨师。"

    old "I flip the parchment over, making sure I didn't miss anything but that's it. That's the end of the letter."
    new "I flip the parchment over, making sure I didn't miss anything but that's it. That's the end of the letter.\n我把羊皮纸翻过来，确认没有漏掉什么，但仅此而已。信到这儿就结束了。"

    old "I don't think this is code for anything either."
    new "I don't think this is code for anything either.\n我也不觉得这是什么暗语。"

    old "Enok seriously sent me an 'urgent' letter regarding food."
    new "Enok seriously sent me an 'urgent' letter regarding food.\nEnok 竟真为吃的，给我寄了封“紧急”信。"

    old "Well, as odd as it is, I might as well get him the ingredients he asked for. They're all easy enough to find here in Grimoire and part of my job does involve keeping my team members happy."
    new "Well, as odd as it is, I might as well get him the ingredients he asked for. They're all easy enough to find here in Grimoire and part of my job does involve keeping my team members happy.\n好吧，虽然古怪，我还是去把他要的食材买了吧。这些东西在 Grimoire 都挺好找，而且让队友开心，本就是我工作的一部分。"

    old "I let out a sigh and then resign myself to purchasing the requested items."
    new "I let out a sigh and then resign myself to purchasing the requested items.\n我叹了口气，认命地去采购那些列出的物品。"

    old "Once I've done that, I head to the swamps and meet up with Enok who breaks out in a wide smile when he sees what I'm carrying."
    new "Once I've done that, I head to the swamps and meet up with Enok who breaks out in a wide smile when he sees what I'm carrying.\n办完这些，我便前往沼泽去见 Enok。他一看到我拎的东西，立刻咧开了大大的笑容。"

    old "You got the message then!"
    new "You got the message then!\n这么说你收到信了！"

    old "Yes, the very 'urgent message'."
    new "Yes, the very 'urgent message'.\n是啊，那封“非常紧急的信”。"

    old "Sorry if I alarmed you, but I wanted to make sure I got the ingredients today."
    new "Sorry if I alarmed you, but I wanted to make sure I got the ingredients today.\n抱歉让你受惊了，可我想确保今天就能拿到食材。"

    old "Why today?"
    new "Why today?\n为什么非要今天？"

    old "Because of this!"
    new "Because of this!\n因为这个！"

    old "Enok goes and fetches a large, golden colored fish and shows it to me proudly. I'm not exactly a fish expert, but I'm guessing that this is a rare one."
    new "Enok goes and fetches a large, golden colored fish and shows it to me proudly. I'm not exactly a fish expert, but I'm guessing that this is a rare one.\nEnok 去取来一条金灿灿的大鱼，得意地展示给我看。我不算什么鱼类专家，但猜这应该是条稀罕货。"

    old "It's a Loka Fish. As far as I know, they only live in the cold, salty water up north near where the lizardmen live."
    new "It's a Loka Fish. As far as I know, they only live in the cold, salty water up north near where the lizardmen live.\n这是 Loka Fish。据我所知，它们只生活在北边靠近蜥蜴人聚居地的那片寒冷咸水里。"

    old "Please don't tell me you went back up there to catch a fish. You know how dangerous that area is."
    new "Please don't tell me you went back up there to catch a fish. You know how dangerous that area is.\n拜托别告诉我，你又跑回那儿去抓鱼了。你知道那片地方有多危险。"

    old "Of course not! I wanted the fish, but I'm not crazy."
    new "Of course not! I wanted the fish, but I'm not crazy.\n当然没有！我是想要这条鱼，可我又没疯。"

    old "I, um... I used a dark magic spell called 'possess animal' to mind control it from a distance. After that, all i needed to do was swim down the river and let Sylrissa pierce me with one of her daggers."
    new "I, um... I used a dark magic spell called 'possess animal' to mind control it from a distance. After that, all i needed to do was swim down the river and let Sylrissa pierce me with one of her daggers.\n我，呃……我用了个叫 possess animal 的黑暗魔法咒语，从远处操控了它的心智。之后，我只需要顺着河游下去，让 Sylrissa 用她的匕首刺中我。"

    old "Pierce you?"
    new "Pierce you?\n刺中你？"

    old "Err, yes. As the fish. Sorry. I didn't explain that, did I? I take over the fish's consciousness during the duration of the spell so I end up seeing and feeling everything it does."
    new "Err, yes. As the fish. Sorry. I didn't explain that, did I? I take over the fish's consciousness during the duration of the spell so I end up seeing and feeling everything it does.\n呃，对。是作为那条鱼。抱歉，我没解释清楚，是吧？施咒期间，我会接管鱼的意识，所以它看到什么、感受到什么，我也都会看到、感受到。"

    old "I couldn't risk letting the fish get away so I maintained it while Sylrissa stabbed me. It hurt quite a bit, but I'd say it was worth it."
    new "I couldn't risk letting the fish get away so I maintained it while Sylrissa stabbed me. It hurt quite a bit, but I'd say it was worth it.\n我不能冒险让鱼跑掉，所以在 Sylrissa 刺我的时候，我一直维持着法术。虽然疼得厉害，但我觉得值了。"

    old "Getting stabbed by Sylrissa? Yeah. I'm sure it was worth it."
    new "Getting stabbed by Sylrissa? Yeah. I'm sure it was worth it.\n被 Sylrissa 刺一刀？是啊，我敢说肯定值。"

    old "Judging by the sarcasm in your tone, I can assume that you've never eaten one of these?"
    new "Judging by the sarcasm in your tone, I can assume that you've never eaten one of these?\n从你话里的嘲讽劲儿来看，我猜你从没吃过这种鱼？"

    old "I haven't."
    new "I haven't.\n我没吃过。"

    old "Well, lucky you! Today you'll be able to try one! And I get to use this great recipe straight from Dingirra!"
    new "Well, lucky you! Today you'll be able to try one! And I get to use this great recipe straight from Dingirra!\n那你可真有口福！今天你就能尝到一条了！而且我还能用上这份正宗的 Dingirra 秘方！"

    old "Dingirra?!"
    new "Dingirra?!\nDingirra？！"

    old "Yes. You know where that is?"
    new "Yes. You know where that is?\n是的。你知道那是哪儿吗？"

    old "I know it's in Zoltar."
    new "I know it's in Zoltar.\n我知道它在 Zoltar。"

    old "Once, when I went to collect money, a man who couldn't pay me in gold offered me Dingirran Chocolate instead. I was reluctant to accept it at first, but he eventually managed to convince me it was worth more than the sum he owed."
    new "Once, when I went to collect money, a man who couldn't pay me in gold offered me Dingirran Chocolate instead. I was reluctant to accept it at first, but he eventually managed to convince me it was worth more than the sum he owed.\n有一次我去收账，一个还不起金币的人提出用 Dingirran Chocolate 抵债。起初我不太情愿接受，但最后他还是说服了我，说那东西比他所欠的还要值钱。"

    old "Interesting. Was it?"
    new "Interesting. Was it?\n有意思。真的值吗？"

    old "Turns out, it was. I even got a decent amount of bonus pay when I broght it back!"
    new "Turns out, it was. I even got a decent amount of bonus pay when I broght it back!\n结果证明，还真值。我把它带回去，还额外领了一笔相当可观的赏钱呢！"

    old "Every worthwhile merchant has traveled to Dingirra at least once. Their magic portals are really convenient."
    new "Every worthwhile merchant has traveled to Dingirra at least once. Their magic portals are really convenient.\n每个上得了台面的商人，都至少去过一次 Dingirra。他们的魔法传送门实在太方便了。"

    old "Oh, yes! I've heard of those. They're supposed to be really powerful."
    new "Oh, yes! I've heard of those. They're supposed to be really powerful.\n哦，对！我听说过。据说那些传送门非常厉害。"

    old "They are. But they also cost a lot to make. And forget about buying one. Anyway, to answer your original question, yes, I've been there."
    new "They are. But they also cost a lot to make. And forget about buying one. Anyway, to answer your original question, yes, I've been there.\n确实厉害。可它们的造价也高得惊人，想买一座更是想都别想。总之，回到你最初的问题，是的，我去过那儿。"

    old "I once composed a ballad about a Dragon and four heroes that took place in Dingirra. At least, I think it was a dragon... No. Wait, yes. At least, I'm pretty sure. If I'm being completely honest, I can't quite remember."
    new "I once composed a ballad about a Dragon and four heroes that took place in Dingirra. At least, I think it was a dragon... No. Wait, yes. At least, I'm pretty sure. If I'm being completely honest, I can't quite remember.\n我曾为一场发生在 Dingirra 的 Dragon 与四位英雄的故事写过一首歌谣。至少，我记得那是一条龙……不，等等，没错。至少我相当确定。可说实话，我记不太清了。"

    old "What kind of bard forgets the songs they compose?"
    new "What kind of bard forgets the songs they compose?\n什么样的吟游诗人会忘掉自己写的歌？"

    old "It was over five years ago! And I had to sing it in the ancient dingirran language. I'd like to see you try to remember it."
    new "It was over five years ago! And I had to sing it in the ancient dingirran language. I'd like to see you try to remember it.\n那都是五年多前的事了！而且我还得用古老的 dingirran 语唱。我倒想看看你试试能不能记住。"

    old "I would. I have a good memory."
    new "I would. I have a good memory.\n我会的。我记性很好。"

    old "Hmph. I guess the point is that, yes, I know about Dingirra."
    new "Hmph. I guess the point is that, yes, I know about Dingirra.\n哼。我想重点在于，没错，我了解 Dingirra。"

    old "I've always been fascinated by their teleportation portals. I mean, they're amazing feats of magic on their own, but when you consider how they've been applied to large scale commerce they become even more interesting. It's something both ingenious and risky."
    new "I've always been fascinated by their teleportation portals. I mean, they're amazing feats of magic on their own, but when you consider how they've been applied to large scale commerce they become even more interesting. It's something both ingenious and risky.\n我一直对他们的传送门着迷不已。它们本身已是了不起的魔法造物，可再想想它们被用于大规模商贸，就愈发有趣了。那东西既巧妙，又充满风险。"

    old "Risky?"
    new "Risky?\n有风险？"

    old "Yes. It's actually very easy to teleport yourself to the wrong place. The dingirrans have perfected their magic for the most part, but from the research I've done that took a lot of trial and error. Their first expeditions didn't always go so well."
    new "Yes. It's actually very easy to teleport yourself to the wrong place. The dingirrans have perfected their magic for the most part, but from the research I've done that took a lot of trial and error. Their first expeditions didn't always go so well.\n是的。其实很容易把自己传送到错误的地方。dingirran 人的魔法大体上已经炉火纯青，但据我所做的研究，那也是历经无数次试错才达到的。他们最初的几次远征，可并不总那么顺利。"

    old "Let me guess: caravans teleported in the middle of the ocean?"
    new "Let me guess: caravans teleported in the middle of the ocean?\n让我猜猜：商队被传送到了汪洋中央？"

    old "If they were lucky."
    new "If they were lucky.\n那还算他们走运。"

    old "Lucky?"
    new "Lucky?\n走运？"

    old "There are worse places to end up. For instance, the inside of a volcano. A few of the caravans were unfortunate enough to meet that particular fate."
    new "There are worse places to end up. For instance, the inside of a volcano. A few of the caravans were unfortunate enough to meet that particular fate.\n还有更糟糕的去处呢。比如火山内部。就有那么几支商队不幸落得了那种下场。"

    old "That's terrible."
    new "That's terrible.\n太可怕了。"

    old "Anyway. Sorry for interrupting: you were saying that this is a Dingirran recipe? How'd you get your hands on it?"
    new "Anyway. Sorry for interrupting: you were saying that this is a Dingirran recipe? How'd you get your hands on it?\n总之，抱歉打断你：你刚说这是份 Dingirran 菜谱？你是怎么弄到手的？"

    old "Ahem, about that... I found it on the ground on the road to Grimoire..."
    new "Ahem, about that... I found it on the ground on the road to Grimoire...\n咳咳，这个嘛……是我在通往 Grimoire 的路上捡到的……"

    old "Enok... I may not know you that well yet, but the one thing I know for sure is that you're not very good at lying to me."
    new "Enok... I may not know you that well yet, but the one thing I know for sure is that you're not very good at lying to me.\nEnok……我可能还不太了解你，但有件事我很确定：你不太会对我撒谎。"

    old "All right, all right! I got it from a merchant who was passing by the swamps."
    new "All right, all right! I got it from a merchant who was passing by the swamps.\n好吧，好吧！我是从一个路过沼泽的商人那里弄来的。"

    old "Ugh. Enok, please don't steal anymore!"
    new "Ugh. Enok, please don't steal anymore!\n唉。Enok，求你别再偷东西了！"

    old "Really? We have an assassin in our ranks and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?"
    new "Really? We have an assassin in our ranks and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?\n真的吗？我们队伍里有个刺客，你却操心我偷了一张小纸片？"

    old "Really? We have a berserker in our ranks and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?"
    new "Really? We have a berserker in our ranks and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?\n真的吗？我们队伍里有个狂战士，你却操心我偷了一张小纸片？"

    old "Really? We are facing a undead threat never seen before, and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?"
    new "Really? We are facing a undead threat never seen before, and you're concerned about me stealing a small piece of paper?\n真的吗？我们正面临前所未见的不死之患，你却操心我偷了一张小纸片？"

    old "...I guess that's a fair point."
    new "...I guess that's a fair point.\n……我想这话说得在理。"

    old "Besides, I didn't steal it. I convinced him to give it to me using my charm."
    new "Besides, I didn't steal it. I convinced him to give it to me using my charm.\n而且我也没偷。我是用我的魅力说服他送给我的。"

    old "Oops, did I really say that out loud?"
    new "Oops, did I really say that out loud?\n哎呀，我该不会真把这话说出口了吧？"

    old "Enok responds with an amused chuckle."
    new "Enok responds with an amused chuckle.\nEnok 发出一声觉得好笑的轻笑。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. I'm pleased that you noticed my charm."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. I'm pleased that you noticed my charm.\n谢谢你，[protag]。我很高兴你注意到了我的魅力。"

    old "In my embarrassment, I avoid making eye contact with Enok and instead pretend to have taken a renewed interest in the fish."
    new "In my embarrassment, I avoid making eye contact with Enok and instead pretend to have taken a renewed interest in the fish.\n我窘迫地避开与 Enok 的眼神接触，转而装出对那条鱼重新来了兴致的样子。"

    old "Yes, yes. So he just gave it to you?"
    new "Yes, yes. So he just gave it to you?\n是，是。所以他就那么送给你了？"

    old "I already told you! I didn't pay anything for it. The man gave it to me as a gift."
    new "I already told you! I didn't pay anything for it. The man gave it to me as a gift.\n我不是说了嘛！我没花一分钱。是那人把它当礼物送给我的。"

    old "Enok crosses his arms, suddenly looking a bit irritated with me."
    new "Enok crosses his arms, suddenly looking a bit irritated with me.\nEnok 抱起双臂，忽然显得有些生我的气。"

    old "Really. We talked a bit and I... Well, I may have flirted with him a bit and-"
    new "Really. We talked a bit and I... Well, I may have flirted with him a bit and-\n真的。我们聊了会儿，然后我……嗯，我可能跟他调了会儿情，然后——"

    old "I didn't know you were into men."
    new "I didn't know you were into men.\n我不知道你还喜欢男人。"

    old "Hm, really? We haven't told you that nagas are bisexual yet?"
    new "Hm, really? We haven't told you that nagas are bisexual yet?\n嗯，真的吗？我们还没告诉过你，naga 是双性恋？"

    old "Ah, right. I think you did tell me that. Or was Sylrissa? Anyway, you're telling me that you seduced that merchant and conned him into giving away this precious recipe?"
    new "Ah, right. I think you did tell me that. Or was Sylrissa? Anyway, you're telling me that you seduced that merchant and conned him into giving away this precious recipe?\n啊，对。我想你们确实告诉过我。还是 Sylrissa 说的？总之，你的意思是，你勾引了那个商人，骗他交出了这份珍贵的菜谱？"

    old "Absolutely not! It's not like that at all. And it's not like he's going to miss it either. He didn't even know what it was. Besides, it wasn't like he didn't get anything in return. His cart got stuck in a hole in the ground and I helped him lift the cart."
    new "Absolutely not! It's not like that at all. And it's not like he's going to miss it either. He didn't even know what it was. Besides, it wasn't like he didn't get anything in return. His cart got stuck in a hole in the ground and I helped him lift the cart.\n绝对不是！事情完全不是那样。再说，他也不会惦记这东西——他根本不知道那是什么。何况，他也不是没得到回报。他的货车陷进了地上的坑里，是我帮他把车抬出来的。"

    old "You used brute force? That doesn't sound like you."
    new "You used brute force? That doesn't sound like you.\n你用蛮力？这可不像你的作风。"

    old "Of course not. I used a minor version of my tornado spell to dislodge the cart. It got the job done just fine."
    new "Of course not. I used a minor version of my tornado spell to dislodge the cart. It got the job done just fine.\n当然没有。我用了低阶版的龙卷风咒语把车弄了出来。事情办得挺顺当。"

    old "Heh. Figures."
    new "Heh. Figures.\n嘿。果然如此。"

    old "Anyway, if that merchant willingly, more or less, gave you the recipe in exchange for your help I guess that's okay."
    new "Anyway, if that merchant willingly, more or less, gave you the recipe in exchange for your help I guess that's okay.\n总之，如果那商人或多或少是自愿地、拿菜谱换取你的帮助，那我想也说得过去。"

    old "Exactly. It was a mutual agreement!"
    new "Exactly. It was a mutual agreement!\n没错。这是一桩双方情愿的交易！"

    old "I still don't feel like I'm getting the whole truth from Enok, but I have more pressing matters to attend to. I'm not going to spend more time worrying about some recipe."
    new "I still don't feel like I'm getting the whole truth from Enok, but I have more pressing matters to attend to. I'm not going to spend more time worrying about some recipe.\n我仍觉得自己没从 Enok 那里听到全部实情，但我还有更要紧的事要办，不想再为一张菜谱多费心思。"

    old "Now, if you're done questioning me, I'd like to get started."
    new "Now, if you're done questioning me, I'd like to get started.\n好了，你要是盘问完了，我想开做了。"

    old "I let Enok off the hook for now and take a seat nearby."
    new "I let Enok off the hook for now and take a seat nearby.\n我暂时放过 Enok，在附近坐了下来。"

    old "I originally intended to chat with Enok while he cooked, but I mostly end up watching him instead. There's something very graceful about the way he gently and confidently handles the whole process."
    new "I originally intended to chat with Enok while he cooked, but I mostly end up watching him instead. There's something very graceful about the way he gently and confidently handles the whole process.\n我原本想趁 Enok 做饭时和他聊聊天，结果大多时候却只是看着他。他轻柔而自信地操持整个过程的样子，有种说不出的优雅。"

    old "It's really starting to smell good too."
    new "It's really starting to smell good too.\n味道也真的开始飘香了。"

    old "That being said, it's taking longer than I thought it would. I have to go soon so I don't know if I'll be able to stay until it's done."
    new "That being said, it's taking longer than I thought it would. I have to go soon so I don't know if I'll be able to stay until it's done.\n话虽如此，它花的时间比我想象的要长。我很快就得走了，不知道能不能等到它做好。"

    old "Well, either way, I can still enjoy watching Enok make the dish. That's proven to be more interesting than I thought it'd be. Enok really is skilled with his hands."
    new "Well, either way, I can still enjoy watching Enok make the dish. That's proven to be more interesting than I thought it'd be. Enok really is skilled with his hands.\n不过，无论怎样，我仍能乐在其中地看 Enok 做菜。事实证明，这比我预想的更有趣。Enok 的一双手确实灵巧。"

    old "Are my hands that interesting, [protag]?"
    new "Are my hands that interesting, [protag]?\n我的手就那么有意思吗，[protag]？"

    old "I quickly snap out of the dazed like state I'd unconsciously slipped into. I really hope the expression I was making wasn't too weird."
    new "I quickly snap out of the dazed like state I'd unconsciously slipped into. I really hope the expression I was making wasn't too weird.\n我赶紧从不知不觉陷入的出神状态中回过神来，只希望自己刚才的表情别太古怪。"

    old "Ahem, sorry. I just... got caught up in watching you cook."
    new "Ahem, sorry. I just... got caught up in watching you cook.\n咳咳，抱歉。我只是……看你做菜看得入了神。"

    old "You don't have to apologize. I don't mind."
    new "You don't have to apologize. I don't mind.\n你不用道歉。我不介意。"

    old "I decide now is probably a good time to excuse myself. After all, I feel like this conversation will only get more embarrassing for me as it continues."
    new "I decide now is probably a good time to excuse myself. After all, I feel like this conversation will only get more embarrassing for me as it continues.\n我心想，现在或许是告辞的好时机。毕竟，我觉得这话再聊下去，只会让我更加难为情。"

    old "Uh, good. I'm glad I didn't upset you. Anyway, it's time for me to get going."
    new "Uh, good. I'm glad I didn't upset you. Anyway, it's time for me to get going.\n呃，那就好。很高兴没惹你不快。总之，我该走了。"

    old "Ah, wait! Don't you want to try my cooking first?"
    new "Ah, wait! Don't you want to try my cooking first?\n啊，等等！你不想先尝尝我的手艺吗？"

    old "Enok hastily pulls the fish off the fire. I guess he really wants me to try it. Obviously, I can't say that I'm not tempted..."
    new "Enok hastily pulls the fish off the fire. I guess he really wants me to try it. Obviously, I can't say that I'm not tempted...\nEnok 急忙把鱼从火上拿开。我想他是真的很想让我尝尝。显然，我也没法说自己不心动……"

    old "Alright. Just a bite though. Then, I really have to go."
    new "Alright. Just a bite though. Then, I really have to go.\n好吧。不过就尝一口。然后我真的得走了。"

    old "Enok nods and quickly cuts off a piece of the fish for me to try."
    new "Enok nods and quickly cuts off a piece of the fish for me to try.\nEnok 点点头，迅速切下一块鱼给我尝。"

    old "Careful. It's still hot."
    new "Careful. It's still hot.\n小心，还很烫。"

    old "I give it a second to cool and then take a bite."
    new "I give it a second to cool and then take a bite.\n我让它凉了一小会儿，然后咬了一口。"

    old "So? What do you think?"
    new "So? What do you think?\n怎么样？味道如何？"

    old "The world won't perish if I stay just a little longer, right?"
    new "The world won't perish if I stay just a little longer, right?\n我多待一小会儿，世界也不会因此毁灭，对吧？"

    old "Enok chuckles."
    new "Enok chuckles.\nEnok 轻笑出声。"

    old "It might."
    new "It might.\n说不定会哦。"

    old "Well, I'm going to have a little more anyway."
    new "Well, I'm going to have a little more anyway.\n管他呢，反正我要再多吃一点。"

    old "That good, huh?"
    new "That good, huh?\n真有那么好吃？"

    old "Enok, this is quite possibly the best fish-based food that I have ever eaten. You're an amazing cook."
    new "Enok, this is quite possibly the best fish-based food that I have ever eaten. You're an amazing cook.\nEnok，这可能是我吃过的最棒的鱼类菜肴。你真是个了不起的厨师。"

    old "A slight, embarrassed blush creeps into his cheeks. My words must have flattered him."
    new "A slight, embarrassed blush creeps into his cheeks. My words must have flattered him.\n一抹羞怯的红晕悄悄爬上他的脸颊。我的话想必让他十分受用。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. But, in this case, I must say that having such rare ingredients made everything easy."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. But, in this case, I must say that having such rare ingredients made everything easy.\n谢谢你，[protag]。不过这一次，我得说，多亏有了这么稀有的食材，一切才变得简单。"

    old "Now this is interesting. I'm not used to Enok being so humble."
    new "Now this is interesting. I'm not used to Enok being so humble.\n这倒有趣了。我还不习惯 Enok 如此谦逊。"

    old "Seeing this new side of Enok and being able to eat something so delicious has made this trip worthwhile. The next time he sends me an urgent list of ingredients I won't even question it."
    new "Seeing this new side of Enok and being able to eat something so delicious has made this trip worthwhile. The next time he sends me an urgent list of ingredients I won't even question it.\n看到 Enok 这全新的一面，还能吃到如此美味，这一趟当真值了。下次他再给我寄“紧急食材清单”，我连问都不会再问。"

    old "I linger a bit longer to finish up my food and chat with Enok a bit more before actually taking my leave this time."
    new "I linger a bit longer to finish up my food and chat with Enok a bit more before actually taking my leave this time.\n我多逗留了一会儿，吃完了食物，又和 Enok 多聊了几句，这次才真正起身告辞。"

    old "As I leave the swamp, I can't help but think what other dishes I'm missing out on. I really should come by more often. For the food and for Enok, of course."
    new "As I leave the swamp, I can't help but think what other dishes I'm missing out on. I really should come by more often. For the food and for Enok, of course.\n离开沼泽时，我忍不住想，自己还错过了多少美味佳肴。我真该多来几次——当然，为了美食，也为了 Enok。"

    old "Enok immediately lights up when he sees me approach."
    new "Enok immediately lights up when he sees me approach.\nEnok 一看到我走近，立刻容光焕发。"

    old "[protag]! You came! Welcome to my humble home."
    new "[protag]! You came! Welcome to my humble home.\n[protag]！你来了！欢迎光临我的寒舍。"

    old "Your home? Ah, you mean the swamps."
    new "Your home? Ah, you mean the swamps.\n你家？啊，你是说这片沼泽。"

    old "Well, yes, but look here. I built something to make the place feel more comfortable."
    new "Well, yes, but look here. I built something to make the place feel more comfortable.\n嗯，是啊，不过你来看这儿。我搭了点东西，让这地方更舒服些。"

    old "I follow Enok behind a large rock and, to my surprise, he's crafted a sort of shelter with wood, rocks, pieces of metal... there's even a tent for rainy days."
    new "I follow Enok behind a large rock and, to my surprise, he's crafted a sort of shelter with wood, rocks, pieces of metal... there's even a tent for rainy days.\n我跟着 Enok 走到一块大岩石后面，惊讶地发现，他用木头、石块、金属片搭起了一个类似遮蔽所的东西……甚至还有一顶下雨天用的帐篷。"

    old "It's not as cozy as one of the bedrooms at Grimoire's inn, but at least it's something."
    new "It's not as cozy as one of the bedrooms at Grimoire's inn, but at least it's something.\n它虽不如 Grimoire 旅店里的卧房舒适，但好歹是个落脚之处。"

    old "It's impressive. Considering where you are, I think you've managed to do a great job, Enok."
    new "It's impressive. Considering where you are, I think you've managed to do a great job, Enok.\n很了不起。考虑到你身处的地方，我觉得你干得相当出色，Enok。"

    old "It wasn't as hard as you'd think. Unfortunately, with all of the undead and lizardmen around, it's easy enough to find abandoned carts on the few trade routes that still pass by the swamps. They're left behind by merchants that are assaulted, robbed, or worse."
    new "It wasn't as hard as you'd think. Unfortunately, with all of the undead and lizardmen around, it's easy enough to find abandoned carts on the few trade routes that still pass by the swamps. They're left behind by merchants that are assaulted, robbed, or worse.\n没你想的那么难。不巧的是，四下满是不死族和蜥蜴人，那些仍经过沼泽的少数商路上，被遗弃的货车随处可见。它们是被袭击、被洗劫，甚至遭遇更糟厄运的商人们留下的。"

    old "I've heard as much from the council. The situation sounds pretty dire. I mean, they're always discussing what should be done about the bandits and nagas..."
    new "I've heard as much from the council. The situation sounds pretty dire. I mean, they're always discussing what should be done about the bandits and nagas...\n这些我从议会那里听说了不少。局势听起来相当严峻。他们总是在讨论该如何处置匪徒和 naga……"

    old "I trail off, realizing I've said one word too much."
    new "I trail off, realizing I've said one word too much.\n我声音渐渐低了下去，意识到自己说多了。"

    old "I'm sorry, Enok. You do know I didn't mean you and Sylrissa, right?"
    new "I'm sorry, Enok. You do know I didn't mean you and Sylrissa, right?\n抱歉，Enok。你知道我说的不是你和 Sylrissa，对吧？"

    old "Of course. I know that you didn't mean it in a bad way. Still, when you say things like that... it hurts."
    new "Of course. I know that you didn't mean it in a bad way. Still, when you say things like that... it hurts.\n当然。我知道你不是恶意。不过，当你那样说的时候……还是会伤人。"

    old "I take a step towards Enok and place a hand on his shoulder, gently squeezing it. He says nothing, but he does smile back at me."
    new "I take a step towards Enok and place a hand on his shoulder, gently squeezing it. He says nothing, but he does smile back at me.\n我朝 Enok 走近一步，把手搭在他肩上，轻轻一捏。他什么也没说，只是对我回以微笑。"

    old "I will be more careful in future. I didn't mean to hurt your feelings."
    new "I will be more careful in future. I didn't mean to hurt your feelings.\n以后我会更注意的。我不是有意伤你的心。"

    old "Enok, you and Sylrissa aren't like the other nagas. You're both special cases."
    new "Enok, you and Sylrissa aren't like the other nagas. You're both special cases.\nEnok，你和 Sylrissa 与别的 naga 不同。你们俩都是特例。"

    old "So when other people and I talk about nagas in instances like this, you shouldn't assume whatever is said applies to you too. You don't have to feel bad about it."
    new "So when other people and I talk about nagas in instances like this, you shouldn't assume whatever is said applies to you too. You don't have to feel bad about it.\n所以，当别人和我在这种时候谈起 naga 时，你不必觉得那些话也针对你。你不必为此难过。"

    old "I know that doesn't excuse how insensitive it sounds, but..."
    new "I know that doesn't excuse how insensitive it sounds, but...\n我知道，这并不能为那些话听来有多伤人和开脱，可是……"

    old "What? No, you misunderstood. I wasn't offended because I thought you were equating Sylrissa and I with the other nagas. I was sad."
    new "What? No, you misunderstood. I wasn't offended because I thought you were equating Sylrissa and I with the other nagas. I was sad.\n什么？不，你误会了。我并不是因为觉得你把我和 Sylrissa 与其他 naga 相提并论而生气。我是难过。"

    old "I think that if Sylrissa and I managed to change, the other nagas should be able to too. But, everytime I hear you and others bring up nagas, it serves as a reminder that most of us are still basically monsters. That's why I said it hurt."
    new "I think that if Sylrissa and I managed to change, the other nagas should be able to too. But, everytime I hear you and others bring up nagas, it serves as a reminder that most of us are still basically monsters. That's why I said it hurt.\n我想，既然我和 Sylrissa 都能改变，其他 naga 应该也能。可每次听到你和其他人提起 naga，都像是在提醒我：我们中的大多数，骨子里依然是怪物。所以我才说那很伤人。"

    old "Ah, so you meant it in that sense. Hmm..."
    new "Ah, so you meant it in that sense. Hmm...\n啊，原来你是这个意思。嗯……"

    old "I'm not sure. I mean, it's possible but, if you think about it, when a group of people are used to behaving and thinking in a cetain way... it's really hard for them to change."
    new "I'm not sure. I mean, it's possible but, if you think about it, when a group of people are used to behaving and thinking in a cetain way... it's really hard for them to change.\n我也说不准。我是说，那或许可能，但你想想，当一群人习惯了某种行为和思维方式……要他们改变，真的很难。"

    old "But can't they see that what they're doing is wrong? It should be common sense! As they are now, they're worse than bandits. They don't just rob caravans, they actually enjoy killing people. It's disgusting."
    new "But can't they see that what they're doing is wrong? It should be common sense! As they are now, they're worse than bandits. They don't just rob caravans, they actually enjoy killing people. It's disgusting.\n可他们难道看不出自己的所作所为是错的吗？这本该是常识！他们现在这样，比匪徒还不如。他们不只是抢劫商队，还真的以杀人为乐。真令人作呕。"

    old "I know and I agree. To me, what they're doing is wrong too. But-- and note that I'm definitely not trying to justify their actions-- this way of life is all they've known since they were born."
    new "I know and I agree. To me, what they're doing is wrong too. But-- and note that I'm definitely not trying to justify their actions-- this way of life is all they've known since they were born.\n我知道，我也同意。对我而言，他们做的也是错的。不过——先说清楚，我绝不是要为他们的行为开脱——这种生活方式，是他们打出生起就只知道的一切。"

    old "Let's see... It might be easier to explain using an example."
    new "Let's see... It might be easier to explain using an example.\n让我想想……也许用个例子更容易说清。"

    old "Think of the Amazons. In their culture, men aren't seen as equals. They're used for sex and that's about it. They'd never be allowed to rule or fight. It wouldn't matter how talented a man was."
    new "Think of the Amazons. In their culture, men aren't seen as equals. They're used for sex and that's about it. They'd never be allowed to rule or fight. It wouldn't matter how talented a man was.\n想想 Amazons。在她们的文化里，男人不被视为平等的存在。他们被用来满足欲望，仅此而已。他们永远不被允许掌权或作战。无论一个男人多有才华，都没用。"

    old "Yes, but this is different. Amazon's don't ruthlessly kill other races."
    new "Yes, but this is different. Amazon's don't ruthlessly kill other races.\n是，但这是两码事。Amazon 不会残暴地屠杀其他种族。"

    old "That's because that isn't a part of their culture. It doesn't mean that they don't do other things that, in other people's eyes, seem completely crazy and unjustifiable."
    new "That's because that isn't a part of their culture. It doesn't mean that they don't do other things that, in other people's eyes, seem completely crazy and unjustifiable.\n那是因为那并非她们文化的一部分。这并不意味着她们不会做出在别人眼里荒唐至极、毫无道理的其他事。"

    old "For instance, I heard an interesting story from a healer in Grimoire the other day."
    new "For instance, I heard an interesting story from a healer in Grimoire the other day.\n比如，前几天我从 Grimoire 一位治疗师那里听了个有趣的故事。"

    old "And this healer is related to the amazons somehow?"
    new "And this healer is related to the amazons somehow?\n这位治疗师和 amazons 有什么关联吗？"

    old "Yes. The healer is a half elf who has lived in Grimoire for centuries. Anyway, a long time ago, way before Queen Karen was even born, one of the best fighters the amazons had to offer got sick. Back then, the Five Hundred Years War was raging across Aravorn."
    new "Yes. The healer is a half elf who has lived in Grimoire for centuries. Anyway, a long time ago, way before Queen Karen was even born, one of the best fighters the amazons had to offer got sick. Back then, the Five Hundred Years War was raging across Aravorn.\n有。那治疗师是个在 Grimoire 生活了几个世纪的半精灵。总之，很久以前，早在 Karen 女王出生之前，amazons 麾下最出色的战士之一病倒了。那时，Five Hundred Years War 正在 Aravorn 全境蔓延。"

    old "Ah, yes. I know about that war. I've read about it in books."
    new "Ah, yes. I know about that war. I've read about it in books.\n啊，对。我知道那场战争。我在书里读到过。"

    old "Then you know that while the humans and elves waged war, the Amazons remained neutral. They cut themselves off from the rest of the world. For them, that was fine. They didn't need anyone else after all."
    new "Then you know that while the humans and elves waged war, the Amazons remained neutral. They cut themselves off from the rest of the world. For them, that was fine. They didn't need anyone else after all.\n那你该知道，当人类与精灵交战时，Amazons 保持中立。她们把自己与世界其他部分隔绝开来。对她们来说，那样挺好。毕竟她们不需要任何人。"

    old "At least, until Herza, one of the strongest amazon warriors who'd ever lived, got seriously ill. Nobody knows exactly how it happened, but all that mattered was that she was dying."
    new "At least, until Herza, one of the strongest amazon warriors who'd ever lived, got seriously ill. Nobody knows exactly how it happened, but all that mattered was that she was dying.\n至少，直到 Herza 重病缠身——她是史上最强的 amazon 战士之一。没人确切知道是怎么回事，但关键只在于：她快死了。"

    old "It just so happened that, at the same time, the amazons happened to be holding a talented healer prisoner."
    new "It just so happened that, at the same time, the amazons happened to be holding a talented healer prisoner.\n而偏偏就在同一时间，amazons 恰好关押着一位才华横溢的治疗师。"

    old "Should I know who this healer was?"
    new "Should I know who this healer was?\n我该认识这位治疗师吗？"

    old "Ah, no. Not necessarily. I mean, you can find his name if you look hard enough, but... well, I guess now is where admit that I can't actually recall it myself."
    new "Ah, no. Not necessarily. I mean, you can find his name if you look hard enough, but... well, I guess now is where admit that I can't actually recall it myself.\n啊，不，不一定。我是说，你若肯下功夫查，是能找到他名字的，但……嗯，我想现在我得承认，我自己其实也想不起来了。"

    old "There goes my immersion."
    new "There goes my immersion.\n我的代入感顿时没了。"

    old "Look, the name isn't the important part. This healer felt that it was his duty to save Herza, so he offered his help to the amazons. In the end though, the amazon elders predictably refused to let him help."
    new "Look, the name isn't the important part. This healer felt that it was his duty to save Herza, so he offered his help to the amazons. In the end though, the amazon elders predictably refused to let him help.\n听着，名字并不重要。那位治疗师觉得救 Herza 是他的职责，于是主动向 amazons 提出帮忙。可最终，amazon 的长老们如预料般拒绝了他。"

    old "I knew amazons didn't like magic, but that seems foolish."
    new "I knew amazons didn't like magic, but that seems foolish.\n我知道 amazons 不喜欢魔法，但那也太愚蠢了。"

    old "Hold on. Magic wasn't the reason he was refused. Yes, amazons tend to dislike magic and some even despise it, but they might have given in and allowed it if that was their only issue."
    new "Hold on. Magic wasn't the reason he was refused. Yes, amazons tend to dislike magic and some even despise it, but they might have given in and allowed it if that was their only issue.\n等等。他被拒绝，不是因为魔法。不错，amazons 往往不喜欢魔法，有些人甚至深恶痛绝，但若这是唯一的问题，她们说不定也就让步同意了。"

    old "The main issue was that he was a man. They followed their traditons and determined that he couldn't be a healer. He was a man so all he was in their eyes was a slave."
    new "The main issue was that he was a man. They followed their traditons and determined that he couldn't be a healer. He was a man so all he was in their eyes was a slave.\n主要问题在于，他是个男人。她们遵循自己的传统，认定他不能当治疗师。他是男人，所以在她们眼里，他只是个奴隶。"

    old "He tried to convince them to change their minds but it didn't work. They ended up whipping him until he lost his resolve and stopped asking to help."
    new "He tried to convince them to change their minds but it didn't work. They ended up whipping him until he lost his resolve and stopped asking to help.\n他试图说服她们回心转意，却无济于事。最后，她们鞭打他，直到他放弃坚持，不再请求帮忙。"

    old "That's awful. And insane. Herza didn't stand a chance, did she?"
    new "That's awful. And insane. Herza didn't stand a chance, did she?\n太可怕了。简直是疯了。Herza 根本没有活路，对吧？"

    old "I shake my head."
    new "I shake my head.\n我摇了摇头。"

    old "No. Her fellow amazons and their traditons were Herza's greatest enemy in this case."
    new "No. Her fellow amazons and their traditons were Herza's greatest enemy in this case.\n没有。在那件事上，Herza 最大的敌人，正是她的 amazon 同胞和她们的传统。"

